ort Jeuno, go downstairs into the Auction House area, and find a ??? on some crates just outside the Duty-Free Shop (Jeuno) at (Port Jeuno (H-8)).",["zone"]="Port Jeuno",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click on the ??? for a cutscene and ask to have the gloves repaired.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Castle Zvahl Baileys (F-8) and touch one of the torches to spawn Dark Spark.",["zone"]="Castle Zvahl Baileys",["grid"]="F-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Dark Spark.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Touch one of the torches again to receive the Key item: Shadow Flames.\010\010If other players in the party also need this key item, they can touch the torch at this time as well; you do not need to fight Dark Spark for each party member who needs the Key item: Shadow Flames.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Port Jeuno and click on the ??? at the toolbox for another cutscene and your Fighter's Mufflers. This completes the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional\010\010The quest must be active or completed in order for the following coffers to yield their respective artifact attire.\010\010These coffers are not required to complete the quest.\010\010You must have Warrior as your main job when you open these coffers.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Guslam mentions something about armor scattered about Vana'diel. You can find two more pieces of armor by opening coffers in the following zones:\010\010Zvahl Coffer Key: Fighter's Cuisses\010\010Crawlers' Nest: Fighter's Mask",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Warrior (WAR)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Warrior (WAR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Fighter's Mufflers",["revision"]="18902"},{["job"]="Warrior (WAR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Fighter's Cuisses",["revision"]="18863"},{["job"]="Warrior (WAR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Fighter's Mask",["revision"]="18904"},{["job"]="Warrior (WAR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Borghertz's Warring Hands",["revision"]="73740"}}},{["id"]="wiki_2067",["title"]="Borghertz's Wild Hands",["page_title"]="Borghertz's Wild Hands",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Borghertz%27s_Wild_Hands",["revision"]="3872",["requirements"]="Start: Guslam \226\128\148 Upper Jeuno (H-8)\010Requirements: Beastmaster 50+\010Must have started Scattered into Shadow\010Items: Nest Coffer Key\010Key item: Old Gauntlets\010Key item: Shadow Flames\010Optional:\010Garlaige Coffer Key\010Beadeaux Coffer Key\010Previous: Scattered into Shadow",["rewards"]="Beast Gloves\010Optional:\010Beast Helm\010Beast Jackcoat",["repeatable"]="af",["summary"]="Gauntlets wrought by Borghertz, the legendary craftsman, lie hidden somewhere in Vana'diel.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="If you have any other Borghertz's Hands quest active, you must complete that one before you can start this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Guslam at Upper Jeuno (H-8) in the Durable Shields shop and accept the quest.\010\010After starting the quest, you can obtain the rewards in any order.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Main Quest",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Crawlers' Nest and open a coffer there, so either:\010\010Obtain a Nest Coffer Key or\010\010Come as a Thief and bring along Thief's Tools to pick the lock (see Picking your Coffers and Chests).\010You will obtain a pair of Key item: Old Gauntlets from the coffer.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Upper Jeuno and talk to Guslam again, who tells you he cannot repair them.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If this is your first time completing AF gear (for any job), do the following: \010\010Deadly Minnow, behind the counter in the same shop, will tell you to find a Mithra at the Tenshodo for more information.\010\010Go to Lower Jeuno and go into Neptune's Spire and talk to Yin Pocanakhu at (Lower Jeuno (J-8)). Pay her 1,000 gil to hear her story.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Port Jeuno, go downstairs into the Auction House area, and find a ??? on some crates just outside the Duty-Free Shop (Jeuno) at (Port Jeuno (H-8)).",["zone"]="Port Jeuno",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click on the ??? for a cutscene and ask to have the gloves repaired.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Castle Zvahl Baileys (F-8) and touch one of the torches to spawn Dark Spark.",["zone"]="Castle Zvahl Baileys",["grid"]="F-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Dark Spark.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Touch one of the torches again to receive the Key item: Shadow Flames.\010\010If other players in the party also need this key item, they can touch the torch at this time as well; you do not need to fight Dark Spark for each party member who needs the Key item: Shadow Flames.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Port Jeuno and click on the ??? at the toolbox for another cutscene and your Beast Gloves. This completes the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional\010\010The quest must be active or completed in order for the following coffers to yield their respective artifact attire.\010\010These coffers are not required to complete the quest.\010\010You must have Beastmaster as your main job when you open these coffers.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Guslam mentions something about armor scattered about Vana'diel. You can find two more pieces of armor by opening coffers in the following zones:\010\010Garlaige Citadel: Beast Helm\010\010Beadeaux: Beast Jackcoat",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Beastmaster (BST)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Beastmaster (BST)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Beast Gloves",["revision"]="19384"},{["job"]="Beastmaster (BST)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Beast Helm",["revision"]="28808"},{["job"]="Beastmaster (BST)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Beast Jackcoat",["revision"]="19386"},{["job"]="Beastmaster (BST)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Borghertz's Wild Hands",["revision"]="3872"}}},{["id"]="wiki_379",["title"]="Breaking Barriers (San d'Oria Mission 9-1)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 9-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_9-1",["revision"]="118361",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 8-2|Lightbringer",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Darkness looms over San d'Oria. Report to the Audience Chamber in Chateau d'Oraguille for further details.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 4 stacks of crystals to a Conquest NPC to unlock this mission, then speak to a San d'Oria Gate Guard to start it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional: Interact with the two doors to the Princes' quarters for short cutscenes.\010\010Speak with Curilla and Rahal for small talk about the previous mission. They will also have different dialogue after the KIs are obtained but before the mission is completed. \010 I was unable to get these cutscenes --Pyrra0 (talk) 02:18, 3 April 2024 (UTC)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the Chateau and check the Great Hall for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You must now travel to three ???s and obtain 3 Key Items. They must be done in order.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Valley of Sorrows",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Cape Teriggan and head to the (Cape Teriggan (J-8)) entrance to Valley of Sorrows. This is the same entrance used for Adamantoise/Aspidochelone. Sneak and Invisible across to (Valley of Sorrows (I-8)) and check the ??? to receive the Figure of Titan.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Xarcabard",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head for Xarcabard and go to (Xarcabard (H-7)) go up the hill at H-7 and turn left. The ??? is in a group of 3 clustered trees with their leaves to your left closest to the cliff (still in H-7). Select the ??? to obtain the Figure of Garuda.",["zone"]="Xarcabard",["grid"]="H-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Batallia Downs",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head for the southern Eldieme Necropolis entrance at (Batallia Downs (I-10)). Make your way to the southern room, and then to the center hole at (The Eldieme Necropolis (G-9)). You will likely need Sneak in the basement, do so before dropping down. After you drop down the hole, turn right and zone back out to Batallia Downs. \010\010If Ahtu is up, kill it first, it should not pose a problem to anyone in the party.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the ??? near the cliff to spawn two Roc NMs: Suparna (WAR) and Suparna Fledgling (WHM).\010\010 Note: There are multiple ??? on this island. Check the one near the Stone Monument at the rear of this island.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="They can both use Horde Lullaby and Massacre Elegy as well as their own respective abilities, such as Mighty Strikes and Benediction, and typical Greater Bird TP attacks.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can pull just one, but it is difficult. Recommended that you kite one NM and kill the other, then finish the kited one off.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat both NMs and check the ??? again to receive a cutscene and the Figure of Leviathan.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to the Chateau and check the Great Hall for a final cutscene that completes the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7504",["title"]="Breaking Stones",["page_title"]="Breaking Stones",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Breaking_Stones",["revision"]="119319",["requirements"]="Start: Horatius \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (I-9)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Dangruf Stone",["rewards"]="400g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Horatius wants you to bring him a rare stone that can only be found in the Dangruf Wadi.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Horatius. \010You may have to talk to him a second time to get the quest, and you must have the quest before you can trade him the stone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He needs a Dangruf Stone for his gem collection and says they can be found in Dangruf Wadi, of course, but only on sunny days.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Dangruf Wadi on a sunny day or when there is no weather and at Dangruf Wadi (I-5, J-5) location target select the ???, to receive the stone.",["zone"]="Dangruf Wadi",["grid"]="I-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Horatius and trade him the Dangruf Stone for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57935",["title"]="Breaking the Bonds of Fate",["page_title"]="Breaking the Bonds of Fate",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Breaking_the_Bonds_of_Fate",["revision"]="123879",["requirements"]="Start: ??? \226\128\148 Arrapago Reef (H-10)\010Level: Corsair 66+\010Items: Corsair's Testimony\010Previous: Against All Odds",["rewards"]="Instant Warp\010Level Cap at 75",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Obtain a Corsair's Testimony from Merrow Icedancers in Arrapago Reef or Lamia Fatedealers in Caedarva Mire.\010\010Lamia Fatedealers respawn in 5 minutes, but Merrow Icedancers take 15 minutes to respawn.\010\010Two Lamia Fatedealers spawn near the Lamian Fang Key ??? in Caedarva Mire.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the ??? at (H-10) in Arrapago Reef for a cutscene (the same ??? used in Luck of the Draw). Unfortunately this will flag AF quest line if not already completed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the testimony to the ??? to be transported to Talacca Cove.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you are ready, trade the testimony to the Rock Slab in Talacca Cove to enter a battlefield against Qultada. Any buffs you have on you except Signet/Sanction/Sigil and food will be lost.\010\010You have 10 minutes as with any of the 70 Limit Break quests.\010\010If you fail, you will need a new Corsair's Testimony to reattempt the fight.\010\010If you fail, you can simply walk to Talacca Cove. You do not need to return to the ??? in Arrapago Reef.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Opo-opo Necklace + Sleep Potions or Icarus Wings are useful to build TP for an opening Weapon Skill.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Qultada uses Phantom Roll, Quick Draw, and Wild Card.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The best strategy is to use Quick Draw as often as possible and to build TP and use Slug Shot as often as possible.\010\010Hunter's Roll is a must due to Slug Shot's low accuracy.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7423",["title"]="Brown Magic",["page_title"]="Brown Magic",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Brown_Magic",["revision"]="51126",["requirements"]="Start: Parike-Poranke - Lower Jeuno (H-8)\010Items: Gysahl Greens",["rewards"]="Removes Food (Status Effect)",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="This is a side quest, and does not show up in your Quests list.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To start this quest, trade Parike-Poranke a single Gysahl Green. He will then attempt to remove your Food (Status Effect).\010\010 He will not remove the effect of food that does not give the Food (Status Effect), such as juices.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Depending on whether you have food effect active or not will decide whether he is successful or not.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Parike tracks the amount of times he has succeeded and failed. This count is server wide.\010\010To increase the \034success\034 rate, you must have one food effect active and trade one bunch of Gysahl Greens.\010\010To increase the \034failure\034 rate, you must trade one bunch of Gysahl Greens, but have no food effect active.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If the success count reaches a multiple of 1000, a message will indicate that \034Parike-Poranke's digestive magic skill rises 0.1 points.\034 When the trader reaches a multiple of 10,000, Porike-Poranke skills up by 1.0 and you get the title \034Brown Mage Guinea Pig\034 after a cutscene. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="For getting the title \034Brown Magic By-Product\034, you have to skill up his science skill (failure skill). It follows the pattern of digestive magic skill up. At 10,000 you will be granted the title. [Wiki: needs verification] \010\010The type and quality of food doesnt matter, as long as it gives a food effect.\010\010Food items such as drinks, milk and colored drops give a status effect and do not count as food. \010\010Set up a macro (/targetnpc /item \034Gysahl Greens\034 <t>) and use the cheapest foods available - either a 99 stack of cookies (Ginger Cookies from Dream Hat +1, for example), or multiple stacks of Rarab Tails.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7532",["title"]="Brygid the Stylist",["page_title"]="Brygid the Stylist",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Brygid_the_Stylist",["revision"]="105404",["requirements"]="Start: Brygid \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (K-9)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Bronze Subligar x 1\010Robe x 1",["rewards"]="Gloves",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Brygid, the \034stylist extraordinaire,\034 gave you some fashion advice: she wants you to come back wearing a robe and a bronze subligar.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Brygid at Bastok Markets (K-9). She advises you to wear a Bronze Subligar and a Robe.",["zone"]="Bastok Markets",["grid"]="K-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain and equip these items. This combination of equipment only can be worn by: [Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 BLU,]BRD, DRK, MNK, RDM, [Conditional wiki content: wotg \226\128\148 DNC,][Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 COR,]or THF.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you are wearing both items, speak with her to receive the Gloves to complete the set.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7553",["title"]="Brygid the Stylist Returns",["page_title"]="Brygid the Stylist Returns",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Brygid_the_Stylist_Returns",["revision"]="109698",["requirements"]="Start: Brygid \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (K-9)\010Requirements: Level 52+\010At least one Artifact Armor piece equipped\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: See below\010Previous: Brygid the Stylist",["rewards"]="See below",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Brygid, the \034stylist extraordinaire,\034 has given you more fashion advice, so it's time to go shopping.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Brygid while wearing any artifact armor piece (artifact +1 and artifact weapons do not work). You only need to have one piece of AF armor on your body to trigger this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Brygid will ask that you get a new body armor and leg armor to meet the demands of the fashion world (she asks for armor equippable by your current job, with level requirements up to Level 60).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Recommend always starting the quest with her on the same job as you will see repeat requests for gear, making the hunt for pieces much easier\010\010She does not accept +1 versions of armor.\010\010She does accept augmented normal-quality armor.\010\010You can change jobs to meet the requirements of the items she has requested even though you talked to her as a different job.\010\010Some possible requests:\010!align=center colspan=4|Body\010|- \010|\194\160\194\160Banded Mail\010|\194\160\194\160Beak Jerkin\010|\194\160\194\160Bishop's Robe\010|\194\160\194\160Breastplate\010|-\010|\194\160\194\160Carapace Harness\010|\194\160\194\160Cloak\010|\194\160\194\160Cuir Bouilli\010|\194\160\194\160Frost Robe\010|- \010|\194\160\194\160Gambison\010|\194\160\194\160Iron Scale Mail\010|\194\160\194\160Linen Doublet\010|\194\160\194\160Padded Armor \010|- \010|\194\160\194\160Pyro Robe\010|\194\160\194\160Raptor Jerkin \010|\194\160\194\160Silk Coat \010|\194\160\194\160Silver Mail\010|- \010|\194\160\194\160Velvet Robe\010|\194\160\194\160White Cloak \010|\194\160\194\160Wool Doublet\010|\194\160\194\160Wool Gambison\010|- \010\010|- \010!align=center colspan=4|Legs\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#E0E0E0\034\010|\194\160\194\160Beak Trousers\010|\194\160\194\160Breeches\010|\194\160\194\160Carapace Subligar\010|\194\160\194\160Cuir Trousers\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#E0E0E0\034\010|\194\160\194\160Cuisses\010|\194\160\194\160Hose\010|\194\160\194\160Iron Cuisses \010|\194\160\194\160Iron Subligar \010|- BGCOLOR=\034#E0E0E0\034\010|\194\160\194\160Linen Slacks\010|\194\160\194\160Raptor Trousers \010|\194\160\194\160Scorpion Subligar \010|\194\160\194\160Silk Slops\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#E0E0E0\034\010|\194\160\194\160Silver Hose\010|\194\160\194\160Velvet Slops \010|\194\160\194\160White Slacks \010|\194\160\194\160Wool Hose",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you come back wearing the equipment she offers 13 types of level 50 body armor:\010!Job||Body Armor||Subligar||Dropped By\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|\194\160\194\160MNK\010|\194\160\194\160Aikido Gi\010|\194\160\194\160Aquarius Subligar\010|\194\160\194\160Fomor Monk\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|\194\160\194\160BRD/RDM[Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 /BLU/PUP][Conditional wiki content: soa \226\128\148 /RUN]\010|\194\160\194\160Cerise Doublet\010|\194\160\194\160Libra Subligar\010|\194\160\194\160Fomor Bard\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|\194\160\194\160BLM/SMN[Conditional wiki content: soa \226\128\148 /GEO]\010|\194\160\194\160Duende Cotehardie \010|\194\160\194\160Aries Subligar\010|\194\160\194\160Fomor Black Mage\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|\194\160\194\160BRD/BST\010|\194\160\194\160Gaudy Harness \010|\194\160\194\160Ophiuchus Subligar \010|\194\160\194\160Fomor Beastmaster\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|\194\160\194\160RDM[Conditional wiki content: wotg \226\128\148 /SCH]\010|\194\160\194\160Glamor Jupon \010|\194\160\194\160Scorpius Subligar \010|\194\160\194\160Fomor Red Mage\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|\194\160\194\160DRK\010|\194\160\194\160Gloom Breastplate\010|\194\160\194\160Sagittarius Subligar \010|\194\160\194\160Fomor Dark Knight\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|\194\160\194\160WHM/SMN[Conditional wiki content: soa \226\128\148 /GEO]\010|\194\160\194\160Nimbus Doublet \010|\194\160\194\160Capricornus Subligar \010|\194\160\194\160Fomor Summoner\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|\194\160\194\160NIN\010|\194\160\194\160Nokizaru Gi \010|\194\160\194\160Taurus Subligar \010|\194\160\194\160Fomor Ninja\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|\194\160\194\160WAR/PLD\010|\194\160\194\160Parade Cuirass \010|\194\160\194\160Pisces Subligar \010|\194\160\194\160Fomor Paladin\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|\194\160\194\160THF[Conditional wiki content: wotg \226\128\148 /DNC]\010|\194\160\194\160Rapparee Harness\010|\194\160\194\160Gemini Subligar \010|\194\160\194\160Fomor Thief\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|\194\160\194\160RNG[Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 /COR]\010|\194\160\194\160Shikaree Aketon\010|\194\160\194\160Virgo Subligar \010|\194\160\194\160Fomor Ranger\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|\194\160\194\160SAM\010|\194\160\194\160Shinimusha Hara-Ate \010|\194\160\194\160Cancer Subligar \010|\194\160\194\160Fomor Samurai\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|\194\160\194\160DRG\010|\194\160\194\160Wyvern Mail\010|\194\160\194\160Leo Subligar \010|\194\160\194\160Fomor Dragoon",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you select a body armor, Brygid demands the corresponding subligar. These are dropped by Fomors in Phomiuna Aqueducts as well as in the Sacrarium. All of these subligars are level 50 and Rare/EX, so you must personally go acquire it.\010\010Once you request a specific body armor, you are locked into that request until you trade her the subligar for it.\010\010If you leave Bastok Markets after showing Brygid the armor she requests but before choosing the body armor you want, you must wear the requested armor again when you return before you can choose your armor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the requested subligar to Brygid to receive your new body armor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7529",["title"]="Buckets of Gold",["page_title"]="Buckets of Gold",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Buckets_of_Gold",["revision"]="105804",["requirements"]="Start: Foss \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (F-7)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Rusty Bucket x 5",["rewards"]="300 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Foss is willing to buy rusty buckets off you, if you happen to catch five of them.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Foss and tell him you fish. He tells you that he will buy five rusty buckets from you.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="These can be caught while fishing, or purchased from the auction house.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have five, trade them to him to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_51540",["title"]="Bugi Soden",["page_title"]="Bugi Soden",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bugi_Soden",["revision"]="114812",["requirements"]="Start: Ryoma \226\128\148 Norg (H-8)\010Requirements: Ninja 72+ \010 Katana Skill 250+ (Merits not included, only base skill)\010 No other weaponskill quest active",["rewards"]="Grants the weaponskill Blade: Ku",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Wield the katana given to you by Ryoma until it has been drained of its power. Only then will you be ready to inherit the knowledge of the ancient ninja masters.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You cannot unlock this quest if you already have another Weapon Skill quest active.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="As Ninja, talk to Ryoma (H-8) in Norg who will give you the Kodachi of Trials and the Key item: Weapon Training Guide.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the Kodachi of Trials until the latent effect disappears. \010\010 How to remove the latent effect: \010\010 You must obtain 300 Weapon Skill Points.\010\010 Only Weapon Skills performed on Easy Prey or higher will count, even while under the effect of Level Sync.\010\010 Weapon Skills performed in Reives will count.\010\010 You receive 1 point for opening/soloing a Weapon Skill, 2 points for closing a Lv.1 Skillchain, 3 points for closing a Lv.2 Skillchain and 5 points for closing a level 3 Skillchain.\010\010 To check to see if the latent effect has disappeared simply open your equipment menu, and if the elemental bonuses granted by the Kodachi of Trials are gone you are done. The description of the weapon will not change.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you no longer receive the latent effect bonus, head back to Norg and trade the Kodachi of Trials back to Ryoma, who will take the weapon from you and give you a Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth and tell you to head to Labyrinth of Onzozo.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In the Labyrinth of Onzozo go to the lower right corner of I-5 and click the ??? to spawn the NM named Megapod Megalops. (Testimonials)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After defeating Megapod Megalops, re-examine the ??? to obtain the Key item: Annals of Truth.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring this back to Ryoma for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_542",["title"]="Call of the Wyrmking (Promathia Mission 3-1)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 3-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_3-1",["revision"]="118410",["requirements"]="Start: N/A\010Previous: Ancient Vows",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Not moments after arriving in Bastok, Prishe begins her search for the father of airships, Cid.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After defeating the three Mammets-19 Epsilon (Mission 2-5), you will appear in South Gustaberg.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Port Bastok and approach the Departures Entrance of the Air Travel Agency to receive a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the Metalworks in Bastok Markets and talk to Cid. You may need to talk to him multiple times before you get the cut scene. Ensure you get the cut scene before heading back to Jeuno for the next part.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_589",["title"]="Calm Before the Storm (Promathia Mission 7-4)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 7-4",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_7-4",["revision"]="120180",["requirements"]="Previous: Fire in the Eyes of Men",["rewards"]="Key item: Vessel of light\010Key item: Letters from Ulmia and Prishe",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="The crystal propulsion unit of Cid's airship has been damaged. You are to call Louverance back from Carpenters' Landing, and Shikaree Z from Bibiki Bay. You must also find the Chebukki siblings in Tavnazia and retrieve the vessel of light.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After getting the cutscene with Cid at the end of Mission 7-3, wait until the next Vana'diel game day and to talk to Cid again for the first cutscene of Mission 7-4.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will now have to kill three NMs. They can be done in any order and all are uncapped.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bibiki Bay",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Bibiki Bay (F-6) and find the ??? inside a cave.",["zone"]="Bibiki Bay",["grid"]="F-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Buff up and select the ??? to spawn a Sea Monks NM named Dalham.\010\010Dalham is level 65 (verified by tracking with Wide Scan then checking).\010\010The number of attacks this monster gets each round increases as his HP drops. He will start the fight with normal attack speed, only hitting once per round. As his HP drops (about 70%) he will use a \0342 Hour\034 animation and begin attacking twice per round. At about 40%, he will use the \0342 Hour\034 animation again, and begin attacking 3 times per round. He will use it once more around 10~15%, attacking at near Hundred Fists speed.\010\010Builds resistance to Bind and Gravity extremely quickly.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A level 75 THF/NIN can solo this monster with capped Marksmanship, Blind Bolts, Bloody Bolts, and some decent evasion gear.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A level 75 NIN/WAR can solo this. Good evasion gear, and enfeebles are needed. meds reccomended.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A level 75 RDM/NIN can solo this melee style with some effort.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A level 75 BST/WHM can solo this with minimal effort.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Has an Additional Effect: Water damage for about 21~ damage on a 75THF.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After it is dead click the ??? again for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Carpenters' Landing",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Jugner Forest (J-8) and enter Carpenters' Landing. The ??? is at Carpenters' Landing (I-9) on the edge of the water to the northeast of the docks.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Buff up and select the ??? to spawn a NM Cryptonberry Executor (NIN)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the Nin takes at least 1% of Dmg, three Cryptonberry Assassins (BLM, SMN, THF) will spawn.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Tonberries helpers are very resistant to sleep.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Executor will use Mijin Gakure unless you kill it first; this can do up to 4000 damage each.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Assassins use Manafont, Astral Flow and Perfect Dodge.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The NMs all /say something when they use their 2h. The NIN says, \034Through this we ssseek our just reward...\034 The Assassin's say, \034...Take up thy laternsss. The truth we shall illuminate.\034 The Nin's 2h can also be wasted by a person kiting it and staying out of range. The NIN will always use Mijin Gakure exactly 3 minutes after he spawns his buddies.\010\010The SMN has a random elemental pet. It will often use the Astral Flow of the same element, so you can try that Barspell. Its Astral Flow does about 800 damage to a level 75 player if not resisted. Note, the SMN Cryptonberry can summon TWO pets at once, so ignore his elemental, and be careful as he gets low on HP.\010\010The Executor has about 5000 HP.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring Reraise items for the fight and if you have a Summoner have them use Earthen Ward to negate most of Mijin Gakure's damage. Members with less then 1,000 HP when Mijin Gakure is used will still get KO'd so plan accordingly.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the Tonberries are dead click the ??? again for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="<s>It is possible to only defeat one of the Tonberries and still successfully complete this part of the mission and receive the cutscene. Once all four Tonberries are popped, if your party loses all Enmity (due to a wipe, etc.), the Tonberries will return to the ???, refill their HP, and despawn in the order that they reach the ???. If you manage to pull the last Tonberry before it despawns, you can kill that one and still get the cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="NOTE: On spawn if you pull the Cryptonberry Executor away from the ??? you wont aggro the other 3 when they spawn. The others will despawn over time and you'll be able to select the ??? for CS after killing the Cryptonberry Executor. Solo'd 75NIN/37RDM, 75BST/37WHM.</s> \010\010These strategies no longer work after the rebase. The adds spawn at the location of Cryptonberry Executor and all 4 must be defeated.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It is possible to use a THF to pop, hit the Executor 1 time with a melee to pop adds, then chain powder boots through the zone until the Executor is dead. Then pick them off 1 by 1 like Mammets.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Misareaux Coast",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Misareaux Coast (E-7) and check a Storage Compartment in the shed to spawn the NM bugard Boggelmann.\010\010Remember to Dispel its Defense Boost special (Scutum).\010\010It has about 7600 HP, and will use Blood Weapon at low health.\010\010Easily soloed as 75 RDM with Bind, Gravity, and tier III nukes. Bind and Gravity resistance builds quickly. Alternativly sub NIN and kill it slow and steadily. Will take some time so make sure you are prepared.",["zone"]="Misareaux Coast",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After it is dead click the Storage Compartment again for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Finishing the Mission",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Cid in the Metalworks (H-8) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Sueleen in the Sealion's Den (H-6) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Sealion's Den",["grid"]="H-6",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2119",["title"]="Can Cardians Cry?",["page_title"]="Can Cardians Cry?",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Can_Cardians_Cry%3F",["revision"]="56779",["requirements"]="Start: Apururu \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (H-9)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 6\010Items: Bruised Starfruit\010Previous: The All-New C-3000",["rewards"]="5000 gil",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Apururu beseeches that you find the Queen of Diamonds Cardian, who was sent on an expedition to faraway lands. Seeing that the Cardian could not make it back on her own, it's likely that she's literally gone to pieces somewhere.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Apururu asks you to find the Queen of Diamonds Cardian, who is said to be in Xarcabard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Cursed Weapons in Xarcabard until you receive a Bruised Starfruit. \010\010The Bruised Starfruit can also be bought at the Auction House under the category Others > Misc.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return the Bruised Starfruit to Apururu for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5961",["title"]="Candle-making",["page_title"]="Candle-making",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Candle-making",["revision"]="119143",["requirements"]="Start: Ilumida \226\128\148 Upper Jeuno (G-8)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Lanolin",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Bring a lanolin cube to Rouliette so she can make you a candle.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Ilumida, who lives inside a House at (Upper Jeuno (G-8)). She'll ask you to obtain a candle from the Temple of the Goddess.\010Head to the Temple of the Goddess right outside her house and speak with Rouliette (Upper Jeuno (H-9)).",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Rouliette agrees to make you a candle if you can get her a Lanolin Cube.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Lanolin Cubes are dropped by Battering Rams in La Theine Plateau.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Lanolin Cube to Rouliette to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2482",["title"]="Carbuncle Debacle",["page_title"]="Carbuncle Debacle",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Carbuncle_Debacle",["revision"]="118724",["requirements"]="Start: Carbuncle \226\128\148 Windurst Walls (G-4)\010Requirements: Summoner 50+\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Lightning Pendulum\010Wind Pendulum\010Previous: Class Reunion",["rewards"]="Evoker's Horn",["repeatable"]="af",["summary"]="Carbuncle needs your help. The Mana Orb held by the energy thief has grown so powerful it is threatening to enslave all the Carbuncles in the world. You must act now to save them!",["changes"]="This quest awards 4 HAAP points, 2 per each BCNM.",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must change zones after completing Class Reunion, or the cutscene will not activate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the House of the Hero in Windurst Walls and hear Carbuncle's cry for help.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next go and speak to Koru-Moru. located at Windurst Walls (E-7)",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Mhaura and speak to Ripapa, Mhaura (I-9) located in the Upper level outside the Sailors' Stay Inn to get the Lightning Pendulum.",["zone"]="Mhaura",["grid"]="I-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to The Boyahda Tree and walk to the Cloister of Storms and trade the Lightning Pendulum to the Lightning Protocrystal and enter the battlefield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat the two weapons, Lightning Gremlin (WAR) and Thunder Gremlin (RDM).\010\010The Lightning Gremlin's attacks have the additional effect of draining TP.\010\010The Thunder Gremlin's attacks have the additional effect of draining MP.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back and speak to Koru-Moru. He will give you the key item Daze-breaker charm.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Rabao and talk to Agado-Pugado Rabao (G-9), who will give you the Wind Pendulum.",["zone"]="Rabao",["grid"]="G-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Cape Teriggan and walk to the Cloister of Gales. Trade the Wind Pendulum to the Wind Protocrystal to fight Ogmios.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Windurst Walls, and talk to Koru-Moru for a cutscene and to receive the Evoker's Horn.\010If you fail one of the fights you will need to obtain a new Pendulum to try again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={"Summoner (SMN)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Summoner (SMN)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Evoker's Horn",["revision"]="104798"},{["job"]="Summoner (SMN)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Carbuncle Debacle",["revision"]="118724"}}},{["id"]="wiki_4803",["title"]="Cargo",["page_title"]="Cargo",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Cargo",["revision"]="117469",["requirements"]="Start: Vuntar \226\128\148 Selbina (H-9)\010Fame: Selbina\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Rolanberry 864 or\010Rolanberry 874 or\010Rolanberry 881",["rewards"]="800-3,000 gil depending on item turned in (see below)",["repeatable"]="daily",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Vuntar will pay you for aged Rolanberries.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take fresh Rolanberries to the Crawlers' Nest and place them one at a time in the various baskets until a NM crawler spawns which drops the aged Rolanberries. The different baskets will spawn different crawlers.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the aged Rolanberries to Vuntar to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is some level requirement to this quest. I just talked to Vuntar on my level 17 thief and got the message \034Yeah? Who the heck are you? If you wanna be somebody, get some experience under your belt!\034\010\010Rolanberry 881: 800g\010\010Rolanberry 874: 2000g\010\010Rolanberry 864: 3000g\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Vuntar (Foot of Central Stairs, Selbina)\010 / summary=Vuntar will pay premium price for Rolanberries, but for only those that are thoroughly aged and can serve as food for long voyages.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Selbina",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2528",["title"]="Catch It If You Can!",["page_title"]="Catch It If You Can!",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Catch_It_If_You_Can%21",["revision"]="106294",["requirements"]="Start: Ohruru \226\128\148 Port Windurst (E-7)\010Requirements: Muted, Baned, or Plagued",["rewards"]="1,000 - 1,500 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="If you ever receive a rare or remarkable status ailment, rush to show it to Ohruru.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Get a rare or remarkable status ailment: Mute, Bane, or Plague. These are added effect from hits from specific mobs. The normal status ailments Silence, Curse, or Disease will not work.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Many of these effects will not last long, so it is best to set your home point at HP #1 in Port Windurst, which is very close to Ohruru, and carry a scroll of Instant Warp to get there quickly once you are afflicted.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mute is given by Eight of Cups in the Outer Horutoto Ruins - Dahlia Tower (F-11) in West Sarutabaruta.\010\010Eight of Cups inflicts Mute through an Additional Effect by its weapon. This will have a difficult time inflicting a high level player.\010\010Note: The status effect from The Mute in Beadeaux does not work as it is actually Silence.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bane is given by Lost Soul mages in the Eldieme Necropolis.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Buffalo in Uleguerand Range can give you Plague, however its time affecting the player is limited (see talk page).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Promathia can also inflict Plague. [Conditional wiki content: soa \226\128\148 Deathmaw Orobon in Ceizak Battlegrounds can inflict Plague on a high level player with Vile Belch, however, the only way to get this quest done using them is to set your Home Point to the crystal directly outside of Ohruru's location and warp as soon as it is inflicted. It does not last long.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Simply speak with Ohruru when you're afflicted with any of the status ailments.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She will give you 1,000 gil for Mute, 1,200 gil for Bane, or 1,500 gil for Plague. She will also heal the status ailment.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_583",["title"]="Chains and Bonds (Promathia Mission 7-1)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 7-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_7-1",["revision"]="106547",["requirements"]="Previous: One to be Feared",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="You have escaped the wrath of Bahamut, but what of your companions? Could they already be back within the safehold?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Zone into Tavnazian Safehold for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Sealion's Den for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Tavnazian Safehold and check the Sewer Entrance in the basement at Tavnazian Safehold (I-7) / Basement for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="I-7 / Basement",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the top floor of the Tavnazian Safehold and check the Walnut Door at Tavnazian Safehold (K-7) / Top Floor for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="K-7 / Top Floor",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_613",["title"]="Chasing Dreams",["page_title"]="Chasing Dreams",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Chasing_Dreams",["revision"]="121212",["requirements"]="Start: Rudolfo \226\128\148 Rabao (J-7)\010Requirements: Promathia Mission 2-1: An Invitation West\010Items: Eastern Gem x5\010Key item: Washu's Flask\010Key item: Flask of Clam Water\010Key item: Storeroom Key",["rewards"]="Venerer Ring\0104000 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A young cargo hauler named Sanctia has suddenly left Rabao and Zoriboh wants you to find her. According to Zoriboh, she has probably headed for Norg to board a ship bound for the Tavnazian Marquisate...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Starting Up",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="First head to Rabao and talk to Rudolfo near the Auction House at (Rabao (J-7)). You will get a cutscene involving a man named Chelvadurai, who is looking for his daughter, Sanctia.",["zone"]="Rabao",["grid"]="J-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next head over by the tent close to the oasis and talk to Zoriboh at (Rabao (F-6)). You will get a cutscene. He will ask you to go find Sanctia.",["zone"]="Rabao",["grid"]="F-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Norg",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Norg. Go up the stairs and through the Oaken Door on the left and talk to Sohyon (Norg (J-8)). You will get a cutscene.",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Then talk to Washu, who is right behind Sohyon, and receive Key item: Washu's Flask.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Korroloka",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next head to Korroloka Tunnel to fill your flask with water from one of four Giant Clams. [Horizon change] - This change doesn't seem to exist anymore. I've done this quest on 2 chars in Aug/2026 and had to interact with all four clams.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The first Giant Clam can be found at F-10 on Map 1 as you zone into Korroloka Tunnel from Zeruhn Mines. Click on the Giant Clam in this room to partially fill your flask.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The second Giant Clam can be found at K-6 on Map 3. \010\010To get there, cross over the bridge at F/G-9, and head west to Tunnel H. This will take you to Map 3. \010\010Head west to Tunnel G. You will be on Map 2. \010\010Head west to Tunnel F. You will be back on Map 3. \010\010Head north, take the first right and head east until you reach the Giant Clam. Fill your flask again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The third Giant Clam can be found at G-11 on Map 5. \010\010Go back the way you came, but this time take Tunnel E. You will be on Map 2. \010\010Head west to Tunnel D. You will be on Map 5. \010\010Just follow the tunnel straight west to the Giant Clam. Fill up your flask.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The final Giant Clam can be found at I-10 on Map 2. \010\010Head back the way you came onto Map 2. \010\010Cross south over the bridge a H/I-8. \010\010The path will veer west, then south until it reaches a T intersection. \010\010Head east to the Giant Clam. Fill your flask up all the way.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Your flask will now be full and be changed into the Key item: Flask of Clam Water.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel, Travel, Travel",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="First, in Norg, talk to Sohyon (Norg (J-8)). He'll give you a Key item: Storeroom Key.",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, while still in Norg, talk to Gimb (Norg (H-9)) who is near the Chocobo Renter.\010\010For the next part you will need five Eastern Gem, which drop from Sahagin nearby, which you may want to farm before you leave.\010\010They drop from Stream Sahagin and River Sahagin in Yuhtunga Jungle, and from Pond Sahagin, Spring Sahagin, Riparian Sahagin and Lake Sahagin in Sea Serpent Grotto, or may be bought at the Auction House under Materials -> Goldsmithing.",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Then, in Port Bastok talk to Kagetora (Selbina (F-6)) in the Tenshodo Warehouse 2 on the top floor.",["zone"]="Selbina",["grid"]="F-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After talking to him, go downstairs and out the door (on your left) and trade 5 Eastern Gems to Patient Wheel (Port Bastok (F-5)). Regardless of your answer, you will get a cut scene.",["zone"]="Port Bastok",["grid"]="F-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, in Selbina, talk to the mayor Abelard at (Selbina (G-9)).",["zone"]="Selbina",["grid"]="G-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After that, take the Swirling Vortex in Valkurm Dunes in a cave at (Valkurm Dunes (I-9)) to Lufaise Meadows.",["zone"]="Valkurm Dunes",["grid"]="I-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will get a cutscene when you zone into Lufaise Meadows.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Finally, go back to Rabao. Talk to Zoriboh for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2605",["title"]="Chasing Quotas",["page_title"]="Chasing Quotas",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Chasing_Quotas",["revision"]="113081",["requirements"]="Start: Ceraulian \226\128\148 Port San d'Oria (I-10)\010Requirements: Dragoon 50+\010Items: Gold Hairpin\010Previous: A Craftsman's Work",["rewards"]="Drachen Brais",["repeatable"]="af",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="With your Main Job set to Dragoon, go to Cargo Room A located at Port San d'Oria (I-10) and talk to Arminibit or Ceraulian.\010\010Talking with either one will start the quest. It doesn't matter who you pick.",["zone"]="Port San d'Oria",["grid"]="I-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="During the cut-scene, agree to help Ceraulian obtain a Gold Hairpin.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From this point on, you can change to any other job to complete the quest. Once you've flagged the quest, you don't need to be Dragoon to finish.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Gold Hairpin to Ceraulian for a cut-scene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait AFTER JP MIDNIGHT and talk to Ceraulian again for another cut-scene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Northern San d'Oria (E-6) and talk to Miaux, on the upper level in front of the Blacksmith's Guild shop for a cut-scene. She will give you the Key item: Shiny Earring",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="E-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) You may now speak with Ceraulian for a clue to visit the Goldsmith's Guild.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Bastok Markets (H-8) and talk to Ardea in front of the Goldsmiths Guild.",["zone"]="Bastok Markets",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to West Ronfaure (F-6) and into the tower, speak with Esca for a cut-scene. She will mention you must go to the small island in Batallia Downs, which can only be reached through The Eldieme Necropolis.",["zone"]="West Ronfaure",["grid"]="F-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Batallia Downs (J-10) and locate the small cave on the side of the hill. Follow the tunnel into The Eldieme Necropolis.",["zone"]="Batallia Downs",["grid"]="J-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to The Eldieme Necropolis (G-9), Point D's hole at.",["zone"]="The Eldieme Necropolis",["grid"]="G-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will need at least one other person with you to operate the gates inside of The Eldieme Necropolis as follows.\010\010There is a switch to manipulate the gates in each of the four large square rooms. \010\010Wait at (H-9) where Lich spawn and face South at the closed Titan's Gate.\010\010Once there, have someone flip the switch at (H-8) to open Titan's Gate. \010\010If you require their assistance for the upcoming fight, you will need to operate a second switch in your area at (G-9) before they will be able to join you. \010\010If Lich and Tomb Wolf aggro to you, then you must put Sneak up before falling down. Fall down the CENTER hole.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you are at the bottom, follow the path until it forks and turn right. Proceed South and zone at The Eldieme Necropolis (J-9) / Map 3 out to Batallia Downs.",["zone"]="The Eldieme Necropolis",["grid"]="J-9 / Map 3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Outside on the island, make a turn to the north-west of the entrance (left) and go to the depression on the edge of the island.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the ??? Batallia Downs (I-11) to spawn the NM Sturmtiger.\010\010The ??? is on the opposite side of the island from the Stone Monument.\010\010Sturmtiger attacks extremely fast, so Blink-Tanking will be relatively ineffective.\010\010Highly susceptible to both slow and paralyze.\010\010Susceptible to bind, gravity and sleep.\010\010 (see testimonials)",["zone"]="Batallia Downs",["grid"]="I-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat it, and examine the ??? again for Key item: Ranchuriome's Legacy. Bring it back to Ceraulian Port San d'Oria (I-10) to finish the quest.",["zone"]="Port San d'Oria",["grid"]="I-10",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Dragoon (DRG)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Dragoon (DRG)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Drachen Brais",["revision"]="19665"},{["job"]="Dragoon (DRG)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Chasing Quotas",["revision"]="113081"}}},{["id"]="wiki_2546",["title"]="Chasing Tales",["page_title"]="Chasing Tales",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Chasing_Tales",["revision"]="63827",["requirements"]="Start: Tosuka-Porika \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (G-8) / North\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 3\010Previous: Early Bird Catches the Bookworm",["rewards"]="2,800 Gil",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="The Library of Magic wants you to help retrieve its overdue library books. In this case, Hae Jakkya, that Mithra who runs the auction house in Windurst Woods, has checked out the book \034A Song of Love\034, but has failed to return it by the due date.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Windurst\010\010NOTE: You must zone after completing the previous quest before you can start this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the East Optistery Windurst Waters (G-8) / North.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="G-8 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Tosuka-Porika, then talk to Furakku-Norakku.\010\010If you have activated The Jester Who'd Be King Mission, you will not be able to activate this quest until that is complete.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Hae Jakkya at Windurst Woods (I-12). \010\010Auction House employees An Shanaa and An Polaali will have some interesting dialogue after this point in the quest.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="I-12",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Return to Furakku-Norakku for some extra dialogue.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="San d'Oria and Back",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Southern San d'Oria and talk to Hae Jakhya at (Southern San d'Oria (G-9)).\010\010Note: To get to Hae Jakhya you have to go upstairs at (Southern San d'Oria (F-8)).\010\010Consider getting a Frost Turnip in San d'Oria. They have a standard merchant that sells them depending on San d'Oria's current rank. The turnip is used in the next quest in the series.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="G-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Furakku-Norakku for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) return to Hae Jakkya, An Shanaa, An Polaali for additional dialoge",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5912",["title"]="Child's Play",["page_title"]="Child's Play",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Child%27s_Play",["revision"]="101194",["requirements"]="Start: Karl \226\128\148 Port Jeuno (H-8)\010Requirements: Started the quest The Wonder Magic Set\010Items: White Rock",["rewards"]="Wonder Magic Set",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Karl will trade you a Wonder Magic Set for a white rock.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Karl (Port Jeuno (H-8)), a kid who is standing near the stairs down to the Chocobo Stables, will give a Wonder Magic Set to you if you bring him a White Rock.",["zone"]="Port Jeuno",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the White Rock to Karl and he will give you the Wonder Magic Set. \010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Karl (Port Jeuno)\010 / summary=Karl will trade you a Wonder Magic Set for a white rock.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_27834",["title"]="Chips",["page_title"]="Chips",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Chips",["revision"]="120225",["requirements"]="Start: Ghebi Damomohe \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (I-7)\010Items: Carmine Chip\010Gray Chip\010Cyan Chip\010Previous: Promathia Mission 6-3: More Questions Than Answers",["rewards"]="CCB Polymer Pump",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Ghebi Damomohe at the Neptune's Spire. \010\010Pick the first dialogue option to start the quest. Otherwise you will have to zone to restart the quest. \010\010Even though the quest is started in Lower Jeuno with Ghebi Damomohe, the quest appears as a Bastok quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Farm the chips in Pso'Xja, and then trade them all to Cid.\010\010 The Gray Chip is dropped by all Diremite type mobs.\010\010 The Carmine Chip is dropped by Snow Lizards and Frost Lizards.\010(Note that Maze Lizards and Labyrinth Lizards do not drop Carmine Chips.)\010\010 The Cyan Chip is dropped by the Mimic type mobs Treasure Chests and Archaic Chest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To repeat the quest you only need to trade the chips to Cid. You do not need to talk to Ghebi Damomohe again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2026",["title"]="Chocobilious",["page_title"]="Chocobilious",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Chocobilious",["revision"]="56787",["requirements"]="Start: Kuoh Rhel \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (K-12)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Papaka Grass",["rewards"]="1500 gil",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="One of the Chocobos in the stables has taken ill. Kuoh Rhel has asked the Mithran apothecary to make her \034secret cure-all medicament\034 for the sick bird, but when you go to pick it up, the apothecary says she is lacking one of the ingredients...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Kuoh Rhel to learn that a Chocobo is sick and she needs help getting the medicine to cure him.\010\010You will need a sprig of Papaka Grass. Papaka Grass drops from Dhalmels in Tahrongi Canyon and Buburimu Peninsula, as well as can be obtained through Chocobo Digging in East Sarutabaruta.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go talk to Tapoh Lihzeh at Windurst Woods (I-8), then trade her the Papaka Grass.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Now go and talk to Kuoh Rhel again to let her know the medicine is on its way, and receive your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_280",["title"]="Chocobo's Wounds",["page_title"]="Chocobo's Wounds",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Chocobo%27s_Wounds",["revision"]="101576",["requirements"]="Start: Brutus \226\128\148 Upper Jeuno (G-7)\010Level: 20+\010Items: Gausebit Grass x4\010Previous: None",["rewards"]="Key item: Chocobo License",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="You may feed the chocobo roughly once per in-game hour.",["steps"]={{["text"]="To begin, speak to Brutus at Upper Jeuno (G-7) on any job level 20 or higher[Conditional wiki content: raising \226\128\148 , this starts the quest Chocobo on the Loose!].",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to him two more times to start the correct quest, and choose \034Nope, never!\034.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain Gausebit Grass x4.\010\010They can be purchased from the Auction House under Weapons > Ammo & Misc. > Pet Items\010\010Can be farmed in Meriphataud Mountains from Crane Flies.\010\010They are found around the outpost, or around the entrance to Castle Oztroja\010\010Do not confuse this with Gysahl Greens which are sold from the stables NPC. They do not work.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Feed the chocobo standing next to Osker one Gausebit Grass by trading it to the chocobo.\010\010It is possible to feed the chocobo one time every in-game hour on ALL FEEDINGS. [Horizon change] \010\010It will take 6 feeding attempts to complete the quest.\010\010The first 2 attempts will automatically fail, and will not consume a grass.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the chocobo eats the 4 Gausebit Grass you are presented with a Key item: Chocobo License.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7517",["title"]="Cid's Secret",["page_title"]="Cid's Secret",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Cid%27s_Secret",["revision"]="117877",["requirements"]="Start: Cid \226\128\148 Metalworks (H-8)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Rolanberry 874",["rewards"]="Ram Mantle",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Do Cid a personal favor. Go see if there is any way you can help the matron of the Steaming Sheep Restaurant.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Cid, who will ask you to check on Hilda (Port Bastok (E-6)) in the Steaming Sheep Restaurant.",["zone"]="Port Bastok",["grid"]="E-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Port Bastok and talk to Hilda in the restaurant.\010\010If she is on the stairs, stand across from Sawyer at the counter to target her.\010\010It she is on the upper floor, stand at the counter beneath her to target her.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Rolanberry 874 from the mini-quest in Crawlers' Nest or purchased in the Auction House under Food -> Ingredients.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Rolanberry 874 to Hilda and she will give you an Key item: Unfinished Letter to take to Cid.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Metalworks and talk to Cid to deliver the letter and complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2481",["title"]="Class Reunion",["page_title"]="Class Reunion",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Class_Reunion",["revision"]="119757",["requirements"]="Start: Carbuncle \226\128\148 Windurst Walls (Windurst Walls (G-4))\010Requirements: Level 50 SMN\010Level: 50\010Items: Astragalos x4\010Ice Pendulum\010Previous: The Puppet Master",["rewards"]="Evoker's Spats",["repeatable"]="Yes, see Vingijard after AF is complete",["summary"]="Using the gemstones you received from Carbuncle, you must jog the memory of Professor Koru-Moru and get his help in reuniting the advanced class from several generations back.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Go to the House of the Hero in Windurst Walls (Windurst Walls (G-4)) as a SMN and obtain Carbuncle's Tear. \010\010You must zone if you do this straight after your Category:Artifact Weapons AF Weapon quest or any quest involving Carbuncle. \010\010Visiting the Moghouse does not count as zoning.\010\0105/27/2026 - I came to Windurst long after completing AF weapon to flag this, switched to SMN, door would not give me a CS. I clicked it 7 times, even tried Koru-Moru in case I had flagged it and didn't know, but no dice. I then zoned into Windurst Waters and back, clicked the door (twice) and it finally worked. Reported on Discord here.\010\010Make sure you're not on the quest \034Early bird catches the bookworm\034 with Furakku-Norakku as it might break this quest, even after completing it!",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From this point on, this quest can be completed on any job.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Koru-Moru in Windurst Walls (Windurst Walls (E-7)) who asks you to bring him 4 Astragalos.\010\010These can be bought from the AH under Ammunition or the Boneworkers' Guild (Windurst) in Windurst Woods, if any have been sold to the Guild.\010\010If you already have the Astragalos x4 on hand, just trade them to Koru-Moru.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Fuepepe located at the Aurastery, Windurst Waters North (Windurst Waters (L-6) / North). (May need to talk multiple times until they mention Uran-Mafran.)\010\010This is the ministry due north of the Windurst Waters Mog House. It's easiest just to run from Koru-Moru's Manor to there.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Furakku-Norakku at the Optistery, Windurst Waters North (Windurst Waters (G-8) / North).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Shantotto at her home in Windurst Walls (Windurst Walls (K-7)). She mentions that Sunny-Pabonny left for San d'Oria and to seek him out there.\010\010If you have high enough level and staff skill (230+), Shantotto may give you the cutscene for Blood and Glory. You must talk to her again to receive the correct dialogue.\010 [Wiki: out-of-era content]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Gulmama located in Northern San d'Oria at (Northern San d'Oria (E-7)) who will give you the Ice Pendulum.\010\010This is the Tarutaru you pass on the way into the Watchtower.\010\010This the also the Tarutaru who gives the Key item: Tuning fork of ice for Shiva Prime fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Fei'Yin and go to the Cloister of Frost at (Fei'Yin (I-5) / Map 2). \010\010NOTE: you do not have to do this fight as Summoner.\010\010Fei'Yin is outside Cloister of Frost.\010\010The exit from this fight is on the first floor about (Fei'Yin (K-6) / Map 1).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once inside, trade the Ice Pendulum to the Protocrystal and enter the battlefield after a short cutscene.\010\010Buffs do wear upon entering.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Here you will engage 6 Dryads, Sapling type monsters.\010\010They will automatically attack once you approach them at the top.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Windurst Walls (Windurst Walls (E-7)) and talk to Koru-Moru for your reward.\010\010If you chose not to talk to Fuepepe and Furakku-Norakku earlier, you will have to talk to them before Koru-Moru will give you your Evoker's Spats.\010\010The Ice Pendulum can be safely tossed after you have completed the fight.\010\010If you fail the BCNM fight in Cloister of Frost, you need to throw away the Ice Pendulum from your inventory and talk to Gulmama at (Northern San d'Oria (E-7)) who will give you a new Ice Pendulum to try the BCNM fight once more.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Summoner (SMN)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Summoner (SMN)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Evoker's Spats",["revision"]="113229"},{["job"]="Summoner (SMN)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Class Reunion",["revision"]="119757"}}},{["id"]="wiki_14828",["title"]="Cloak and Dagger",["page_title"]="Cloak and Dagger",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Cloak_and_Dagger",["revision"]="32505",["requirements"]="Start: Jakoh Wahcondalo \226\128\148 Kazham (J-9)\010Requirements: WAR, RDM, THF, BST, BRD, RNG, NIN[Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 , COR][Conditional wiki content: wotg \226\128\148 , or DNC] Level 71+\010Dagger Skill 230+\010No other WSNM quest active\010Items: Dagger of Trials\010Key item: Weapon Training Guide\010Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth\010Key item: Annals of Truth",["rewards"]="The weapon skill Evisceration",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The Chieftainess has come up with a deadly new dagger technique, but needs you to help her devise a way of dodging it. However, you must first complete your training.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Jakoh Wahcondalo in Kazham (J-9) who will give you the Dagger of Trials and a Key item: Weapon Training Guide.",["zone"]="Kazham",["grid"]="J-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Dagger of Trials has a latent effect that is active when the number of \034Weapon Skill Points\034 it has accumulated is less than 300. The goal is to \034break\034 the weapon by performing weaponskills and skillchains until the latent effect on the Dagger of Trials no longer functions. Please note the actual description of the weapon will not change. You must open your equipment menu and check if you are still receiving the elemental bonuses. The text, \034Latent Effect: HP+20, etc. etc.\034 will STILL BE THERE. See the section below for details on Weapon Skill Points.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optionally, you may talk to Jakoh Wahcondalo at any time to \034give up\034 and cancel the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the latent effect has been removed from the dagger, return to Kazham and trade the Dagger of Trials back to Jakoh Wahcondalo. She will take the weapon and give a Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth with instructions to head to Gustav Tunnel.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Gustav Tunnel and find (Gustav Tunnel (J-8) / Map 2) on the second map; click the ??? to spawn the quest NM named Baronial Bat. Be careful of the undead that roam the area.",["zone"]="Gustav Tunnel",["grid"]="J-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the Baronial Bat is dead, return to the ??? and examine it to obtain the Key item: Annals of Truth.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return the Annals of Truth to Jakoh Wahcondalo and she will award the weapon skill Evisceration.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5934",["title"]="Collect Tarut Cards",["page_title"]="Collect Tarut Cards",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Collect_Tarut_Cards",["revision"]="10979",["requirements"]="Start: Chululu - Lower Jeuno (I-8)\010Requirements: Jeuno Reputation 2\010Items: Tarut: Death\010Tarut: Hermit\010Tarut: King\010Tarut: Fool",["rewards"]="Chululu begins fortunetelling",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_377",["title"]="Coming of Age (San d'Oria Mission 8-1)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 8-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_8-1",["revision"]="119101",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 7-2|The Secret Weapon",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Princess Claidie will soon celebrate her coming-of-age, and the court in d'Oraguille needs help with the ceremonies. Speak to Monarlais Halver and offer your assistance.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 25 crystals to a Conquest NPC to unlock this mission, then talk to a San d'Oria Gate Guard to start it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Chateau d'Oraguille, where you'll receive a cutscene upon entering.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Halver for instructions.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional: Interact with the two doors to the Princes' quarters for short cutscenes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="NM Fight",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the Quicksand Caves and reach the Fountain of Kings at (Quicksand Caves (G-14) / Map 2) [Map 2].\010\010 The cave entrance at Eastern Altepa Desert (Eastern Altepa Desert (H-10)) will place you on [Map 2].\010\010You will need to drop in a hole at (Quicksand Caves (E-11) / Map 2) [Map 2] to reach this isolated portion of the map.",["zone"]="Quicksand Caves",["grid"]="G-14 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Clear the area and check Fountain of Kings. This will spawn two kraken NMs, Honor and Valor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="They spawn in the lake and allow for easy pulling.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can pull them one at a time, they will not link, but will aggro to sound. \010\010Valor uses Hundred Fists.\010\010Honor casts Paralyga and Silencega.\010\010It is possible to land Blind and Gravity on either, but both resist Sleep.\010\010Letting one depop and then defeating the other makes this a lot easier to deal with. \010\010Use caution when sneak popping, as they will aggro others at the fountain.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="7/2/25 - Solo'd Valor as 75BST/NIN - Sneak Popped then set Melodia on Valor I never even engaged, easy fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Fountain of Kings again, after the bodies disappear, for some Drops of Amnio.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Halver.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait until after JST midnight, and then zone in to Northern San d'Oria for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5935",["title"]="Community Service",["page_title"]="Community Service",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Community_Service",["revision"]="49093",["requirements"]="Start: Zauko \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (I-6)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 1",["rewards"]="Key item: Lamp Lighter's Membership Card (if repeated)\010Jeuno Fame",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Zauko needs someone to help light the streetlamps.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="This quest can be offered to only once per day in Vana'Diel time to one player.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Zauko in Zauko between 18:03 and 21:00.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Light all the streetlamps before 01:00 however, you may only start lighting the streetlamps from 21:00. \010You will receive a message from Zauko at 21:01, reminding you that you need to light the lamps by 01:00, regardless of your distance from him so long as you are in Lower Jeuno. If you attempt to light the streetlamps before 21:00, you will receive a false alarm with a failure message that you didn't light it in time. (This is a minor bug directly from era.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There are 12 streetlamps along the West side of Lower Jeuno (Your right side as you exit from the moghouse). Click on each streetlamp to light them in any order. You will be reminded of how many streetlamps you have left each time you light one.\010It takes around 1 to 1.5 game hours to walk to all of the streetlamps and light them so plan accordingly.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you light all the streetlamps, return to Zauko. If you completed lighting all the lamps before 01:00, you can still receive credit by speaking with Zauko afterwards. (Most likely until 18:03 the next day but is not confirmed.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5463",["title"]="Confessions of a Bellmaker",["page_title"]="Confessions of a Bellmaker",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Confessions_of_a_Bellmaker",["revision"]="121078",["requirements"]="Start: ??? \226\128\148 Riverne - Site A01 (C-7)\010Items: Key item: Ornamented Scroll\010Giant Scale x4\010Previous: Promathia Mission 2-4: An Eternal Melody",["rewards"]="Minstrel's Dagger",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A mysterious figure has requested your help repairing an old bell damaged in recent earthquakes.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Go to Riverne - Site #A01 and head towards Monarch Linn. On the last island (the one with all the Cloud Hippogryphs) don't go to the gate that zones to the small island before Monarch Linn; instead, go a little further to the other distortion. On the last island, there is a Stone Monument at Riverne - Site A01 (C-7); select that for a cutscene. \010\010Each time you go to the Stone Monument, you will need two Giant Scales that drop from the wyverns in Riverne. A total of four are needed to complete the quest.",["zone"]="Riverne - Site A01",["grid"]="C-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At the end you will obtain an Key item: Ornamented Scroll. \010\010It may be required to select monument again after the CS.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Bastok Markets and talk with Reinberta at Bastok Markets (I-8) inside the Goldsmiths' Guild (Bastok) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Bastok Markets",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Northern San d'Oria and talk with Mevreauche at Northern San d'Oria (E-6) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="E-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Riverne - Site #A01 and select the Stone Monument for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select it again to spawn the Fomor NM, Arcane Phantasm.\010\010All party members with quest flagged receive credit for killing NM.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select the Stone Monument again for a cutscene to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_53606",["title"]="Confessions of Royalty",["page_title"]="Confessions of Royalty",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Confessions_of_Royalty",["revision"]="121348",["requirements"]="Start: Raillefal \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate\010Items: Key item: Raillefal's Letter\010Previous: Knight of Gold",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Deliver Raillefal's letter to Halver in the Chateau d'Oraguille.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Knight of Gold to receive the Key item: Raillefal's Letter and begin this mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Northern San d'Oria.\010\010 If you can enter Chateau d'Oraguille, enter the Chateau and speak with Halver at Chateau d'Oraguille (I-9).\010\010 Choose the option to present Raillefal's Letter.\010\010 If you cannot enter Chateau d'Oraguille, speak with Guilerme at Northern San d'Oria (I-7) and accept his help.\010\010 You will be moved into the Chateau for the mission cutscene and returned to Northern San d'Oria afterward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete the resulting cutscene to finish the mission.\010\010 Raillefal's Letter is removed upon completion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue to Easterly Winds.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5936",["title"]="Cook's Pride",["page_title"]="Cook's Pride",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Cook%27s_Pride",["revision"]="10741",["requirements"]="Start: Naruru - Lower Jeuno (H-10)\010Requirements: Jeuno Reputation 4\010Items: Royal Jelly\010Key item: Super Soup Pot\010Previous: The Wonder Magic Set",["rewards"]="3000 gil\010Mythril Ring",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Naruru Lower Jeuno (H-10) wants a new Key item: Super Soup Pot and asks you to go to Windurst Waters to get a new one for her at the Culinarian's Guild.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="H-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In Windurst Waters, talk to Maysoon Windurst Waters (E-9) / North at the Culinarians' Guild (Windurst) who will ask for Royal Jelly in exchange for a Key item: Super Soup Pot.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="E-9 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you have obtained the pot, head back to Naruru Lower Jeuno (H-10) in Lower Jeuno to complete the quest and receive 3000 gil and a Mythril Ring.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Naruru (Merchant's House, Lower Jeuno)\010 / summary=Naruru can't find her favorite cooking pot. Get her a new one from the Windurst Culinarians' Guild.]",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="H-10",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57515",["title"]="Cook-a-roon?",["page_title"]="Cook-a-roon?",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Cook-a-roon%3F",["revision"]="121851",["requirements"]="Start: Ququroon \226\128\148 Nashmau (H-6) / Map 1\010Fame: None\010Items: 1 Ahtapot\0101 Istakoz\0101 Istavrit\0101 Istiridye\0101 Mercanbaligi",["rewards"]="Nashmau Stew (50% chance)",["repeatable"]="yes",["summary"]="Ququroon wants to practice cooking so he can open a restaurant one day. Help him out by bringing him the ingredients he requires.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Ququroon north of the weapon shop at Nashmau (H-6) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="H-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Agree to help him practice cooking.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain one of each of the following:\010\010 1 Ahtapot\010\010 1 Istakoz\010\010 1 Istavrit\010\010 1 Istiridye\010\010 1 Mercanbaligi",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade all five ingredients to Ququroon at the same time.\010\010 Ensure that you have at least one free inventory slot before completing the trade.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ququroon attempts to prepare the stew:\010\010 If he succeeds, you receive a Nashmau Stew.\010\010 If he fails, you receive no reward.\010\010 Ququroon has a 50% chance to succeed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The quest is completed regardless of whether Ququroon",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Repeat Completions",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After completing the quest once, another attempt can be made by trading Ququroon a new set of all five ingredients.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The quest does not need to be accepted again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="No change of area or waiting period is required between attempts.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Every repeat attempt has the same 50% chance to produce a Nashmau Stew.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Rat Race",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Rat Race requires the same five ingredients during one of its steps.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When Rat Race is active at that step, trading the ingredients to Ququroon progresses Rat Race instead of Cook-a-roon?.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Rat Race turn-in is guaranteed to produce a Nashmau Stew.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Completing that turn-in does not complete Cook-a-roon?.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2023",["title"]="Creepy Crawlies",["page_title"]="Creepy Crawlies",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Creepy_Crawlies",["revision"]="56790",["requirements"]="Start: Illu Bohjaa \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (I-6)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Silk Thread x3\010or\010Crawler Calculus x3",["rewards"]="600 gil",["repeatable"]="yes",["summary"]="The dhalmel farmer wants you to cull the crawler pests that eat up all the dhalmel food. Bring her three Silk Threads or three Crawler Calculi as proof of your efforts in order to gain a reward.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Illu Bohjaa wants you to clear out the Crawlers that have been eating up all of her food supplies.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She will reward you if you bring her either 3 Silk Threads or 3 Crawler Calculi.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="They both drop off Crawlers in Sarutabaruta.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5963",["title"]="Crest of Davoi",["page_title"]="Crest of Davoi",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Crest_of_Davoi",["revision"]="122449",["requirements"]="Start: Baudin \226\128\148 Upper Jeuno (G-8)\010Requirements: Magicite Mission active\010Key item: Silver Bell\010Items: Coeurl Meat",["rewards"]="Key item: Crest of Davoi (Key Item)",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Baudin asks for a piece of coeurl meat. He offers a crest of Davoi in return.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="note: you must have spoken with Aldo at Lower Jeuno (J-8) to obtain Key item: Silver Bell needed for this quest. This is a sub quest of the Magicite missions: Magicite (San d'Oria), Magicite (Windurst), and Magicite (Bastok)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Baudin, located at Upper Jeuno (G-8), wants Coeurl Meat.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade him a piece of Coeurl Meat to complete the quest and receive the Key item: Crest of Davoi (Key Item).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2521",["title"]="Crying Over Onions",["page_title"]="Crying Over Onions",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Crying_Over_Onions",["revision"]="122140",["requirements"]="Start: Kohlo-Lakolo \226\128\148 Port Windurst (G-5)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 5\010Items: Star Spinel\010Previous: Onion Rings",["rewards"]="Star Necklace",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Honoi-Gomoi, a merchant who lives in Windurst Waters, has ordered the Star Onion Brigade to return the Mana Orb to him. Help the gang out of this fix before they're framed as a bunch of thieves.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must change areas after completing the previous quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kohlo-Lakolo will tell you Honoi-Gomoi wants the mana orb back.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Honoi-Gomoi in Windurst Waters (E-7) / South, upstairs in the back of the house. He'll rant about the orb and Nanaa Mihgo.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="E-7 / South",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(optional) Talk to Nanaa Mihgo and she'll talk about the merchant, saying you should just give him the orb back.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Find a Star Spinel and bring it to Honoi-Gomoi. This will trigger a cutscene and you will be given your reward: a Star Necklace.\010\010Star Spinels are Rare/Exclusive items that drop from Spelunking Sabotenders in Quicksand Caves.\010\010You will need to pass through 2 weight sensors. The weight sensors can be activated by one Galka, or three Tarutaru, or any combination of 2 individuals that are Elvaan, Hume, Mithra, or Tarutaru. You can reach them by taking the entrance at (D-12) of Western Altepa Desert by taking the tunnel on the border of (C-11) and (D-11), which leads off the map. You can also find them in the caves outside the Chamber of Oracles. \010\010Or enter Quicksand Caves from Western Altepa Desert (G-5). You will need to pass through two weight sensors to reach the camp. The first at J-6. The second at H-7.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Like all Cactuar monsters, they can and will use 1000 Needles, which can cause significant damage to a solo player even at level 75.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you trade Star Spinels to Honoi-Gomoi, talk to Kohlo-Lakolo for a CS, then talk to Honoi-Gomoi a final time to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2314",["title"]="Curses, Foiled A-Golem!?",["page_title"]="Curses, Foiled A-Golem!?",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Curses%2C_Foiled_A-Golem%21%3F",["revision"]="123011",["requirements"]="Start: Shantotto \226\128\148 Windurst Walls (K-7)\010Requirements: Level 10+\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Key item: Shantotto's New Spell\010Previous: Curses, Foiled...Again!?",["rewards"]="Scroll of Warp II",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Shantotto wants you to go ask the Rhinostery's Rukususu about how her magic is performing. Rukususu's party is said to be at the tower ruins on the Beaucedine Glacier.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must zone after completing Curses, Foiled...Again!?. Logging out and back in will count as zoning.\010\010If you are on certain quests or missions, speaking to Shantotto more than once may be necessary.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Shantotto, who asks a question. Choose the second option, \034Ask if you're worthy.\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Shantotto then asks another question; choose the second option, \034Whatchu talkin' 'bout Shantotto?\034 \010\010Shantotto bestows you with the title \034Total Loser\034 if you choose the first option, \034Yes mommy\034 instead of the second option. If you do not choose this option, however, you can still get the title at the title-changing NPC after the quest has been completed.\010\010The title \034Total Loser\034 is not necessary for this quest. Choosing the second option on the first question is, however. It is possible to get the title without activating the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Shantotto tells you to go to the Beaucedine Glacier and find Rukususu. The quest now appears in the log.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the tower at (Beaucedine Glacier (I-7)) in Beaucedine Glacier\010\010From the Beaucedine Glacier outpost, take the downramp and turn left at the bottom. Follow this around to another downramp. Follow it and turn left at the bottom. The tower appears shortly.",["zone"]="Beaucedine Glacier",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Torino-Samarino, who asks a question. Select the first option to get Key item: Shantotto's New Spell.\010\010If you are on Desires of Emptiness, Torino-Samarino may give you optional dialogue from that mission. Simply speak with Torino-Samarino again to get the dialogue for this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back outside to the glacier and to Fei'Yin. \010\010Take the slope down at (Beaucedine Glacier (I-9)). Weave your way northwards to another slope down at (Beaucedine Glacier (J-6)). The entrance to Fei'Yin is near the southwest corner of (Beaucedine Glacier (J-4)).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once inside Fei'Yin, head to (Fei'Yin (F-6) / Map 2) on the second map.",["zone"]="Fei'Yin",["grid"]="F-6 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click the first cermet door on your right (approaching from the north; Rukususu is visible through the door) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Windurst Walls and talk to Shantotto for Warp II scroll and the title \034Doctor Shantotto's Flavor of the Month.\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2038",["title"]="Curses, Foiled Again!",["page_title"]="Curses, Foiled Again!",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Curses%2C_Foiled_Again%21",["revision"]="105161",["requirements"]="Start: Shantotto \226\128\148 Windurst Walls (K-7)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Bone Chip x2\010Bomb Ash",["rewards"]="Brass Rod",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Shantotto is being bothered by an unseen Peeping Tom. To get revenge, she wants you to gather two Bone Chips and some Bomb Ash.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Shantotto Windurst Walls (K-7) Windurst Walls to begin the quest.\010\010The quest Blood and Glory may prevent you from flagging the quest, return with a job that does not meet the prerequisites for Blood and Glory.",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="K-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade her 2 Bone Chips and 1 Bomb Ash to complete the quest\010\010Both items are dropped by monsters in Inner Horutoto Ruins. The Bomb Ash is dropped by Balloons and the Bone Chips by Magicked Bones. \010\010Both items can be bought from the Auction House as well: Bomb Ash is under Materials > Alchemy, and Bone Chip is under Materials > Bonecraft.\010\010Bomb Ash can be purchased from Olaf at the Gunpowder Room on the second floor in Metalworks at (Metalworks (G-7)).\010\010Bone Chips can be purchased from Retto-Marutto or Shih Tayuun at the Boneworker's Guild in Windurst Woods (H-12).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After trading the items to Shantotto go out and speak to Hiwon-Biwon for some additional dialogue, then return and speak to Shantotto once more.\010\010To pick up the next quest in the chain, Curses, Foiled...Again!?, you must wait one game day after the final dialogue and zone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2476",["title"]="Curses, Foiled...Again!?",["page_title"]="Curses, Foiled...Again!?",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Curses%2C_Foiled...Again%21%3F",["revision"]="118590",["requirements"]="Start: Shantotto \226\128\148 Windurst Walls (K-7)\010Level: 5\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Bomb Arm x2\010Revival Tree Root\010Hiwon's Hair\010Previous: Curses, Foiled Again!",["rewards"]="Misery Staff",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The dancing spell Shantotto cast on her bothersome Peeping Tom turned out to be a deadly curse. To remove the curse, she'll need a revival tree root, two bomb arms, and some hair from the victim. Hurry, before it's too late!",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="If you are on certain quests or missions, speaking to Shantotto more than once may be necessary.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait for the next game day after the previous quest. Zone into Windurst Walls and speak with Shantotto and Hiwon-Biwon, who is just south of Shantotto's Manor at Windurst Walls (K-8). Zone out of Windurst Walls again. \010\010Blast from the Past can prevent you from beginning this quest, in which case you need to complete that quest first.\010\010This quest has been completed with Making Headlines active, however, Hiwon-Biwon's scoop is taken before this quest is started.\010After you speak to both zone out and zone in again to start quest",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="K-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Logging out and back in will count as zoning for this.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Answer two questions when you speak with Shantotto, who accuses you of being an accomplice to her crime and sent to jail. \010\010For the first question she asks, you can pick either option.\010\010For the second question you MUST pick 'No Way! Not on your life!' or the quest will not begin.\010\010Your title now becomes \034Tarutaru Murder Suspect\034.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She asks for 2 Bomb Arms, a Revival Tree Root, and Hiwon's Hair.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Hiwon-Biwon at Windurst Walls (K-8) to obtain a Hiwon's Hair.",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="K-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Collect the rest of the items and trade them to Shantotto for your reward.\010\010Your title now becomes \034Hexer Vexer.\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7549",["title"]="Dark Legacy",["page_title"]="Dark Legacy",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Dark_Legacy",["revision"]="104327",["requirements"]="Start: Raibaht \226\128\148 Metalworks (G-8)\010Requirements: Dark Knight 40+\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: none\010Items: Key item: Letter from the Darksteel Forge\010Yagudo Cherry x1 or 2 (A second cherry is only needed if you wish to receive optional dialogue from Quu Bokye)\010Key item: \034Darksteel Formula\034\010Previous: Blade of Darkness",["rewards"]="Raven Scythe",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="You have been asked to find and bring back a book pertaining to the Galka's darksteel formula.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="With your main job set to level 40+ Dark Knight, talk to Raibaht in Cid's Lab in the Metalworks. Raibaht asks you to find a book detailing the Darksteel Formula.\010After this point, the rest of the quest can be completed on any job.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Mighty Fist in the Darksteel Forge to receive a Key item: Letter from the Darksteel Forge.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Cochal-Monchal in the west wing of the Optistery in Windurst Waters North at (Windurst Waters (F-8) / North).",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="F-8 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain 2 Yagudo Cherry (only 1 is required) one to trade to Quu Bokye and one to spawn Vaa Huja the Erudite.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Giddeus. \010\010Optional: Drop down Drop E at (Giddeus (G-8) / Ground Level). Continue north to the storage room located at (Giddeus (G-6) / Underground Level) and speak to Quu Bokye. He will mention Vaa Huja the Erudite and something about Yagudo Cherries. Trade him a Yagudo Cherry and he will reveal Vaa Huja the Erudite's location and some interesting information about him.\010\010Return to the first map via the Connection A at (Giddeus (F-8) / Underground Level)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed to (Giddeus (H-7) / Ground Level) on Map 1. Drop down the hole there (Drop D).",["zone"]="Giddeus",["grid"]="H-7 / Ground Level",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head south to transition back to Map 1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed southeast to (Giddeus (H-14) / Ground Level).\010\010Do not drop off any of the cliffs after you exit the cave.",["zone"]="Giddeus",["grid"]="H-14 / Ground Level",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Yagudo Cherry to the ??? at (Giddeus (H-14) / Ground Level) to spawn Vaa Huja the Erudite.(You only need one Yagudo Cherry if you're going with a group).",["zone"]="Giddeus",["grid"]="H-14 / Ground Level",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Vaa Huja the Erudite and check the ??? again to receive the Key item: \034Darksteel Formula\034.\010\010Optional: Talk to Cochal-Monchal in the Optistery.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Metalworks.\010\010Optional: Talk to Mighty Fist.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Raibaht to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={"Dark Knight (DRK)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Dark Knight (DRK)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Raven Scythe",["revision"]="118220"},{["job"]="Dark Knight (DRK)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Dark Legacy",["revision"]="104327"}}},{["id"]="wiki_7550",["title"]="Dark Puppet",["page_title"]="Dark Puppet",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Dark_Puppet",["revision"]="119199",["requirements"]="Start: Cid \226\128\148 Metalworks (G-8)\010Requirements: Dark Knight 50+\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: none\010Items: Darksteel Ingot\010Previous: Dark Legacy",["rewards"]="Chaos Sollerets",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="Zeid's letter to Cid reports him finding one of the weapons forged by Gerwitz, the legendary darksteel smith... but it has taken the form of an evil weapon. You must meet Zeid and help him with his task.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Go to Cid's Lab in the Metalworks and talk to Cid to hear comments about the Darksteel Formula you found during the Dark Legacy quest. Raibaht informs Cid that Zeid sent him a letter indicating that he found one of the weapons forged by Gerwitz, the legendary darksteel smith, but it has taken the form of an evil weapon. You must meet Zeid and help him with his task. \010You can be on any job from here on.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Darksteel Ingot (only one is needed per group).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Ordelle's Caves from La Theine Plateau for a cutscene where Zeid comes up to you and tells you that a merchant who had been in the caves was attacked by Gerwitz's Axe.",["zone"]="La Theine Plateau",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the east path and head towards (Ordelle's Caves (I-8) / Map 1)",["zone"]="Ordelle's Caves",["grid"]="I-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When ready, trade the Darksteel Ingot to the ??? next to the stalagmite and spawn Gerwitz's Axe.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Gerwitz's Axe and it will drop Gerwitz's Axe (Item).\010\010Note: If you die and must leave the zone you will need another Darksteel Ingot to repop.\010\010Note: Gerwitz's Axe has bad evasion and low defense but has near perfect accuracy and can hit pretty hard. (DO NOT attempt to shadow/evade tank). Successfully solo'd as 75THF/NIN with full Haste Gear; was nowhere near in danger by the time I killed it.\010\010Note: Gerwitz's Axe's melee attacks have an added Drain TP effect.\010\010Note: Gerwitz's Axe will not aggro if spawned with sneak.. Confirmed incorrect; popped Silent Oil before spawning, still aggro'd.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After obtaining Gerwitz's Axe (Item), take the south passage in (Ordelle's Caves (H-9) / Map 1) which climbs upwards.",["zone"]="Ordelle's Caves",["grid"]="H-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you finish climbing, head all the way south to the hole at (Ordelle's Caves (H-12) / Map 2). Drop down the hole.",["zone"]="Ordelle's Caves",["grid"]="H-12 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After landing, do not drop off the ledge you land upon. Go slightly north-east to the path at (Ordelle's Caves (I-11) / Map 1)and you'll find yourself at (Ordelle's Caves (J-8) / Map 3) third map.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow the path up the stairs. Go south at the fork until you reach (Ordelle's Caves (H-8) / Map 3).",["zone"]="Ordelle's Caves",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Spawn Gerwitz's Sword by trading Gerwitz's Axe (Item) to the ??? found between the cluster of stalagmites and the wall.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Gerwitz's Sword and it will drop Gerwitz's Sword (Item).\010\010Note: Gerwitz's Sword will use Blood Weapon around 50% of HP and it's not as tough as Gerwitz's Axe.\010\010Note: Gerwitz's Sword will not aggro if spawned with sneak.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The final ??? is just a bit farther south, at (Ordelle's Caves (H-10) / Map 3) in the Morbolger room.",["zone"]="Ordelle's Caves",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Spawn Gerwitz's Soul by trading Gerwitz's Sword (Item) to the ???.\010\010Gerwitz's Soul is a Ghost NM around level 54.\010\010Note: Gerwitz's Soul will not aggro if spawned with sneak.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Gerwitz's Soul.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exit to La Theine Plateau from the same map at (Ordelle's Caves (G-10) / Map 3) and you'll get a cutscene, receive your reward, and complete the quest.",["zone"]="Ordelle's Caves",["grid"]="G-10 / Map 3",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={"Dark Knight (DRK)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Dark Knight (DRK)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Chaos Sollerets",["revision"]="21413"},{["job"]="Dark Knight (DRK)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Dark Puppet",["revision"]="119199"}}},{["id"]="wiki_550",["title"]="Darkness Named (Promathia Mission 3-5)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 3-5",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_3-5",["revision"]="114980",["requirements"]="Level: 40 Cap\010Items: Gray Chip OR Carmine Chip OR Cyan Chip (one per character)\010Key item: Pso'Xja Pass\010Previous: Tending Aged Wounds",["rewards"]="1000 Experience Points\010Access to Dreamworld Dynamis\010Access to Waking Dreams quest\010Mog Wardrobe 2: 5 Slots",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Prishe has been taken to Doctor Monberaux's clinic! What ails her fragile body and what, if anything, can save her!?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Getting the Pso'Xja Pass",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Upper Jeuno (G-10) and talk to Monberaux in the Infirmary Monberaux.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Lower Jeuno (I-7) and talk to Ghebi Damomohe the receptionist at the Neptune's Spire.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, obtain a colored chip from Pso'Xja: Travel to Beaucedine Glacier and enter one of the uncapped Pso'Xja towers to farm chips, as for the later Chips quest. To obtain a Key item: Pso'Xja Pass, each player only needs one, it doesn't matter which color (Gray Chip, Carmine Chip, Cyan Chip).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Lower Jeuno (I-7) and trade your chip to Ghebi Damomohe in exchange for 500 Gil and a Key item: Pso'Xja Pass.\010\010Note: This is the first of at least two times you'll visit Pso'Xja. Consider completing A Reputation in Ruins at, or after this time. This quest grants you the Key item: Blue Bracelet and Key item: Green Bracelet which allow full access to the zone through the blue and green doors. This might be needed if you seek the Map of Pso'Xja.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Diabolos",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Gear up for a level 40 BCNM, and enter the tower at (Beaucedine Glacier (H-8)) in Beaucedine Glacier.",["zone"]="Beaucedine Glacier",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will need sneak and invis through some of the areas and not through others.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In this Pso'Xja tower, there are shimmering walls of different color. Every time you enter one you zone and all your buffs wear off.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The order of walls you want is red, black(purple looking), red, black(purple looking).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the last black zone, sneak up and ride the elevator down. There is a gate to the left, which your pass will open, and you will enter The Shrouded Maw where you will fight Diabolos. Sometimes at the last corner are sight-aggro Bombs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is an uncapped area before you start the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You start on a platform above and once someone jumps, everyone else is dragged down, and the battle begins.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The battlefield consists of 25 floor squares which may be removed by Diabolos during the fight. If you fall or are on a square that is removed, you will be eaten alive by about 8 waiting and hungry Diremite Assaulters.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can see which tiles will disappear before you drop into the arena. The tiles which will disappear have a thicker outline.\010\010If some of the corners aren't going to drop, the tank should pull Diabolos into one of the corners. With Diabolos in one corner, the three tiles in the opposite corner are outside the AoE of Nightmare, so a mage can stand there and wake people up if necessary.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The tiles will light up momentarily before they disappear.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The party will land in the center of the arena and Diabolos will be in front of you.\010\010Initial battle positions: \010D - Diabolos\010P - where party lands\010 O O D O O\010 O O O O O\010 O O P O O\010 O O O O O\010 O O O O O",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Choose tiles to stand on that won't drop, preferably with the mages outside Nightmare range. If you just want to go with tiles that will never drop in any layout, here's where to stand during battle:\010X - Tiles that may drop\010O - Tiles that will not drop\010 X X D X X\010 O X X O O - Melee on \034OO\034 to the right or on \034D\034 where Diabolos stands\010 X X X X X\010 X O X X X\010 X X O O X - Mages on \034OO\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Pull Diabolos to the 2nd row down onto the tiles marked as \034OO\034. Mages should be stand on the \034OO\034 tiles on the bottom row.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Diabolos' TP attacks:\010\010Nightmare: Inflicts anyone on the floor with Sleep and 21HP/tick Bio. Damage will not wake you up from Nightmare, only Cure and Benediction. (Benediction will also remove the Bio effect, which otherwise must be erased.) Nightmare can and should be interrupted with Stun, Head Butt or stun weaponskills such as Smash Axe. NOTE:Weapon Bash will NOT stun Nightmare! The Bard song Fowl Aubade, combined with Barsleepra, is pretty effective for helping people to wake up fast from Nightmare.\010\010Camisado: Single-target physical damage and knockback. Stand with your back to the wall so that this doesn't knock you into the pit below.\010\010Noctoshield: Gives Diabolos the effect of Phalanx (Dispel or Magic Finale).\010\010Ultimate Terror: AOE Absorb-All. Drains multiple attributes. Not too bad on its own, but it interferes with Dispelling Noctoshield and Erasing Nightmare Bio. Absorbed by Utsusemi.\010Diabolos also casts various Dark elemental spells: Sleepga, Sleep II, Bio II, Drain, Aspir, Blindga, and Dispelga.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Finishing the Mission",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you defeat Diabolos, head back to Upper Jeuno and talk to Monberaux (Upper Jeuno (G-10)) to complete the mission.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Additional Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Dealing with Nightmare is the key to this mission. If you are using weapon skills to stun Nightmare, the stunners should bring Icarus Wings so that they don't have to build TP first. If you're using a DRK for stun, that is their primary role, damage dealing is a secondary concern. It is very highly recommended to have at least two stunners (DRK[Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 or BLU]), as Diabolos can use Nightmare twice or more in a short time. \010[Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 It's been reported that Blue Mage with capped Blue Magic skill has a high rate (but not 100%) of stunning Diabolos with Head Butt. The advantage over Stun is the low MP cost, 10 second recast, and the added bonus of doing damage.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Poison Potions won't keep players safe from Nightmare's Sleep effect, but they will guard against Sleepga, so at least the stunners should drink them.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_331",["title"]="Darkness Rising (Bastok Mission 5-1)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 5-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_5-1",["revision"]="116594",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Level: 50\010Previous: Bastok Mission 4-1|Magicite",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You are to head north to a place called Fei'Yin on the Beaucedine Glacier. Go to the President's Office for a full briefing. Naji will show you in.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="[Optional] Speak to a Gate Guard. You'll be directed to the President's Office.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Naji for a cutscene, and to receive the Key item: New Fei'Yin Seal.\010\010[Template :Nation Mission 5-1: ]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Finishing the Mission",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Naji to complete the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_600",["title"]="Dawn (Promathia Mission 8-4)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 8-4",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_8-4",["revision"]="118654",["requirements"]="Previous: When Angels Fall",["rewards"]="Rajas Ring or Sattva Ring or Tamas Ring,\010Mog Wardrobe 2: 5 Slots",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Revelations of truth accompany the awakening of Promathia. The world and its people stand in the twilight of the apocalypse. Dawn Goddess Altana, grant us victory!",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Zone into Al'Taieu for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to The Garden of Ru'Hmet and pass through the Cermet Portal to get to the main garden elevator. Choose to descend from the first floor and zone into the Empyreal Paradox. Check the Transcendental Radiance for a cutscene and then check it again to enter the battleground.\010\010All buffs and TP are removed upon entering the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will now face Promathia himself. The time limit for the battle is 30 minutes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Prishe and Selh'teus will appear to help. They will generally take care of themselves, but Prishe can be healed if she draws aggro. If she's KO'd, you can cast Raise on her and she will go back to fighting with full HP and no weakness. Selh'teus cannot be healed by players, but has several abilities he can use to heal himself. If Selh'teus is KO'd, the battle immediately ends and the party will be removed from the battlefield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In addition to this, if the entire party is KO'd at any point during the fight, they will be immediately removed from the battlefield. The game will not allow you the usual 3 minutes for someone to get back up like it typically does in other battlefields. Because of this, you cannot fully wipe and Reraise to recover if needed; one party member must always remain alive.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Promathia has two forms. Once you beat the first form, you can rest before engaging the second form, though eventually Prishe gets tired of waiting and runs in.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Promathia has low evasion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon defeating Promathia's second form, every living party member (including those doing it for the first time) will receive 2000 Experience Points or Limit Points.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="First form",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Promathia's first form has about 8000 HP. It uses the following special attacks:\010\010 Empty Salvation: AoE (range 25?) damage (~250) and Dispel 3 effects\010\010 Pestilent Penance: Cone Attack damage (~400) and Plague\010\010 Malevolent Blessing: Cone Attack damage (400-500) and Curse\010\010 Infernal Deliverance: AoE (targeted?) damage and Stun, ignores Utsusemi\010\010 Chains of (Apathy, Arrogance, Cowardice, Envy and Rage): No effect, due to the lights from the mothercrystals.\010\010 Comet (Spell): Single-target magic damage (600-900). Can be absorbed by Utsusemi.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Prishe fights along with you.\010\010She uses a Daedalus Wing when you start to fight.\010\010She uses the Auroral Uppercut Weapon Skill, which is rather weak (23 damage).\010\010She also casts Divine Magic nukes on Promathia and Cures herself and the party.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Selh'teus fights along with you a bit too.\010\010His Luminous Lance attack does a bit of damage and stuns Promathia for about 25 seconds.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Second form",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Promathia's second form has about 12000 HP. It uses the following special attacks:\010\010 Empty Salvation, Pestilent Penance, Malevolent Blessing, Infernal Deliverance as above\010\010 Seal of Quiescence: AoE Silence, lasts up to 75 seconds. It cannot be healed by things like Silena or Echo Drops, you must wait it out.\010\010 Winds of Oblivion: AoE Amnesia (disable Job Abilities and Weapon Skills), lasts up to 75 seconds.\010\010 Meteor (spell): AoE magic damage (300-600)\010\010 He casts this once a minute; it takes 10 seconds to cast, which is plenty of time to run out of range.\010\010 Bastion of Twilight: Magic Shield effect\010\010 Wheel of Impregnability: Invincible effect",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can tell which shield is up by looking at the big ring below Promathia. Red is physical, green is magic.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Prishe continues to fight beside you.\010\010 She eats Ambrosia when you start to fight.\010\010 This time she uses Nullifying Dropkick, which breaks Promathia's shields.\010\010 She continues to nuke Promathia and Cure herself and the party.\010\010 After a while (4m15?), she uses a Carnal Incense and Hundred Fists.\010\010 She can also use Benediction if she's in trouble.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Selh'teus continues to fight against the second form.\010\010 His Luminous Lance attack does a bit of damage and stuns Promathia for about 25 seconds.\010\010 His Revelation attack just does damage(?).\010\010 If he gets in trouble, he has Rejuvenation and Redemption moves that give HP, MP, and TP to him and any party members that may be near him.\010\010Strategy tips\010\010 Kiting Promathia is a good way to avoid most of his damaging attacks.\010\010In particular, if you have hate when he starts casting Meteor, run away from him so that his casting fails, like with King Behemoth.\010\010This is the single most important thing for winning the BC.\010\010 Watch out for Prishe and she will watch out for you.\010\010 Both of Promathia's forms can be Straight Tanked by a War/nin without Haste gear, using Luck and Skill.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Final Cutscenes\010\010Wait until JP midnight, to finish the following cutscenes for CoP. Bid farewell to some of your companions. You can visit the companions in any order but must do the cutscenes in order for that companion.\010Louverance\010\010Head to Southern San d'Oria and talk to Hinaree in the Count's Manor (Southern San d'Oria (B-6)) for a cutscene.\010\010Zone into Uleguerand Range for a cutscene.\010\010Head to Southern San d'Oria and approach the Count's Manor (Southern San d'Oria (B-6)) for a cutscene.\010Chebukkis\010\010Head to Port Windurst and talk to Chipmy-Popmy at the Fishing Guild (Port Windurst (C-8)) for a cutscene.\010\010Head to Bibiki Bay - Purgonorgo Isle and talk to ??? Warmachine at (Bibiki Bay - Purgonorgo Isle (H-11)) for a cutscene. When it ends you will receive a Colored Drop that appears to be random.\010Shikarees\010\010Zone into Mhaura for a cutscene.\010Jabbos\010\010Zone into Oldton Movalpolos for a cutscene.\010Tenzen\010\010Head to Metalworks and talk to Cid at (Metalworks (H-8)) for a cutscene.\010Once you've talked to all of them:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Ru'Lude Gardens and approach the palace for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Upper Jeuno and click on the Marble Bridge Eatery door for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At this point you can click on the Marble Bridge door again to choose one of the three \034CoP rings\034: Rajas Ring, Sattva Ring, or Tamas Ring. You can continue with the cutscenes without making your decision yet.\010\010If you discard your CoP ring, you will be able to obtain one of the three rings again by revisiting the Marble Bridge. The first time you discard the ring, you must wait until JP midnight before the CS will trigger at the Marble Bridge. If the ring is discarded again, you must wait 27 real life days before you will be able to once again choose and obtain another ring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Tavnazian Safehold and check the Walnut Door (Tavnazian Safehold (K-7) / Map 2), (upper floor: north) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="K-7 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Lufaise Meadows and approach the Blueblade Fell (Lufaise Meadows (J-6)) for the final fullscreen cutscene. SNEAK / INVISIBLE IS REQUIRED in the open area right before Blueblade Fell as there are monsters here level 81 RAM's and Birds that AGGRO.\010\010Additional note: Distant Worlds will play during the final cutscene. If you want to hear the song make sure you turn game music on. Also, it may be a good idea if you have fomor hate to cast Sneak or use a Silent Oil prior to viewing the cutscene--a party of VT-to-75 fomor spawn at Blueblade Fell and can kill you when the cutscene ends. (Invisible will wear off as soon as you enter the cutscene, but Sneak will not. Casting Sneak before approaching the edge of Blueblade Fell will ensure your safety should you exit the cutscene during the night.)",["zone"]="Lufaise Meadows",["grid"]="J-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene, the title Banisher of Emptiness will be awarded and both the Storms of Fate and Requiem of Sin quests become available.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5937",["title"]="Deal with Tenshodo",["page_title"]="Deal with Tenshodo",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Deal_with_Tenshodo",["revision"]="10147",["requirements"]="Start: Garnev - Lower Jeuno (J-7)\010Requirements: Tenshodo Reputation 5\010Items: Gold Orcmask\010Previous: A Clock Most Delicate",["rewards"]="Clock tower oil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Garnev in the Tenshodo in Lower Jeuno.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Garnev a Gold Orcmask to complete the quest and receive the clock tower oil. \010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Garnev (Tenshodo, Lower Jeuno)\010 / summary=Garnev will trade you some clock tower oil for a gold Orcmask.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57451",["title"]="Delivering the Goods",["page_title"]="Delivering the Goods",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Delivering_the_Goods",["revision"]="121568",["requirements"]="Start: Fochacha \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-9) / Map 1\010Requirements: Access to Aht Urhgan Whitegate\010Fame: None\010Items: None",["rewards"]="Imperial Bronze Piece x3",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Fochacha's cooking supplies have been stolen! Her son has gone to retrieve them, but how is he faring? You might try looking for him at Shararat's Teahouse, where gourmet aficionados are known to reside...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Fochacha in Serpentking Square at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-9) / Map 1 to begin the quest.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with either Qutiba or Ulamaal on the second floor of the Shararat Teahouse at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-12) / Map 1 for a cutscene.\010\010 Either NPC advances the quest; you do not need to speak with both.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-12 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Fochacha at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-9) / Map 1 to complete the quest and receive three Imperial Bronze Pieces.\010\010 You must have enough inventory space to receive all three pieces.\010\010 To begin Vanishing Act, wait until after the next Japanese midnight and change zones at least once.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_562",["title"]="Desires of Emptiness (Promathia Mission 5-2)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 5-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_5-2",["revision"]="115117",["requirements"]="Level: 50 Cap\010Previous: The Enduring Tumult of War",["rewards"]="1500 Experience Points (there is no message indicating this but you do gain it on repeat runs)\010Mog Wardrobe 2: 5 Slots",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="As with the other Promyvion areas in Promathia Mission 1-3: The Mothercrystals, your objective is to climb to the top by locating the gates guarded by a Memory Receptacle, defeat the Memory Receptacle and use the teleport to the next level.\010(Note: Sometimes defeating a Memory Receptacle does not spawn a teleport. If the gate remains dark you need to locate another Memory Receptacle on the same floor.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On levels three, four, and five, you will have to search for Memory Flux gates. They will spawn NMs; defeating these is required to proceed with the mission: \010\010The Memory Flux on the third floor will spawn Propagator, a Gorger type NM. \010\010Uses Fission to spawn Offspring mobs. \010\010The Memory Flux on the fourth floor, will spawn Solicitor, a Craver type NM. \010\010Uses Carousel for AOE damage (300-600 damage).\010\010Uses Impalement which reduces target's HP to 5% and causes Hate Reset.\010\010Uses Promyvion Brume, an AOE attack that also causes severe poison. Be sure to use Antidote in case you are targeted by Impalement.\010\010The Memory Flux on the fifth floor spawns Ponderer, a Thinker type mob.\010\010Uses Trinary Tap to absorb status effects from its target, including food. This can be dangerous if the NM absorbs e.g. protect and defensive food like Tavnazian Tacos. \010\010Uses Shadow Spread for AOE Sleep and Curse. Since hate seems to be bugged with this NM, this move is extremely dangerous if not dealt with. Sometimes Ponderer will move around, sleeping entire parties and picking off people one by one. Bring Poison Potions to counter the sleep effect. Also consider using anima here. \010After you defeat each NM, check the Memory Flux a second time for a cutscene. If you don't defeat all three Memory Flux NMs and get the respective cutscenes afterwards, you will not be able to cross to the Web of Recollections within the Spire of Vahzl and participate in the boss fight. \010\010These cutscenes grant you the option to warp to their respective Memory Flux gate from the entrance to Promyvion - Vahzl in Pso'Xja. This allows you to continue the mission at these points should you choose not to do it in one go.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you beat the Ponderer, head to the Spire of Vahzl and enter. Inside you can rest and prepare for the boss fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When ready, enter the Web of Recollections to face each of the earlier Promyvion bosses one at a time. From left to right, they are \010\010Procreator (Gorger type)\010\010Cumulator (Craver type)\010\010Agonizer (Thinker type)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can choose which boss to fight first; the next boss in the sequence will then aggro when the previous is at about 20% HP. \010\010If you pull Cumulator first, Procreator attacks next, and then Agonizer.\010\010If you pull Agonizer first, Cumulator attacks next, and then Procreator.\010\010If you pull Procreator first, Agonizer attacks next, and then Cumulator.\010(see below for strategies)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you beat all of the NMs, you will receive 1500 experience for winning the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) When the Spire battle is cleared, head out to Beaucedine Glacier (I-7) and talk to the three Tarutarus in the tower. There will not be a cutscene from the three Tarutarus, nor will the mission log change.",["zone"]="Beaucedine Glacier",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Metalworks and talk to Cid to finish the mission and receive your +5 Mog Wardrobe 2 slots reward. This will automatically start Promathia Mission 5-3: Three Paths.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Boss Fight Strategy",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="As with all Empty, their elements will be random. Make sure to note the bosses' elements so as not to cast spells that will be ineffective.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Procreator can usually be tanked for some time when it's HP is high without having to fear bad TP moves or an invasion of the Offspring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The next boss in the sequence will always aggro when the current boss is at 20% HP. Delay this mob with Terroanima and/or Bind/Shadowbind until you can finish off the weakened mob, which shouldn't take long. Also Rdm can kite with Stoneskin/Phalanx and Bind.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If your party has a full set of anima, use one Psychoanima/Hysteroanima pair at about 50%, and a second at about 25% on each boss. If you only have one set per boss, use it at 25%.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Watch out for Cumulator's Impalement early on. If it kills the tank, it's probably easier to leave the BC and try again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Any Offspring Procreator spawns will die when it dies, so just finish it off to get rid of the Offspring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Agonizer continues to be the strongest. Save resources (2-hours, MP, etc.) for finishing it quickly. Cast \034dummy\034 buffs; use Poison Potions if you brought any.[Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 Blue Mage's Headbutt is very helpful, as it can prevent many melee and TP attacks by the bosses.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The tank must not eat defense food until Agonizer is dead. If you have a Paladin tank, pulling Agonizer first allows them to use food for the other two bosses.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="With a setup including two or more BLM it is possible to win this fight without using anima or 2-hours (a good setup example is RDM, BLM x2, NIN x2 and WHM because this setup minimises the TP gain of the enemy). The strategy is to have the black mages both cast Freeze at 19-22% to kill the boss you are fighting, and have one NIN temporarily tank or a RDM Gravity kite the next one for a few seconds if necessary. It is better to use Freeze a little bit too late than too early, as the ideal is to make sure the boss you are fighting dies from the spells, then have the black mages heal to full in a safe corner and repeat the same thing on the next. Naturally if you have more than two BLM it is probably safe to start casting around 25%.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Also a setup of WHM, RDM, SAM (tank), and 3 DDs can be used throughout all the fights. Have everyone bring full sets of anima, and do not use any until you fight in the BCNM. Just be sure the mages stay back away to avoid the AoE, and all DDs to bring poison potions.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_536",["title"]="Distant Beliefs (Promathia Mission 2-3)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 2-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_2-3",["revision"]="121031",["requirements"]="Level: 40\010Items: Bronze Key \010\010Thief with a Skeleton Key will work as an alternative.\010Previous: The Lost City",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have volunteered to journey into the Phomiuna Aqueducts to defeat the minotaur. It appears that Nag'molada has set off ahead of you.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Enter Phomiuna Aqueducts from Tavnazian Safehold (I-6) / Basement. \010\010Note: When first clicking the gate to Phomiuna Aqueducts, you may get the message \034The door is locked tight.\034. Click a second time to enter. This seems to be a bug [Wiki: needs verification] . \010\010Note: Phomiuna Aqueducts is a level cap 40 zone.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="I-6 / Basement",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to Phomiuna Aqueducts (J-2) / Map 2 to find the Taurus NM Minotaur.\010\010Once one person in the alliance aggros the Minotaur, the entire alliance, regardless of where they are on the map, will be drawn in to Phomiuna Aqueducts (J-2) / Map 2 for the fight. \010\010 Make sure to move before it respawns; there is no cutscene. The Minotaur is said to have a respawn time of ten Earth minutes.\010\010 After you kill the Minotaur, you may leave the Aqueducts at any time and resume with the rest of the mission at any time.",["zone"]="Phomiuna Aqueducts",["grid"]="J-2 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you killed the Minotaur, you need to pass through the locked Iron Door at Phomiuna Aqueducts (G-8) / Map 2. \010\010Be careful not to drop off the ledge at Phomiuna Aqueducts (G-8) / Map 2 or you will need to go around again. \010\010The Iron Door can be opened with a Bronze Key, which drops from Fomor in Phomiuna Aqueducts, or by a Thief using a Skeleton Key. \010\010Note: Positioning is important in order for the Skeleton Key to work and you must be right in front of the middle of the gate for it to take the key.",["zone"]="Phomiuna Aqueducts",["grid"]="G-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue on to the Wooden Ladder at Phomiuna Aqueducts (E-8) / Map 2 for a cutscene, then climb up.",["zone"]="Phomiuna Aqueducts",["grid"]="E-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On the next map, take the north corridor. \010\010 The southern room/path has no true exit, and cannot directly access the corridor at F-8.\010\010 However, there is a one way hidden door in the room that can only be opened from the other side.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to the ??? in the south west corner of the room at Phomiuna Aqueducts (F-7) / Map 3 (Bookshelf). The bottom room, F-9, is NOT the right room. Click the ??? to open a hidden door at the south wall. \010\010 Make sure to click the correct ???. There is another one-way door in the east wall, which leads to a dead end. The only exit from this room is via a trapdoor in the floor, unless someone opens the door and lets you back out.",["zone"]="Phomiuna Aqueducts",["grid"]="F-7 / Map 3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="WARNING*\010\010If you do this solo you will need to bring some type of Reraise (Earrings,Scrolls,etc). There are lots of Stegotaur's in your path and no way to get around them.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Behind the southern door is a passage Phomiuna Aqueducts (F-8) / Map 3 where you must solve a puzzle. \010\010 The puzzle varies based on the current Vana'diel day. \010\010 Push the torches simultaneously that correspond to the following:\010\010 To push the switches, have someone count down, and press theirs before giving the \034Go\034 command. The second player should press theirs as soon as they see \034Go\034\010\010 On Firesday: Fire and Ice\010\010 On Icesday: Ice and Wind\010\010 On Windsday: Wind and Earth\010\010 On Earthsday: Earth and Thunder\010\010 On Lightningday: Thunder and Water\010\010 On Watersday: Water and Fire\010\010 On Lightsday: Light and Dark\010\010 On Darksday: Dark and Light\010Side note: Most people assume this must be done with two people. Unfortunately, you may encounter bad luck and have party members disconnect, disband or possibly get KO'd without (Re)Raise. To do this solo, target the first Oil Lamp you need and hit enter, then run to the second, target and hit enter. If done fast enough the secret door will open.",["zone"]="Phomiuna Aqueducts",["grid"]="F-8 / Map 3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After completing the puzzle, go though the hidden door at the western wall. It can be opened from the other side by someone that has already passed through.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the second Ornate Door and receive the final cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back to Tavnazian Safehold and talk to Justinius at Tavnazian Safehold (J-6) / Map 2 on the upper floor.\010\010Note: Fomors do not become true sound when your Fomor hate is at it's maximum. Though, they do not aggro at all when your Fomor hate is at it's minimum. To lower your Fomor hate, kill beastmen in Lufaise Meadows or Misaraux Coast. You must kill two beastmen for every one Fomor you killed to lower hate.\010\010Note: This missions is known soloable by THF, though with much difficulty and large gil loss.\010\010Note: It is highly recommended that players do not lock onto the Minotaur and taurus type mobs while fighting, and also switch damage to on screen only. This helps to quickly spot and avoid Mortal Ray by turning around.\010\010Note This mission is soloable by beastmaster - Godsgift soloed 9/20/2025\010\010It is recommended that you use sub WHM for the fight but it is not entirely necessary. Look for a high level oil spill to charm and use your 2hr. when fighting Minotaur put your slime on it and pull it to the corner of the room. let the slime solo it while you stand in the opposite corner. You will need to keep an eye out for mortal ray and use heel to move your slime out of the way. Be prepared to use reward x2. Also bringing antidotes if you are not /WHM would be a wise decision.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="J-6 / Map 2",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7434",["title"]="Distant Loyalties",["page_title"]="Distant Loyalties",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Distant_Loyalties",["revision"]="60835",["requirements"]="Start: Femitte \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (I-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Mythril Ingot",["rewards"]="White Cape",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A goldsmith is needed to fill an order. Only Elvaan need apply.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Femitte needs a goldsmith to make a special earring for her, and not just any goldsmith will do. She gives you a Key item: Goldsmithing Order and specifically requests that you find an Elvaan goldsmith to complete this work. If you have already done \034The Elvaan Goldsmith\034 you may recall Michea meets the requirements.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Bastok Markets, you will find Michea, an Elvaan living on the top floor above Brunhilde the Armorer at Bastok Markets (F-10). You find out she's Femitte's niece.",["zone"]="Bastok Markets",["grid"]="F-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She asks you to fetch her a Mythril Ingot to complete the order, find her this and trade it to her.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She takes some time to make this item (zone out and back into Bastok Markets). When she is finished, she will give you Key item: Mythril Hearts.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Femitte for a cutscene and your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional Return to Michea for extra dialogue.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3631",["title"]="Divine Might",["page_title"]="Divine Might",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Divine_Might",["revision"]="56263",["requirements"]="Requirements: Zilart Mission 13 complete\010Items: Illuminink and \010Parchment to get\010Ark Pentasphere\010<small>(required also when repeating the quest)</small>\010\010Light Ore to get\010\010Key item: Moonlight Ore \010(required only when repeating)\010Previous: The Gate of the Gods",["rewards"]="Key item: Shard of Apathy\010Key item: Shard of Arrogance\010Key item: Shard of Cowardice\010Key item: Shard of Envy\010Key item: Shard of Rage\010One of the following:\010Abyssal Earring\010Beastly Earring\010Bushinomimi\010Knight's Earring\010Suppanomimi",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Use the Ark Pentasphere at the La'Loff Amphitheater to confront and defeat all five Crystal Warriors simultaneously.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Note: If you complete this quest, ZM 14, will be considered completed as well.\010\010<p style=\034text-align:center; color:red;\034>!!!NOTE:!!! You must flag this quest at the blank target in The Shrine of Ru'Avitau or you WILL NOT receive credit and will have to re-aquire another Ark Pentasphere.\010Note: If you are repeating this quest, meaning you are reflagging the quest, you will need to drop the earring and have Key item: Moonlight Ore .",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Preparation",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter The Shrine of Ru'Avitau from the (H-9) entrance in Ru'Aun Gardens.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head North a short distance to find a Blank Target at (G/H-11).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Blank Target for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]=">>>>Examine the Blank Target a second time for dialogue about how to obtain an Ark Pentasphere.<<<<\010\010Divine Might now appears in your Outlands Quests log.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You, or someone in your group, will need to obtain an Ark Pentasphere.\010\010Ark Pentaspheres are created by trading 1 Illuminink and 1 Parchment to the Qu'Hau Spring at (H-6) in Ro'Maeve during a full moon and between 0:00 and 03:00 game time (clear weather)\010\010Illuminink drops off Cursed Puppet and Magic Flagon in Ro'Maeve.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Ark Pentasphere to any of the Shimmering Circles in La'Loff Amphitheater to access the battlefield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Battle",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This battle has a 30 minute time limit and allows for a full alliance of 18 people will be allowed to enter.\010\010This battle is uncapped at level 75 and is relatively challenging.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will need to defeat Ark Angel MR, Ark Angel TT, Ark Angel EV, Ark Angel HM, and Ark Angel GK in order to win.\010\010Everyone should bring some form of re-raise in order to minimize down time.\010\010The Ark Angels share alliance hate, so people should wait to re-raise until the entire alliance is down and the mobs are back at their starting position.\010\010If you feel like you're about to die, try to move out of the center of the arena. People left in the center of the arena are often near impossible to raise again without getting aggro.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you happen to have an alliance wipe, re-raise, heal, and then finish off whoever remains.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The general strategy at level 75 was to divide and conquer. Have one tank/kiter on each mob, while the rest of the group kills the others one by one.\010\010Make sure someone is keeping the pets slept at all times. They can cause chaos if left alone for too long.\010\010The Ark Angel TT should be defeated as fast as possible because he has access to wide selection of nasty spells.\010\010Along with having a pet, the Ark Angel MR will also charm at least one player before she falls.\010\010Fealty, light elemental resistance equipment, and magic evasion in general are effective at resisting this.\010\010Every time the Ark Angel GK uses Meikyo Shisui, it will try to make a Light Skill Chain. This can be prevented if utsusemi absorbs any of the weaponskills.\010\010When fighting the Ark Angel HM it is recommended to have as many people out of Mijin Gakure range as possible.\010\010Barfira does not reduce Mijin Gakure damage. \010\010The Ark Angel EV Spirits Within is very strong and can take out someone in just one hit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have finished the battle, return to the Blank Target in The Shrine of Ru'Avitau to choose your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Re-Questing\010\010Note: You are only allowed to re-quest this once per Conquest Tally.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Drop your current earring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Receive the quest at the unmarked target (G/H-11) in the main entrance of The Shrine of Ru'Avitau.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The quest appears as a second Divine Might quest in your quest log with a different description.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Light Ore.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you need a new Ark Pentasphere, obtain an Illuminink and Parchment as well.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Light Ore to the Qu'Hau Spring in Ro'Maeve during a Full Moon between 00:00 and 3:00 to receive the Key item: Moonlight Ore.\010\010 Warning: if you need both the Key item: Moonlight Ore and the Ark Pentasphere, you must make TWO separate trades. \010\010 If all three items are traded, only the Key item: Moonlight Ore will be obtained.\010\010 Each individual restarting this quest must possess their own Key item: Moonlight Ore.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Illuminink and Parchment to the Qu'Hau Spring in Ro'Maeve during a Full Moon between 0:00 and 3:00 to obtain an Ark Pentasphere.\010\010 Only one alliance member needs the Ark Pentasphere to initiate the battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter and complete the Divine Might battlefield at La'Loff Amphitheater.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the unmarked target in The Shrine of Ru'Avitau to pick up a new earring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Rise of the Zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_22292",["title"]="Divine Might (Divine Might (Repeat))",["page_title"]="Divine Might (Repeat)",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Divine_Might_%28Repeat%29",["revision"]="108351",["requirements"]="Start: Yve'noile \226\128\148 Shrine of Ru'Avitau (-)\010Requirements: Discard earring from Divine Might\010Items: Everyone repeating the fight:\010Light Ore\010Key item: Moonlight Ore\010At least one member:\010Illuminink\010Parchment\010Ark Pentasphere\010Previous: Divine Might",["rewards"]="Choice of one of the following:\010\010Abyssal Earring\010Beastly Earring\010Bushinomimi\010Knight's Earring\010Suppanomimi",["repeatable"]="conquest",["summary"]="The dissipated essence of the Crystal Warriors has once again coalesced into physical form. Your battle is not yet over!",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Drop your current earring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Receive the quest at the unmarked target (G/H-11) in the main entrance of The Shrine of Ru'Avitau.\010\010The quest appears as a second Divine Might quest in your quest log with a different description.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Light Ore.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you need a new Ark Pentasphere, obtain an Illuminink and Parchment as well.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Warning: if you need both the Key item: Moonlight Ore and the Ark Pentasphere, you must make TWO separate trades. If all three items are traded, only the Key item: Moonlight Ore will be obtained.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Light Ore to Ro'Maeve's Qu'Hau Spring during the Full Moon between 0:00 and 3:00 to receive the Key item: Moonlight Ore.\010\010Each individual restarting this quest must possess their own Key item: Moonlight Ore.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Illuminink and Parchment to Ro'Maeve's Qu'Hau Spring during the Full Moon between 0:00 and 3:00 to obtain an Ark Pentasphere.\010\010Only one alliance member needs the Ark Pentasphere to initiate the battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter and complete the Divine Might battlefield at La'Loff Amphitheater.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the unmarked target in The Shrine of Ru'Avitau to pick up a new earring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Rewards\010\010You can choose one of the following five earrings (Level 72, All Jobs):\010! width=\034150\034 | Name\010! | Stats\010|- valign=\034top\034\010| Abyssal Earring\010| [Template Stat: INT / +2] [Template Stat: Scythe Skill / +5]\010[Template Stat: Great Sword Skill / +5]\010[Template Stat: Dark Magic Skill / +5]\010|- valign=\034top\034\010| Beastly Earring\010| [Template stat: chr / +2] [Template stat: Polearm Skill / +5]\010[Template stat: Axe Skill / +5]\010[Template stat: Pet] [Template stat: Accuracy / +10]\010|- valign=\034top\034\010| Bushinomimi\010| [Template stat: str / +2] [Template stat: Great Katana Skill / +5]\010[Template stat: Great Axe Skill / +5]\010[Template stat: Parrying Skill / +5]\010|- valign=\034top\034\010| Knight's Earring\010| [Template stat: vit / +2] [Template stat: Shield Skill / +5]\010[Template stat: Sword Skill / +5]\010[Template stat: Club Skill / +5]\010|- valign=\034top\034\010| Suppanomimi\010| [Template stat: dex / +2]\010[Template stat: Evasion Skill / +5]\010[Template stat: Dagger Skill / +5]\010[Template stat: Katana Skill / +5]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_359",["title"]="Doll of the Dead (Windurst Mission 9-1)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 9-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_9-1",["revision"]="119919",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Items: Goobbue Humus\010Previous: Windurst Mission 8-2|The Jester Who'd be King",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The Orastery Minister has awoken and the Bearer of Darkness once again terrorizes Heavens Tower. At the request of the Manustery you are to speak with a person imprisoned within the Boyahda Tree and discover the truth behind the doll of the dead.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 37 crystals to any Conquest Overseer to unlock the mission then accept it from any Windurst Gate Guard.\010\01036 Water used and 1 Fire",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Windurst",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Apururu at Windurst Woods (H-9) in the Manustery for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Heavens Tower to trigger a cutscene.\010\010After the cutscene, you will exit in front of the Vestal Chamber.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click the Vestal Chamber on the top floor of the tower for a cutscene with the Star Sibyl.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Apururu at Windurst Woods (H-9) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Boyahda Tree",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Farm Goobbue Humus, a rare/ex drop from the Old Goobbues found in The Boyahda Tree or Goobbue Gardener in The Sanctuary of Zi'Tah.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Goobbue Humus to the single Mandragora Warden in The Boyahda Tree at The Boyahda Tree (F-4) on the west side in the hidden area for a cutscene. You will receive a Key item: Letter from Zonpa-Zippa.\010\010The pair of Mandragora Warden are the wrong ones.",["zone"]="The Boyahda Tree",["grid"]="F-4",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Apururu at Windurst Woods (H-9) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Full Moon Fountain",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head into Toraimarai Canal. To get there, you can either:\010\010go through the Three Mage Gate at Inner Horutoto Ruins (H-9) / Rose Tower 1, which requires you either to have the Key item: Portal Charm or to be in a party with a Black Mage, a Red Mage and a White Mage\010\010or go through the Priming Gate in Windurst Walls (G-3), which requires you to possess the Key item: Rhinostery Certificate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Full Moon Fountain located at Toraimarai Canal (G-7) / Map 1 for a cutscene that completes the mission.",["zone"]="Toraimarai Canal",["grid"]="G-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6428",["title"]="Don't Forget the Antidote",["page_title"]="Don't Forget the Antidote",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Don%27t_Forget_the_Antidote",["revision"]="11026",["requirements"]="Start: Edigey - Rabao (F-9)\010Requirements: Selbina/Rabao Reputation 4\010Items: Desert Venom",["rewards"]="Dotanuki\0101800 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Edigey Rabao (F-9). He needs Desert Venom so he can make an antidote for desert caravans.\010\010Desert Venom drops from Doom Scorpion in Eastern Altepa Desert and Tulwar Scorpion in Western Altepa Desert or can be bought at Auction House Category: Others > Misc",["zone"]="Rabao",["grid"]="F-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Desert Venom to Edigey for your reward.\010\010The first time you trade it to him, you will receive the Dotanuki.\010\010Each subsequent time you repeat the quest, you will receive 1800 gil.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Edigey (Rabao)\010 / summary=Edigey wants you to bring him some sand scorpion poison so he can make an antidote, an essential item for the desert caravans.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4804",["title"]="Donate to Recycling",["page_title"]="Donate to Recycling",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Donate_to_Recycling",["revision"]="8491",["requirements"]="Start: Romeo - Selbina (H-9)\010Requirements: Selbina/Rabao Reputation 1\010Items: Onion Dagger x5 or\010Onion Knife x5 or\010Onion Rod x5 or\010Onion Staff x5 or\010Onion Sword x5",["rewards"]="Wastebasket",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade five pieces of onion equipment (of the same type) to Romeo to complete the quest.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Romeo (Atop Fishermen's Guild Salesroom, Selbina)\010 / summary=Donate five pieces of onion equipment to help new recruits everywhere. Donors may receive a reward.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7521",["title"]="Drachenfall",["page_title"]="Drachenfall",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Drachenfall",["revision"]="122132",["requirements"]="Start: Black Mud \226\128\148 Bastok Mines (J-7)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Drachenfall Water",["rewards"]="2000g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Black Mud has asked you to fetch him some Drachenfall water from North Gustaberg.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Black Mud, who gives you a Brass Canteen to fill with water from the Drachenfall. \010\010If you drop the Brass Canteen, you can talk to him again to get another one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the canteen to Dangruf Wadi and head north. You will pass through two geysers that shoot you up to a higher ledge. The first geyser is at Dangruf Wadi (I-8), and the next is at Dangruf Wadi (J-3), the far northeast area of the zone. After going up that geyser you will follow an unmarked path leading northeast into a hidden section of North Gustaberg.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in North Gustaberg, head east along the river, cross the bridge, then go further east to the waterfall.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Brass Canteen to the Waterfall Base, not the ???, to receive the Drachenfall Water. \010\010Alternatively, the Drachenfall Water can be bought from the Auction House.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Bastok and trade the Drachenfall Water to Black Mud to complete the quest and receive your gil reward.\010\010Note The North Gustaberg location for the quest An Explorer's Footsteps is in the cave nearby, and it is easy to complete them both at the same time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_11059",["title"]="Ducal Hospitality",["page_title"]="Ducal Hospitality",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Ducal_Hospitality",["revision"]="73732",["requirements"]="Start: Taillegeas \226\128\148 Ru'Lude Gardens (I-7)\010Requirements: A Vessel Without a Captain\010Fame: Jeuno\010Items: See below",["rewards"]="4000 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Taillegeas has asked you to collect several items desired by guests of the duchy.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Taillegeas, located in the Dining Hall Ru'Lude Gardens (I-7), will tell you that Nag'molada (or Esha'ntarl, if you've completed most of the Chains of Promathia missions) has a guest who requested strange items and will ask for 3-5 items.",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the items to Taillegeas to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Possible Requests\010\010|+ Items List\010|-\010! width=\034100%\034 colspan=\0343\034 | Items\010|-\010|Chocobo Bedding\010|Dart\010|Counterfeit Gil\010|-\010|Fernan's Diaries\010|Goblin Bread\010|Eastern Paper\010|-\010|Goblin Doll\010|Goblin Pie\010|Goblin Mushpot\010|-\010|Kongou Inaho\010|My First Magic Kit\010|Kaiserin Cosmetics\010|-\010|Naphille Pochette\010|Silver Obi\010|Nyumomo Doll\010|- \010|Shuriken\010|Sphene Earring\010|Tonosama Rice Ball\010|-\010|Snoll Gelato\010|Turquoise Ring\010|",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4444",["title"]="Dyer's Woad Quest",["page_title"]="Dyer's Woad Quest",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Dyer%27s_Woad_Quest",["revision"]="108048",["requirements"]="Start: Sorutoto \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (G-12)\010Items: 2x Dyer's Woad",["rewards"]="800 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="[Wiki: needs verification]",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade the Dyer's Woad to Sorutoto in Windurst Woods (G-12).",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="G-12",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="These can be obtained by Harvesting in West Sarutabaruta and Giddeus.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="HorizonXI",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2547",["title"]="Early Bird Catches the Bookworm",["page_title"]="Early Bird Catches the Bookworm",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Early_Bird_Catches_the_Bookworm",["revision"]="105190",["requirements"]="Start: Tosuka-Porika \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (G-8) / North\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Silver Beastcoin\010Previous: Glyph Hanger",["rewards"]="1,500 Gil",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="The Library of Magic wants you to help retrieve its overdue library books. In this case, a Hume by the name of Orn has checked out the book \034Art for Everyone,\034 but has failed to return it by the due date.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must zone after completing the previous quest before you can start this quest. Quest cannot be started if you are currently on Lost for Words or The Sixth Ministry.\010[Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 If currently on Adventure Fellow quest Past Reflections, this cut-scene may trigger first when speaking with Tosuka-Porika. After the cut-scene, speak with him again to flag the quest.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Tosuka-Porika.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you accept the quest, talk to Furakku-Norakku, behind the counter in the same room, who gives you an Key item: Overdue Book Notification.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Orn can be found in Hostelry Room #2 above the Timbre Timbers Tavern at Windurst Waters (F-10) / North. After talking with him, you can ask Furakku-Norakku for an extension, but it isn't necessary.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="F-10 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To save time, you may wish to purchase or obtain a Silver Beastcoin before proceeding. You may also wish to flag the quest A Crisis in the Making before heading out, as this quest also requires you to go to the Treasure Room in Giddeus.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Giddeus and go down into the cave area through \034Drop E\034 or \034Drop F\034 (Giddeus (G-8, I-8) / Ground Level) to arrive on the underground level at (Giddeus (G-8, I-8) / Underground Level). The Yagudo Mendicant and Yagudo Persecutor can drop Silver Beastcoins if you didn't purchase one earlier.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Giddeus (F-7) / Underground Level, where the storage room is (Wistaria Doors), and just walk in, even though Uu Zhoumo tells you to go away. Quu Bokye will be walking around, talk to him, then trade him a Silver Beastcoin, and he'll give you the book, Key item: \034Art For Everyone\034.\010\010If you have the DRK AF quest Dark Legacy active and are ready for the battle with Vaa Huja the Erudite, Quu Bokye will not ask for a Silver Beastcoin but will mention a Yagudo Cherry instead. You must defeat Vaa Huja the Erudite before Quu Bokye will initiate the Silver Beastcoin dialogue.\010\010If you have the quest The Lost Book active, he'll ask for a Mythril Beastcoin instead. You may still trade him the Silver Beastcoin for this quest.",["zone"]="Giddeus",["grid"]="F-7 / Underground Level",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Talk to Orn again for extra quest dialogue.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Windurst Waters and talk to Furakku-Norakku to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_56997",["title"]="Easterly Winds",["page_title"]="Easterly Winds",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Easterly_Winds",["revision"]="122480",["requirements"]="Start: Halver \226\128\148 Chateau d'Oraguille (I-9)\010Previous: Confessions of Royalty",["rewards"]="10 Imperial Bronze Pieces",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="An international summit is to be held in Jeuno. You have been called upon to speak of what you have witnessed in the Empire of Aht Urhgan.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After completing Confessions of Royalty, wait until the next Japanese midnight (JST).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Approach the Audience Chamber in the Grand Duke Palace at Ru'Lude Gardens Ru'Lude Gardens (H-6) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="H-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Choose the reward dialogue options if you want to receive 10 Imperial Bronze Pieces.\010\010 Choose \034Yes\034 for the first question.\010\010 Choose \034That's what I'm here for!\034 for the final reward-related question.\010\010 - These are the default selections",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete the cutscene to finish the mission and continue to Westerly Winds.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7408",["title"]="Eco-Warrior (Bastok)",["page_title"]="Eco-Warrior (Bastok)",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Eco-Warrior_%28Bastok%29",["revision"]="119753",["requirements"]="Start: Raifa \226\128\148 Port Bastok (D-6)\010Requirements: Level Cap: 20\010Eco-Warrior (San d'Oria) or Eco-Warrior (Windurst) not currently active\010 [Horizon change] You have not already completed an Eco-Warrior quest in the current Conquest period\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Key item: Indigested Ore",["rewards"]="Tale Of The Wandering Heroes\010Dragon Chronicles\01010,000 gil [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="eco-warrior",["summary"]="Raifa wants you to exterminate an ecological threat, and bring her evidence of the feat.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You can check which Eco-Warrior quest you are able to take for the current week with Eeko-Weeko, located at Ru'Lude Gardens (I-9).",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="I-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Before attempting this quest, designate a leader so that the group functions as a team. This is essential for the success of this quest. Make sure you have a near-full alliance unless you are using two or more Summoners with Ifrit's Astral Flow ability, Inferno.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Raifa in the Steaming Sheep Restaurant in Port Bastok at (Port Bastok (D-6)).\010\010 If you cannot take the quest, Raifa will say either:\010\010 Something about the food. (Either you don't have enough fame, you already completed an Eco-Warrior quest this Conquest period, or need to complete Eco-Warrior (Windurst) and/or Eco-Warrior (San d'Oria) before repeating Bastok.)\010\010 \034...Can I have a moment of your time? Oh, but you look busy...\034 (You are currently involved in another Eco-Warrior quest.)",["zone"]="Port Bastok",["grid"]="D-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Gusgen Mines.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Degga at (Gusgen Mines (H-9) / Map 1). You will see him on your right, toward the end of the entry corridor. He will apply an ointment that restricts your level to 20. Buffs are removed with this level restriction.\010\010 You must have the level restriction on in order to get the Key Item, once you have your Key Item you can log out to wipe it without issues to progess.\010\010 Note that, once the level restriction is applied, only others with the same level restriction are able to heal or buff you.\010\010 Make sure everyone gets the ointment. If any alliance member lacks the level restriction, the enemies will not spawn.\010\010 You lose the level restriction if you are defeated. It may be reapplied at any time by speaking to Degga again once raised.\010\010 Note: if you Reraise, you keep the level restriction.\010\010 If you return to your Home Point after being defeated or otherwise leave the area in any way, you lose any progress made in the quest since talking to Degga.",["zone"]="Gusgen Mines",["grid"]="H-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At the very first 4-way intersection (Gusgen Mines (H-9) / Map 1), go down the east corridor (turn right).",["zone"]="Gusgen Mines",["grid"]="H-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Turn left at (Gusgen Mines (I-9) / Map 1).",["zone"]="Gusgen Mines",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Turn right at (Gusgen Mines (I-8) / Map 1).",["zone"]="Gusgen Mines",["grid"]="I-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow the path north to (Gusgen Mines (I-6) / Map 1).",["zone"]="Gusgen Mines",["grid"]="I-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Camp on the eastern side of (Gusgen Mines (H-6) / Map 1).",["zone"]="Gusgen Mines",["grid"]="H-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The ??? is on a chest in the middle of the deck at (Gusgen Mines (H-6) / Map 1). Have someone with Sneak pop the NMs, or clear the area around the chest if needed.",["zone"]="Gusgen Mines",["grid"]="H-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When ready, click the ??? to spawn two Pudding NMs.\010\010 You must have the level restriction applied to spawn and engage this NM.\010\010 [Horizon change] Any player without the level restriction who attempts to assist a player with the level restriction will be instantly defeated.\010\010 The NMs spawn with aggro toward the party member who spawns them. If Sneak is applied, the spawner is still aggroed. Clicking the ??? removes any Sneak effect.\010\010 The Puddings are Slime-type NMs. As such, they are weak against magic, but highly resistant to physical attack. As they gain TP, they use a strong version of Fluid Spread, the Slime AOE attack, that causes critical damage to anyone in range. This is a common cause of wipes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the NMs are defeated, touch the ??? again to receive an Key item: Indigested Ore.\010\010 If you leave the zone before checking the ???, you may return to it and check it to receive the key item before the next Conquest tally. Note you must reapply the level restriction, but you do not need to kill the NM again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Degga, who will tell you to return to Port Bastok. You will have to speak with Degga to be able to finish the quest with Raifa.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Raifa in Port Bastok (Port Bastok (D-6)) to receive your reward.",["zone"]="Port Bastok",["grid"]="D-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="[Horizon change] As of the June 15th 2024 update, adventurers must now clear all three Eco-Warrior quests before they can repeat an Eco-Warrior quest in a particular nation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can only have one Eco-Warrior quest active at any time. This includes Eco-Warrior (Windurst), Eco-Warrior (San d'Oria) and Eco-Warrior (Bastok).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Eco-Warrior quests cannot be cancelled.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Only one Eco-Warrior quest can be completed per Conquest period.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Strategies",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="For strategies, see Talk:Eco-Warrior (Bastok).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6852",["title"]="Eco-Warrior (San d'Oria)",["page_title"]="Eco-Warrior (San d'Oria)",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Eco-Warrior_%28San_d%27Oria%29",["revision"]="119420",["requirements"]="Start: Norejaie \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (K-6)\010Requirements: Level Cap: 20\010Eco-Warrior (Bastok) or Eco-Warrior (Windurst) not currently active\010 [Horizon change] You have not already completed an Eco-Warrior quest in the current Conquest period\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Key item: Indigested Stalagmite",["rewards"]="Tale Of The Wandering Heroes\010Dragon Chronicles\01010,000 gil [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="eco-warrior",["summary"]="Norejaie wants you to exterminate an ecological threat, and bring her evidence of the feat.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You can check which Eco-Warrior quest you are able to take for the current week with Eeko-Weeko, located at Ru'Lude Gardens (I-9).",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="I-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Before attempting this quest, designate a leader so that the group functions as a team. This is essential for the success of this quest. Make sure you have a near-full alliance unless you are using two or more Summoners with Ifrit's Astral Flow ability, Inferno.\010\010 As of 1/30/26 Rebase, Ifrit 2HR does extremely low damage. SMN spam still works, but use physical BP: Rage, and create skillchains if able. You may need to edit your clear strategies or bring more people. Please add testimonials to the Discussion page. (Also, feel free to delete this bullet point if no longer true.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Norejaie in the Lion Springs Tavern in Southern San d'Oria (K-6).\010\010 If you cannot take the quest, Norejaie will say either:\010\010 Something about the food. (Either you don't have enough fame, you already completed an Eco-Warrior quest this Conquest period, or need to complete Eco-Warrior (Windurst) and/or Eco-Warrior (Bastok) before repeating San d'Oria.)\010\010 \034...Can I have a moment of your time? Oh, but you look busy...\034 (You are currently involved in another Eco-Warrior quest.)",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="K-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Ordelle's Caves using the entrance at the south end of the ravine in La Theine Plateau at (La Theine Plateau (F-7)). \010\010 You will appear in Ordelle's Caves at (Ordelle's Caves (H-2) / Map 2) on Map 2.",["zone"]="La Theine Plateau",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Rojaireaut at (Ordelle's Caves (G-3) / Map 2). He will apply an ointment that restricts your level to 20. Buffs are removed with this level restriction.\010\010 You must have the level restriction on in order to get the Key Item, once you have your Key Item you can log out to wipe it without issues to progress.\010\010 Note that, once the level restriction is applied, only others with the same level restriction are able to heal or buff you.\010\010 Make sure everyone gets the ointment. If any alliance member lacks the level restriction, the enemy will not spawn.\010\010 You lose the level restriction if you are defeated. It may be reapplied at any time by speaking to Rojaireaut again once raised.\010\010 Note: if you Reraise, you keep the level restriction.\010\010 If you return to your Home Point after being defeated or otherwise leave the area in any way, you lose any progress made in the quest since talking to Rojaireaut.",["zone"]="Ordelle's Caves",["grid"]="G-3 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From Rojaireaut head east, through the puddle and take the long corridor, exiting Map 2 at B (Ordelle's Caves (I-6) / Map 2).",["zone"]="Ordelle's Caves",["grid"]="I-6 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You enter Map 1 at B (Ordelle's Caves (I-6)). Follow the path and head to (Ordelle's Caves (G-8)) where you head through the narrow tunnel to the east.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The ??? is located in the southwest corner of a small room on a stalagmite (top right corner of (Ordelle's Caves (G-9))). The designated tank/puller should spawn the Necroplasm NM by touching the ???.",["zone"]="Ordelle's Caves",["grid"]="G-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat the Necroplasm.\010\010 You must have the level restriction applied to spawn and engage this NM.\010\010 [Horizon change] Any player without the level restriction who attempts to assist a player with the level restriction will be instantly defeated\010\010 The NM spawn with aggro toward the party member who spawns them. If Sneak is applied, the spawner is still aggroed. Clicking the ??? removes any Sneak effect.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the NM is defeated, touch the ??? again to receive an Key item: Indigested Stalagmite.\010\010 If you leave the zone before checking the ???, you may return to it and check it to receive the key item before the next Conquest tally. Note you must reapply the level restriction, but you do not need to kill the NM again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Rojaireaut, who will tell you to return to Southern San d'Oria. Note that you must have the level restriction on in order to speak with Rojaireaut, who will remove it for you in the process. You may also remove the restriction by logging out or warping.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Norejaie in Southern San d'Oria (Southern San d'Oria (K-6)) to receive your reward.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="K-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="[Horizon change] As of the June 15th 2024 update, adventurers must now clear all three Eco-Warrior quests before they can repeat an Eco-Warrior quest in a particular nation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can only have one Eco-Warrior quest active at any time. This includes Eco-Warrior (Windurst), Eco-Warrior (Bastok) and Eco-Warrior (San d'Oria).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Eco-Warrior quests cannot be cancelled.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Only one Eco-Warrior quest can be completed per Conquest period.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Strategies",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="For strategies, see Talk:Eco-Warrior (San d'Oria).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7411",["title"]="Eco-Warrior (Windurst)",["page_title"]="Eco-Warrior (Windurst)",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Eco-Warrior_%28Windurst%29",["revision"]="119422",["requirements"]="Start: Lumomo \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (F-10) / North\010Requirements: Level Cap: 20\010Eco-Warrior (Bastok) or Eco-Warrior (San d'Oria) not currently active\010 [Horizon change] You have not already completed an Eco-Warrior quest in the current Conquest period\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Key item: Indigested Meat",["rewards"]="Tale Of The Wandering Heroes\010Dragon Chronicles\01010,000 gil [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="eco-warrior",["summary"]="Lumomo wants you to exterminate an ecological threat, and bring her evidence of the feat.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You can check which Eco-Warrior quest you are able to take for the current week with Eeko-Weeko, located at Ru'Lude Gardens (I-9).",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="I-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Before attempting this quest, designate a leader so that the group functions as a team. This is essential for the success of this quest. Make sure you have a near-full alliance unless you are using two or more Summoners with Ifrit's Astral Flow ability, Inferno.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Lumomo inside the Timbre Timbers Tavern in Windurst Waters (F-10) / North.\010\010 If you cannot take the quest, Lumomo will say either:\010\010 \034...Nothing beats good old Windurstian cooking! Those foreign foods make me feel so bloaty-woated!\034 (Either you don't have enough fame, you already completed Eco-Warrior this Conquest period, or need to complete Eco-Warrior (San d'Oria) and/or Eco-Warrior (Bastok) before repeating Windurst.)\010\010 \034...Can I have a moment of your time? Oh, but you look busy...\034 (You are currently involved in another Eco-Warrior quest.)",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="F-10 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Maze of Shakhrami and immediately after entering the maze, you will see Ahko Mhalijikhari. Talk to her and she will apply an ointment that restricts your level to 20. 'Buffs are removed with this level restriction.\010\010 You must have the level restriction on in order to get the Key Item, once you have your Key Item you can log out to wipe it without issues to progess.\010\010 Note that, once the level restriction is applied, only others with the same level restriction are able to heal or buff you.\010\010 Make sure everyone gets the ointment. If any alliance member lacks the level restriction, the enemies will not spawn.\010\010 You lose the level restriction if you are defeated. It may be reapplied at any time by speaking to Ahko again once raised.\010\010 Note: if you Reraise, you keep the level restriction.\010\010 If you return to your Home Point after being defeated or otherwise leave the area in any way, you lose any progress made in the quest since talking to Ahko.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Hug the left wall and continue NE to (Maze of Shakhrami (E-7)), where the corridor opens up into a huge room. Continue east to the tunnel at (Maze of Shakhrami (H-7)), taking exit C, which will lead south to a new map.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On the new map, you will reach an open area at (Maze of Shakhrami (H-8) / Map 2), entering at C.",["zone"]="Maze of Shakhrami",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the path at (Maze of Shakhrami (I-9) / Map 2) that leads south from the open area and at (Maze of Shakhrami (I-10) / Map 2), you'll see the ??? which spawns the NM on a rock.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Clear the room.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Have the tank/puller click the ??? to spawn 3 Wyrmfly NMs. \010\010 You must have the level restriction applied to spawn and engage this NM.\010\010 [Horizon change] Any player without the level restriction who attempts to assist a player with the level restriction will be instantly defeated.\010\010 The NMs spawn with aggro toward the party member who spawns them. If Sneak is applied, the spawner is still aggroed. Clicking the ??? removes any Sneak effect.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the NMs are defeated, touch the ??? again to receive an Key item: Indigested Meat.\010\010 If you leave the zone before checking the ???, you may return to it and check it to receive the key item before the next Conquest tally. Note you must reapply the level restriction, but you do not need to kill the NM again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Ahko Mhalijikhari, who will tell you to return to Windurst Waters. Note that you must have the level restriction on in order to speak with Ahko, who will remove it for you in the process. You may also remove the restriction by logging out or warping.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Lumomo in Windurst Waters (Windurst Waters (F-10) / North) for your reward.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="F-10 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="[Horizon change] As of the June 15th 2024 update, adventurers must now clear all three Eco-Warrior quests before they can repeat an Eco-Warrior quest in a particular nation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can only have one Eco-Warrior quest active at any time. This includes Eco-Warrior (San d'Oria), Eco-Warrior (Bastok) and Eco-Warrior (Windurst).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Eco-Warrior quests cannot be cancelled.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Only one Eco-Warrior quest can be completed per Conquest period.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Strategies",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="For strategies, see Talk:Eco-Warrior (Windurst).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4805",["title"]="Elder Memories",["page_title"]="Elder Memories",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Elder_Memories",["revision"]="122299",["requirements"]="Start: Isacio - Selbina Selbina (G-10)\010Requirements: Level 18+\010Items: Damselfly Worm\010Magicked Skull\010Crab Apron",["rewards"]="Ability to use Support Job\0105 Mog Wardrobe [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You must prove yourself worthy before you can learn Isacio's fighting techniques.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Isacio (G-10) Selbina to activate quest Elder Memories or talk to Vera (G-10) Mhaura to activate quest The Old Lady.\010\010Once one quest is active the other can never be activated.\010\010Both quests have varied objectives but will result in the same reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you talked to Isacio, obtain Damselfly Worm, Magicked Skull, and Crab Apron.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade in the items to the respective NPCs to unlock Support Job access for player.\010\010You will not be able to change your Support Job until after changing zones.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_53600",["title"]="Elderly Pursuits",["page_title"]="Elderly Pursuits",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Elderly_Pursuits",["revision"]="119611",["requirements"]="Start: Despachiaire \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold (K-10) / Map 2\010Items: Key item: Antique Amulet\010Key item: Cathedral Medallion\010Previous: Secrets of Ovens Lost",["rewards"]="Elegant Ribbon",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Despachiaire has asked you to investigate the origin of his late wife's amulet.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Despachiaire, who is upstairs behind the Walnut Door at Tavnazian Safehold (K-10) \226\128\148 Map 2, for a cutscene that starts the quest and to receive an Key item: Antique Amulet.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="K-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Southern San d'Oria and talk to Rouva.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Jugner Forest and exit at Jugner Forest (E-6) into Carpenters' Landing.",["zone"]="Jugner Forest",["grid"]="E-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Find the ??? at Carpenters' Landing (F-9) on a glowing mushroom spore and select to spawn the Funguar NM Para.\010\010The ??? is roughly in the center of the square.",["zone"]="Carpenters' Landing",["grid"]="F-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Para.\010\010When Para is at 10-50% of it's health, it will replicate itself when it uses a TP move if not defeated quickly. It is helpful to save MP or TP to do large damage once it reaches low HP.\010\010The first incarnation and all of its replications can easily be disposed of by most 70+ jobs. It has about 1000 HP.\010\010Although no more than three to four copies seem to be up at a given time (there may be a limit), there is no known limit to the total number of times it can replicate itself. A reasonable source of spike damage is necessary for this fight.\010\010The replications are exact copies with the same amount of Max HP and strength.\010\010The NM seems to be around the same strength as Funguars in the area but with substantially more HP.\010\010Para cannot be slept using Lullaby.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once Para is defeated, select the ??? to obtain a Key item: Cathedral Medallion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Southern San d'Oria and talk with Rouva.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Tavnazian Safehold and talk with Despachiaire to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6241",["title"]="Empty Memories",["page_title"]="Empty Memories",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Empty_Memories",["revision"]="59131",["requirements"]="Start: Harith \226\128\148 Ru'Lude Gardens (H-5)\010Requirements: Access to: \010\010Promyvion - Mea\010\010Promyvion - Holla\010\010Promyvion - Dem\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Recollection of Fear or\010Recollection of Pain or\010Recollection of Guilt or\010Recollection of Suffering or\010Recollection of Animosity or\010Recollection of Anxiety",["rewards"]="Psychoanima or\010Hysteroanima or\010Terroanima or\010Hamayumi or\010Dia Wand or\010Stone Gorget",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="To obtain this quest, first go to any Promyvion location, enter, and return to Harith in the Grand Duke's Palace without erasing your memory at the large apparatus. He will then give you this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Harith one Recollection + 2,000 gil. Harith will immediately synth the appropriate bottle of anima for you:\010\010Recollection of Pain --> Hysteroanima (Amnesia)\010\010Recollection of Guilt --> Terroanima (Run in Terror)\010\010Recollection of Fear --> Psychoanima (Intimidation)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Harith one of the Recollections from the Notorious Monsters in Promyvion - Vahzl to receive the weapon/armor listed below. Unlike with the anima, you do not need to trade any gil to receive the item.\010\010Recollection of Animosity --> Dia Wand \010\010Recollection of Suffering --> Hamayumi \010\010Recollection of Anxiety --> Stone Gorget \010Note If you give Harith the Recollection and gil to synth an item that you already possess, Harith will still carry out his task. However, he will not hand over the item because they are all Rare. Harith will not accept any other Recollections until you dispose of your current Rare item and take the one he's holding. \010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Harith (Grande Duke Palace, Ru'Lude Gardens)\010 / summary=The mysterious \034society\034 that Harith works for is supposedly performing research on a strange life form known as the Empty.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_338",["title"]="Enter the Talekeeper (Bastok Mission 8-2)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 8-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_8-2",["revision"]="105861",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 8-1|The Chains that Bind Us",["rewards"]="Rank 9\01080,000 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You are to investigate the Kuftal Tunnel which connects Zepwell Island with Cape Teriggan. Zeruhn Mines guard Drake Fang will provide you with further details.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 12~30 crystals to unlock the next mission, then speak with a Gate Guard to accept it. [Wiki: needs verification] (14 Water Crystals was enough for me.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Visit Drake Fang in Zeruhn Mines (H-6).",["zone"]="Zeruhn Mines",["grid"]="H-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head for Kuftal Tunnel. Just inside from the Western Altepa entrance, there is a ??? at (Kuftal Tunnel (H-8) / Map 1). This ??? is up top.\010\010Everyone must check this ???. You'll receive a message about a piece of wood falling to the level below. \010\010If anyone does not check this, they can check it after the NM fight downstairs, and then return to the NM ??? and still receive the key item.",["zone"]="Kuftal Tunnel",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head down around, in to the Cancer pop room. The ??? is directly under the first one. Sneak up, and check the ???. Three NM ghosts will spawn, Dervo's Ghost, Gizerl's Ghost, and Gordov's Ghost.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You only need to defeat Gordov's Ghost, so you can Sneak pop, pull him and wait for the other two to depop. Defeat the remaining NM, and then check the ??? again for the Old Piece of Wood.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In order to use despawn trick you MUST wait til other mobs despawn BEFORE you kill the pulled mob, otherwise it will not work.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Drake Fang for a final cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional: Talk to Gumbah (Bastok Mines (J-7)) and Detzo (Bastok Mines (I-6)) in Bastok Mines, and Iron Eater (Metalworks (J-8)) in Metalworks for mini-cutscenes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1138",["title"]="Enveloped in Darkness",["page_title"]="Enveloped in Darkness",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Enveloped_in_Darkness",["revision"]="122672",["requirements"]="Start: Curilla \226\128\148 Chateau d'Oraguille (I-9)\010Requirements: Red Mage Level 50+\010San d'Oria Rank 2\010or Bastok/Windurst Mission 2-3\010Items: Key item: Old Pocket Watch\010Velvet Cloth\010Key item: Old Boots\010Nest Chest Key\010Key item: Crawler Blood\010Previous: The Crimson Trial",["rewards"]="Warlock's Boots [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="Investigate reports of a ghost in the cathedral.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Note: Bring a Velvet Cloth with you to save some time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Curilla at (Chateau d'Oraguille (I-9)) in Chateau d'Oraguille until she gives you an Key item: Old Pocket Watch.\010\010You may need to talk to her numerous times.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="I-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Note: The rest of the quest can be done on any job, including opening the chest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Pagisalis in the basement of the Cathedral in Northern San d'Oria.\010\010 To find the basement, take an immediate left once entering the Cathedral and then a right before the double doors.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Pagisalis the Velvet Cloth to activate a cutscene and receive Key item: Old Boots.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Curilla where she asks you to retrieve the Key item: Crawler Blood and bury it and the Key item: Old Boots in the nest. (OPTIONAL)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Crawlers' Nest and obtain a Nest Chest Key. Then, find a treasure chest and open it with the key to receive the Key item: Crawler Blood.\010\010You can open this chest as a thief with Thief's Tools, Skeleton Key or Living Key to obtain the Key item: Crawler Blood.\010\010CAUTION: Upon opening the chest, Sneak will be lost. Be wary of agro.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to (I-10) on map 2 and click the ??? to bury the boots.\010\010This is the map with the back door to Rolanberry Fields.\010\010The location is marked on the maps above.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait till JP midnight, then click the ??? once more to obtain a pair of Warlock's Boots [Horizon change] .",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Red Mage (RDM)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Red Mage (RDM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Warlock's Boots",["revision"]="107741"},{["job"]="Red Mage (RDM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Enveloped in Darkness",["revision"]="122672"}}},{["id"]="wiki_57612",["title"]="Equipped for All Occasions",["page_title"]="Equipped for All Occasions",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Equipped_for_All_Occasions",["revision"]="122790",["requirements"]="Start: ??? \226\128\148 Arrapago Reef (H-10)\010Requirements: Corsair as Main Job 40+\010Level: Corsair 40+\010Items: Lamian Fang Key x2\010Previous: Luck of the Draw",["rewards"]="Trump Gun",["repeatable"]="Yes, After AF Memory is erased.",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Ratihb at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-12) at the Shararat Teahouse.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the ??? at Arrapago Reef (H-10) / Map 1 on the first map of Arrapago Reef (the same ??? on the ruined ship used in Luck of the Draw) as Corsair, level 40 or higher (go to the 2nd boat at the very top of (H-10), not the first one outside the cave from the survival guide).",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will need a Lamian Fang Key (or a Thief) to open an Iron Gate inside Arrapago Reef. You may farm this key either in Caedarva Mire or Arrapago Reef, or can obtain one by checking a ??? in Caedarva Mire (I-7), on a small ledge behind a Jnun. A character can obtain a free Lamian Fang Key once per Conquest period.\010\010You do not need a Lamian Fang Key to get to the ???. Using the Ilrusi Atoll Staging Point will get you to Map 2. From there, go to point A to get to Map 1. Then go to the tunnels using point m. That puts you at the same spot as if you used the Lamian Fang Key with the method above. Exit using the lower left Iron Gate to get to the ???. (Note: There are Soulflayers along this route that are True Hearing. There are also Heraldic Imps in the cave right next to the staging point that are True Sight. Going this way is NOT ideal for your level 40 Corsair and you would be wise to have reraise.)",["zone"]="Caedarva Mire",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the ??? for a cutscene during which Aznahf will present you with three choices: Maze of Shakhrami, Gusgen Mines, or Ordelle's Caves. Choose the Maze of Shakhrami (the only correct choice).\010\010Note: Even if you make the wrong choice, you will still be able to pop the Lost Soul (NM) in the Maze of Shakhrami.\010\010Your objective is (K-9) in the Maze of Shakhrami.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to (L-9) and down the tunnel in the Maze of Shakhrami, then go to the western edge of (K-9) on the next map in Maze of Shakhrami (right where Argus spawns) and examine the Iron Door to spawn the Lost Soul (NM). You do not need to have your job set to COR to spawn the NM.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After defeating the Lost Soul (NM), examine the Iron Door again for another cutscene, in which you will be given the Key item: Wheel Lock Trigger.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the ??? in Arrapago Reef for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Shararat Teahouse in Aht Urhgan Whitegate and speak with Ratihb for your reward.\010\010Note: If you had not previously received the final cutscene from Ratihb after finishing Luck of the Draw, you will need to complete that cutscene first, then speak with Ratihb again to obtain the Trump Gun.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urghan",["jobs"]={"Corsair (COR)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Corsair (COR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Trump Gun",["revision"]="123452"},{["job"]="Corsair (COR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Equipped for All Occasions",["revision"]="122790"}}},{["id"]="wiki_57196",["title"]="Eternal Mercenary",["page_title"]="Eternal Mercenary",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Eternal_Mercenary",["revision"]="120939",["requirements"]="Previous: The Empress Crowned",["rewards"]="NoneAbility to purchase Key item: Atma of the Sellsword",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The glory crown has finally been returned to you. However, President Naja's iron grip is not so easily broken. It appears your repayments to Salaheem's Sentinels will continue into the foreseeable future...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete The Empress Crowned; this mission begins immediately afterward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Naja Salaheem in Salaheem's Sentinels at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1 for the final Treasures of Aht Urhgan story cutscene.\010\010 The dialogue choices alter portions of the scene but do not change its rewards or mission state.\010\010 This is the terminal Treasures of Aht Urhgan mission. It remains active in the mission log after viewing the cutscene.\010\010 Speaking with Naja again allows the finale dialogue to be viewed again.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_10188",["title"]="Even More Gullible's Travels",["page_title"]="Even More Gullible's Travels",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Even_More_Gullible%27s_Travels",["revision"]="73737",["requirements"]="Start: Magriffon \226\128\148 Kazham (I-7)\010Fame: Kazham\010Fame level: 7\010Items: 15,000 - 35,000 Gil\010Key item: Treasure Map\010Previous: Gullible's Travels",["rewards"]="Rafflesia Nectar",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Magriffon has spent all of his (your?) money to save a maiden in distress. Now he needs someone to save him (again) from getting kicked out of the bed & breakfast before he has completed his \034top-secret\034 mission.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must zone if you have just completed Gullible's Travels.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Magriffon.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade him the 15,000-35,000 gil that he asks of you.\010\010You will receive the title \034Even More Gullible's Travels\034, and the Key item: Treasure Map.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine all three Blue Rafflesia in Yuhtunga Jungle at Yuhtunga Jungle (F-7), Yuhtunga Jungle (H-10), and Yuhtunga Jungle (I-12). Each one will contain a Rafflesia Nectar.\010\010After clicking on the final plant, you are told that the pollen makes you dizzy.\010\010Rafflesia Nectar has no use and can be sold at the shop.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Magriffon to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Kazham",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_9691",["title"]="Everyone's Grudge (Quest)",["page_title"]="Everyone's Grudge (Quest)",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Everyone%27s_Grudge_%28Quest%29",["revision"]="103118",["requirements"]="Start: Magephaud - Norg (Norg (I-8))\010Requirements: Killed at least one Tonberry\010Norg reputation level 2\010Items: Gold Beastcoin x 3",["rewards"]="Key item: Tonberry Key",["repeatable"]="Only the The Tonberry Priest portion",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Magephaud, who offers to tell you about the dangerous Tonberry attack Everyone's Grudge if you pay him 3 Gold Beastcoins.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade 3 Gold Beastcoins to Magephaud to receive the Key item: Tonberry Key and complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional: The Tonberry Priest\010\010This can be done any number of times once you have the Key item: Tonberry Key.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In the Temple of Uggalepih, open the door at (Temple of Uggalepih (F-11) / Map 1).",["zone"]="Temple of Uggalepih",["grid"]="F-11 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Tonberry Priest inside offers to clear your Tonberry rancor to minimize the damage done by Everyone's Grudge and other Tonberry rancor-based attacks. \010\010The priest asks for a price of 250 to 6100 gil, depending on the intensity of your Tonberry rancor.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Magephaud (Next to the central staircase, Norg)\010 / summary=Bring back three gold beastcoins if you want to learn how to rid yourself of the Tonberries' rancor.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_53404",["title"]="Everyone's Grudging",["page_title"]="Everyone's Grudging",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Everyone%27s_Grudging",["revision"]="121241",["requirements"]="Start: Jakoh Wahcondalo \226\128\148 Kazham (J-9)\010Fame: Kazham\010Fame level: 6\010Items: Unlit Lantern\010Rancor Flame\010Paintbrush of Souls\010Previous: A Question of Taste",["rewards"]="11,000 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have been cursed by the Tonberries' rancor flames, and Kazham's chieftainness has ordered you out of the village.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Note: To obtain this quest, you must have traded an Unlit Lantern to the Altar of Rancor to receive a Rancor Flame at some point. Such as during Zilart Mission 4. If you have received a Rancor Flame at any point prior to the rebase, you will not be able to start the quest. You must trade an unlit lantern and receive a flame in order to be flagged with the 'curse'. This means you have to make an initial trip to the den, do this, then return to Jakoh to start the quest.\010\010Note: To get into the Den of Rancor, at least one person will need a Paintbrush of Souls.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have used a Rancor Flame, talk to Jakoh Wahcondalo in Kazham who will tell you to leave her village. The other NPCs in the room tell you to go the Den of Rancor/Temple of Uggalepih complex to be cleansed and then come back. [Wiki: needs verification] \010\010You get the title \034Excommunicate of Kazham\034 as soon as this quest becomes active.\010If you don't have an Unlit Lantern see below.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have the Unlit Lantern, go back to the main entrance and make all right turns following the walls to exit at (Temple of Uggalepih (F-5) / Map 1). Hug the left wall to re-enter the temple at (Yhoator Jungle (H-11) / Map 1).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in the temple, head to (Temple of Uggalepih (I-10) / Map 2) and defeat the Temple Guardian. After you kill the Temple Guardian, the door will open.",["zone"]="Temple of Uggalepih",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Past the guardian's door, head north to (Temple of Uggalepih (I-7) / Map 2) inside the paintings room. The party member with the Paintbrush of Souls will use it on the empty frame on the east wall to open the door to the Den of Rancor.",["zone"]="Temple of Uggalepih",["grid"]="I-7 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the door is open run in and zone to Den of Rancor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you are in the Den of Rancor, you want to go to the Altar of Rancor at (Den of Rancor (D-5, E-5) / Map 1). You can easily get there by hugging the right wall from where you enter the Den. You or the party should trade any Unlit Lanterns to the Altar of Rancor to receive a Rancor Flame. You need four total, either in one or multiple trips. This room has a bat and two bombs, which sound aggro and sight/magic aggro respectively. You can trade without clearing the room by having sneak and waiting until both bombs are facing away. Use a prism powder to avoid magic aggro afterward. Use an /item macro if necessary.",["zone"]="Den of Rancor",["grid"]="D-5 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have your Rancor Flame(s), you need to visit the other Altar of Rancor at (Den of Rancor (I-13, J-13) / Map 1). This room has two slime enemies which are sound aggro. Trade four Rancor Flames to the Altar of Rancor total. Each trade will print a message noting the number of lit flames. When you trade a flame to the altar, the flame reverts to a normal unlit lantern in your inventory. After the fourth lantern is lit, a bomb NM called Rancor Torch will appear and immediately aggro on the person who traded the last flame. If you do not want to clear the room, you can trade to the altar from behind it in sneak, and pull the NM to the back of the room to fight it.",["zone"]="Den of Rancor",["grid"]="I-13 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill the Rancor Torch and head back to Kazham and talk to the Chieftainess for your reward. There is no special message after defeating the NM.\010\010Rancor Torch has high HP and can cast Berserk. Similar to Dark Spark, it can use Self-Destruct, but rarely. It is possible that it may not be used until it is at low health. [Wiki: needs verification] \010\010Its attacks are relatively weak and its accuracy versus a level 75 melee is very low.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Kazham",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3722",["title"]="Exit the Gambler",["page_title"]="Exit the Gambler",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Exit_the_Gambler",["revision"]="121245",["requirements"]="Start: Aurege \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (F-3) \226\128\148 Outside the carpenter's guild\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1",["rewards"]="Map of King Ranperre's Tomb",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Varchet of the Carpenters' Guild has run off again. Find the slacker and get him back to work.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Aurege, he and Guilberdrier discuss one of their workers who is gambling again and late for work.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Varchet in Southern San d'Oria (L-6), the missing worker. He will agree to go back to work only if you win against him gambling. Bet 5 gil until you win against him (it may take several tries), then he says he will return to work.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="L-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Aurege again to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can still gamble with Varchet after the quest is over. It will be a bet of 5 gil, with the winner getting 10 gil.\010Note You can start this quest if you have started and not completed the quest The Pickpocket. but it may not show up as active in the current quest log. It will show up when completed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4806",["title"]="Expertise",["page_title"]="Expertise",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Expertise",["revision"]="109608",["requirements"]="Start: Take \226\128\148 Mhaura (I-8)\010Requirements: Windurst Reputation \226\137\165 3\010Fame: Mhaura\010Fame level: 3+\010Items: Land Crab Meat\010Scream Fungus\010Previous: His Name is Valgeir",["rewards"]="Tableware Set",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Take wants you to bring back one of Valgeir's dishes from Selbina.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After completing His Name is Valgeir you will need to wait an unknown amount of time before you will be given this quest; 8 game days is likely.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take says she wants to sample a taste of Valgeir's cooking and while she doesn't quite ask you to go to Selbina, you should now see the quest flagged.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once there, talk to Valgeir and he'll ask you to collect a Scream Fungus and a piece of Land Crab Meat.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It will take Valgeir 24 game hours to make the dish after you give him the items.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the Land Crab Bisque back to Take in Mhaura for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Mhaura",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4208",["title"]="Faded Promises",["page_title"]="Faded Promises",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Faded_Promises",["revision"]="111641",["requirements"]="Start: Romualdo \226\128\148 Metalworks (K-9)\010Requirements: Ninja Level 20+\010Fame: Tenshodo\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Palborough Chest Key\010Key item: Diary of Mukunda\010Previous: Ayame and Kaede",["rewards"]="Fukuro",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You are to seek out the person sending threatening letters to Senator Alois and eliminate him. First, you must find a diary hidden somewhere in the Palborough Mines and take it to Kagetora of the Tenshodo.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="With your job set to ninja level 20+, talk to Romualdo for a cutscene to start the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the other Cannonry room and talk to Ayame. \010\010You may get a scene related to the quest Out of the Depths the first time you speak to her.\010\010 You do not have to stay on NIN after starting the quest. The rest can be done on any job.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Palborough Chest Key in the Palborough Mines and open a treasure chest there to obtain the Key item: Diary of Mukunda.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Bastok and talk to Kagetora (F-6) in Port Bastok, then talk to Ayame again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Finally, talk to Alois (J-8) in Metalworks to receive your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Tenshodo",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7511",["title"]="Fallen Comrades",["page_title"]="Fallen Comrades",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Fallen_Comrades",["revision"]="104243",["requirements"]="Start: Pavvke \226\128\148 Bastok Mines (I-7)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Silver Name Tag",["rewards"]="550g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Bring Pavvke the name tags of the Galka who lost their lives in the Palborough Mines twenty years ago.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Pavvke.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Silver Name Tag, either from killing Onyx Quadav or Greater Quadav in Palborough Mines, or purchasing it from the Neck section of the Auction House.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Silver Name Tag to Pavvke for your gil reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57190",["title"]="Fangs of the Lion",["page_title"]="Fangs of the Lion",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Fangs_of_the_Lion",["revision"]="120930",["requirements"]="Previous: Path of Darkness",["rewards"]="Key item: Mythril Mirror",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have failed in your attempt to rescue Luzaf. Return to the offices of Salaheem's Sentinels and regroup with President Naja.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Path of Darkness; this mission begins during its ending cutscene in the Alzadaal Undersea Ruins.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Aht Urhgan Whitegate and enter the second platform of Salaheem's Sentinels at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.\010\010 The cutscene triggers automatically as you enter the platform; speaking with an NPC is not required.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The cutscene completes the mission, grants the Key item: Mythril Mirror, awards the title \034Nashmeira's Loyalist,\034 and begins Nashmeira's Plea.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6196",["title"]="Father and Son",["page_title"]="Father and Son",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Father_and_Son",["revision"]="60796",["requirements"]="Start: Ailbeche \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (J-9)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1",["rewards"]="Willow Fishing Rod",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A child stands crying in the Parade Grounds. Find his father for him.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Part 1",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Ailbeche, a small crying boy just south of the fountain at Northern San d'Oria (J-9), to get a cutscene. He says he became separated with his father, and doesn't know what to do. You must look for someone in armor but no helmet.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="J-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Ailbeche's father, Exoroche, shopping in Southern San d'Oria in Helbort's Blades Southern San d'Oria (K-7).",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="K-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Ailbeche Northern San d'Oria (J-9) again to get another cutscene. His father appears and scolds him for crying and turning to strangers for help. As punishment, he takes the boy's fishing rod away and gives it to you. This completes the quest.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="J-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Part 2",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you talk to Ailbeche Northern San d'Oria (J-9) again, he tells you that he would really like his fishing rod back. You can give it back to him by trading it.\010\010There is no immediate reward for doing this but it is necessary to start the Sharpening the Sword quest.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="J-9",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7519",["title"]="Father Figure",["page_title"]="Father Figure",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Father_Figure",["revision"]="118773",["requirements"]="Start: Michea\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Silver Ingot\010Previous: The Elvaan Goldsmith",["rewards"]="2,200 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Bring Michea a silver ingot so that she may craft a present for her surrogate father, Dalzakk.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Michea.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Silver Ingot to Michea.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Post-rebase it is possible to flag this quest even if you have started Distant Loyalties.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7525",["title"]="Fear of Flying",["page_title"]="Fear of Flying",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Fear_of_Flying",["revision"]="104194",["requirements"]="Start: Kurando \226\128\148 Port Bastok (H-6)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Silkworm Egg x 1",["rewards"]="Black Neckerchief",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Kurando claims airships are dangerous - that every time one passes over the Rolanberry Fields, a horrible beast appears. He needs you to bring back whatever the beast drops as proof to back his claims.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Kurando to accept the quest. He can be found at the end of the tunnel between the construction area and the water side.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Rolanberry Fields and hunt the Silk Caterpillar (see testimonials) - it spawns every 11 minutes in the area of Rolanberry Fields (K-7), when the Airship flies by overhead. Kill it to get the Silkworm Egg. You will see a piece of Crag material sticking out of the ground. The Silk Caterpillar spawns just behind this.",["zone"]="Rolanberry Fields",["grid"]="K-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back to Kurando and trade him the Silkworm Egg to get your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1089",["title"]="Fear of the Dark",["page_title"]="Fear of the Dark",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Fear_of_the_Dark",["revision"]="68266",["requirements"]="Start: Secodiand \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (F-6)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Bat Wing x 2",["rewards"]="200 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Fetch two bat wings.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After talking to Secodiand, find him two bat wings. The closest location for farming is West Ronfaure where bat wings may be obtained from Ding Bats and Mouse Bats even by low level characters.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Secodiand and trade the wings to him to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The quest is repeatable and Secodiand will continue to buy bat wings at the rate of 200 gil for two.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57513",["title"]="Fear of the Dark II",["page_title"]="Fear of the Dark II",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Fear_of_the_Dark_II",["revision"]="121774",["requirements"]="Start: Suldiran \226\128\148 Al Zahbi (J-10) / Map 1\010Fame: None\010Items: 2 Imp Wings",["rewards"]="200 gil",["repeatable"]="yes",["summary"]="Bring Suldiran two Imp Wings.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Suldiran on the upper level of Galeserpent Square at Al Zahbi (J-10) / Map 1.\010\010 Agree to help him obtain the materials needed to make a charm.\010\010 Suldiran can be taken prisoner during Besieged. If he is not present, the quest cannot be started or completed until he is rescued.",["zone"]="Al Zahbi",["grid"]="J-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain 2 Imp Wings.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Suldiran at Al Zahbi (J-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Al Zahbi",["grid"]="J-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade him exactly 2 Imp Wings to complete the quest.\010\010 The first completion awards:\010\010 200 gil and The title Dark Resistant",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Repeat Completions",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After completing the quest once, trade another pair of Imp Wings directly to Suldiran.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The quest does not need to be accepted again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="No change of area or waiting period is required.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Each repeat trade awards 200 gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_323",["title"]="Fetichism (Bastok Mission 1-3)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 1-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_1-3",["revision"]="111737",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 1-2|A Geological Survey",["rewards"]="Rank 2\0101000 gil\010Bastokan Ring [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Hunt the Quadav in the Palborough Mines and collect the four parts of a Quadav fetich.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Select the mission from one of the Bastok Gate Guards",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You need to farm all four fetich pieces (Fetich Head, Fetich Torso, Fetich Arms, and Fetich Legs). Amber, Brass, Greater, Old, Onyx, and Veteran Quadavs in multiple zones drop them, but the highest drop rates are in Palborough Mines.\010\010 (Optional) To get to Palborough Mines, go to North Gustaberg (K-3). You can reach North Gustaberg from Port Bastok (L-6) or from South Gustaberg (H-5).\010\010 (Optional) Palborough Mines (()) / Map 2 is filled with Greater, Onyx, and Veteran Quadavs about Lv.13. To get there, travel North until you hit the big room at G-7. Make your way over to H-7 and head south, turning right at the split, followed by a left. This will put you on a straight path down to H-9 where you'll follow the bend into a circular room, followed by another bend twisting North and finally end up at the elevator in the center. Take the elevator up to the second floor by pulling the lever to make it go up and down. Be careful of Zi'Ghi Boneeater, a Lvl.15-16 NM.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade all four fetich pieces simultaneously to one of the Bastok Gate Guards to complete the mission.\010\010|+ Fetich drop rates*\010|-\010! scope=\034col\034 | Zone\010! scope=\034col\034 | Level\010! scope=\034col\034 | Quadav\010! scope=\034col\034 | Head\010! scope=\034col\034 | Torso\010! scope=\034col\034 | Arms\010! scope=\034col\034 | Legs\010|-\010| North Gustaberg\010| data-sort-value=\0345.5\034 | 3\226\128\1478\010| Amber || 1% || 1% || 2% || 2%\010|-\010| South Gustaberg\010| data-sort-value=\0345.5\034 | 3\226\128\1478\010| Amber || 1% || 1% || 2% || 2%\010|-\010| Palborough Mines\010| data-sort-value=\0346.5\034 | 3\226\128\14710\010| Amber || 1% || 1% || 1% || 1%\010|-\010| Konschtat Highlands\010| data-sort-value=\03413\034 | 10\226\128\14716\010| Onyx || 1% || 1% || 2% || 2%\010|-\010| Konschtat Highlands\010| data-sort-value=\03413\034 | 10\226\128\14716\010| Veteran || 1% || 1% || 2% || 2%\010|-\010| Konschtat Highlands\010| data-sort-value=\03413\034 | 10\226\128\14716\010| Greater || 1% || 1% || 2% || 2%\010|-\010| Palborough Mines\010| data-sort-value=\03414.5\034 | 11\226\128\14718\010| Veteran || 3% || 3% || 6% || 5%\010|-\010| Palborough Mines\010| data-sort-value=\03414.5\034 | 11\226\128\14718\010| Greater || 1% || 2% || 1% || 3%\010|-\010| Palborough Mines\010| data-sort-value=\03414.5\034 | 11\226\128\14718\010| Onyx || 4% || 5% || 2% || 4%\010|-\010| Pashhow Marshlands\010| data-sort-value=\03418\034 | 16\226\128\14720\010| Veteran || 1% || 1% || 2% || 2%\010|-\010| Pashhow Marshlands\010| data-sort-value=\03418\034 | 16\226\128\14720\010| Greater || 1% || 1% || 2% || 2%\010|-\010| Pashhow Marshlands\010| data-sort-value=\03418\034 | 16\226\128\14720\010| Onyx || 2% || 4% || 2% || 4%\010|-\010| Palborough Mines\010| data-sort-value=\03422\034 | 21\226\128\14723\010| Old || 7% || 3% || 2% || 3%\010|-\010| Palborough Mines\010| data-sort-value=\03422\034 | 21\226\128\14723\010| Brass || \226\128\148 || 2% || 2% || \226\128\148\010|-\010| Pashhow Marshlands\010| data-sort-value=\03423\034 | 20\226\128\14726\010| Old || 1% || 1% || 2% || 2%\010|-\010| Pashhow Marshlands\010| data-sort-value=\03423\034 | 20\226\128\14726\010| Brass || 1% || 1% || 2% || 2%\010|-\010| Beadeaux\010| data-sort-value=\03425\034 | 22\226\128\14728\010| Brass || 3% || 3% || 1% || 4%\010|-\010| Rolanberry Fields\010| data-sort-value=\03428\034 | 26\226\128\14730\010| Old || 1% || 1% || 2% || 2%\010|-\010| Rolanberry Fields\010| data-sort-value=\03428\034 | 26\226\128\14730\010| Brass || 1% || 1% || \226\128\148 || \226\128\148\010Assumes default AirSkyBoat drop rates",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2511",["title"]="Fill In",["page_title"]="Fill In",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Fill_In",["revision"]="123893",["requirements"]="Start: Nanaa Mihgo \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (J-3)\010Fame: Windurst\010Items: Broken Charm Bracelet\010Four-Leaf Mandragora Bud\010 Lucky Egg\010Sand Charm \010 Wild Rabbit Tail",["rewards"]="Nanaa's Charm [Horizon change] [Template Item Sections: ]",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Part 1",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Flickering Lantern from (61-67)Tonberry Pursuer's in Temple of Uggalepih or (62 - 65)Tonberry Trailer's in Den of Rancor. View here to see (Temple of Uggalepih (J-8) / Map 3) map 3 one spot to farm them)",["zone"]="Temple of Uggalepih",["grid"]="J-8 / Map 3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Flickering Lantern to the ??? at (Temple of Uggalepih (G-8) / Map 3) to spawn Sozu Rogberry. The staircase(Temple of Uggalepih (G-7) / Map 3) is a common place to fight the nm due to the (64 - 67) magic pot(called hover tank) magic agro nearby its spawn point. It will drop a Broken Charm Bracelet [Horizon change] and also possible a Thief's Knife. Once you have the charm, you can move on to part 2.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Part 2",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Windurst Woods (J-3) and trade the Broken Charm Bracelet to Nanaa Mihgo to start the quest. Having the 4 items needed when you start the quest will save a trip. Gather a Four-Leaf Mandragora Bud, Lucky Egg, Sand Charm and a Wild Rabbit Tail. See notes below.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="J-3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade all 4 items to Nanaa Mihgo. You will get the text telling you \034I'll leave the necklace for you at my hideout deep in the Horutoto Rrruins.\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Lily Tower entrance of Inner Horutoto Ruins at (East Sarutabaruta (J-7)) in East Sarutabaruta. Go to (Inner Horutoto Ruins (G-8) / Lily Tower) and enter the cracked wall on the North side of the room.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to (Inner Horutoto Ruins (G-8) / Beetle's Burrow) and click the Mahogany Door to enter. \034DO NOT CLICK WITH FULL INVENTORY!\034 Click the ??? on the table for your Nanaa's Charm. Enjoy Nanaa's hideout while you're there!",["zone"]="Inner Horutoto Ruins",["grid"]="G-8 / Beetle's Burrow",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="horizonxi",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57151",["title"]="Finders Keepers",["page_title"]="Finders Keepers",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Finders_Keepers",["revision"]="120836",["requirements"]="Previous: Teahouse Tumult",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="After snatching the Olduum artifact, Lady Karababa has left for Salaheem's Sentinels. What business could she possibly have with a mercenary company?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Teahouse Tumult; this mission begins immediately after its ending cutscene in Aydeewa Subterrane.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Aht Urhgan Whitegate and enter the second platform of Salaheem's Sentinels at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.\010\010 The cutscene triggers automatically as you enter the platform; speaking with Naja Salaheem is not required.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The cutscene completes the mission and begins Shield of Diplomacy.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57471",["title"]="Finding Faults",["page_title"]="Finding Faults",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Finding_Faults",["revision"]="121727",["requirements"]="Start: Hishahma \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-8) / Map 1\010Fame: None",["rewards"]="One correct weakness: 200 Imperial Standing\010Both correct weaknesses: ??? Box",["repeatable"]="daily",["summary"]="Journey to the lands where dangerous monsters reside and investigate their weak points. According to previous research, each type of monster should possess two weak points.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="The weakness rotation, one-attempt restriction, reset timing, and follow-up quest conditions below require confirmation on HorizonXI. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Investigation Targets\010\010Speak with Hishahma and select one of the following investigations:\010\010{| class=\034horizon-table table-xl quest-table\034\010! Investigation\010! Notorious Monster\010! Spawn Point\010! Branch-Specific Weakness Categories\010|-\010| Lamiae\010| Lamia Deathdancer\010| Caedarva Mire (I-7) / Map 1\010|",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A particular sound",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Low physical strength\010|-\010| Trolls\010| Troll Speculator\010| Mount Zhayolm (L-6) / Map 1\010|",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A particular scent",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Sluggish movement\010|-\010| Mamool Ja\010| Mamool Ja Mimicker\010| Wajaom Woodlands (E-13) \226\128\148 On the isolated ledge reached through Mamook.\010|",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A particular irritant",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Difficulty landing after a fall\010|}",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Quest Flow",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Hishahma at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select the Lamia, Troll, or Mamool Ja investigation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the corresponding spawn point listed above.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the ??? to spawn the selected Notorious Monster.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Attempt to determine which two weakness categories are active.\010\010 The monster becomes intimidated whenever an active weakness is triggered.\010\010 Two of the five possible categories for that investigation are active.\010\010 You do not need to trigger either weakness during the fight. The monster may still be defeated, after which you may guess two answers.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat the Notorious Monster.\010\010 Do not change areas or allow the monster to despawn.\010\010 The ??? does not immediately provide another attempt for the accepted investigation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Hishahma and select the two categories you believe were the monster's weaknesses.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Change areas and wait until after the next Japanese Midnight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Hishahma again to receive the result and any applicable reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Shared Weakness Categories\010\010Three possible weakness categories are shared by all three investigations:\010\010! Weakness Category\010! Testing Method\010|-\010| A particular weapon skill\010| Use different weapon skills and watch for the monster to become intimidated.\010|-\010| A weapon skill used from a particular direction\010| Use weapon skills from the monster's front, rear, left, and right sides.\010|-\010| A particular element\010| Use attacks or spells representing different elements and watch for intimidation.\010\010Each investigation also has the two branch-specific categories described below.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Lamia Investigation",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If the Azouph Isle Staging Point is activated:\010\010 Use the Runic Portal in the Chamber of Passage at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-7) / Map 1.\010\010 Exit the staging point into Caedarva Mire at Caedarva Mire (K-9) / Map 1.\010\010 Travel northwest to the ??? at Caedarva Mire (I-7) / Map 1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Without the staging-point route:\010\010 Take the Silver Sea route to Nashmau from Port Ephramad at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-5) / Map 1.\010\010 Leave Nashmau through its northern gate at Nashmau (H-6) / Map 1.\010\010 Travel north through Caedarva Mire to the ??? at Caedarva Mire (I-7) / Map 1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Branch-Specific Tests",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A particular sound:\010\010 Examine the nearby Peculiar Plants after spawning Lamia Deathdancer.\010\010 The sound corresponding to the active weakness causes Lamia Deathdancer to become intimidated.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Low physical strength:\010\010 Strike Lamia Deathdancer with ordinary melee attacks and watch for intimidation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Troll Investigation",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If the Halvung Staging Point is activated:\010\010 Use the Runic Portal in the Chamber of Passage at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-7) / Map 1.\010\010 Exit the staging point into Mount Zhayolm at Mount Zhayolm (K-6) / Map 1.\010\010 Travel east to the ??? at Mount Zhayolm (L-6) / Map 1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Without the staging-point route:\010\010 Leave Aht Urhgan Whitegate for Bhaflau Thickets through the gate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-7) / Map 1.\010\010 Cross Bhaflau Thickets and enter Halvung at Bhaflau Thickets (F-8) / Map 1.\010\010 Cast Escape to emerge in Mount Zhayolm at Mount Zhayolm (L-7) / Map 1.\010\010 Alternatively, follow the Halvung route to the same Mount Zhayolm exit.\010\010 Travel north to the ??? at Mount Zhayolm (L-6) / Map 1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Branch-Specific Tests",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A particular scent:\010\010 Examine the nearby Peculiar Seed after spawning Troll Speculator.\010\010 The scent corresponding to the active weakness causes Troll Speculator to become intimidated.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Sluggish movement:\010\010 Pull Troll Speculator away from its spawn point and observe its movement speed.\010\010 If this weakness is active, it moves substantially slower than an ordinary Troll.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mamool Ja Investigation",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel\010\010The spawn point is on an isolated ledge in Wajaom Woodlands and cannot be reached directly from the main portion of the zone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Leave Aht Urhgan Whitegate for Wajaom Woodlands through the gate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You enter Wajaom Woodlands near Wajaom Woodlands (M-7).",["zone"]="Wajaom Woodlands",["grid"]="M-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel southwest and enter Mamook through the Wajaom Woodlands entrance at Wajaom Woodlands (D-12).",["zone"]="Wajaom Woodlands",["grid"]="D-12",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You arrive in Mamook at Mamook (J-7) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Mamook",["grid"]="J-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Cross Mamook Map 1 and take the exit at Mamook (M-9) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Mamook",["grid"]="M-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You emerge on the isolated Wajaom Woodlands ledge at Wajaom Woodlands (E-13), beside the quest targets.",["zone"]="Wajaom Woodlands",["grid"]="E-13",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Branch-Specific Tests",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A particular irritant:\010\010 Examine the nearby Peculiar Bud after spawning Mamool Ja Mimicker.\010\010 Examine the bud before leading the monster down from the ledge, as the target may no longer be accessible afterward.\010\010 The reported irritant message is: A liquid drips from the plant when you touch it, making your eyes blink rapidly.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Difficulty landing after a fall:\010\010 Lead Mamool Ja Mimicker over the nearby one-way ledge.\010\010 Watch for the monster to become intimidated when it lands.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Rewards\010\010After reporting your answers, changing areas, and waiting until after the next Japanese Midnight, speak with Hishahma to receive the result.\010\010! Correct Weaknesses\010! Reward\010|-\010| 0\010| None\010|-\010| 1\010| 200 Imperial Standing\010|-\010| 2\010| ??? Box",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A ??? Box must be traded to an appraiser to reveal its contents.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Identifying at least one correct weakness counts as a successful completion of the selected investigation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Unlocking The Art of War",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Lamia, Troll, and Mamool Ja investigations are tracked separately.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Successfully complete all three investigations by identifying at least one correct weakness for each branch.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After all three branches have been completed successfully, The Art of War becomes available from Hishahma after the applicable quest reset. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Hishahma may continue to offer repeat attempts of Finding Faults after the follow-up quest becomes available.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The active weakness categories are reported to change at the weekly Conquest Tally.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The exact weapon skill, attack direction, element, sound, scent, or environmental trigger may vary between rotations or attempts.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2125",["title"]="Fire and Brimstone",["page_title"]="Fire and Brimstone",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Fire_and_Brimstone",["revision"]="119340",["requirements"]="Start: Perih Vashai \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (K-7)\010Requirements: Ranger 50+\010Items: Old Earring\010Previous: Sin Hunting",["rewards"]="Hunter's Beret",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="Go to Mhaura and meet Koh Lenbalalako. It is said that she knows the whereabouts of the sinner's daughter.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Part 1: Eldieme Necropolis",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Perih Vashai and watch a cutscene where she tells you that there is information to be had in Mhaura regarding the Traitor's Daughter and that the Mithra Tracker has already left to follow up on it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You are then sent to Mhaura to talk to Koh Lenbalalako in the Blacksmiths' Guild (Mhaura) at Mhaura (F-9) for more information.",["zone"]="Mhaura",["grid"]="F-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you speak to Koh Lenbalalako, another cutscene ensues, which directs you to The Eldieme Necropolis.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter The Eldieme Necropolis through the entrance at Batallia Downs (I-10) and watch another cutscene in which the Mithra Tracker wants you to go ahead of her and \034clear the way\034 to the Gravestone at The Eldieme Necropolis (G-9) / Map 1. \010\010Note: To reach The Eldieme Necropolis (G-9) \226\128\148 Map 1, you will need someone to hit the switch for you once you are in the chamber with the locking doors.\010\010Note: As of 9/24/2025, checking the Gravestone in the first room The Eldieme Necropolis (H-8) \226\128\148 Map 1 works. This may be unintended and patched out at some point).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Gravestone (in a small hallway off the north side of the southernmost chamber), watch the cutscene, and then leave The Eldieme Necropolis. \010\010Note that the Azer near the Gravestone will aggro by sight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Part 2: Castle Oztroja\010\010Note: For a part of this Quest some form of Sneak and Invisible is strongly advised to avoid aggro.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back to Windurst and talk to Perih Vashai once more where you will see another cutscene, which directs you to Castle Oztroja to find an Old Earring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you get to Castle Oztroja you need to go past the first doorway with the trapdoor and proceed to floor 2 at Castle Oztroja (J-8) \226\128\148 Map 1. There, make your way to the 4 lever door at the SW corner of Castle Oztroja (G-8) \226\128\148 Map 3. \010\010You can find the combination to the door at the dead-end at Castle Oztroja (I-10) \226\128\148 Map 3.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once inside this doorway proceed all the way up the stairs to floor 3 at Castle Oztroja (F-9) \226\128\148 Map 3.",["zone"]="Castle Oztroja",["grid"]="F-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On floor 3, you find a chamber with a pool in the middle of it at Castle Oztroja (H-9) \226\128\148 Map 4. This pool will be surrounded by Yagudo and full of Yagudo Parasites.",["zone"]="Castle Oztroja",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Yagudo Parasites aggro by sound and the Yagudo aggro by sight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Run into the pool and when no Yagudo are looking, Scavenge, Camouflage, and run back out of the room to the safety of the hallway. \010\010You may not get the Old Earring the first try. If you do not get it, wait 5 minutes, reapply sneak and invisible and repeat.\010\010If you have a high level job, you can set Ranger as your subjob and still get the item using Scavenge; a more practical solution than spending a lot of money on Silent Oils and Prism Powders. \010\010If you are still unsuccessful, try relaunching the game and trying again. See: Talk: Fire and Brimstone",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Perih Vashai in Windurst Woods (K-7) and trade her the Old Earring for a final cutscene and your reward.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="K-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Ranger (RNG)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Ranger (RNG)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Hunter's Beret",["revision"]="101729"},{["job"]="Ranger (RNG)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Fire and Brimstone",["revision"]="119340"}}},{["id"]="wiki_587",["title"]="Fire in the Eyes of Men (Promathia Mission 7-3)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 7-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_7-3",["revision"]="106635",["requirements"]="Previous: Flames in the Darkness",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Travel to the Moblin city of Movalpolos to find a path to the fifth and final mothercrystal.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Head to Mine Shaft #2716 and check the Shaft Entrance for a cutscene.\010\010Note: Check Navigating Newton Movalpolos for options on how to get to Mine Shaft #2716.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Metalworks (H-8) and talk to Cid for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait until the next Vana'diel day while Cid performs maintenance on the airship. Then talk to him again for a second cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_19852",["title"]="Fisherman's Heart",["page_title"]="Fisherman's Heart",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Fisherman%27s_Heart",["revision"]="106230",["requirements"]="Start: Katsunaga \226\128\148 Mhaura (G-10)\010Requirements: Fishing Skill: 20 minimum\010(includes gear)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Gugru Tuna",["rewards"]="Provides information about the character's fishing history.",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Bring Katsunaga a gugru tuna and he'll tell you all he knows about your fishing history.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Katsunaga, standing on the waterfront at Mhaura (G-10), says he can tell you about your fishing history if you bring him a Gugru Tuna.",["zone"]="Mhaura",["grid"]="G-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade him a Gugru Tuna to learn:\010\010The total number of times you have cast your line.\010\010The number of times you actually caught a fish.\010\010Your longest fish ever caught (measured in ilms).\010\010Your heaviest fish ever caught (measured in ponzes).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5938",["title"]="Fistful of Fury",["page_title"]="Fistful of Fury",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Fistful_of_Fury",["revision"]="120344",["requirements"]="Start: Vola - Lower Jeuno (J-8)\010Requirements: Tenshodo Reputation 3\010Items: Nue Fang\010Morbolger Vine\010Dodo Skin\010Previous: Silence of the Rams",["rewards"]="Brown Belt",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Collect the three items required by Vola (Tenshodo HQ in Lower Jeuno). \010\010All three items are Rare/Ex.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Dodo Skin from either Deadly Dodo (Lv39 - Lv40) in Sauromugue Champaign or from the KSNM Moa Constrictors.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Nue Fang from either Nue (Lv41 - Lv42) in Beaucedine Glacier or from the BCNM Eye of the Tiger.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Morbolger Vine from either Morbolger (Lv42 - Lv44) in Ordelle's Caves or from the BCNM Steamed Sprouts.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade these items to Vola to complete the quest.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Vola (Tenshodo, Lower Jeuno)\010 / summary=To receive your brown belt, find a nue fang, a morbolger vine, and a dodo skin. Only then will you be worthy.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7450",["title"]="Fit for a Prince",["page_title"]="Fit for a Prince",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Fit_for_a_Prince",["revision"]="118832",["requirements"]="Start: Halver \226\128\148 Chateau d'Oraguille (I-9)\010Requirements: Access to Chateau d'Oraguille\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 3",["rewards"]="Castor's Ring and\010Pollux's Ring",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You are to find a suitable bride for Prince Trion based on the requirements explained to you.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Not Active on Horizon",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Halver for a cutscene. He will ask you to find a female adventurer that fits Prince Trion's preferences.\010\010Halver is involved with many quests. You may need to speak to him several times.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Consult the table below to pinpoint the player model you need to find. Have a matching player in your party and in the zone, then talk to Halver again.\010\010You may cancel the quest at any time. You can restart the quest every in-game hour with no need to zone, and Halver will give you a new description.\010\010If you are female, Halver will never describe an adventurer with your race.\010\010Some race/face combinations are very common, and some are very rare. These will be indicated by gold and gray boxes in the table, respectively.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will be rewarded with Castor's Ring and the title \034Royal Wedding Planner\034. Your partner will be rewarded with Pollux's Ring and the title \034Consort Candidate\034.\010\010The RareExclusive quality on these rings can be removed by synthing them with a Wind Crystal, and they can be signed by using a Cyclone Crystal. These synths have a 100% success rate.\010\010!| Race !!|Description !!| Face\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|Elvaan\010|Shoulder-length blonde hair parted in the middle.\010|1A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|Elvaan\010|Shoulder-length red hair parted in the middle.\010|1B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Elvaan\010|Pinned-up, braided silver hair.\010|2A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Elvaan\010|Pinned-up, braided black hair.\010|2B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Elvaan\010|Blonde hair brushed to the right, and braided on the left.\010|3A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Elvaan\010|Red hair brushed to the right, and braided on the left.\010|3B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|Elvaan\010|Blonde hair tied into two braids in the back.\010|4A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|Elvaan\010|Red hair tied into two braids in the back.\010|4B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Elvaan\010|White hair bound backwards while leaving the sides to frame the face.\010|5A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Elvaan\010|Red hair bound backwards while leaving the sides to frame the face.\010|5B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Elvaan\010|Long, straight silver hair parted in the middle.\010|6A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Elvaan\010|Long, straight black hair parted in the middle.\010|6B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Elvaan\010|Shoulder-length silver hair brushed back from the face.\010|7A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Elvaan\010|Shoulder-length black hair brushed back from the face.\010|7B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Elvaan\010|Black hair braided behind the left ear.\010|8A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Elvaan\010|Silver hair braided behind the left ear.\010|8B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Hume\010|Blonde hair that almost hides the eyebrows and is tied back in a short ponytail.\010|1A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Hume\010|Brown hair that almost hides the eyebrows and is tied back in a short ponytail.\010|1B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Hume\010|Long blonde hair parted on the left and tied back in a ponytail.\010|2A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Hume\010|Long black hair parted on the left and tied back in a ponytail.\010|2B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Hume\010|Flowing, shoulder-length black hair.\010|3A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Hume\010|Flowing, shoulder-length chestnut-colored hair.\010|3B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|Hume\010|Short black hair brushed neatly over to the right.\010|4A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|Hume\010|Short blonde hair brushed neatly over to the right.\010|4B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Hume\010|Short-cropped blonde hair that stands up in the front.\010|5A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Hume\010|Short-cropped brown hair that stands up in the front.\010|5B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Hume\010|Long black hair brushed over to the left.\010|6A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Hume\010|Long brown hair brushed over to the left.\010|6B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Hume\010|Very short, wavy brown hair.\010|7A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Hume\010|Very short, wavy blonde hair.\010|7B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|Hume\010|Short brown hair brushed to the right in the front, and tied in a small ponytail in the back.\010|8A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|Hume\010|Short blonde hair brushed to the right in the front, and tied in a small ponytail in the back.\010|8B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Mithra\010|Longish red hair held back with a brown band.\010|1A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Mithra\010|Longish chestnut-colored hair held back with a red band.\010|1B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Mithra\010|Short white hair and white markings on the cheeks.\010|2A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Mithra\010|Short silver hair and white markings on the cheeks.\010|2B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Mithra\010|Silver hair cut straight across the forehead, and white markings around the eyes and on the cheeks.\010|3A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Mithra\010|Red hair cut straight across the forehead, and purple markings around the eyes and on the cheeks.\010|3B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Mithra\010|Blonde hair tied in two braids on either side of the face.\010|4A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Mithra\010|Red hair tied in two braids on either side of the face.\010|4B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|Mithra\010|Voluminous red hair tied back with a lavender ribbon.\010|5A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|Mithra\010|Voluminous chestnut-colored hair tied back with a lavender ribbon.\010|5B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Mithra\010|Wild white hair flowing over a headband.\010|6A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Mithra\010|Wild red hair flowing over a headband.\010|6B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Mithra\010|Blonde hair that almost hides the eyebrows, and is tied back in a short ponytail.\010|7A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Mithra\010|Brown hair that almost hides the eyebrows, and is tied back in a short ponytail.\010|7B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|Mithra\010|A colorful headband and brown hair tied in the back in two small pigtails.\010|8A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#e3e6ff\034\010|Mithra\010|A colorful headband and blonde hair tied in the back in two small pigtails.\010|8B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Red hair parted in the front, and tied back in a ponytail.\010|1A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Reddish-blonde hair parted in the front, and tied back in a ponytail.\010|1B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Bluish-black hair tied in three braids and cut straight across the forehead.\010|2A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Green hair tied in three braids and cut straight across the forehead.\010|2B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Brown hair tied up in two pigtails.\010|3A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Red hair tied up in two pigtails.\010|3B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Voluminous blonde hair parted in two and tied back behind the ears.\010|4A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Voluminous reddish-blonde hair parted in two and tied back behind the ears.\010|4B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Blue hair parted in the front, and tied back in a ponytail.\010|5A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Brown hair parted in the front, and tied back in a ponytail.\010|5B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Silver hair tied in three braids and cut straight across the forehead.\010|6A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Bluish-white hair tied in three braids and cut straight across the forehead.\010|6B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Green hair tied up in two pigtails.\010|7A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#c0c0c0\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Blonde hair tied up in two pigtails.\010|7B\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Voluminous brown hair parted in two and tied back behind the ears.\010|8A\010|- BGCOLOR=\034#F0E68C\034\010|Tarutaru\010|Voluminous green hair parted in two and tied back behind the ears.\010|8B\010|-",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57470",["title"]="Five Seconds of Fame",["page_title"]="Five Seconds of Fame",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Five_Seconds_of_Fame",["revision"]="121726",["requirements"]="Start: Balakaf \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-5) / Map 1\010Requirements: Completion of Get the Picture, including returning the recovered Imperial Gold Piece to Balakaf\010Fame: None\010Items: Key item: Photopticator (provided when the quest begins)\010Previous: Get the Picture",["rewards"]="3 Imperial Bronze Pieces\0102 Imperial Silver Pieces\0101 Imperial Mythril Piece",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="You are to scour the city for various intriguing events and record them on Balakaf's new photopticator.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="The recording windows and scene cues below are based on retail-era documentation and require confirmation on HorizonXI. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Balakaf on the second floor of Port Ephramad at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-5) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-5 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After completing the lost-gold portion of Get the Picture, Balakaf gives you the Key item: Photopticator and asks you to investigate five incidents around Aht Urhgan Whitegate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The five cases may be completed in any order.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Recording Rules",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Balakaf immediately after recording a scene.\010\010 Recording another scene before Balakaf reviews the stored footage erases the previous recording.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Each staged incident can occur once per Vana'diel day.\010\010 The five cases are independent, so different cases may be completed during the same Vana'diel day when their time windows permit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If Balakaf rejects the footage as blurry, change zones before attempting that same case again.\010\010 A different case may be attempted without waiting for the failed case to reset.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speaking with a recording NPC outside the required time can prevent the correct cutscene from playing later that day.\010\010 Change zones before speaking with the NPC again during the correct window.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A Pickpocket's Paradise",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Zyfhil near the marionette show at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-9) / Map 1 to hear about a pickpocket targeting his audience.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="F-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At 15:00 or later, speak with Talwahn at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-9) / Map 1 to begin the recording scene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="F-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Four spectators enter the scene.\010\010 The fourth spectator is the thief.\010\010 Wait until the thief takes position directly behind another spectator, then begin recording.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The recording succeeds if it captures the thief picking the spectator's pocket.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Balakaf and have him review the footage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Special of the Day",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Ulamaal inside the Shararat Teahouse at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-12) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-12 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Qutiba at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-12) / Map 1 to receive a clue about the teahouse's daily special.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-12 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use Qutiba's clue to determine the correct response for Ratihb:\010\010! Qutiba's Clue\010! Response\010|-\010| She praises the teahouse for using only the finest ingredients.\010| Water\010|-\010| She suggests that the cook should move away from traditional Aht Urhgan seasonings.\010| Spices\010|-\010| She complains that the selection of ingredients is too limited.\010| Ingredients",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Between 05:00 and 07:00, speak with Ratihb at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-12) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="J-12 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select the response indicated by Qutiba's clue.\010\010 The correct response is fixed for each character and does not change between attempts.\010\010 If the incorrect response is selected, the pumpkin-headed customer will not appear during the recording.\010\010 Ratihb can only be questioned once per Vana'diel day. Change zones and retry on the following Vana'diel day after an incorrect response.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="During the same 05:00\226\128\14707:00 window, speak with Zubyahn at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-12) / Map 1 to begin the recording scene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-12 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Watch for the Galka wearing a pumpkin head as he reaches the front of the queue.\010\010 Do not begin recording as soon as he reaches the counter; the recording may end too early.\010\010 Wait until he has been served and begins leaving the front of the line, then start recording.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The recording succeeds if it captures him returning to the back of the queue.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Balakaf and have him review the footage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="An Early Exit",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Between 12:00 and 14:00, speak with Hishahma at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-8) / Map 1 to observe a military drill.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Four soldiers repeatedly run across the scene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait for their third pass.\010\010 Begin recording when the lead soldier reaches the right side of the screen.\010\010 The recording should capture all four soldiers during the third pass and show that the rear soldier is missing during the fourth pass.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Balakaf and have him review the footage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Smells Like a Rat",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with both Hadahda and Mushayra above the Mog House at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="F-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Between 14:00 and 15:00, speak with Tehf Kimasnahya on Balrahn Way at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-8) / Map 1 to begin the recording scene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="F-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Watch Mushayra as she approaches the pillar.\010\010 She enters, pauses, moves farther toward the pillar, and pauses a second time.\010\010 Begin recording at her second pause, immediately before the chase begins.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The recording succeeds if it captures the Qiqirn circling the pillar to evade Mushayra.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Balakaf and have him review the footage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Strangers in the Night",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Ahaadah outside the Alchemists' Guild at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-6) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="G-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Mathlouq at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-5) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="F-5 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Between 22:00 and 00:00, speak with Nijaom in the nearby alley at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-7) / Map 1 to begin the recording scene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="F-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait until the second person enters and both figures begin interacting.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Begin recording before the medicine is handed over.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The recording succeeds if it captures the exchange and the two figures subsequently parting ways.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Balakaf and have him review the footage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Completion",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After Balakaf has accepted all five recordings, speak with the people who originally reported each incident:\010\010 Zyfhil\010\010 Ulamaal\010\010 Hishahma\010\010 Hadahda and Mushayra\010\010 Ahaadah",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Balakaf after hearing the outcome of all five investigations.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Balakaf completes the quest and rewards you with:\010\010 3 Imperial Bronze Pieces\010\010 2 Imperial Silver Pieces\010\010 1 Imperial Mythril Piece\010\010 The title Photopticator Operator",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_585",["title"]="Flames in the Darkness (Promathia Mission 7-2)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 7-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_7-2",["revision"]="106549",["requirements"]="Previous: Chains and Bonds",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Tenzen is nowhere to be found. You must locate him before returning to Jeuno to meet with Esha'ntarl.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Head to Misareaux Coast (F-7) and check the Dilapidated Gate for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Misareaux Coast",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Sealion's Den and talk to Sueleen at Sealion's Den (H-6).",["zone"]="Sealion's Den",["grid"]="H-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Ru'Lude Gardens (H-8) and approach the palace for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Upper Jeuno (F-7) and check the door of the Marble Bridge Eatery for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2470",["title"]="Flower Child",["page_title"]="Flower Child",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Flower_Child",["revision"]="75290",["requirements"]="Start: Ojha Rhawash \226\128\148 Windurst Walls (C-13)\010Fame: windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Lilac x1",["rewards"]="Exit to any area within the city from Mog House",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="The little Mithra cub seems to want a certain flower. Help the budding flower girl achieve the bloom of her youth.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade a Lilac to Ojha Rhawash. You do not need to talk to her first.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2574",["title"]="Fly High",["page_title"]="Fly High",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Fly_High",["revision"]="114881",["requirements"]="Start: Ferchinne \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold (G-9)\010Items: Hippogryph Tailfeather x2\010Previous: Promathia Mission 4-1: Sheltering Doubt",["rewards"]="Mistmelt",["repeatable"]="yes",["summary"]="\034A noble bird that walks on four legs. A proud beast that has the wings of an eagle.\034 No, this is not a riddle; it is a description of the beast from which you must retrieve two tailfeathers.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Ferchinne asks for two Hippogryph Tailfeathers.\010\010Hippogryph Tailfeathers can be retrieved from any Hippogryph type mob in Riverne - Site #A01 or Riverne - Site #B01.\010\010The Auction House may have Hippogryph Tailfeathers in stock under Clothcraft, or Mistmelt in stock under Goldsmithing.\010\010Note: Hippogryph type mobs have True Sight and their normal attacks have the added effect of Weight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6864",["title"]="Flyers for Regine",["page_title"]="Flyers for Regine",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Flyers_for_Regine",["revision"]="106937",["requirements"]="Start: Regine \226\128\148 Port San d'Oria (J-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Magicmart Flyer x 15",["rewards"]="440 Gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Hand out fifteen flyers for the struggling magic shop. Pass them only to townsfolk, not adventurers.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Rugiette or Regine in the magic shop. They talk about the lack of floor traffic. After this, when you talk to Regine and she asks how she can help you, you'll have the option to say you're looking for work. Choose it, and Regine gives you some flyers to hand out to boost business. You get 15 flyers and must trade them all to various people in the San d'Oria, but very few will actually take them. An indication that a NPC will accept the flyer is by a system message stating \034NPCname looks over curiously for a moment.\034 when you approach that specific NPC.\010\010You must have two inventory slots free, as you will receive 1 stack (12) and 3 flyers.\010\010If you need more flyers, go back to Regine and trade her 10 gil per flyer. You can't trade Regine 150 gil for 15 flyers, you must continuously trade her 10 gil per flyer and then sort them into your inventory. You may also find them at the Auction House.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the flyers to NPC's until you have given away all 15.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Regine again to complete the quest.\010\010The 15 NPC's are (in the most efficient order):\010\010Port San d'Oria\010\010Answald Port San d'Oria (J-10) - front of Mog house\010\010Prietta Port San d'Oria (H-9) - up the stairs above cargo rooms \010\010Miene Port San d'Oria (I-9) - open area by water\010\010Portaure - Cargo room B\010\010Auvare Port San d'Oria (H-6) - behind the Air Travel Agency\010\010Northern San d'Oria\010\010Guilberdrier Northern San d'Oria (F-3) - front of Carpenter`s guild\010\010Villion Northern San d'Oria (F-3) - Carpenter`s guild, 2nd floor balcony\010\010Capiria Northern San d'Oria (F-6) - Near Laborman's Way arch, overlooking the sluice gates\010\010Boncort Northern San d'Oria (F-8) - Phoenix Perch Inn, 2nd floor\010\010Coullene Northern San d'Oria (M-6) - Cathedral 1st floor Main Hall\010\010Southern San d'Oria\010\010Leuveret Southern San d'Oria (F-8) - Raimbroy's Grocery, 2nd floor balcony\010\010Blendare Southern San d'Oria (J-9) - under tree near Auction House\010\010Maugie Southern San d'Oria (L-9) - near Eastgate\010\010Adaunel Southern San d'Oria (K-9) - up the stairs on top of Eastgate archway\010\010Rosel Southern San d'Oria (K-8) - Rosel's Armour Shop",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57154",["title"]="Foiled Ambition",["page_title"]="Foiled Ambition",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Foiled_Ambition",["revision"]="120859",["requirements"]="Previous: Social Graces",["rewards"]="5 Imperial Gold Pieces",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have been caught in a conflict between Lady Karababa and President Naja. Probably best if you let President Naja cool down for a while...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After completing Social Graces, zone once and wait until the next Vana'diel day.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the second platform of Salaheem's Sentinels in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.\010\010 The cutscene triggers automatically as you enter the platform; speaking with Naja Salaheem is not required.\010\010 Speaking with Naja before the wait has elapsed only provides additional dialogue and does not advance the mission.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The cutscene completes the mission, grants 5 Imperial Gold Pieces, awards the title \034Karababa's Secret Agent,\034 and begins Playing the Part.\010\010 To continue Playing the Part, zone once and wait until after the next Japanese midnight (15:00 UTC).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2548",["title"]="Food for Thought",["page_title"]="Food for Thought",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Food_for_Thought",["revision"]="109970",["requirements"]="Start: Kerutoto \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (J-8) / South\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Grilled Hare\010Hard-Boiled Egg\010Pamtam Kelp\010Tortilla\010Windurstian Tea",["rewards"]="1,000 Gil",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="You've been asked to buy food for the two busy researchers and one freshly-awoken meditator. You'll have to ask each of them what they want... if you can understand them, that is.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="This quest can not be started if the quest Say It with Flowers or mission The Price of Peace has been started.\010To receive this quest, you absolutely must talk to the following NPCs in this exact order!",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Ohbiru-Dohbiru in Windurst Waters (J-9) / South in the southern building.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="J-9 / South",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Kerutoto in the northern Rhinostery building. \010\010She will tell you to go talk to Ohbiru-Dohbiru and Kenapa-Keppa in the \034higgledy-piggledy laboratory\034 next door. (At this point the quest is added to your Quest log.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Ohbiru-Dohbiru and Kenapa-Keppa to verify their orders.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back to Kerutoto and talk to her repeatedly if Waking Dreams cut-scene triggers until you get the correct dialog about her order.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make sure you talk to Ohbiru-Dohbiru and Kenapa-Keppa especially a few times for their orders. You are now ready to doordash.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Grilled Hare for Kerutoto (Not Grilled Black Hare)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Hard-Boiled Egg for Kenapa-Keppa",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Windurstian Tea for Ohbiru-Dohbiru",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Tortilla for Ohbiru-Dohbiru (not Tortilla Buena)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Pamtam Kelp for Ohbiru-Dohbiru",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="NPC merchant Taajiji at Windurst Waters (F-10) / North will sell item 3 and 4.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="F-10 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Pamtam Kelp can be bought at Mep Nhapopoluko in Bibiki Bay (H-7).\010\010If you speak with Leepe-Hoppe on the roof during this quest, it becomes obvious who ate all their food supplies (optional).",["zone"]="Bibiki Bay",["grid"]="H-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_11389",["title"]="For the Birds",["page_title"]="For the Birds",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/For_the_Birds",["revision"]="118325",["requirements"]="Start: Koblakiq - Oldton Movalpolos (H-11)\010Items: Arnica Root\010Previous: Missionary Moblin",["rewards"]="Jaguar Mantle",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A letter has arrived from Zeelozok asking for an \034arnica root\034 to be brought to Castle Oztroja. Koblakiq has entrusted this task to you...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="When attempting to activate this quest, you must zone and re-zone after completing Missionary Moblin for Koblakiq to give you the quest. Horizon Change- You can log out and back in. [Horizon change]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Koblakiq and agree to help her to start the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain an Arnica Root. This drops from cactuar mobs in either Eastern Altepa Desert or Western Altepa Desert. It is also available in the Auction House.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Arnica Root to the NPC Daa Bola the Seer located in Castle Oztroja (Map 7, I-7)\010\010Go through the brass door at I-8 on the first map, then through the exit at G-7 on the second. On the next map, head north to the alcove at I-7.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Oldton Movalpolos and talk with Koblakiq who will give you a Key item: Glittering Fragment and send you to Beadeaux.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Beadeaux and head through the underground area. Go back up to the upper level using the ramp, across the small then large bridge to the north side of G-10. The NPC Ge'Fhu Yagudoeye is located by the smokestacks Beadeaux (G-10).",["zone"]="Beadeaux",["grid"]="G-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Clear the surrounding Quadav near him, then talk to him to spawn four NMs: two Nickel Quadav (Paladin) and two Magnes Quadav (Black Mage). They can be slept and silenced (very high resistance to Silence) to make the fight easier; the Magnes Quadav have far fewer HP and should generally be killed first.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill the four NM Quadav and then talk to Ge'Fhu Yagudoeye for a cutscene. If the cutscene does not appear, re-zone into Beadeaux to receive it; however, it usually triggers. If multiple people are doing the quest at once, it is necessary to respawn and kill the NMs for each character who is on the quest; they can be spawned without zoning, by each different character, about every 5 minutes from the NPC.\010\010 This may not be required on HorizonXI. Just ran with a party of 4 characters, killed the 4 NMs everyone in party got the cutscene and was able to turn in quest. Dyrwolfette 6/5/2024 - 3/3/2026 post rebase they absolutely repopped per person.\010\010See testimonials on the Talk Page.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Oldton Movalpolos and talk with Koblakiq to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_574",["title"]="For Whom the Verse is Sung (Promathia Mission 6-1)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 6-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_6-1",["revision"]="75056",["requirements"]="Previous: Three Paths",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Prishe has been spotted in Jeuno! Journey to the Grand Duke Palace to learn more of her whereabouts--before Ulmia is overcome by worry for her long-time friend.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Head to Ru'Lude Gardens (G-6) and talk to Pherimociel inside the Guard Post of the Grand Duke Palace for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="G-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Upper Jeuno and click on the door to the Marble Bridge at (Upper Jeuno (F-7)) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Ru'Lude Gardens for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7509",["title"]="Forever to Hold",["page_title"]="Forever to Hold",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Forever_to_Hold",["revision"]="104355",["requirements"]="Start: Qiji \226\128\148 Port Bastok (I-7)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Brass Hairpin",["rewards"]="300 Gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Qiji wants you to get him a brass hairpin to give to his wife, Romilda, as a present.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Qiji and he will tell you he wants to give his wife a Brass Hairpin.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Give Qiji's wife, Romilda, who is standing next to him, a Brass Hairpin.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Qiji for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3879",["title"]="Forge Your Destiny",["page_title"]="Forge Your Destiny",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Forge_Your_Destiny",["revision"]="119296",["requirements"]="Start: Jaucribaix \226\128\148 Norg (K-8)\010Requirements: Level 30\010Items: Oriental Steel\010Sacred Sprig\010Hatchet\010Sacred Branch\010Bomb Steel",["rewards"]="Mumeito\010Ability to become a Samurai",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Jaucribaix, located on the upper level at the end of the hallway, Norg (K-8), who will tell you about the ways of a samurai. \010\010He requests a Bomb Steel and Sacred Branch and will tell you that if you want to know how to get those items to go talk to his assistants.",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="K-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go down the long steps and talk to Aeka, Norg (I-8), who will give you the Oriental Steel.",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next talk to Ranemaud, Norg (I-7), who will give you the Sacred Sprig. \010If you need to reacquire these items (if you drop them or fail to defeat the NM), you can purchase them from these NPCs. Aeka will demand one Darksteel Ore for payment, and Ranemaud will want one Platinum Ore and two Gold Ore.",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Using the Sacred Sprig and Oriental Steel, you must now retrieve the Sacred Branch and Bomb Steel. The following two steps can be done in either order.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Sanctuary of Zi'Tah",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Hatchet and go to the far east end of The Sanctuary of Zi'Tah.\010\010If multiple players in a party are completing this quest simultaneously, only one of them needs a hatchet.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At The Sanctuary of Zi'Tah (K-10) there is a pathway which leads to an unmapped area. Continue east straight to The Sanctuary of Zi'Tah (L-10) where you will see a large tree. There are rocks at the base of the tree that you can climb up in order to get close enough to the ??? to initiate the next sequence.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade or use your hatchet on the ??? and a Guardian Treant will spawn. (Your hatchet will be consumed.)\010\010Guardian Treant has a 10 minute respawn timer.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill the Guardian Treant and trade the Sacred Sprig to the ??? to receive the Sacred Branch. \010\010 Multiple people can trade the Sacred Sprig to the ??? to receive the Sacred Branch after the NM has been killed. You do not need to kill an NM for each person that requires a Sacred Branch.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Konschtat Highlands",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Konschtat Highlands (D-8) and look for the ??? inside a cave. (There are 2 interactable spots, but only 1 ???.)",["zone"]="Konschtat Highlands",["grid"]="D-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Oriental Steel to the ??? and Forger will spawn. When killed, Forger will drop one Bomb Steel. \010\010Note that should you fail to defeat Forger, you will need to return to Aeka with a Darksteel Ore for a replacement Oriental Steel.\010\010If there is more than one person with a Oriental Steel, it seems you have to wait a minute or two before you can respawn Forger even though the ??? is still there.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have obtained the Sacred Branch and Bomb Steel, return to Norg and trade them to Jaucribaix. He will inform you that your reward will be ready in 3 in-game days (nearly 3 real life hours).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return later and speak with Jaucribaix for a cutscene, in which Gilgamesh will hand you your Mumeito and give you the ability to become a Samurai.\010\010 The Mumeito is used during the Samurai AF Great Katana quest (The Sacred Katana). It is advisable to hold on to this weapon in storage; if it was dropped you will need to pay Ranemaud 30,000 gil in order to obtain a new Mumeito after you have accepted the quest.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Jaucribaix (Near the Captain's Quarters, Norg)\010 / summary=A lump of bomb steel and a sacred branch are required to make a new katana. You will have to ask Jaucribaix's pupils to find out how and where you can get these items.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Samurai (SAM)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Samurai (SAM)",["kind"]="Job unlock",["page"]="Samurai",["revision"]="123578"}}},{["id"]="wiki_2120",["title"]="From Saplings Grow",["page_title"]="From Saplings Grow",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/From_Saplings_Grow",["revision"]="75381",["requirements"]="Start: Perih Vashai \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (K-7)\010Requirements: Able to wield Bow of Trials\010Archery Skill 250+\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1",["rewards"]="Grants the Weapon Skill Empyreal Arrow",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="You are to undertake training to still the doubt within you. Use the bow you have been given until it no longer responds to your inner turmoil.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Perih Vashai in at Windurst Woods (K-7), who will give you the Bow of Trials and the Key item: Weapons Training Guide.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="K-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the Bow of Trials until the latent effect disappears. \010\010How to remove the latent effect: \010\010You must perform Archery Weapon Skills and Skillchains using the Bow of Trials on monsters that check as Easy Prey or higher.\010\010Weapon Skills performed with a main handed weapon, such as Axes or Daggers, will not count.\010\010Weapon Skills performed while under Level Sync count.\010\010You receive:\010\0101 point for opening/soloing a Weapon Skill\010\0102 points for closing a Lv.1 Skillchain\010\0103 points for closing a Lv.2 Skillchain\010\0105 points for closing a Lv.3 Skillchain.\010\010You must accumulate 300 total points. \010\010To see if you are done, check your equipment screen. If you still see the status enhancments given to you by the bow, you need to continue skillchaining. (The text on the Bow of Trials does not change, only your physical stats.)[Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 You can not gain points in Besieged]\010[Conditional wiki content: wotg \226\128\148 You can not gain points in Campaign Battles]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you no longer receive the latent effect bonus, head back to Windurst Woods and trade the Bow of Trials back to Perih Vashai, who will take the weapon from you and give you a Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth and tell you to head to Cape Teriggan.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in Cape Teriggan go to (Cape Teriggan (G-7)) and click the ??? to spawn the NM named Stolas.",["zone"]="Cape Teriggan",["grid"]="G-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the NM is dead, re-examine the ??? to obtain the Key item: Annals of Truth.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring this back to Perih Vashai for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_353",["title"]="Full Moon Fountain (Windurst Mission 6-1)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 6-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_6-1",["revision"]="123865",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Previous: Windurst Mission 5-2|The Shadow Awaits",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="At the request of the Orastery, you are to go to the southwestern magic tower of the Horutoto Ruins, located in West Sarutabaruta. Deep within you will find a laboratory, where you are ordered to switch on the magical gizmo.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade about 24 crystals to any Conquest Overseer to unlock the mission then accept it from any Windurst Gate Guard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Hakkuru-Rinkuru in Port Windurst (E-7), Orastery for a cutscene and the Southwestern star charm.",["zone"]="Port Windurst",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the southwestern tower (Dahlia Tower) in West Sarutabaruta (F-11)and enter Outer Horutoto Ruins.",["zone"]="West Sarutabaruta",["grid"]="F-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Outer Horutoto Ruins (J-8) / Dahlia Tower and click the Gate: Magical Gizmo to spawn 4 Jack Cardians.\010\010Jack of Batons (BLM) , Jack of Coins (RDM), Jack of Cups (WHM), Jack of Swords (PLD)\010\010It is not necessary to kill them all. \010\010Sneak up before examining the door to prevent aggro on pop.*\010\010They are magic aggressive so make sure mages are well out of range.\010\010Make sure you do not kill the one you pulled before the others depop, if you do, you will not receive the cutscene when you examine the door.",["zone"]="Outer Horutoto Ruins",["grid"]="J-8 / Dahlia Tower",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Cardians NMs link with each other.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the door after defeating them for a cutscene.\010\010The cutscene may not trigger until the last Cardian's body as disappeared.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Return to Hakkuru-Rinkuru Port Windurst (E-7) for some dialogue on Ajido-Marujido's whereabouts.",["zone"]="Port Windurst",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Full Moon Fountain for a cutscene which completes the mission.\010\010NOTE:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Multiple sneak+carby-pull attempts failed on 11/15/2025. However, the cardians can be slept/silenced.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Sneak+Ranged Pull on 72THF worked just fine on 2/3/2026. EZPZ.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Confirming Sneak pop + ranged pull one (*not* using pet) worked. Keep the one you pull alive until the others despawn, as the mission text mentions. 75 SMN, 11 Jun 2026",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Holding one and waiting for the other 2 to depop, then killing it, did NOT yield a cutscene. However, sneak pulling one, killing it, then sneak pulling a second and killing it, DID provide a cutscene. Third one depopped. 6/26/2026",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Consider bringing Escape for after the Cardian NM fight as it brings you outside the Lily Tower at East Sarutabaruta (J-7) in East Sarutabaruta, saving part of the walk to Full Moon Fountain.",["zone"]="East Sarutabaruta",["grid"]="J-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6851",["title"]="Gates to Paradise",["page_title"]="Gates to Paradise",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Gates_to_Paradise",["revision"]="106100",["requirements"]="Start: Olbergieut \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (L-7)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 2",["rewards"]="Cotton Cape",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Bring the \034Scripture of Wind\034 to a friar on retreat. Find him at the Crag of Holla on the La Theine Plateau.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Olbergieut, in the Manuscript room of the Northern San d'Oria Cathedral. He asks you to take a Key item: Scripture of Wind to Faurbellant.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to La Theine Plateau, and find Faurbellant located at the east wall of the Crag of Holla (K-8).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Faurbellant. He will give you a Key item: Scripture of Water.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Cathedral in Northern San d'Oria, and talk to Olbergieut for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57168",["title"]="Gaze of the Saboteur",["page_title"]="Gaze of the Saboteur",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Gaze_of_the_Saboteur",["revision"]="120878",["requirements"]="Start: Gessho \226\128\148 Talacca Cove, Talacca Cove (F-6) / Map 1\010Previous: Legacy of the Lost",["rewards"]="Key item: Luminian Dagger",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Gessho believes Nashmeira's life may be in danger. Hurry to the Hazhalm Testing Grounds to protect her from the conniving Flit.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Legacy of the Lost; this mission begins during its victory cutscene at the Rock Slab in Talacca Cove.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Leave Talacca Cove through the southern exit at Talacca Cove (G-10) / Map 1, returning to Caedarva Mire Map 1 at E-9.",["zone"]="Talacca Cove",["grid"]="G-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel west to the Hazhalm Testing Grounds entrance at Caedarva Mire (D-9, D-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Caedarva Mire",["grid"]="D-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Hazhalm Testing Grounds for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Entry Gate for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The cutscene consumes the Key item: Percipient Eye, completes the mission, grants the Key item: Luminian Dagger, awards the title \034Emissary of the Empress,\034 and begins Path of Blood.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57469",["title"]="Get the Picture",["page_title"]="Get the Picture",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Get_the_Picture",["revision"]="121725",["requirements"]="Start: Balakaf \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-5) / Map 1\010Requirements: Access to Aht Urhgan Whitegate\010Fame: None\010Items: Key item: Image recorder\0105 Light Crystals\0103 Light Clusters\010Ahriman Lens after an unsuccessful photograph",["rewards"]="8 Imperial Silver Pieces\0101 Imperial Gold Piece",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Take pictures with Balakaf's \034image recorder\034 at the places he specifies.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="The exact weather and time windows below still require confirmation on HorizonXI. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Photograph Procedure",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Balakaf at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-5) / Map 1 on the second floor of Port Ephramad to begin the quest.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-5 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Balakaf gives you the Key item: Image recorder and describes the first scene he wants recorded.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the corresponding ??? listed below.\010\010 Trade the required Light Crystal or Light Cluster to the ???.\010\010 Select the indicated scene during the cutscene.\010\010 If a particular time or weather condition is required, the picture cannot be taken until those conditions are met.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Balakaf after taking each picture.\010\010 An accepted picture rewards one Imperial Silver Piece.\010\010 After each accepted picture, change zones and wait until after the next Japanese Midnight before speaking with Balakaf for the next assignment.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If Balakaf rejects a picture:\010\010 Change zones and speak with Balakaf again.\010\010 Trade him an Ahriman Lens to repair the Image recorder.\010\010 Change zones and wait until after the next Japanese midnight before attempting the same picture again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Do not use an Aurora Crystal in place of a Light Crystal. Balakaf will reject the signed picture.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Required Pictures\010\010All listed times are in Vana'diel time.\010\010! #\010! Requested Subject\010! Location\010! Required Conditions\010! Flash Item\010! Scene\010|-\010| 1\010| Mount Zhayolm's volcano\010| Wajaom Woodlands (F-6)\010| Cloudy with no active weather icon and a completely overcast sky. Avoid fog.\010| Light Crystal\010| First\010|-\010| 2\010| rowspan=\0342\034 | Lovers' Rocks\010| rowspan=\0342\034 | Arrapago Reef (G-8) / Map 1\010| rowspan=\0342\034 | Ice weather\010| Light Crystal\010| Second\010|-\010| 3\010| Light Cluster\010| Second\010|-\010| 4\010| Distant ruins\010| Mount Zhayolm (C-9) / Map 1\010| 16:00\226\128\14718:00\010| Light Crystal\010| Third\010|-\010| 5\010| Lava flows\010| Halvung (I-8) / Map 1\010| 03:00\226\128\14706:00\010| Light Crystal\010| First\010|-\010| 6\010| Olduum ruins\010| Aydeewa Subterrane (G-10) / Map 3\010| Wind weather\010| Light Cluster\010| Third\010|-\010| 7\010| Waterfall\010| Mamook (E-8) / Map 1\010| Fair or sunny weather between 07:30 and 10:30\010| Light Crystal\010| Third\010|-\010| 8\010| Graveyard\010| Caedarva Mire (E-10) / Map 1\010| 20:00\226\128\14722:00\010| Light Cluster\010| First",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Pictures 2 and 3 are separate assignments at the same location.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After returning picture 2, Balakaf comments that it is too dark but still awards an Imperial Silver Piece.\010\010 This does not count as a failed picture, and an Ahriman Lens is not required.\010\010 Change zones, wait until after the next Japanese midnight, and speak with Balakaf before returning with a Light Cluster for picture 3.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wajaom Woodlands:\010\010 From Aht Urhgan Whitegate, use the exit at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-10) / Map 1 to enter Wajaom Woodlands near Wajaom Woodlands (M-7).\010\010 Travel northwest to the ??? at Wajaom Woodlands (F-6).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Arrapago Reef:\010\010 Enter Arrapago Reef through the entrance in Caedarva Mire at Caedarva Mire (I-6) / Map 1.\010\010 Use a Lamian Fang Key on the locked Iron Gate at Arrapago Reef (J-10) / Map 1.\010\010 Continue west to the ??? at Arrapago Reef (G-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mount Zhayolm:\010\010 The photo point is on the isolated western section of Mount Zhayolm.\010\010 Bring the Key item: Cast metal plate and open the Gates of Halvung at Mount Zhayolm (J-7) / Map 1.\010\010 Continue northwest and enter Halvung through the zone line at Mount Zhayolm (G-7) / Map 1.\010\010 Inside Halvung, cross the bridge and take the first path to the right to return to Mount Zhayolm near Mount Zhayolm (D-10) / Map 1.\010\010 Travel northwest to the ??? at Mount Zhayolm (C-9) / Map 1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Halvung:\010\010 Leave Aht Urhgan Whitegate for Bhaflau Thickets through the exit at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-7) / Map 1.\010\010 In Bhaflau Thickets, enter Halvung at Bhaflau Thickets (F-8) / Map 1.\010\010 Follow the western path southwest to the bridge containing the ??? at Halvung (I-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Aydeewa Subterrane:\010\010 Enter Aydeewa Subterrane from Wajaom Woodlands at Wajaom Woodlands (E-10).\010\010 Follow the path to the first drop, take the right-hand path, and then take the next path to the left.\010\010 The required ??? is northeast of the Olduum ruins at Aydeewa Subterrane (G-10) / Map 3.\010\010 This is not the separate ??? located on the damaged stairway for What Friends Are For.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mamook:\010\010 Enter Mamook from Wajaom Woodlands at Wajaom Woodlands (D-12).\010\010 Descend through the lower passages and continue toward the waterfall on the western side of the zone.\010\010 The ??? is on the ground floor near the waterfall at Mamook (E-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Caedarva Mire:\010\010 Leave Nashmau through its western gate and travel northwest through Caedarva Mire.\010\010 The ??? is in the graveyard at Caedarva Mire (E-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Lost Gold",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After returning the eighth accepted picture, the quest is completed and you will have received a total of eight Imperial Silver Pieces.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Change zones and wait until after another Japanese midnight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Balakaf again. He recalls losing some gold during his travels.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Revisit the seven photography locations listed above.\010\010 Arrapago Reef only needs to be checked once despite being used for two pictures.\010\010 Examine each ??? normally; no additional Light Crystal or Light Cluster is required.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="One randomly selected ??? provides an Imperial Gold Piece.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Imperial Gold Piece to Balakaf.\010\010 He returns the coin after the cutscene.\010\010 Completing this step allows Five Seconds of Fame to be started.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7537",["title"]="Ghosts of the Past",["page_title"]="Ghosts of the Past",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Ghosts_of_the_Past",["revision"]="104337",["requirements"]="Start: Oggbi \226\128\148 Port Bastok (E-6)\010Requirements: Monk 40+\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: non\010Items: Pickaxe",["rewards"]="Tekko Kagi [Horizon change] \010<s>Beat Cesti<s>",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="You are to go to the Gusgen Mines and pass the same trial as Oggbi's former student, Cornelia. Use a pickaxe on a certain hole in the mines to lure the Wandering Ghost out. Defeat it and bring back its \034miner's pendant.\034",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Oggbi in Port Bastok inside the Steaming Sheep Restaurant located at (E-6) as a MNK level 40+.\010\010Note: If you have hand-to-hand skill above 250 he will offer you the Knuckles of Trials for the quest The Walls of Your Mind first. Talk to him again for the right quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once flagged, you can complete the quest on any high-level job, not just monk.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Pickaxe (you can buy one from Numa (E-7) in Port Bastok for about 190 gil).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Gusgen Mines and look for a ??? in the lowest level around G-7. \010\010Go due north across the first map and down the stairs. Use the western door to enter the second map. \010\010Go to the room in the northwest corner and follow the corridor that runs on the west side from this room to the next room.\010\010Take the passage in the NW corner, which is in the SW corner of (F-5). Follow it down.\010\010Go to the second room. The ??? is located on the left side of the room in the NW corner.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use a pickaxe there and it will trigger the Wandering Ghost to spawn.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat it and it will drop the Miner's Pendant (make sure to Cast Lots on it if doing it with others).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Port Bastok and trade it to Oggbi for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={"Monk (MNK)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Monk (MNK)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Tekko Kagi",["revision"]="72854"},{["job"]="Monk (MNK)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Ghosts of the Past",["revision"]="104337"}}},{["id"]="wiki_57142",["title"]="Ghosts of the Past (Aht Urhgan Mission 16: Ghosts of the Past)",["page_title"]="Aht Urhgan Mission 16: Ghosts of the Past",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Aht_Urhgan_Mission_16%3A_Ghosts_of_the_Past",["revision"]="122500",["requirements"]="Start: Gessho \226\128\148 Nashmau (G-8) / Map 1\010Previous: The Black Coffin",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have uncovered the truth behind the Ashu Talif and its ghostly crew. Report your findings to President Naja.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete The Black Coffin; this mission begins during its ending cutscene in Nashmau (G-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="G-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Salaheem's Sentinels in Aht Urhgan Whitegate and speak with Naja Salaheem at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.\010\010 Your current equipment changes portions of the cutscene, but no particular outfit is required to complete this mission.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The cutscene completes the mission and begins Guests of the Empire.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2060",["title"]="Give a Moogle a Break",["page_title"]="Give a Moogle a Break",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Give_a_Moogle_a_Break",["revision"]="119603",["requirements"]="Start: Moogle - Mog House in your home city\010Requirements: Reputation 3 in your home city\010Items: Bronze Bed\010Power Bow\010Beetle Ring",["rewards"]="Upgrades the Mog Safe to a 60 item capacity.",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After you achieve Reputation 3, your moogle will say \034Bronze beds might bring a certain je ne sais quoi to your Mog House, kupo!\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In order for this quest to become available, you must place a Bronze Bed in your Mog House at least one full Vana'diel day before the weekly conquest results are tallied.\010\010Bronze beds can be crafted with Smithing or purchased at the Auction House under Furnishings.\010\010Other Furniture Quests such as Unexpected Treasure may override this quest. To guarantee you get this quest, remove any other quest-giving furniture from your layout. The furniture can remain in your safe.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the weekly conquest results are tallied, head to your home nation and speak to your moogle.\010\010This quest cannot be started in a Rent-A-Room; it can, however, be completed in one.\010\010The bronze bed may be removed at any time after the quest has been flagged; it does not need to be in the Mog House for the quest to be completed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Moogle asks you for a Power Bow and a Beetle Ring.\010\010Power bows can be crafted with Woodworking or purchased at the Auction House under Weapons > Ranged.\010\010Beetle rings can be crafted with Bonecraft or purchased at the Auction House under Armor > Rings.\010\010The HQ versions of either item cannot be used to complete this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the moogle both items. You can make the trade at any mog house, it does not need to be in your home nation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After going away on his trip -- oddly, he doesn't physically leave your Mog House as far as you can tell -- he will come back with a new Mog Safe that now holds 60 items! This takes until Japanese Midnight to occur.\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Moogle - Mog House in your home city\010 / summary=Your moogle wants to take a power bow and a beetle ring to his family for the holidays. He sure would be happy if you found them for him.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2549",["title"]="Glyph Hanger",["page_title"]="Glyph Hanger",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Glyph_Hanger",["revision"]="60752",["requirements"]="Start: Hariga-Origa \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (F-8) / North\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Key item: Note From Hariga-Origa\010Key item: Note From Ipupu",["rewards"]="Key item: Map of the Horutoto Ruins",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="While transcribing an ancient manuscript. Hariga-Origa chanced upon a glyph that he cannot read. He wants you to track down Ipupu, a specialist in paleography, and hand her a note that contains the unknown letter.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Accept the quest to receive a Key item: Note From Hariga-Origa.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go speak with Ipupu in West Sarutabaruta, in the tower between West Sarutabaruta (I-8) and West Sarutabaruta (J-8), to receive a Key item: Note From Ipupu.\010\010 If you exit to West Sarutabaruta from Windurst Waters, the tower is right next to the exit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Hariga-Origa to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5475",["title"]="Go! Go! Gobmuffin!",["page_title"]="Go! Go! Gobmuffin!",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Go%21_Go%21_Gobmuffin%21",["revision"]="115640",["requirements"]="Start: Epinolle \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold (F-8)\010Requirements: Promathia Mission 4-2: The Savage or higher",["rewards"]="Key item: Map of Cape Riverne",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Epinolle wants you to find and bring back a Goblin that has left for Cape Riverne to make a map of the area.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="To activate this quest, you must be on or past Promathia Mission 4-2: The Savage, and must zone into Riverne - Site #B01 for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Tavnazian Safehold and speak with Epinolle on the middle floor at (Tavnazian Safehold (F-8)) by the nomad moogles, and she will give you the quest after 5 lines of text, where she implores you to go find her gobmuffin. There is no cutscene. The quest shows up in the \034Other Areas: Current Quests\034 log. (While listed in quest log, the quest information incorrectly states the start NPC Epinolle is on third floor.)",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="F-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After she has given you the quest, return to Riverne - Site #B01.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the first spatial distortion at (Riverne - Site B01 (M-9)) then to the second spatial distortion at (Riverne - Site B01 (K-8)) and finally to the third spatial distortion at (Riverne - Site B01 (K-7)). This brings you to the island at (Riverne - Site B01 (J-6)).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon emerging from the third portal, the three Moblins spawn immediately:\010\010Chemical Cook Chemachiq (WHM)\010\010Book Browser Bokabraq (BLM)\010\010Spell Spitter Spiluspok (RDM)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Moblins aggro the first person who goes inside, so you may have need for a Black Mage to ES and Sleepga. All 3 Moblins build resistance to sleep quickly.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="They may take up to 5 minutes to spawn if they were recently killed by another group. Only one group of these NMs will appear at a time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the three Moblins are dead, return to Epinolle and receive a cutscene to complete the quest. There is no acknowledgement that you defeated the Moblins until you talk to Epinolle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="See the discussion page for testimonials.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57380",["title"]="Got It All",["page_title"]="Got It All",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Got_It_All",["revision"]="121430",["requirements"]="Start: Tehf Kimasnahya \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-8) / Map 1 \226\128\148 Balrahn Way, near Zabahf.\010Requirements: Access to Aht Urhgan Whitegate\010Fame: none\010Items: None\010Previous: None",["rewards"]="Bibiki Seashell",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Tehf Kimasnahya wants you to get a vial of luminous water from Ekhu Pesshyadha.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Tehf Kimasnahya on Balrahn Way at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-8) / Map 1 to begin the quest.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="F-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Ekhu Pesshyadha at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-6) / Map 1 for a cutscene.\010\010 Speaking with Ekhu Pesshyadha again at this point provides additional dialogue, but is not required to advance the quest.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="H-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Zabahf at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="F-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Ekhu Pesshyadha to receive the Key item: Vial of Luminous Water.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Tehf Kimasnahya and agree to give her the vial.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Walk through the archway on the ground floor at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-10) / Map 1, next to Hajaom, to trigger a cutscene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="J-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Tehf Kimasnahya for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After this cutscene, wait until after the next Japanese midnight (15:00 UTC) and change zones at least once.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Tehf Kimasnahya to complete the quest and receive a Bibiki Seashell.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_402",["title"]="Gourmet",["page_title"]="Gourmet",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Gourmet",["revision"]="108326",["requirements"]="Start: Salimah \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (L-8)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Sleepshroom or\010 Treant Bulb or\010Wild Onion",["rewards"]="100 - 350 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes (after changing areas)",["summary"]="Salimah is requesting one of three different items depending on the time of day.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Salimah, who will always want one of three items for her cooking.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to her daughter next to her, Rothais, or check the chart below to see which item is currently wanted.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the appropriate item to Salimah at the right hours gametime to get the higher amount of gil; trading her the item at any other time will give 100 gil. \010\010Sleepshroom: Trade during 18:00-5:59 for 200 gil \010\010Treant Bulb: Trade during 6:00-11:59 for 200 gil \010\010Wild Onion: Trade during 12:00-17:59 for 350 gil",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6853",["title"]="Grave Concerns",["page_title"]="Grave Concerns",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Grave_Concerns",["revision"]="60762",["requirements"]="Start: Andecia \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (M-7)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1",["rewards"]="560 Gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Replace the water for King Ranperre's gravestone with a fresh offering.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Andecia. She wants you to replace the offering water at the King's tomb. Speak to her again to receive the Well Water.\010\010If you drop the Well Water, you will be asked to retrieve the Tomb Waterskin from the grave, fill it at the well in Southern San d'Oria (F-6), then go back to the tomb to leave the water.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to King Ranperre's Tomb and find the tombstone at the center of the maze at (I-10) on the first map.\010\010Monsters in the tomb aggro up to level 14. Also undead are around the tomb at night so take precautions.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Well Water to the tombstone to receive the Tomb Waterskin.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Andecia and trade her the Tomb Waterskin for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_12326",["title"]="Greetings to the Guardian",["page_title"]="Greetings to the Guardian",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Greetings_to_the_Guardian",["revision"]="118698",["requirements"]="Start: Hari Pakhroib \226\128\148 Kazham (I-11)\010Requirements: Kazham Reputation 7\010Items: Wild Pamamas",["rewards"]="5,000 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Take your offering to the guardian of Kazham to the altar on the crater of Mount Yuhtunga.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Hari Pakhroib (Kazham (I-11)) to start the quest.",["zone"]="Kazham",["grid"]="I-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will need to obtain a bunch of Wild Pamamas.\010\010They drop from Opo-opos in Yuhtunga Jungle.\010\010 They can also be purchased from the Auction House under Food > Ingredients.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take your Wild Pamamas to Ifrit's Cauldron's (G-6) entrance in Yhoator Jungle. \010\010Note: Silent Oil & Prism Powder are recommended as Bombs aggro to magic and have long sensory range.\010\010Don't worry about the Ice Cluster unless you want to explore. There are no flame spouts along this path.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the first right and follow the path to tunnel C on the first map.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Then just follow that path into the second map where you will find the Altar of Ashes at (I-9).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You do not need to actually shout your name, just trade the Wild Pamamas to the altar.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Hari Pakhroib and speak with her to collect your 5k.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You may repeat this quest, but you must zone from Kazham before you can get it again. Warping to the nearby Home Point is sufficient.\010\010Upon repeating this quest you may have to obtain a Wild Melon, or Wild Pineapple.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6858",["title"]="Grimy Signposts",["page_title"]="Grimy Signposts",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Grimy_Signposts",["revision"]="60820",["requirements"]="Start: Maugie \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (L-9)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 2",["rewards"]="1500 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Maugie wants you to clean off the signposts in Jugner Forest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There are 4 signposts in Jugner Forest, located at (E-11), (G-8), (H-7), and (J-5). To clean them, just click on them, read the garbled message, then choose to clean it when given the option.\010\010Tigers, goblins, and orcs aggro by sight in Jugner Forest",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you clean all 4 signposts, return to Maugie for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7526",["title"]="Groceries",["page_title"]="Groceries",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Groceries",["revision"]="104264",["requirements"]="Start: Tami \226\128\148 Bastok Mines (J-8)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Meat Jerky",["rewards"]="Rabbit Mantle\01010 Gil",["repeatable"]="Yes, until you receive the Rabbit Mantle.",["summary"]="Hand Tami's note to her husband, Zelman, a miner in the Zeruhn Mines.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Tami at Bastok Mines (J-8).",["zone"]="Bastok Mines",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She'll give you the Key item: Tami's Note to take to her husband.\010\010Note: If you read the note, the quest is no longer repeatable.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you do not read the note:\010\010Take the note to Zelman at (Zeruhn Mines (I-8)) in Zeruhn Mines.\010\010He will tell you that he is busy and to report back to his wife.\010\010Return to Tami and get a reward of 10 gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you read the note:\010\010He asks you to go and get some Meat Jerky for him.\010\010Meat Jerky can be bought from Griselda at the Bat's Lair inn Bastok Mines.\010\010Go back to Tami and trade her the Meat Jerky and get the Rabbit Mantle reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1915",["title"]="Growing Flowers",["page_title"]="Growing Flowers",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Growing_Flowers",["revision"]="60775",["requirements"]="Start: Kuu Mohzolhi \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (F-7)\010Fame: sandoria\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Marguerite x1",["rewards"]="Exit to any area within the city from San d'Oria Mog House",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Give the tiny Mithra some flowers so she can plant them in Queen Leaute's garden.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Kuu Mohzolhi; she's obsessed with flowers and will tell you about gardening. She doesn't ask for help but she'd like to have flowers to plant in her garden. \010\010(Optional) Trade a flower to her and she'll mention Chalvatot who likes carnations, but what she really wants is a Marguerite.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Marguerite and trade it to her to complete the quest.\010Note: It is not required to talk to Kuu Mohzolhi first.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7500",["title"]="Guest of Hauteur",["page_title"]="Guest of Hauteur",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Guest_of_Hauteur",["revision"]="104200",["requirements"]="Start: Powhatan \226\128\148 Port Bastok (E-6)\010Requirements: Level 31+\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Maul or Replica Maul\010Key item: Letter from Domien\010Previous: Welcome to Bastok",["rewards"]="Targe",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Greet Powhatan's guest at the air travel agency. Wear a maul on your hip so he'll know who you are.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Powhatan.\010\010If you have just completed the previous quest Welcome to Bastok, you will have to zone before being able to start this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain and equip a Maul or Replica Maul.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Bartolomeo in the Arrivals section of the Air Travel Agency in Port Bastok with the weapon equipped; he won't even mention the passenger you're supposed to be meeting.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Powhatan again and select the second option. He suggests that you talk to the guards in the area.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Steel Bones, the guard near the Port Bastok/Bastok Markets zone, for a cutscene with the passenger and to receive a Key item: Letter from Domien.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Powhatan and talk to him to deliver the letter and complete the quest. You will receive a Targe as your reward, and you will still have your maul.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57144",["title"]="Guests of the Empire",["page_title"]="Guests of the Empire",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Guests_of_the_Empire",["revision"]="122634",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1\010Previous: Aht Urhgan Mission 16: Ghosts of the Past|Ghosts of the Past",["rewards"]="1 Imperial Mythril Piece\010Access to Salvage",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have received an invitation to the palace from the Grand Vizier. President Naja has offered to help you find appropriate clothing for the occasion.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Ghosts of the Past; this mission begins immediately afterward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Naja Salaheem in Salaheem's Sentinels at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1 for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Equip one approved body piece from the table below, along with equipment in your hands, legs, and feet slots.\010\010 Head equipment is not required.\010\010 Equipment that leaves one of the required slots empty does not satisfy the check, even if its model visually covers multiple slots.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Naja Salaheem again while wearing the required equipment.\010\010 If you were already properly dressed during the first interaction, Naja may approve your attire immediately.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Keep the approved armor equipped, but completely empty your main and sub weapon slots.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Imperial Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-8, L-9) / Map 1 for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="L-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The cutscene completes the mission, grants 1 Imperial Mythril Piece, awards the title \034Ovjang's Errand Runner,\034 unlocks access to Salvage,and begins Passing Glory.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_10184",["title"]="Gullible's Travels",["page_title"]="Gullible's Travels",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Gullible%27s_Travels",["revision"]="20120",["requirements"]="Start: Magriffon - Kazham (I-7)\010Requirements: Kazham Reputation 6\010Items: 10,000 - 30,000 gil",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Magriffon.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade him the amount of gil he asks for.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Magriffon (Kazham)\010 / summary=Magriffon has given all his worldy possessions to save a pack of poor Opo-opos from starvation. Now he needs someone to save him from getting kicked out of the bed & breakfast before he has completed his \034top-secret\034 mission.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2550",["title"]="Hat in Hand",["page_title"]="Hat in Hand",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Hat_in_Hand",["revision"]="105216",["requirements"]="Start: Baren-Moren \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (H-7) / South\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Key item: New Model Hat",["rewards"]="50 - 400 Gil\010Windshear Hat (not guaranteed)",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Advertise Baren-Moren's latest creation by chatting with the local inhabitants of Windurst Waters. He'll pay you according to the number of townsfolk you speak to. But, you are not to leave Windurst Waters before completing the task.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Baren-Moren, in the Hat shop (South Windurst Waters), wants you to show off the Key item: New Model Hat. Accept the offer and then go around and talk to the NPCs in Windurst Waters. The following NPCs say special things when you talk to them during this quest: \010\010Bondada at the hat shop (after you talk to a certain number of people)\010\010After you have talked to a certain number of NPCs, Bondada agrees to buy a hat when you talk to her again. This does not mean that you have earned the maximum reward, however.\010\010Honoi-Gomoi at Windurst Waters (E-7) / South, he is in a 2-story building you must go behind and climb up the ramp to get to.\010\010Kenapa-Keppa at the Rhinostery, Windurst Waters (J-9) / South.\010\010Clais near the Rarab's Tail, Windurst Waters (G-10) / North.\010\010Kyume-Romeh in the Timbre Timbers Tavern, Windurst Waters (F-10) / North.\010\010Tosuka-Porika in the east Optistery building, Windurst Waters (G-8) / North.\010\010Pechiru-Mashiru in the east Aurastery building, Windurst Waters (L-6) / North.\010\010Machitata near the residence area, Windurst Waters (L-11) / North.\010\010 Talking to only the mentioned NPCs will net you 175 gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You must talk to a certain number of NPCs in order to complete this quest with the maximum reward. It is unknown how many are required, but talking to all NPCs in Windurst Waters works. The eight listed above may be mandatory but are not enough by themselves to give you any reward from the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Don't leave Windurst Waters before you finish.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The more NPCs you talk to, the greater your final reward, up to a maximum of 400 gil and a Windshear Hat. (It seems that the quest is bugged - not everyone is receiving the hat as a reward.)\010\010Talking to 65 NPCs in Windurst Waters gives 200 gil and the Windshear Hat.\010\010Talking to 133 NPCs in Windurst Waters gives the maximum reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To finish the quest talk to Baren-Moren and choose \034Hang up your hat\034 to get your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Nearly all NPCs in Windurst Waters work for this quest. A few, however, do not.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2194",["title"]="Headstone Pilgrimage (Zilart Mission 5)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 5",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_5",["revision"]="120608",["requirements"]="Start: Grav'iton \226\128\148 Sacrificial Chamber\010Level: 60+\010Previous: The Temple of Uggalepih",["rewards"]="Key item: Fire Fragment\010Key item: Earth Fragment\010Key item: Water Fragment\010Key item: Wind Fragment\010Key item: Ice Fragment\010Key item: Lightning Fragment\010Key item: Light Fragment",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Somewhere on the island of Zepwell lie the remains of an ancient temple.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After defeating Zilart Mission 4, Grav'iton tells you that you need to collect eight different fragments from across Vana'diel.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To get a fragment, click on the headstone. Make sure to select yes and that you see the message that says you obtained the key item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After getting the last fragment, you will see the message You now have all 8 fragments of light!. This message triggers the beginning of the next mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Rise of the Zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2697",["title"]="Healing the Land",["page_title"]="Healing the Land",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Healing_the_Land",["revision"]="117453",["requirements"]="Start: Eperdur \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (M-7)\010Level: 10\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 4",["rewards"]="Scroll of Teleport-Holla",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Spirits of the dead in the Gusgen Mines blow an evil wind upon the land. Take a seal of banishing to a shack in the deepest tunnel within.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Eperdur on the second floor of the cathedral in Northern San d'Oria. \010\010He will tell you that there is word of a foul wind coming from the Gusgen Mines that is blowing on the Crag of Dem in Konschtat Highlands. The seal that stops the dead from walking is weakening. Eperdur gives you a Key item: Seal of Banishing.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the Gusgen Mines and follow the path straight and down some stairs until you get to the first set of three levers. Pull the center one. (You can also take the leftmost lever and hug the left wall, staying to the left all the way to the shed in (Gusgen Mines (G-8) / Map 4) using sneak and invisible as needed.)\010\010Continue on north ahead and down a second set of stairs until you get to the second set of levers. Pull the west-most lever.\010\010Simply hug the left-hand wall until you come to a hole in the ground. Cast Invisible or use your Prism Powder BEFORE dropping down the hole - it contains bombs, which aggro sight and magic. Do not forget to cast Sneak or use a Silent Oil! The flies down the hole aggro sound.\010\010Take particular note of a NM that pops once a day directly beneath the hole: Juggler Hecatomb.\010\010The ??? is behind the shed to the southwest, located at (Gusgen Mines (G-8) / Map 4). Deactivate Invisible when nothing is looking your way, check the ???, and warp out.\010\010NOTE: There are 2 sets of ??? in this room, pay attention to the location AND Make sure that you get the message: \034You have found the location of the seal. You place a Key item: Seal of Banishing on it.\034 After examining the ???, if you re-examine the ???, you will get the message: \034A Key item: Seal of Banishing is on this seal.???.\010\010Everything in this dungeon detects by sound except for the bombs at the end, which detect by sight and magic.\010\010Level 50 and above will not get aggro from normal mobs.",["zone"]="Gusgen Mines",["grid"]="G-8 / Map 4",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Eperdur for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Note: You must zone before you can be offered follow up quest, Sorcery of the North.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7503",["title"]="Hearts of Mythril",["page_title"]="Hearts of Mythril",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Hearts_of_Mythril",["revision"]="104164",["requirements"]="Start: Elki \226\128\148 Bastok Mines (H-5)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1",["rewards"]="Sitabaki",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Go to North Gustaberg and lay Elki's bouquet at the foot of the monument honoring the Palborough Pioneers.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Elki in the Bat's Lair Inn; his grandfather Omran is buried at a monument at the top of Zegham Hill in North Gustaberg. He gives you the Key item: Bouquet for the Pioneers to lay at the foot of the grave.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow the paths up to the top of Zegham Hill in North Gustaberg (J-7) to find the monument. (The path starts on the south side at I-8. Look for a grassy spot with trees.)",["zone"]="North Gustaberg",["grid"]="J-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Palborough Pioneers Monument to place the bouquet; you see the name of Elki's ancestor, Omran, and a partially readable name, Vig****t O**. This is the name of Vigilant Owl, which ties the quest The Eleventh's Hour to this one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Elki again to complete the quest. He doesn't seem to recognize the partial name but he might if you get more information.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2551",["title"]="Heaven Cent",["page_title"]="Heaven Cent",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Heaven_Cent",["revision"]="105688",["requirements"]="Start: Ropunono \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (F-7) / North\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 5\010Items: Ahriman Lens\010Rusty Key",["rewards"]="4,800 Gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The lenses of the Optistery's telescopes need replacing. It would help out the stargazers astronomically if you could focus on gathering the items they need to repair them.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="NOTE: Although both required items have the Exclusive tag, they can be delivered between characters on the same account using the Delivery Box.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you talk to Ropunono, on the roof of the Optistery, you discover that the telescope lens is going bad, and she needs to fix it. To this end, she needs an Ahriman Lens\010\010Ahriman Lens",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ahriman Lenses are Exclusive items, so you need to go farm it yourself. They drop from Ahriman in:\010\010Ranguemont Pass (there's some around H/I-6)\010\010Beaucedine Glacier\010\010Xarcabard\010\010Castle Zvahl\010\010Uleguerand Range",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have the Ahriman Lens, go back to Windurst Waters and trade it to Ropunono.\010\010Maze of Shakhrami",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Now head to the Maze of Shakhrami to fight the Wights and get a Rusty Key. This is a Rare / Exclusive item that also may take a while to get.\010\010Wights are found mostly in the deeper parts of the Maze. Specifically, if you enter Maze of Shakhrami / Map 2 through the point marked \034G\034, you will eventually come into a room filled with Wights.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you get the Rusty Key you want to head over to the area in the upper right corner of Maze of Shakhrami (J-9) / Map 2 to find a Iron Door. Trade your Rusty Key to this door.",["zone"]="Maze of Shakhrami",["grid"]="J-9 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once inside you'll find six chests (three of which will not open). The object is to find an authentic Shelling Piece in the chests which do open. It doesn't matter which chest you pick from, it just matters that you get a real Shelling Piece and not a fake.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the player has seen the correct coin from a chest, the chest will then only give the incorrect Shelling Piece.\010The way to tell if the piece is real or fake is by seeing if the direction it says the Celestial Avatar is facing is the correct direction.\010\010Alexander: North-East\010\010Garuda: South-East\010\010Ifrit: North-West\010\010Leviathan: West\010\010Odin: North\010\010Ramuh: South-West\010\010Shiva: East\010\010Titan: South\010Most of the pieces you'll pull will actually have the Avatar facing the wrong way. Just choose NOT to take that piece and open another chest or the same chest once again. Keep trying until you find a piece with the Avatar facing the right way. Take that Shelling Piece.\010\010Windurst",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back to Ropunono and trade her the Shelling Piece for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3723",["title"]="Her Majesty's Garden",["page_title"]="Her Majesty's Garden",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Her_Majesty%27s_Garden",["revision"]="99735",["requirements"]="Start: Chalvatot \226\128\148 Chateau d'Oraguille (F-7)\010Requirements: Access to Chateau d'Oraguille\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Derfland Humus",["rewards"]="Key item: Map of the Northlands Area",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Bring some Derfland humus to use as fertilizer so that flowers might grow in the late queen's garden.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Enter Chateau d'Oraguille and go to the Queen Leaute Memorial Garden (Chateau d'Oraguille (F-7)).",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Chalvatot, who is nearby. He will seem upset and not willing to help if you are not of the San d'Oria allegiance.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Chalvatot again and receive a cutscene(if you do not get the cutscene you must zone out of Chateau d'Oraguille and back in.) Accept the Quest. Default Selection is No, so make sure you're not spamming enter to skip through the dialogue.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Chalvatot a Derfland Humus to complete the quest.\010\010Derfland Humus drops from Doom Scorpions in Crawlers' Nest and can be bought and sold at the Auction House",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After another cutscene, you will receive Key item: Map of the Northlands Area.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4807",["title"]="His Name is Valgeir",["page_title"]="His Name is Valgeir",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/His_Name_is_Valgeir",["revision"]="114565",["requirements"]="Start: Rycharde\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: \226\137\165 3 [Wiki: needs verification]\010Previous: Unending Chase",["rewards"]="Map of the Toraimarai Canal",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Rycharde wants you to deliver a dish to Valgeir in Selbina, and report on how he liked it.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must wait at least two (possibly three) complete game days after the previous quest is completed to obtain this quest.\010\010For example: If you completed Unending Chase on Fire, this quest would be available on Wind after letting Earth and Water completely pass.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Rycharde gives you a Key item: Aragoneu Pizza to deliver to Valgeir in Selbina.\010\010If you decide to take the ferry, the trip is paid for by Rycharde.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Valgeir can be found at (Selbina (I-9)) inside the Shepherd's Muster.",["zone"]="Selbina",["grid"]="I-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Deliver the pizza and return back to tell Rycharde what Valgeir thinks about his food.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Reward is Map of the Toraimarai Canal",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2123",["title"]="Hitting the Marquisate",["page_title"]="Hitting the Marquisate",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Hitting_the_Marquisate",["revision"]="118726",["requirements"]="Start: Nanaa Mihgo \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (J-3)\010Requirements: Thief 50+\010Items: Quake Grenade x 4\010Previous: As Thick as Thieves",["rewards"]="Rogue's Poulaines",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="Visit two of the eight active thieves gathered by the Tenshodo, and confirm the signatures of the people who originally wrote the documents in the \034letter from the Tenshodo.\034",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Thief (THF)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Thief (THF)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Rogue's Poulaines",["revision"]="22083"},{["job"]="Thief (THF)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Hitting the Marquisate",["revision"]="118726"}}},{["id"]="wiki_2552",["title"]="Hoist the Jelly, Roger",["page_title"]="Hoist the Jelly, Roger",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Hoist_the_Jelly%2C_Roger",["revision"]="60719",["requirements"]="Start: Maysoon \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (E-9) / North\010Requirements: Start Cook's Pride quest.\010Items: Royal Jelly\010Previous: Cook's Pride",["rewards"]="Key item: Super Soup Pot",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Maysoon says she'll give you one of her super soup pots if you bring her some royal jelly.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Maysoon says she'll give you one of her Super Soup Pots if you bring her a serving of Royal Jelly.\010The Key item: Super Soup Pot is a key item needed for the quest Cook's Pride.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5941",["title"]="Hook, Line, and Sinker",["page_title"]="Hook, Line, and Sinker",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Hook%2C_Line%2C_and_Sinker",["revision"]="120716",["requirements"]="Start: Omer - Lower Jeuno (G-10)\010Requirements: Jeuno Reputation ?\010A Vessel Without a Captain\010Items: Egret Fishing Rod",["rewards"]="3000 Gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Warning: to prevent the game from freezing, you have to use its default frame rate (30 Hz) before speaking to Omer. Once this first cutscene is over, you can switch back to your preferred frame rate if you wish.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After completing Chains of Promathia Mission 3-2 \034A Vessel Without a Captain\034, talk to Omer to begin the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain an Egret Fishing Rod, which drops from Kraken (NM) fished up on Qufim Island. No skill is required to hook these.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return it to Omer to complete the quest.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Omer (Market Bridge, Lower Jeuno)\010 / summary=Help Omer retrieve his prized fishing rod that was stolen from him by an Elvaan girl. Apparently the rod was lost when she fished up a monster out on Qufim Island...]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_52124",["title"]="Hyper Active",["page_title"]="Hyper Active",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Hyper_Active",["revision"]="119948",["requirements"]="Start: Raibaht \226\128\148 Metalworks (G-8)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 4\010Previous: Teak Me to the Stars",["rewards"]="3,000 gil",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="The adventurer hired to bring Cid a hyper altimeter has been arrested and ordered to kill a monster named Orna in Delkfutt's Tower. Find the man and obtain the equipment.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="If Teak Me to the Stars was just completed, you may have to re-enter the zone or log out and back in to start the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Raibaht gives you a Key item: Molybdenum Box in which to smuggle the Key item: Hyper Altimeter through Jeuno customs once the adventurer reveals its location to you.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Delkfutt's Tower in Qufim and use the Delkfutt Key, obtained from Mission 3-3 to open the door to the basement inside level 1 at E-8.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed downstairs to basement, and head to I-6, where the passage dead ends into a cermet door.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon attempting to open the door, a message will be displayed, \034A bloodthirsty monster has appeared!\034, and the monster Orna, and two Fomorian Spear will spawn.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon defeating Orna, the two Fomorian Spears will despawn.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Attempt to open the door again and watch a cutscene with the adventurer that was sent to kill Orna. He tells you that he hid the Key item: Hyper Altimeter in one of the streetlamps in lower Jeuno.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Lower Jeuno and search the streetlamps until you find the Key item: Hyper Altimeter, which you put into the Key item: Molybdenum Box.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Bastok and talk to Raibaht to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2478",["title"]="I Can Hear a Rainbow",["page_title"]="I Can Hear a Rainbow",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/I_Can_Hear_a_Rainbow",["revision"]="119160",["requirements"]="Start: House of the Hero \226\128\148 Windurst Walls (G-3)\010Requirements: Level 30+\010Items: Carbuncle's Ruby",["rewards"]="The Summoner job\010The avatar Carbuncle",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A strange voice from within Carbuncle's Ruby is asking you to gather the seven colors of light...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Obtain Carbuncle's Ruby.\010\010This is a Rare/Exclusive item that may be obtained from nearly any type of Leech-type mob, though drop rate is incredibly low overall.\010\010The drop rate can be improved if you have Thief main/support job, with Treasure Hunter job trait.\010\010Carbuncle's Ruby cannot be delivered to other characters on the same account and therefore must be obtained on the character that wants to finish the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="With the Ruby in your inventory, go to the House of the Hero at Windurst Walls (G-3). Check the front door for a cutscene, where you will be asked to find \034the seven colors\034. Some players have reported they needed to check the door TWICE to receive the cutscene.",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="G-3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The \034seven colors\034 that are required correspond to the colors of a rainbow. They are obtained by zoning into an outdoor, enemy-populated area while one of six weather effects is active\226\128\148the seventh is obtained by zoning into an outdoor, enemy-populated area with no weather effect at all.\010\010To clarify: \034Outdoor\034 means that you may not zone into a cave or dungeon area to obtain a color.\010\010To clarify: \034Enemy-Populated\034 means that you may not zone into a town or city to obtain a color.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zoning into an area with the above requirements (that you have not yet obtained) and with the ruby in your Inventory, triggers a short cutscene upon entering the area, where Carbuncle will remark on the color of light that you have found. Note that you will not see the same cutscene again.\010\010This can be done by logging out and back into the zone.\010\010This can be done while riding a chocobo or mount.\010\010This can be done by using an outpost teleport into the zone.\010\010This can be done by teleporting into the zone (Teleport-Dem, etc).\010\010Weather Checker NPCs in each town or city can help predict when and where the weather you will be looking for will be in effect. Bear in mind, however, that these Weather Checkers are not completely accurate; some weather effects may occur on days they are not forecasted, and vice-versa.\010\010After receiving the cutscene to start the quest, the weathers can be obtained on jobs lower than level 30.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Locations of areas meeting the requirements for Carbuncle's \034colors of light\034 are as follows:\010! style=\034background:#ffdead;\034 align=\034center\034 width=\0345%\034 |Color\010! style=\034background:#ffdead;\034 align=\034center\034 width=\03414%\034 |Element\010! style=\034background:#ffdead;\034 align=\034center\034 width=\03410%\034 |Weather Type\010! style=\034background:#ffdead;\034 align=\034center\034 width=\03471%\034 |Possible Areas\010|-\010| bgcolor=\034red\034 |Red\010| bgcolor=\034#ffd9d9\034 |Fire Fire\010| bgcolor=\034#ffd9d9\034 |Heat Wave\010| bgcolor=\034#ffd9d9\034 |Valkurm Dunes, Cape Teriggan, Rolanberry Fields, Eastern Altepa Desert, Western Altepa Desert, Meriphataud Mountains, Yuhtunga Jungle, Yhoator Jungle\010|-\010| bgcolor=\034orange\034 |Orange\010| bgcolor=\034#ffe3bb\034 |(None)\010| bgcolor=\034#ffe3bb\034 |Clear Skies\010| bgcolor=\034#ffe3bb\034 |West Sarutabaruta, East Sarutabaruta, Buburimu Peninsula, Yuhtunga Jungle, Yhoator Jungle, Eastern Altepa Desert, North Gustaberg, Valkurm Dunes\010|-\010| bgcolor=\034yellow\034 |Yellow\010| bgcolor=\034#fff9bb\034 |Earth Earth\010| bgcolor=\034#fff9bb\034 |Dust Storms\010| bgcolor=\034#fff9bb\034 |Tahrongi Canyon, Sauromugue Champaign, Konschtat Highlands, Valkurm Dunes, Batallia Downs, Eastern Altepa Desert, Western Altepa Desert, Meriphataud Mountains\010|-\010| bgcolor=\034green\034 |Green\010| bgcolor=\034#daffcb\034 |Wind Wind\010| bgcolor=\034#daffcb\034 |High Winds\010| bgcolor=\034#daffcb\034 |Tahrongi Canyon, Buburimu Peninsula, La Theine Plateau, Cape Teriggan, Valley of Sorrows\010|-\010| bgcolor=\034blue\034 |Blue\010| bgcolor=\034#e3e6ff\034 |Water Water\010| bgcolor=\034#e3e6ff\034 |Rain\010| bgcolor=\034#e3e6ff\034 |La Theine Plateau, Jugner Forest, Pashhow Marshlands, Rolanberry Fields, Buburimu Peninsula, Yuhtunga Jungle, Yhoator Jungle, Sanctuary of Zi'Tah\010|-\010| bgcolor=\034indigo\034 |Indigo\010| bgcolor=\034#e3e6ff\034 |Ice Ice\010| bgcolor=\034#e3e6ff\034 |Snow\010| bgcolor=\034#e3e6ff\034 |Beaucedine Glacier, Batallia Downs, Xarcabard\010|-\010| bgcolor=\034violet\034 |Violet\010| bgcolor=\034#fdcbff\034 |Lightning Lightning\010| bgcolor=\034#fdcbff\034 |Thunderstorms\010| bgcolor=\034#fdcbff\034 |Konschtat Highlands, Sauromugue Champaign, Pashhow Marshlands, Jugner Forest, Sanctuary of Zi'Tah\010Note: Both Qufim Island and Behemoth's Dominion do NOT work for this quest, regardless of where you zone in from. Nor is Carpenters' Landing.\010|-\010\010Click Expand See Fire Weather Forecasts\010\010Valkurm Dunes\010\010Cape Teriggan\010\010Rolanberry Fields\010\010Eastern Altepa Desert\010\010Western Altepa Desert\010\010Meriphataud Mountains\010\010Yuhtunga Jungle\010\010Yhoator Jungle",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When all seven colors are obtained, you will receive an additional cutscene where Carbuncle will fly off to La Theine Plateau. Head there and go to the stone circle at (La Theine Plateau (G-6)).",["zone"]="La Theine Plateau",["grid"]="G-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Carbuncle's Ruby to the ??? at the center of the circle. After a final cutscene, the Summoner job, the avatar Carbuncle will be available to you. \010\010Each time that a player completes this quest, a rainbow (the same one as seen in the cutscene) appears over the Crag of Holla on the next Vana'diel day (so long as the weather is not rain). Should it be rainy weather, the rainbow should appear shortly after the rainy weather stops if it is before 18:00 in-game. The rainbow will appear the same Vana'diel day if you complete the summoner quest early enough in the game day.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Summoner (SMN)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Summoner (SMN)",["kind"]="Job unlock",["page"]="Summoner",["revision"]="123874"}}},{["id"]="wiki_4206",["title"]="I'll Take the Big Box",["page_title"]="I'll Take the Big Box",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/I%27ll_Take_the_Big_Box",["revision"]="119354",["requirements"]="Start: Ryoma \226\128\148 Norg (H-8)\010Requirements: Ninja 50+\010Items: Oak Pole\010Previous: 20 in Pirate Years",["rewards"]="Ninja Hakama",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="The trick box you brought back to Norg has been identified as a fake. Your assistance is required in finding the real box. Start your search by pressing Ensetsu in Bastok for more information.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="NOTE: You must zone after completing the quest 20 in Pirate Years for Ryoma to give you the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="With your main job as Ninja, speak with Ryoma Norg (H-8) in Norg who will give you the quest and tell you to track down Ensetsu Port Bastok (I-5) in Port Bastok.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ensetsu will tell of a new player in the story, Leodarion Rabao (F-7), who resides in Rabao. He will not mention his name - he will tell you to track down the grandson that used to live in a tent somewhere in Altepa Desert.",["zone"]="Rabao",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain an Oak Pole and head to Rabao.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Leodarion will ask you for the Oak Pole. Trade it to him and wait for the next game day before speaking to him again. He will then give you the Key item: Seance Staff and tell you to head to Mhaura.\010\010Leodarion will not accept an Oak Pole +1.\010\010Take note not to get an Oak Staff",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From Mhaura, board the ferry to Selbina around 16:00 or midnight (if you are boarding from Selbina, take the ferry that departs 16.00, and re-board in Mhaura).\010\010Be careful not to board the ferry to Al Zahbi by mistake. Check with the NPC to see where the ship is heading.\010\010There is a chance Pirates will spawn on the ferry.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have departed, head onto the deck and a ghost named Enagakure will spawn. \010\010Enagakure will only spawn from 20:00 to 4:00; like most Ghost type monsters.\010\010If you board the 16:00 ferry to Selbina, the NM will spawn at 20:00.\010\010Enagakure will NOT spawn on the Selbina to Mhaura ride.\010\010You do not need to be Ninja for the NM to spawn; however, you must possess the Key item: Seance Staff.\010\010Does not spawn claimed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Enagakure, and Leodarion will meet you when the ship docks for a cutscene completing the quest.\010\010If your inventory was full, you don't have to fight the NM again. Just make room in your inventory, zone out, then back into Selbina. The cutscene will play again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Ninja (NIN)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Ninja (NIN)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Ninja Hakama",["revision"]="19584"},{["job"]="Ninja (NIN)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="I'll Take the Big Box",["revision"]="119354"}}},{["id"]="wiki_51262",["title"]="Immortal Sentries",["page_title"]="Immortal Sentries",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Immortal_Sentries",["revision"]="121335",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10)\010Previous: Land of Sacred Serpents",["rewards"]="Key item: PSC Wildcat Badge\010\010 150 Imperial Standing\010\010 Mog Locker access\010\010 Sanction access",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Deliver a package to one of the Immortals found at the Staging Points and Naja will consider you for a mercenary contract.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Land of Sacred Serpents and receive the Key item: Supplies Package.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Deliver the Key item: Supplies Package to one of the five standard Assault Staging Point Immortal NPCs listed below.\010\010 Only one Staging Point delivery is required to complete this mission.\010\010 Nyzul Isle Staging Point does not count for this mission. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with the Immortal NPC inside the selected Staging Point and show the Key item: Supplies Package.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the delivery cutscene, use the local Runic Portal to return to the Chamber of Passage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Naja Salaheem at Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10).",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue to President Salaheem.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57194",["title"]="Imperial Coronation",["page_title"]="Imperial Coronation",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Imperial_Coronation",["revision"]="120935",["requirements"]="Previous: Aht Urhgan Mission 45: Ragnarok|Ragnarok",["rewards"]="Imperial Standard\010Choice of Balrahn's Ring, Ulthalam's Ring, or Jalzahn's Ring",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have been chosen to accompany President Naja to the Empress's coronation. Once you are properly attired, make your way to the palace.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Ragnarok; this mission begins during its ending cutscene in Salaheem's Sentinels.\010\010 Speaking with Naja Salaheem afterward provides additional dialogue but is not required for progression.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Equip one palace-approved body piece from the list used during Guests of the Empire, along with equipment in your Hands, Legs, and Feet slots.\010\010 Head equipment is not required.\010\010 Equipment that leaves a required slot empty does not satisfy the attire check.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Completely empty your Main and Sub equipment slots.\010\010 Remove any shield or second weapon equipped in the Sub slot.\010\010 Ranged and Ammo equipment do not need to be removed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Have 2 free inventory slots if you intend to claim both the ring and the Imperial Standard during the initial cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Imperial Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-8, L-9) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="L-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="During the cutscene, choose one of the following rewards:\010\010 Balrahn's Ring\010\010 Ulthalam's Ring\010\010 Jalzahn's Ring\010\010 You may defer the ring choice and return later.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue through the cutscene to receive the Imperial Standard, complete the mission, and begin The Empress Crowned.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Unclaimed Rewards\010\010If you deferred the ring choice or lacked sufficient inventory space:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Equip the required palace attire again and empty your Main and Sub slots.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Imperial Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-8, L-9) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="L-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select any unclaimed ring or receive the missing Imperial Standard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57121",["title"]="Imperial Schemes",["page_title"]="Imperial Schemes",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Imperial_Schemes",["revision"]="121667",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1)\010Previous: Astral Waves",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The reward from the A.A.R.I. has been confiscated by President Naja to cover your \034fines.\034 The mercenary life is no picnic...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After completing Astral Waves, zone once and wait until the next Vana'diel day.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the first platform of Salaheem's Sentinels in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1 for a cutscene that completes the mission and advances you to Royal Puppeteer.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2553",["title"]="In a Pickle",["page_title"]="In a Pickle",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/In_a_Pickle",["revision"]="60744",["requirements"]="Start: Chamama \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (F-10) / North\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Smooth Stone",["rewards"]="200 Gil\010Bone Hairpin",["repeatable"]="yes",["summary"]="The weighting stone used to make the Rarab Tail Hostelry's specialty dish, \034Rarab Tail Pickles\034, was broken. Chamama wants you to find her a replacement stone that is just the right size, shape, and weight.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Chamama in the Rarab Tail Hostelry at Windurst Waters (F-10) / North.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="F-10 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She will ask you to find her a replacement stone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Crawlers in East Sarutabaruta or West Sarutabaruta until one drops a smooth stone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the smooth stone to Chamama.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="One of two things may happen:\010\010She will tell you that the stone is no good. You will have to bring her another stone to get your reward and complete the quest.\010\010She will take the stone and give you your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2115",["title"]="In a Stew",["page_title"]="In a Stew",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/In_a_Stew",["revision"]="56783",["requirements"]="Start: Kuoh Rhel \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (K-12)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Woozyshroom x3\010Previous: Chocobilious",["rewards"]="900 gil",["repeatable"]="weekly",["summary"]="Kuoh tried to feed the sick Chocobo some \034secret cure-all medicament,\034 but it wouldn't swallow it. She wants to try and hide the taste by mixing it in some of the bird's favorite food, if you can help obtain some...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1771",["title"]="In Defiant Challenge",["page_title"]="In Defiant Challenge",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/In_Defiant_Challenge",["revision"]="118262",["requirements"]="Start: Maat \226\128\148 Ru'Lude Gardens (H-5)\010Level: 50\010Items: Bomb Coal\010Exoray Mold\010Ancient Papyrus",["rewards"]="Raises Level Cap to 55\010Mog Wardrobe: 5 Slots [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Apparently, your innate limits can be breached by acquiring the necessary items.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Maat asks you to collect three items. Trade them to him for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bomb Coal",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bomb Coal drops from Explosures in Garlaige Citadel. \010\010Droprate seems to be around 25%-50%, depending on your Treasure Hunter. [Horizon change] [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Explosures can be found at Garlaige Citadel (I-8) / Map 2, which requires passing through the First Banishing Gate.",["zone"]="Garlaige Citadel",["grid"]="I-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exoray Mold",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exoray Mold drops from Exorays in Crawlers' Nest. \010\010Droprate seems to be around 25%-50%, depending on your Treasure Hunter. [Horizon change] [Wiki: needs verification] \010\010Exorays can be used for exp parties.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exorays are located throughout the Crawlers' Nest (G-7) / Map 3, or at Crawlers' Nest (I-7) / Map 2 and Crawlers' Nest (G-9) / Map 2 of the Crawlers' Nest / Map 2",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exorays have two dangerous, status effect inflicting attacks:\010\010a wind-based conal AOE attack called Silence Gas which inflicts silence. It is highly recommended to have someone with Silena in the group and that the tank faces the Exoray away from the mages at all times. To be safe, bring Echo Drops because mistakes happen. \010\010an ice-based radial AOE attack called Spore which inflicts paralysis. It is recommended that mages use White Mage as their subjob for Paralyna.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ancient Papyrus",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ancient Papyrus drops from Lichs in The Eldieme Necropolis.\010\010Droprate seems to be around 25%-50%, depending on your Treasure Hunter. [Horizon change] [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There are three places where you can find Lichs:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter The Eldieme Necropolis through Batallia Downs (F-5). \010\010This entrance can only be reached by going through Beaucedine Glacier (H-11).",["zone"]="Batallia Downs",["grid"]="F-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter The Eldieme Necropolis through Batallia Downs (I-10).\010\010You can find Lich on the first level as you travel around although spawns are sparse.",["zone"]="Batallia Downs",["grid"]="I-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Human Bones Room) Enter The Eldieme Necropolis through Batallia Downs (I-10).\010\010You will need 2 or more members of the party to control the plates that open doors.\010\010Head through the center doors, and go down hole marked A at The Eldieme Necropolis (G-8). \010\010Once you land, head east and you'll quickly reach the room with the Human Bones at The Eldieme Necropolis (M-10) / Map 2. \010\010There are 2 to 4 Lichs available for pulling. \010\010Warning: Elemental danger: If you don't want to aggro elementals, you may camp in the large staircase between the Ka room and Lich room, but you will have to pull the Fallen Knights or Carby/jug pull the Lichs under the effect of sneak.",["zone"]="Batallia Downs",["grid"]="I-10",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_53503",["title"]="In Search of the Truth",["page_title"]="In Search of the Truth",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/In_Search_of_the_Truth",["revision"]="118462",["requirements"]="Start: Tressia \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold (J-6) / Map 2\010Requirements: Promathia Mission 3-5: Darkness Named completed\010Items: Key item: Shaded Cruse",["rewards"]="Gramary Cape",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Search for information regarding what happened on the day Wazozo's treasure was stolen.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Tressia (top floor at Tavnazian Safehold (J-6) / Map 2) to start the quest.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="J-6 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Raminey (Tavnazian Safehold (J-7) / Map 2) and Fouagine (Tavnazian Safehold (I-8) / Map 2) on the top floor(at the bottome left of I-8), and Zadant (Tavnazian Safehold (H-9) / Map 1) and Noam (Tavnazian Safehold (G-9) / Map 1) on the main floor to get four witness accounts.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Tressia will then ask you to put them in order (you get as many tries as you need). The order is Fouagine, Zadant, Noam, Raminey.\010\010Quest may vary in the order in which you present the accounts. One player's order was Fouagine, Zadant, Raminey, and then Noam.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk with Mengrenaux and Chemioue (both near Tressia) and view all 4 reports, then talk to Tressia again and give the locations of the witnesses in order. The correct order is: I-8, H-8, G-9, and J-7.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On the main floor, go to G-9 down by the Tributary and examine the ??? to find a Key item: Shaded Cruse.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From G-9, start walking toward the Breakaway Bridge in the middle of the Safehold. Along the way, examine the ???s at G-7 (near Nilerouche), G-8, and H-8 (where there are two).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you reach the Breakaway Bridge and select the fifth and final ???, you will see a cutscene that explains the mystery. At the end of this cutscene the victory fanfare plays and the quest is considered complete.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Tressia, and then to Ondieulix at the entrance (Tavnazian Safehold (I-7) / Map 1, main floor), for your reward.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="I-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57162",["title"]="In the Blood",["page_title"]="In the Blood",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/In_the_Blood",["revision"]="120868",["requirements"]="Start: Razfahd \226\128\148 Dvucca Isle Staging Point, Caedarva Mire (I-9) / Map 2\010Previous: Shades of Vengeance",["rewards"]="1 Imperial Gold Piece",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The true identity of the court puppetmaster has been revealed. However, the Grand Vizier has ordered you to return to Al Zahbi and report the completion of your mission to President Naja.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Shades of Vengeance; this mission begins during its post-battle cutscene after returning to Caedarva Mire.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Salaheem's Sentinels in Aht Urhgan Whitegate and speak with Naja Salaheem at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The resulting cutscene completes the mission, grants 1 Imperial Gold Piece, and begins Sentinels' Honor.\010\010 To continue Sentinels' Honor, zone once and wait until after the next Japanese midnight (15:00 UTC).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5942",["title"]="In the Mood for Love",["page_title"]="In the Mood for Love",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/In_the_Mood_for_Love",["revision"]="10153",["requirements"]="Start: Odasel - Lower Jeuno (H-9)\010Requirements: Chains of Promathia Mission 3-2: A Vessel Without a Captain\010Items: Chameleon Diamond",["rewards"]="4800 Gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Odasel is standing on the 2nd floor of Lower Jeuno in front of \034Gems by Kshama\034.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Odasel a Chameleon Diamond to complete the quest.\010\010Chameleon Diamonds will drop from Gigas in Lufaise Meadows.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Matoaka for a further cutscene (optional).\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Odasel (Gems by Kshama, Lower Jeuno)\010 / summary=Odasel wants to find out which of the three beauties in the gem store has feelings for him. According to a passing Elvaan girl, a jewel known as the \034Chameleon Diamond\034 could help solve his dilemma...]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6543",["title"]="In the Name of Science",["page_title"]="In the Name of Science",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/In_the_Name_of_Science",["revision"]="121168",["requirements"]="Start: Yurim \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold (J-8) / Map 2, upstairs\010Requirements: Al'Taieu access\010Items: See Items",["rewards"]="See Rewards",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Yurim wants to show you the fruits of her research, but lacks the materials to begin the final stage of the experiment. You know what you have to do!",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk with Yurim to start the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Decide which of the final rewards you wish to obtain (see chart below).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Yurim the proper \034base\034 item and colored chip.\010\010IMPORTANT: Once the \034base\034 item and colored chip are traded, you are committed to that item and can not get another until that is complete. For this reason, it is recommended that you not trade the first items until you have all of the organs at hand as well.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk further with Yurim, for information on her research.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade an Apple Pie to Yurim (optional), for more hints on how to finish the research steps.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Al'Taieu and obtain the necessary items as shown in the chart below.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Tavnazian Safehold and trade the organs (all at once) to Yurim to receive your reward and complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6935",["title"]="Indomitable Spirit",["page_title"]="Indomitable Spirit",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Indomitable_Spirit",["revision"]="65569",["requirements"]="Start: Irmilant - Rabao (G-7)\010Requirements: Fishing Skill 78+\010Key item: Serpent Rumors\010Items: Lik\010Gugrusaurus\010Saber Shoot\010Opal Silk\010Previous: Inside the Belly",["rewards"]="Ebisu Fishing Rod",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Irmilant has asked you to bring the two base materials required to craft a legendary fishing rod. These materials seem to have found their way into the bellies of sea creatures that still elude the finest fishermen.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Irmilant to start the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He requests a Saber Shoot and Opal Silk, which can be obtained through the Inside the Belly quest.\010\010Saber Shoot can be obtained by trading Gugrusaurus to Zaldon. The rate at which Zaldon gives out Saber Shoots is rumored to be between 0.5% and 2%\010\010Gugrusaurus bite on the Ferry - Mhaura/Selbina during pirate attacks, on the Manaclipper during the part the routes to and from Purgonorgo Isle that are closest to Purgonorgo Isle[Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 , as well as on the Ferry - Mhaura/Al Zahbi (no special requirements for this ferry)].\010\010Gugrusaurus bite on Meatball and Drill Calamary. Drill Calamary can be obtained by trading Sea Zombies to Zaldon (approximately 25% of Sea Zombies will yield a Drill Calamary). Occasionally the Pirate's Chart Quest will also yield a Drill Calamary.\010\010When hooked with a Meatball, Gugrusaurus will only stay on the hook for a very short period of time unless the fisherman has the effect of an Albatross Ring active. Drill Calamary does not suffer this penalty.\010\010Opal Silk can be obtained by trading a Lik to Zaldon. Approximately 0.5% to 2% of Lik traded will yield an Opal Silk.\010\010Lik can be caught in Leremieu Lagoon in Lufaise Meadows.\010\010Lik bite on Minnow and Dwarf Pugil. Dwarf Pugils can be obtained by trading a Cave Cherax to Zaldon (approximately 25% of Cave Cheraxes will yield a Dwarf Pugil). \010\010Lik will stay on the hook for a shorter period of time when hooked with a Minnow than when hooked with a Dwarf Pugil; however, the difference is not as pronounced as with the two Gugrusaurus baits.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Saber Shoot and Opal Silk to Irmilant.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return after Conquest tally and talk to Irmilant to end the quest, and receive your reward. \010\010Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Fishing Guild Point key item Serpent Rumors is required to start the quest as well as hook and catch Gugrusaurus and Lik.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Mooching key item will extend the time that the fish will stay on the hook when a live bait (Drill Calamary or Dwarf Pugil) is used.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Albatross Rings are highly recommended to extend the time that the fish will stay on the hook, especially in the case of Gugrusaurus.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Level 78 Fishing is required in order to get the Serpent Rumors key item, so that is the absolute minimum level; however, fishers lower than level 90 fishing will have a very difficult time reeling in the fish necessary for the quest. Close to level 100 fishing is highly recommended.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will break your rod a lot trying to catch these fish, please consider either raising woodworking or bringing a woodworking mule along for repairs. Please also be aware that you will lose your rod if you are repairing it when the Ferry docks.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_367",["title"]="Infiltrate Davoi (San d'Oria Mission 3-1)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 3-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_3-1",["revision"]="101299",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 2-3|Journey Abroad",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="The scout in Davoi needs the help of an adventurer.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 6 Crystal's to the Conquest NPC to unlock the mission then accept it from the Gate Guard.\010\010You may also repeat other missions to unlock it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Prince Trion who can be reached by clicking on the door at Chateau d'Oraguille (G-7, H-7) of Chateau d'Oraguille for a cutscene. It is the room on the North side of the court yard.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="G-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to Davoi.\010\010Follow the right wall of Jugner Forest to the zone into Davoi at (Jugner Forest (G-12)).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Davoi for a cutscene.\010\010Invisible is recommended for this mission, bring Prism Powders or have a spell for Invisiblity.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Quemaricond when it is safe to drop Invisibility. You will obtainKey item: Royal Knights' Davoi report.\010\010He is the patrolling NPC at (Davoi (H-7)).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Prince Trion to complete the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3714",["title"]="Inheritance",["page_title"]="Inheritance",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Inheritance",["revision"]="104259",["requirements"]="Start: Gumbah \226\128\148 Bastok Mines (J-7)\010Requirements: Level 71 minimum\010Great Sword skill 250 minimum\010No other WSNM quest active",["rewards"]="Unlocks Ground Strike",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Gumbah has received a letter from the Dark Knight, Zeid. This correspondence states that to prevent Werei's technique from fading into oblivion, we are to train with a certain sword the great warrior left behind.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Gumbah in Bastok Mines (J-7) who will give you the Sword of Trials and the Key item: Weapon Training Guide.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the Sword of Trials until the latent effect disappears.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="How to remove the latent effect: \010\010You must perform Weapon Skills and Skillchains on monsters that con Easy Prey or higher.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Weapon Skills performed while under Level Sync will count.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You receive 1 point for opening/soloing a weaponskill, 2 points for closing a Lv.1 Skillchain, 3 points for closing a Lv.2 Skillchain and 5 points for closing a level 3 Skillchain.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You must accumulate 300 total points.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To check to see if the latent effect has disappeared, simply check your equipment menu stats. If the latent effects aren't there anymore, you are done (it is unnecessary to unequip and reequip the weapon).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you no longer receive the latent effect bonus, head back to Bastok Mines and trade the Sword of Trials back to Gumbah, who will take the weapon from you and give you a Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth and tell you to head to Western Altepa Desert.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to (E-9) and touch the ??? there to spawn the NM tiger Maharaja.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the NM is dead, re-examine the ??? to obtain the Key item: Annals of Truth.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring this back to Gumbah for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4800",["title"]="Inside the Belly",["page_title"]="Inside the Belly",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Inside_the_Belly",["revision"]="122569",["requirements"]="Start: Zaldon \226\128\148 Selbina (H-9) inside Fishermen's Guild (Selbina)\010Requirements: Minimum of 30 Fishing Skill (does not include gear and synthesis support bonuses)\010Items: Various fish (see below).\010Previous: The Real Gift",["rewards"]="Varies; see below\010Notable:\010Brigand's Chart (from Bhefhel Marlin)\010Pirate's Chart (from Bhefhel Marlin)\010Saber Shoot (from Gugrusaurus)\010Opal Silk (from Lik)",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Zaldon with a natural fishing skill of 30 or above to begin the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If there is an item in the fish he'll give it to you and he'll give you some gil for compensation for taking the fish. \010\010Some of these items are used in the quests Indomitable Spirit, Brigand's Chart, and Pirate's Chart.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When questing the Ebisu Fishing Rod you DO NOT have to have the Key item: Serpent Rumors prior to getting your items. You do, however, have to have Serpent Rumors in order to catch the Lik and Gugrusaurus. And to start Indomitable Spirit to get the Ebisu Fishing Rod.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Fish List\010\010Those listed with Skill 100 and above are considered \034legendary\034 fish.\010\010! Fish !!Skill !!Gil Reward !!Possible Item(s)\010|- class=\034wotg\034\010|Abaia\010|100\010|960 gil\010|1x Aurora Bass[Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010\0102x Aurora Bass[Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010\0103x Aurora Bass[Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010\010Plumb Boots[Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|- class=\034toau\034\010|Ahtapot\010|90\010|350 gil\010|Decayed Ingot [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010\010Mildewy Ingot [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010\010|- class=\034soa\034\010|Apkallufa\010|75\010|95 gil\010|Ice Spikes [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|-\010|Bhefhel Marlin\010|61\010|150 gil\010|Brigand's Chart [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010 Pirate's Chart [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|-\010|Bladefish\010|71\010|200 gil\010|Robber Rig [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-class=\034soa\034\010|Bloodblotch\010| 82\010| 165 gil\010|Confectioner's Ring [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010Venom Dust [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034soa\034\010|Bonefish\010| 30\010| ?? gil\010|Skeleton Key (up to 4) [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Cave Cherax\010|100\010|800 gil\010|Dwarf Pugil [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034abyssea\034\010|Crocodilos\010|100\010|1763 gil\010|Puffin Ring [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Dark Bass\010|33\010|10 gil\010|Green Rock [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034abyssea\034\010|Dorado Gar\010|?\010|568 gil\010|Gold Ingot (between 1-4) [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Emperor Fish\010|94\010|300 gil\010|Cuir Highboots [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|- class=\034rov\034\010|Far East Puffer\010|110+\010|735 gil\010|Stinky Subligar [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Gavial Fish\010|81\010|250 gil\010|Drone Earring [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034wotg\034\010|Gerrothorax\010|100\010|423 gil\010|Risky Patch [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- \010|Giant Catfish\010|31\010|50 gil\010|Earth Wand [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010 Title: Cordon Bleu Fisher\010|-\010|Giant Chirai\010|100\010|550 gil\010|Twinthread [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Giant Donko\010|49\010|96 gil\010|Broken Halcyon Rod [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034wotg\034\010|Gigant Octopus\010|80\010|119 gil\010|Black Ink (between 1-6) [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Gigant Squid\010|91\010|300 gil\010|Flame Shield [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Grimmonite\010|90\010|350 gil\010|Gold Ring [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010 Silver Ring [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010 Mythril Ring [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Gugrusaurus\010|110+\010|880 gil\010|Saber Shoot [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 23 / 5148]\010|-\010|Gugru Tuna\010|41\010|50 gil\010|Tiny Tathlum [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034wotg\034\010|Hakuryu\010|110+\010|1512 gil\010|Hakuryu's Liver [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034toau\034\010|Istavrit\010|40\010|50 gil\010|Venom Dust (between 1-6) [Wiki: needs verification] [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Jungle Catfish\010|80\010|300 gil\010|Broken Hume Rod [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034toau\034\010|Kalkanbaligi\010|100\010|390 gil\010|Flat Shield [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034toau\034\010|Kilicbaligi\010|61\010|150 gil\010|Rusty Greatsword [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034abyssea\034\010|Kokuryu\010|110+\010|1512 gil\010|Kokuryu's Liver [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034toau\034\010|Lakerda\010|41\010|51 gil\010|Pearl [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010 Black Pearl [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Lik\010|110+\010|880 gil\010|Opal Silk [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 32 / 5222]\010|- class=\034soa\034\010|Malicious Perch\010| 66\010| 483 gil\010|Patissiere's Ring [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010Venom Dust [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034wotg\034\010|Matsya\010|110+\010|12592 gil\010|Shaper's Shawl [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034wotg\034\010|Megalodon\010|93\010|532 gil\010|Broken Mithran Rod [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010\010Mithran Fishing Rod [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034toau\034\010|Mola Mola\010|110+\010|487 gil\010|Mercurial Spear [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Monke-Onke\010|51\010|150 gil\010|Poison Dust (between 1-6) [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034toau\034\010|Morinabaligi\010|94\010|300gil\010|Cuir Gloves [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Ogre Eel\010|35\010|16 gil\010|Turquoise Ring [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034abyssea\034\010|Pelazoea\010|100\010|360 gil\010|Noddy Ring [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034wotg\034\010|Pirarucu\010|89\010|516 gil\010|Wyvern Skin [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010 Peiste Skin [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034toau\034\010|Pterygotus\010|99\010|390 gil\010|Lapis Lazuli [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034toau\034\010|Rhinochimera\010|72\010|300 gil\010|Solon Torque [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Ryugu Titan\010|100\010|800gil\010|Mercurial Sword [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Sea Zombie\010|100\010|350 gil\010|Drill Calamary [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034abyssea\034\010|Sekiryu\010|110+\010|1512 gil\010|Sekiryu's Liver [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034soa\034\010|Shen\010|110+\010|1280 gil\010|Riftdross [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010Riftcinder [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Silver Shark\010|76\010|250 gil\010|Trident [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010 Title: Ace Angler\010|- class=\034abyssea\034\010|Soryu\010|110+\010|1512 gil\010|Soryu's Liver [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Takitaro\010|100\010|350 gil\010|Philosopher's Stone [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Three-eyed Fish\010|81\010|250 gil\010|Paralysis Dust (between 1-10) [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034abyssea\034\010|Tiger Shark\010|\010|\010|Duck Ring [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Titanic Sawfish\010|100\010|810 gil\010|Aizenkunitoshi [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Titanictus\010|100\010|350 gil\010|Ancient Sword [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010 Seashell [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] [Wiki: needs verification] \010Title: Lu Shang-like Fisher King\010|- class=\034toau\034\010|Tricorn\010|100\010|810 gil\010|Darksteel Ore [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034toau\034\010|Turnabaligi\010|100\010|340 gil\010|Dark Ore [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010 Ice Ore [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010 Water Ore [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034toau\034\010|Veydal Wrasse\010|52\010|225 gil\010|Nebimonite [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0] \010 Seashell [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034soa\034\010|Yawning Catfish\010| 64\010| 300 gil\010|Seabird's Ring [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- class=\034toau\034\010|Yayinbaligi\010|31\010|50 gil\010|Telluric Ring [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Zafmlug Bass\010|48\010|15 gil\010|Blue Rock [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010<!--",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Drop Rates While Keeping Charts\010\010It is wellknown that if you store either a Pirate's Chart or a Brigand's Chart in your inventory and continue trading Zaldon marlins that you will eventually receive the other chart from him. What is not known is whether this affects the drop rate of the second chart. Obviously, the game must check your inventory in order to know that you are holding the chart. Thus, there are two possibilities:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The game checks your inventory, sees that you are holding a chart, then gives you the other one. In this case, the drop rate of the chart when holding should be equal to the combined drop rates for both charts when not holding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The game checks your inventory, sees that you are holding a chart, then drops the chart without informing you. In other words, the drop rates for the charts are independent of each other. In this case, the drop rate when holding a chart will be equal to the drop rate of the chart when not holding.\010Clearly, the first case is preferable. It would mean that players can hold on to a chart without fear that they are silently missing out on obtaining more. The way to determine which is happening is to also keep track of drop rates when holding charts. A preliminary study posted on Titanictus.com showed that the drop rate when holding is equal to the drop rate when not holding, meaning the second case is how the game actually works. The sample size of that experiment was too small to be conclusive though.\010\010If you trade marlins without holding on to a chart, please post those drop rates in the table above. If, however, you trade marlins to Zaldon while holding a chart in your inventory, please post the drop rates below.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Pirate's Chart (While holding a Brigand's Chart in your inventory) - [Template Drop Rate: 114 / 2546]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Brigand's Chart (While holding a Pirate's Chart in your inventory) - [Template Drop Rate: 77 / 2590]\010<!--",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2516",["title"]="Inspector's Gadget!",["page_title"]="Inspector's Gadget!",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Inspector%27s_Gadget%21",["revision"]="105299",["requirements"]="Start: Kohlo-Lakolo \226\128\148 Port Windurst (G-5)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Saruta Cotton x4\010Previous: Know One's Onions",["rewards"]="Heko Obi",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The Mana Orb the Star Onion Brigade \034confiscated\034 from the Cat Burglar has gone missing. In order to track down the culprit, the gang will need the seven gadgets found in the Junior Investigator's toolkit! Pichichi will tell you what to bring.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Kohlo-Lakolo. In a cutscene he will tell you that each member of the Onion Brigade must bring one gadget from the Junior Investigator\226\128\153s Toolkit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Pichichi. She notices your confusion and suggests that you speak with her mother, Chamama in Windurst Waters (F-10) / North, inside the Rarab Tail Hostelry.\010\010(Optional) Speak with each child for additional humorous dialogue.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="F-10 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Chamama needs you to collect 4 balls of Saruta Cotton.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the 4 balls of Saruta Cotton to her and she will give you a Key item: Fake Moustache to take back to Kohlo-Lakolo.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3725",["title"]="Intermediate Teamwork",["page_title"]="Intermediate Teamwork",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Intermediate_Teamwork",["revision"]="122748",["requirements"]="Start: Vilatroire \226\128\148 West Ronfaure (H-5)\010Level: None\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 3\010Previous: Introduction To Teamwork",["rewards"]="Scroll of Mage's Ballad",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="In order to form a cohesive party, gather adventurers of the same race.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Vilatroire in the Watchtower, accessed from Northern San d'Oria (C-7).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Form a party of 6 people of the same Race, then talk to him again to complete the quest. All party members must be in the Watchtower area.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="No level requirement for completing this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To quickly gain the Bastok or San d'Oria fame needed for an alt Character to be able to accept this quest you can trade 3 stacks of Millioncorn as part of the quest Only the Best see also: Quick Reputation",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7428",["title"]="Introduction To Teamwork",["page_title"]="Introduction To Teamwork",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Introduction_To_Teamwork",["revision"]="121303",["requirements"]="Start: Vilatroire \226\128\148 West Ronfaure (H-5)\010Level: 10 [Wiki: needs verification]\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 2",["rewards"]="Shell Ring",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="In order to form a cohesive party, gather adventurers of the same allegiance.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Vilatroire in the Watchtower, accessed from Northern San d'Oria (C-7).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Form a party of 6 people from the same nation, then talk to him again to complete the quest. All party members must be in the Watchtower area.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is NOT a restriction of level 10 on all party members to be able to complete this quest. The level restriction is only to accept the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_11985",["title"]="It's Not Your Vault",["page_title"]="It's Not Your Vault",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/It%27s_Not_Your_Vault",["revision"]="121199",["requirements"]="Start: Keal \226\128\148 Norg (H-8)\010Requirements: Job level 5+\010Fame: Tenshodo\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Key item: Sealed Iron Box",["rewards"]="Scroll of Tonko: Ichi",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Bring back a sealed iron box from the Sahagin-infested Norg vault.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Keal at (Norg (H-8)) to start the quest.\010\010You may have to speak to him twice to engage the quest.",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exit Norg (Sea Serpent Grotto (F-3) / Map 1) and make your way to the door marked (Sea Serpent Grotto (H-6) / Map 1).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Turn right and head to the door marked (Sea Serpent Grotto (C-8) / Map 1); then continue to the door at (Sea Serpent Grotto (C-6) / Map 1).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You should now be in a room with a boarded floor. Examine the ??? (Sea Serpent Grotto (C-5) / Map 1) in the room to receive a Key item: Sealed Iron Box.",["zone"]="Sea Serpent Grotto",["grid"]="C-5 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Norg (or, if your Homepoint is set at Norg, just Warp or get KO'd) and talk to Keal to receive Tonko: Ichi",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Alternate Map.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Every monster in this area detects by sound, so some form of Sneak is needed if your level is low. Silent Oils work.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Invisible is not necessary.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Tenshodo",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_20628",["title"]="It's Raining Mannequins",["page_title"]="It's Raining Mannequins",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/It%27s_Raining_Mannequins",["revision"]="115600",["requirements"]="Start: Fyi Chalmwoh \226\128\148 Mhaura (G-8)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Mannequin Head\010Mannequin Body\010Mannequin Hands\010Mannequin Legs\010Mannequin Feet\010Key item: Ye Olde Mannequin Catalogue\010Key item: Mannequin Joint Diagrams",["rewards"]="One of the following:\010Elvaan F Mannequin\010Elvaan M Mannequin\010Galka Mannequin\010Hume F Mannequin\010Hume M Mannequin\010Mithra Mannequin\010Tarutaru F Mannequin\010Tarutaru M Mannequin",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Fyi Chalmwoh at Mhaura (G-8) in Mhaura (in the Goldsmithing shop).",["zone"]="Mhaura",["grid"]="G-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once finished, talk to her again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Selbina",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Now go to Selbina (catching the boat is the easiest way!) and talk to Ramona at Selbina (H-9) in the Weaver's shop. She'll give you Key item: Ye Olde Mannequin Catalogue.",["zone"]="Selbina",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="San d'Oria",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Now go to Northern San d'Oria and talk to Cheupirudaux at Northern San d'Oria (F-3) in front of the Woodworking Guild. He'll give you Key item: Mannequin Joint Diagrams.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="F-3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Body Parts",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Now you need to collect all 5 of the mannequin parts. You can either get them from the source, or buy them from bazaars and through trades. They can not be sold through the Auction House. Click on the link to find out how to get the part:\010\010Mannequin Head\010\010Mannequin Body\010\010Mannequin Hands\010\010Mannequin Legs\010\010Mannequin Feet",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Put it Together",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Now go back to Mhaura and trade all 5 pieces to Fyi Chalmwoh. You have to wait until midnight JST to get it back from her.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She will give you the mannequin that is the same Race and gender as your character. If you want a different mannequin then trade the one that you have back to Fyi Chalmwoh and she'll let you choose another one for 10,000 gil. (Note: You must complete all three quests from this quest line to change the race and gender of your mannequin.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_329",["title"]="Jeuno (Bastok Mission 3-3)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 3-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_3-3",["revision"]="29081",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 3-2|To the Forsaken Mines",["rewards"]="Rank 4\0105,000 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You are to be sent to work for the Embassy of Bastok in Jeuno. First obtain a letter of recommendation from the Presidential Aide, Sir Lucius.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to a Bastok Gate Guard to accept this mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Lucius in Metalworks (J-9), located at the Presidential Aide's Office, to receive the Key item: Letter to the Ambassador.",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="J-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Jeuno and talk to Goggehn in Ru'Lude Gardens (H-10) in the Bastokan Embassy (Jeuno).",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="H-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Lower Delkfutt's Tower.\010\010If you do not possess a Key item: Delkfutt Key or Delkfutt Key (Item), you need to obtain one for the next step, see Obtaining a Delkfutt Key.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Lower Delkfutt's Tower (E-8) / First Floor and either trade Delkfutt Key (Item) to the cermet door or simply interact with the door if in possession of Key item: Delkfutt Key. \010\010If you just obtained a Delkfutt Key (Item), trade it to the elevator ??? in the room Upper Delkfutt's Tower (H-8) / Floor 10 where Porphyrion spawns and proceed taking the spiral staircase downwards until you reach Lower Delkfutt's Tower (H-8) / Basement.",["zone"]="Lower Delkfutt's Tower",["grid"]="E-8 / First Floor",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in the basement, head east into the large room interact with the door at Lower Delkfutt's Tower (L-9) / Basement for a cutscene. \010\010If you still have your Delkfutt Key (Item), trade it to the door to receive the cutscene. \010\010If you do not get the cutscene you are probably at the wrong door.",["zone"]="Lower Delkfutt's Tower",["grid"]="L-9 / Basement",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene, return to the Bastokan Embassy (Jeuno) in Ru'Lude Gardens and interact with the door to the ambassador's office at Ru'Lude Gardens (H-10) to finish the mission.",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="H-10",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_366",["title"]="Journey Abroad (San d'Oria Mission 2-3)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 2-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_2-3",["revision"]="123666",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Level: 25 (recommended)\010Items: Parana Shield (Windurst Path) or Mythril Sand (Bastok Path)\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 2-2|The Davoi Report",["rewards"]="Rank 3\0103,000 gil\01010 Mog Wardrobe [Horizon change] \010Outpost Teleportation from Jeuno [Horizon change] \010Key item: Adventurer's Certificate",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Visit the faraway nations of Bastok and Windurst and receive official recognition as an adventurer.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5916",["title"]="Kazham Airship Pass",["page_title"]="Kazham Airship Pass",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Kazham_Airship_Pass",["revision"]="113979",["requirements"]="Start: Guddal \226\128\148 Port Jeuno (I-7)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Giddeus Chest Key\010Ghelsba Chest Key\010Palborough Chest Key",["rewards"]="Key item: Airship pass for Kazham[Conditional wiki content: soa \226\128\148 ,\010Unlocks Key item: Kazham warp rune and Key item: Norg warp rune for purchase]",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You have 2 options when you first talk to Guddal: pay 148,000g or take the \034Adventurer's Deal\034 (do a quest). \010\010Note: If you back out of the dialog before selecting one of the two options, this may glitch his conversation, so that talking to Guddal again doesn't ask which option you want to choose. Zoning will reset this glitch, and allow you to select the option normally.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The quest requires you to collect a Giddeus Chest Key, Ghelsba Chest Key, and Palborough Chest Key. \010\010Giddeus Chest Key drops from Yagudo Priest, Yagudo Votary, and Yagudo Theologist in Giddeus. \010\010Ghelsba Chest Key drops from Orcish Fighter, Orcish Serjeant, and Orcish Cursemaker in Yughott Grotto or Fort Ghelsba. \010\010Palborough Chest Key drops from Old Quadav, Brass Quadav, Copper Quadav, Mine Scorpion [Wiki: needs verification] and Scimitar Scorpion in Palborough Mines.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once all three chest keys are obtained, trade them to Guddal for the Key item: Airship pass for Kazham.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Location",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Giddeus: Stay to the right and make your way to the cave at (G-7). Head left after you enter and drop down the hole concealed by bramble Giddeus (H-7) / Ground Level. Head south outside the tunnel and follow the path all the way to the bottom of the map, taking care to not fall down. Giddeus (G-12) / Ground Level.",["zone"]="Giddeus",["grid"]="H-7 / Ground Level",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ghelsba Outpost: Hang left after you enter and zone into Yughott Grotto. Go through the Grotto until Yughott Grotto (I-6).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Palborough Mines: Take the elevator at Palborough Mines (I-8) / Map 1 (approach from the east side) to the third floor and make your way to the area just before Waughroon Shrine. Palborough Mines (G-9, G-10, H-9, H-10) / Map 3.",["zone"]="Palborough Mines",["grid"]="I-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Note",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Foes that drop the required keys are level 21 - 23 and can be soloed by most level 25 or higher Damage Dealing jobs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mage jobs may require additional support if attempting this quest at 25.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_641",["title"]="Kazham's Chieftainess (Zilart Mission 3)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_3",["revision"]="20466",["requirements"]="Start: Jakoh Wahcondalo \226\128\148 Kazham (J-9)\010Previous: Welcome t'Norg",["rewards"]="Sacrificial Chamber Key",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Before you travel to the Temple of Uggalepih, you are to meet with the Kazham chieftainness, Jakoh Wahcondalo.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Jakoh Wahcondalo at (Kazham (J-9)) in Kazham to obtain the Key item: Sacrificial Chamber Key, which is required to enter the deeper areas of the Temple of Uggalepih.",["zone"]="Kazham",["grid"]="J-9",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Rise of the Zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57414",["title"]="Keeping Notes",["page_title"]="Keeping Notes",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Keeping_Notes",["revision"]="121470",["requirements"]="Start: Ahkk Jharcham \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10)\010Items: Black Ink \010 Parchment",["rewards"]="Exit to Commoner's Ward or Merchant's Ward from Al Zahbi Rent-a-Room",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Ahkk Jharcham wants you to bring her a sheet of parchment and a jar of black ink so she can write down her secret.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Ahkk Jharcham.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a sheet of Parchment and a jar of Black Ink to her for a cutscene and your reward.\010Note: You can give her either answer to finish the quest.'",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="ToAU",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_51831",["title"]="Knight of Gold",["page_title"]="Knight of Gold",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Knight_of_Gold",["revision"]="121634",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10)\010Previous: President Salaheem",["rewards"]="Key item: Raillefal's Letter",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Bring Raillefal back to Salaheem's Sentinels and help teach him the proper attitude for a mercenary.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Cacaroon in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-11).\010\010 The correct cutscene opens with \034Cacaroon got cheeep info, ya?\034",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="G-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Cacaroon either:\010\010 1,000 gil; or\010\010 1 Imperial Bronze Piece\010\010 You must physically trade 1,000 gil or 1 Imperial Bronze Piece to Cacaroon after the custscene has finished. Selecting one or the other during the cutscene does not satisfy this part of the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Walahra Temple in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-8) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the second floor of Shararat Teahouse in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-12) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-12",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="During the cutscene, choose the answer related to Raillefal's secret when prompted.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete the cutscene to receive the Key item: Raillefal's Letter.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue to Confessions of Royalty.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7444",["title"]="Knight Stalker",["page_title"]="Knight Stalker",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Knight_Stalker",["revision"]="118339",["requirements"]="Start: Rahal \226\128\148 Chateau d'Oraguille (H-9)\010Requirements: Dragoon 50+\010San d'Oria Rank: 2\010Bastok/Windurst Rank: 3 or Mission 2-3\010Items: Kuftal Coffer Key\010Previous: Chasing Quotas",["rewards"]="Drachen Armet",["repeatable"]="Yes, see Vingijard after AF is complete",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You MUST complete the previous quest Chasing Quotas, before Rahal will allow you to flag this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Rahal in Chateau d'Oraguille (H-9) for a cutscene. \010\010 Rahal is in the Royal Knights' Quarters (to the left after you enter the Chateau).\010\010 You must be Dragoon to flag the quest.\010\010 Make sure you choose the first option at the end of the cutscene. If you didn't, talk to him again to choose the right option.\010You may change to any job to complete the next few steps, including opening the coffer. However, you must return to being a Dragoon before going to the Temple of Uggalepih.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Ceraulian (in Cargo Room A) in Port San d'Oria (I-10) for another cutscene where Brugaire asks you to find the helm of the last Dragoon for him.",["zone"]="Port San d'Oria",["grid"]="I-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Open the coffer in Kuftal Tunnel for Key item: Challenge to the Royal Knights.\010\010 You do not need to be Dragoon when you open the coffer.\010\010 You can either obtain a Kuftal Coffer Key or simply pick the lock as Thief.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Chateau d'Oraguille (H-9) and speak with Rahal.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Balasiel in Southern San d'Oria (F-7)",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back and speak to Rahal Chateau d'Oraguille (H-9) one more time. Rahal hints that the writer of the challenge may be in the south, dabbling in black arts.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Temple of Uggalepih in Yhoator Jungle.\010\010You will need your Wyvern out to spawn the NMs. (Call Wyvern)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to south to F-11 on the first map and walk through the granite door to the North of F-11 to enter a room in F-9/10. (Note: The ??? here is very close to the one used to spawn the Death from Above NM.)\010\010Only invisible is needed to make it to this room safely.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Clear out the Tonberries, bees and doll in F-9/10 and then you are ready to spawn the 2 NM shadows. The Rumble Crawlers aren't aggressive like the ones in Crawlers' Nest, so they may be ignored.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When ready, cast Sneak (or have a mage cast it on you) and hit the ??? on the floor, in the area north of the short bridge, to spawn Cleuvarion M Resoaix and Rompaulion S Citalle. \010\010The NMs will not aggro if you spawn them with Sneak active. NMs do not appear to link when pulled with a summon but do link when pulled with magic or with a BST pet.\010\010Both NMs will aggro by low HP, even if Sneak is active.\010\010NMs will aggro a level 75 and will grant exp/limit points to a 75 (about 39 or so).\010\010It is only necessary to kill ONE of the NM's, if doing so, let the other despawn first before killing it.\010\010Other NM must despawn before the first dies in order to obtain the cutscene.\010\010 Both NMs are either Highly Resistant to Repose and Sleep or Immune to it all together.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the shadows are dead, touch the ??? again for a cutscene after which you will receive your helmet.\010\010(Please note, that if you get the message, \034It seems some kind of ceremony occurred here...,\034 you may be too far from the ???. Play around with the angle at which you're standing, and the cutscene will start.)\010\010OPTIONAL\010 This can be done in either order.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Ceraulian in Port San d'Oria for a short cutscene with Brugaire.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Rahal in Chateau d'Oraguille who will thank you for solving the mystery behind the last Dragoon.\010\010Notes:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If and when you get to fight for the shadows please note that a party that's there can claim one shadow. We killed 1 shadow and a nearby party killed the second one. Please note that as of now I do not know which shadow must be killed to trigger cutscene but for my party we killed Rompaulion S Citalle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If multiple party members need to complete this quest, only one member's wyvern is needed. The other party members can get the final cutscene after the fight is complete.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can get this cutscene with all jobs so only one DRG is needed to pop NM but ALL party members can get the cut scene after fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(see testimonials)\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Rahal (Royal Knights' Quarters, Chateau d'Oraguille)\010 / summary=Rahal wants you to gather information regarding the attacks on the Royal Knights.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2515",["title"]="Know One's Onions",["page_title"]="Know One's Onions",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Know_One%27s_Onions",["revision"]="113455",["requirements"]="Start: Kohlo-Lakolo \226\128\148 Port Windurst (G-5)\010Requirements: Level 5\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Wild Onion x 4\010Previous: Truth, Justice, and the Onion Way!",["rewards"]="Scroll of Blaze Spikes",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="There are reports that the Cat Burglar has been loitering around the Ghosty House in Windurst Walls. This looks like a job for the Star Onion Brigade! Gather four wild onions so Kohlo-Lakolo and his gang can create the perfect trap!",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Kohlo-Lakolo at Port Windurst (G-5).",["zone"]="Port Windurst",["grid"]="G-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Kohlo-Lakolo four Wild Onions for a cutscene.\010\010In some cases, this will end the quest, showing you the cut-scene and giving you the reward. (Not sure what causes this - possibly having finished the main Windurst storyline)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to House of the Hero in Windurst Walls (G-3) and try to enter to see a cut-scene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Kohlo-Lakolo to finish the quest.\010\010You will receive a cutscene and the Scroll of Blaze Spikes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_51261",["title"]="Land of Sacred Serpents",["page_title"]="Land of Sacred Serpents",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Land_of_Sacred_Serpents",["revision"]="121374",["requirements"]="Start: N/A",["rewards"]="Key item: Supplies Package",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A land of new adventures lies to the east of Mindartia. What splendors and terrors await the curious...?",["changes"]="HorizonXI ToAU launch access is handled through The Road to Aht Urhgan and the Imperial Relief Effort.",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete The Road to Aht Urhgan and obtain the Key item: Boarding Permit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Aht Urhgan Whitegate.\010\010 Standard travel uses the mercenary transport from Mhaura.\010\010 During the temporary launch restriction, players who reached the 10,000 Imperial Standing tier through the Imperial Relief Effort may receive an instant teleport option. [Horizon change] [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Salaheem's Sentinels in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10).",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Watch the cutscene to receive the Key item: Supplies Package.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue to Immortal Sentries.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_373",["title"]="Leaute's Last Wishes (San d'Oria Mission 6-1)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 6-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_6-1",["revision"]="34326",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 5-2|The Shadow Lord",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="This mission involves the late Queen Leaute. Visit Monarlais Halver in Chateau d'Oraguille to learn more.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Make sure you've checked the Door to the Great Hall and received the final cutscene for 5-2 in Chateau d'Oraguille, then speak with a gate guard. You'll need to trade crystals to the Conquest NPC to unlock this mission. Two stacks of crystals was enough.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Chateau d'Oraguille and speak with Halver.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select the Great Hall door for a cutscene. \010\010 Make sure to get the cutscene where the King asks you to retrieve a Dreamrose.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to (Western Altepa Desert (G-7)) in Western Altepa Desert.",["zone"]="Western Altepa Desert",["grid"]="G-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Dreamrose flowers to spawn Sabotender Enamorado. It is recommended that you bring enough people, pets and/or NPCs to reduce the damage done by 1000 Needles. It is possible to do it with less, but spreading the damage out will help any HP concerns.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Dreamrose flowers after defeating the NM to receive the Key item: Dreamrose.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Halver.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go toward the Garden at (Chateau d'Oraguille (F-8)) for another cutscene. At the end of the cutscene, you'll receive the Piece of Paper.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="F-8",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57454",["title"]="Led Astray",["page_title"]="Led Astray",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Led_Astray",["revision"]="123384",["requirements"]="Start: Mhasbaf \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-8) / Map 1\010Requirements: Access to Aht Urhgan Whitegate\010Fame: None\010Items: None",["rewards"]="Imperial Silver Piece",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Help Galiwao and his colleagues locate their employer before their worst fears are realized.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Mhasbaf on the upper level of Way of the Devout at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-8) / Map 1 to begin the quest.\010\010 Although the quest log names Galiwao as the client, Mhasbaf is the NPC who begins the quest.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="J-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Move to the lower level of Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-8) / Map 1 and approach the pillar to trigger a cutscene automatically.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="J-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Tohka Telposkha at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-8) / Map 1 for another cutscene.\010\010 When prompted, direct the Galka to Port Ephramad.\010\010 Selecting another destination repeats the dialogue until Port Ephramad is chosen.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with both of the NPCs below in the following order:\010\010 Rubahah at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-9) / Map 1.\010\010 Cacaroon at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-11) / Map 1.\010\010 When prompted during each conversation, direct the Galka to Port Ephramad.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go down the ramp beside the ferry dock at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-11) / Map 1 to trigger another cutscene automatically and receive the Letter from Bernahn key item.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-11 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Nashmau and speak with Tataroon at Nashmau (G-8) / Map 1 to complete the quest and receive an Imperial Silver Piece.\010\010 Ensure that you have at least one free inventory slot before speaking with Tataroon.",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="G-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57165",["title"]="Legacy of the Lost",["page_title"]="Legacy of the Lost",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Legacy_of_the_Lost",["revision"]="120877",["requirements"]="Start: Prince Luzaf \226\128\148 The Ashu Talif\010Previous: Testing the Waters",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have been ordered to guard the treasury of Ephramad. But first, you must find the hidden treasury, concealed somewhere inside Talacca Cove...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Testing the Waters; this mission begins during its ending cutscene and leaves you in Talacca Cove.\010\010 Retain the Key item: Percipient Eye obtained from the previous mission. It is not consumed during this battlefield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed northwest through the cove and follow the tunnel to the Rock Slab at # Proceed northwest through the cove and follow the tunnel to the Rock Slab at Talacca Cove (F-6) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Talacca Cove",["grid"]="F-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Rock Slab and select \034Legacy of the Lost\034 to enter the battlefield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Gessho within 30 minutes.\010\010 The battle ends when the main Gessho reaches 15% HP.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The victory cutscene completes the mission, grants the title \034Gessho's Mercy,\034 and begins Gaze of the Saboteur.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2117",["title"]="Legendary Plan B",["page_title"]="Legendary Plan B",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Legendary_Plan_B",["revision"]="108347",["requirements"]="Start: Kopuro-Popuro \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (H-10)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Luminicloth\010Revival Tree Root\010Wolf Hide\010Previous: A Greeting Cardian",["rewards"]="Scentless Armlets\010700 gil",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="In order to pull itself out of debt, the Manustery has decided to carry out \034Legendary Plan B.\034 They want you to gather a Revival Tree Root, a Wolf Hide, and a Luminicloth, that nocturnal monsters drop, so they can make charms to sell to trekkers.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must zone after completing the previous quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Kopuro-Popuro in the Manustery in Windurst Woods (H-10) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will need to get three items:\010\010Luminicloth which drops off Ghost family mobs or can be bought at the Auction House > Materials > Clothcraft.\010\010Revival Tree Root which drop off all Undead mobs or can be bought at the Auction House > Materials > Alchemy.\010\010Wolf Hide which drops off Hound family mobs or can be bought at the Auction House > Materials > Leathercraft.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade all three items to Kopuro-Popuro to receive another cutscene and your rewards: the Scentless Armlets and 700 gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2555",["title"]="Let Sleeping Dogs Lie",["page_title"]="Let Sleeping Dogs Lie",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Let_Sleeping_Dogs_Lie",["revision"]="119915",["requirements"]="Start: Mashuu-Ajuu \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (K-6) / North\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Blazing Peppers",["rewards"]="Hypno Staff",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Paku-Nakku keeps falling asleep in class. It seems as though something happened during the class excursion to the Orastery. Find out the cause of his sleepiness and wake him up, before he fails the grade.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="The quest Reap What You Sow, and Windurst Mission 8-1: Vain, will interfere with this quest. If either is active, you must complete it or both before beginning this one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Reap What You Sow is NOT required for this quest. In fact, if the player has the appropriate fame they won't be able to accept Reap What You Sow until they finish this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Paku-Nakku at Windurst Waters (K-6) / North. This quest appears in your quest log after speaking to Paku-Nakku. You may obtain this quest prior to Reap What You Sow as long as you talk to Paku-Nakku first, instead of Mashuu-Ajuu.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="K-6 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional talk to the fellow students to hear about Paku's issues.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Maabu-Sonbu at the Orastery in Port Windurst (E-7).",["zone"]="Port Windurst",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain Blazing Peppers. It can be purchased on the Auction House, or by trading a Sickle to the ??? in Pashhow Marshlands (E-5). Bring several Sickles, as they are likely to break. This ??? does not function like normal harvesting nodes and will break sickles even if the player has a full set of Field or Worker gear equipped. [Horizon change]",["zone"]="Pashhow Marshlands",["grid"]="E-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Blazing Peppers to Paku-Nakku, who will wake up halfway and fall asleep again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Talk to Maabu-Sonbu at the Orastery in Port Windurst (E-7).",["zone"]="Port Windurst",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Pechiru-Mashiru in the eastern building of the Aurastery in Windurst Waters (L-6) / North.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="L-6 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Paku-Nakku. Choose the option \034The automaton butler did it!\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Pechiru-Mashiru for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57174",["title"]="Light of Judgment",["page_title"]="Light of Judgment",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Light_of_Judgment",["revision"]="120885",["requirements"]="Start: Rodin-Comidin \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-7) / Map 1\010Previous: Unraveling Reason",["rewards"]="Key item: Nyzul Isle Route",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The Endymion has been blasted out of the sky by an intense beam of light... However, the mission must continue. Make your way to Aht Urhgan Whitegate and rendezvous with Rodin-Comidin.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Unraveling Reason; this mission begins during its final cutscene in Wajaom Woodlands.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Aht Urhgan Whitegate and speak with Rodin-Comidin on the upper level outside the Automaton Workshop at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-7) / Map 1.\010\010 Speaking with Naja Salaheem while this mission is active provides additional dialogue but does not advance the mission.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When prompted, select \034Leave it to me!\034\010\010 Selecting \034Not likely...\034 does not complete the mission. Speak with Rodin-Comidin again when ready.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The cutscene completes the mission, grants the Key item: Nyzul Isle Route, and begins Path of Darkness.\010\010 No additional zoning or time wait is required before beginning the next mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_378",["title"]="Lightbringer (San d'Oria Mission 8-2)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 8-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_8-2",["revision"]="123637",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 8-1|Coming of Age",["rewards"]="Rank 9\01080,000 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Royaulais Destin himself has summoned you for a vital mission. Seek audience with His Majesty in Chateau d'Oraguille immediately.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade crystals to a Conquest NPC to unlock this mission, then proceed to a San d'Oria Gate Guard to start it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Chateau d'Oraguille and check the Great Hall for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Rahal (Chateau d'Oraguille (H-9)) to receive the Key item: Crystal Dowser and further instructions.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Temple of Uggalepih",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Temple of Uggalepih and farm a Prelate Key from the Tonberry Stabbers (Map 3/4).\010\010 Alternatively you may farm Tonberry Choppers in the Yhoator Jungle or Tonberry Slashers in the Den of Rancor.\010\010You can bypass the key by pulling a mob from behind the door. The door will open once the mob walks into the door.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way through the Temple until you reach the door at Temple of Uggalepih (I-10) / Map 2, that can only be opened by killing the Temple Guardian.\010\010The guardian will not be there and the door will be open if someone has defeated it in the last 15 minutes.",["zone"]="Temple of Uggalepih",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From west to east, go through the first, third, and fourth doors in the hall, checking the ??? in each.\010\010Each ??? will provide a Piece of a Broken Key.\010\010Each player in the party must obtain the three Piece of a Broken Key in order to complete the final cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you have all three keys, select the second door to spawn two Doll NMs: Nio-Hum and Nio-A.\010\010Both have around 6500HP, do regular Doll attacks, and cannot be slept. \010\010You may pull one at a time if Sneak is activated before spawning.\010\010Only one needs to be defeated if the other despawns while fighting. \010\010Worked by killing Nio-A, unknown if this also works killing Nio-Hum instead.\010\010The dolls are aggressive to magic so you may not pull with magic.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the dolls have been defeated, check the door again for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Chateau d'Oraguille and check the Great Hall door for a cutscene.\010\010You will be awarded Rank 9 and 80,000 gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1805",["title"]="Like a Shining Subligar",["page_title"]="Like a Shining Subligar",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Like_a_Shining_Subligar",["revision"]="105984",["requirements"]="Start: Heiji \226\128\148 Norg (I-7))\010Fame: Tenshodo\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Rusty Subligar x 10",["rewards"]="Scroll of Kurayami: Ichi",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Ten rusty subligaria are needed for the training of young ninjas. Heiji will accept them one at a time.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 10 Rusty Subligaria to Heiji, who is situated at the top of the ramp, just to the left of the large staircase in the main room.\010\010Despite the quest description text, he will accept multiple subligaria in each trade.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Tenshodo",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1800",["title"]="Like Shining Leggings",["page_title"]="Like Shining Leggings",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Like_Shining_Leggings",["revision"]="105979",["requirements"]="Start: Heizo \226\128\148 Norg (H-7)\010Fame: Tenshodo\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Rusty Leggings x 10",["rewards"]="Scroll of Dokumori: Ichi",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Ten pairs of rusty leggings are needed for the training of young ninjas. Heizo will accept them one at a time.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 10 Rusty Leggings (these can be attained by fishing in starting areas or from the auction house) to Heizo, who is situated at the top of the ramp, just to the left of the large staircase in the main room.\010\010Despite the in-game description text, he will accept multiple leggings in one trade.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Tenshodo",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6859",["title"]="Lizard Skins",["page_title"]="Lizard Skins",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Lizard_Skins",["revision"]="60789",["requirements"]="Start: Hanaa Punaa \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (D-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Lizard Skin x 3\010Previous: The Seamstress",["rewards"]="Lizard Gloves",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Collect three lizard skins for Hanaa, and she'll make something in return.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Hanaa needs your help again. Fetch her 3 Lizard Skins and she'll make you something nice.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_344",["title"]="Lost for Words (Windurst Mission 2-1)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 2-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_2-1",["revision"]="120184",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Previous: Windurst Mission 1-3|The Price of Peace",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="There are reports that the Cat Burglar has her paws on a \034Book of the Gods,\034 a restricted book that was lost twenty years ago. Assist the Optistery in investigating the reports, and attempt to retrieve the priceless, but dangerous, tome.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="NOTE: This mission cannot be skipped.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Windurst",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trading 3 crystals to a conquest overseer unlocks this mission. Trading 12 will max out your rank points for Rank 2.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to any Windurst Gate Guard and accept the misson.\010\010 Mokyokyo, Windurst Waters (Windurst Waters (F-5) / North)\010\010 Janshura-Rashura, Port Windurst (Port Windurst (B-5)) \010\010 Rakoh Buuma, Windurst Woods (Windurst Woods (K-10))\010\010 Zokima-Rokima, Windurst Walls (Windurst Walls (H-7))",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Tosuka-Porika in the east wing of the Optistery, Windurst Waters (G-8) / North.\010\010 You may have to talk to Tosuka-Porika twice if you've started[Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 Lure of the Wildcat or] Past Reflections.\010 No need to zone, just talk to him again.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="G-8 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Nanaa Mihgo at the very north of Windurst Woods (J-3) and obtain the Key Item: Key item: Lapis Monocle.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="J-3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Maze of Shakrami",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Maze of Shakhrami, which can be found in Tahrongi Canyon, (Tahrongi Canyon (K-5)).\010\010 The quickest two ways to get here are: Teleport-Mea (if you have the Mea Gate Crystal) or via the Kolshushu outpost warp, if you've completed the supplied quest.\010\010 Adventurers below level 40 are advised to bring some form of Sneak & Invisible to evade monsters.",["zone"]="Tahrongi Canyon",["grid"]="K-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to (Maze of Shakhrami (G-6) / Map 1) on the upper map and take the right-hand tunnel labeled \034D\034\010\010Along the way you can expect to find goblins, scorpions and ghouls, all of which will aggro lower level players.",["zone"]="Maze of Shakhrami",["grid"]="G-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continuing on that path will bring you to a Maze of Shakhrami (H-5) / Map 2",["zone"]="Maze of Shakhrami",["grid"]="H-5 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check each Fossil Rock until you receive the Key item: Lapis Coral.\010\010There are about 14 Fossil Rocks on Map 2.\010\010There are 4 at Maze of Shakhrami (H-5) / Map 2,\010\0102 at Maze of Shakhrami (I-7) / Map 2,\010\0101 at Maze of Shakhrami (H-7) / Map 2,\010\0102 at Maze of Shakhrami (G-7) / Map 2,\010\0101 at Maze of Shakhrami (F-7) / Map 2,\010\0101 at Maze of Shakhrami (F-8) / Map 2,\010\0101 at Maze of Shakhrami (G-8) / Map 2,\010\0101 at Maze of Shakhrami (I-8) / Map 2,\010\0101 at Maze of Shakhrami (I-9) / Map 2.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Many mobs aggro sound, while Goblins will aggro to sight, so keep Sneak and Invisible up if you are a lower-level player.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Windurst",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have a Key item: Lapis Coral, return to Windurst Woods (J-3) and Nanaa Mihgo to receive the Key item: Hideout Key.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="J-3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Now head to East Sarutabaruta (J-7) and enter the Lily Tower entrance of Inner Horutoto Ruins.",["zone"]="East Sarutabaruta",["grid"]="J-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Inner Horutoto Ruins\010\010NOTE: It is possible to do Making Headlines in conjunction with this mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you are level 20 or above there is no need for Sneak nor Invisible.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to (Inner Horutoto Ruins (G-9) / Lily Tower), the lower-left corner of the big room shaped like a rectangular ring.",["zone"]="Inner Horutoto Ruins",["grid"]="G-9 / Lily Tower",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Here you enter a room with an Ancient Magical Gizmo. Head to the left and go through the Cracked Wall and you will enter a new map: Beetle's Burrow, at (Inner Horutoto Ruins (K-9) / Beetle's Burrow).",["zone"]="Inner Horutoto Ruins",["grid"]="K-9 / Beetle's Burrow",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In the burrow, head to (Inner Horutoto Ruins (G-8) / Beetle's Burrow) and continue along the tunnel extension.",["zone"]="Inner Horutoto Ruins",["grid"]="G-8 / Beetle's Burrow",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Mahogany Door at the end of the tunnel for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Windurst",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Windurst and head to the very north of Windurst Walls (G-3) to reach the House of the Hero.",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="G-3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the front door for a cutscene",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Windurst Waters (G-8) / North Tosuka-Porika at the Optistery to complete the mission.\010\010 As usual, the NPCs around the Windurst Gate Guards have additional dialogue.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="G-8 / North",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57124",["title"]="Lost Kingdom",["page_title"]="Lost Kingdom",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Lost_Kingdom",["revision"]="123420",["requirements"]="Start: Pyopyoroon, \226\128\148 Nashmau (H-7) / Map 1\010Previous: Royal Puppeteer",["rewards"]="Key item: Ephramadian Gold Coin \010 Mog Wardrobe 3: 5 slots [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Pyopyoroon of Nashmau has advised you to head west to a place with many \034stooones\034 to find a special \034ghooost.\034 Perhaps it will lead you to the ghost ship...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Royal Puppeteer; this mission begins immediately afterward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Leave through Nashmau (F-7) / Map 1 and travel to Jazaraat's Headstone at Caedarva Mire (E-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the headstone for a cutscene.\010\010 The Key item: Vial of Spectral Scent is consumed at the end of the cutscene.\010\010 Note: All party members must have completed this cutscene before spawning Jazaraat in order to receive credit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the headstone again to spawn Jazaraat.\010\010 If you are defeated by Jazaraat, it is not necessary to acquire another Vial of Spectral Scent in order to spawn him again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Jazaraat, then examine the headstone once more for a cutscene that completes the mission, grants the Key item: Ephramadian Gold Coin, and begins The Dolphin Crest.\010\010 After completing the mission, the headstone will replace the coin if you examine it without possessing one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7490",["title"]="Love and Ice",["page_title"]="Love and Ice",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Love_and_Ice",["revision"]="114784",["requirements"]="Start: Carmelo \226\128\148 Port Bastok (E-6)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 5\010Items: Key item: Carrier Pigeon Letter\010Key item: Carmelo's Song Sheet\010Previous: The Siren's Tear\010The Stars of Ifrit",["rewards"]="Lamia Harp",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Carmelo wants to start his life anew. You must go throw the song sheet he had written for his former love into the Mirror Lake on the Beaucedine Glacier.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Examine the Key item: Carrier Pigeon Letter permanent key item that you received during The Stars of Ifrit quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Carmelo who is at (Port Bastok (E-6)) in Port Bastok. He will give you Key item: Carmelo's Song Sheet and ask you to place it at the Mirror Pond.",["zone"]="Port Bastok",["grid"]="E-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the pond at Beaucedine Glacier (G-10). \010\010A portion of the pond will become selectable (the target is named \034Mirror Pond\034) in the presence of dark-element weather or clear weather. This target disappears when there is single or double ice-element weather. \010\010Check with Maleme, the Weather Checker in Southern San d'Oria (J-8) or the Weather Forecast, before going to the glacier to see what the weather will be like there. A weather message of \034gloom with occasional snow\034 means that snow will taper on and off.",["zone"]="Beaucedine Glacier",["grid"]="G-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select the \034Mirror Pond\034 for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Bastok and talk to Carmelo to complete the quest and receive your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7494",["title"]="Lovers in the Dusk",["page_title"]="Lovers in the Dusk",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Lovers_in_the_Dusk",["revision"]="106818",["requirements"]="Start: Carmelo \226\128\148 Port Bastok (E-6)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 7\010Previous: A Test of True Love",["rewards"]="Siren Flute",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Carmelo would like you to take the completed \034Chanson de Liberte\034 to a place in the Sancuary of Zi'Tah where \034clear spring water bubbles up around a ring of white-flowered trees\034, and bury it there at dusk.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Change zones then talk to Carmelo after completing A Test of True Love and he will give the key item Key item: Chanson de Liberte and ask you to place it in the Sanctuary of Zi'Tah at Dusk.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the Sanctuary of Zi'Tah and find the ??? located there, in the middle of H-8.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select this at Dusk (between the hours of 17:00-18:00) for a cut-scene to complete the story for this set of quests, and to obtain your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_14145",["title"]="Luck of the Draw",["page_title"]="Luck of the Draw",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Luck_of_the_Draw",["revision"]="121718",["requirements"]="Start: Ratihb \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-12)\010Level: 30\010Items: Lamian Fang Key or Thief with Thief's Tools or Access to Ilrusi Atoll Staging Point",["rewards"]="Unlock Corsair job; Ninja Die",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Ratihb wants you to check on his son Wasuhd, who has gone in search of his older brother.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="1 - Whitegate",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-12) As a level 30+ job, talk to Ratihb, second floor, at the Shararat Teahouse for a cutscene.\010\010Note: This cutscene must deal with Corsair quest, not The Die Is Cast quest that deals with throwing dice.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="J-12",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-9)Talk to Mafwahb by the Imperial Whitegate for another cutscene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="L-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Arrapago Reef\010\010This can be achieved by taking the Ferry from Port Ephramad to Nashmau\010\010Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-5) Take the ferry to Nashmau.\010\010Nashmau (H-6) Take the North exit to Caedarva Mire\010\010Caedarva Mire (I-6) Zone into Arrapago Reef\010\010Keep Sneak and Invisible up due to the Chigoes and Treants in the Mire. Use caution around the imps as they have True Sight. If you want to avoid a few mobs, it is recommended doing this during the day as the Jnun in Caedarva Mire are asleep during this time (although can also be avoided easily during the day).\010\010Alternatively, use Runic Portal to the Azouph Isle Staging Point and head to the tunnel at Caedarva Mire (I-6) into Arrapago Reef.\010\010You will need a Lamian Fang Key (or a Thief using Thief's Tools) to open an Irongate inside Arrapago Reef. You may farm this key either in Caedarva Mire or Arrapago Reef or you can obtain it once per Conquest tally per character by simply checking a ??? in the Mire Caedarva Mire (H-7, I-7) beneath a ledge at the back of a small bog; you can reach the key from the ledge without having to trudge through the muck.\010\010If you have the Ilrusi Atoll Staging Point, you do not need a Lamian Fang Key (or a Thief) to get to the required ???. Please see directions below. However, the journey back from Ilrusi Atoll Staging Point is very dangerous and it's easy to get lost. Picking up a Lamian Fang Key is far safer.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="2a - Arrapago Reef - Reach H-10 (past Iron Gates on Map 1)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Arrapago Reef (J-10) / Map 1 Map 1 - You will need a Lamian Fang Key to open the iron gate.\010\010Once inside the Reef, travel north in the tunnel until you see a ship. Board and walk through it, crossing the plank, and travel down the eastern shore.\010\010Remain alert of any Lamiae (detect by sight) and Draugars (detect by sound) that may agro you in the reef.\010\010Travel Northeast to a cave and the Iron Gate (J-10, Lamian Fang Key required). If you are traveling in a group, just one key will be enough to let everyone pass.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="J-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Arrapago Reef (I-9) / Map 1 Map 1 - Once you go through the first gate, turn left and you will find another Iron Gate (I-9) guarded by a ghost mob (Sneak).\010\010A Lamia Fang Key is not required to open this gate, just drop Invisible and open it.\010\010(Make sure not to have low HP, or the ghost will aggro you.)",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Arrapago Reef (H-10) / Map 1 Map 1 - Once you're past the gate, the Corsair ??? is ahead on a ship (H-10).\010\010There is a Lamia on the ship, be cautious when dropping invisible to start the cutscene.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="2b - Arrapago Reef (Alternate)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Using the Ilrusi Atoll Staging Point will put you at Arrapago Reef (G-5) / Map 2 on Map 2.\010\010 Please be wary of Merrow #5 when leaving the staging point.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="G-5 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Arrapago Reef (J-8) / Map 2 to get to Map 1 (point A).\010\010 Watch out for the Soulflayer (True Hearing) along the way.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="J-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the caves at (I-8)/(I-9) Arrapago Reef (I-9) / Map 1. Now you're on Map 6.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exit using the Iron Gate at Arrapago Reef (G-9) / Map 6. Now you're back on Map 1.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="G-9 / Map 6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the ??? marked on the map, Arrapago Reef (H-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="NOTE:If your Black Mage or /BLM is high enough to Escape, you can travel to Ilrusi Atoll Staging Point and then use Escape, which will transport you to Caedarva Mire just outside Entrance 1 of Arrapago Reef. This route requires you to use a Lamian Fang Key, but deposits you close to the ??? to obtain one. This also allows you to avoid having to dodge all the Heraldic Imps near the Azouph Isle Staging Point.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="3 - Talacca Cove",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Talacca Cove\010\010Arrapago Reef (I-12) / Map 1 Map 1 - You can backtrack along the path through the Iron Gates and exit into Caedarva Mire (1) at I-12 of Arrapago Reef Map 1 (where you just did your cutscene). \010\010Caedarva Mire (I-6) Map 1 - Head to Nashmau by going mostly south or hugging the right wall. Please take note of aggroing Treants and wandering true sight Imps, before you reach Nashmau.\010\010Caedarva Mire (E-9) - From Nashmau, take the western exit into Caedarva Mire and head to (E-9)\010\010 You must pass through a cemetery (E-10) to reach the zone, there are Imps (True Sight) in the cemetery. \010\010During night hours, the Qiqirn turn into undead, so if you can avoid the imps, sneak is still advised to avoid aggroing undead. Watch HP (blood) aggro, also.\010\010Note: There are actually two caves through the graveyard: take the northernmost one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Talacca Cove) Once inside the cove, travel along the left shore until you find a ??? (located on a big rock outside a tunnel).\010\010There are no regular enemies in Talacca Cove.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the ??? for a cutscene. You will receive a key item: Forgotten Hexagun.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel West from the ??? into the adjacent tunnel and follow it to its end.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Rock Slab for the final cutscene. (Ensure you have at least one free inventory slot.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene you will receive a Ninja Die.\010\010You will now be able to become a Corsair!\010If you did not receive Ninja Die, free up one inventory slot and check the Rock Slab again.\010If you already have a Ninja Die in your inventory, you will need to drop it before clicking the Rock Slab, otherwise you cannot complete the quest.\010\010Optional: Go back to Ratihb for final cutscene. (This \034optional\034 cutscene is necessary to start future Artifact quests.)\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Ratihb (Shararat Teahouse, Aht Urhgan Whitegate)\010 / summary=Ratihb wants you to check on his son Wasuhd, who has gone in search of his older brother.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={"Corsair (COR)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Corsair (COR)",["kind"]="Job unlock",["page"]="Corsair",["revision"]="123557"}}},{["id"]="wiki_6865",["title"]="Lufet's Lake Salt",["page_title"]="Lufet's Lake Salt",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Lufet%27s_Lake_Salt",["revision"]="62022",["requirements"]="Start: Nogelle \226\128\148 Port San d'Oria (G-7)\010Fame: sandoria\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Lufet Salt x3",["rewards"]="600 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Fetch three chunks of salt from Lufet's Lake. Beans at the Rusty Anchor are famous for their special salty taste.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Nogelle; she needs 3 Lufet Salts for her bean surprise and hints you might get it from river crabs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain the Lufet Salt by defeating River Crabs in West Ronfaure at the Knightwell. You cannot buy it as it is an Exclusive item.[Conditional wiki content: wotg \226\128\148 Note: Get 5 Lufet Salts if you plan on continuing with the next quest.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade 3 salts to Nogelle to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_56994",["title"]="Lure of the Wildcat (Jeuno)",["page_title"]="Lure of the Wildcat (Jeuno)",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Lure_of_the_Wildcat_%28Jeuno%29",["revision"]="121589",["requirements"]="Start: Ajithaam \226\128\148 Upper Jeuno, Upper Jeuno (F-5)\010Requirements: Immortal Sentries Complete\010Level: None\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 1 [Wiki: needs verification]\010Items: None",["rewards"]="Key item: White Invitation Card\010\010Imperial Bronze Piece",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The mercenary company \034Salaheem's Sentinels\034 has asked you to help recruit new members.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Ajithaam in Upper Jeuno at Upper Jeuno (F-5) to begin the quest and receive the Key item: White Sentinel Badge.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="F-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with the 20 NPCs listed below.\010\010 Checking the White Sentinel Badge gives hints for the required NPCs.\010\010 When speaking to a correct NPC, the badge flashes brightly.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Ajithaam after speaking with all 20 NPCs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ajithaam takes the Key item: White Sentinel Badge and gives you the Key item: White Invitation Card.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="ToAU",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_330",["title"]="Magicite (Bastok Mission 4-1)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 4-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_4-1",["revision"]="100100",["requirements"]="Start: Bastokan Embassy in Ru'Lude Gardens\010Previous: Bastok Mission 3-3|Jeuno",["rewards"]="Rank 5\01010,000 gil\010Key item: Airship Pass\010(If already in possesion of an Key item: Airship Pass you receive 20,000 gil)",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Capture the three magicites in Davoi, Beadeaux, and Castle Oztroja to prevent the Shadow Lord's return.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_370",["title"]="Magicite (San d'Oria Mission 4-1)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 4-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_4-1",["revision"]="100118",["requirements"]="Start: Embassy of San d'Oria in Ru'Lude Gardens\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 3-3|Appointment to Jeuno",["rewards"]="Rank 5\01010,000 gil\010Key item: Airship Pass\010(If already in possesion of an Key item: Airship Pass you receive 20,000 gil)",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Seize the three types of magicite from Davoi, Beadeaux, and Castle Oztroja to prevent the Shadow Lord's return.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_350",["title"]="Magicite (Windurst Mission 4-1)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 4-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_4-1",["revision"]="100119",["requirements"]="Start: Embassy of Windurst in Ru'Lude Gardens\010Previous: Windurst Mission 3-3|A New Journey",["rewards"]="Rank 5\01010,000 gil\010Key item: Airship Pass\010(If already in possesion of an Key item: Airship Pass you receive 20,000 gil)",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Confiscate the three kinds of magicite in Davoi, Beadeaux, and Castle Oztroja to prevent the resurrection of the Shadow Lord.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2517",["title"]="Making Amends",["page_title"]="Making Amends",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Making_Amends",["revision"]="75369",["requirements"]="Start: Hakkuru-Rinkuru \226\128\148 Port Windurst (E-7)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Animal Glue",["rewards"]="1,500 Gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Hakkuru-Rinkuru has snapped Minister Ajido-Marujido's favorite wand in two! He wants you to find some \034Animal Glue\034 so he can temporarily stick the wand together until he can obtain a replacement.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Hakkuru-Rinkuru in the Orastery then trade him an Animal Glue.\010\010If you are on The Horutoto Ruins Experiment, you need to complete the mission before you can activate the quest.\010\010If you are on Saintly Invitation, you need to complete the BC with the Yagudo before you can activate the quest.\010\010Even if you have not started the mission, if you have completed (or possibly started) the previous mission, you will not be able to receive this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2525",["title"]="Making Amens!",["page_title"]="Making Amens!",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Making_Amens%21",["revision"]="118354",["requirements"]="Start: Kuroido-Moido \226\128\148 Port Windurst (E-7)\010Requirements: Windurst Reputation 4\010Items: Garlaige Key\010Key item: Broken Wand\010Previous: Making Amends",["rewards"]="6,000 Gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Hakkuru-Rinkuru's switching of Ajido-Marujido's broken wand has been discovered. It seems that the original wand had some special significance to the minister. Hurry and retrieve the original wand from the furnace in Garlaige Citadel before it's too late.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="It is highly recommended to consider completing the quest Rubbish Day at the same time as it requires visiting the Incinerator room as well.\010\010This quest cannot be completed if the Windurst Missions Vain or Awakening of the Gods are active, or if mission Full Moon Fountain has been completed but The Sixth Ministry has not.\010\010If the A Shantotto Ascension mission That Which Curdles Blood or the quest Orastery Woes is active, it may be required to talk to Kuroido-Moido more than once to get the dialogue for this quest.After completing the previous quest, Making Amends, it is necessary to change areas before starting this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Kuroido-Moido. You may have to zone after completing Making Amends.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Incinerator in Garlaige Citadel.\010\010Each character who wishes to enter the Crematory Hatch (a door) needs a Garlaige Key (Rare/Ex), which can be obtained from Fallen Evacuees in Garlaige Citadel. There are 2 small rooms on the first map with 2 Evacuees in each.\010\010Tractoring someone through the door does not work, as Mashira will not respond to you unless you entered the Incinerator room by using a Garlaige key.\010\010Thieves cannot use Thief's Tools or Skeleton Key to open the Crematory Hatch.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After obtaining the key You will need 4 people to proceed from here to open the gates. proceed through the Banishing Gate #1 at Garlaige Citadel (I-9) \226\128\148 Map 1 of the first map.",["zone"]="Garlaige Citadel",["grid"]="I-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, proceed through the Second Banishing Gate #2 at Garlaige Citadel (H-10) \226\128\148 Map 2 of the second map.",["zone"]="Garlaige Citadel",["grid"]="H-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After past the Banishing Gate #2, go to Garlaige Citadel (I-7) \226\128\148 Map 3 on the third map to find the Crematory Hatch that leads into the Incinerator room.",["zone"]="Garlaige Citadel",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ask Mashira about the wand to receive a Key item: Broken Wand.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Kuroido-Moido.\010\010Note: If Orastery Woes is active, it may be necessary to talk to Kuroido-Moido multiple times, zone out and back and talk to Kuroido-Moido again to finish.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2563",["title"]="Making Headlines",["page_title"]="Making Headlines",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Making_Headlines",["revision"]="121703",["requirements"]="Start: Naiko-Paneiko \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (C-11) / South\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Key item: Windurst Waters Scoop\010Key item: Windurst Woods Scoop\010Key item: Windurst Walls Scoop\010Key item: Port Windurst Scoop",["rewards"]="560 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The editor wants you to gather news articles from the reporters dispatched to each of the four districts of Windurst. In addition, he wants you to confirm the validity of the scoop reported by the reporter in Windurst Woods.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Naiko-Paneiko, in the \034Tarutaru Times\034 offices at Windurst Waters (C-11) / South, wants you to track down several reporters.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="C-11 / South",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to the following: \010\010Kyume-Romeh(Key item: Windurst Waters Scoop) - Timbre's Timbers Tavern in northern Windurst Waters (F-10) / North \010\010Yujuju (Key item: Port Windurst Scoop) - By the Air Travel Agency in Port Windurst (M-6) \010\010Hiwon-Biwon (Key item: Windurst Walls Scoop)- Next to Shantotto's house in Windurst Walls (K-8) \010\010Umumu (Key item: Windurst Woods Scoop)- By the Dhalmel farm in Windurst Woods (I-5)/(Windurst Woods (I-6))",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You must acquire all the articles to proceed in the quest. Be sure to obtain the key item from each NPC.[Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 Some are also affiliated with the quest Lure of the Wildcat (Windurst), which takes priority over this quest. You may need to speak to the NPC twice to get it.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Inner Horutoto Ruins (Lily Tower) through the tower at East Sarutabaruta (J-7). \010\010If you are above level 30, Sneak and Invisible is not necessary.",["zone"]="East Sarutabaruta",["grid"]="J-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you have a map:\010\010Go to (G-8) or (G-9) and go through the cracked wall to reach the second map (Beetle's Burrow).\010\010Go to (G-8) on this second map (Beetle's Burrow), and follow the tunnel south and west (off the map) to the Mahogany Door.\010\010If you run past two greenish stone walls along the way that have magicked bones hanging out near them, you are going in the right direction. The Mahogany Door is at a dead end.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you don't have a map:\010\010Hug the right wall when you enter the Lily Tower until you reach an Ancient Magical Gizmo. The cracked wall at the first (G-8) is to the right of this.\010\010You can then keep following the right wall and you will eventually reach the Mahogany Door at the second (G-8).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click on the door to receive a notification that you confirmed the scoop. \010\010You may need to click multiple times to get the notification that you confirmed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Naiko-Paneiko to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1447",["title"]="Making the Grade",["page_title"]="Making the Grade",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Making_the_Grade",["revision"]="118123",["requirements"]="Start: Fuepepe \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (L-6) / North\010Requirements: Level 10\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Test Answers\010Previous: Teacher's Pet",["rewards"]="Aspir",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="The students' answer sheets from their recent exam have been stolen. The School of Magic urgently requests that you track down the answer sheets and return them.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="NOTE: You cannot have the Let Sleeping Dogs Lie quest flagged while doing this one. Also, if you have just finished that quest, you may need to zone before you can flag Making the Grade.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Fuepepe in the Aurastery, Windurst Waters (L-6) / North, who tells you that the students' answer sheets from their recent written exams were stolen and that The School of Magic urgently requests that you track down the answer sheets and return them. These can be purchased off the Auction House, under Other/Misc, or hunted down yourself.\010\010Enter Inner Horutoto Ruins from East Sarutabaruta (J-7), go through one of the cracked walls at either Inner Horutoto Ruins (G-8) / Lily Tower or (Inner Horutoto Ruins (G-9) / Lily Tower).\010\010Continue through the tunnel section until you reach the Magic Door at (Inner Horutoto Ruins (D-10) / Beetle's Burrow).\010\010Follow through to next crack, keep going until you see a Sealed portal at (Inner Horutoto Ruins (H-9) / Rose Tower 1).\010\010To open the door, you need a party of 3 mages, a WHM, a RDM, and a BLM, or someone with a Key item: Portal Charm.\010\010Alternatively, you may take the path through Toraimarai Canal, however, this will require the Key Item Rhinostery Certificate obtained from the quest Toraimarai Turmoil. From the Priming Gate entrance at (Windurst Walls (H-3)) in Windurst Walls, follow the stairs down, make a right, and go down the small stairs on the right-hand side. After this make a right, then a left. When you reach the Horutoto Ruins section of the canal (keep an eye out for Makara) go straight, right, left, left. You are looking for a small stairwell, take it up. Cross the small bridge and follow the path as far as it goes. Once in Inner Horutoto Ruins, go through the door marked \034Toraimarai Canal\034 and fight the Wendigo to your heart's content.\010\010Head to (Inner Horutoto Ruins (H-7) / Rose Tower 2), the tunnels that lead there look like dead ends, but keep walking and your character will be able to go through them. The room behind the tunnels is where you will find the Wendigos. These will drop the Test Answers.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="L-6 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Test Answers to Fuepepe located in the Aurastery (Windurst Waters (L-6) / North), who tells you to take them to Koru-Moru in Windurst Walls (Windurst Walls (E-7)).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Test Answers to Koru-Moru. He then tells you to return to Fuepepe, and also gives you a Key item: Tattered Test Sheet for Chomoro-Kyotoro.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="OPTIONAL (NOTE: If you skip this, the Tattered Test Sheet will remain in your Temporary Key Items).\010\010Head to Chomoro-Kyotoro located at the top of the West Aurastery in Windurst Waters North (Windurst Waters (K-6) / North).\010\010After talking to Chomoro-Kyotoro, talk to Kirarara in the same location.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Fuepepe to receive your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6022",["title"]="Mama Mia",["page_title"]="Mama Mia",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Mama_Mia",["revision"]="101803",["requirements"]="Start: Mamaulabion \226\128\148 Norg (G-6)\010Requirements: Tenshodo Reputation 4\010Items: Bubbly Water\010Egil's Torch\010Eye of Nept\010Desert Light\010Elder Branch\010Rust 'B' Gone\010Ancients' Key\010Previous: Trial by Earth\010Trial by Fire\010Trial by Ice\010Trial by Lightning\010Trial by Water\010Trial by Wind\010The Moonlit Path",["rewards"]="Evoker's Ring",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Mamaulabion would like you to bring him any \034thuper-dee-duper, overflowing with thpethial power itemth\034 you happen to come across in your travels. However, he was not able to provide you with any details on their whereabouts.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Mamaulabion to start the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He wants you to obtain for him super-duper rare items that can only be obtained from the high level Avatar battles. He needs the following:\010\010Bubbly Water (Trial by Wind).\010\010Egil's Torch (Trial by Fire).\010\010Eye of Nept (Trial by Water).\010\010Desert Light (Trial by Earth).\010\010Elder Branch (Trial by Lightning).\010\010Rust 'B' Gone (Trial by Ice).\010\010Ancients' Key (The Moonlit Path).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The items can be traded as you receive them. Mamaulabion will hold onto all of them until he receives the seventh.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Items must be traded one at a time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Mamaulabion after JP Midnight following the day you turned in your final item to receive the Evoker's Ring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you dispose of any of the items required for the quest prior to turning them in, you can obtain them again by completing the relevant Trial battles again.\010\010If you have turned in an item for the quest but not yet completed it, you are still allowed to choose that item as a reward after defeating the relevant avatar, so choose carefully!\010\010Upon completion of this quest, the above items no longer appear in the rewards list for defeating the Prime Avatars.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2040",["title"]="Mandragora-Mad",["page_title"]="Mandragora-Mad",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Mandragora-Mad",["revision"]="120670",["requirements"]="Start: Yoran-Oran \226\128\148 Windurst Walls (E-5)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Four-Leaf Mandragora Bud\010Cornette\010Snobby Letter\010Three-Leaf Mandragora Bud\010or Yuhtunga Sulfur",["rewards"]="120 - 5,500 Gil",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Yoran-Oran wants you to bring him unusual items that mandragoras drop, to help him in his research on the derivations of the species.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Yoran-Oran needs at least one of the following:\010\010|-\010! style=\034min-width:180px;\034 |Item\010! style=\034min-width:60px;\034 | Reward\010! style=\034min-width:220px;\034 |Drops From \010|-\010|Four-Leaf Mandragora Bud\010| align=\034center\034 |120g\010|Mandragora - Sarutabaruta\010Pygmaioi - Tahrongi Canyon\010Sylvestre - Buburimu Peninsula\010|-\010|Cornette\010| align=\034center\034 |200g\010|Mandragora - Sarutabaruta\010Pygmaioi - Tahrongi Canyon\010|-\010|Yuhtunga Sulfur\010| align=\034center\034 |250g\010|Mandragora - Sarutabaruta\010Pygmaioi - Tahrongi Canyon\010Sylvestre - Buburimu Peninsula\010|-\010|Three-Leaf Mandragora Bud\010| align=\034center\034 |[Template formatnum:1200: ]g\010|Mandragora - near Kazham\010|-\010|Snobby Letter\010| align=\034center\034 |[Template formatnum:5500: ]g\010|Mourioche - Boyahda Tree",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If repeating this quest using Cornettes, you can use the following macro while directly facing Yoran-Oran:\010/targetnpc\010/item \034Cornette\034 <t> or /item \034Cornette\034 <stnpc>",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The quickest route to Yoran's is to exit through Windurst Waters Mog House and turn right to Windurst Walls, cross the bridge, turn left, first house on left.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you are doing this quest for Reputation, be sure that you trade only 1 item at a time.\010If you try more than one item, you will only be credited for the item in the first trade slot.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zoning is not needed to repeat the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will be unable to trade anything if you are in the middle of the Windurstian leg of CoP mission 3-3.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This is a good quest for Windurst Reputation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Cornettes\010\010Trading Cornettes is a commonly used way to quickly increase Windurst reputation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If Bastok is in 2nd place or higher in Conquest, you can purchase Cornettes from Harmodios in Bastok Markets for 219\226\128\147265g, resulting in a net loss of 19\226\128\14765g per Cornette after the 200g quest reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Based on current LandSandBoat fame values, a character starting at exactly 0 Windurst fame requires 62 Cornettes to reach fame level 9.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Fame level 1 covers 0\226\128\14749 fame. A character who is already somewhere within fame level 1 may therefore require only 57\226\128\14762 Cornettes to reach fame level 9.\010\010The following table assumes a starting value of exactly 0 Windurst fame. The net-loss column uses the 19\226\128\14765g per-Cornette range stated above.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Cornettes\010\010Trading Cornettes is a commonly used way to quickly increase Windurst Reputation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If Bastok is in 2nd place or higher in Conquest, you can purchase Cornettes from Harmodios in Bastok Markets for 219\226\128\147265g, resulting in a net loss of 19\226\128\14765g per Cornette after the 200g quest reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A character starting at exactly 0 Windurst fame requires 246 individually traded Cornettes to reach fame level 9, for a total net loss of 4,674\226\128\14715,990g.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Fame level 1 covers 0\226\128\14749 effective fame. A character already partway through fame level 1 may therefore require fewer than 246 Cornettes.\010\010The following table lists the total number of Cornettes required to reach each fame level when starting at exactly 0 Windurst fame. The net-loss column assumes each Cornette costs 219\226\128\147265g and that Yoran-Oran awards 200g per turn-in.\010\010|-\010! style=\034width:33%\034 | Fame Level\010! style=\034width:33%\034 | Total Cornettes Needed\010! style=\034width:34%\034 | Total Net Loss When Buying from Harmodios\010|-\010| 2\010| 20 [Wiki: needs verification] \010| 380g \226\128\147 1,300g\010|-\010| 3\010| 50 [Wiki: needs verification] \010| 950g \226\128\147 3,250g\010|-\010| 4\010| 90 [Wiki: needs verification] \010| 1,710g \226\128\147 5,850g\010|-\010| 5\010| 130 [Wiki: needs verification] \010| 2,470g \226\128\147 8,450g\010|-\010| 6\010| 170 [Wiki: needs verification] \010| 3,230g \226\128\147 11,050g\010|-\010| 7\010| 196 [Wiki: needs verification] \010| 3,724g \226\128\147 12,740g\010|-\010| 8\010| 220 [Wiki: needs verification] \010| 4,180g \226\128\147 14,300g\010|-\010| 9\010| 246 [Wiki: needs verification] \010| 4,674g \226\128\147 15,990g",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3709",["title"]="Mean Machine",["page_title"]="Mean Machine",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Mean_Machine",["revision"]="121010",["requirements"]="Start: Unlucky Rat \226\128\148 Metalworks (G-7)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Slime Oil",["rewards"]="Scroll of Warp",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="One of the factory's machines needs oiling, but Unlucky Rat is out of machine oil. Help him out by bringing him something that can be used as a substitute.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Unlucky Rat inside the Cermet Refinery of Bastok's Metalworks. He muses about how to oil the machine, but does not ask you for anything specific.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Slime Oil from one of the mobs in the Slime family that drop it, or purchase it from the Auction House. (Materials > Alchemy)\010\010Tip: Slime Oil can be found off of the Jelly slimes from Korroloka Tunnel.\010\010For a low level, but distant, option, Oil Slick slimes can drop Slime Oil. Oil Slicks are found in Ranguemont Pass, near East Ronfaure.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Slime Oil to Unlucky Rat to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7439",["title"]="Messenger from Beyond",["page_title"]="Messenger from Beyond",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Messenger_from_Beyond",["revision"]="62064",["requirements"]="Start: Narcheral \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (M-6)\010Requirements: White Mage 40+\010Items: Tavnazia Pass",["rewards"]="Blessed Hammer",["repeatable"]="memory",["summary"]="On the westernmost dune of Valkurm, a dark stalker lurks. Defeat it and bring back its Tavnazia pass.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="As White Mage, talk to Narcheral on the balcony that overlooks the main floor in the cathedral at Northern San d'Oria (M-6).",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="M-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After flagging it, you can complete the remainder of the quest on any job.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Valkurm Dunes (B-8) (secret beach area).",["zone"]="Valkurm Dunes",["grid"]="B-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait until night (18:00 game time) and a ??? will appear near the Song Runes. Click on the ??? to spawn the Shadow NM Marchelute. \010\010The ??? will depop at 5:00 Vana'diel time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Marchelute, and it will drop a Tavnazia Pass.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the pass to Narcheral to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"White Mage (WHM)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="White Mage (WHM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Blessed Hammer",["revision"]="119367"},{["job"]="White Mage (WHM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Messenger from Beyond",["revision"]="62064"}}},{["id"]="wiki_7445",["title"]="Methods Create Madness",["page_title"]="Methods Create Madness",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Methods_Create_Madness",["revision"]="66346",["requirements"]="Start: Balasiel \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (F-7)\010Requirements: Warrior, Dragoon, or Samurai Lv.71+\010Base Polearm Skill 240+\010No other WSNM quest active\010Items: Spear of Trials\010Key item: Weapon Training Guide\010Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth\010Sahagin Key\010Key item: Annals of Truth",["rewards"]="Grants the Weapon Skill Impulse Drive",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Balasiel requires your assistance in constructing a new set of polearm training guidelines for the San d'Orian knights.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Balasiel in Southern San d'Oria who will give you the Spear of Trials and the Key item: Weapon Training Guide.\010\010If you chose the the wrong answer by mistake, zone out and back in to get the cutscene again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Perform Weapon Skills with the Spear of Trials until the latent effect disappears. \010\010To remove the latent effect, you must acquire 300 Weapon Skill Points.\010\010You receive 1 point for opening/soloing a Weapon Skill, 2 points for closing a Lv.1 Skillchain, 3 points for closing a Lv.2 Skillchain and 5 points for closing a Lv.3 Skillchain.\010\010See the Skillchain Chart for more details.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You must perform Weapon Skills and Skillchains on monsters that directly grant experience points to you.\010\010You CANNOT acquire points from Weapon Skills performed during Campaign Battles or Besieged.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Weapon Skills performed while under Level Sync count.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It is not necessary to remove the weapon in order to see when the latent effect is removed. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you no longer receive the latent effect bonus, head back to Southern San d'Oria and trade the Spear of Trials back to Balasiel, who will take the weapon from you and give you a Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth and tell you to head to Sea Serpent Grotto. (Note: The latent effect will not always be removed once you hit the 300 Weaponskill points; to check your progress if unsure trade the weapon back to Balasiel.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You need to get a Sahagin Key from the Sahagin Key Quest.\010\010When everyone is ready, trade the Sahagin Key to the Ornamented door at (J-10/11). You cannot open it from inside and you lose the key, so make sure everyone gets in together. Pass the bridge into the next room.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click the ??? to spawn the NM Water Leaper.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the NM is dead, reexamine the ??? to obtain the Key item: Annals of Truth.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring this back to Balasiel for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="NOTE: You cannot unlock this quest if you already have another WSNM quest active, though you CAN cancel the quest by talking to the NPC that gave it to you.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you're on Dragoon, you can use Wheeling Thrust to close Light. If you have another party member, you can do the following:\010\010Spinning Slash from a Dark Knight or Paladin.\010\010Ground Strike from a Dark Knight, Paladin or Warrior.\010\010Savage Blade from a Paladin, Red Mage, Blue Mage, Corsair, Dark Knight or Warrior.\010\010Dragon Kick from a Puppetmaster or Monk.\010\010Black Halo from a White Mage, Warrior, Monk, Black Mage, Paladin, Summoner, Blue Mage or Scholar.\010\010King's Justice from a Warrior.\010\010Mordant Rime from a Bard.\010\010Blade: Kamu from a Ninja.\010\010Trueflight from a Ranger.\010\010Vidohunir from a Black Mage.\010\010Death Blossom from a Red Mage.\010\010Shark Bite from a Thief or Dancer.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2210",["title"]="Mihgo's Amigo",["page_title"]="Mihgo's Amigo",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Mihgo%27s_Amigo",["revision"]="118765",["requirements"]="Start: Nanaa Mihgo \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (J-3)\010Fame: norg\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Yagudo Necklace x4",["rewards"]="200 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="If you want to befriend the infamous Cat Burglar, then you'll have to give her something she likes.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Nanaa Mihgo and then talk to her henchman, Cha Lebagta at Windurst Woods (I-4).",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="I-4",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Nanaa Mihgo asks for four Yagudo Bead Necklaces.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7527",["title"]="Minesweeper",["page_title"]="Minesweeper",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Minesweeper",["revision"]="104261",["requirements"]="Start: Gerbaum \226\128\148 Bastok Mines (F-8)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Zeruhn Soot x3",["rewards"]="150g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Rid the Zeruhn Mines of a few monsters to keep them off the miners' backs. Bring three pinches of Zeruhn soot to Gerbaum as proof of your success.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Gerbaum; he complains about the monsters in Zeruhn Mines and asks you to clear them out and bring back Zeruhn Soot as proof.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain three Zeruhn Soot and trade them to Gerbaum to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57157",["title"]="Misplaced Nobility",["page_title"]="Misplaced Nobility",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Misplaced_Nobility",["revision"]="120862",["requirements"]="Start: Razfahd \226\128\148 Imperial Whitegate, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-8, L-9) / Map 1\010Previous: Seal of the Serpent",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The Grand Vizier has ordered you to search for Lady Aphmau. First, locate the Immortal, Rishfee, within the Aydeewa Subterrane.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Seal of the Serpent; this mission begins during its ending cutscene at the Imperial Whitegate.\010\010 Speaking with Naja Salaheem afterward provides additional dialogue but is not required for progression.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the Aydeewa Subterrane.\010\010 A direct route begins at Wajaom Woodlands (G-7) / Map 1.\010\010 Sneak and Invisible are recommended while traveling through the subterrane.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On Aydeewa Subterrane (D-8, E-9) / Map 2, use either connection leading to Map 5.",["zone"]="Aydeewa Subterrane",["grid"]="D-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the unlabeled target near the tree root at Aydeewa Subterrane (F-8, G-8) / Map 5.\010\010 This is the same target examined during Teahouse Tumult. Use target cycling near the tree root if it is difficult to select.",["zone"]="Aydeewa Subterrane",["grid"]="F-8 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The resulting cutscene completes the mission and begins Bastion of Knowledge.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2368",["title"]="Missionary Man",["page_title"]="Missionary Man",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Missionary_Man",["revision"]="119612",["requirements"]="Start: Rauteinot \226\128\148 Kazham (G-9)\010Fame: Kazham\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Elshimo Marble\010Key item: Rauteinot's Parcel\010Key item: Sublime Statue of the Goddess",["rewards"]="Scroll of Teleport-Yhoat",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="First, find a slab of Elshimo marble in the Yuhtunga Jungle to help the young missionary realize his vision.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Rauteinot in Kazham across from the Chocobo NPC. He asks you to retrieve a slab of Elshimo Marble from Yuhtunga Jungle.\010\010Elshimo Marble is Rare/Ex and drops from Ivory Lizards in Yuhtunga Jungle.\010\010Be prepared to take a significant amount of time just farming one slab of marble. Reports of going over 50 kills to actually obtainn one Marble are not uncommon.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Elshimo Marble to Rauteinot to receive Key item: Rauteinot's Parcel.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring the parcel to Mulaujeant in Northern San d'Oria (E-5). He is on the second level, a few steps North of the Blacksmiths' Guild (San d'Oria).",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="E-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait until JP midnight and talk to Mulaujeant again to receive a Key item: Sublime Statue of the Goddess to give to Rauteinot.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the statue to Rauteinot in Kazham to receive a scroll of Teleport-Yhoat.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Kazham",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_11391",["title"]="Missionary Moblin",["page_title"]="Missionary Moblin",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Missionary_Moblin",["revision"]="119432",["requirements"]="Start: Koblakiq - Oldton Movalpolos (Oldton Movalpolos (H-11))\010Items: Soiled Letter",["rewards"]="4,000 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Koblakiq has stopped receiving letters from her brother Zeelozok after he went to speak with the Orcish overlord in Davoi. Koblakiq wants you to go there and search for him.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Note: Farm the Soiled Letter first to save time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Prepare for sneak and invisible if you are going with a character under Level 54 to Oldton Movalpolos.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Koblakiq (Oldton Movalpolos (H-11)). She will tell you to go find her brother in Davoi.\010\010Obtain a Soiled Letter from the Orcish Footsoldiers in either Davoi or Castle Zvahl Baileys/Castle Zvahl Keep. The castle footsoldiers have the best drop rates, but there are only 5 in each area, compared to 26 in Davoi.\010\010There is a good amount of Orcish Footsoldiers in Davoi around (F-6), in the big open area, and also the little corridors.\010\010Soiled Letter is Rare/Ex, so do an \034/itemsearch soiled letter\034 before you try to get one.",["zone"]="Oldton Movalpolos",["grid"]="H-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Oldton Movalpolos and trade the Soiled Letter to Koblakiq to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Oldton Movalpolos (H-11)) heading east is the same path to reach Tarnotik the goblin to trade the snow lily to teleport to Mine Shaft #2716 for cop 5-3.",["zone"]="Oldton Movalpolos",["grid"]="H-11",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4289",["title"]="Mithran Delicacies",["page_title"]="Mithran Delicacies",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Mithran_Delicacies",["revision"]="119945",["requirements"]="Start: Anguenet - Carpenters' Landing (J-10)\010Items: Muddy Siredon, 100 gil",["rewards"]="Blackened Muddy Siredon",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="To get to Anguenet zone in from the entrance at Jugner Forest (J-8) Jugner Forest.",["zone"]="Jugner Forest",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Anguenet and take the fourth option (Newtpool) for him to talk about the Muddy Siredon.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Lourdaude a Muddy Siredon. Then trade him 100 gil. He will give you back a Blackened Muddy Siredon, and complete the quest.\010\010Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Blackened Muddy Siredon is helpful in defeating the Mithran Trackers during Promathia Mission 5-3. It can also be given to Lehko Habhoka during the quest When One Man Is Not Enough.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Muddy Siredon can be fished up in Carpenters' Landing with a Fly Lure or Lufaise Fly.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Muddy Siredon can also be purchased from the Auction House under Food > Fish.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Anguenet (Carpenters' Landing)\010 / summary=If you give a \034Muddy Siredon\034 to Lourdaude, the Tonberry that stands beside Anguenet, he will make you one of the Mithra's favorite foods.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7513",["title"]="Mom, the Adventurer?",["page_title"]="Mom, the Adventurer?",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Mom%2C_the_Adventurer%3F",["revision"]="113485",["requirements"]="Start: Nbu Latteh \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (J-9)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Copper Ring",["rewards"]="100g / 200g",["repeatable"]="Yes, see below",["summary"]="Bring Nbu Latteh's daughter a Copper Ring as a gift from her mother.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Nbu Latteh. She wants a Copper Ring for her daughter, Roh Latteh, but only has a Fire Crystal which she gives you so you can synthesize one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Copper Ring. (Copper Ring +1 will not work)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Copper Ring to Roh Latteh in Bastok Mines at (Bastok Mines (H-7)) in a house on the bottom floor; she gives you a key item Key item: Letter from Roh Latteh.",["zone"]="Bastok Mines",["grid"]="H-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Do not peek at the letter. If you do you only get half the reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Nbu Latteh again to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will receive 100 gil if you examined the letter or 200 gil if you did not.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The quest is repeatable - to a point. You can repeat it every time you zone, until you attain Bastok reputation 2, whereupon speaking to Nbu Latteh begins The Signpost Marks the Spot.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The letter reads \034Dear Mom, Thank you for all the presents you bring me. I like them a lot...but I'd be more happy if you came home early sometimes, even if you don't bring me anything.\034 -Roh",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Copper Ring can be bought nearby from Carmelide or Raghd in Carmelide's Jewelry at (Bastok Markets (I-8)).",["zone"]="Bastok Markets",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It can also be fished up in areas such as Bastok Markets and Windurst Woods with Insect Paste and a rod which can catch fish such as Moat Carp. It can also be fished up in Port Jeuno with a Sabiki Rig.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) When you talk to the nearby guard Parnika before/during this quest, she mentions something suspicious about Nbu Latteh; while at the same time Nbu Latteh also complaints about Parnika making her life difficult. But after this quest is completed, Parnika will change to giving general directions around Bastok Markets; whereas Nbu Latteh is still complaining about her difficult life, but in a different way (hehe).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3751",["title"]="Moogles in the Wild",["page_title"]="Moogles in the Wild",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Moogles_in_the_Wild",["revision"]="119606",["requirements"]="Start: Moogle - Mog House in your home city\010Requirements: Reputation 7 in your home city\010Items: Noble's Bed\010Raptor Mantle\010Wool Hat\010Previous: The Moogle's Picnic!",["rewards"]="Upgrades the Mog Safe to an 80 item capacity",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After both requirements are met, your Moogle will mention that a Noble's Bed would look nice in your Mog House.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In order for this quest to become available, you must place the bed in your Mog House at least one full Vana'diel day before the weekly conquest results are tallied.\010\010A Noble's Bed can be crafted or purchased at the Auction House under Furnishings.\010\010WARNING: Other Furniture Quests such as Unexpected Treasure can possibly override this quest. To guarantee you get this quest, remove any other quest-giving furniture from your Layout. The items can remain in your storage.\010\010The Noble's Bed may be removed at any time after the quest has been flagged; it does not need to be in the Mog House for the quest to be completed.\010\010This quest cannot be started in a Rent-A-Room. It can, however, be completed in one.\010\010If any other Mog House Moogle quest starts you must zone and talk to your moogle again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Your moogle wishes to take a break and asks you if it can go see its friends on a trip overseas. Allow him to do so.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Your moogle wants a Raptor Mantle for his west sea friends for protection against the searing sun and a Wool Hat for his east sea friends for the torrential rains. He asks that you get them for him.\010\010A raptor mantle can be crafted or purchased at the Auction House under Armor -> Back.\010\010A wool hat can be crafted or purchased at the Auction House under Armor -> Head, or purchased from Chetak in Lower Jeuno (H-9) (Upper Level Othon's Garments) or Orez-Ebrez in Windurst Waters (H-7) / South (Baren-Moren Hatter).\010\010The HQ versions of either item cannot be used to complete this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade him both items (you can make the trade at any Mog House, it does not need to be in your home nation).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After going away on his trip -- oddly, he doesn't physically leave your Mog House as far as you can tell -- he will come back with a new Mog Safe that now holds 80 items! This takes until Japanese Midnight to occur.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Moogle - Mog House in your home city\010 / summary=Your moogle wants to take a raptor mantle and a wool hat to his friends in the Outlands. He sure would be happy if you found them for him.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_360",["title"]="Moon Reading (Windurst Mission 9-2)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 9-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_9-2",["revision"]="120098",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Previous: Windurst Mission 9-1|Doll of the Dead",["rewards"]="Rank 10\010100,000 gil\010Windurstian Flag\010Mog Wardrobe: 10 Slots [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="To lure the Bearer of Darkness to the Full Moon Fountain, you must collect the three verses of the ancient people. As her guiding star, the Star Sibyl is counting on you to help her decide the path for Windurst's future. The fate of Windurst rests upon your shoulders!",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 34 crystals to any Conquest Overseer to unlock the mission then accept it from any Windurst Gate Guard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Collecting Verses",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click the Vestal Chamber on the top floor of Heavens Tower for a cutscene with Star Sibyl.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Collect the following three key items in any order:\010\010Ancient Verse of Ro'Maeve\010\010Head to Qu'Hua Spring at (Ro'Maeve (H-6)) in Ro'Maeve, and examine it for a cutscene and the verse.\010\010Ancient Verse of Altepa\010\010Heading towards Chamber of Oracles.\010\010Head to (Western Altepa Desert (D-12)) of Western Altepa Desert to enter Quicksand Caves. You will need Sneak. You will need to open the pressure switch door at (Quicksand Caves (I-9) / Map 4) and also pressure plate at (H-7). \010\010This can be done with the required amount of people. Requires 3 points to open the doors. Galka = 3 points, Hume/Elvaan/Mithra = 2 points and Tarutaru = 1 point.\010\010 Keep left to enter Chamber of Oracles to trigger a cutscene.\010\010Ancient Verse of Uggalepih\010\010 Go to the second map of Temple of Uggalepih by entering from Yhoator Jungle at (Yhoator Jungle (J-11)), heading to (Temple of Uggalepih (F-5) / Map 1) in Temple of Uggalepih out into the jungle, then back in at (Yhoator Jungle (H-11)). \010\010Examine the ??? at (Temple of Uggalepih (E-8) / Map 2) to get the verse. An Uggalepih Key, from Tonberry Cutters, is needed to access the room, the ??? is located on the West side of this room on the floor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Vestal Chamber at the top floor of Heavens Tower for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Full Moon Fountain (BCNM)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Full Moon Fountain and clear a two part Burning Circle fight.\010\010The first part is against four Ace Cardians. A good strategy is to cast Sleepga on them and and kill Ace of Batons (BLM), followed by Ace of Swords (PLD) and then Ace of Coins (RDM). Sleep Ace of Cups (WHM) and rest to full. \010\010The cardians will eventually start resisting sleep. However, unless you take a long time to kill the first three it should not be a problem. \010\010The cardians will aggro from outside casting player casting range. The Ace of Swords will move to melee range while the other three will cast before moving.\010\010As soon as the last Cardian dies you will get a cutscene. The next fight is with Tatzlwurm (a wyvern) and Yali (a manticore). You will be assisted by Ajido-Marujido. If he dies, you lose the fight, so be sure to cure him.\010\010Letting Ajido-Marujido choose will aggro both NMs. Be prepared to pull both off of him.\010\010Players have reported phase 2 of the fight not starting due to interference from cutscene related addons and /fps toggles. This can generally be cleared by taking a screenshot to advance the frames. Please add info about your clear in the Discussion page, so recommendations can be made here for future adventurers!",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you use the Enternity addon the final cutscene may not play while using Windower or ashita.\010\010You might want to unload it '//lua u enternity' or '/addon unload enternity'.\010\010If you crash the game, the top door will not provide a cutscene. The remedy is to click the blank, glowing spot right outside of Heaven's Tower to complete Rank 10.\010\010Not everyone has this issue but if you do the above should work for you.\010\010It may look like its crashed on the multiple 30 second black screens but it eventually loads.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Vestal Chamber for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Finally click the Vestal Chamber again for the final cutscene with the Star Sibyl and to end the Windurst story line.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_10799",["title"]="Moongate Pass Quest",["page_title"]="Moongate Pass Quest",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Moongate_Pass_Quest",["revision"]="34373",["requirements"]="Requirements: Rise of the Zilart\0100:00-3:00 on a night with a Full Moon and Clear Weather or a party member with Key item: Moongate Pass",["rewards"]="Key item: Moongate Pass",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="In Ro'Maeve, between 0:00-3:00 on a night with a Full Moon and Clear Weather, or with the help of someone who already has a Key item: Moongate Pass, open the a Moongate and find a ??? on the other side. See map below.\010\010The pass can be acquired at any time if someone else lets you enter using their own Key item: Moongate Pass.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A ??? appears in a few locations beyond the moongate doors. Touch the ??? to obtain the Key item: Moongate Pass.\010\010There are at least 4 possible locations within both Moongate sections: 2 on the upper floor rooms, 1 on the lower, and one at the top center of (O-8), the 'middle-outer' room on the right.Tab around everywhere, including all rooms.\010\010Respawn on the ??? appears to be 30 minutes. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_579",["title"]="More Questions Than Answers (Promathia Mission 6-3)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 6-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_6-3",["revision"]="14470",["requirements"]="Previous: A Place to Return",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Esha'ntarl has returned to the Grand Duke Palace and is preparing the Jeuno Armada for its attack on Bahamut. At the same time, Prishe and Ulmia have finally solved the mystery that has been haunting them for the past twenty years.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Head to Ru'Lude Gardens and talk to Pherimociel at Ru'Lude Gardens (G-6) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="G-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Ru'Lude Gardens and check the Audience Chamber door upstairs at Ru'Lude Gardens (H-6) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="H-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Selbina and talk to Mathilde at Selbina (H-9), inside of the Weavers' Guild, for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Selbina",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Metalworks and talk to Cid at Metalworks (H-8) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5943",["title"]="Mysteries of Beadeaux I",["page_title"]="Mysteries of Beadeaux I",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Mysteries_of_Beadeaux_I",["revision"]="73651",["requirements"]="Start: Sattal-Mansal \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (J-8)\010Requirements: Magicite Mission active\010Items: Quadav Charm",["rewards"]="Key item: Coruscant Rosary",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Bring back a Quadav Charm and Sattal-Mansal will trade a Coruscant Rosary for it. Only then can you enter the depths of Beadeaux.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Sattal-Mansal inside the Tenshodo Headquarter in the Neptune's Spire at Lower Jeuno (J-8) after you talked to the Aldo while you are on the Magicite mission.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He will ask you for a Quadav Charm and in return he will give you a Key item: Coruscant Rosary.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Quadav Charm dropped off De'Vyu Headhunter located at Beadeaux (I-9) on the upper level. \010\010De'Vyu Headhunter will drop 6 Quadav Charms when killed, so every party member gets one.",["zone"]="Beadeaux",["grid"]="I-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Sattal-Mansal to receive the Key item: Coruscant Rosary. \010\010[Template :Beadeaux/Path to the Upper Level: ]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5944",["title"]="Mysteries of Beadeaux II",["page_title"]="Mysteries of Beadeaux II",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Mysteries_of_Beadeaux_II",["revision"]="101360",["requirements"]="Start: Sattal-Mansal \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (J-8)\010Requirements: Magicite Mission active\010Items: Quadav Augury Shell",["rewards"]="Key item: Black Matinee Necklace",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Bring back a Quadav augury shell and Sattal-Mansal will trade a black matinee necklace for it. Only then can you enter the depths of Beadeaux.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Sattal-Mansal inside the Tenshodo Headquarter in the Neptune's Spire at Lower Jeuno (J-8) after you talked to the Aldo while you are on the Magicite mission.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He will ask you for a Quadav Augury Shell and in return he will give you a Key item: Black Matinee Necklace.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Quadav Augury Shell dropped off Go'Bhu Gascon located at Beadeaux (F-6) on the upper level. \010\010Go'Bhu Gascon will drop 6 Quadav Augury Shells when killed, so every party member gets one.",["zone"]="Beadeaux",["grid"]="F-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Sattal-Mansal to receive the Key item: Black Matinee Necklace. \010\010[Template :Beadeaux/Path to the Upper Level: ]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57191",["title"]="Nashmeira's Plea",["page_title"]="Nashmeira's Plea",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Nashmeira%27s_Plea",["revision"]="120932",["requirements"]="Previous: Fangs of the Lion",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Escort Nashmeira as she sets out to convince Razfahd to halt his radical plan. Head to Nyzul Isle and show your true mercenary mettle.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Fangs of the Lion; this mission begins during its ending cutscene in Salaheem's Sentinels.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ensure you possess the Key item: Mythril Mirror.\010\010 If the mirror is missing, speak with Naja Salaheem at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1 to receive another.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the Nyzul Isle Staging Point.\010\010 If its Runic Portal has been activated, use a Runic Portal Use Permit at the Chamber of Passage in Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-7) / Map 1.\010\010 Otherwise, enter the ruins through Bhaflau Thickets and follow the teleporter route to Map 5.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Every player who needs mission credit must examine the Blank Target at Alzadaal Undersea Ruins (J-9) / Map 5 and select \034Yes.\034",["zone"]="Alzadaal Undersea Ruins",["grid"]="J-9 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Runic Seal at Alzadaal Undersea Ruins (I-9) / Map 5 and select \034Nashmeira's Plea.\034\010\010 The party registrant must be on this mission, have activated the Blank Target, and possess the Key item: Mythril Mirror.\010\010 Players who have progressed beyond this mission may assist without repeating the mission flagging step.\010\010 The mirror is consumed upon entry from each player carrying one.",["zone"]="Alzadaal Undersea Ruins",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete the instance within 45 minutes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After victory, continue through the automatic cutscene in the Alzadaal Undersea Ruins. It completes the mission, awards the title \034Preventer of Ragnarok,\034 and begins Ragnarok.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If the Mission Fails",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Naja Salaheem at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1 to receive another Key item: Mythril Mirror.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The current implementation does not require a time wait before obtaining the replacement.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Blank Target cutscene does not need to be repeated if your mission status was already advanced.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57616",["title"]="Navigating the Unfriendly Seas",["page_title"]="Navigating the Unfriendly Seas",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Navigating_the_Unfriendly_Seas",["revision"]="123227",["requirements"]="Start: ??? \226\128\148 Arrapago Reef (H-10) / Map 1\010Requirements: Corsair as Main Job 50+\010Level: Corsair 50+\010Previous: Equipped for All Occasions",["rewards"]="Corsair's Culottes",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The seas around Arrapago Reef cannot be navigated without a hydrogauge, and it is your job to find one. Ships from the Kingdom of Ephramad all had one, but that was long ago...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Examine the ??? in Arrapago Reef (H-10) / Map 1 Map 1 for a cutscene. \010\010A Lamian Fang Key is required to reach this point.\010\010Lamian Fang Keys drop from Lamiae and Draugers in the area.\010\010You can also receive a Lamian Fang Key from a ??? spot in Caedarva Mire (I-7) Map 1 (southern part of the block). You can obtain a new key from there once every conquest tally.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You no longer have to be on Corsair for the rest of this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You are asked to fish up a Hydrogauge.\010\010The item you need must be fished up in Al Zahbi, Aht Urhgan Whitegate, Nashmau, or the Ferry - Nashmau/Al Zahbi.\010\010You may use any rod and bait\010\010The fishing message you will receive is the standard item message, \034You feel something pulling at your line\034.\010\010It is suggested to use any rod for large fish (ie: S.H. Fishing Rod) and Insect Balls in Aht Urhgan Whitegate as this has a limited number of fish that may interfere with your fishing attempts.\010\010Complete the fishing mini-game. When the fish gauge turns dark grey, press the Action button (A on Xbox controller) to reel in the fish/item",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you've fished up a Hydrogauge, trade it to Leleroon, Nashmau (G-7).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to (G-8) in Wajaom Woodlands and trade the Hydrogauge to the Leypoint.\010\010 This can be reached quickly using an Olduum Ring",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return after Japanese Midnight, then examine the Leypoint again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the ??? in Arrapago Reef at (H-10) Map 1 for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urghan",["jobs"]={"Corsair (COR)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Corsair (COR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Corsair's Culottes",["revision"]="123513"},{["job"]="Corsair (COR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Navigating the Unfriendly Seas",["revision"]="123227"}}},{["id"]="wiki_5945",["title"]="Never to Return",["page_title"]="Never to Return",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Never_to_Return",["revision"]="75273",["requirements"]="Start: Kurou-Morou \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (I-7)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 5\010Items: Horn Hairpin\010Previous: Your Crystal Ball",["rewards"]="Garnet Ring\0101,200 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Kurou-Morou has thrown his precious hairpin into the rubbish, so he needs a new one made.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Prerequisites",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete Your Crystal Ball and have Kurou-Morou tell your fortune on three separate game days. Talk to him on a fourth day to begin this quest.\010\010If you are doing this quest for the Sleepga II quest line, it is suggested that you work on the quest Collect Tarut Cards, the prerequisite for Rubbish Day, at the same time. Both quests require several game days to complete.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Never to Return",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kurou-Morou asks for a Horn Hairpin.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Horn Hairpin to Kurou-Morou to complete the quest.\010\010Note: Horn Hairpin +1 does not work, it has to be the NQ.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57004",["title"]="No Strings Attached",["page_title"]="No Strings Attached",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/No_Strings_Attached",["revision"]="120431",["requirements"]="Start: Shamarhaan \226\128\148 Bastok Markets, Bastok Markets (F-9)\010Requirements: Access to Aht Urhgan Whitegate\010Level: 30\010Fame: Aht Urhgan\010Fame level: Unknown\010Items: None",["rewards"]="Animator\010\010 Ability to become a Puppetmaster",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="If you want to learn how to become a puppetmaster, you must bring an automaton to Iruki-Waraki.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Shamarhaan in Bastok Markets at Bastok Markets (F-9) on a level 30+ job.",["zone"]="Bastok Markets",["grid"]="F-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Iruki-Waraki in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-9).",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Ghatsad in the Automaton Workshop at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-7).",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Arrapago Reef and examine the ??? at Arrapago Reef (H-10) / Map 1 to receive the Key item: Antique automaton.\010\010 The ??? is hidden beneath the stairs on the southern boat.\010\010 A Lamian Fang Key is not required for this quest. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Ghatsad in Aht Urhgan Whitegate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait until the next Vana'diel day and speak with Ghatsad again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Iruki-Waraki.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Choose a name for your Automaton to complete the quest and receive an Animator.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="ToAU",["jobs"]={"Puppetmaster (PUP)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Puppetmaster (PUP)",["kind"]="Job unlock",["page"]="Puppetmaster",["revision"]="123812"}}},{["id"]="wiki_6270",["title"]="Northward",["page_title"]="Northward",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Northward",["revision"]="108413",["requirements"]="Start: Radeivepart - Ru'Lude Gardens (H-9)\010Requirements: Jeuno Reputation 4\010Items: Flame Degen",["rewards"]="Map of Castle Zvahl",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Radeivepart Ru'Lude Gardens (H-9) asks you to bring him a Flame Degen.",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A Flame Degen drops from Napalm, can be crafted Alchemy skill 47, can be bought at AH\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Radeivepart (Peace Monument, Ru'Lude Gardens)\010 / summary=Prove you are worthy to receive the map of Castle Zvahl by bringing a flame degen back to Radeivepart.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2477",["title"]="Nothing Matters",["page_title"]="Nothing Matters",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Nothing_Matters",["revision"]="101795",["requirements"]="Start: Koru-Moru \226\128\148 Windurst Walls (E-7)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 8\010Items: Cold Bone\010Warm Egg\010Previous: Blast from the Past",["rewards"]="10,000 Gil\010Vile Elixir (possible mid-quest reward)",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Professor Koru-Moru is currently engrossed in an experiment to create \034something\034 out of \034nothing.\034 To get closer to the truth of alchemy, he wants you to track down an old \034Thesis on Alchemy\034 for him.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="This quest appears to be currently bugged and inaccessible.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you have just completed the previous quest, Blast from the Past, you will need to zone before this quest will be given to you. Also, if you have started another quest involving Koru-Moru (such as Carbuncle's Debacle) and not completed it yet, he might not give you the following dialogue. In that case, complete the other quest first.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Koru-Moru asks you to find someone practiced in the art of Alchemy.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Shantotto at Windurst Walls (K-7) who will tell you that she remembers that there was a student who was formerly in the school who had interests in alchemy. Yoran-Oran, found in his manor at Windurst Walls (E-5) also gives additional dialogue.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head over to the Aurastery in Windurst Waters (L-6) / North and speak to Fuepepe, who will tell you to search in the Acolyte Hostel for a record.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="L-6 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head north, past the Aurastery, and note the door on the left side of the front of the building. Run between the two sides of the building, and go to each of the doors on the left. Answer the trivia questions correctly, and move to the next door. There are 3 doors, and 3 more to the right side of the building. After answering all the questions correctly (they will ask 2 or 3 other questions if you fail, then begin to loop back to the first), go back to the door on the left side of the front of the Acolyte Hostel to get Key item: Thesis on Alchemy.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you answer all 6 questions correctly you will receive a Vile Elixir.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you already have a Vile Elixir, and therefore cannot obtain this one, you also cannot receive the Key item: Thesis on Alchemy, and will have to in some way dispose of the Vile Elixir you have and then come back to get the cutscene again.\010\010There is a pool of questions. They include:\010\010! Question\010! Answer\010|-\010| A Four-Leaf Mandragora Bud increases...\010| AGI\010|-\010| After Fire comes...\010| Earth\010|-\010| All kids in Windurst love the...\010| Agatha Crystalie mystery series\010|-\010| An Airship Pass costs...\010| 500,000 gil\010|-\010| Bag of Herb Seeds cannot be used...\010| a Marguerite\010|-\010| Bastok is watched over by...\010| the Titan constellation\010|-\010| Cardians in Windurst Waters are...\010| hearts\010|-\010| Curilla's hair is covering her...\010| left eye\010|-\010| Delkfutt's Tower has...\010| thirteen floors\010|-\010| Facing north, the waterwheels in Bastok...\010| turn counter clockwise\010|-\010| Galka can eat raw...\010| meat\010|-\010| In Kazham, you cannot learn...\010| the weather in Sarutabaruta\010|-\010| In Rabao Oasis there are...\010| Six springs\010|-\010| Karaha-Baruha was the Minister of...\010| the Optistery\010|-\010| M & P's Market is found in...\010| Kazham or Upper Jeuno\010|-\010| Mithra can eat raw...\010| fish\010|-\010| Musketeer Ayame's sister is...\010| Kaede\010|-\010| Musketeer Iron Eater's master was...\010| Werei\010|-\010| Naji is...\010| The 5th Musketeer\010|-\010| Not found on Elshimo is...\010| The Cloister of Storms\010|-\010| Prince Trion lost...\010| An entire company\010|-\010| The Quadav do not possess a...\010| Quadav hand fetich\010|-\010| The quarry for the great Autumn Hunt was...\010| A Giant Sheep\010|-\010| Rhinostery minister Rukususu likes...\010| Peanuts\010|-\010| San d'Oria's younger Prince is...\010| Pieuje\010|-\010| The archduke of Jeuno is...\010| Kam'lanaut\010|-\010| The armorer in Bastok Markets is on...\010| Kulatz Bridge\010|-\010| The auction house in Bastok has...\010| 5 Counters\010|-\010| The constellation map was written by...\010| Lago-Charago\010|-\010| The dragon that appears at Balga's Dais is...\010| Black Dragon\010|-\010| The ex-Minister of the Manustery...\010| Zonpa-Zippa\010|-\010| The falls in N. Gustaberg are called...\010| Drachenfall\010|-\010| The Galka that lived with Werei is...\010| Gumbah\010|-\010| The girl who wants a red flower...\010| Valah Molkot\010|-\010| The Goldsmiths' Guild is closed...\010| from 23:00 to 8:00\010|-\010| The highest producer of mythril is...\010| Palborough Mines\010|-\010| The kid in N. San d'Oria is looking for...\010| Exoroche\010|-\010| The Konschtat Highlands houses...\010| the Crag of Dem\010|-\010| The lost kid in San d'Oria is looking for...\010| a Willow Fishing Rod\010|-\010| The map of Mindartia was drawn by...\010| Enid Ironheart\010|-\010| The Mithra Chieftainness is...\010| Perih Vashai\010|-\010| The monster that does not belong...\010| Zu\010|-\010| The Norg auction clerk on the far left is...\010| Atrevaux\010|-\010| The President of Bastok...\010| Karst\010|-\010| The President of Bastok sleeps in...\010| the Presidential Suite\010|-\010| The principal of the Aurastery is...\010| Koru-Moru\010|-\010| The restaurant in Port Bastok is...\010| The Steaming Sheep\010|-\010| The river near San d'Oria is...\010| Cheval River\010|-\010| The San d'Orian delivery boy's mom has...\010| Davoi Fever\010|-\010| The San d'Orian papsque's name is...\010| Shamonde P Grauche\010|-\010| The San d'Orian Royal Knight general is...\010| Rahal\010|-\010| The sea to the east of Mindartia is...\010| Gugru Blue\010|-\010| The Tenshodo leader's cape is...\010| black\010|-\010| The Troupe Valeriano is made up of...\010| five members\010|-\010| The war 20 years ago was the...\010| Crystal War\010|-\010| The Windurstian flag has...\010| five stars\010|-\010| The Windurstian weapon shop's greeting is...\010| Hohbiba-Mubiba\010|-\010| West of Zulkheim is...\010| Vollbow\010|-\010| You can catch Crystal Bass in...\010| Maiden's Spring",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back to Koru-Moru, who will send you to get the \034Lifeforce\034 and the \034Power of Death\034.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He is referring to a Warm Egg and a Cold Bone.\010\010The Warm Egg is dropped by Anemone in Yhoator Jungle.\010\010The Cold Bone is dropped by Doom Soldiers in Cape Teriggan. You need to kill goblins to get the skellies to spawn as they are the placeholders.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade both to Koru-Moru. He will ask you to come back in a few days.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait until after Japanese Midnight and return to Koru-Moru for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4402",["title"]="Old Wounds",["page_title"]="Old Wounds",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Old_Wounds",["revision"]="121209",["requirements"]="Start: Curilla \226\128\148 Chateau d'Oraguille (I-9)\010Requirements: Warrior, Red Mage, Paladin, Dark Knight[Conditional wiki content: toau \226\128\148 , Blue Mage, Corsair][Conditional wiki content: soa \226\128\148 , or Rune Fencer] level 71+\010Sword Skill 240+\010No other Key item: Annals of Truth quest active\010Items: Sapara of Trials\010Key item: Weapon Training Guide\010Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth\010Key item: Annals of Truth",["rewards"]="The weapon skill Savage Blade",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Curilla has agreed to help you polish your single-handed sword skills for the upcoming tourneys.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="NOTE: You cannot activate this quest if you already have another Weapon Skill quest opened.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Curilla in Chateau d'Oraguille to obtain a Sapara of Trials and a Key item: Weapon Training Guide.\010\010The General's Secret quest also prioritizes over this weapon skill quest and must complete it first to get the weapon skill quest dialogue.\010\010San d'Oria Mission 8-2 also prioritizes over this weapon skill quest. Curilla will mention something about the Vollbow coast, and will not give you this quest until it's finished.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the Sapara of Trials until the latent effect disappears. (This does not always disappear. Check with Quest Giver NPC periodically by trading her the sword to see your status.) \010\010How to remove the latent effect: \010\010You must perform Weapon Skills and Skillchains on monsters that con Easy Prey or higher. \010\010Weapon Skills performed while under Level Sync will count.\010\010You must accumulate 300 total Weapon Skill Points. \010\010You receive 1 point for opening/soloing a weaponskill, 2 points for closing a Lv.1 Skillchain, 3 points for closing a Lv.2 Skillchain and 5 points for closing a level 3 Skillchain.\010\010Unless you are using the sapara with Paladin (and therefore can use Swift Blade), you will not be able to close any Lv.3 chains at this point using a sword.\010\010To check to see if the latent effect has disappeared, look at your equipment screen for the elemental resistance. Though it is easy to see the HP drop, it should be even easier to see you lose a good 10 resistance in both schools below.\010\010At any time, you can talk to Curilla to end the quest. If you do end it, all work on the latent effect will be lost as you will need to start the quest again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you no longer receive the latent effect bonus, head back to Chateau d'Oraguille and TRADE the Sapara of Trials back to Curilla to exchange the weapon for a Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth and instructions to head to Quicksand Caves.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Western Altepa Desert. Here you must open the Altepa Gate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in Quicksand Caves go to I-6 on the map to the right and click the ??? to spawn the NM named Girtablulu. On the way there, you may encounter an Antican Praetor that hears through sneak at the 4-way intersection. Wait for that antica to move to the far southwest corner of that room before heading north.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you enter the room, be sure to clear it out first as you might be unlucky like me and aggro all the nearby Antica, rendering you dead and having to open the Gate again if you haven't cast Reraise in advance.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Girtablulu causes high damage when it connects. Uses Wild Rage and Earth Pounder like other scorpions, which can cause high damage. Wild Rage can do about 400-600 damage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Girtablulu's use of Death Scissors can do upwards of 1000 damage on a well-equipped level 75 Paladin. It may be best to bring a blink tank.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the NM is dead, reexamine the ??? to obtain the Key item: Annals of Truth. \010\010Only one character from a party will need to spawn Girtablulu for the whole party that defeated it to get the Key Item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring this back to Curilla for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If more than one individual in your party needs the item, they may check the ??? as well. You do not need to fight the NM for each of them.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talking to Curilla may trigger a cut-scene for the quest The General's Secret. Simply talk to her again after accepting the The General's Secret quest to obtain the correct cutscene for Old Wounds. (this is incorrect you have to finish \034The Generals Secret\034)-Valraven",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_19459",["title"]="Olduum",["page_title"]="Olduum",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Olduum",["revision"]="121530",["requirements"]="Start: Dkhaaya \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-9)\010Items: Pickaxe \010one of the following\010\010Electrocell\010\010Electropot\010\010Electrolocomotive",["rewards"]="Lightning Band \010Olduum Ring",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Dkhaaya at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-9) for a cutscene and to obtain Dkhaaya's Research Journal (key item).",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="G-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Pick up some Pickaxes.\010\010 Kahah Hobichai in Al Zahbi (J-7) sells them.\010\010You will want a few because they can break. Up to eight in a row have broken, and bringing a stack of pickaxes is recommended.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Bhaflau Thickets from Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-7). This is the tunnel behind Sajahb Port Ephramad (the north exit)\010\010Or take a Chocobo from Al Zahbi through Wajaom Woodlands to Bhaflau Thickets.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="H-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the cave Bhaflau Thickets (I-7) to zone into Aydeewa Subterrane. The Ameretats can aggro to sound at level 75.\010\010Follow the path to a room with columns, (I-8).\010\010Drop off a ledge North-West into a room with Aydeewa Diremites (they aggro level 75's - use Sneak to avoid aggro).\010\010Go down the ramp immediately to the left (H-8), that leads south and down to a room with leeches and a large pool in the center that looks like a Teleporter (H-9).\010\010Note: This is the same room that is involved in the Blue Mage flag quest An Empty Vessel. If you are doing both quests at the same time, make sure you get the key item for this quest before starting the Blue Mage cutscene, as it will teleport you back to Whitegate automatically after the scene has finished.",["zone"]="Bhaflau Thickets",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Find the Excavation Site and mine it to get one of three key items: Electrocell, Electropot, or Electrolocomotive (G-9).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Dkhaaya; he rewards you with a Lightning Band.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At this point, the quest is gone from the log and technically complete, but the real reward is to trade the Lightning Band to the Leypoint in Wajaom Woodlands (G-8) to obtain the Olduum Ring.\010\010NOTE: As of August 9, 2026, the Leypoint does not accept the Lightning Band, so this last step of obtaining the Olduum Ring cannot be completed.\010\010If you drop your ring, this quest is repeatable by talking with Dkhaaya.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57388",["title"]="Omens",["page_title"]="Omens",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Omens",["revision"]="123570",["requirements"]="Start: Waoud \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-10) / Map 1 \226\128\148 On the upper level of Heretic's Alley.\010Requirements: Blue Mage level 50+ as the player's main job to begin\010Complete Beginnings\010Zone after completing Beginnings\010Fame: None\010Items: Key item: Sealed Immortal Envelope\010Previous: Beginnings",["rewards"]="Magus Charuqs",["repeatable"]="af",["summary"]="Pursue greater power by defeating the monstrous flan in the Navukgo Execution Chamber.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Starting the Quest",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete Beginnings.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait until Japanese midnight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Set Blue Mage as your main job at level 50 or higher.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Waoud at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-10) / Map 1 to begin the quest.\010\010 Blue Mage is required as the main job to begin Omens.\010\010 After the quest has been accepted, the remaining steps may be completed on another job.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="J-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Navukgo Execution Chamber",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the Navukgo Execution Chamber entrance at Mount Zhayolm (D-8) / Map 1.\010\010 Some overland routes pass through the Gates of Halvung and require the Key item: Cast Metal Plate.\010\010 The battlefield entrance itself is reached through Mount Zhayolm at D-8.",["zone"]="Mount Zhayolm",["grid"]="D-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the Navukgo Execution Chamber.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Decorative Bronze Gate and select Omens.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat every Immortal Flan within 30 minutes.\010\010 The battlefield has no level cap and permits up to 18 players.\010\010 The number of Immortal Flans increases with the number of players entering.\010\010 All spawned flans must be defeated to win.\010\010 NOTE: The flan was easily defeated by a level 75 SMN in two BP's.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After winning, exit the battlefield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Sealed Immortal Envelope",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Waoud at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="J-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete the resulting cutscene to receive the Key item: Sealed Immortal Envelope.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Lathuya at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-8) / Map 1.\010\010 Lathuya is on the upper level inside the merchant stall.\010\010 Speak with Lathuya normally; the envelope is not traded through the Trade menu.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="F-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Aydeewa Subterrane",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exit Aht Urhgan Whitegate to Wajaom Woodlands at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel through Wajaom Woodlands to the Aydeewa Subterrane entrance at Wajaom Woodlands (K-9).",["zone"]="Wajaom Woodlands",["grid"]="K-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Aydeewa Subterrane on Map 6 at Aydeewa Subterrane (H-9) / Map 6.",["zone"]="Aydeewa Subterrane",["grid"]="H-9 / Map 6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head north and examine the unnamed target beside the pond at Aydeewa Subterrane (H-7) / Map 6 for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Aydeewa Subterrane",["grid"]="H-7 / Map 6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Lathuya at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="F-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete the resulting cutscene to receive:\010\010 Magus Charuqs\010\010 The title Immortal Lion\010\010 The Key item: Sealed Immortal Envelope is removed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone and wait until the following Vana'diel day before attempting to begin Transformations.\010\010 This is a Vana'diel-day wait, not a Japanese-midnight wait.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={"Blue Mage (BLU)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Blue Mage (BLU)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Magus Charuqs",["revision"]="122095"},{["job"]="Blue Mage (BLU)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Omens",["revision"]="123570"}}},{["id"]="wiki_13026",["title"]="Omni Aketon",["page_title"]="Omni Aketon",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Omni_Aketon",["revision"]="120590",["requirements"]="Start: Milia \226\128\148 Ru'Lude Gardens (H-6)",["rewards"]="Ducal Aketon",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="None, This quest does not show up in the quest log",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Milia at Ru'Lude Gardens (H-6).\010\010This is a hidden quest, nothing will show up in your quest log.",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="H-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She will ask you to become a hero of Bastok, Windurst and San d'Oria. And to bring an aketon from each.\010\010 If you are already rank 10 in your nation, she will say \034Ah! So that's how you became the hero of <current nation>, eh?\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade her the Federation Aketon, Kingdom Aketon or the Republic Aketon. Whichever you were currently Rank 10 in.\010\010You can purchase them for gil from other players or spend your Conquest Points.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She will give you dialogue about how she knows a skilled Goblin Tailor who can make something special for you and then asks you to become the Hero of all three nations.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You Must have Rank 10 in all Three Nations.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade her all 3 Aketons. She'll tell you to return next week.\010You may pick up your Ducal Aketon on the server's weekly reset \034JP Midnight\034 Sunday.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="horizonxi",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_336",["title"]="On My Way (Bastok Mission 7-2)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 7-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_7-2",["revision"]="105802",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 7-1|The Final Image",["rewards"]="Rank 8\01060,000 gil\010Mog Wardrobe: 10 Slots",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A search has begun for information regarding the whereabouts of the missing Galkan elder, Werei. The president will brief you on the details of this mission.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Accept the Mission from any Gate Guard.\010\010Trade 21 Crystals to a gate guard to unlock this mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Karst in the Metalworks for details on the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Hilda at the Steaming Sheep in Port Bastok (Port Bastok (E-6)).\010\010You can talk to Hilda from the bottom floor.",["zone"]="Port Bastok",["grid"]="E-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel through Palborough Mines to Waughroon Shrine",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the BCNM Battle \034On My Way\034.\010\010 This is a 6 person uncapped fight.\010\010 There is no EXP loss in this fight.\010\010 Buffs will be erased upon entry into the battlefield.\010\010 Your opponents are 4 Quadavs.\010\010 Sa'Nha Soulsaver - WHM\010\010 Go'Bha Slaughterer - DRK\010\010 Ku'Jhu Graniteskin - WAR\010\010 Da'Shu Knightslayer - RDM\010\010 All opponents will use their SP Abilities.\010\010 Standard tactic is to use Sleepga and fight one at a time.\010\010 Using this tactic, pull the WHM first down to the bottom of the ramp so that Benediction does not wake the others.\010\010 Easily completed by 75 WAR/SAM, 75 DRK/BLM, 75 WHM/SMN.\010\010 Upon completion, you will receive a Key item: Letter from Werei.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Metalworks and speak to Karst. You will be rewarded with Rank 8.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Gumbah in Bastok Mines (Bastok Mines (J-7)) for a cutscene.\010\010 This will complete the mission.",["zone"]="Bastok Mines",["grid"]="J-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Cornelia's door (behind President Karst) is no longer locked. Interact with the door for a cutscene.\010\010 You can return for a different cutscene after you've completed Beauty and the Galka, Fallen Comrades, and Rivals.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2526",["title"]="One Good Deed?",["page_title"]="One Good Deed?",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/One_Good_Deed%3F",["revision"]="119970",["requirements"]="Start: Chipmy-Popmy \226\128\148 Port Windurst (C-8)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 5",["rewards"]="3,200 Gil\010Key item: Map of the Attohwa Chasm",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A mysterious character living on Purgonorgo Isle in Bibiki Bay insists that the island belongs to him. Chipmy-Popmy wants you to participate in the next \034debate\034 over ownership, set to take place in the center of the island.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Chipmy-Popmy to get a cutscene. (You may have to talk to him twice to get the cutscene.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the Manaclipper in Bibiki Bay to Bibiki Bay - Purgonorgo Isle. The clipper does three tours. You want the tour that goes out to Bibiki Bay - Purgonorgo Isle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once on the Isle, follow the path to (H-9), near the center of the isle. There is a ???.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the ??? to spawn six Peerifools (Mandragora-type monsters). Defeat them.\010\010The Peerifools use Dream Flower rapidly, often within seconds of each other when they are awake, but a 75 character should have no difficulty evading or resisting the sleep effect.\010\010They are very susceptible to a BLM's Sleep spells.\010\010Will link with any other Mandragora mobs in the area. Not really a threat, but you should be aware of this.\010\010Their attacks have a chance of processing an \034Additional Effect: Sleep\034 when they hit you.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once defeated, examine the ??? again for a cutscene and the Deed to Purgonorgo Isle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Chipmy-Popmy for another cutscene. (You may have to talk to him twice again to get the cutscene.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Now you need to track down one of the Mithran Trackers in Attohwa Chasm.\010\010Attohwa Chasm, even with a map, can be very confusing. Monsters in the central and eastern areas tend to be non-aggressive to level 60+ characters, while monsters on the west side of the map (the side that Tiamat and Xolotl spawn on) will still be aggressive to a level 75 character.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Attohwa Chasm from the Maze of Shakhrami; the entrance is labeled on your map.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Cross the bridge (this is very important) and follow the path.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At (H-10), there is an intersection. You want to head east, not west. This will take you into the lower-leveled eastern side of the map.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow the mountainside north to (I-8). There is a cave to take you back into the mountain/chasm area.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow the path (there is another intersection shortly into the area; head south, not north). The path winds in all directions and takes you all over the chasm. There will be a fork in the path, follow either one south.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will come to another bridge that crosses the chasm. Continue west.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At (G-7), there is another intersection; head north, not east. You will cross three bridges before you get to the end.\010\010Be very careful once you see the tunnel exit, as Antlions come very close to the mountain. Use Sneak and Invisible and follow the mountain north again.\010\010Also beware of the gasponia flowers along the way, as they can cause a very potent poison effect when getting too close.\010\010Antlions detect by sound so it is safe to renew Invisible near one while avoiding the goblins. As most people know you can cast invisible while its still up so as long as the mob does not detect magic (if you're not using ninjutsu).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At (F-6), there is another tunnel entrance. Follow this tunnel, one bridge to the Boneyard Gully zone, in the eastern part of (G-6).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you zone, you will have another cutscene, at the end of which you will receive the Map of the Attohwa Chasm.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Chipmy-Popmy to complete the quest and receive the 3200gil reward.\010\010You will need to speak to Chipmy-Popmy three times to activate this scene if you are on the final portion of Promathia Mission 8-4:Dawn.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_581",["title"]="One to be Feared (Promathia Mission 6-4)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 6-4",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_6-4",["revision"]="111809",["requirements"]="Level: 60 Cap\010Previous: More Questions Than Answers",["rewards"]="1500 Exp (Once per day, upon completing the BC),\010Ducal Guard's Ring\010Mog Wardrobe 2: 3 Slots",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="The fifth verse of \034Memoria de la S^tona\034 has been discovered. Now, with the help of Cid, you must fly beyond the sea of clouds and face Bahamut for what may be the final time...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Head to Sealion's Den and view a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Iron Gate and enter the BC for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will only have 45 minutes to complete all three battles, including the cutscenes before and between the fights; if you run out of time before all three battles are cleared, you will be thrown out of the BC. You will have to work fast, but there is sufficient time, with records being set as low as 22 minutes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Before and between each fight, you will zone into a room on the airship. Here, you will be able to buff and eat food without interruption. Your HP and MP will be also healed to full, and you have the option of leaving the BC if you so desire.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Being moved from a battle (e.g., after defeating the Mammets or Omega) into the buffing area will reset TP, but TP gained in the buffing area (such as from an Icarus Wing) will last into the next battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Immediately buff up, rest MP and then have someone check the airship\226\128\153s communication room, telling it to approach. Everyone on the airship will automatically get a cutscene that interrupts rest and any spells or items they were using. Consider skipping the cutscene to save time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A fair objective to set is starting the first battle with about 41 minutes left on the timer.\010\010Notes:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It's highly recommended that any melee damage dealers sub Ninja to absorb AoE damage by the two weapons. However, a Samurai with capped archery may find it beneficial to sub Ranger for this fight instead, tanking mammets with Seigan and shooting the two weapons from out of range.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Blue Mage excels at this with Head Butt for stun.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The level cap on this battle is 60.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="All Summoner party can win this fight. 2 Summoners Astral Flow on Omega at around 40%, using only regular blood pacts until that time (reference to the element of the day for avatar preferance). On Ultima, the remaining 4 summoners Astral Flow at around 50% health. Bring Hi-ethers or comparable items for gaining MP back while waiting for 60 second timer on Blood Pact and Yagudo Drinks for refresh.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Having at least three damage dealers should be enough to win the fight, assuming the party does not wipe out. Damage dealers can include NIN and PLD/NIN(WAR also works if defender is off).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If a party runs out of time, it is usually because they have wiped once or twice during battle.\010\010In other words, fighting the battle \034Slow, steady, and safe\034 will usually ensure victory.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mammet-22 Zeta x5",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will enter the battlefield facing five Mammet-22 Zeta.\010\010These Mammets will change jobs, just like the Mammets-19 Epsilon you fought in Promathia Mission 2-5. Mages have staves and cast -ga II spells; Warriors have swords and spam TP; Dragoons have lances and concentrate on physical attack. They all have AoE TP abilities and magic. Transmogrification is still a very dangerous ability. However, these Mammets are significantly weaker (relative to the party) than the 19 Epsilon variety. They have 4000 HP each.\010\010They are resistant to Sleep; however, they are susceptible to Bind and Shadowbind (the latter of which can buy up to 30 seconds).\010\010Due to the size of the battlefield, kiting individual Mammets is no longer much of an option. Tanking is a safer bet. Ninja (and jobs that sub Ninja) can blink tank individual Mammets; Paladins can hold one, maybe two, for damage-dealers to finish off; Summoner Avatars and Beastmaster pets can tank single Mammets for a while.\010\010Yellow Liquid will again drop from defeated Mammets, as the fight goes on, so you may want to set one person to Quartermaster--that way, they can be immediately used. It can still be used to prevent Mammets from changing jobs for thirty seconds. Dragoon seems to to remain the most useful job to lock Mammets into for tanking.\010\010Strategy tips",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Remember to use Yellow Liquid to speed up the fight. Due to the number of additional Mammets and two to three Liquids dropping from each, you'll most likely end the fight with more than you use.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Silence all of the Mammets from the start; Ensure that Silence sticks, even on the Mammets that have melee weapons out. When they switch to their Staves, it will keep them from using -ga AoE magic. (Staff Form may still have increased Silence resistance and shortened duration in general; Elemental Seal may help if Silence is immediately resisted. Debuffers should pay close attention.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Since most of the Mammet moves are AoE, the kiters and the rest of the party should spread out as much as possible to avoid damage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue to watch the log for Transmogrification. If you see yourself healing a Mammet with physical damage, drop target lock and turn around for about fifteen to eighteen seconds, \034testing\034 occasionally with single swings.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="All players need to be self-sufficient at the beginning. If a player is having trouble handling a Mammet until he or she can receive backup, consider altering your strategy.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="An alternative strategy is to have one party member (probably your main tank or a Thief) receive sight aggro from all five Mammets, but do nothing that would \034claim\034 them, or turn their name red (Provoke, use of Yellow Liquid, etc.), When this is done, the member could either run them all into a corner or kite them around. Since the player hasn't done anything aggressive to the Mammets, they have no hate, only aggro, so mages healing them will not receive hate, either. The rest of the party can then pull the Mammets off of the train one at a time, killing them at their leisure.\010\010A Paladin using Bat Earrings and Blinding Potions (or Melody Earrings and Dragonfoe Mambo and Sheepfoe Mambo from a Bard) would be effective for this strategy, as Mammets have poor accuracy. For this, it's best if the Paladin stand in one spot and cure himself rather than trying to kite.\010\010 Note that anyone resting on the battlefield will draw aggro from the unclaimed Mammets, as will a Summoner or Beastmaster releasing a pet (the act of summoning, however, will not cause aggro).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Try to conserve resources; however, don't try to save TP for the next battle, because it will be lost. Your objective should be to finish this fight without any deaths, with as much items as possible, and with no two-hour abilities used. Don't worry about the fight taking a couple of minutes longer as a result.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Also remember that, should it be necessary, you can exit and re-enter the battle an unlimited number of times in order to practice Mammet strategies.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A fair goal would be to have about 36 minutes left on the clock by the time you get through the next cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Omega",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When the mammets are defeated, everyone alive will be returned to full HP/MP (weakened members will still be weakened however). Raise your dead and rest to full as quickly as possible. When ready, re-enter the Battlefield to fight the Biotechnological Weapon Omega.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Omega has around 18,000 HP. It uses damaging AoE attacks, and becomes especially dangerous when its HP reaches 25% or lower. Defeating Omega quickly as soon as it reaches low HP can be the most crucial part of the entire mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Omega has an innate Additional Effect of Stun on all of its physical attacks.\010\010 Initially it attacks about once per 3.6 seconds. Slow+Elegy reduce this to about once per 6 seconds.\010\010 Around 60% it speeds up, so it's attacking about every 4.2 seconds with Slow+Elegy.\010\010 Around 25% it speeds up again, so it attacks about every 2.8 seconds with Slow+Elegy.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Omega is known to use the following abilities:\010From 25-100% HP:\010\010 Ion Efflux: Cone Attack Paralyze (moderate).\010\010 Rear Laser: Used if someone behind Omega gets hate. Damages the attacker and causes Petrification.\010\010 Target Analysis: AoE Absorb-All, like Diabolos's Ultimate Terror. Absorbed by Utsusemi.\010\010 Guided Missile: Physical damage AoE centered on the primary target. ~400 to Paladin, ~700 to others. Absorbed by Utsusemi.\010\010 Hyper Pulse: AoE (magic?) damage and Bind. Strips Utsusemi like a Wyrm Wing attack.\010From 0-25% HP:(Started using occasionally at 50% HP for our pt.)\010\010 Discharger: Gives Omega a Magic Shield effect that makes it 100% resist all spells for a limited period.\010\010Magic Shield does not protect from magic damage in general, just spells; elemental Weapon Skills and Astral Flow are not affected.\010\010Dispel or Magic Finale will not remove Discharger's effect; it must wear off on its own.\010\010Also gives Omega Shock Spikes (~25 damage per hit) for a short time; if the spikes have the same duration as the Magic Shield, that would be a convenient way to see when the Magic Shield has worn off.\010\010 Pile Pitch: Reduces the target's HP to 5% of its current value and resets hate (similar to the Tonberry ability Throat Stab).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Using a CCB Polymer Pump on Omega or Ultima will prevent them from using any special moves for exactly one minute.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Contrary to popular belief, Ultima and Omega DO have a slight HP regen. It is very small and slow but they DO regen HP. After about 5 minutes they gain about 1% HP.\010\010Strategy tips",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When the battle begins, the tank should remain where he or she is, and engage Omega from there. Everyone else should move past Omega and stay in front of the airship door. Everyone should move away from the tank before engaging, as Omega always uses a special attack when it aggroes, and you don't want your mages getting hit by Guided Missile.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Almost all of Omega\226\128\153s moves before 25% HP are AoEs. Mages and ranged attackers should keep as much distance from Omega as possible. Any melee attackers other than the tank need to sub Ninja for Utsusemi to absorb Guided Missile, and stand at the sides of Omega to avoid Ion Efflux and Rear Lasers. If they lose any shadows, they should run away to recast Utsusemi before continuing to attack.\010\010Anyone with a damage-dealing job that can't sub Ninja seems to be best off bringing out their Ranged Weapon for Omega. Ranged Attacks can be used to build TP from a distance; each time the damage-dealers' TP reaches 100, they can run up to Omega, use their Weapon Skill, then quickly run back out of AoE range. They do not have to deal heavy ranged damage or be Rangers to do this, though some damage-dealers sub Ranger in this mission for that purpose.\010\010Once Omega starts using Discharger and Pile Pitch, it won't do any more AoE attacks, so they can move in and melee at this point, and reraise immediately if they get KO'd. Just don't let them suicide on the Shock Spikes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Omega won't go down quickly. Keep chipping away at it, but try not to cause any hate issues; do everything in your power to keep Omega facing the tank and only the tank.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use Yagudo Drinks and Potions, but try to conserve as much as you can for the next battle. However, don't try to save TP for the next battle, because it will be lost. Rest only when someone else can cover your job.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="CCB Polymer Pumps make this mission MUCH easier. Everyone in your party should have one. Plan to use 2 or 3 on Omega. Use one to give you some breathing room after 50% HP if necessary. Just before Omega reaches 25%, use a CCB Polymer Pump. A minute later, use another CCB Polymer Pump.\010\010Try to use a CCB before Omega switches modes and then kill it fast before it can use Discharger.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Below 25%, hit Omega hard to kill it as fast as possible. You probably want to use Astral Flow, Icarus Wings or a melee DD 2-hour to finish off Omega. Discharger will prevent Black Mages from doing any damage. Hundred Fists also doesn't work too well with Discharger, as the Monk will spend a lot of time Stunned and/or kill themselves on the spikes.\010\010 Don't use up all your damage on Omega, though, you'll need plenty for Ultima.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Paladin tanks should not use Invincible on Omega, as the hate reset caused by Pile Pitch will most likely cause them to be ignored altogether.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In the event a party member, who isn't the tank, gains hate after use of Pile Pitch, it may be necessary for that member to kite Omega around until the tank can regain hate. If you're a heavy damage dealer, be prepared to kite it for several seconds if possible.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeating Omega with 15-20 minutes left on the timer would be a modest goal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ultima",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ultima has slightly more HP than Omega (around 15,000). It only uses AoE attacks between 20-40% HP, but it has a wider variety of status-causing abilities, and has a tendency to go around one-shotting everyone once it drops below 20% HP.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ultima has an innate Additional Effect of Paralyze on all of its physical attacks.\010\010 Ultima attacks about every 3.3 seconds, and has Double Attack.\010\010 With Elegy, it attacks about every 5 seconds. With Slow+Elegy, about every 6 seconds.\010\010 Ultima's attacks do not speed up at low HP.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ultima is known to use the following abilities:\010\010From 70%-100% HP:\010\010Wirecutter: Single-target physical damage (~400 to PLD), absorbed by Utsusemi (2 shadows)\010\010Particle Shield: Strong Defense Boost. Remove with Dispel/Magic Finale\010\010Chemical Bomb: Cone Attack Elegy and Slow (stronger than Haste). Remove with two Erases\010\010From 40-70% HP:\010\010Nuclear Waste: Causes a status effect that reduces all elemental resistances by 50. AoE\010Followed 5 seconds later by one of the following elemental Cone Attacks, all of which do 490 damage if unresisted:\010\010Smoke Discharger: Earth damage and Petrification for ten to twenty seconds\010\010Hydro Canon: Water damage and Poison\010\010Cryojet: Ice damage and Paralyze\010\010Turbofan: Wind damage and Silence\010\010Flame Thrower: Fire damage and Plague\010\010High-Tension Discharger: Thunder damage and Stun[?]\010\010From 20-40% HP:\010\010Equalizer: AoE heavy physical damage (300-400 to Paladin, 600-900 HP to others). Absorbed by Utsusemi.\010\010Also Particle Shield and Chemical Bomb\010\010From 0-20% HP:\010\010Antimatter: Heavy \034ranged\034 physical attack (300-900 HP) with a five second charge time; can likely be Stunned. It ignores Utsusemi and Blink, but damage can vary greatly.\010\010Also Particle Shield\010Ultima spams WS at this point: one second after finishing one move, it starts the next.\010\010Strategy tips",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the same placing strategies as Omega: tank where you spawn, all other members on the other side. And again have everyone move away from the tank before pulling to avoid Chemical Bomb.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wipe where you spawn, so you can Reraise if need be.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mages should constantly use Yagudo Drinks, if they don't already have Refresh from a Red Mage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ultima doesn't use any AoE attacks until 40% HP, so melees can move in right away even if they're weakened; just stand to the back or sides.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you have 3 CCB Polymer Pumps and start using them shortly after Ultima starts to use Equalizer, they ought to last until it is dead.\010\010At this point start to use damage two-hours (Mighty Strikes, Astral Flow, Hundred Fists, etc.) and Icarus Wings to wear it down as quickly as possible.\010\010If you run out of CCBs during the Antimatter stage, Invincible can protect everyone for another 30 seconds.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Again, note that Ultima WILL Regenerate HP if left alone and unaggroed, but it is a very slow gain. Over 5 minutes he only gains 1%.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The tank will need lots of White Mage attention, curing and status removal. Make sure the WHM has the meds or support (Mage's Ballad, Refresh) to stay casting without any rest, if necessary.\010\010A Paladin tank has decent survivability in this battle (provided they pack many Hi-Potions), and status effects will not have much of an impact (there have even been reports of parties with a Paladin tank completing this mission without a White Mage!).\010\010A Ninja tank will require more attention, and will need to be Hasted and Erased to keep damage output and shadows up. The Ninja must not cast Utsusemi with both Elegy and Slow on. But trying to keep up Haste early on will drain MP fast, so you may want to skip it until Ultima stops using Chemical Bomb.\010\010The White Mage should Haste themselves to lower Erase recast time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Keep mages as far away as possible to limit damage from the very deadly Equalizer.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It is safe for a Paladin to move around for Cover once Ultima starts using Equalizer, as it won't use any more breath attacks after that point.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete the mission successfully and you will appear in Lufaise Meadows. At the end of the cutscene, you will obtain a Ducal Guard's Ring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will receive 1,500 experience points upon winning. (Only once per day) You will not receive experience if you are KO'ed upon Ultima's defeat, however.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2520",["title"]="Onion Rings",["page_title"]="Onion Rings",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Onion_Rings",["revision"]="113321",["requirements"]="Start: Kohlo-Lakolo \226\128\148 Port Windurst (G-5)\010Requirements: Received the Castle Oztroja cutscene from Windurst Mission 3-1: To Each His Own Right\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Key item: Old Ring\010Previous: Inspector's Gadget!\010Windurst Mission 3-1: To Each His Own Right",["rewards"]="Bouncer Club",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Now that the Star Onion Brigade has the old Optistery ring, they can unlock the door to the spooky old abandoned Ghostly House. Yikes! Once inside, will they be able to uncover the Cat Burglar's plot and foil her evil scheme? Go, go, Onions!",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must change areas after completing the previous quest. Logging out/in is not enough.\010The quest will not appear in your quest log until returning with the Key item: Old Ring.\010YOU DO NOT HAVE TO CHANGE AREA ANYMORE>",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At the end of the quest Inspector's Gadget!, Kohlo-Lakolo will lament not having the minister's ring to open the door of the House of the Hero.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Castle Oztroja and proceed to Castle Oztroja (I-8) on the first map, where you will find a door with two handles. \010\010One handle will open the door and the other will open a trap door beneath the handles.\010\010You must stand right next to a switch, directly in front of the doorway, to pull a handle.",["zone"]="Castle Oztroja",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Find the handle that opens the trap door, pull it, and fall to the room below.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check a blank target on the floor to find an Key item: Old Ring.\010\010 To receive the Key item: Old Ring you must be the one to pull the lever and activate the trapdoor, you cannot have a high-level friend helping you pull the lever.\010\010It is possible for a Non-Windurst citizen to get the ring. Just touch the trap door and you will get it.\010\010A Windurst citizen must be on or past Windurst Mission 3-1 to get the ring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Checking the target again will open an escape door. \010\010 Dropping down this hole will place you in a long stairway, at the end of which is Castle Oztroja's main courtyard, through which you can easily return to the main exit. This is a safe way out of the castle for players who don't have a means of Warp; however, the Yagudo in the stairway and courtyard are fourth-tier and highly dangerous to anyone under Level 50.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring the ring back to Kohlo-Lakolo. One of two events will occur:\010\010You will be told to go to the House of the Hero in Windurst Walls at Windurst Walls (G-3). There you will check its door to see a cutscene, and the quest will be completed.\010\010You will be told that you were \034too late,\034 receive a similar cutscene, and the quest will be completed.\010(The timer starts as soon as you talk to Kohlo-Lakolo and 3 Earth days was too long. In either case, your reward will not be affected.)\010If you already have the Key item: Old Ring before activating the quest you will just get the final cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Port Windurst (or in the latter case, zone out of Port Windurst and zone back in), then speak to Kohlo-Lakolo again to obtain your reward.\010If you didn't get your Bouncer Club please zone out and zone back in and talk to Kohlo-Lakolo once more.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3703",["title"]="Only the Best",["page_title"]="Only the Best",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Only_the_Best",["revision"]="117446",["requirements"]="Start: Melyon \226\128\148 Selbina (I-9)\010Items: La Theine Cabbage x5 or\010Millioncorn x3 or\010Boyahda Moss x1",["rewards"]="100g-600g depending on items turned in",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade Melyon any of the below to complete the quest.\010\010La Theine Cabbage x5 = 100g reward (240g/stack)\010\010Millioncorn x3 = 120g reward (480g/stack)\010\010 You can trade a full stack (12) of Millioncorn to Melyon and he'll only take 3.\010\010Boyahda Moss x1 = 600g reward (7200g/stack)\010\010 The following macro can be used to trade the Moss while directly facing Melyon.\010This macro will only work with Boyahda Moss because it is not possible to trade more than one item at a time via a macro.\010\010 /targetnpc\010\010 /item \034Boyahda Moss\034 <t>",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This Quest will raise Reputation in two of the main nations (Bastok and San d'Oria) plus Jeuno. It does not affect Windurst reputation. Contrary to popular rumor, this quest has been shown NOT to lower Tenshodo (Norg) reputation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It takes approximately 5 seconds per trade when using the Boyahda Moss macro and going through the NPC chat prompts as quickly as possible; mostly due to Melyon having extended pauses between chat lines.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Achieving Specific Reputation Levels\010\010Entries without the caution symbol have been confirmed by Horizon users (see \034Discussion\034 page.) Add testimonials to discussion page if you have new info, but please note before editing: this table is only for fresh characters with 0 regional quests and 0 missions completed!\010\010|align=\034center\034 colspan=\0344\034|Bastok/San d'Oria/Jeuno reputation from Millioncorn: (from zero reputation)\010|- \010!width=\03420%\034|Total Stacks\010!width=\03420%\034|Total # of trades\010!width=\03430%\034|Bastok & San d'Oria Reputation Level\010!width=\03430%\034|Jeuno Reputation Level\010|- \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|2\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034|9\010|align=\034center\034|36\010|align=\034center\034|3\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|4\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|- \010|align=\034center\034|14\010|align=\034center\034|56\010|align=\034center\034|5\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|-\010|align=\034center\034|24\010|align=\034center\034|96\010|align=\034center\034|6\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034|25\010|align=\034center\034|100\010|align=\034center\034|7\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|8\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034|30\010|align=\034center\034|120\010|align=\034center\034|9\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification]\010|align=\034center\034 colspan=\0344\034|Bastok/San d'Oria/Jeuno reputation from Boyahda Moss: (from zero reputation)\010|- \010!width=\03420%\034|Total Stacks\010!width=\03420%\034|Total # of trades\010!width=\03430%\034|Bastok & San d'Oria Reputation Level\010!width=\03430%\034|Jeuno Reputation Level\010|- \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|2\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|3\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|4\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|- \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|5\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|-\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|6\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|7\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|8\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034|7 [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|84 [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|9\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification]\010|align=\034center\034 colspan=\0344\034|Bastok/San d'Oria/Jeuno reputation from La Theine Cabbage: (from zero reputation)\010|- \010!width=\03420%\034|Total Stacks\010!width=\03420%\034|Total # of trades\010!width=\03430%\034|Bastok & San d'Oria Reputation Level\010!width=\03430%\034|Jeuno Reputation Level\010|- \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|2\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034|30\010|align=\034center\034|72\010|align=\034center\034|3\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|4\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034|60\010|align=\034center\034|144\010|align=\034center\034|5\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|-\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|6\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034|90\010|align=\034center\034|216\010|align=\034center\034|7\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|align=\034center\034|8\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification] \010|- \010|align=\034center\034|120\010|align=\034center\034|288\010|align=\034center\034|9\010|align=\034center\034| [Wiki: needs verification]\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Melyon (Outside the Weavers' Guild, Selbina)\010 / summary=Melyon will pay premium prices for any of the following: five heads of La Theine cabbage, three ears of millioncorn, one clump of Boyahda moss.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57033",["title"]="Operation Teatime",["page_title"]="Operation Teatime",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Operation_Teatime",["revision"]="123859",["requirements"]="Start: Iruki-Waraki \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-9)\010Requirements: The Wayward Automaton completed\010Level: Puppetmaster 50\010Fame: Aht Urhgan\010Items: Sleeping Potion\010\010 Chai\010\010 Lamian Fang Key\010Previous: The Wayward Automaton",["rewards"]="Puppetry Churidars",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Iruki-Waraki needs your help recovering his automaton from the thief who stole it.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Zone after completing The Wayward Automaton.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Iruki-Waraki in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-9) as Puppetmaster level 50 or higher.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Iruki-Waraki:\010\010 1 Sleeping Potion\010\010 1 Chai - This can be bought from Fayeewah at the Shararat Teahouse in Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-12) for 68 gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Nashmau and speak with Dnegan at Nashmau (H-6).\010\010 Do not choose \034Ask about the automaton.\034\010\010 Choose either of the other first dialogue options to continue.",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="H-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When asked what to drink, choose either Chai or coffee.\010\010 Do not choose \034I'll pass, thanks.\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When choosing a cup, select the cup with the suspicious VAPOR.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Lamian Fang Key.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Arrapago Reef from Caedarva Mire at Caedarva Mire (I-6).",["zone"]="Caedarva Mire",["grid"]="I-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the Lamian Fang Key to pass through the Iron Gate at Arrapago Reef (J-10). in Arrapago Reef.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="J-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exit the enclosed area through the north Iron Gate Arrapago Reef (J-8).",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue through Arrapago Reef and exit back into Caedarva Mire at Arrapago Reef (J-6).",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="J-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the ??? at Caedarva Mire (K-5) / Map 1/6 for a cutscene and reward.\010SIDE NOTE: DO NOT DROP DOWN THE LEDGE BY ACCIDENT!!!",["zone"]="Caedarva Mire",["grid"]="K-5 / Map 1",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="ToAU",["jobs"]={"Puppetmaster (PUP)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Puppetmaster (PUP)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Puppetry Churidars",["revision"]="122655"}}},{["id"]="wiki_2527",["title"]="Orastery Woes",["page_title"]="Orastery Woes",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Orastery_Woes",["revision"]="114063",["requirements"]="Start: Kuroido-Moido \226\128\148 Port Windurst (E-7)\010Requirements: Able to wield Club of Trials\010Club Skill 230+",["rewards"]="Black Halo Weapon Skill",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The Operations Division of the Orastery has asked you to assist them in their plan to deliver the ministry from misery. Use the magical club that you have been given to record combat information for the Orastery.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Kuroido-Moido in Port Windurst (E-7) (inside the Orastery). He will give you the Club of Trials and the Key item: Weapon Training Guide.",["zone"]="Port Windurst",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the Club of Trials until the latent effect disappears. \010\010How to remove the latent effect: \010\010You must perform Weapon Skills and Skillchains on monsters that check as Easy Prey or higher. \010\010You can not gain points in Campaign Battles, Besieged, etc.\010\010You get 1 point for performing the weapon skill Starlight regardless of the opponent.\010\010Weapon Skills performed while under Level Sync count.\010\010You receive 1 point for opening/soloing a weapon skill, 2 points for closing a Lv.1 Skillchain, 3 points for closing a Lv.2 Skillchain and 5 points for closing a level 3 Skillchain.\010\010You must accumulate 300 total points.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you no longer receive the latent effect bonus, head back to Port Windurst and trade the Club of Trials back to Kuroido-Moido, who will take the weapon from you and give you a Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth and tell you to head to Ro'Maeve.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in Ro'Maeve go to Ro'Maeve (M-8) and click the ??? to spawn the NM named Eldhrimnir (best camp is at far south end in Ro'Maeve (M-10), just a few mobs to kill for clear path to ???).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the NM is dead, re-examine the ??? to obtain the Key item: Annals of Truth.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring this back to Kuroido-Moido for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="PLEASE NOTE: If you have another Weapon Skill Notorious Monster quest opened and not finished, you will not be able to acquire the Club of Trials.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can cancel an active quest by talking to the quest-giver again and choosing to give up.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You must have your BASE club skill at 230. Merits that add skill levels do not count.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4841",["title"]="Orlando's Antiques",["page_title"]="Orlando's Antiques",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Orlando%27s_Antiques",["revision"]="100395",["requirements"]="Start: Orlando - Mhaura (G-9)\010Requirements: Windurst Reputation 2\010Items: Fish Bones or\010Chicken Bone or\010Goblin Die or\010Rotten Meat or\010Goblin Cup or\010Fingernail Sack or\010Teeth Sack or\010Beastcoin or\010Silver Beastcoin or\010Mythril Beastcoin or\010Gold Beastcoin",["rewards"]="100g-900g, depending on items turned in",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Orlando is a collector seeking \034junk\034 buried by Goblins.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="These items may be dug up while on a Chocobo. They may be found by tracing the path of Goblin Diggers. The diggers will occasionally stop to bury an item. Wait for them to move on, then dig at the spot the item was buried to retrieve it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Many of these items may also be purchased (from other players). In some cases, a few may also be obtained through Mining or Excavation. Buying these items will be a less time-intensive method for completing the quest, though they can cost more than the reward you will obtain.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a stack of eight of one type of item to Orlando. (He will only accept items in stacks of eight.) Rewards vary by the type of item traded:\010\010Fish Bones - 100 Gil \010\010Chicken Bone - 120 Gil \010\010Goblin Die - 120 Gil \010\010Rotten Meat - 150 Gil \010\010Goblin Cup - 200 Gil \010\010Fingernail Sack - 200 Gil \010\010Teeth Sack - 250 Gil \010\010Beastcoin - 600 Gil \010\010Silver Beastcoin - 750 Gil \010\010Mythril Beastcoin - 800 Gil \010\010Gold Beastcoin - 900 Gil",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You must speak with Orlando again before you are able to trade another 8 items.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Orlando (Orlando's Antiques, Mhaura)\010 / summary=Find where the Goblins bury their junk. Bring back eight of the same type and Orlando will reward you well.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7502",["title"]="Out of One's Shell",["page_title"]="Out of One's Shell",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Out_of_One%27s_Shell",["revision"]="108457",["requirements"]="Start: Ronan \226\128\148 Port Bastok (K-6)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Shell Bug x 3\010Previous: The Quadav's Curse",["rewards"]="Monk's Headgear",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Ronan wants you to help him get his son, Corann, \034to come out of his shell.\034 (Or at least his Quadav shell...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Ronan to activate the quest.\010\010(optional) Talk to Mine Konte Port Bastok (D-7) and then with Panana.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade 3 Shell Bugs to Ronan.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Give him his \034time\034 by zoning out of Port Bastok and back in. Talk to him again for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_51856",["title"]="Out of the Depths",["page_title"]="Out of the Depths",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Out_of_the_Depths",["revision"]="120269",["requirements"]="Start: Ayame \226\128\148 Metalworks (K-7)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Hoary Bomb Ash x 11",["rewards"]="2,200 Gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A Goblin lair known as Movalpolos has suddenly appeared in North Gustaberg. Ayame wishes you to investigate this lair with the cooperation of a visiting scholar waiting in Port Bastok.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Ayame at Ayame, for a cutscene. Accept her job offer to start the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next go talk to Ravorara in Port Bastok (E-7) in front of the Steaming Sheep Resturant.",["zone"]="Port Bastok",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Oldton Movalpolos and talk to Brakobrik at Oldton Movalpolos (K-11) and select the option \034I getting you.\034",["zone"]="Oldton Movalpolos",["grid"]="K-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Ancient Bombs to gather Hoary Bomb Ashes. (11 are required for the quest, get 12 to be sure)\010\010Ancient Bombs are found in the tunnels across the zone and can drop up to 4 Hoary Bomb Ashes. \010\010Hoary Bomb Ash cannot be bought/sold on the Auction House but traded and bought/sold on Bazaars.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Brakobrik and trade him the Hoary Bomb Ashes in chunks:\010\0101 Hoary Bomb Ash will get you a Key item: Dusty Tome\010\0102 Hoary Bomb Ashes will get you a Key item: Pointed Jug\010\0103 Hoary Bomb Ashes will get you a Key item: Cracked Club\010\0104 Hoary Bomb Ashes will get you a Key item: Peeling Hairpin",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After obtaining all four Key Items, return to Ravorara in Port Bastok (E-7).",["zone"]="Port Bastok",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Ravorara four times - once for each key item. You will receive a total of 1,000 gil for these four items (100, 200, 300, 400g).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back to Oldton Movalpolos and trade one more Hoary Bomb Ash to Brakobrik. When he asks if you'll accept his item or not, choose NOT to accept it this time. He will thengive you the Key item: Old Nametag. **If he gives you another Key item: Dusty Tome instead of the Key item: Old Nametag, trade him one more Hoary Bomb Ash to recieve the Key item: Old Nametag.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Port Bastok (E-7) and speak with Ravorara.",["zone"]="Port Bastok",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Then go to Bastok Mines (I-7) and speak with Pavvke, located in a house on the lower level, for the final cutscene and your reward.",["zone"]="Bastok Mines",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_51857",["title"]="Out of the depths (A Question of Faith)",["page_title"]="A Question of Faith",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/A_Question_of_Faith",["revision"]="104308",["requirements"]="Start: Ayame \226\128\148 Metalworks (K-7)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 5\010Previous: Out of the Depths",["rewards"]="3000 Gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A holy tome was among the items you retrieved from Movalpolos. A friar known as Virnage is asking for the help of an adventurer to investigate this matter further.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Ayame at Metalworks (K-7) (upper level) to start the quest.",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="K-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, go to Bastok Mines and talk to Virnage at (Bastok Mines (I-5)) (in the Bats Lair Inn) to receive the Key item: Dawn Talisman.",["zone"]="Bastok Mines",["grid"]="I-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next head out to Oldton Movalpolos to speak with Rakorok at (Oldton Movalpolos (K-10)). \010\010When you click on Rakorok, the NM Bugallug (level 45-50) will immediately appear. Defeat Bugallug.",["zone"]="Oldton Movalpolos",["grid"]="K-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Rakorok again, and get a cut-scene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back to Bastok Mines and speak with Virnage again to get your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3724",["title"]="Over the Hills and Far Away",["page_title"]="Over the Hills and Far Away",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Over_the_Hills_and_Far_Away",["revision"]="118669",["requirements"]="Start: Antreneau \226\128\148 Port San d'Oria (G-7)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 8\010Items: Moblin Hotrok",["rewards"]="Map of the Uleguerand Range",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Antreneau's Uncle Louverance set out on a journey to cross the Uleguerand Range quite some time ago. Antreneau tells you that the other side of the mountains can be reached through a cave found on the slopes of Thousandfall Ridge...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="To activate this quest, first go to the second floor of the house at (G-7) in Southern San d'Oria.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Read the diary there a couple of times until you have read Page 4.\010\010Pages 2 and 3 of the diary refer to the quests A Squire's Test II and The Medicine Woman, which do not need to be completed to get to the page 4, unless they have been activated.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Antreneau in the Rusty Anchor Pub in Port San d'Oria.\010\010The quest A Taste For Meat might interfere with Antreneau speaking about Uleguerand Range. Complete A Taste For Meat and restart the walkthrough starting with reading the Diary at (G-7) in Southern San d'Oria. If Antreneau continues to say, \034All right, then! I am ready to eat!\034 you do not have sufficient Reputation to participate in this quest.\010\010Although previously listed as having a reputation requirement of 9, it has since been confirmed that the quest can be flagged by having a San d'Oria reputation of 8.\010\010If you're still unable to get the cutscene from Antreneau, complete the quest The Medicine Woman and try again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He will tell you that the Map of the Uleguerand Range is top secret and his uncle has gone there to investigate the mountains. He asks you to find his uncle and tell him he wishes him back soon.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Now you have the quest, but first you need a Moblin Hotrok. \010\010Moblin Hotroks are dropped by the Moblin Ashman in Oldton Movalpolos and Moblin Groundman in Newton Movalpolos . There is a Moblin Ashman spawn at (K-10) in the \034pit\034 area at the center of the platforms.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After obtaining the Moblin Hotrok, go to Uleguerand Range.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will need to find a ??? in the caves at around (F-8), but it cannot be reached directly from the entrance. Once in Uleguerand Range, you'll need to make your way counter-clockwise across the zone, slowly climbing to the top of the Thousandfall Ridge. \010\010Do not jump down holes on the way.\010\010Use sneak and invisible. \010\010Avoid Brontotaurs, Tyrannotaurs and Molechs, which are true sight.\010\010Avoid Jormungand, a HNM which spawns in your path and also has true sight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you are at the top, start walking towards (F-8) and you will see two slopes. One to the south and one to the west.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you slide down the southern slope, you need to land on a small ledge leading to cave S3 on the map of the Southern Slope to the right.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you slide down the western slope, you need to land on a small ledge leading to cave W2 on the map of the Western Slope to the right.\010\010If you fall into one of the holes on the slopes (S1 or W1), you must go back onto the slope and land on the proper ledge.\010\010Once you start down a slope, you're committed. You can steer a little to the left and right and you can slow your descent by running against gravity. If you miss the outcropped cave ledge, you will have to climb back up the entire mountain.\010\010It is possible to have Tractor cast on you to put you on the ledge should you miss.\010\010S1 and W1 lead to the black tunnel path which can be seen in the cave insert on the Uleguerand Range map to the right. Caves S2 and W3 lead to the white path. The ledges you seek (S3 or W2) lead to the red path and the ???.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you reach either S3 or W2, follow the path to the ???.\010\010There is also a hole above W3 that's leads to the W2 path. There is an eye at the bottom of the hole so sneak or silent oil is recommended before going down.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade in the Moblin Hotrok for a cutscene and to complete the quest.\010\010You will receive a different reward if you already have bought a Map of the Uleguerand Range. This is also reflected in the dialogue, which will mention \034a reward\034 rather than the map explicitly.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1813",["title"]="Overnight Delivery",["page_title"]="Overnight Delivery",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Overnight_Delivery",["revision"]="113538",["requirements"]="Start: Kenapa-Keppa \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (J-9) / South\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 2\010Previous: Food for Thought",["rewards"]="Power Gi",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You couldn't quite make out what Kenapa-Keppa was trying to say, but you guess he wants you to go pick up something from Mhaura. This doesn't look like your ordinary delivery job...?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must change areas after completing the previous quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Kenapa-Keppa in the Rhinostery until he gives you this quest. You must talk to him after 7:00 Vana'diel time.\010\010You must talk to Kenapa-Keppa four times and tell him you accept the quest before you can go to Mhaura.\010\010 If you have the quest Say It with Flowers started, Kenapa-Keppa may just mumble about Tahrongi Canyon and how dangerous it is. Finish that quest first, then you can proceed with this one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Mhaura and look for Kotan-Purutan. He stands at (Mhaura (I-9)) talk to him during night hours (after 18:00); he will give you a Key item: Small Bag to take back.",["zone"]="Mhaura",["grid"]="I-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You have to make it back to Kenapa-Keppa before dawn (6:00) for your reward. \010\010If you log out or disconnect after you get the key item, it will disappear from your inventory when you get back.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional: Talk to Ohbiru-Dohbiru.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_10090",["title"]="Painful Memory",["page_title"]="Painful Memory",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Painful_Memory",["revision"]="74374",["requirements"]="Start: Mertaire \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (I-8)\010Requirements: Bard 40+\010Items: Key item: Mertaire's Bracelet\010Previous: Path of the Bard",["rewards"]="Paper Knife",["repeatable"]="af",["summary"]="Take Mertaire's bracelet to Ranguemont Pass and immerse it in the Waters of Oblivion.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Mertaire inside the Merry Minstrel's Meadhouse, and he'll ask you to get rid of a bracelet for him. Agree to help him and you'll receive Key item: Mertaire's Bracelet.\010\010You can change jobs after receiving the key item if you wish. You do not have to be a Bard to fight Tros.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Ranguemont Pass (D-5) and interact with the Waters of Oblivion to spawn Tros.",["zone"]="Ranguemont Pass",["grid"]="D-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Tros and click the Waters of Oblivion again for a cutscene and your Paper Knife.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Bard (BRD)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Bard (BRD)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Paper Knife",["revision"]="118218"},{["job"]="Bard (BRD)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Painful Memory",["revision"]="74374"}}},{["id"]="wiki_53391",["title"]="Paradise, Salvation, and Maps",["page_title"]="Paradise, Salvation, and Maps",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Paradise%2C_Salvation%2C_and_Maps",["revision"]="107159",["requirements"]="Start: Nivorajean \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold (I-9) / Map 1\010Requirements: The Secrets of Worship or later, to have access to the Sacrarium\010Items: Sacrarium Chest Key\010Key item: Piece of Ripped Floorplans\010Sealion Crest Key (possible, depending on chest location)\010Coral Crest Key (possible, depending on chest location)",["rewards"]="Map of the Sacrarium",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="To complete a map of the Sacrarium, Nivorajean needs you to find a piece of the old floorplans.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Nivorajean at (I-9) on the main floor of the Tavnazian Safehold to receive the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Sacrarium.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Sacrarium Chest Key.\010\010If your main job is Thief, you may attempt to pick the chest instead of getting a chest key.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Locate a Treasure Chest, but, IMPORTANT!** before you open it, note the <pos> where it is and write it down.\010\010If the Treasure Chest is at H-9, there are two ways to access this area.\010\010If you don't have a Temple Knight Key, you will need another player to help you. One of you must have a Sealion Crest Key and the other must have a Coral Crest Key to open the Small Keyhole/Large Keyhole door.\010\010If you DO have a Temple Knight Key, you can use it to open this door solo.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Open the Treasure Chest to obtain the Key item: Piece of Ripped Floorplans.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Nivorajean who will ask you where you found the floorplans. \010\010He will first show you the map on which the treasure chests are found, and then give you a listing of locations from which you must choose the <pos> where your treasure chest was. \010\010You may choose to take another look at the map, by selecting \034Think a little longer.\034 but you cannot cancel the NPC dialog unless you forcibly disconnect (and you will presumably keep the Key item: Piece of Ripped Floorplans.\010\010! width=\03420%\034|Chest Location\010! width=\03480%\034|Choices Given (Bold correct answer)\010|-\010|align=\034center\034 |H-9\010|align=\034center\034 |F-7 G-7 H-7 F-9 G-9 H-9\010|-\010|align=\034center\034 |L-8\010|align=\034center\034 |J-7 K-7 I-8 L-8 J-9 K-9\010|-\010|align=\034center\034 |F-5\010|align=\034center\034 |F-5 G-5 H-5 F-11 G-11 H-11\010|-\010|align=\034center\034 |H-5\010|align=\034center\034 |F-5 G-5 H-5 F-11 G-11 H-11 \010|-\010|align=\034center\034 |J-5/J-6\010|align=\034center\034 |I-6 J-6 K-7 K-9 I-10 J-10\010|-\010|align=\034center\034 |F-11\010|align=\034center\034 |F-5 G-5 H-5 F-11 G-11 H-11 \010|-\010|align=\034center\034 |H-11\010|align=\034center\034 |F-5 G-5 H-5 F-11 G-11 H-11\010|-\010|align=\034center\034 |J-10\010|align=\034center\034 |I-6 J-6 K-7 K-9 I-10 J-10",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From the start of the following game-day, if you chose the correct <pos>, he will reward you with the Map of the Sacrarium.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Nivorajean again at the start of the next game day to receive your map.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57146",["title"]="Passing Glory",["page_title"]="Passing Glory",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Passing_Glory",["revision"]="121666",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1\010Previous: Guests of the Empire",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Your reward from the Empress has been confiscated by President Naja. Earn the right to wear it by becoming the best mercenary you can be.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7515",["title"]="Past Perfect",["page_title"]="Past Perfect",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Past_Perfect",["revision"]="104357",["requirements"]="Start: Evi \226\128\148 Port Bastok (H-6)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 2",["rewards"]="Scale Mail",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Bring Evi his old mission orders, buried near one of the windmills on the Konschtat Highlands.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Evi, talk to Rafaela next to him, and then talk to Evi again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Konschtat Highlands and select the ??? near the windmills at Konschtat Highlands (G-8) to receive the Key item: Tattered Mission Orders.",["zone"]="Konschtat Highlands",["grid"]="G-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Port Bastok and talk to Evi to deliver the orders and complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_567",["title"]="Past Sins (Louverance's Path) (Promathia Mission 5-3/Louverance's Path)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 5-3/Louverance's Path",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_5-3%2FLouverance%27s_Path",["revision"]="120781",["requirements"]="Start: Cid \226\128\148 Metalworks (H-8)\010Level: 60 Cap (BCNM)\010Previous: Desires of Emptiness",["rewards"]="1000 Experience Points",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Louverance has set off on his investigation into the celestial capital of Al'Taieu.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Despachiaire in Tavnazian Safehold (K-10) / Map 2, top level, behind Walnut Door).",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="K-10 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="5-3L1: Southern Legend",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Perih Vashai in Windurst Woods (K-7).",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="K-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="5-3L2: Partners Without Fame",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Bibiki Bay (H-7), buy a ticket from Tswe Panipahr and take the Manaclipper to Bibiki Bay - Purgonorgo Isle (H-11), and examine the ??? Warmachine.\010\010Talk to Fheli Lapatzuo at Bibiki Bay (H-7) at the docks to find out where the next ferry is headed since there are different destinations for the ferries.\010\010Alternatively, you can use a Summer Swimsuit such as the Custom Gilet +1 to get to Bibiki Bay - Purgonorgo Isle",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Talk to Yoran-Oran in Windurst Walls (E-5) (No cutscene)",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="E-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="5-3L3: A Century of Hardship",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mine Shaft #2716 - Level 60 Cap BCNM - A Century of Hardship",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Oldton Movalpolos for a cutscene with Louverance.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Mine Shaft #2716 for BCNM fight (A Century of Hardship). \010\010(See Navigating Newton Movalpolos for options and details on how to reach Mine Shaft #2716.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will enter the battlefield facing four Moblins and one Bugbear:\010\010Moblins:\010\010Chekochuk (Black Mage)\010\010Movamuq (White Mage)\010\010Swipostik (Thief)\010\010Trikotrak (Red Mage)\010\010Bugbear:\010\010Bugbby (Warrior)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bugbby uses the Warrior two-hour ability Mighty Strikes, and attacks twice each round like a Monk.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bugby is extremely susceptible to Stun.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="All Moblins possess two-hour abilities for their job and all have the ability to call Bugbby to the center of the Battlefield, ignoring any kiting in progress and resetting hate. Whoever is kiting Bugbby should make sure to reclaim hate when this happens.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="All mobs in this BC are highly resistant to Sleep/Sleepga, though Elemental Seal has been known to assist in making it stick for a few seconds.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="1000 Experience Points awarded to each member, even on first win.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="No Experience Points loss on death.\010\010Strategy tips\010\010 Kiting the Moblins can make this fight much easier. Ensure your party is capable of kiting one Moblin each) (melees with higher HP are recommended) while your main tank kites Bugbby in the meantime. Gravity will help. Bugbby is not completely resistant to bind on Horizon, it can be landed. (Confirmed 17th July 2023).\010\010 Assist your highest-damaging DD (Damage Dealer) in killing the moblin that he or she is tanking, first, then assist your main healer on any Moblin(s) that he or she might have pulled in the meantime.\010\010 Remember to Silence Chekochuk, Movamuq and Trikotrak early, in that order. Chekochuk takes priority from the very beginning for Silence order, as his magic is highly damaging, in addition to his potential use of Sleepga.\010\010 With all of the Moblins dead, there will be no reason to rush when fighting Bugbby. Take him down slowly, recover your MP, and stay alive.\010\010Different parties have different strategies as to which Moblins to kite and which to tank. (Some have even successfully taken Bugbby before the Moblins.) Adjust your strategy as needed to suit your party. Many claim this to be the easiest of the three BC battles in this mission.\010\010Bugbby is immune to Charm-bind, but the Moblins can't call him if he's all the way back at the entrance of the BC. A BST can pull him to the entrance and use a jug pet to keep him occupied while the rest of the party deals with the Moblins.\010\010The \034Super-Kite\034 strategy works here like it does for the Mammets. One party member runs in, gets aggro from all the mobs, and kites them around while the rest of the party pulls off one at a time. The moblins will all keep following the kiter, though Buggby will break off when he is called unless he's back at the entrance at the time. NIN is good for this at night with Ninja AF, and provoke for if Buggby gets called away.\010Note: You need to stay within 10' of the mobs while kiting, if any get out of range they will catch up/teleport to you. This is more advanced for those who have done kiting as the arena is quite narrow causing you to more easily get cornered if they catch up.\010With this strategy, anyone resting or releasing a pet will get aggro from the kited mobs.\010\010A variant is the \034Super-Paladin\034 strategy, where your main Paladin tank gets initial aggro and just lets everything beat on him while the party kills one at a time.\010Note: If someone other than the Paladin gets hate from the Moblin you're killing, they can send Buggby after them. So either the Paladin needs to provoke Buggby, or the party needs to avoid pulling hate from him on the Moblins.\010As usual with this strategy, anyone resting or releasing a pet will get aggro from the kited mobs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="5-3L4: Departures",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to the Metalworks (H-8), and speak with Cid.",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Farm one Gold Key per person from the lower level Moblins in Newton Movalpolos.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Mine Shaft #2716 and trade the Gold Key to the BC entrance for another cutscene. NB: You will need another Snow Lilly if you used this method of transportation before. Or you can gamble. Snow Lilly's are usually cheaper.\010Logistical Note: If you are in a party (CoP static, for example) and helping with the moblin/bugbear fight from the previous phase of the mission, do not trigger this cutscene before you enter the battlefield. The cutscene spits you out at the battlefield exit in Newton Movalpolos, and you will not be able to Escape and teleport back to Mine Shaft #2716 if you have just used Twinkbrix to get there. But you can use the Moblin just outside the exit and pay him 2000 Gil and choose to warp back to the mine shaft entrance. That will bring you right back to the BCNM.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Metalworks and talk to Cid again for a cutscene, ending this fork.\010\010If Louverance's Path is your final path to complete on Mission 5-3, you will get an additional cutscene at Cid that leads into the next mission; If not, you may head to another fork.\010\010! colspan=\0343\034 | Three Paths Overview\010|- class=\034copmissions-alt\034\010! Fork 1\010! Fork 2\010! Fork 3\010|-\010|align=\034center\034 | Tenzen Path\010|align=\034center\034 | Ulmia Path\010|align=\034center\034 | Louverance Path",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57170",["title"]="Path of Blood",["page_title"]="Path of Blood",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Path_of_Blood",["revision"]="120881",["requirements"]="Previous: Gaze of the Saboteur",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have returned unharmed from your close encounter with the underworld, but were unable to rescue Nashmeira. Follow her last orders and deliver her message to President Naja.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Gaze of the Saboteur; this mission begins immediately afterward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Aht Urhgan Whitegate and enter the second platform of Salaheem's Sentinels at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.\010\010 The cutscene triggers automatically as you enter the platform; speaking with Naja Salaheem is not required.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue through the chained cutscenes.\010\010 The game automatically repositions you within Aht Urhgan Whitegate between the two scenes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The second cutscene completes the mission and begins Stirrings of War.\010\010 To continue Stirrings of War, zone once and wait until after the next Japanese midnight (15:00 UTC).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57175",["title"]="Path of Darkness",["page_title"]="Path of Darkness",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Path_of_Darkness",["revision"]="120929",["requirements"]="Start: Blank Target \226\128\148 Nyzul Isle Staging Point, Alzadaal Undersea Ruins (J-9) / Map 5\010Previous: Light of Judgment",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Using the map given to you by Rodin-Comidin, find a route through Nyzul Isle and rescue the captured Luzaf!",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Light of Judgment; this mission begins immediately afterward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ensure you possess the Key item: Nyzul Isle Route.\010\010 If it is missing, speak with Rodin-Comidin at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-7) / Map 1 to receive another.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the Nyzul Isle Staging Point.\010\010 If its Runic Portal has been activated, use a Runic Portal Use Permit at the Chamber of Passage in Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-7) / Map 1.\010\010 Otherwise, speak with Kamih Mapokhalam at Bhaflau Thickets (F-6) / Map 1, trade 1 Imperial Silver Piece if required, and follow the teleporter route to Map 8.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Every player who needs mission credit must examine the Blank Target at Alzadaal Undersea Ruins (J-9) / Map 5 and select \034Yes.\034\010\010 After flagging the battlefield, attempting to enter Salaheem's Sentinels triggers a blocking cutscene until the mission is completed.",["zone"]="Alzadaal Undersea Ruins",["grid"]="J-9 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Runic Seal at Alzadaal Undersea Ruins (I-9) / Map 5 and select \034Path of Darkness.\034\010\010 The party registrant must be on this mission, have activated the Blank Target, and possess the Key item: Nyzul Isle Route.\010\010 The key item is consumed from each entrant carrying it.",["zone"]="Alzadaal Undersea Ruins",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete the instance within 30 minutes while keeping Naja Salaheem alive.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After victory, continue through the automatic cutscene in the Alzadaal Undersea Ruins. It completes the mission, grants the title \034Naja's Comrade-in-arms,\034 and begins Fangs of the Lion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If the Mission Fails",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Rodin-Comidin at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-7) / Map 1 to receive another Key item: Nyzul Isle Route.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3159",["title"]="Path of the Bard",["page_title"]="Path of the Bard",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Path_of_the_Bard",["revision"]="29957",["requirements"]="Start: Mertaire \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (I-8)\010Level: 30\010Previous: A Minstrel in Despair",["rewards"]="Unlocks the Bard job\0103000g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have taken the first step. The path of the bard lies before you.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="This quest is hidden, and does not appear in your quest log until completed.\010You should have already completed The Old Monument & A Minstrel in Despair.\010Do not buy a parchment for the runes; that's only for the quest before this one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="OPTIONAL: Talk with Mataligeat(Lower Jeuno (I-8)) for some insight.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Bki Tbujhja(Lower Jeuno (I-8)) in Lower Jeuno again. She mentions another set of Song Runes in Valkurm Dunes.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the secret beach at the far west of Valkurm Dunes (Valkurm Dunes (C-6)).",["zone"]="Valkurm Dunes",["grid"]="C-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On the hidden beach, head southeast to the bottom right of (Valkurm Dunes (B-7)).",["zone"]="Valkurm Dunes",["grid"]="B-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click on the Song Rune for another cutscene to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Bard (BRD)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Bard (BRD)",["kind"]="Job unlock",["page"]="Bard",["revision"]="123160"}}},{["id"]="wiki_278",["title"]="Path of the Beastmaster",["page_title"]="Path of the Beastmaster",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Path_of_the_Beastmaster",["revision"]="105781",["requirements"]="Start: Brutus \226\128\148 Upper Jeuno (G-7), outside the Chocobo Stables\010Previous: Save My Son",["rewards"]="Ability to become a Beastmaster",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Brutus in Upper Jeuno (G-7) who is standing outside the Chocobo stable, for a final cutscene and to receive the ability to become a Beastmaster. \010\010You may have to talk to him multiple times to get the cutscene.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Beastmaster (BST)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Beastmaster (BST)",["kind"]="Job unlock",["page"]="Beastmaster",["revision"]="122066"}}},{["id"]="wiki_2024",["title"]="Paying Lip Service",["page_title"]="Paying Lip Service",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Paying_Lip_Service",["revision"]="119020",["requirements"]="Start: Tapoh Lihzeh \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (I-8)\010Fame: windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: 3x Beehive Chips\010or\0102x Remi Shells",["rewards"]="150 gil or 200 gil",["repeatable"]="yes",["summary"]="The apothecary has requested your assistance in gathering ingredients for her most popular preparation. She'll pay you for bringing her three Beehive Chips or two Remi Shells.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Tapoh Lihzeh is always in need of some special ingredients. \010\010She will reward you with",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="150 gil for 3 Beehive Chips (can be obtained from Bees in East/West Sarutabaruta or Giddeus).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="200 gil for 2 Remi Shells (can be obtained from River Crabs in East/West Sarutabaruta).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Please note: This quest does not increase your Windurst Fame. E.g. trading in tweleve stacks of beehive chips to Tapoh Linzeh, at zero fame, and then speaking to Zabirego-Hajigo gave the following message: <char name>? Hmm... Now, was that the name of the...? No, that was some other guy. Either way, you're still not making much of a name for yourself here yet. Hard work and perseverance--that's what's going to put you on the map.\010(This is the LV1 Fame response.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1308",["title"]="Peace for the Spirit",["page_title"]="Peace for the Spirit",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Peace_for_the_Spirit",["revision"]="120433",["requirements"]="Start: Curilla \226\128\148 Chateau d'Oraguille (I-9)\010Requirements: Red Mage Level 50+\010Completed Enveloped in Darkness\010Access to Chateau d'Oraguille\010Fame: none\010Items: Antique Coin\010Nail Puller\010Previous: Enveloped in Darkness",["rewards"]="Warlock's Chapeau",["repeatable"]="af",["summary"]="The spirit of Curilla's father Rainemard seems to be trying to say something.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="As a Red Mage, speak to Curilla at Chateau d'Oraguille (I-9) in Chateau d'Oraguille to begin the quest.\010\010 You must be on Red Mage to start the quest, but the remaining steps can be completed on any job.\010\010 If Curilla gives dialogue for The General's Secret instead, complete that quest and speak to her again.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="I-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Sharzalion at Southern San d'Oria (K-6) in the Lion Springs Tavern.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="K-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Fei'Yin from Beaucedine Glacier. If you are on the correct quest step and do not already have an Antique Coin, Miser Murphy will spawn near the Dry Fountain at Fei'Yin (H-8) on the first floor.\010\010 Miser Murphy is immune to Sleep and Silence, and is highly resistant to Bind, Stun, Paralyze, and Blind.\010\010 His melee attacks can occasionally drain a large amount of HP.",["zone"]="Fei'Yin",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Miser Murphy and obtain an Antique Coin.\010\010 Only one Antique Coin drops at a time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Antique Coin to the same Dry Fountain for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Lion Springs Tavern and speak to Sharzalion again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Daggao at Southern San d'Oria (K-5) in the Lion Springs Tavern.\010\010 If Lure of the Wildcat (San d'Oria) is active and Daggao gives unrelated dialogue, speak to him again.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="K-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Garlaige Citadel. Past the first Banishing Gate, examine the Oaken Box at Garlaige Citadel (G-8) / Map 2 in the first room on the left to spawn Guardian Statue.\010\010 You do not need to be on Red Mage to spawn Guardian Statue.\010\010 Guardian Statue is immune to Blind, Sleep, Stun, Paralyze, Slow, and Elegy.",["zone"]="Garlaige Citadel",["grid"]="G-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Guardian Statue and obtain a Nail Puller.\010\010 Only one Nail Puller drops at a time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Nail Puller to the same Oaken Box for a cutscene.\010\010 If you zone out after obtaining the Nail Puller, trade it to the Oaken Box when you return.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Northern San d'Oria for the final cutscene and your Warlock's Chapeau.\010\010 You need at least one free inventory slot. If zoning from your Mog House does not trigger the cutscene, zone from Southern San d'Oria into Northern San d'Oria.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="none",["jobs"]={"Red Mage (RDM)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Red Mage (RDM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Warlock's Chapeau",["revision"]="118356"},{["job"]="Red Mage (RDM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Peace for the Spirit",["revision"]="120433"}}},{["id"]="wiki_12233",["title"]="Personal Hygiene",["page_title"]="Personal Hygiene",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Personal_Hygiene",["revision"]="25596",["requirements"]="Start: Gatih Mijurabi \226\128\148 Kazham (I-8)\010Requirements: Kazham Reputation ?\010Previous: Even More Gullible's Travels\010The Opo-opo and I",["rewards"]="Mithran Stone",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The Mithra of Kazham are having a hard time holding in their lunches, thanks to the hideous odor you obtained after getting too close to the blue Rafflesia pollen. The only way to get clean is by taking a long dip in a hot spring located deep beneath the sea.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Upon completion of Even More Gullible's Travels you will be bathed in a scent from the Rafflesia flowers. This is a scent that Opo-Opos love but Mithra hate. To get rid of this scent, you start by talking to Gatih Mijurabi in M&P's Market in Kazham. She'll mention that you have to go stand under a hot spring somewhere \034deep under the sea.\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Note: Although you can start this quest before The Opo-opo and I, if you ever plan to do The Opo-opo and I, do not get the scent washed off until you have started The Opo-opo and I. Otherwise you will need to get the scent reapplied later (See below). Once you have started that quest, the scent is no longer necessary.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The hot spring is in Korroloka Tunnel at G-9 of the 3rd Map. If you enter from the Zeruhn Mines, head to point B to reach the third map. If you enter from the Eastern Altepa Desert, head to point C to reach the third map.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There are three Jammer Leeches guarding the waterfall. \010\010The mobs are roughly level 60.\010\010Leeches aggro sound and track via scent. If you aggro the Leeches, be sure to run through as many water puddles as possible to lose their scent.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Stand under the waterfall for roughly five minutes. When you leave the waterfall, you will receive a message that tells you the scent has been removed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Gatih Mijurabi in Kazham for completion of the quest and your reward of the Mithran Stone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Quest Completed Too Soon",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you complete this quest before starting The Opo-opo and I and need to reapply the scent, it is still possible to do so.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Rafflesia flowers can be respawned by killing the Jammer Leeches. For each Jammer Leech killed, one flower will respawn.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_52539",["title"]="Petals for Parelbriaux",["page_title"]="Petals for Parelbriaux",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Petals_for_Parelbriaux",["revision"]="104112",["requirements"]="Start: Chemioue \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold / Map 2J-6\010Previous: Promathia Mission 3-5: Darkness Named",["rewards"]="Powerful Rope",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Head to the Top section and talk to Chemioue (Tavnazian Safehold (J-6) / Map 2) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="J-6 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Parelbriaux at (Tavnazian Safehold (K-7) / Map 2) for another cutscene.\010\010If you receive the cutscene about the Mithran Tracker talk to Talk to Despachiaire (Tavnazian Safehold (K-10) / Map 2) start Tango with a Tracker quest then talk to Parelbriaux again for the correct cutscene.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="K-7 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Now go to the Main section and talk to Ondieulix (Tavnazian Safehold (I-7)) for a cutscene, and the actual activation of the quest.\010\010Ondieulix is located at the entrance to Tavnazian Safehold (in the tunnel; past the Home Point)",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Lufaise Meadows to the ??? at (Lufaise Meadows (G-6)); it needs to be selected during fog weather.\010\010Fog shows up sporadically, during the morning from 2:00-7:00. It can only show when there is no weather icon up.\010\010Atomic Clusters will spawn during fog; one will spawn at (Lufaise Meadows (F-7)).",["zone"]="Lufaise Meadows",["grid"]="G-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Flytrap NM Baumesel will spawn when the ??? is selected during fog, and must be defeated.\010\010If multiple people in a group need the quest, it only has to be defeated once for all of them.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the NM is defeated, select the ??? again for a cutscene and to receive a Key item: Particularly poignant petal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Tavnazian Safehold and talk with Ondieulix (Tavnazian Safehold (I-7)) for a cutscene to complete the quest.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7440",["title"]="Pieuje's Decision",["page_title"]="Pieuje's Decision",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Pieuje%27s_Decision",["revision"]="110062",["requirements"]="Start: Door \226\128\148 Chateau d'Oraguille (H-8)\010Requirements: White Mage 50+\010Items: Tavnazia Bell\010Tavnazian Mask\010Previous: Prelude of Black and White",["rewards"]="Healer's Bliaut",["repeatable"]="Yes, see Vingijard after AF is complete",["summary"]="Once you've found a Tavnazia bell in the Eldieme Necropolis, journey to Fei'Yin and commence the battle against the undead.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Make sure you are a White Mage to begin.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the door marked \034Prince Regent's Rm\034, located on south side of the small courtyard at (Chateau d'Oraguille (H-8)) in Chateau d'Oraguille. You will be asked to obtain a Tavnazia Bell.\010\010You do not need to be on White Mage for the rest of this quest in either Eldieme Necropolis or Fei'Yin, including the upcoming battle.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Dark Stalkers in the Eldieme Necropolis until one drops a Tavnazia Bell. \010\010The Dark Stalkers can be found after dropping down A onto the second map, they are around the Hume Bones.\010\010 Four Dark Stalkers can also be found on the first map, two in the north room and two in the far west room.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Fei'Yin for another cutscene. \010\010If you are on Mission 5-1 for your country, you might get the cutscene for this first. Make sure to zone out and back in so that you see the cutscene with the prince and his aide.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Tavnazia Bell to the ??? at (Fei'Yin (J-10) / Map 1) to spawn the NM Altedour I Tavnazia.",["zone"]="Fei'Yin",["grid"]="J-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill him to obtain a Tavnazian Mask.\010\010If you wipe fighting this NM and he depops, you must obtain another Tavnazia Bell to make another attempt.\010\010If you need to do this NM more than once, you must wait 15 minutes to respawn it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the mask to Narcheral upstairs in the cathedral in Northern San d'Oria (Northern San d'Oria (M-6)) to complete the quest.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="M-6",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"White Mage (WHM)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="White Mage (WHM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Healer's Bliaut",["revision"]="26233"},{["job"]="White Mage (WHM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Pieuje's Decision",["revision"]="110062"}}},{["id"]="wiki_14543",["title"]="Pirate's Chart Quest",["page_title"]="Pirate's Chart Quest",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Pirate%27s_Chart_Quest",["revision"]="116608",["requirements"]="Start: Zaldon \226\128\148 Selbina (H-9)\010Level: 20 (capped) (recommended)\010Items: Pirate's Chart\010Previous: Inside the Belly",["rewards"]="Albatross Ring\010Plus three items from the following list: Arrowwood Log, Coral Butterfly, Coral Fragment, Drill Calamary, Dwarf Pugil, Fuscina, High-Quality Pugil Scales, Mercurial Kris, Oxblood, Pamtam Kelp, Salinator, Shall Shell, Zebra Eel",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="This miniquest does not appear in your current or completed quests in the quest log.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Pirate's Chart from Zaldon from the Inside the Belly quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Pirate's Chart to the ??? in Valkurm Dunes on the Whitebone Sands (F-9).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A mysterious tarutaru will appear and start talking about fishing. Start fishing as soon as you can!",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="About 15 seconds after you trade the chart, the tarutaru will die, and three NMs will appear.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Fight",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can have three people total in the fight and once you start, the whole party will be under the effect of level restriction at 20. All buffs except for food will be canceled. Healing from outside party will also be disabled.\010\010Heike Crab (Crab)\010\010Houu the Shoalwader (Sahagin)\010\010Beach Monk (Sea Monk)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="All three have Hundred Fists which they will use at half life. Use any Tarutaru Snares and/or Mithra Snares that you fished up in your 15 seconds above, to impair the NMs and prevent them from using Hundred Fists.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There's a limit of around 10 minutes in this fight. If you can't kill all three NMs within the time limit the message \034Too much time has passed. The monster has lost interest.\034 will appear and all remaining NMs will despawn.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If the battle is lost, a new chart will be needed to start the fight again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill all three to have a Barnacled Box appear, with four items inside it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Also see: Testimonials",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Treasure\010\010|- valign=top\010\010|width=20%|\010|- BGCOLOR=#ffdead\010! One of:\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Coral Fragment [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Drill Calamary [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Dwarf Pugil [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|High-Quality Pugil Scales [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Pamtam Kelp [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Salinator [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Shall Shell [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Zebra Eel [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|width=20%|\010|- BGCOLOR=#ffdead\010! One of:\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Arrowwood Log [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Coral Butterfly [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Coral Fragment [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Drill Calamary [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Dwarf Pugil [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Nebimonite [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Shall Shell [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|width=20%|\010|- BGCOLOR=#ffdead\010! One of:\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Fuscina [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Mercurial Kris [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Oxblood [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|width=20%|\010|- BGCOLOR=#ffdead\010! One of:\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010|Albatross Ring [Template Hxi Drop Rate: 100%]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57155",["title"]="Playing the Part",["page_title"]="Playing the Part",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Playing_the_Part",["revision"]="120860",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1\010Previous: Foiled Ambition",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have obtained your reward from Lady Karababa, but have been reminded of the burden of your duty. Is the Astral Candescence truly so dangerous? Keep improving your reputation with the palace and dig deeper into the mystery...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After completing Foiled Ambition, zone once and wait until after the next Japanese midnight (15:00 UTC).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Naja Salaheem in Salaheem's Sentinels at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.\010\010 Before the zoning and time requirements have been met, Naja only provides additional dialogue and does not advance the mission.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="During the cutscene, select \034Aphmau\034 when prompted to continue.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The cutscene completes the mission and begins Seal of the Serpent.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5447",["title"]="Prelude of Black and White",["page_title"]="Prelude of Black and White",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Prelude_of_Black_and_White",["revision"]="62071",["requirements"]="Start: Door \226\128\148 Chateau d'Oraguille (H-8)\010Requirements: White Mage Lv.50 \010 Access to Chateau d'Oraguille \010\010For citizens of San d'Oria:\010Mission 1-3 \010\010For citizens of Bastok:\010Mission 2-3 \010\010For citizens of Windurst\010Mission 2-3\010Items: Yagudo Holy Water\010Moccasins\010Previous: Messenger from Beyond",["rewards"]="Healer's Duckbills",["repeatable"]="Yes, see Vingijard after AF is complete",["summary"]="White mages of renown will be given a blessed item for the war against the undead. But first, they must bring Yagudo holy water to prove their worth.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Start this quest by checking the door marked \034Prince Regent's Rm\034, which is on the south side of the small courtyard located at (Chateau d'Oraguille (H-8)) in Chateau d'Oraguille. You will be asked to obtain the Yagudo Holy Water and a pair of Moccasins.\010\010Make sure you are a White Mage when clicking the door, if you changed to another job to fight the NM of the previous quest\010\010Moccasins +1 are not accepted.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Castle Oztroja and kill the Yagudo Abbots for the Yagudo Holy Water and Moccasins.\010You may also craft or purchase the Moccasins from the Auction House.\010\010Yagudo Abbots have extremely low drop rate for Moccasins (<1%). \010\010Yagudo Abbots spawn behind the brass door at (Castle Oztroja (G-8) / Map 3) on map 3. \010\010The combination to these levers can be found behind the secret door at (Castle Oztroja (I-10) / Map 3) on the same map.\010\010Yagudo Abbots located at (Castle Zvahl Keep (G-9) / Map 2) & (Castle Zvahl Keep (G-10) / Map 2) on map 2 in Castle Zvahl Keep can also drop Yagudo Holy Water. Although fewer of them spawn in this zone, they are 1-7 levels lower than Yagudo Abbots in Castle Oztroja.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade both items to Narcheral (Northern San d'Oria (M-6)) upstairs in the cathedral in Northern San d'Oria to complete the quest.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="M-6",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"White Mage (WHM)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="White Mage (WHM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Healer's Duckbills",["revision"]="26236"},{["job"]="White Mage (WHM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Prelude of Black and White",["revision"]="62071"}}},{["id"]="wiki_51266",["title"]="President Salaheem",["page_title"]="President Salaheem",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/President_Salaheem",["revision"]="121594",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Salaheem's Sentinels,\010Previous: Immortal Sentries",["rewards"]="Assault access",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have become an employee of Salaheem's Sentinels. Becoming a mercenary is not quite what you expected...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Naja Salaheem at Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10).",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone after the cutscene.\010\010 Entering and exiting the nearby Mog House is sufficient.\010\010 Quick /logout works.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Naja Salaheem again to complete the mission and begin Knight of Gold.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_375",["title"]="Prestige of the Papsque (San d'Oria Mission 7-1)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 7-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_7-1",["revision"]="121203",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 6-2|Ranperre's Final Rest",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The papsque has requested an adventurer of renown. Speak to His Holiness in the cathedral. His chambers lie upstairs.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade crystals to a Conquest NPC to unlock this mission, then talk to any San d'Oria Gate Guard and accept it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Cathedral in Northern San d'Oria and go to the Papal Chambers, located on the third floor at (Northern San d'Oria (M-6)).",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="M-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Form your party (at least a full party of 65+, a party of 70+ should have no problems).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Bostaunieux Oubliette. Head for Bostaunieux Oubliette (E-7) / Map 1 and use Sneak. Speak to the NPC Couchatorage standing by the Sewer Lid to drop down. Follow the right wall to Bostaunieux Oubliette (E-10) / Map 2- where you will zone out to West Ronfaure at (West Ronfaure (E-8)). There will be a ??? in front of you.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When prepared, check the ??? to spawn an Orc NM called Marauder Dvogzog. \010\010It is a level 67 Monk with approximately 16,000 HP. He does use the two hour Hundred Fists.\010\010A level 75 BLM/RDM and a 72 SMN/WHM easily completed it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the ??? again to receive the Ancient San d'Orian Tablet. \010\010Might need to let the body full despawn and disappear.\010\010Should you fall off of the ledge, you'll need to run back through the Oubliette and fight the NM again. If it is popped too early or you happen to zone, you will have to fight the NM again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Cathedral and visit the Papal Chambers for the final cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3706",["title"]="Pretty Little Things",["page_title"]="Pretty Little Things",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Pretty_Little_Things",["revision"]="30846",["requirements"]="Start: Zona Shodhun \226\128\148 Port Jeuno (E-8)\010Fame: jeuno\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Yellow Rock x1",["rewards"]="Exit to any zone within the city from Jeuno Rent-a-Room.",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Zona likes pretty flowers and pebbles. Find some for her.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Zona Shodhun. She's obsessed with flowers and will tell you about gardening. She doesn't ask for help but she collects colored rocks to decorate her garden. (Note that this step is not required).\010\010(Optional) Trade a colored rock to her and she'll say how pretty and smooth it is, but what she really wants is a Yellow Rock.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Yellow Rock to her for your reward.\010Note: <s>This quest will not appear in the quests log.</s>\010As of a past version update, it is now possible to view this quest in the quest log when you talk to the Mithra cub.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57160",["title"]="Prevalence of Pirates",["page_title"]="Prevalence of Pirates",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Prevalence_of_Pirates",["revision"]="120866",["requirements"]="Start: Rishfee \226\128\148 Jade Sepulcher (entrance: Bhaflau Thickets (H-8) / Map 2)\010Previous: Puppet in Peril",["rewards"]="Key item: Periqia Assault Area Entry Permit",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Aphmau and her puppets have been taken by the mysterious Luzaf. Track down the corsair and his captives, and repay Rishfee's noble sacrifice.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Puppet in Peril; this mission begins during its victory cutscene in Jade Sepulcher.\010\010 Speaking with Naja Salaheem afterward provides additional dialogue but is not required for progression.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Arrapago Reef from any entrance for a cutscene.\010\010 The most direct route is to use a Runic Portal Use Permit to reach the Dvucca Isle Staging Point at Caedarva Mire (I-9) / Map 2.\010\010 From the staging point, travel west to the Arrapago Reef entrance at Caedarva Mire (F-9, G-9) / Map 2.\010\010 Other Arrapago Reef entrances and direct Survival Guide travel also trigger the initial cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene, approach the Cutter at Arrapago Reef (H-8) / Map 5.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The resulting cutscene completes the mission, grants the Key item: Periqia Assault Area Entry Permit, and begins Shades of Vengeance.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57553",["title"]="Promotion: Lance Corporal",["page_title"]="Promotion: Lance Corporal",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promotion%3A_Lance_Corporal",["revision"]="122555",["requirements"]="Start: Abquhbah \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1\010Requirements: Complete Promotion: Superior Private\010Accumulate 25 rank-up points as a Superior Private\010Fame: None\010Previous: Promotion: Superior Private",["rewards"]="Key item: LC Wildcat Badge\010Potential currency bonus based on the quality of the mythralline mixture",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Falzum, your fellow mercenary, has been given the task of creating a batch of mythralline liquid. As his superior, it is your job to teach him how a mercenary carries out his duty.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Promotion: Superior Private and accumulate 25 rank-up points as a Superior Private.\010\010 Completing an Assault mission for the first time awards 5 rank-up points.\010\010 Repeating an Assault mission that you have already completed awards 1 rank-up point.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Abquhbah on the upper floor of Salaheem's Sentinels at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1 to begin the quest.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Nafiwaa in the Alchemists' Guild at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-5) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="G-5 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Nafiwaa provides five temporary key items:\010\010 Key item: Empty test tube #1\010\010 Key item: Empty test tube #2\010\010 Key item: Empty test tube #3\010\010 Key item: Empty test tube #4\010\010 Key item: Empty test tube #5",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Fill each test tube at its corresponding Mythralline Wellspring.\010\010 The tubes may be filled in any order.\010\010 All five tubes must be filled before Nafiwaa will begin the first mixing attempt.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mythralline Wellsprings\010\010! Test Tube\010! Wellspring Location\010! Relative Concentration per Pour\010|-\010| #1\010| Wajaom Woodlands (H-11)\010| 1\010|-\010| #2\010| Wajaom Woodlands (G-11)\010| 3\010|-\010| #3\010| Wajaom Woodlands (I-7)\010| 4\010|-\010| #4\010| Wajaom Woodlands (J-8)\010| 3\010|-\010| #5\010| Bhaflau Thickets (G-7) / Map 1\010| 2",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Wajaom Woodlands from Aht Urhgan Whitegate through the Ironbound Gate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Bhaflau Thickets from Aht Urhgan Whitegate through the Ironbound Gate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-7) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="H-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Bhaflau Thickets wellspring is on Map 1 at Bhaflau Thickets (G-7) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Bhaflau Thickets",["grid"]="G-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mixing the Mythralline",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After filling all five tubes, return to Nafiwaa at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-5) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="G-5 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Each test tube contains three portions.\010\010 Selecting a tube during the mixing process uses one-third of its contents.\010\010 The relative concentration values in the table above apply to each one-third portion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Inspecting the tubes provides the following clues:\010\010 Tube #1: The liquid appears to be very light.\010\010 Tube #2: The liquid has the same concentration as Tube #4.\010\010 Tube #3: The liquid appears to be very dense.\010\010 Tube #4: The liquid reacts three times faster than Tube #1.\010\010 Tube #5: The liquid has half the concentration of the densest sample.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select Start the Process to begin combining the liquids.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="For the best result, create Luminium with one of the following combinations:\010\010{| class=\034horizon-table table-md quest-table\034\010! Method\010! Selections\010! Total Concentration\010|-\010| Recommended\010|",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Tube #3 three times",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Tube #2 once",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Tube #4 once",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Tube #5 once\010| 20\010|-\010| Alternate\010|",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Tube #2 twice",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Tube #3 twice",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Tube #4 twice\010| 20\010|}",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select Hand it to the Guild! after completing the desired mixture.\010\010 If you discard the mixture instead, any remaining liquid is retained.\010\010 Return to the corresponding Mythralline Wellsprings to refill the partially used or emptied tubes before trying again.\010\010 Once the mixture is submitted to the guild, all five test-tube key items are removed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mixture Quality and Bonus Reward\010\010The mixture quality is determined by the total relative concentration of the portions used.\010\010{| class=\034horizon-table table-lg quest-table center-col-1\034\010! Concentration Total\010! Mixture\010! Currency Bonus\010|-\010| 2-3\010| Silver\010| None\010|-\010| 4-7\010| Mythril\010| None\010|-\010| 8-11\010| Gold\010| None\010|-\010| 12-19\010| Platinum\010|\010One of the following:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="3-4 Imperial Mythril Pieces",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="1 Imperial Gold Piece\010|-\010| 20\010| Luminium\010| 2 Imperial Gold Pieces\010|-\010| 21\010| Smoke\010| None\010|}",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The LC Wildcat Badge and promotion are awarded regardless of mixture quality.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Platinum randomly awards either the Imperial Mythril Pieces or the single Imperial Gold Piece.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Luminium provides the highest possible currency reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Using too much concentrated mythralline produces smoke and no currency bonus.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Completing the Quest",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After submitting the mixture, wait until the next Vana'diel day.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ensure that you have at least one free inventory slot if your mixture qualifies for a currency reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the Salaheem's Sentinels office area at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1 after the day has changed to trigger the final cutscene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select Helping his fellow mercenaries when prompted.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The quest is completed:\010\010 Your Key item: SP Wildcat Badge is removed.\010\010 Your accumulated rank-up points are reset.\010\010 You receive the Key item: LC Wildcat Badge.\010\010 You receive the title Lance Corporal.\010\010 Lance Corporal Assault missions become available.\010\010 You receive any currency bonus earned from the mythralline mixture.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57417",["title"]="Promotion: Private First Class",["page_title"]="Promotion: Private First Class",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promotion%3A_Private_First_Class",["revision"]="121659",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem - Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) upstairs\010Requirements: Obtain 25 Mercenary Rank points\010Items: Imp Wing\010Previous: President Salaheem",["rewards"]="Key item: PFC Wildcat Badge\010Mog Wardrobe 3: 5 slots [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You will be unable to start this quest if you have started, but not yet completed Path of Darkness.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Naja Salaheem for a cutscene that starts the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Naja an Imp Wing for a cutscene and your promotion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57549",["title"]="Promotion: Superior Private",["page_title"]="Promotion: Superior Private",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promotion%3A_Superior_Private",["revision"]="121969",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1\010Requirements: Complete Promotion: Private First Class\010Accumulate 25 rank-up points as a Private First Class\010Fame: None\010Items: Key item: Dark Rider hoofprint (obtained during the quest)\010Previous: Promotion: Private First Class",["rewards"]="Key item: SP Wildcat Badge\010Access to Superior Private-rank Assault missions",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Your task is to find some hard evidence that the \034Dark Rider\034 has truly appeared out of legend and is terrorizing the Empire.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Promotion: Private First Class and accumulate 25 rank-up points.\010\010 First-time completion of an individual Assault awards 5 rank-up points.\010\010 Repeating an already-completed Assault awards 1 rank-up point.\010\010 Abquhbah can provide a rough assessment of your current promotion progress.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Naja Salaheem on the upper floor of Salaheem's Sentinels at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Search for a targetable Warhorse Hoofprint in one of the following zones:\010\010 Wajaom Woodlands\010\010 Bhaflau Thickets\010\010 Mount Zhayolm\010\010 Caedarva Mire",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Warhorse Hoofprint to obtain the Key item: Dark Rider hoofprint.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Naja Salaheem at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with her for a cutscene and your promotion.\010\010 Your Key item: PFC Wildcat Badge and Dark Rider hoofprint are removed.\010\010 Your accumulated rank-up points are reset.\010\010 You receive the Key item: SP Wildcat Badge.\010\010 You receive the title Superior Private.\010\010 Superior Private Assault missions become available.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57159",["title"]="Puppet in Peril",["page_title"]="Puppet in Peril",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Puppet_in_Peril",["revision"]="120865",["requirements"]="Start: Aphmau \226\128\148 Walahra Temple, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-7, K-7, J-8, K-8) / Map 1\010Previous: Bastion of Knowledge",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You are to escort Aphmau to Mamook on her mission to recover Ovjang. Will you find the automaton in the land of the savage Mamool Ja?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Bastion of Knowledge; this mission begins during its ending cutscene in Walahra Temple.\010\010 Speaking with Naja Salaheem afterward provides additional dialogue but is not required for progression.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the Jade Sepulcher.\010\010 The most direct route is to use the Runic Portal to reach the Mamool Ja Staging Point at Bhaflau Thickets (H-11) / Map 2.\010\010 Use a Runic Portal Use Permit to travel there. Players using an Assault Order cannot leave through the staging point's exterior gate.\010\010 If the staging point has not been activated, travel through Mamook and exit into Bhaflau Thickets Map 2.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From the staging point, proceed north to the Jade Sepulcher entrance at Bhaflau Thickets (H-8) / Map 2.",["zone"]="Bhaflau Thickets",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Jade Sepulcher and examine the Ornamental Door for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the door again and select \034Puppet in Peril\034 to enter the battlefield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Lancelord Gaheel Ja within 30 minutes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The victory cutscene completes the mission and begins Prevalence of Pirates.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57034",["title"]="Puppetmaster Blues",["page_title"]="Puppetmaster Blues",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Puppetmaster_Blues",["revision"]="123773",["requirements"]="Start: Iruki-Waraki \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-9)\010Requirements: Operation Teatime completed\010Level: Puppetmaster 50\010Fame: Aht Urhgan\010Items: None\010Previous: Operation Teatime",["rewards"]="Puppetry Taj",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Iruki-Waraki has lost all faith in himself. Meet with his teacher and try to find a way to get Elisabeth to come around.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Iruki-Waraki in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-9) as Puppetmaster level 50 or higher.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Shamarhaan in Bastok Markets at Bastok Markets (F-9) to receive the Key item: Valkeng's memory chip.",["zone"]="Bastok Markets",["grid"]="F-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the ??? in Mount Zhayolm at Mount Zhayolm (L-8) to receive the Key item: Toggle switch.",["zone"]="Mount Zhayolm",["grid"]="L-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Talacca Cove.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Rock Slab at Talacca Cove (F-6) to enter the battlefield.",["zone"]="Talacca Cove",["grid"]="F-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Valkeng.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Shamarhaan in Bastok Markets.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Iruki-Waraki in Aht Urhgan Whitegate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Sajhra in Nashmau at Nashmau (H-9).",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Iruki-Waraki to receive Puppetry Taj.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="ToAU",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57024",["title"]="Puppetmaster: Upgrading Your Automaton",["page_title"]="Puppetmaster: Upgrading Your Automaton",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Puppetmaster%3A_Upgrading_Your_Automaton",["revision"]="122680",["requirements"]="Start: Ghatsad \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-7)\010Requirements: Puppetmaster unlocked\010Level: Puppetmaster 10, 20, 30, 40, 50\010Items: See tables below",["rewards"]="New Automaton head and/or frame",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Ghatsad can build new Automaton heads and frames for experienced Puppetmasters.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Ghatsad in the Automaton Workshop at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-7) as Puppetmaster.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select the available automaton upgrade.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the requested materials and payment.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return after the required wait to receive the new Automaton head and/or frame.\010\010You may only have one automaton upgrade in progress at a time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="ToAU",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57192",["title"]="Ragnarok (Aht Urhgan Mission 45: Ragnarok)",["page_title"]="Aht Urhgan Mission 45: Ragnarok",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Aht_Urhgan_Mission_45%3A_Ragnarok",["revision"]="120933",["requirements"]="Previous: Nashmeira's Plea",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The second coming of Ragnarok has been averted. Return to Al Zahbi and report to President Naja.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Nashmeira's Plea; this mission begins during its ending cutscene in the Alzadaal Undersea Ruins.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Aht Urhgan Whitegate and enter the second platform of Salaheem's Sentinels at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.\010\010 The cutscene triggers automatically as you enter the platform; speaking with Naja Salaheem is not required.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The resulting cutscene completes the mission and begins Imperial Coronation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_374",["title"]="Ranperre's Final Rest (San d'Oria Mission 6-2)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 6-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_6-2",["revision"]="119230",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 6-1|Leaute's Last Wishes",["rewards"]="Rank 7\01040,000 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Prince Trion seeks an adventurer. Find the prince in his chamber to learn more.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade crystals to the Conquest NPC to unlock this mission. Speaking to the San d'Oria Gate Guard, you'll be instructed to go see Prince Trion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Visit Prince Trion in his room in Chateau d'Oraguille (H-7).",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="H-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="NM Fight",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After a cutscene, gather a party and head for (King Ranperre's Tomb (H-8)) in King Ranperre's Tomb, on the first map. When ready, check the Heavy Stone Door. Sneak popping works! \010\010 April 18, 2026: NMs did not aggro when using the Sneak pop method.",["zone"]="King Ranperre's Tomb",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Three Skeleton NMs will pop - Corrupted Soffeil, Corrupted Yorgos and Corrupted Ulbrig. Yorgos is a Warrior, the other two are Black Mages.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Your main target is Corrupted Yorgos. This fight is made easier by pulling this NM, and allowing the other two to depop, and then finally killing Yorgos. \010\010The NMs are immune to Sleep and Lullaby but not Sheep Song. March 15, 2025 - The NMs are NOT immune to lullaby.\010\010They will use Blood Saber, so keep damage negating buffs up to reduce the HP regained. \010\010Corrupted Yorgos has approximately 7250 HP.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When defeated, check the Heavy Stone Door again, and enter. Check the Tombstone inside for a cutscene, at the end of which, you'll receive the Ancient San d'Orian Book.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="San d'Oria",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional: Return to Prince Trion, and you will be instructed to go see the Gate Guard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to any Gate Guard. The guard will tell you that it will take some time to decipher.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone and talk to the guard again who will tell you to see Prince Trion (you may need to talk to him twice).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Prince Trion again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Heavy Stone Door again for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to a Gate Guard to complete the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57467",["title"]="Rat Race",["page_title"]="Rat Race",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Rat_Race",["revision"]="122145",["requirements"]="Start: Kakkaroon, Nashmau (H-8)\010Fame: Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["rewards"]="Imperial Gold Piece x2 \010\010Imperial Mythril Piece x2 \010\010Imperial Silver Piece x3",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Young Rapipi adores the Qiqirn and wants to make friends with all the furry beastmen in Nashmau. However, therein lies the dilemma for poor Kakkaroon, who is deathly afraid of children. Perhaps \034Nadee\034 can provide some advice on how to bring the two together.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Kakkaroon.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Nadee Periyaha Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-9).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Cacaroon Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-11).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Cacaroon one Imperial Bronze Piece.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Now you must complete Cook-a-roon? for a Nashmau Stew (this step does not seem to be compatible with this quest on Horizonxi.)\010\010Buying one from the Auction House will not work.\010\010Keeping one from a previous repeat of Cook-a-roon? will not work.\010\010If this is your first time completing Cook-a-roon?, you will need to make a second stew (not verified).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Nashmau Stew to Kyokyoroon back in Nashmau (H-7) (Note: Trading a stew to this npc does nothing.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Kakkaroon to complete the quest.\010\010Note: This quest and the tie-in quest Cook-a-roon? appear to be incomplete as far as working together. I followed all the steps, but once it came to Kyokyoroon, he would not acknowledge or accept the stew. Save your money/time/effort.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasues of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2554",["title"]="Reap What You Sow",["page_title"]="Reap What You Sow",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Reap_What_You_Sow",["revision"]="60755",["requirements"]="Start: Mashuu-Ajuu \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (K-6) / North\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Deathball or \010Sobbing Fungus",["rewards"]="500 - 700 Gil\010Stationery Set",["repeatable"]="Yes (if trading Sobbing Fungus)",["summary"]="Mashuu-Ajuu wants help with this horticultural homework assignment. He asks that you use \034Herb Seeds\034 to grow something that will impress his classmates, such as a \034Sobbing Fungus.\034",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Players will not be able to start this quest if they are eligible for Let Sleeping Dogs Lie - and up until they complete the quest. Moreover, this quest is not required to start Let Sleeping Dogs Lie.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you have just completed Let Sleeping Dogs Lie, you must zone before starting.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Mashuu-Ajuu on top of the Aurastery, Windurst Waters North (K-6). He will give you a bag of Herb Seeds.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade either a Sobbing Fungus or a Deathball.\010\010They can be obtained by planting the Herb Seeds in a flowerpot, or from the Auction House.\010\010If you trade a Sobbing Fungus, you will receive 500g and a Stationery Set.\010\010If you trade a Deathball, you will receive 700g and a Stationery Set. After trading a Deathball, you will be unable to repeat the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2751",["title"]="Recollections",["page_title"]="Recollections",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Recollections",["revision"]="115854",["requirements"]="Start: Chumimi \226\128\148 Heavens Tower / Basement\010Requirements: Black Mage Level: 50+\010Items: Bag of Seeds\010Whine Cellar Key\010Previous: The Three Magi",["rewards"]="Wizard's Sabots",["repeatable"]="af",["summary"]="Some strange occurrence from twenty years ago is now casting a shadow on the growth of the star tree saplings. Two of the ex-ministers may have an idea of the cause. After receiving instructions from them, head to Jeuno and then on to the Northlands.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="As a level 50+ Black Mage, go to Heavens Tower in Windurst Walls and speak to Chumimi in the basement (Star Tree Farm).\010\010 If you just completed The Three Magi, you must zone out of Heavens Tower before this will start (relogging also works).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Note: After this step, you no longer need to be a Black Mage for the remainder of the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Travel to Ru'Lude Gardens and speak with Laityn at Ru'Lude Gardens (G-9) for an additional cutscene.",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="G-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Crawlers' Nest",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Crawlers' Nest and defeat a Water Elemental or Fire Elemental to obtain a Bag of Seeds.\010\010 These elementals are found in the Crawlers' Nest / Map 3, accessed through the tunnel at Crawlers' Nest (J-10) / Map 1 (marked \034B\034 on the player-made map).\010\010 Best method: Use the Weather Forecast page to see when elemental weather is due.\010\010 Rolanberry Fields shares weather with Crawlers' Nest, so either zone works for checking the forecast.\010\010 Set Weather Type to Any Weather Type and Zone to Crawlers' Nest, then click Show Weather.\010\010 The table shows the possible weather rolls for each window: Normal (50%), Common (35%), 'Rare (15%). If you see water weather listed (e.g. Rain/Squalls or Fire/Heat Wave), that is the chance for that window.\010\010 You can also ask Weather Reporter NPCs for quick in-game guidance, but the forecast page is usually faster and more precise.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After obtaining the Bag of Seeds, return to Heavens Tower in Windurst Walls and trade it to Chumimi.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Castle Zvahl",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Castle Zvahl Baileys and defeat Demon Commanders, Demon Generals, Demon Magistrates, or Demon Chancellors until you obtain a Whine Cellar Key.\010\010 These enemies can be found on Castle Zvahl Baileys / Map 3 on the bottom floor near the corner drop-offs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring the key to Castle Zvahl Keep.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon entering Castle Zvahl Keep, follow the right wall and enter the first Iron Bar Gate to the north at Castle Zvahl Keep (H-7).",["zone"]="Castle Zvahl Keep",["grid"]="H-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bear right and trade the key to the locked Ore Door on the left, before the next Iron Bar Gate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene, you will obtain Key item: Foe Finder Mark I. Return to Chumimi in Heavens Tower in Windurst Walls for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Black Mage (BLM)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Black Mage (BLM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Wizard's Sabots",["revision"]="18807"},{["job"]="Black Mage (BLM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Recollections",["revision"]="115854"}}},{["id"]="wiki_4322",["title"]="Recycling Rods",["page_title"]="Recycling Rods",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Recycling_Rods",["revision"]="117041",["requirements"]="Start: Keshab-Menjab \226\128\148 Mhaura (H-9)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Cleanly Snapped Rod",["rewards"]="1500g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You've been asked to help bring in cleanly snapped rods for recycling. The recycled rods are supposedly sold somewhere around Bibiki Bay.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Keshab-Menjab at Mhaura (H-9) to start the quest. He asks you to bring him a broken rod, but it has to be one \034busted clean in two.\034",["zone"]="Mhaura",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Bibiki Bay - Purgonorgo Isle and fish with a Composite Fishing Rod and Minnow until you catch the NM Lancet Jagil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="See the Talk:Lancet Jagil page for additional ways to fish this up and relative difficulty of the monster.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill the Lancet Jagil and obtain the Cleanly Snapped Rod [Template Rare2: ][Template Exclusive2: ].",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Mhaura and trade the rod to Keshab-Menjab at Mhaura (H-9) to complete the quest.",["zone"]="Mhaura",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_12353",["title"]="Requiem of Sin",["page_title"]="Requiem of Sin",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Requiem_of_Sin",["revision"]="114764",["requirements"]="Start: Despachiaire \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold (K-10)\010Requirements: One conquest tally after the cutscene \034In the Name of Justice\034 in Mhaura after defeating Promathia during Dawn.\010Items: First time: Key item: Letter from Shikaree Y. \010 When repeating: Key item: Letter from the Mithran Trackers.\010Previous: Tango with a Tracker",["rewards"]="Various, with the chance of nothing.",["repeatable"]="Once per Conquest cycle.",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Despachiaire to obtain the Key Item: Letter from Shikaree Y.\010\010 The quest will not be flagged in your current quests. It will only appear in your completed quests if you are victorious.\010\010 Furthermore, the cutscene \034In the Name of Justice\034 in Mhaura after defeating Promathia during Dawn is required for the quest to activate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Boneyard Gully and enter the battlefield for: Requiem of Sin.\010\010 The battlefield has a 30 minute time limit, up to 6 party members may enter, and it is uncapped. Buffs including TP are not lost upon entry, and experience points are lost from KO.\010\010 The Letter from Shikaree Y is lost upon entry. If the battle is not completed successfully, Despachiaire will give a new one after the next Conquest tally.\010\010 If this is your first time entering this battlefield. meaning you have the Letter from Shikaree Y) and you enter with others that have completed it before, having a different key item, the Letter from the Mithran Trackers), and if they are the ones to enter first, and you fail, you will not be able to obtain a new Key item until the next Conquest tally.\010\010 After successfully clearing the battlefield and waiting until the next Conquest tally, you may return to Despachiaire to obtain the new key item, Letter from the Mithran Trackers, which will allow you to repeat the battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Battle",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Again you face harder versions of the Shikarees from Promathia Mission 5-3-2:\010\010 Shikaree X: BST/NIN with two Daggers.\010\010 Shikaree X's Rabbit\010\010 Shikaree Y: DRK/MNK with Scythe.\010\010 Shikaree Z: DRG/WHM with Trident.\010\010 Shikaree Z's Wyvern\010\010 As in Head Wind, the Shikarees have extremely high TP gain, sometimes using a weapon skill only one second after their last one.\010\010 They will switch to the same target to make Skillchains, which effectively results in sharing hate.\010\010 The pets do not share hate with their masters, so they can be \034kited\034 indefinitely.\010\010 The Shikarees can be slept only with Elemental Seal. Also, Sleep only lasts for about 30 seconds, Sleep II lasting for around 40. (Everything can be easily slept with lullaby.)\010\010 Unlike during the mission, Shikaree X's Rabbit and Shikaree Z's Wyvern can not be slept.\010\010 The rabbit is susceptible to Bind and Gravity, though Bind only sticks for about 10 seconds. The Wyvern seems to resist Bind.\010\010 If you defeat Shikaree X's Rabbit before defeating Shikaree X, she will summon another one.\010\010 If you defeat Shikaree X or Shikaree Z but not their pet and then you are defeated, the pet will not return to the original spawn locations, but will instead stay where it was. This can be dangerous because if you are defeated by the pet or are within their range for other reasons, it is not possible to be revived without being attacked by them. It should also be noted that no matter where any of the enemies are after going passive, if the pets engage a player character, the others will join in.\010\010 Since Shikaree Z's Wyvern cannot be slept, you need another strategy to prevent Healing Breath (for ~900 each time).\010\010 \034Kiting\034 the Wyvern away works well. Silencing Z may also work.\010\010 You must defeat all enemies, including the pets, for the Armoury Crate to appear and to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Rewards\010\010There is a chance you will receive no reward from this battle.\010|- valign=top\010\010|width=20%|\010! Zero to One of:\010|-align=center\010| Cassia Lumber [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=150/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-align=center\010| Dragon Bone [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=75/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-align=center\010| Eltoro Leather [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=120/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|width=20%|\010! Zero to One of:\010|-align=center\010| Galateia [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-align=center\010| Kejusu Satin [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010| Viridian Urushi [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|width=20%|\010! Zero to One of:\010|-align=center\010| Cassia Lumber [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=150/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-align=center\010| Dragon Bone [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=75/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-align=center\010| Eltoro Leather [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=120/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|width=20%|\010! Zero to One of:\010|- align=center\010| Galateia [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- align=center\010| Kejusu Satin [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- align=center\010| Viridian Urushi [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|- valign=top\010\010|width=20%|\010! Zero to One of:\010|- align=center\010| X's Knife [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- align=center\010| Y's Scythe [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- align=center\010| Z's Trident [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|width=20%|\010! Zero to One of:\010|- align=center\010| Lacquer Tree Log [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- align=center\010| Phoenix Feather [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|width=20%|\010! Zero to One of:\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010| Philosopher's Stone [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010\010|width=20%|\010! Unknown Groupings:\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010| Raxa [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010| Granite [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010| Beetle Blood [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010| Petrified Log [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010| Shining Cloth [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|- BGCOLOR=#e3e6ff align=center\010| Divine Log [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_333",["title"]="Return of the Talekeeper (Bastok Mission 6-1)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 6-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_6-1",["revision"]="119880",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 5-2|Xarcabard, Land of Truths",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A new Talekeeper is rumored to have appeared among the Galka. Speak to Medicine Eagle, the Mines District guard on post near the entrance to Ore Street, for further details.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 18~20 Crystals to a gate guard until your Rank Points are full to unlock this mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to a Gate Guard to accept the mission. They'll instruct you to see Medicine Eagle Bastok Mines (H-6), he is found at the top of the ramp.",["zone"]="Bastok Mines",["grid"]="H-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You must then speak with Drake Fang located in Zeruhn Mines (H-6), near the boat. You will get a cutscene telling you to go to Altepa Desert.",["zone"]="Zeruhn Mines",["grid"]="H-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Western Altepa Desert (G-8), and seek out a ??? on the west side of (G-8) , inbetween three glowing rocks. Buff up and check it. This will spawn two NMs, Western Sphinx and Eastern Sphinx.",["zone"]="Western Altepa Desert",["grid"]="G-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the ??? again to receive the Key item: Altepa Moonpebble.\010\010Note: If you zone before receiving the Key item: Altepa Moonpebble, you will have to fight both NMs again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Tall Mountain, Bastok Mines (J-7) on the bottom level near the restricted area. After the cutscene, the mission will be complete.",["zone"]="Bastok Mines",["grid"]="J-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="NM's are immune to sleep",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="NM's can be pulled solo if you sneak before popping the ???",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="NM's are not immune to bind but build resistance quickly",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Killing one NM after the other despawns will allow you to obtain the Altepa Moonpebble",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Sneak pull nolonger work.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Solo able by lv75 Bst.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3683",["title"]="Return to Delkfutt's Tower (Zilart Mission 8)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 8",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_8",["revision"]="118541",["requirements"]="Level: 65+\010Previous: The Chamber of Oracles",["rewards"]="Mog Wardrobe 2: 5 slots",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Hurry to Delkfutt's Tower and stop the Zilartian princes from completing their plan to open the Gate of the Gods.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="rise of the zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5946",["title"]="Return to the Depths",["page_title"]="Return to the Depths",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Return_to_the_Depths",["revision"]="113057",["requirements"]="Start: Ayame \226\128\148 Metalworks (K-7)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 5\010Items: Misareaux Garlic\010Ahriman Tears\01010,000 gil\010Previous: A Question of Faith",["rewards"]="12,000gil\010Bowyer Ring\010Optional: 1,000 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You are to find the one who speaks both the common and the Moblin language, and learn more about the city of Movalpolos.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Ayame for a cutscene that starts the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Oldton Movalpolos, watch a cutscene, and proceed to Misareaux Coast and obtain a Misareaux Garlic that drops from the Orcs there. \010(You don't necessarily need to watch the CS before obtaining the garlic.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Lower Jeuno and trade the Misareaux Garlic to Muckvix (located at (Lower Jeuno (H-10)) in Goblins' Goblet, through Muckvix's Junk Shop.) You will receive 2,000 gil and a Key item: Letter from Muckvix.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="H-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Kazham and talk with Magriffon, located at (Kazham (I-7)) in Celodehki's Bed & Breakfast.",["zone"]="Kazham",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade him 10,000 gil for a cutscene and two key items: Key item: Letter from Magriffon and Key item: Providence Pot.\010\010You will receive the 10,000 gil back at the end of the quest.\010\010Trading Magriffon the 10,000 gil will continue this specific quest even if other quests are currently active that involve giving Magriffon gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Lower Jeuno and talk with Muckvix for another cutscene where you deliver the key items and receive a Key item: Pungent Providence Pot in return.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Oldton Movalpolos for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Tarnotik at (Oldton Movalpolos (K-10)), answering in the affirmative to both his questions.",["zone"]="Oldton Movalpolos",["grid"]="K-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade one Ahriman Tears to Tarnotik to be teleported to Mine Shaft #2716. \010\010Each person who is involved in the quest must trade a tear to Tarnotik to be teleported to the BCNM zone. EACH PERSON MUST HAVE DONE OR ACTIVATED THIS QUEST IN ORDER FOR THIS TO WORK.\010\010Tarnotik will continue to perform this service for you even after the quest is completed. One Ahriman Tears is still required for each teleport.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Shaft Entrance for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check it again and select the battlefield Return to the Depths.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Buffs wear on entry",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will receive a cutscene as you enter the battlefield. Answer with the top option every time you are asked a question.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Moblins Twilotak (Dark Knight) and three Moblin Clergymen (White Mage) and three Moblin Wisewomen (Red Mage) are in the back of the BCNM arena.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Only Twilotak has to be defeated to complete the BCNM; the other six can be killed if you wish. They do not attack with melee hits even when engaged. They only stand in the background and cast. \010\010Twilotak casts standard Dark Knight spells and has around 5800HP. \010\010The Moblin Clergymen and Moblin Wisewomen use Draw In, which makes Twilotak very difficult to kite unless the supporting Moblins are defeated.\010\010Twilotak can use Blood Weapon multiple times.\010\010The three Moblin Wisewomen cast spells such as Haste on Twilotak and cast spells like Sleep II and Dispel on players.\010\010The three Moblin Clergymen cast spells such as Protect III and Cure IV on Twilotak and Holy on players.\010\010This fight is capped at level 40.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Twilotak to end the BCNM and receive a cutscene and 10,000 gil.\010\010Once you complete the BCNM, when you zone out of Mine Shaft #2716 you'll be in Newton Movalpolos on a ledge, safe from the standard Moblins. If you do not have someone in your group who can Escape, talk to the NPC Sleakachiq on that ledge to receive a teleport back out to North Gustaberg, at the cost of 800 gil per person.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Metalworks and talk with Ayame for the Bowyer Ring reward and to end the quest. You may have to talk to her twice to trigger the cutscene.\010\010Optional: Talk to the Tarutaru Ravorara in Port Bastok (E-7) to sell the Pungent Providence Pot for 1,000 gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1773",["title"]="Riding on the Clouds",["page_title"]="Riding on the Clouds",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Riding_on_the_Clouds",["revision"]="118265",["requirements"]="Start: Maat \226\128\148 Ru'Lude Gardens (H-5)\010Level: 61\010Items: Key item: Scowling Stone\010Key item: Smiling Stone\010Key item: Somber Stone\010Key item: Spirited Stone\010Kindred's Seal x 4\010Previous: Whence Blows the Wind",["rewards"]="Raises level cap to 70\010Mog Wardrobe: 5 Slots [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Use Maat's hints to search out for people who will trade you a strange stone for a Kindred's seal. Only then will you know your true limits.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Maat at level 61+ to receive this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He will give you four random clues from the list below. Trade a Kindred's Seal to the people you have been assigned and they will each in turn give you a different strange stone. (key item)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Maat when you have collected all four stones. \010\010! style=\034background:#ffdead;\034 | Clue\010! style=\034background:#ffdead;\034 | NPC\010! style=\034background:#ffdead;\034 | Location\010|-\010|A boy who only thinks of his sick mother.\010|Raminel\010|Southern San d'Oria (F-8)\010|-\010|An Elvaan who likes her knives sharp.\010|Sobane\010|Southern San d'Oria (D-6)\010|-\010|A little girl who wants to be a Royal Knight, just like her brother.\010|Taurette\010|Northern San d'Oria (F-7)\010|-\010|A young elvaan whose breath stinks.\010|Maloquedil\010|Northern San d'Oria (J-8)\010|-\010|A young man looking for a job where they're not too rough with him.\010|Sheridan\010|Port San d'Oria (H-10)\010|-\010|An old man running the Consortium warehouses.\010|Fontoumant\010|Port San d'Oria (H-10)\010|-\010|A second knight who specializes in the nirvana slash.\010|Brifalien\010|Port San d'Oria (H-8)\010|-\010|A shopkeeper who longs for customers that want more than scrolls of Stone.\010|Rugiette\010|Port San d'Oria (J-8)\010|-\010|A pioneer of the Palborough Mines.\010|Babenn\010|Bastok Mines (J-6)\010|-\010|A boy watching over Dalzakk's home while he's off adventuring.\010|Gwill\010|Bastok Markets (E-11) \010|-\010|A girl who is positive robes and bronze subligar are the lastest fashion.\010|Brygid\010|Bastok Markets (K-9) \010|-\010|A girl who thinks she can never be as good as her sister.\010|Kaede\010|Port Bastok (J-5)\010|-\010|A woman who lost her husband in an accident in the Palborough Mines. \010|Hilda\010|Port Bastok (E-6)\010|-\010|Bastok's number five \034doorman.\034\010|Naji\010|Metalworks (J-8)\010|-\010|A man so quiet, his boss is ready to call him \034Silent Mountain\034.\010|Raibaht\010|Metalworks (G-8)\010|-\010|A man who is ready to move Bastok into the age of magic. \010|Lucius\010|Metalworks (J-9)\010|-\010|The smartest looking mithra child. \010|Koko Lihzeh\010|Windurst Waters (K-6) / North\010|-\010|The man with a sharp discerning eye who perceives the right and wrong of NETA. \010|Naiko-Paneiko\010|Windurst Waters (C-11) / South\010|-\010| A woman everybody called a \034strange little poppet\034 when she was younger.\010|Kerutoto\010|Windurst Waters (J-8) / South\010|-\010| A little girl sick of being left out all the time. \010|Shanruru\010|Port Windurst (H-5)\010|-\010|A man that gets upset when anyone tells him that \034hats suck.\034 \010|Boizo-Naizo\010|Windurst Woods (H-10)\010|-\010|A lady looking for another tasty frog. \010|Sola Jaab\010|Windurst Woods (K-10)\010|-\010|A man known for his magic doll upgrades. \010|Koru-Moru\010|Windurst Walls (E-7)\010|-\010|A lady that jumps for joy at the sight of Rolanberry souveniers. \010|Kupipi\010|Heavens Tower \010|-\010|A man looking for something snappy to hook his customers. \010|Naiko-Paneiko\010|Windurst Waters (C-11) / South\010|-\010|A weaving woman who lost her memory in Selbina.\010|Mathilde\010|Selbina (H-9)\010|-\010|A Galkan child who is great at hiding. \010|Vobo\010|Selbina (I-7)\010|-\010|A man who started raising his own sheep to get some good wool. \010|Melyon\010|Selbina (I-9)\010|-\010|A pupil of Zaldon who knows his fish.\010|Gabwaleid\010|Selbina (H-9)\010|-\010|A girl whose fianc\195\169 is all the way in Selbina.\010|Celestina\010|Mhaura (G-8) \010|-\010|The small mayor of a small town. \010|Ekokoko\010|Mhaura (F-9)\010|-\010|A guy who knows a lot about pirates for somebody that's never met one.\010|Bihoro-Guhoro\010|Mhaura (G-9)\010|-\010|A kid that wants to work with monsters when he grows up.\010|Jikka-Abukka\010|Mhaura (H-9)\010|-",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7512",["title"]="Rivals",["page_title"]="Rivals",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Rivals",["revision"]="104248",["requirements"]="Start: Detzo \226\128\148 Bastok Mines (I-6)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Mythril Sallet",["rewards"]="Wolf Gorget",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Lend Detzo a mythril sallet so he can win a contest against his rival.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Detzo.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Mythril Sallet and trade it to Detzo for the cut-scene and to receive your reward.\010You retain the Mythril Sallet after trading it to Detzo.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3684",["title"]="Ro'Maeve (Zilart Mission 9)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 9",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_9",["revision"]="20472",["requirements"]="Previous: Return to Delkfutt's Tower",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="The Gate of the Gods, Tu'Lia, has been restored by Eald'narche. What do his words \034Ro'Maeve\034 and \034blessed by the light\034 mean? What is Lion's next move?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="rise of the zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_546",["title"]="Road Forks (Promathia Mission 3-3)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 3-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_3-3",["revision"]="118544",["requirements"]="Level: 70+ (solo)\010Previous: Vessel Without a Captain",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="To capture the mysterious boy, you must first locate the fourth mothercrystal. To do this, you have been ordered to travel to the nations of Bastok, Windurst, and San d'Oria to learn of the Multinational Expedition that was held nearly thirty years ago.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="This is a long mission, with a lot of legwork and two uncapped NM fights.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This mission is divided into 2 parts - San d'Oria route and Windurst route. Route details are given below. You can complete the routes in either order, and you can even do them both at the same time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="3-3A: San d'Oria Route: \034Emerald Waters\034\010\010Vicissitudes (3-3A1)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Northern San d'Oria to start this leg of the mission. You will receive a cutscene as soon as you zone in.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Arnau at Northern San d'Oria (M-6), the priest giving sermons in the Cathedral's main hall.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="M-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Chasalvige at Northern San d'Oria (L-6) in the Manuscript Room (off to the the left side as you enter the Cathedral; Chasalvige is on the dais in front of you as you enter the room.).\010Descendents of a Line Lost (3-3A2)",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="L-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Carpenters' Landing via the entrance at Jugner Forest (E-6) and look for Guilloud at Carpenters' Landing (H-10) beside a boulder. Talking to him will spawn a Morbol NM named Overgrown Ivy.\010\010Overgrown Ivy can use the two-hour ability Hundred Fists.\010\010 Those at the general base level for this mission (level 40 or so) may wish to consider partying (perhaps even forming an Alliance) or bringing higher-level help for fighting this NM.\010Louverance (3-3A3)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After defeating Overgrown Ivy, talk to Guilloud again. (If you zone before speaking to Guilloud, then you will have to fight the NM again.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Then head to Southern San d'Oria and speak to Hinaree on the second floor of Count Caffaule's Manor at (Southern San d'Oria (B-6)). \010This ends the San d'Orian leg.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="3-3B: Windurst Route: \034Memories of a Maiden\034\010\010Comedy of Errors (Act I)(3-3B1)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Windurst Waters to start this leg of the mission. You will receive a cutscene upon zoning in.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Rhinostery's right-hand room located at Windurst Waters (J-9) / South and talk to Ohbiru-Dohbiru.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="J-9 / South",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, go to Windurst Walls (E-5) and talk to Yoran-Oran in his house. You may need to speak to him a few times before you get the cutscene.",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="E-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, go back to Windurst Waters (F-10) / North and and talk to Kyume-Romeh inside Timbre Timbers Tavern.\010Comedy of Errors (Act II)(3-3B2)",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="F-10 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Windurst Waters (E-7) / South and enter the house from the back entrance, atop of the stairs. Talk to Honoi-Gomoi to receive Key item: Cracked Mimeo Mirror. (This KI will NOT show in your Key Items list.)",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="E-7 / South",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Yoran-Oran at Windurst Walls (E-5) and talk to him again to learn the method for repairing the mirror.",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="E-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Attohwa Chasm through the Maze of Shakhrami / Map 1F-4. \010\010Note: While on this part of the mission, consider obtaining a Flaxen Pouch from Jakaka at Attohwa Chasm (G-10), near the zone entrance. Trading this to the Cradle of Rebirth that you will visit later on will give you Parradamo Stones which you can return to Jakaka for the Key item: Miasma Filter that will grant access to the ENM area Boneyard Gully.",["zone"]="Maze of Shakhrami",["grid"]=" / Map 1F-4",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the East section, then work your way to (Attohwa Chasm (K-8)) and find a target called \034Loose Sand.\034 Checking the target will spawn an Antlion-type NM named Lioumere.\010\010A tank is recommended to spawn the NM with, as the Lioumere will use Pit Ambush on the spawning member as it appears. Sneaking the tank to avoid initial aggro will not work in this instance.\010\010The Lioumere will \034lose\034 all hate and return to its Spawn Point after it uses a special ability. If the Lioumere is allowed to return to its Spawn Point, it will recover all HP. The antlion is susceptible to Bind, Gravity, and Sleep.\010\010The Lioumere can be very easily Stunned, using the spell (and all other known methods, most likely). Stun can be used to buy time for Provoke, making the two a potent combination.\010\010Spell-voking usually doesn't work, as the Lioumere returns to the spawn point at a rate of movement that places it out of range before most useful magic can be cast.\010\010Flash is ineffective.\010\010Pulling the Lioumere as far from the spawn as possible can be known to buy some hate-returning time. (It would be good for a party to ensure that the area they're pulling to is clear of mobs before luring the Lioumere there, however. The Lioumere can link with other antlions.)\010\010By pulling back and to the left, you can force Lioumere through a small gap in the rocks and turn him around to ensure you can get a hit in as he tries to move through you.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon defeating the Lioumere, check the Loose Sand again to get the Key item: Mimeo Jewel.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, you'll need to climb the convoluted mountain Parradamo Tor [here is a guide to walk up the mountain]. From obtaining your Jewel, you will have 30 minutes (Earth time) to reach the \034Cradle of Rebirth\034 target on the Tor's summit before the Jewel breaks.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will be warned at various intervals of the Jewel's status. If you can't get to the top in time (you will receive a message that the Jewel has \034grown completely dark and shattered\034), you'll have to return to the Loose Sand, obtain a new Mimeo Jewel, without having to fight the NM again, and try to climb again.\010\010You will lose the Key item: Mimeo Jewel if you disconnect or log off.\010\010On successive runs (unless there is a new member of your party between then and now who has not yet fought Lioumere), you will not need to fight the NM a second time to get a new Jewel.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The starting point for the climb up is located somewhere around the southeast corner of the Tor near the Loose Sand. The path is very narrow with no natural barriers to keep you on the trail; one wrong step and you will fall off, or onto an earlier part of the path.\010\010Be very careful with your camera control while on the Tor. It's just as easy to fall off the Tor through a misaligned camera especially around corners as losing your way.\010\010It is advised to not auto-follow in this situation. This way, if one of your leading members makes a mistake and falls off the Tor (which can be more often than one would think), you will maintain your position on the path.\010\010While on the Tor, you will be out of aggro range of most (if not all) mobs. (If you're on a path close to the ground, however, you may wish to check mob positions, using Sneak and Invisible if necessary.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Along the way, you will encounter vents of miasma that block your path, similar to the vents in the area surrounding the Tor itself. Unlike those, however, there are some on the Tor that stop venting for a moment, allowing you (very brief) access.\010\010To distinguish between a \034permanent\034 or \034temporary\034 vent, wait about one minute while pushing against the vent; if you do not pass through, the vent is permanent. If you encounter a \034permanent\034 vent, it usually indicates that you need to continue by carefully falling off the side of the Tor, landing on a path below. Try to run at an angle with the wall so you keep rubbing against it. This prevents you from getting too far off the narrow path and falling. Be extra careful when crossing the bone bridges as one bad step can cause you to fall.\010\010The first two vents you will encounter on the proper path are \034permanent.\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Try to work your way around the Tor in a counter-clockwise direction until you land on a path very close to the base. Stay on it; as soon as you find a ramp leading upward, climb it, then move clockwise as soon as you get off that ramp until you reach the summit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the target marked \034Cradle of Rebirth\034 at a crack near the center of the summit. After a brief waiting period, you will obtain the following Key Items:\010\010Key item: Mimeo Feather\010\010Key item: Second Mimeo Feather\010\010Key item: Third Mimeo Feather\010Exit Stage Left (3-3B3)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Yoran-Oran and talk to him at Windurst Walls (Windurst Walls (E-5)).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Port Windurst and talk to Yujuju at (Port Windurst (M-6)): You may need to speak with her twice.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Windurst Waters North (Windurst Waters (G-8) / North) and talk to Tosuka-Porika, inside the Optistery.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Windurst Walls and talk to Yoran-Oran (Windurst Walls (E-5)) again\010The Windurstian leg of the mission is now complete.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Completing the Mission",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In order to complete the mission, talk to Cid in Bastok Metalworks.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2116",["title"]="Rock Racketeer",["page_title"]="Rock Racketeer",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Rock_Racketeer",["revision"]="120904",["requirements"]="Start: Nanaa Mihgo \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (J-3)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Sharp Stone Pickaxe's\010Previous: Mihgo's Amigo",["rewards"]="2,100 gil",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="The Cat Burglar wants you to see if a sharp gray rock she \034found\034 is of any value, by having it valued at the Goldsmiths' Guild in Bastok. If the rock is of any value, she wants you to sell it for her.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Nanaa Mihgo and obtain the quest and the Key item: Sharp Gray Stone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Bastok Markets, talk to Ardea at Bastok Markets (H-8). She will buy the Key item: Sharp Gray Stone for 10g.",["zone"]="Bastok Markets",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back to Nanaa Mihgo and she'll scold you for selling the stone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Varun twice at Windurst Woods (H-9) next to the homepoint crystal. He'll wonder where his stone has gone and send you to Palborough Mines.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head into Palborough Mines. Go to the 3rd floor to the east half of Palborough Mines (I-9) / Map 3. There is a round dead-end room with two mithril seams.",["zone"]="Palborough Mines",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mine up the Sharp Stone RareExclusive from the western seam with a pickaxe. (Your Pickaxe may break, so bring a few)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back to Windurst again and trade the Sharp Stone to Varun to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6854",["title"]="Rosel the Armorer",["page_title"]="Rosel the Armorer",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Rosel_the_Armorer",["revision"]="99281",["requirements"]="Start: Rosel \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (K-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1",["rewards"]="200g (if correct)\010100g (if incorrect)",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Deliver the receipt for the prince's cloak to the chateau guards.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Rosel and you will get a cutscene. Rosel has finished a cape for one of the Princes, and someone comes to pick it up. In the confusion, Rosel forgets to give the man his receipt. He asks you to deliver the Key item: Receipt for the Prince for him.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In this quest the receipt is for one of the San d'Orian Princes, either Trion or Pieuje. Remember which prince it is, for you get a lesser reward for delivering to the incorrect person.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Northern San d'Oria and talk to Guilerme who is stationed in front of the Chateau d'Oraguille at I-7. He will ask you who to give the receipt to, and will deliver it for you. The guard comes back out, insults your clothing, and sends you on your way.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Rosel for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57581",["title"]="Royal Painter Escort",["page_title"]="Royal Painter Escort",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Royal_Painter_Escort",["revision"]="122531",["requirements"]="Start: Halshaob \226\128\148 Nashmau (H-10)\010Previous: Scouting the Ashu Talif",["rewards"]="??? Item. Goldsmithing Gemstones. Koga Shuriken",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade an Imperial Silver Piece to Halshaob (H-10) in the southeast corner of the Nashmau Port to begin the quest.\010\010Once per week after Scouting the Ashu Talif. Entire chain resets on the weekly reset.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the Cutter in Arrapago Reef, and enter when ready. Buffs DO NOT wear upon entering.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once inside, the NPC Faluuya will request you open a door to the ship's hold to continue. Make sure you are buffed before opening the door for her.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once inside the hold, several Ashu Talif Crew spawn and attempt to attack Faluuya. These enemies will attack Faluuya regardless of whether they are provoked or not. It seems the only way to draw their attention away from her is to damage them. They are no more difficult than the Ashu Talif crew of the previous quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If she should become damaged (a likely occurrence) she will Flee to the rear of the ship. Fight off whatever Ashu Talif crew are on her, and also the Ashu Talif Marines which spawn. The Marines are more difficult than their crew mates. Don't forget to cure Faluuya if she takes damage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="An NM crewman, Black Bartholomew, stands on the other side of the hold. If this crewman is defeated, all crew on board will vanish, and Faluuya will be able to sketch in peace. For this reason, you should aim to defeat it, although you should not neglect Faluuya while you are completing this task. IMPORTANT NOTE: Black Bartholomew is NOT there at start. After killing a few crew and/or marines, the NM is spawned.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once Faluuya completes her work, treasure chests appear on deck. One will appear for completing the BCNM, another for killing Black Bartholomew, and a third if Faluuya took no damage. Open them, and click on the Life Raft to finish the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="ToAU",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57123",["title"]="Royal Puppeteer",["page_title"]="Royal Puppeteer",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Royal_Puppeteer",["revision"]="121996",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1\010Previous: Imperial Schemes",["rewards"]="Key item: Vial of Spectral Scent",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Under the command of the court puppetmaster, you are to uncover the truth behind the ghost ship, the Ashu Talif. Investigate the Arrapago Islands.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After completing Imperial Schemes,",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain 1 Vial of Jody's Acid from an Ameretat.\010\010 Ameretats can be found in Bhaflau Thickets / Map 1 at levels 65-66 and Wajaom Woodlands / Map 1 at levels 66-68.\010\010 Each player must obtain their own vial.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Nashmau (H-7) / Map 1 and speak with Pyopyoroon for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="H-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade exactly 1 Vial of Jody's Acid to Pyopyoroon to complete the mission, receive the Key item: Vial of Spectral Scent, and begin Lost Kingdom.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5948",["title"]="Rubbish Day",["page_title"]="Rubbish Day",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Rubbish_Day",["revision"]="120097",["requirements"]="Start: Chululu \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (I-8)\010Requirements: Have Chululu tell your fortune on three separate game days to flag\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Key item: Magic Trash\010Garlaige Key\010Previous: Collect Tarut Cards",["rewards"]="6000 gil\010Chain Choker",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Chululu needs you to dispose of what she forgot to put out on rubbish day.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Prerequisite\010\010Consider completing the quest Making Amens! at the same time as it requires visiting the Incinerator room as well.\010\010If doing this quest only for the Sleepga II quest, it is wise to do the Never to Return quest at the same time, as both quests have a 3 game day waiting period.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After completing Collect Tarut Cards, have Chululu test your compatibility (you can do them back to back).\010\010To test compatibility, input the name of any character within the area as the password. It can be the same person three times. It can also be an NPC (e.g. one of the two standing in front of her stall, herself or Kurou-Morou) It needs to be a player character, you can choose anyone standing in front of the Auction House.\010\010Enter the name exactly as it is in-game, with the first letter capitalized.\010\010Even after you've completed Collect Tarut Cards Chululu may still start a dialog with \034Oh, what a crying-wying shame!\034 which launches the quest again. Simply reply \034No, Thanks\034. She will see dark clouds in the horizon, but you'll be able to talk with her again to test your compatibility.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to her on a fourth game day to receive this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Quest",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Chululu gives you some Key item: Magic Trash to take to the Incinerator in Garlaige Citadel.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Incinerator in Garlaige Citadel.\010\010Each character who wishes to enter the Crematory Hatch (a door) needs a Garlaige Key (Rare/Ex), which can be obtained from Fallen Evacuees in Garlaige Citadel. There are 2 small rooms on the first map with 2 Evacuees in each.\010\010Tractoring someone through the door does not work, as Mashira will not respond to you unless you entered the Incinerator room by using a Garlaige key.\010\010Thieves cannot use Thief's Tools or Skeleton Key to open the Crematory Hatch.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After obtaining the key You will need 4 people to proceed from here to open the gates. proceed through the Banishing Gate #1 at Garlaige Citadel (I-9) \226\128\148 Map 1 of the first map.",["zone"]="Garlaige Citadel",["grid"]="I-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, proceed through the Second Banishing Gate #2 at Garlaige Citadel (H-10) \226\128\148 Map 2 of the second map.",["zone"]="Garlaige Citadel",["grid"]="H-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After past the Banishing Gate #2, go to Garlaige Citadel (I-7) \226\128\148 Map 3 on the third map to find the Crematory Hatch that leads into the Incinerator room.",["zone"]="Garlaige Citadel",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Mashira and ask about the trash. (If you have Making Amens! active, you will also have the option to ask about Ajido-Marujido's wand)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Chululu for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4810",["title"]="Rycharde the Chef",["page_title"]="Rycharde the Chef",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Rycharde_the_Chef",["revision"]="107701",["requirements"]="Start: Rycharde \226\128\148 Mhaura (I-8)\010Items: Dhalmel Meat (x2)",["rewards"]="1500g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Rycharde needs your help to find some dhalmel meat.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Before talking to Rycharde, talk to Somo Aatsula, the mithra at the entrance to Mhaura. Follow her directions to get to Ekokoko, the Governor of Mhaura. If she doesn't give you directions, you may have already spoken to her before. Simply go and find Ekokoko to begin the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to the Governor, talk to her aide, Numi Adaligo, and ask her about each option, inquiring about work last, then speak to Take in Sailors' Stay (Mhaura (I-8)). Now speak to Rycharde Up the stairs from Take.",["zone"]="Mhaura",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Rycharde wants you to bring him two slices of Dhalmel Meat.\010\010These drop off of any Dhalmel. Bring him the two slices and he will reward you.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Rycharde is located on the 2nd floor of the Sailors' Stay.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5893",["title"]="Sahagin Key Quest",["page_title"]="Sahagin Key Quest",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Sahagin_Key_Quest",["revision"]="103089",["requirements"]="Start: Gimb - Norg (H-9)\010Requirements: Key item: Airship pass for Kazham\010Items: Gold Beastcoin\010Silver Beastcoin\010Norg Shell\0103 Mythril Beastcoins (depending on luck)",["rewards"]="Sahagin Key",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="The Sahagin Key opens the Ornamented Door in Sea Serpent Grotto at (J-11).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtaining Your First Key",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Gimb (Norg (H-9)) in Norg (next to the Chocobo Rental)",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head into Sea Serpent Grotto. Trade a Gold Beastcoin to the \034Gold Door\034 at (I-14) on map 1. You will not lose the item.\010\010If you have not passed through this door before, examine it several times until you see a glitter of gold.\010\010Apply some form of Sneak to avoid aggro.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Bou the Righteous (Sea Serpent Grotto (H-11) / Map 4).\010\010If you leave Sea Serpent Grotto after this point (or accept Tractor), you will have to talk to Bou the Righteous again.",["zone"]="Sea Serpent Grotto",["grid"]="H-11 / Map 4",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Gold Door.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Silver Beastcoin to the \034Silver Door\034 at (N-14). You will not lose the item.\010\010If you have not passed through this door before, examine it several times until you see a glitter of silver.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Hurr the Betrayer (Sea Serpent Grotto (H-3) / Map 2).\010\010He will ask for a Norg Shell, and he will choose randomly between if he wants either 3 Mythril Beastcoins or a Gold Beastcoin.",["zone"]="Sea Serpent Grotto",["grid"]="H-3 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade him the items he requests for a Sahagin Key.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtaining Subsequent Keys",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go through the Silver Door at (Sea Serpent Grotto (N-14) / Map 1).",["zone"]="Sea Serpent Grotto",["grid"]="N-14 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Hurr the Betrayer (Sea Serpent Grotto (H-3) / Map 2).\010\010He will ask for a Norg Shell, along with either 3 Mythril Beastcoins or a Gold Beastcoin.",["zone"]="Sea Serpent Grotto",["grid"]="H-3 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade him the items he requests for a Sahagin Key.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_354",["title"]="Saintly Invitation (Windurst Mission 6-2)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 6-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_6-2",["revision"]="117416",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Previous: Windurst Mission 6-1|Full Moon Fountain",["rewards"]="Rank 7\01040,000 gil\010Ashura Necklace",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A mission issued by Heavens Tower. In reply to the Yagudo Holy One's invitation, you are to compete and triumph at the contest held at Balga's Dais deep within Giddeus.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade ~24 crystals to unlock the mission, then accept it from the Gate Guard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At the top floor of Heavens Tower click on the Vestal Chamber door for a cutscene. \010\010You will receive Key item: Holy One's invitation and the title: \034Hero on Behalf of Windurst\034.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed to Balga's Dais and enter the BCNM \034Saintly Invitation.\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The BCNM fight",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The BCNM is uncapped and up to 6 players are allowed to enter.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Inside are 4 NM Yagudo, all of which need to be defeated: \010\010Chaa Paqa the Profound (SMN)\010\010Juu Zeni the Poisonmist (NIN)\010\010Buu Xolo the Bloodfaced (SAM)\010\010Nuu Kofu the Gentle (WHM)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Yagudo can be slept. It is recommended to fight them in the order listed above, leaving the WHM for last so that Benediction cannot wake the others. This can also take care of Astral Flow and Mijin Gakure early on.\010\010See Discussion for further strategy notes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="They can (and will) use their respective 2-hours.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="They are susceptible to Bard Lullaby, Black Mage Sleep and Sheep pet Sheep Song. \010\010For Strategies, see Testimonials.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Winning the BCNM awards the Key item: Balga champion certificate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Castle Oztroja",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Castle Oztroja and proceed all the way up to the Castle Oztroja / Map 5.",["zone"]="Castle Oztroja",["grid"]=" / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You need to pass through the second Brass Door at Castle Oztroja (H-5) / Map 5 to talk to Kaa Toru the Just.\010\010To open the second Brass Door, you need a Judgment Key, which drops from Yagudo Flagellants in this area. \010\010Note: Those in the area before the first Brass Door Castle Oztroja (G-7, H-7, G-8, H-8) / Map 5 are level 62-66, while the ones in the open area after the first Brass Door Castle Oztroja (G-5, H-5, G-6, H-6) / Map 5 are 70-72. \010Reaching the Castle Oztroja / Map 5",["zone"]="Castle Oztroja",["grid"]="H-5 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To reach this floor, starting from the main entrance on map 1, go through the first brass door by turning the correct lever or running away from the trap and go upstairs at point A.\010\010On this floor proceed to your left towards the other brass door that requires a combination of 4 levers to be opened at (G-8). While you can find the solution you can also easily brute force by turning the levers until it opens.\010\010On this floor just keep going straight at the only available path until you reach Castle Oztroja / Map 5.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To open the door, touch the torch in one of the four corner rooms on the top floor the map.\010\010You have enough time to make through the door without movement speed increase [Horizon change] .",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To proceed through the first Brass Door at Castle Oztroja (H-7) / Map 5, you will need to crack the passwords to the Brass Statue. \010\010Visit the Brass Statue page to see possible combinations and further details.",["zone"]="Castle Oztroja",["grid"]="H-7 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed to the second Brass Door on the platform at Castle Oztroja (H-5) / Map 5\010\010You need to get past one Yagudo High Priest, who has True Sight. \010\010The door is just past the first set of ramps in the center. If you see Yagudo Avatar or Yagudo Templar, then you went too far up.\010\010Whoever has the Judgment Key must trade it to the Brass Door. The key has one use only and the door closes quickly so make sure your party/alliance members are ready to enter.\010\010If someone does not make it through the door before it closes, there are two options, get another key, or have the person die outside the door, then use tractor and raise.",["zone"]="Castle Oztroja",["grid"]="H-5 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Kaa Toru the Just inside the door to obtain the Key item: Holy One's Oath and an Ashura Necklace.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Door:Vestal Chamber at the top of Heavens Tower to complete the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6263",["title"]="Save My Sister",["page_title"]="Save My Sister",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Save_My_Sister",["revision"]="22395",["requirements"]="Start: Baudin \226\128\148 Upper Jeuno (G-8)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 4\010Previous: Crest of Davoi",["rewards"]="Holy Mace\0103000 gil",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Help rid Baudin's sister of the demon that has possessed her.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="NOTE: this quest will not appear in your quest log.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Baudin Upper Jeuno (G-8) tells you that his sister, Audia, has become cursed by some unknown force and craves the bloody raw meat of coeurl. Baudin is very concerned with his sister's well being and wishes he could do something to help. He mentions that Audia's fiance, Albrecht, prays at the Cathedral every day for her well-being.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Cathedral in Upper Jeuno (H-9) and speak with the minster Mailloquetat for a cutscene with Albrecht, who tells you that none of his prayers have been answered and that his fiancee is still cursed.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Baudin Upper Jeuno (G-8) who will ask if you have any news of his sister's condition. No matter what you say, Albrecht appears and inquires if there were any changes.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Side note: an unreferenced girl child NPC turns up again, named Alista. She also appears in the Cathedral above, at the end of the scene with Albrecht and Mailloquetat.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Ru'Lude Gardens (G-7) and speak with Neraf-Najiruf , in the Jeuno guards', who tells you about a similar problem which was cured by a magical torch. He hands you the Ducal Guard's Lantern (key item) and asks you to light it in Eldieme Necropolis. (Various missions/quests, including the Promathia mission Below the Arks, will take priority for this NPC. Neraf-Najiruf will first talk about the broken crystals at the crags or some other quest. If he does, just talk to him once again and you'll get the lantern.)",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="G-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If after talking with him Neraf-Najiruf, he only mentions that \034One time, a rookie of ours got cursed in the necropolis of Eldieme, and I didn't know what to do.\034 then its likely you've not spoken to all of the NPCs the correct amount of times. Baudin, then Mailloquetat (for a cutscene), then Baudin again (another cutscene) and now Neraf-Najiruf should give the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exit to Batallia Downs from Upper Jeuno and enter Eldieme Necropolis at Batallia Downs (I-10)",["zone"]="Batallia Downs",["grid"]="I-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You must travel to four braziers in the following order. WARNING: If you visit a brazier out of sequence, your progress with lighting the lantern will be completely reset, forcing you to start over.\010\010First Brazier: Southwest, Location The Eldieme Necropolis (F-9) / Map 1\010\010Second Brazier: Northeast, Location The Eldieme Necropolis (H-7) / Map 1\010\010Third Brazier: Northwest, Location The Eldieme Necropolis (F-7) / Map 1 \010\010Fourth Brazier: Southeast, Location The Eldieme Necropolis (H-9) / Map 1",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After touching the first brazier in F-9, you will receive a message saying, \034The Ducal Guard's lantern lights dimly.\034 Find your way to the second brazier in H-7, and after lighting it you will receive a message saying, \034The light of Ducal Guard's lantern has intensified.\034 Head to the third brazier at F-7 and you will receive the same message as with the second brazier. Finally, the fourth and last brazier in H-9 you will give you the message, \034The Ducal Guard's lantern is fully lit!\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Upper Jeuno (G-8) and speak with Baudin for a cutscene to complete the quest.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Neraf-Najiruf in Ru'Lude Gardens (G-7) to give his lantern back.",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="G-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_279",["title"]="Save My Son",["page_title"]="Save My Son",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Save_My_Son",["revision"]="120194",["requirements"]="Start: Dietmund \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (G-11)\010Level: 30\010Previous: Chocobo's Wounds",["rewards"]="Beast Whistle\0102,100 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="To cure Dietmund's son of his affliction, go to Qufim Island. Once there, find the flower that only blooms at night, and bring back its roots.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="To start the quest, examine the Door: Merchant's House in Lower Jeuno (G-11), above the chocobo stables for a cutscene. Dietmund will answer the door and will ask for a herb. Agree to bring him a herb.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="G-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Shalott in Upper Jeuno (G-7), who is standing outside the chocobo stables, for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Qufim Island and examine the Night Flowers down the ramp that's on the side of the cliff in Qufim Island (F-8) between 21:32 and 05:40 for a cutscene.\010\010 Was able to get the cutscene at 13:00. [Horizon change] - with rebase update the era+ has been removed.\010\010 A Kraken (37-38) may spawn above the Night Flowers. Sneak or Silent Oil can be used to avoid it entirely.",["zone"]="Qufim Island",["grid"]="F-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Door: Merchant's House in Lower Jeuno (G-11) for a cutscene and your rewards.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="G-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Brutus in Upper Jeuno (G-7), who is standing outside chocobo stables, for final cutscene and unlock BST.\010(*Make sure you are on a LV30 job to complete this quest, or Brutus will make inane comments about standing around doing nothing.)",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Beastmaster (BST)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Beastmaster (BST)",["kind"]="Job unlock",["page"]="Beastmaster",["revision"]="122066"}}},{["id"]="wiki_363",["title"]="Save the Children (San d'Oria Mission 1-3)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 1-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_1-3",["revision"]="121166",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 1-2|Bat Hunt",["rewards"]="Rank 2\0101,000 Gil\010San d'Orian Ring [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Mission Orders: Rescue the children held captive in the Orcish camp in Ghelsba Outpost.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to any San d'Oria Gate Guard and accept the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next speak to Arnau in the Cathedral in Northern San d'Oria (M-6). \010\010He is the main NPC at the Altar in the Chapel section of the Cathedral.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="M-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene, head to Ghelsba Outpost. \010\010The entrance is located in West Ronfaure (E-4).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to the Hut Door located at Ghelsba Outpost (F-10).",["zone"]="Ghelsba Outpost",["grid"]="F-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click the Hut Door and clear the BCNM Save the Children. You will obtain Orcish Hut Key.\010\010Very important to RECLICK the Hut Door after clearing the BCNM for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to a San d'Oria Gate Guard to complete the Mission and receive Rank 2.\010\010There is another optional cutscene at Arnau after speaking with the Gate Guard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5913",["title"]="Save the Clock Tower",["page_title"]="Save the Clock Tower",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Save_the_Clock_Tower",["revision"]="10897",["requirements"]="Start: Derrick - Lower Jeuno (H-7)\010Requirements: Jeuno Reputation 5\010Items: Clock Tower Petition\010Previous: Deal with Tenshodo\010A Clock Most Delicate",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Derrick, who will give you the option to start a petition. When you agree, he gives you the Clock Tower Petition to take to other NPCs to sign.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There are 10 NPCs in total that you need to trade the petition to, who agree to sign it. They are in the following locations: \010\010Pitantimand - Port Jeuno (H-7) (San d'Oria travel agency, arrivals exit)\010Zauko - Lower Jeuno (I-6) (Lightpost next to fountain)\010Teigero-Bangero - Lower Jeuno (H-10)(Merchant's House)\010Souren - Upper Jeuno (G-9) (Infirmary)\010Constance - Upper Jeuno (G-9) (Infirmary)\010Monberaux - Upper Jeuno (G-10) (Infirmary)\010Baudin - Upper Jeuno (G-8) (House steps)\010Zuber - Upper Jeuno (F-7) (Inside Marble Bridge)\010Collet - Upper Jeuno (G-7) (Corner by the dancing troupe)\010Radeivepart - Ru'Lude Gardens (H-9) (Fountain between the San d'Oria, Bastok, and Windurst embassies)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you've traded the Clock Tower Petition to all the NPCs, take it back to Derrick, who will tell you that it seems unlikely that the clock tower will be torn down with that much support.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Game Description\010\010Client: Derrick (Chamber of Commerce and Industry, Lower Jeuno)\010\010Summary:\010The famous clock tower of Jeuno is scheduled for demolition. Gather enough signatures to save it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2556",["title"]="Say It with Flowers",["page_title"]="Say It with Flowers",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Say_It_with_Flowers",["revision"]="116980",["requirements"]="Start: Moari-Kaaori \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (C-9) / South\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Tahrongi Cactus (for success)\010or any other flower (for failure)",["rewards"]="Iron Sword (first time)\010400 gil (repeat)",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Help the poor love-struck youth by going to the Rhinostery and buying him the perfect flower he needs to win over his sweetheart.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="This quest may block Food for Thought depending on quest progress.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Moari-Kaaori will tell you he is lovesick and wants to give his girlfriend the rarest flower you can find. He will describe the flower with three adjectives. He tells you the people at the Rhinostery will have one for him.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ohbiru-Dohbiru in the southern half of the Rhinostery at Windurst Waters (J-9) / South will ask you about the flower. Answer his three questions using the same order and adjectives as used by Moari-Kaaori: rare, mystical, elegant.\010\010Answering incorrectly will cause Ohbiru-Dohbiru to give a different flower, and he will charge you for it. On top of this, he will refuse to sell you another one until you zone.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="J-9 / South",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He will tell you it's the Tahrongi Cactus, but that they've already used their last one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Kenapa-Keppa to learn they come from... the Tahrongi Canyon!",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To get a Tahrongi Cactus, go to Tahrongi Canyon (F-6), which is located in the mountains along the North-Western side. There you find Tahrongi Cacti.",["zone"]="Tahrongi Canyon",["grid"]="F-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the flower back to Moari-Kaaori for your reward.\010\010If you answer the questions incorrectly, you will be sold a different flower from the Rhinostery, and Moari-Kaaori will give you a smaller reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Repeating this quest correctly nets you 400 gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2105",["title"]="Scattered into Shadow",["page_title"]="Scattered into Shadow",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Scattered_into_Shadow",["revision"]="120954",["requirements"]="Start: Brutus \226\128\148 Upper Jeuno (G-7)\010Requirements: Beastmaster 50+\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 1\010Previous: Wings of Gold",["rewards"]="Beast Gaiters",["repeatable"]="af",["summary"]="Many animals conscripted during the war did not return. Brutus wants you to put their souls to rest.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Note: Some form of Sneak (Status Effect) is highly recommended: The area is populated by level 40-49 monsters on the upper level and 50-59 monsters on the lower level, along with level ~80 monsters in the big room leading to the Cloister of Frost.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Part 1: Fei'Yin",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Brutus in Upper Jeuno who will give you three Key item: Aquafloras to put in some Underground Pools in Fei'Yin.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Note: You can do the rest of Part 1 as any Job.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Fei'Yin. The entrance is located at Beaucedine Glacier (J-4).",["zone"]="Beaucedine Glacier",["grid"]="J-4",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in Fei'Yin, proceed to the lower level at (Fei'Yin (G-9) / Map 1) (Connection 'A').",["zone"]="Fei'Yin",["grid"]="G-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On the lower level, there are 3 pools at (Fei'Yin (H-8, H-5, F-5) / Map 2)\010\010When the pool at (Fei'Yin (F-5) / Map 2) is inspected, a Ghost NM named Dabotz's Ghost appears. He can cast Tornado and does a variety of black magic (Smash Axe can stun it). \010\010Dabotz's Ghost is comfortably soloable at level 60+ (see testimonials). It is advised to bring help with you if attempting at 52. \010\010After Dabotz's Ghost dies, inspect the pool again to watch a cutscene.",["zone"]="Fei'Yin",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you inspected all 3 of the Underground Pools, head back to Upper Jeuno.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Brutus and he will send you to Castle Oztroja next. (This step is important, otherwise the Treasure Chest in Castle Oztroja will not yield the Beast Collar.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Part 2: Castle Oztroja\010\010Castle Oztroja Maps\010\010The larger map icons are where the chests can spawn. The smaller map icons are given for convenience of navigation. Hover over a map icon to display the map in a larger size.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Castle Oztroja and obtain a Oztroja Chest Key. \010\010Note: Chest and Coffer Keys drop with a fixed probability of 10% on HorizonXI [Horizon change]\010\010Oztroja Chest Keys drop from:\010\010Yagudo Conquistador (43-47)\010\010Yagudo Prior (45-49)\010\010Yagudo Zealot (42-46)\010\010Yagudo Lutenist (44-48)\010\010Yagudo Parasite (45-49)\010\010Ooze (38-40)\010\010 has plenty of Yagudo which can drop the Oztroja Chest Key. To get there, zone to the third map at Castle Oztroja (J-8) / Map 1, then to the seventh map at Castle Oztroja (G-7) / Map 3 and finally into the basement at Castle Oztroja (I-7) / Map 7 (Connections 'A' -> 'F' -> 'I').",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you obtain a Oztroja Chest Key, search for a Treasure Chest and open it to obtain a Beast Collar.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, locate Tebhi, a monkey NPC which roams , and trade the Beast Collar to him. \010\010Tebhi can be spotted on Wide Scan. \010\010Tebhi will disappear for 15min after receiving the Beast Collar. (Might have been bugged in the past but seems to work as intended as of 2024-01-28, see Talk:Scattered into Shadow#Tebhi.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Upper Jeuno and talk to Brutus one final time to receive the Beast Gaiters.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={"Beastmaster (BST)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Beastmaster (BST)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Beast Gaiters",["revision"]="19388"},{["job"]="Beastmaster (BST)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Scattered into Shadow",["revision"]="120954"}}},{["id"]="wiki_2557",["title"]="Scooped!",["page_title"]="Scooped!",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Scooped%21",["revision"]="119740",["requirements"]="Start: Naiko-Paneiko \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (C-11) / South\010Items: Bronze Box\010Previous: Making Headlines",["rewards"]="1500 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The latest edition of the \034Magic Paradise Weekly,\034 which features the exclusive report on \034Where the Cat Burglar Hides her Kitty,\034 has been stolen. The editor asks that you help retrieve it.",["changes"]="Multiple people have noted that the Sea Crabs that spawn on the boat throughout the trip drop the Bronze Box when it was only fished up Ocean Crabs before. No one has been able to fish up mobs on a regular route and pirate routes haven't been tested. [Wiki: needs verification] \010Please see Talk page.\010\010Was able to fish up Ocean crab during a regular route and get a Bronze box after rebase.",["steps"]={{["text"]="If you have just completed Making Headlines, zone before attempting to start this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Naiko-Paneiko who explains that the next \034Magic Paradise Weekly\034 proof copy was stolen.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional: Talk to Cha Lebagta and Bopa Greso in Windurst Woods for additional information.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Bronze Box to Naiko-Paneiko.\010\010One can be obtained by killing Sea Crab, or Ocean Crab fished up while on the Ship bound for Selbina/Ship bound for Mhaura. [Wiki: needs verification] \010\010Clothespole with Lugworm is a good combination for this.\010Please see Talk page.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57458",["title"]="Scouting the Ashu Talif",["page_title"]="Scouting the Ashu Talif",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Scouting_the_Ashu_Talif",["revision"]="122573",["requirements"]="Start: Halshaob \226\128\148 Nashmau (H-10) / Map 1\010Requirements: Completion of Guests of the Empire\010Fame: None\010Items: 3 x Imperial Bronze Piece\010Previous: Guests of the Empire",["rewards"]="Koga Shuriken\010Up to two Ancient Lockboxes",["repeatable"]="weekly",["summary"]="Investigate the armed crew aboard the Ashu Talif and eliminate them if the Maelstrom Company determines the threat can be overcome.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Guests of the Empire.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Halshaob at Nashmau (H-10) / Map 1 for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Halshaob again and ask for additional details about the assignment.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade three Imperial Bronze Pieces to Halshaob to accept the quest.\010\010 The Imperial Bronze Pieces are consumed.\010\010 Halshaob allows one new Ashu Talif quest acceptance per Conquest Update.\010\010 Different quests from the chain can be held simultaneously if they were accepted after separate resets.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the Cutter in Arrapago Reef.\010\010 A direct route is to use a Runic Portal Use Permit to reach the Dvucca Isle Staging Point at Caedarva Mire (I-9) / Map 2.\010\010 From the staging point, travel west and enter Arrapago Reef at Caedarva Mire (F-9, G-9) / Map 2.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In Arrapago Reef, proceed north to the Cutter at Arrapago Reef (H-8) / Map 5.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ensure every participating party member has Scouting the Ashu Talif active.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Cutter and select \034Scouting the Ashu Talif\034 to enter The Ashu Talif.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat every wave of Ashu Talif Crew and Watch Imp within 30 minutes.\010\010 Swiftwinged Gekko is an optional objective and does not need to be defeated for quest completion.\010\010 Defeating Swiftwinged Gekko causes a second Ancient Lockbox to appear.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the required enemies have been defeated, open the spawned Ancient Lockboxes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine Gate: Lifeboat near the battlefield entrance to leave the ship and complete the quest.\010\010 Use the exit before the battlefield timer expires or the completion may not register. [Wiki: needs verification] \010\010 Completion unlocks Royal Painter Escort.\010\010 Whether the battlefield succeeds or fails, another attempt requires accepting the quest again from Halshaob and trading another three Imperial Bronze Pieces.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57156",["title"]="Seal of the Serpent",["page_title"]="Seal of the Serpent",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Seal_of_the_Serpent",["revision"]="120861",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1\010Previous: Playing the Part",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The Grand Vizier has summoned you to the palace. You are required to divest yourself of all weapons before passing through the Imperial Whitegate.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Playing the Part; this mission begins during its ending cutscene with Naja Salaheem.\010\010 Speaking with Naja again provides additional dialogue but is not required for progression.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Completely empty your Main and Sub equipment slots.\010\010 Remove any shield or second weapon equipped in the Sub slot.\010\010 Ranged and Ammo equipment do not need to be removed.\010\010 The approved palace attire from Guests of the Empire is not required.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Imperial Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-8, L-9) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="L-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The resulting cutscene completes the mission and begins Misplaced Nobility.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_8319",["title"]="Searching for the Right Words",["page_title"]="Searching for the Right Words",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Searching_for_the_Right_Words",["revision"]="113511",["requirements"]="Start: Ilumida \226\128\148 Upper Jeuno (G-8)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 7\010Items: Key item: Moondrop\010Previous: A Candlelight Vigil\010Rubbish Day\010Never to Return",["rewards"]="3000 gil\010Scroll of Sleepga II",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A \034moondrop\034 from the Boyahda Tree is required to open the chest Ilumida's late husband left for her.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Kurou-Morou after completing the prerequisite quests. After a short cutscene, go to Upper Jeuno and speak to Ilumida - aka the one who asked for the candle earlier -for another, in which you learn that Ilumida wants a Key item: Moondrop.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="NOTE: There is a prompt in this cutscene. If you do not agree to help you will not be able to spawn Agas. You may have to talk multiple times to get the cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Boyahda Tree, and examine the ??? at (H-8) of the 2nd map in between 19:00 and 04:00 to spawn Agas.\010\010Will only spawn when the moon can be seen, in other words, not during New Moon.\010\010Agas uses Level 5 Petrify, which means that characters whose level is divisible by 5 (for example 65, 70, 75, etc.) will be Petrified.\010\010The monster can be defeated solo by certain jobs with varying difficulty, and duo by various job combinations at around level 75.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After defeating Agas, examine the ??? again between 19:00 and 04:00 to get the Key item: Moondrop.\010\010If there is no time to obtain the item before 04:00, there is no need to defeat the monster again, even after changing areas or logging out. However, it still cannot be obtained during New Moon.\010\010Only one party member needs to spawn Agas to enable everyone to obtain the Key item: Moondrop.\010\010As long a player is in the party when the monster is defeated, it is possible to obtain the key item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Upper Jeuno and talk to Ilumida for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_8351",["title"]="Secret of the Damp Scroll",["page_title"]="Secret of the Damp Scroll",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Secret_of_the_Damp_Scroll",["revision"]="118457",["requirements"]="Start: Shivivi \226\128\148 Norg (J-8)\010Requirements: Level 10\010Damp Scroll in inventory\010Fame: Tenshodo\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Damp Scroll",["rewards"]="Scroll of Jubaku: Ichi",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Shivivi tells you to go to Horlais Peak to clear up a scroll and make it more readable.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Before beginning the quest you need to acquire a Damp Scroll. \010Damp Scrolls can be acquired in two ways:\010\010Fish it up in the Sea Serpent Grotto\010\010Buy it at the Auction House under Other -> Miscellaneous",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="With the Damp Scroll in your inventory, go and talk to Shivivi at (Norg (J-8) / Map 1) in Norg to start the quest. Shivivi tells you to dip the scroll in the hot spring on Horlais Peak.",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="J-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From West Ronfaure head to Ghelsba Outpost. Stick to the left wall to enter Yughott Grotto. Run through the grotto and exit at the top entrance to Fort Ghelsba at (Yughott Grotto (K-5) / Map 1). From this exit hug the left wall to enter Yughott Grotto through the hut at (Fort Ghelsba (J-8) / Map 1). Take the exit at (Yughott Grotto (J-9) / Map 2) to Horlais Peak's hot spring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the scroll to the hot spring to complete the quest and receive a scroll of Jubaku: Ichi.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Tenshodo",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_12358",["title"]="Secrets of Ovens Lost",["page_title"]="Secrets of Ovens Lost",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Secrets_of_Ovens_Lost",["revision"]="119207",["requirements"]="Start: Jonette \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold (G-9)\010Requirements: Access to Sacrarium (Promathia Mission 4-3)\010Items: Optional:\010Bronze Key\010(Only needed if you do the quest in Phomiuna Aqueducts; can also use Thief's Tools if your main job is set to Thief)\010Previous: Spice Gals",["rewards"]="Miratete's Memoirs",["repeatable"]="conquest",["summary"]="Jonette's dream is to revitalize the safehold's children by serving them an array of traditional Tavnazian dishes. However, she needs a cookbook to fulfill that dream.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Despachiaire at Tavnazian Safehold (K-10) / Top Floor for an initial cutscene. \010\010Despachiaire is behind the Walnut Door at Tavnazian Safehold (K-9) / Top Floor. \010\010There are a number of cutscenes triggered by talking with Despachiaire. Keep at it until he mentions his past as a merchant.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="K-10 / Top Floor",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, go to Jonette at Tavnazian Safehold (G-9) / Ground Floor to receive the quest. \010Note: If you have already done the quest once, to repeat just talk to Jonette at Tavnazian Safehold (G-9) / Ground Floor and she will thank you and ask you to bring any other cookbooks you find to her. That will re-activate the quest in your log.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="G-9 / Ground Floor",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Key item: Tavnazian Cookbook that she seeks can be found in one of four rooms in the Sacrarium or one of four rooms in Phomiuna Aqueducts.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Option 1: Sacrarium",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Sacrarium / Map 2",["zone"]="Sacrarium",["grid"]=" / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A ??? will appear on the backside of a bookshelf (not to be confused with the ??? on the desks) in one of the four corner rooms at (Sacrarium (H-5, F-5, H-11, F-11) / Map 2. Upon selecting the ??? you will receive a Key item: Tavnazian Cookbook.\010\010The ??? stays in each room for exactly 10min Earth time (4h10m game time) and will then disappear for 10sec Earth time (4m10s game time) before appearing in the next room. Thus it is possible to check all four rooms and miss it because of this short period of being gone.\010\010The pattern of movement is \010NE Sacrarium (H-5) / Map 2 -> NW Sacrarium (F-5) / Map 2 -> SE Sacrarium (H-11) / Map 2 -> SW Sacrarium (F-11) / Map 2 -> NE Sacrarium (H-5) / Map 2 and so on in that order.",["zone"]="Sacrarium",["grid"]="H-5 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Option 2: Phomiuna Aqueducts",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The cookbook can be found in one of the four libraries in Phomiuna Aqueducts (map 3).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The ??? for the key item rotates between the rooms at (F-7), (F-9), (J-7), (J-9).\010\010The third map is comprised of two completely distinct areas that are not connected. You must climb up different ladders to reach each section.\010\010The time the ??? spends in reach room seems to be 10 minutes, like in Sacrarium. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will need a Bronze Key from the Fomors in the Aqueducts or some Thief's Tools with your main job set as Thief to get past a locked gate to reach the third map of Phomiuna Aqueducts.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To reach the possible ??? locations at F-7 and F-9, go the same path as in Distant Beliefs (Use Bronze Key at (G-8) of the second map, then climb the ladder at (E-8).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To reach the possible ??? locations at (J-7) and (J-9), use a Bronze Key at (J-6) of the second map and climb the ladder at (M-8).\010\010This path is much shorter.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Completion",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the Key item: Tavnazian Cookbook back to Jonette at Tavnazian Safehold (G-9) / Ground Floor for your reward.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="G-9 / Ground Floor",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Note: If you started Promathia Mission 5-3 by talking to Cid you can't start this quest until you have reached a certain point in the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57163",["title"]="Sentinels' Honor",["page_title"]="Sentinels' Honor",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Sentinels%27_Honor",["revision"]="120870",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1\010Previous: In the Blood",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A villain by the name of \034Duzaf the Blackheart\034 is rumored to have made an attempt on the life of the Empress. President Naja has vowed to claim the bounty on his head in the name of Salaheem's Sentinels.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After completing In the Blood, zone once and wait until after the next Japanese midnight (15:00 UTC).\010\010 While waiting, make sure you possess the Key item: Ephramadian Gold Coin, which is required during Testing the Waters.\010\010 If you no longer possess one, examine Jazaraat's Headstone at Caedarva Mire (E-10) / Map 1 to obtain another.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Naja Salaheem in Salaheem's Sentinels at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.\010\010 Before both the zoning and timing requirements have been met, Naja provides additional dialogue but does not advance the mission.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The resulting cutscene completes the mission and begins Testing the Waters.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57161",["title"]="Shades of Vengeance",["page_title"]="Shades of Vengeance",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Shades_of_Vengeance",["revision"]="120867",["requirements"]="Start: Amnaf \226\128\148 Cutter, Arrapago Reef (H-8) / Map 5\010Previous: Prevalence of Pirates",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have been ordered to participate in the search for Aphmau by the Immortal, Amnaf. You are to begin in Periqia, ancestral land of the corsairs.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Prevalence of Pirates; this mission begins during its ending cutscene at the Cutter.\010\010 Each player who needs to complete this mission receives the Key item: Periqia Assault Area Entry Permit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Dvucca Isle Staging Point at Caedarva Mire (I-9) / Map 2.\010\010 From the Cutter, travel south and use the nearby exit to Caedarva Mire.",["zone"]="Caedarva Mire",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Runic Seal and select \034Shades of Vengeance\034 to enter Periqia.\010\010 Every player currently on this mission must possess the Key item: Periqia Assault Area Entry Permit. It is consumed upon entry.\010\010 Players who have already progressed beyond this mission may assist without possessing a permit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed to the group of K23H1-LAMIA at Periqia (H-9).",["zone"]="Periqia",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat K23H1-LAMIA until the mission objective is completed.\010\010 Ten Lamiae spawn. The required number of defeats is randomized and may range from 3 to all 10.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow the automatic exit and cutscene in Caedarva Mire to complete the mission, receive the title \034Nashmeira's Mercenary,\034 and begin In the Blood.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If the Mission Fails",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Key item: Periqia Assault Area Entry Permit is still consumed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait until the next Vana'diel day, then speak with Nahshib at Caedarva Mire (I-9) / Map 2 to receive another permit.",["zone"]="Caedarva Mire",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 2",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_632",["title"]="Shadows of the Departed",["page_title"]="Shadows of the Departed",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Shadows_of_the_Departed",["revision"]="118983",["requirements"]="Start: Esha'ntarl \226\128\148 within Ru'Lude Gardens palace\010Items: Key item: Whisper of the Wyrmking\010Previous: Awakening\010Storms of Fate",["rewards"]="Key item: Note Written by Esha'ntarl\010Key item: Promyvion - Dem Sliver\010Key item: Promyvion - Holla Sliver\010Key item: Promyvion - Mea Sliver\010Mog Wardrobe 2: 5 slots",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After receiving Key item: Whisper of the Wyrmking from Storms of Fate and returning to Ru'Lude Garden Palace for cutscene, you must wait until the next Japanese Midnight update to activate this quest. NOTE: If you do not return to Ru'Lude Garden after the fight before the next conquest tally, you will have to wait another week. Zilart Mission 17 \034Awakening\034 must also be completed to trigger this cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Walk into the palace in Ru'Lude Gardens for a cutscene and the Key item: Note Written by Esha'ntarl.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Visit the three Promyvions and get the following key items at the Memory Fluxes on the 4th floor:\010\010Promyvion - Holla (J-10): Key item: Promyvion - Holla Sliver\010\010Promyvion - Dem (K-4): Key item: Promyvion - Dem Sliver\010\010Promyvion - Mea (K-6): Key item: Promyvion - Mea Sliver",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the palace in Ru'Lude Gardens for a final cutscene with Esha'ntarl.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7498",["title"]="Shady Business",["page_title"]="Shady Business",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Shady_Business",["revision"]="101206",["requirements"]="Start: Talib \226\128\148 Port Bastok (F-6)\010Fame: Tenshodo\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Zinc Ore x4\010Previous: Beauty and the Galka",["rewards"]="350 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Talib of the Tenshodo is buying zinc. Bring him four chunks of the ore to receive gil.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Talib (located downstairs in Warehouse 2) who tells you he wants four more Zinc Ore.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain four Zinc Ore and trade them to Talib to complete the quest and receive the gil reward. \010Note This is one of the primary quests used to raise Tenshodo fame, which is required for many quests in Norg. This quest can be repeated by continuing to trade sets of four ore to Talib; zoning is not required. It does not raise Bastok reputation when it is completed, only Tenshodo reputation\010\010It takes 109 Zinc Ore (27 trades of 4 plus the 1 from the pre-quest) in order to go from 0 Norg fame to level 4 and be able to get the Trial by Water, Utsusemi: Ichi and Tonko: Ichi quests. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Tenshodo",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1322",["title"]="Sharpening the Sword",["page_title"]="Sharpening the Sword",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Sharpening_the_Sword",["revision"]="107794",["requirements"]="Start: Ailbeche \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (J-9)\010Requirements: Paladin 40+\010Previous: Father and Son and A Knight's Test",["rewards"]="Honor Sword",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="The boy needs a whetstone to sharpen an old blade. Find one for him in Ordelle's Caves.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete the Father and Son quest and make sure to give the Willow Fishing Rod back to the son.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Ailbeche again who will ask you for an Key item: Ordelle Whetstone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Sobane in Southern San d'Oria (D-6). Be sure to talk to her twice if you get a cutscene the first time. The cutscene is the beginning of either the quest Signed in Blood or Tea with a Tonberry? and not part of this quest.\010From this point on, the quest can be completed on any job.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="D-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Ordelle's Caves, entering from the western most entrance of La Theine Plateau (F-7).",["zone"]="La Theine Plateau",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From the first map of Ordelle's Caves, head east to the ramp at Ordelle's Caves (I-6) / map1. This puts you on the second map. Head southwest to the room at Ordelle's Caves (G-8) / map2 , then take a left. Next, head south up the ramp at Ordelle's Caves (H-9) / map2. This puts you back on the first map. The Stalagmite is next to the hole in the first small room.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select the Stalagmite to spawn and defeat the NM Polevik, an Earth Elemental.\010\010Can be defeated on any job, as long as quest is active.\010\010Should be level 65+ to solo the fight.\010\010If completing with multiple Paladins, NM only needs to be defeated once and all Paladins can loot the KI.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Touch the Stalagmite again to receive the Key item: Ordelle Whetstone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Ailbeche to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="For strategies",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Paladin (PLD)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Paladin (PLD)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Honor Sword",["revision"]="16953"},{["job"]="Paladin (PLD)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Sharpening the Sword",["revision"]="107794"}}},{["id"]="wiki_1774",["title"]="Shattering Stars",["page_title"]="Shattering Stars",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Shattering_Stars",["revision"]="119019",["requirements"]="Start: Maat \226\128\148 Ru'Lude Gardens (H-5)\010Level: 66 (on a non-ToAU job)\010Items: Relevant Testimony\010Previous: Riding on the Clouds",["rewards"]="Raises level cap to 75\010Mog Wardrobe: 5 Slots [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Maat has issued a final challenge to test your limits. Return with the items he has requested and the trial will begin.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Maat at level 66 or higher non-ToAU job to receive this final test. He will ask you to bring him a testimony of your job. These are dropped by various mobs depending on job.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you bring Maat the testimony, he will challenge you to a fight to prove once and for all you have ultimate mastery over your job. You will be warped to the BCNM area after a confirmation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Maat assumes your job and has all the abilities of it including your 2hr.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Regardless of your job, he fights with his fists and can use Asuran Fists several times in succession, the limit of which is uncertain.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Your sub-job is disabled for this fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You have 10 minutes to beat Maat.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you succeed, you will receive a scroll of Instant Warp, unless you already have one in your bag or mog safe/locker, in which case you will get nothing.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Maat again in Ru'Lude Gardens to complete the quest!!!!!!",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="While not actually required to limit break to 75 on all jobs, in order to receive Maat's Cap, you must beat him on all 15 non-ToAU jobs. This means the quest is repeatable, but you only need to do it once to break the level cap.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If Maat fails to teleport you to your respective BC area upon presenting him your testimony try traveling to the BC itself and trading your testimony there.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once Maat has been initially defeated, all subsequent battles can be fought uncapped. The 65 lower level cap may still apply.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Shattering Stars THF: Once Maat has been defeated once and you are fighting for a second time or more - stealing the scroll of instant warp does NOT allow you to win. You must either kill him or fight until he tells you that you have won.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you lose the fight, or fail to defeat Maat in time your testimony will be rendered unusable, you must drop your used testimony and farm a new one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_552",["title"]="Sheltering Doubt (Promathia Mission 4-1)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 4-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_4-1",["revision"]="120082",["requirements"]="Previous: Darkness Named",["rewards"]="Access to Riverne - Site #B01",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Prishe has returned to Tavnazia, and it would be wise to follow. The winds of twenty years past have once again begun to swirl about the islands. What evils do these winds carry?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Return to Tavnazian Safehold for a cutscene.\010\010Tavnazian Safehold AH will now be linked to the Jeuno AH.\010\010You will now be able to do the Lufaise Meadows supplies quest.\010If your nation owns the region the supplies can be picked up before heading to Tavnazia saving an additional trip.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Despachiaire at Tavnazian Safehold (K-10) / Map 2, on the top floor, behind the Walnut door.\010\010You may need to speak to him multiple times in order to receive the correct cutscene involving Tenzen.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="K-10 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Justinius at Tavnazian Safehold (J-6) / Map 2, on the top floor, for another brief cutscene.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="J-6 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Misareaux Coast (I-11) and inspect the Dilapidated Gate.",["zone"]="Misareaux Coast",["grid"]="I-11",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57152",["title"]="Shield of Diplomacy",["page_title"]="Shield of Diplomacy",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Shield_of_Diplomacy",["revision"]="120857",["requirements"]="Previous: Finders Keepers",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You are once again in the employ of Lady Karababa. This time, your role is to protect the ambassador within the ominous Navukgo Execution Chamber. Will you be able to redeem your reputation with President Naja...?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Finders Keepers; this mission begins immediately afterward.\010\010 Speaking with Naja Salaheem at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1 provides additional mission dialogue but is not required for progression.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the Navukgo Execution Chamber entrance at Mount Zhayolm (D-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the Navukgo Execution Chamber for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Decorative Bronze Gate for a second cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the gate again and select \034Shield of Diplomacy\034 to enter the battlefield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Khimaira 13 within 30 minutes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The victory cutscene completes the mission, grants the title \034Karababa's Bodyguard,\034 and begins Social Graces.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3715",["title"]="Shoot First, Ask Questions Later",["page_title"]="Shoot First, Ask Questions Later",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Shoot_First%2C_Ask_Questions_Later",["revision"]="119650",["requirements"]="Start: Cid \226\128\148 Metalworks (H-8)\010Requirements: Marksmanship Skill 250+\010Level 72+ Ranger\010No other WSNM quest active\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: none\010Items: Gun of Trials\010Key item: Weapon Training Guide\010Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth\010Key item: Annals of Truth",["rewards"]="Detonator Weapon Skill",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Cid would like you to assist him in testing a new firearm. Return to the lab when the weapon no longer functions properly.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="NOTE: You cannot begin this quest if you already have another quest involving the Key item: Weapon Training Guide active.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Cid in Metalworks to receive the Gun of Trials and a Key item: Weapon Training Guide.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the Gun of Trials until the latent effect disappears. \010\010The Weapon Skills must be performed by this particular gun; using a melee Weapon Skill with this gun merely equipped does not count.\010\010Weapon Skills performed while under Level Sync count.\010\010You receive 1 point for opening/soloing a weapon skill, 2 points for closing a Lv.1 Skillchain, 3 points for closing a Lv.2 Skillchain and 5 points for closing a level 3 skillchain.\010\010No message is given when the latent effect is lost. To check if the latent effect has disappeared, simply check if you have the bonus stats; if not, you are done. It is not necessary to unequip the gun for the latent effect to disappear; the stats disappear immediately upon acquiring the 300th WS point.\010\010Note your Elemental Resistance bonuses from the weapon: they will be gone if the latent is broken.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you no longer receive the latent effect bonus, head back to Metalworks and trade the Gun of Trials to Cid, who takes the weapon from you and gives you a Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth and instructions to head to the Boyahda Tree.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in the Boyahda Tree, go to Map 3 (J-8) and click the ??? to spawn the NM named Beet Leafhopper.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the NM is dead, reexamine the ??? to obtain the Key item: Annals of Truth.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Cid for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7451",["title"]="Signed in Blood",["page_title"]="Signed in Blood",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Signed_in_Blood",["revision"]="116605",["requirements"]="Start: Sobane \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (D-6)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Cathedral Tapestry\010Ordelle Chest Key",["rewards"]="Cunning Earring\0103,500g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Sobane has heard some disturbing news from her husband, the head royal chef. She wishes to make a request concerning that tale, but first requires you to bring a \034cathedral tapestry\034 to prove your integrity.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Sobane (Southern San d'Oria ( Southern San d'Oria (D-6) ), in a house), she is willing to give you a quest, but she needs to be able to trust that you'll keep your mouth shut. She wants you to retrieve a Cathedral Tapestry.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="D-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Cathedral Tapestry by killing Orcish Fighters in Fort Ghelsba or the Yughott Grotto.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the tapestry to Sobane and she'll explain the next step.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Selbina, where you will find that the person you are looking for is nowhere to be found. Talk to the mayor, Abelard, @ ( Selbina (G-9) ) and he'll say he has \034no idea\034 what you're talking about... but he will then mention something about a diary he found, and that some key pages are missing... perhaps his lips will loosen if you help him find them.",["zone"]="Selbina",["grid"]="G-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Ordelle's Caves and hunt for an Ordelle Chest Key. Once you find a key, look for a Treasure Chest and open it.\010\010 Only people who have this quest flagged will receive some Key item: Torn-Out Pages.\010\010 Thief can open chest and receive key item using Thief's Tools, Skeleton Key or Living Key .\010\010 This key item takes precedence over the Magical Pattern from The Goblin Tailor RSE quest; if both are active, a character opening the chest will receive this key item first.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Selbina and talk to the mayor. He'll reveal some information to you which will prove interesting to Sobane.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Sobane to complete this quest and to receive your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7536",["title"]="Silence of the Rams",["page_title"]="Silence of the Rams",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Silence_of_the_Rams",["revision"]="106147",["requirements"]="Start: Paujean \226\128\148 Port Bastok (F-6)\010Fame: Tenshodo\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Rampaging Horn\010Lumbering Horn",["rewards"]="Purple Belt",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You are being tested by the Tenshodo. Defeat the two monstrous rams in the wild and bring back their horns -- a rampaging horn and a lumbering horn -- to Paujean.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Paujean on the bottom floor of Warehouse 2 (Bastok).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Paujean a Rampaging Horn and a Lumbering Horn to complete the quest. \010\010The Lumbering Horn drops from Lumbering Lambert (level 27-28) or Bloodtear Baldurf (level 55-56) in La Theine Plateau. \010\010The Rampaging Horn drops from Rampaging Ram (level 27-28) or Steelfleece Baldarich (level 55-56) in Konschtat Highlands.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Tenshodo",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2124",["title"]="Sin Hunting",["page_title"]="Sin Hunting",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Sin_Hunting",["revision"]="119962",["requirements"]="Start: Perih Vashai \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (K-7)\010Requirements: Ranger 40+\010Items: Glittersand\010Previous: The Fanged One",["rewards"]="Hunter's Zamburak [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="Track down Semih Lafihna, who has gone down to check out matters at the Ranguemont Pass, and hand her a twinstone earring.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Perih Vashai will ask you to hand Semih Lafihna the Key item: Chieftainness' Twinstone Earring, and tells you to speak with the Sibyl Guard Semih Lafihna in Ranguemont Pass, which can be reached in the northeast of East Ronfaure near San d'Oria. (You can now swap to another job)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you enter Ranguemont Pass, proceed north until you reach the guarded door, and talk to Perchond at Ranguemont Pass (F-10).",["zone"]="Ranguemont Pass",["grid"]="F-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene, have Myffore open the door and head through.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Start off going north and east, but head north at the T and northwest until you find the Evil Weapons at Ranguemont Pass (E-5). Kill these for the Glittersand.",["zone"]="Ranguemont Pass",["grid"]="E-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return back and trade the Glittersand to Perchond, who will give you Key item: Perchond's Envelope.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Jugner Forest and near the large lake you will find Alexius at Jugner Forest (I-6), who will tell you to inspect the ??? just south of the lake, at Jugner Forest (H-6), during the Full Moon. \010\010For the moon to be full, the cycle needs to be >95%. **I was able to check @ 90% full moon.**",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the ??? during a full moon, watch a cutscene, and return to Perih Vashai for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you started this quest prior to rebase and did not complete it you will more than likely require GM assistance for the cutscene in Jugner forest at the H-6 location(tree ???).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Ranger (RNG)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Ranger (RNG)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Hunter's Zamburak",["revision"]="56796"},{["job"]="Ranger (RNG)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Sin Hunting",["revision"]="119962"}}},{["id"]="wiki_558",["title"]="Slanderous Utterings (Promathia Mission 4-4)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 4-4",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_4-4",["revision"]="104797",["requirements"]="Previous: The Secrets of Worship",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Appalled that Prishe would even think of laying her hands on the statue of Promathia, the elder, Despachiaire, has called her to his quarters for punishment. If Prishe is banished from the safehold, you may be unable to retrieve the amulet you need to find the fourth mothercrystal.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Head to the Despachiaire's room behind the Walnut Door in Tavnazian Safehold (K-10) / Top Floor. Approaching Despachiaire will trigger a cutscene.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="K-10 / Top Floor",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the basement of Tavnazian Safehold and zone into Sealion's Den. Inspect the Iron Gate at Sealion's Den (H-6) to end the mission.",["zone"]="Sealion's Den",["grid"]="H-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional: Speak with Despachiaire again for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6860",["title"]="Sleepless Nights",["page_title"]="Sleepless Nights",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Sleepless_Nights",["revision"]="108355",["requirements"]="Start: Paouala \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (M-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Mary's Milk",["rewards"]="5000g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Paouala cannot sleep, so bring her some Mary's Milk to cure her insomnia.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Paouala (Southern San d'Oria (M-8)), who is located in the southernmost of the three houses there, on the second floor.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="M-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She will say that she has heard that drinking jugs of Mary's Milk would help with her insomnia, and asks if you could bring her one.\010\010Mary's Milk can be found at the Auction House, or by defeating the NM Stray Mary in Konschtat Highlands (100% drop rate).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade her one for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_361",["title"]="Smash the Orcish Scouts (San d'Oria Mission 1-1)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 1-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_1-1",["revision"]="28832",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Items: Orcish Axe",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Mission Orders: Hunt Orcs lurking outside San d'Oria and bring back one of their axes.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to any San d'Orian Gate Guard to begin this mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go outside the city and kill Orcish Fodder until you receive an Orcish Axe. Orcish Fodder can be found in East Ronfaure and West Ronfaure.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you receive an Orcish Axe return to the Gate Guard and trade them the Orcish Axe to finish the Mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7507",["title"]="Smoke on the Mountain",["page_title"]="Smoke on the Mountain",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Smoke_on_the_Mountain",["revision"]="104651",["requirements"]="Start: Hungry Wolf \226\128\148 Metalworks (G-9)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Giant Sheep Meat\010Galkan Sausage",["rewards"]="300 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Hungry Wolf wants you to bring him a Galkan sausage, a dish that his co-worker, Offa, told him was marvelously delectable.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Hungry Wolf in the eatery; he's dissatisfied with the food and wants you to bring him a Galkan Sausage. He mentions that his friend Offa might have more information.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Talk to Offa to learn how to make the sausage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Galkan Sausage either from the Auction House or by following the recipe:\010\010Obtain a piece of Giant Sheep Meat. \010\010Go to South Gustaberg and follow the path starting in the northeast corner of South Gustaberg (K-10) to a goblin camp at the top of a small hill. (See the map.)\010\010Trade the sheep meat to the ??? in the campfire.\010\010Wait one game day for the sausage to cook.\010\010Examine the fire to get your sausage.\010NoteLow-level jobs will catch aggro from goblins at the camp, and there is a chance that they will link; if you are not capable of fighting more than one at a time you may want to bring a friend, wait until you've gained a couple levels, or just buy the sausage from the auction house.\010NoteIt appears that you cannot zone out of South Gustaberg while the sheep meat is cooking, otherwise the campfire will simply give the \034This fire looks perfect for cooking.\034 message. This includes logging out. You must stay in the zone for the whole duration required.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Galkan Sausage to Hungry Wolf to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57153",["title"]="Social Graces",["page_title"]="Social Graces",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Social_Graces",["revision"]="120858",["requirements"]="Previous: Shield of Diplomacy",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="After protecting Lady Karababa and earning her praise, return to Salaheem's Sentinels. President Naja may finally have a bonus for you.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Shield of Diplomacy; this mission begins immediately after its victory cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Aht Urhgan Whitegate and enter the second platform of Salaheem's Sentinels at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.\010\010 The cutscene triggers automatically as you enter the platform; speaking with Naja Salaheem is not required.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The cutscene completes the mission and begins Foiled Ambition.\010\010 To continue Foiled Ambition, zone once and wait until the next Vana'diel day.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2513",["title"]="Something Fishy",["page_title"]="Something Fishy",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Something_Fishy",["revision"]="107196",["requirements"]="Start: Tokaka \226\128\148 Port Windurst (C-8)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Bastore Sardine",["rewards"]="70 Gil",["repeatable"]="zone",["summary"]="Tokaka can tell the flow patterns and temperature of the ocean currents by looking at certain fish. Bring her any Bastore Sardines that you catch so she can help keep the fishermen informed as to where to drop their lines.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Tokaka, in the Fishermen's Guild (Windurst), will pay you 70 Gil for each Bastore Sardine you bring her.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You must leave the zone and come back to restart the quest each time. You also have to talk to her before you make each trade.\010\010You may only trade one Bastore Sardine at a time.\010\010Note you can use Mumbo-Bumbo right next to the guild bridge to warp back and forth between Port Windurst [Template Tooltip-Connection-Map: map=Windurst-port.png / blip=RedBlip / text=C-7 / x=19.70 / y=41.94] and Windurst Woods [Template Tooltip-Connection-Map: map=Windurst-woods.png / blip=RedBlip / text=G-10 / x=40.00 / y=61].",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3734",["title"]="Sorcery of the North",["page_title"]="Sorcery of the North",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Sorcery_of_the_North",["revision"]="107061",["requirements"]="Start: Eperdur \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (M-7)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Fei'Yin Chest Key\010Previous: Healing the Land",["rewards"]="Scroll of Teleport-Vahzl",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="An ancient tome of magic is lost. Journey to Fei'Yin and find another to replace it.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Eperdur to start the quest. He is located at Northern San d'Oria (M-7), on the 2nd floor of the Cathedral.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="M-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Fei'Yin and obtain a Fei'Yin Chest Key. \010\010Mobs here are in the 40-50 range and aggro to sound. Consider bringing a form of Sneak (Status Effect). \010\010Shadows have a 5% drop rate on the Fei'Yin Chest Key. Ore Golems and Underworld Bats have only a 1% drop rate. \010\010Alternatively, one can use Thief's Tools as a Thief to open a Treasure Chest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Open a Treasure Chest and you get the Key item: Fei'Yin Magic Tome.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring it back to Eperdur to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_22567",["title"]="Soul Searching",["page_title"]="Soul Searching",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Soul_Searching",["revision"]="57100",["requirements"]="Requirements: Completed Zilart Mission 7 - The Chamber of Oracles\010Items: Key item: Prismatic Fragment",["rewards"]="Bat Earring",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Dispel the troubled souls of those who perished while on their pilgrimages.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must first have completed Zilart Mission 7 - The Chamber of Oracles.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have received the Key item: Prismatic Fragment you can return to Sanctuary of Zi'Tah.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Cermet Headstone The Sanctuary of Zi'Tah (I-7). You will receive a cutscene and the Bat Earring.",["zone"]="The Sanctuary of Zi'Tah",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7446",["title"]="Souls in Shadow",["page_title"]="Souls in Shadow",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Souls_in_Shadow",["revision"]="121207",["requirements"]="Start: Novalmauge \226\128\148 Bostaunieux Oubliette (G-8)\010Requirements: Warrior, Dark Knight, or Beastmaster Level 71+\010Scythe Skill 240+\010No other WSNM quest active\010Items: Scythe of Trials\010Key item: Weapon Training Guide\010Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth\010Key item: Annals of Truth",["rewards"]="The weapon skill Spiral Hell",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Lift the curse on the scythe that Novalmauge has given you and gain a new weapon technique.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Note: You cannot start this quest if you have another WSNM quest active.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Novalmauge in the hallway at F/H-8 in Bostaunieux Oubliette to receive the Scythe of Trials and a Key item: Weapon Training Guide.\010\010Trading the weapon back gives the option to cancel the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the Scythe of Trials until the latent effect disappears.\010\010To remove the latent effect, you must perform Weapon Skills and Skillchains on monsters that check Easy Prey or higher to accumulate 300 Weapon Skill Points.\010\010To check to see if the latent effect has disappeared, see if you do not get the elemental resistance bonuses. If not, you are done. 'Note' the latent effect itself will not disappear, only the bonuses it gives will.\010\010You do NOT have to un-equip/re-equip the weapon to check for changes in the elemental resistance bonuses.\010\010You cannot earn points towards unlocking the weapon by participating in Campaign Battles, but points can be earned while in Level Sync.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you no longer receive the latent effect bonus, head back to Bostaunieux Oubliette and give the Scythe of Trials back to Novalmauge in exchange for a Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth. He tells you to head to the Den of Rancor.\010---",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Temple of Uggalepih via the main entrance at Yhoator Jungle (J-11).\010\010Follow the wall on your right all the way to Temple of Uggalepih (F-5) and zone into Yhoator Jungle (H-11).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed forward from Entrance 2 to Entrance 3 at Yhoator Jungle (H-11).\010\010There is a Tonberry Chopper in the path which will aggro Lv.75's; he's close enough to the zone line that you can run past him.",["zone"]="Yhoator Jungle",["grid"]="H-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have zoned back into Temple of Uggalepih (I-5) / Map 2, head south to Temple of Uggalepih (I-10) / Map 2.\010\010Defeat the Temple Guardian to open the door.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed to Temple of Uggalepih (I-7) / Map 2 and the door using a Key item: Paintbrush of Souls on the Picture Frame.\010\010Once the door opens, you will zone into Den of Rancor (F-5).",["zone"]="Temple of Uggalepih",["grid"]="I-7 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Sneak/Invis and proceed to Den of Rancor (I-5) to enter Map 2.\010\010Go to Den of Rancor (I-13) / Map 2. Click the ??? to spawn the NM Mokumokuren.\010\010Once the NM is dead, reexamine the ??? to obtain the Key item: Annals of Truth.",["zone"]="Den of Rancor",["grid"]="I-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring this back to Novalmauge for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5467",["title"]="Spice Gals",["page_title"]="Spice Gals",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Spice_Gals",["revision"]="106805",["requirements"]="Start: Rouva \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (I-8)\010Requirements: Ancient Vows Completed\010Level: 40+\010Items: Giant Scale (1-2)\010Key item: Rivernewort",["rewards"]="Miratete's Memoirs",["repeatable"]="yes",["summary"]="Rouva needs a sprig of the rare Rivernewort to spruce up her succulent suppers.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Rouva at Southern San d'Oria (I-8) in Southern San d'Oria to start the quest.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain Key item: Rivernewort from a ??? in either Riverne - Site #A01 or Riverne - Site #B01.\010\010 In Riverne - Site #A01 the ??? is found at Riverne - Site A01 (E-8) on the island that connects to Monarch Linn.\010\010 You need two Giant Scales to get there.\010\010 In Riverne - Site #B01 the ??? is found in Riverne - Site B01 (E-7) near the Spatial Displacement heading south toward Monarch Linn. \010\010 You need one Giant Scale to get there.\010\010Neither ??? ever despawns, allowing any number of players to grab the key item with no wait.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Rouva with the Key item: Rivernewort for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Consider completing Uninvited Guests at the same time; both ??? are found on the way to the battle for that quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7508",["title"]="Stamp Hunt",["page_title"]="Stamp Hunt",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Stamp_Hunt",["revision"]="111322",["requirements"]="Start: Arawn \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (J-10)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1",["rewards"]="Leather Gorget",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Go stamp hunting! Get all the stamps for Arawn's stamp sheet from guards all over Bastok.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Arawn; he and Emrys are stamp collectors and he gives you a blank Stamp Sheet so you can help him collect stamps.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain the stamps by talking to 7 guards spread out all over Bastok. You can get the locations, sort of, by examining the stamp sheet.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Arawn again to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Try to get the Moogle Exit Upgrade. It really makes this time-consuming quest easier and less time consuming!\010\010The 7 guards are:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bastok Markets\010\010Pavel at Bastok Markets (D-11) (West Gate)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bastok Mines\010\010Deadly Spider at Bastok Mines (G-8) (2nd level of the Depot)\010\010Tall Mountain at Bastok Mines (J-7) (Next to Alchemist Guild, guarding off limits area)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Metalworks\010\010Romualdo at Metalworks (K-9) (Southern Cannonry, near President's Office)\010\010Elayne at Metalworks (G-8) (Stand between the elevators and face east, go down stairs to the temple)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Port Bastok\010\010Ehrhard at Port Bastok (G-5) (Standing on the northeast corner outside of Warehouse #1)\010\010Latifah at Port Bastok (J-8) (Just north of the Drawbridge)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2041",["title"]="Star Struck",["page_title"]="Star Struck",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Star_Struck",["revision"]="75398",["requirements"]="Start: Koru-Moru \226\128\148 Windurst Walls (E-7)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Meteorite\010Torn Epistle",["rewards"]="Compound Eye Circlet",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Koru-Moru wants you to find him a rough black stone, for some spaced-out reason.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="To start the quest, kill Savanna Rarabs in West Sarutabaruta until you receive a Torn Epistle. Koru-Moru will not give you the quest until you have a Torn Epistle in your inventory. You must not have the quest Class Reunion active in order to activate this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Koru-Moru will smell the scent of his beloved in the letter you are carrying and asks for a rough black stone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill crawlers until one drops a meteorite and then bring it back to Koru-Moru and he will give you a reward.\010\010Important: The meteorite is only dropped by Crawlers around Starfall Hillock in West Sarutabaruta.\010\010Note: You can also trade him the Torn Epistle for 50 gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7516",["title"]="Stardust",["page_title"]="Stardust",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Stardust",["revision"]="104301",["requirements"]="Start: Baldric \226\128\148 Metalworks (G-9)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Sunsand",["rewards"]="300g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Baldric wants you to bring him a pinch of Valkurm Sunsand for one of his experiments. It is said to only appear during dust storms.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Baldric on the lower level of the Metalworks in the Darksteel Forge.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a a pinch of Valkurm Sunsand to Baldric to complete the quest.\010\010Valkurm Sunsand can be found in Valkurm Dunes during a sandstorm by clicking on the ??? on the overturned ship at the Siren Sands at Valkurm Dunes (H-9), or can be purchased from Auction House Category: Others > Misc.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6855",["title"]="Starting a Flame",["page_title"]="Starting a Flame",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Starting_a_Flame",["revision"]="68265",["requirements"]="Start: Legata \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (K-6)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Flint Stone x 4",["rewards"]="100g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Fetch four stones of flint.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Legata wants 4 flint stones; trade these to her for a reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The 15-minute limitation of A Flash in the Pan does not apply. Consecutive trades can be made.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57171",["title"]="Stirrings of War",["page_title"]="Stirrings of War",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Stirrings_of_War",["revision"]="120882",["requirements"]="Previous: Path of Blood",["rewards"]="Key item: Allied Council Summons",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="After delivering Nashmeira's \034message\034 to President Naja, you learn of an allied forces military council to be convened in the near future...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Path of Blood; this mission begins during its ending cutscene in Aht Urhgan Whitegate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone once and wait until after the next Japanese midnight (15:00 UTC).\010\010 Before both requirements have been met, speaking with Naja Salaheem only provides additional dialogue and does not advance the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Shararat Teahouse at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-12) / Map 1.\010\010 The cutscene triggers automatically upon entering the teahouse.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-12 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The cutscene completes the mission, grants the Key item: Allied Council Summons, and begins Allied Rumblings.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_8477",["title"]="Stop Your Whining",["page_title"]="Stop Your Whining",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Stop_Your_Whining",["revision"]="19341",["requirements"]="Start: Washu, in Norg (J-8)\010Requirements: Tenshodo Reputation 4\010Level 10\010Items: Key item: Empty Barrel",["rewards"]="Scroll of Hojo: Ichi",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Travel to Norg and enter the Buccaneer's Quarters (J-8).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Washu standing on the right side of the wall in front of a door.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Washu will give you the Key item: Empty Barrel and tells you to fill it with Opo-Opo brew found in a Yhoator Jungle tree.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will need to examine the ??? that spawns at random points in Yhoator Jungle. Consult the map to the right for the possible spawn points. The spawn points are noted in Light Blue.\010Once you find the ??? the key item becomes Key item: Barrel of Opo-Opo Brew. An example of what this looks like can be seen in the picture to the right.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Washu and she will give you a scroll of Hojo: Ichi\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Washu (Norg)\010 / summary=Fill up an empty barrel with Opo-opo brew found fermenting in trees in the Yhoator Jungle, and bring it back to Norg ASAP.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_631",["title"]="Storms of Fate",["page_title"]="Storms of Fate",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Storms_of_Fate",["revision"]="111083",["requirements"]="Start: Esha'ntarl \226\128\148 Ru'Lude Gardens (H-6)\010Requirements: Completion of Chains of Promathia\010Items: Giant Scale\010Previous: Dawn",["rewards"]="Key item: Whisper of the Wyrmking",["repeatable"]="No (Can reenter to assist others)",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="[Wiki: needs verification] Please note that when you've begun Dawn for Chains of Promathia and Awakening for Rise of the Zilart, your in-game Mission tracker will stop updating your mission progress until The Last Verse is completed. It will show that you're still on Dawn and Awakening even if you've completed it, so while you're progressing through Storms of Fate, Shadows of the Departed and Apocalypse Nigh, you will need to keep track of your own mission progress.\010To track these missions they now are Quests. Track them by Jeuno Quest in your menu. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Ru'Lude Gardens, enter the Ducal Palace for a cutscene with Esha'ntarl.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Riverne - Site #B01. You will receive a cutscene upon checking the Dilapidated Gate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the green Unstable Displacement on the west side of Riverne - Site B01 (E-7). This acts as a battlefield entrance similar to the mini-battlefield in Ghelsba Outpost.\010\010The island this Unstable Displacement is on is only accessible through another, \034normal\034 Unstable Displacement; one Giant Scale will thus be required to reach it.",["zone"]="Riverne - Site B01",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the green Unstable Displacement once for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check it again and select the battle \034Storms of Fate\034 when ready.\010\010The BCNM menu will not pop-up until everyone in the alliance has viewed the cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Boss Battle for \034Storms of Fate\034\010\010You will enter the battlefield facing the Wyrmking Bahamut. Up to 18 people (one full Alliance) may enter the battlefield. This battle is uncapped. You are given 30 minutes to defeat him. HP/MP will be fully restored upon entry.\010\010Bahamut has about 26000 HP. He casts the following spells:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defensive: Protect V, Shell V, Stoneskin, Phalanx, Cure V\010\010 He is fully buffed at the beginning of the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Offensive: Fire V, Flare II, Firaga IV, Silencega, Dispelga, Graviga\010\010He uses the following special attacks:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Absolute Terror: AoE Terror, absorbed by Utsusemi",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trample: AoE damage (~200-500), Knockback and Bind, absorbed by Utsusemi",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Sweeping Flail: Large AoE (range 20) damage (~100-300) and Knockback, absorbed by Utsusemi\010\010 Used when someone behind him gets hate",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Touchdown: AoE wind damage (~300) and Knockback",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Tempest Wing: Cone Attack wind(?) damage (~400)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Megaflare: Wide Cone Attack fire damage (~800).\010\010 He uses this every 10% HP he loses. \010\010 He insults the players before he uses it: \034Children of Vana'diel, what do you think to accomplish by fighting for your lives?\034\010\010 Don't bother stunning this, he'll just use it again when Stun wears off. Save your Stuns for his spells, particurlarly Firaga IV and Dispelga.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Gigaflare: Wide Cone Attack fire damage (~1200)\010\010 Used instead of Megaflare at 10% HP.\010\010 Before this he says \034Contemplate on the good your death will bring as your mortal form is consumed by my brilliance!\034\010\010When Bahamut is defeated, you will receive the Key item: Whisper of the Wyrmking. Return to Ru'Lude Gardens and enter the palace again for a final cutscene, where you are told to assemble \034an army of adventurers\034 and challenge Bahamut again...\010\010(Note: The Key Item received from this quest is a required item for each Alliance member to have in order to enter the BCNM The Wyrmking Descends.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57510",["title"]="Such Sweet Sorrow",["page_title"]="Such Sweet Sorrow",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Such_Sweet_Sorrow",["revision"]="121770",["requirements"]="Start: Dabhuh \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-11) / Map 1\010Fame: None\010Items: 1 Merrow Scale",["rewards"]="Merrow No. 17's Locket",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Dabhuh wants you to bring him a Merrow scale.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Dabhuh on the ground floor near The Pit at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-11) / Map 1.\010\010 The opening sequence automatically moves you to Caedarva Mire for a brief cutscene and then returns you to Aht Urhgan Whitegate.\010\010 No travel through Caedarva Mire is required.\010\010 The quest is added to the current quest log after the concluding Whitegate cutscene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-11 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain 1 Merrow Scale.\010\010 Merrow Scales are dropped by several Merrow enemies in Arrapago Reef.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Dabhuh at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-11) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-11 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Dabhuh exactly 1 Merrow Scale to complete the quest.\010\010 The Merrow Scale is consumed.\010\010 Ensure that you have at least one free inventory slot before completing the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You receive a Merrow No. 17's Locket.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57147",["title"]="Sweets for the Soul",["page_title"]="Sweets for the Soul",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Sweets_for_the_Soul",["revision"]="120832",["requirements"]="Previous: Passing Glory",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Ambassador Karababa has arrived from the Federation of Windurst. The planned festivities turn into puppet rivalry, and the insulted ambassador bypasses the palace in favor of a visit to the Shararat Teahouse.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Passing Glory; this mission begins immediately afterward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Shararat Teahouse in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-12) / Map 1.\010\010 Speaking with Naja Salaheem is optional and does not advance the mission.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-12 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The resulting cutscene completes the mission, grants the title \034Karababa's Tour Guide,\034 and begins Teahouse Tumult.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_12351",["title"]="Tango with a Tracker",["page_title"]="Tango with a Tracker",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Tango_with_a_Tracker",["revision"]="114694",["requirements"]="Start: Despachiaire \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold (K-10) / Map 2\010Requirements: Dawn\010Items: Key item: Letter from Shikaree X\010Previous: Dawn",["rewards"]="10,000 Gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A letter from Shikaree X addressed to you has arrived in the safehold. It appears she wants to gauge your battle prowess in Boneyard Gully.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Despachiaire at (Tavnazian Safehold (K-10) / Map 2) of the top floor of Tavnazian Safehold, to get the Key item: Letter from Shikaree X\010\010The quest will not be flagged in your current quests. It will only appear in your completed quests if you are victorious.\010\010This quest can be initiated after the player has completed the battlefield in the mission Dawn.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="K-10 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Boneyard Gully and enter the Battlefield: \010\010Time limit 30 minutes for 6 characters without Level Restriction, so buffs are not removed and experience points will be lost upon knock out. [Wiki: needs verification] \010\010The Letter from Shikaree X is lost upon entry. In case of a defeat, Despachiaire will hand over a new one.\010\010The item can only be acquired once per week (Conquest Tally) and it does not matter if a character is still holding the item from the week before, it is still possible to receive another one during the week after the old one is used.\010\010Those who have previously cleared this battle can enter the battlefield to help without any key item, but will not receive any reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57457",["title"]="Targeting the Captain",["page_title"]="Targeting the Captain",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Targeting_the_Captain",["revision"]="122532",["requirements"]="Start: Halshaob \226\128\148 Nashmau (H-10) / Map 1\010Requirements: Completion of Royal Painter Escort\010Fame: None\010Items: Imperial Mythril Piece\010Previous: Royal Painter Escort",["rewards"]="Mog Wardrobe 3: 5 slots [Horizon change] \010Up to three Ancient Lockboxes",["repeatable"]="daily",["summary"]="The Imperial Army has decided that the only way to rid the Empire of the Ashu Talif is to dispose of its captain. The Maelstrom Company is to board the Ashu Talif with a small force and end the threat for good.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Royal Painter Escort.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade an Imperial Mythril Piece to Halshaob at Nashmau (H-10) / Map 1 to accept the quest.\010\010 Once per week after completing Royal Painter Escort. Entire chain resets on the weekly reset.",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the Cutter in Arrapago Reef.\010\010 A direct route is to use a Runic Portal Use Permit to reach the Dvucca Isle Staging Point at Caedarva Mire (I-9) / Map 2.\010\010 From the staging point, travel west and enter Arrapago Reef at Caedarva Mire (F-9, G-9) / Map 2.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In Arrapago Reef, proceed north to the Cutter at Arrapago Reef (H-8) / Map 5.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ensure every party member has Targeting the Captain active before attempting to enter.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Cutter and select \034Targeting the Captain\034 to enter The Ashu Talif.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Cutthroat Kabsalah within 30 minutes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Open the spawned Ancient Lockboxes, then examine the Life Raft to leave the battlefield and complete the quest.\010\010 The first successful completion grants Mog Wardrobe 3: 5 slots. [Horizon change]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7452",["title"]="Tea with a Tonberry?",["page_title"]="Tea with a Tonberry?",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Tea_with_a_Tonberry%3F",["revision"]="105141",["requirements"]="Start: Sobane \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (D-6)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Attohwa Ginseng\010Treasury Gold\010Previous: Signed in Blood",["rewards"]="Willpower Torque",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="According to Sobane's husband Ondieumais, the count who owns the Carpenters' Landing territory is being threatened. Find a way to communicate with the Tonberries of Carpenters' Landing and discover who is making these threats.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="If you just completed Signed in Blood, you must Zone out and back into Southern San d'Oria to flag this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Sobane. She and her husband need your help confirming a threat to a local aristocrat, but the only ones who may know about it are the tight lipped Tonberries in Carpenters' Landing.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Attohwa Chasm and defeat Gallinipper, Ogrefly, or Monarch Ogrefly until they drop Attohwa Ginseng.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to South Landing in Carpenters' Landing.\010\010 Either take the barge from the entrance in Northern San d'Oria, or take a chocobo to the entrance at (J-8) in Jugner Forest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk with the elvaan Anguenet standing next to the Tonberry at the docks for a cutscene. He knows a way to speak with them, but he won't do it for free.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Anguenet the Attohwa Ginseng and he will give you the Key item: Tonberry Blackboard which will allow you to communicate with the Tonberry Riche on the ferry.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Purchase a Key item: Barge Ticket or Key item: Barge Multi-ticket and board a barge headed for Central Landing via Emfea Way. See here for the barge Schedule.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Riche, the Tonberry on board. Ask him all the questions (5); at the end he'll take the key item. Be sure to do this before the ride is over, which is approximately 7 minutes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Fei'Yin and kill Shadow until they drop Treasury Gold.\010\010Shadow appear on Map #1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the Treasury Gold to Davoi and trade it to the ??? at (J-11), which spawns a Hematic Cyst NM.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill the Hematic Cyst and select the ??? again for a cutscene.\010\010A group of characters who are doing this quest can all get the cut-scene by killing just one Hematic Cyst, from one Treasury Gold.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Southern San d'Oria and talk to Sobane to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1442",["title"]="Teacher's Pet",["page_title"]="Teacher's Pet",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Teacher%27s_Pet",["revision"]="60756",["requirements"]="Start: Moreno-Toeno \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (L-6) / North\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Bird Feather\010Two-Leaf Mandragora Bud",["rewards"]="250 gil",["repeatable"]="yes",["summary"]="Moreno-Toeno would like you to collect one bird feather and one two-leaf mandragora bud to be used as teaching materials in the next magic experiment at the School of Magic.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Moreno-Toeno, a teacher in the Aurastery, will reward you if you bring him a Two-Leaf Mandragora Bud and a Bird Feather.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Two-Leaf Mandragora Bud and Bird Feather must be traded together in a single trade. Moreno-Toeno will not accept them separately.\010\010Note: If you are on Windurst Mission 8-1, you cannot talk to Moreno-Toeno to start the quest unless you already started this quest, due to the use of this NPC for the Windurst Mission 8-1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57149",["title"]="Teahouse Tumult",["page_title"]="Teahouse Tumult",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Teahouse_Tumult",["revision"]="120833",["requirements"]="Previous: Sweets for the Soul",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have been asked to guide Lady Karababa to the Olduum ruins found in the tunnels of the Aydeewa Subterrane. How will Naja react to your freelancing? And what are Aphmau and friends planning...?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Sweets for the Soul; this mission begins immediately afterward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Aydeewa Subterrane for a cutscene.\010\010 Any entrance will trigger the cutscene. The most direct route begins at Wajaom Woodlands (G-7) / Map 1.\010\010 Sneak and Invisible are recommended while traveling through the subterrane.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On Aydeewa Subterrane (D-8, E-9) / Map 2, use either connection leading to Map 5.",["zone"]="Aydeewa Subterrane",["grid"]="D-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the unlabeled target near the tree root at Aydeewa Subterrane (F-8, G-8) / Map 5.\010\010 The target has no visible name. Use target cycling near the tree root if it is difficult to select.",["zone"]="Aydeewa Subterrane",["grid"]="F-8 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The resulting cutscene completes the mission and begins Finders Keepers.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_52116",["title"]="Teak Me to the Stars",["page_title"]="Teak Me to the Stars",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Teak_Me_to_the_Stars",["revision"]="119754",["requirements"]="Start: Raibaht \226\128\148 Metalworks (G-8)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Garhada Teak Lumber\010Previous: None",["rewards"]="2,100 gil",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Cid is secretly developing a new airship, but is low on Garhada teak needed to build its sleek interior.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Raibaht in Cid's lab to begin quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Carpenters' Landing via Jugner Forest to obtain a Garhada Teak Lumber.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Can be obtained from monsters that appear on the Phanauet Channel barge or that spawn from Fishing on the barge or on the Carpenters' Landing pier.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(On Horizon the regular enemies do not spawn on any of the barge rides, so the only way to get the lumber is from fishing up monsters.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Raibaht and trade him the lumber to complete quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7987",["title"]="Teleportation to Tu'Lia Guide",["page_title"]="Teleportation to Tu'Lia Guide",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Teleportation_to_Tu%27Lia_Guide",["revision"]="100615",["requirements"]="Start: Aligi-Kufongi \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold,\010Requirements: Access to Tu'Lia\010Key item from your race's tower in The Garden of Ru'Hmet (you must either be on, or have completed, When Angels Fall)\010Current title set to \034Warrior of the Crystal\034\010Items: Clear Chip (1-3, depending on number of desired Hall of Transference teleporters)\010Previous: The Gate of the Gods\010When Angels Fall",["rewards"]="Teleportation device from Hall of Transference to Ru'Aun Gardens unlocked",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Step 1. Registering your Data",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Change your title to \034Warrior of the Crystal\034 for 300 gil by speaking to Aligi-Kufongi located on the main floor of Tavnazian Safehold (H-9).\010\010Acquisition of the key item from your race's tower in The Garden of Ru'Hmet grants you the title \034Warrior of the Crystal\034. This title is required for registering your data in Ru'Aun Gardens---which permits you to use the Large Apparatuses and green teleporters.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Walk onto one of the green teleport pads located at Ru'Aun Gardens (G-9) or Ru'Aun Gardens (I-9) with the title \034Warrior of the Crystal\034. The proper green pad has a floating graphic and is located upstairs, not to be confused with the lower-level green pad that you arrive on later.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you step onto one of the green teleporters, it will say, \034Wel...ome, Warrior of the Crystal.\034. Select \034Use this portal\034 to receive the text: \034Your d...ta wil... be ...gistered.\034 \034Regis... ...omplete.\034\010\010You only need to complete this registration process once; you won't need to step on both teleporters.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Step 2. Teleporting",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To teleport to Ru'Aun Gardens from the Hall of Transference, purchase a Clear Chip from one of the goblins located in the starter cities.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Place this chip into the right Large Apparatus located in one of the Halls of Transference. Then, step onto the pad in front of the Large Apparatus to teleport to Ru'Aun Gardens.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You only need to place the Clear Chip into each apparatus once in order to use it. However, when using the apparatus, there is a chance that the chip will break (especially if you use the same apparatus more than once per Earth day). If this happens, you must replace it in order to teleport.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_548",["title"]="Tending Ages Wounds (Promathia Mission 3-4)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 3-4",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_3-4",["revision"]="1051",["requirements"]="Previous: Road Forks",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="You have learned that the Multinational Expedition was originally organized by the Republic of Bastok. Perhaps Cid knows something more...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Zone into Lower Jeuno to get a cutscene. \010\010NOTE: Don't zone in from the Mog house, it will not play the needed cutscene. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Lower Jeuno and inspect the door of the Tenshodo Headquarters at the Neptune's Spire to get another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5949",["title"]="Tenshodo Membership",["page_title"]="Tenshodo Membership",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Tenshodo_Membership",["revision"]="118141",["requirements"]="Start: Ghebi Damomohe \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (I-7)\010Items: Tenshodo Invite (Optional)",["rewards"]="Key item: Tenshodo Member's Card\010Tenshodo Invite",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="To join the Tenshodo, you need either a membership form or an invitation from a current member.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Option 1 (Requires Jeuno Reputation 3)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Ghebi Damomohe at Lower Jeuno (I-7) behind the counter of the Neptune's Spire. Select the third, blank line of dialogue. Ghebi says that you need either a Tenshodo Invite or a Key item: Tenshodo Application Form.\010\010This step requires 3 Jeuno Fame. Trading 5 or fewer stacks of La Theine Cabbage in the quest Only the Best will suffice.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Port Bastok and into Warehouse #2 across from the Air Travel Agency.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once inside, talk to Jabbar or Silver Owl to receive a Key item: Tenshodo Application Form.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Ghebi Damomohe at Lower Jeuno (I-7) in the Neptune's Spire. She will take the Key item: Tenshodo Application Form and in return give you a Tenshodo Invite and Key item: Tenshodo Member's Card, completing the quest.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Option 2 (Does Not Require Jeuno Reputation)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Buy/trade for a Tenshodo Invite. Return to Ghebi Damomohe in Neptune's Spire. Giving Ghebi Damomohe the Tenshodo Invite grants you a second Tenshodo Invite and Key item: Tenshodo Member's Card, completing the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The fame requirement is only to start this quest by speaking to the NPC behind the counter. If you can't start the quest by talking to the NPC, just buy the invite from the AH and trade it to her. This completes the quest instantly, even if you do not meet the fame requirement to start the quest. You'll get another invite in exchange. (NOTE: This is confirmed to NO LONGER WORK after Rebase. You need fame.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_8398",["title"]="Test My Mettle",["page_title"]="Test My Mettle",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Test_My_Mettle",["revision"]="119942",["requirements"]="Start: Devean \226\128\148 Selbina (I-8)\010Requirements: Level 10 \010Maybe other unknown factors\010Fame: Selbina\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Power Sandals",["rewards"]="Gil (amount varies) or Power Sandals (if you fail or decide not to finish the quest.)",["repeatable"]="Yes, Once per earth day",["summary"]="Find the pair of power sandals hidden in a jar somewhere in Davoi. Bring them back before time runs out for a cash prize.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Devean, behind Shepherd's Muster in Selbina, asks if you want to find some loot he hid in Davoi. If you say yes he will ask you to bring him back a pair of Power Sandals hidden inside a Jar in Davoi, and will ask if you want to bet on how quick you will make it back to him.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You then need to bet either 100, 250, 500, or 1000 gil and if you will make it back in 24, 36, 48, 60, or 72 hours. \010\010If you choose 24 hours you will get 3 times your bet, if you choose 36 you will get 2.5 times your bet, if you choose 48 hours you will get 2 times your bet, if you choose 60 hours you will get 1.5 times your bet, and if you choose 72 hours you will get 1.2 times your bet. \010\010The time is in game hours. If you choose 24 hours, or one game day, you will actually have about one hour in real life.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Davoi and find and interact with the Jar to find the Power Sandals. When a player receives the power sandals, the active jar will change to a different location.\010\010Only one interactable jar is up at a time.\010\010The jar will not change locations if you interact with it without this quest active.\010\010Possible Jar Locations \010Davoi (F-6) North of MNK AF2 ???.\010Davoi (F-7) To the right of a hut and a tree.\010Davoi (F-9) A jar next to a tree stump, bottom of F-9 center.\010Davoi (G-9) Next to the Village Well.\010Davoi (H-8) Near the Oak Door at the top of the Orcish stronghold.\010Davoi (H-8) Coming from the west side not on top of Orcish stronghold.\010Davoi (H-9) Next to the Orc Campfire with a view of the Orcish Stronghold across the river.\010Davoi (I-8) Near the lake at nighttime 18:00-4:00.\010Davoi (J-8) A Jar on top of Platform where Crimson Orb is obtained.\010Davoi (J-9) A Jar south of the platform where Crimson Orb is obtained.\010Davoi (J-9) Very southeastern corner, near huts.\010Davoi (K-9) A jar next to a tree stump.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You must make it back to Devean before your time expires or your will lose the bet.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you chose not to return to him, you may keep the sandals.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This quest may be repeatable, but if you fail at the quest (you didn't find the Jar) and return to him, you will lose your bet and can not immediately start the quest over.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Selbina",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57164",["title"]="Testing the Waters",["page_title"]="Testing the Waters",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Testing_the_Waters",["revision"]="120871",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1\010Previous: Sentinels' Honor",["rewards"]="Key item: Percipient Eye",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A bounty has been placed on the head of Duzaf the Blackbelly...or is it really Luzaf the Blackheart? Seek out the Black Coffin once more and confirm President Naja's suspicions.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Sentinels' Honor; this mission begins during its ending cutscene with Naja Salaheem.\010\010 Speaking with Naja again provides additional mission dialogue but is not required for progression.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ensure you possess the Key item: Ephramadian Gold Coin.\010\010 If you no longer possess one, examine Jazaraat's Headstone at Caedarva Mire (E-10) / Map 1 to obtain another.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the Cutter in Arrapago Reef.\010\010 A direct route is to use a Runic Portal Use Permit to reach the Dvucca Isle Staging Point at Caedarva Mire (I-9) / Map 2.\010\010 From the staging point, travel west to the Arrapago Reef entrance at Caedarva Mire (F-9, G-9) / Map 2.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Approach the Cutter at Arrapago Reef (H-8) / Map 5 for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When asked whether you wish passage to the Black Coffin, select \034I do.\034\010\010 Selecting \034Not at this time\034 does not advance the mission. Zone before approaching the Cutter again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue through the resulting cutscenes and transfer to Talacca Cove.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Talacca Cove cutscene consumes the Key item: Ephramadian Gold Coin, completes the mission, grants the Key item: Percipient Eye, awards the title \034Treasure Trove Tender,\034 and begins Legacy of the Lost.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2025",["title"]="The All-New C-2000",["page_title"]="The All-New C-2000",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_All-New_C-2000",["revision"]="56788",["requirements"]="Start: Kopuro-Popuro \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (H-10)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Rabbit Hide\010Two-Leaf Mandragora Bud\010Insect Wing",["rewards"]="200 gil",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="You have been talked into aiding the training of a new type of Cardian. Bring a Rabbit Hide, a Two-Leaf Mandragora Bud, and an Insect Wing, so the Cardian can learn the odors of monsters he may encounter.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Kopuro-Popuro needs you to bring him some things to help him create a new Cardian.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He needs a Rabbit Hide, a Two-Leaf Mandragora Bud and an Insect Wing.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="These all drop just outside of town.\010\010Note: If you have Lower Jeuno quest The Kind Cardian activated and have not turned in the Ten of Cups (Card) to Apururu, you will not be able to activate this quest. After trading Ten of Cups (Card) to Apururu, you will then be able to begin this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2118",["title"]="The All-New C-3000",["page_title"]="The All-New C-3000",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_All-New_C-3000",["revision"]="56780",["requirements"]="Start: Kopuro-Popuro \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (H-10)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Beetle Shell\010Hecteyes Eye\010Previous: Legendary Plan B",["rewards"]="600 gil",["repeatable"]="yes",["summary"]="Kopuro-Popuro has created a new type of Cardian that has been instructed to return from patrols with the spoils of battle. To teach the Cardian what it should bring back, you have been asked to find a Beetle Shell and a Hecteyes Eye.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Note: You must zone after completing the previous quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kopuro-Popuro asks for a Beetle Shell and a Hecteyes Eye. \010\010You can either buy the items in the Auction House or get them yourself.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Hand Kopuro-Popuro one of each to receive 600 gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2027",["title"]="The Amazin' Scorpio",["page_title"]="The Amazin' Scorpio",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Amazin%27_Scorpio",["revision"]="56786",["requirements"]="Start: Soni-Muni \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (H-10)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Scorpion Stinger",["rewards"]="1500 gil",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Soni-Muni wants something that will rekindle the passion for adventure in his mate Gottah. Something to do with the legend of the great grappler Scorpio might do the trick.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Soni-Muni, at the fountain in the Bomingo Round, Windurst Woods (G-10, G-11, H-10, H-11), will give you 1500 gil for a Scorpion Stinger.\010\010Scorpion Stingers drop from Labyrinth Scorpions and Maze Scorpions in Maze of Shakhrami",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6116",["title"]="The Antique Collector",["page_title"]="The Antique Collector",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Antique_Collector",["revision"]="108415",["requirements"]="Start: Imasuke - Port Jeuno (E-6)\010Requirements: Jeuno Reputation 3\010Items: Kaiser Sword",["rewards"]="Key item: Map of Delkfutt's Tower",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Imasuke (standing at the entrance to Qufim).\010\010If you are on the quest Hook, Line, and Sinker, you may have to talk to Imasuke several times until he mentions Delkfutt's Tower.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Imasuke a Kaiser Sword to complete the quest.\010\010Kaiser Swords are dropped by Dancing Weapons on Qufim Island or can be purchased from the Auction House.\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Imasuke (Gate to Qufim, Port Jeuno)\010 / summary=Present Imasuke with a kaiser sword to receive a map of Delkfutt's Tower.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57508",["title"]="The Art of War",["page_title"]="The Art of War",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Art_of_War",["revision"]="121771",["requirements"]="Start: Hishahma \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-8) / Map 1\010Requirements: Superior Private or higher, and successful completion of all three Finding Faults investigations\010Fame: None\010Items: Lamian Fang Key (standard overland route to Ornery Orobon only)\010Previous: Finding Faults",["rewards"]="??? Box",["repeatable"]="yes",["summary"]="Hishahma's special forces are struggling in their battle against certain monsters. You must find an effective strategy to defeat the enemy.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="The weekly strategy rotation, quest availability timing, Notorious Monster mechanics, and repeat restriction below require confirmation on HorizonXI. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Unlocking the Quest",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Successfully complete all three versions of Finding Faults:\010\010 Lamia Deathdancer\010\010 Troll Speculator\010\010 Mamool Ja Mimicker",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Identify at least one correct weakness during each investigation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Attain the mercenary rank of Superior Private or higher.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Change areas and speak with Hishahma at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-8) / Map 1 after the next Japanese Midnight.\010\010 Hishahma may continue to offer repeat attempts of Finding Faults. Select The Art of War when it appears.\010\010 Original-era documentation disagrees on whether the initial offer appears after Japanese Midnight or the following Conquest Tally. If the quest is not available after Japanese Midnight, return after the next Conquest Tally. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="General Procedure",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Choose one of the three investigations offered by Hishahma:\010\010! Investigation\010! Notorious Monster\010! Spawn Point\010! Strategy to Identify\010|-\010| Orobon\010| Ornery Orobon\010| Arrapago Reef (E-11) / Map 2 \226\128\148 Near Lovers' Rocks.\010| How to calm its rage\010|-\010| Wamouracampa\010| Wheel Wamoura\010| Halvung (L-8) / Map 1 \226\128\148 Beside a magma pool between two passages.\010| How to lower its defenses\010|-\010| Puk\010| Carpophagous Puk\010| Mamook (G-8) / Map 1 \226\128\148 Upper level near the waterfall.\010| How to prevent its escape",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the chosen location and examine the ??? to spawn the corresponding Notorious Monster.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Test the three possible strategies for that monster.\010\010 The active strategy changes periodically and is reported to reset at the weekly Conquest Tally.\010\010 Only one strategy is correct during a given rotation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat the Notorious Monster.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Hishahma and report the strategy that worked.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Change areas and wait until after the next Japanese Midnight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Hishahma again:\010\010 A correct report rewards a ??? Box and completes the quest.\010\010 An incorrect report provides no reward.\010\010 Repeat completion is reported to be limited by the weekly Conquest cycle. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3708",["title"]="The Bare Bones",["page_title"]="The Bare Bones",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Bare_Bones",["revision"]="104206",["requirements"]="Start: Degenhard \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (I-10)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Bone Chip x 1",["rewards"]="Map of the Dangruf Wadi",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Bring Degenhard the item that he uses to keep himself youthful.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="(Optional) Talk to Degenhard; he talks about a vitality formula but won't tell you any more until you bring him his secret ingredient. Unfortunately, he doesn't tell you what the ingredient is.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Talk to Biggorf nearby; he says that he's seen people giving Degenhard Bone Chips. This only happens if you talk to Biggorf after talking to Degenhard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Bone Chip and trade it to Degenhard to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This quest will never appear in Bastok: Current Quests, even after you talk to Degenhard and/or Biggorf, and hence will remain unflagged at an Adventurer's Assistant until completed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4842",["title"]="The Basics",["page_title"]="The Basics",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Basics",["revision"]="113525",["requirements"]="Start: Rycharde \226\128\148 Mhaura (I-8)\010Requirements: Windurst Reputation ?\010Items: Popoto\010Previous: The Clue",["rewards"]="Tea Set and 2000 experience points.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Rycharde wants you to deliver a dish to Valgeir in Selbina, and report on how he liked it.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must wait 8 game days after finishing The Clue before Rycharde will give you this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Rycharde now wants you to deliver his cuisine to his father Valgeir to once again try to show his cooking skills to him. Rycharde will have your ferry fee paid for, so head off to Selbina.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It doesn't matter if you take the ferry or not. The quest will still progress regardless how you get there.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the Key item: Mhauran Couscous (key item) to Valgeir.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Valgeir then hands you a Popoto item to give back to his son.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the Popoto back to Rycharde to complete the quest.\010\010The following steps are optional and not necessary to have the quest show up in the Completed Quests log.\010\010You can go back to Selbina again and talk to Valgeir to find out why he gave the Popoto to his son.\010\010If you return to Rycharde you will find out if he has learned anything.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57407",["title"]="The Beast Within",["page_title"]="The Beast Within",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Beast_Within",["revision"]="121455",["requirements"]="Start: Waoud \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-10) / Map 1 \226\128\148 On the upper level of Heretic's Alley.\010Requirements: Blue Mage level 66+ as the player's main job\010Complete Transformations\010Level: 66\010Fame: None\010Items: Blue Mage's Testimony\010Previous: Transformations",["rewards"]="Raises the level cap from 70 to 75\010Scroll of Instant Warp [Wiki: needs verification]",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="No questions. No refusals. Obtain a Blue Mage's Testimony and present yourself at the Imperial Whitegate.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Starting the Quest",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete Transformations.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Set Blue Mage as your main job at level 66 or higher.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Waoud at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="J-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Accept the challenge to begin the quest.\010\010 Current LandSandBoat does not enforce an additional wait after completing Transformations.\010\010 Waoud may offer an optional 1,000-gil divination after the quest has begun. This does not advance the quest and is not required.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtaining a Blue Mage's Testimony\010\010Obtain a Blue Mage's Testimony from a Mamool Ja Mimicker.\010\010! Monster\010! Level\010! Zone\010! Spawns\010|-\010| Mamool Ja Mimicker\010| 72\226\128\14773\010| Wajaom Woodlands\010| 4\010|-\010| Mamool Ja Mimicker\010| 73\226\128\14775\010| Mamook\010| 13\010\010A usable testimony is required to enter the battlefield. If the game reports that the testimony is worn or otherwise unusable, discard it and obtain another.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Traveling to the Jade Sepulcher",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Aht Urhgan Whitegate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ensure that at least one inventory slot is free for the Scroll of Instant Warp reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Blue Mage's Testimony to the Imperial Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="L-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Confirm that you are prepared to continue.\010\010 The testimony is not consumed by this Whitegate interaction.\010\010 You will be transported directly to the Jade Sepulcher.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="View the cutscene that occurs upon your first arrival.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the same Blue Mage's Testimony to the Ebony Door near the entrance.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select The Beast Within to enter the battlefield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Battlefield",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Raubahn within ten minutes.\010\010 The battle is solo.\010\010 Your support job is disabled.\010\010 You do not lose experience points if defeated.\010\010 Raubahn does not need to be killed. Reduce him below 20% HP while remaining alive to win.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After victory, complete the resulting cutscene to receive:\010\010 A level-cap increase from 70 to 75, if your current level cap is 70.\010\010 Scroll of Instant Warp [Wiki: needs verification] \010\010 The title Master of Ambition",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The quest completes automatically; returning to Waoud is not required.\010\010If the battlefield attempt fails, return to the Imperial Whitegate with a usable Blue Mage's Testimony and trade it again to return to the Jade Sepulcher.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57128",["title"]="The Black Coffin",["page_title"]="The Black Coffin",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Black_Coffin",["revision"]="122879",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1\010Previous: The Dolphin Crest",["rewards"]="Mog Wardrobe 3: 5 slots [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A mercenary colleague has reported feeling an ominous presence to the west of Dvucca Isle...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After completing The Dolphin Crest, speak with Naja Salaheem in Salaheem's Sentinels at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1 for the mission's opening cutscene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ensure every participant has the Key item: Ephramadian Gold Coin (found in temporary key items).\010\010 NOTE: Anyone who fails the fight needs another Ephramadian Gold Coin.\010\010 Anyone who needs another coin can examine Jazaraat's Headstone at Caedarva Mire (E-10) / Map 1.\010\010(you will obtain a new Coin, Jazaraat will NOT spawn again.)\010\010 The party registrant must currently be on this mission. Players who have progressed beyond it may assist if they also possess the coin.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the Runic Portal to reach the Dvucca Isle Staging Point at Caedarva Mire (I-9) / Map 2.\010\010 If you do not have the Dvucca Isle Staging Point, you can take the West exit from Nashmau into Caedarva Mire. From there, go to Entrance 3 (Caedarva Mire (D-11) / Map 1 to Alzadaal Undersea Ruins. \010\010 NOTE: You will need an Imperial Silver Piece to enter. \010\010 In Alzadall Undersea Ruins, you will be on Map 12. Follow the path to the portal, take it, then take the exit back into Caedarva Mire. This will continue at Step 4 below.",["zone"]="Caedarva Mire",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel west to the Arrapago Reef entrance at Caedarva Mire (F-9, G-9) / Map 2.",["zone"]="Caedarva Mire",["grid"]="F-9 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In Arrapago Reef, proceed north to the Cutter at Arrapago Reef (H-8) / Map 5.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Approach the Cutter for a cutscene and select \034I'm Not afraid\034, This does not start the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Cutter now and select \034The Black Coffin\034 to enter The Ashu Talif.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete the battlefield within 30 minutes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After victory, continue through the automatic cutscenes in Arrapago Reef and Nashmau. The Nashmau cutscene completes the mission and begins Ghosts of the Past.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6866",["title"]="The Brugaire Consortium",["page_title"]="The Brugaire Consortium",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Brugaire_Consortium",["revision"]="99269",["requirements"]="Start: Fontoumant \226\128\148 Port San d'Oria (H-9)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1",["rewards"]="Lauan Shield",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Deliver parcels to their proper recipients.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Fontoumant needs you to deliver some packages for him. The packages are given one at a time and take a slot of inventory. All deliveries are in Port San d'Oria.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade each parcel to the following NPCs:\010\010The Magic Shop Parcel is for Regine Port San d'Oria (J-8) in Regine's Magicmart\010\010The Auction Parcel is for Apstaule Port San d'Oria (H-10) at the top of the Auction House\010\010The Pub Parcel is for Thierride Port San d'Oria (G-7) at the Rusty Anchor Pub",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Fontoumant after you deliver each package to receive the next one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you deliver the last package, talk to Fontoumant for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_53511",["title"]="The Call of the Sea",["page_title"]="The Call of the Sea",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Call_of_the_Sea",["revision"]="107560",["requirements"]="Start: Anteurephiaux \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold (J-8) / Map 2",["rewards"]="Memento Muffler",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You've been asked to travel to the Tavnazian coastline and find a rare shell carried by a monster -- preferably a \034spirally\034 one that makes sound when you blow into it.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Leporaitceau. (3rd floor, Tavnazian Safehold at J-8)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Equette. (2nd floor, Tavnazian Safehold at I-9)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Anteurephiaux to obtain the quest. (3rd floor, Tavnazian Safehold at J-8)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to K-12 in Misareaux Coast and touch the ??? to spawn the NM crab Bloody Coffin.\010\010Bloody Coffin has very high defense to both physical and magic combat damage, except when it's casting a spell; timing is important to do major damage to it. It can be debuffed (Silence, Gravity, etc.) as necessary.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After killing the Bloody Coffin, touch the ??? again to obtain the Key item: Whispering Conch. If you zone before touching ??? you have to do the fight again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Tavnazian Safehold and talk to Anteurephiaux.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Equette to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_337",["title"]="The Chains That Bind Us (Bastok Mission 8-1)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 8-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_8-1",["revision"]="115856",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 7-2|On My Way",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The president has ordered a full-scale investigation of Zepwell Island. You are to travel to the Quicksand Caves located in the central Altepa Desert. Report to Iron Eater for a briefing.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with a Gate Guard to accept the mission.\010\010Trade 20~30 crystals. (Traded 25 water crystals)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Visit Iron Eater at the President's Office in Metalworks.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Quicksand Caves, Part 1 (Fight)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head for (Western Altepa Desert (G-5)) in Western Altepa Desert (take the tunnel), and enter Quicksand Caves.",["zone"]="Western Altepa Desert",["grid"]="G-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to (Quicksand Caves (H-8) / Map 5) and open the weighted door.\010\010The door will open by applying enough weight on the nearby sensor. It needs a total of 3 \034points\034: \010\010Galka are worth a full 3 points\010\010Humes, Mithra, and Elvaan are worth 2 points\010\010Tarutaru are worth 1 point",["zone"]="Quicksand Caves",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At (Quicksand_Caves (G-11) / Map 5), you'll find yourself in a small room. Clear it out, and then check the Galka Statue to spawn 3 Antica NMs. They can be slept. \010\010Triarius IV-XIV (Black Mage) \010\010Princeps IV-XLV (Paladin) \010\010Centurio IV-VII (Warrior)",["zone"]="Quicksand_Caves",["grid"]="G-11 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It is recommended you defeat them in that order, however a well-balanced party should have little difficulty with them.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Galka Statue again for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Quicksand Caves, Part 2",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to (Western Altepa Desert (D-12)) of Western Altepa Desert and enter Quicksand Caves Map 5.\010\010 This entrance is accessed at (Western Altepa Desert (C-11))\226\134\146(Western Altepa Desert (D-11)) in the far southwest corner.",["zone"]="Western Altepa Desert",["grid"]="D-12",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Inside, head through the eastern weighted door at (Quicksand_Caves (K-8) / Map 4) this will take you to Map 6.",["zone"]="Quicksand_Caves",["grid"]="K-8 / Map 4",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go east to another weight device at (Quicksand_Caves (G-8) / Map 7) and proceed east again.\010\010The ??? you need is on the floor in front of the mural in the room at (Quicksand_Caves (H-8) / Map 7).",["zone"]="Quicksand_Caves",["grid"]="G-8 / Map 7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the ??? for a cutscene with Zeid.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Iron Eater for a final cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3682",["title"]="The Chamber of Oracles (Zilart Mission 7)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 7",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_7",["revision"]="33777",["requirements"]="Level: 60+\010Items: Key item: Fire Fragment\010Key item: Earth Fragment\010Key item: Water Fragment\010Key item: Wind Fragment\010Key item: Ice Fragment\010Key item: Lightning Fragment\010Key item: Light Fragment\010Previous: Through the Quicksand Caves",["rewards"]="Key item: Prismatic Fragment",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="The Chamber of Oracles is said to be located in the deepest area of the Quicksand Caves.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After winning the battle for Through the Quicksand Caves, you are put in a room with a large device.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Touch all 8 parts of this device to insert your shards from Headstone Pilgrimage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Touch the final pedestal again for your Cutscene",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="rise of the zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_10296",["title"]="The Circle of Time",["page_title"]="The Circle of Time",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Circle_of_Time",["revision"]="119311",["requirements"]="Start: Mertaire \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (I-8)\010Requirements: Bard 50+\010Items: Key item: Star Ring\010Key item: Moon Ring\010Previous: The Requiem",["rewards"]="Choral Justaucorps",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="Solve the riddle of the ring, and find the truth behind it.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="If you've just completed The Requiem on another job, you can save a bit of time and immediately flag the quest with Mertaire on that job. However, you do need to switch back to BRD before talking to Imasuke.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mertaire tells you to take the Star ring obtained from The Requiem to an antique collector, namely Imasuke near the entrance to Qufim Island.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Imasuke says he can't read it and that you should bury it in Perennial Snow. The snow in question is located at (Xarcabard (I-10)) in Xarcabard. Bury it there.\010\010Wait until JP midnight and check the Perennial Snow to purify the ring.",["zone"]="Xarcabard",["grid"]="I-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After digging the ring up, return to Imasuke, who tells you the language is old San d'Orian and that you should find someone that can read it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Chalvatot at Chateau d'Oraguille (F-7) who gives you the Key item: Moon Ring.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Chalvatot sends you to the Monastic Cavern. Head to Monastic Cavern (I-8) in the caverns. Clear the room and examine the altar to pop the NM Bugaboo. \010\010The Orcish Warlord spawns in the same room and has True Sight.\010\010Soloable by a 75 RDM/NIN.\010\010You can simply pull the Orcish Warlord to the nearby zone so all other mobs despawn, then kill the Orc. Go back into the altar room and spawn and kill the Bugaboo.",["zone"]="Monastic Cavern",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you defeat Bugaboo, check the altar again for a short cutscene about the Key item: Star Ring and Key item: Moon Ring. Go back to talk to Chalvatot at Chateau d'Oraguille (F-7) to complete the quest.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Bard (BRD)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Bard (BRD)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Choral Justaucorps",["revision"]="21437"},{["job"]="Bard (BRD)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="The Circle of Time",["revision"]="119311"}}},{["id"]="wiki_5962",["title"]="The Clockmaster",["page_title"]="The Clockmaster",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Clockmaster",["revision"]="10190",["requirements"]="Start: Galmut - Upper Jeuno (G-7)\010Requirements: Jeuno Reputation 5\010Previous: Save the Clock Tower",["rewards"]="Time Hammer\0101200g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After completing the quest Save the Clock Tower, head up and select the door to Galmut's house again, for the ending cutscene and to complete this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) After completing this quest, talk to Collet again for a short cutscene with Galmut.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Galmut (House, Upper Jeuno)\010 / summary=Help the dejected Galmut by saving his clock tower.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4843",["title"]="The Clue",["page_title"]="The Clue",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Clue",["revision"]="118254",["requirements"]="Start: Rycharde \226\128\148 Mhaura (I-8)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 5\010Previous: Expertise",["rewards"]="3000g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Rycharde seeks an ingredient known as crawlers eggs.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must wait 8 game days after finishing Expertise before Rycharde will give you this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After giving him some time to recover from his father Valgeir's harsh words about his cooking, Rycharde is now ready to prove his worth to his father.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He asks you to bring 4 Crawler Eggs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He also says you can take your time on this quest, so there is no time limit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7505",["title"]="The Cold Light of Day",["page_title"]="The Cold Light of Day",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Cold_Light_of_Day",["revision"]="104230",["requirements"]="Start: Malene \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (I-5)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Steam Clock\010Quus",["rewards"]="500g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="A monster that appears near the lighthouse in South Gustaberg has stolen a package addressed to Malene. Ask the adventurer Dalzakk how to lure the beast out, and recover the item.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Malene; a monster stole a parcel she was expecting and she asks you to find it for her. The problem is that monster who stole it is hiding near the lighthouse and won't come out. She mentions another adventurer named Dalzakk who might know how to lure the monster out. Dalzakk lives in a house on Kulatz Bridge.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Go to Dalzakk's house, he isn't home so talk to Gwill. Gwill gives you the hint about the monster, put a Quus behind the lighthouse.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Quus.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Find the ??? behind the lighthouse at South Gustaberg (M-10) and trade the Quus to it. You may have to wait a bit for the monster (Bubbly Bernie) to appear.",["zone"]="South Gustaberg",["grid"]="M-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Bubbly Bernie to obtain a Steam Clock.\010\010The monster is soloable by any job over level ~10.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the clock to Malene to complete the quest.\010Note: If you have a Steam Clock in your inventory Bubbly Bernie will not drop another. You must trade the one you have to Malene before attempting for another.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7436",["title"]="The Competition",["page_title"]="The Competition",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Competition",["revision"]="60837",["requirements"]="Start: Joulet \226\128\148 Port San d'Oria (H-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Moat Carp and/or Forest Carp x10,000",["rewards"]="Lu Shang's Fishing Rod\010Key item: Testimonial\01010g per Moat Carp\01015g per Forest Carp\010(Average 100,000 - 150,000 total gil)",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Catch moat carp by any means possible so Joulet can win a fishing contest against his elder brother, Gallijaux.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Joulet to begin The Competition.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade 10,000 Moat Carps and/or Forest Carps to him.\010\010You can talk to either brother to see which one you've agreed to help.\010\010You can trade multiple stacks at a time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You receive 10 gil for each Moat Carp and 15 gil for every Forest Carp.\010\010To learn your current total of fish, speak with Ufanne, who stands watch behind the two bickering fishermen. You may need to talk to the latter multiple times before she'll tell you.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will get Lu Shang's Fishing Rod and the Key item: Testimonial upon trading the 10,000th carp.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1126",["title"]="The Crimson Trial",["page_title"]="The Crimson Trial",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Crimson_Trial",["revision"]="62031",["requirements"]="Start: Sharzalion - Southern San d'Oria (K-6)\010Requirements: Red Mage Level 40+\010Items: Davoi Storage Key\010Key item: Orcish Dry Food",["rewards"]="Fencing Degen [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="Retrieve some Orcish dried food from a storage hole in Davoi. Sharzalion will let you in on something in return.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Sharzalion at the bar in the Lion Springs Tavern. He wants some Key item: Orcish Dry Food.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To get this food, you need to get a Davoi Storage Key to open the Storage Hole which spawns randomly about Davoi.\010\010You need to start this quest while being a Red Mage. It is not necessary to be on Red Mage for the NM to spawn. You only need to have the quest flagged.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Davoi from Jugner Forest and defeat Purpleflash Brukdok around the western half of (Davoi (E-9))/(Davoi (F-9)) to obtain a Davoi Storage Key.\010\010Purpleflash Brukdok spawns around the western half of (Davoi (E-9)) / (Davoi (F-9)) when you enter the zone with the RDM AF weapon started. Get down to the river at (Davoi (I-8)) or (Davoi (J-10)) and follow it west to (Davoi (D-8)).\010\010There are a few orcs on the way that aggro even at 75.\010\010Additionally, all nearby orcs link when fighting the NM.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Storage Hole spawns randomly around Davoi, so hunt around until you find it. There are patterns on the ground which identify potential spawn positions. The patterns look like someone stretched animal skins over a hole in the ground, except that they are the same colors as the ground (see image). Trade the Davoi Storage Key to it to receive the Key item: Orcish Dry Food. The location changes each game day. May respawn in the same spot after the Davoi Storage Key is used.\010\010Some known locations of the Storage Hole are at (Davoi (E-10)), (Davoi (F-6)), (Davoi (F-7)), (Davoi (F-9)), (Davoi (G-9)), (Davoi (G-10)),(Davoi (I-7)), (Davoi (I-8)), (Davoi (J-7)), (Davoi (K-7)), (Davoi (K-8)), (Davoi (K-9)),(Davoi (K-10)), and another at (Davoi (J-8)). There are other locations it can spawn in, anywhere on the map.\010\010The Storage Hole at (Davoi (H-8)) can be reached from the river below. Running through Monastic Cavern is not necessary.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have obtained the Key item: Orcish Dry Food, return to Sharzalion to receive your Fencing Degen [Horizon change] .",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Red Mage (RDM)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Red Mage (RDM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Fencing Degen",["revision"]="118221"},{["job"]="Red Mage (RDM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="The Crimson Trial",["revision"]="62031"}}},{["id"]="wiki_324",["title"]="The Crystal Line (Bastok Mission 2-1)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 2-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_2-1",["revision"]="100418",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 1-3|Fetichism",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Find a section of the strange structure on the Konschtat Highlands that drains the energy from crystals. Bring a faded crystal back to Chief Engineer Cid for analysis.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 3 Crystals to a gate guard until your Rank Points are full to unlock this mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select the mission from one of the Bastok Gate Guards.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Cid in the Metalworks (H-8) for more information. (This can be done before or after obtaining a Faded Crystal)\010\010He will give you a free crystal.",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Cid a Faded Crystal to receive the C. L. Report.\010\010 Faded Crystal can be obtained by trading a synthesis crystal to any crag's Telepoint, such as the Crag of Dem in Konschtat Highlands at (Konschtat Highlands (I-6)).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Talk to Naji.\010\010Naji guards the President's Office (Metalworks (J-8)).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Ayame in the Cannonry at (Metalworks (K-7)) to finish the mission.\010\010 You may have to speak to her several times to receive the correct dialogue.",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="K-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_368",["title"]="The Crystal Spring (San d'Oria Mission 3-2)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 3-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_3-2",["revision"]="29094",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Items: Crystal Bass\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 3-1|Infiltrate Davoi",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Catch a Crystal Bass from Crystwater Spring, located on the eastern edge of Jugner Forest.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade crystals to a T.K. (Temple Knight) at the gate to unlock this mission, more if you want to skip it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to any gate guard and accept the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Buy a Crystal Bass from the Auction House or you can catch one in Jugner Forest.\010\010See below for fishing tips.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Crystal Bass to the Gate Guard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Chateau d'Oraguille for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Chalvatot at F-7 inside Chateau d'Oraguille for a cutscene. Afterwards the mission is completed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Repeating this missions is similar to Mission 1-2. You do not need to zone between repeating, you also do not have to repeat the steps in Chateau d'Oraguille.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7524",["title"]="The Curse Collector",["page_title"]="The Curse Collector",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Curse_Collector",["revision"]="104287",["requirements"]="Start: Zon-Fobun \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (G-5)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Key item: Cursepaper",["rewards"]="Poison Cesti",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Let the magical statues in Beadeaux -- the Afflictors and the Mutes -- cast their curses on you to capture their spells on Zon-Fobun's cursepaper.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Zon-Fobun and receive a Cursepaper (key item).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Beadeaux and proceed to one of the sets of machines: you need to visit an Afflictor (which Curses whoever comes near it, unless they are currently Silenced) and Mute (which Silences whoever touches it). So it is important to get cursed first, by coming near the Afflictor, and then touch the Mute to become silenced. \010\010The first, and easiest, set of machines: Go straight in when entering Beadeaux, then turn left (go north) when you reach the wall at F-7. Go north to the wall in F-6, then due east to H-6. From here head south and you'll find yourself going into a cave that leads down. Take that down until it exits at H-7 on the lower map. Go west, south, and west again until you near the glowing red Afflictor in G-8. This will curse you, dramatically lowering your maximum HP and MP, as well as your running speed.\010\010Now head back east and then take your first turn north all the way to G-7 where you will find the Mute. Touch it and you will become silenced, so that you now have both the curses on the Cursepaper. \010\010Return to Zon-Fobun and talk to him; he will gladly take the Cursepaper and provide your reward of a Poison Cesti.\010\010Note It is recommended that you complete the quest Beadeaux Smog at the same time.\010Note 2 There is no in-game confirmation upon touching either machine; this is intentional and you will still be rewarded upon returning with both curses.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7528",["title"]="The Darksmith",["page_title"]="The Darksmith",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Darksmith",["revision"]="118994",["requirements"]="Start: Mighty Fist \226\128\148 Metalworks (G-9)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Darksteel Ore x2",["rewards"]="8,000g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Mighty Fist's forge is running low on darksteel ore, and he has asked you bring him two chunks of it. The Gusgen Mines is known to yield darksteel, but some claim to have dug a few chunks from the Zeruhn Mines.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Mighty Fist.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade two Darksteel Ore to Mighty Fist to complete the quest.\010Reward is 8,000 gil",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_365",["title"]="The Davoi Report (San d'Oria Mission 2-2)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 2-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_2-2",["revision"]="119874",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 2-1|The Rescue Drill",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Retrieve the latest scouting report from the Temple Knight scout somewhere in Davoi.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="This Mission is not required. You can skip this mission by trading 3~6 crystals to a Conquest Overseer or by repeating other missions. If you wish to skip this mission, trade crystals to a Conquest Overseer.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to any San d'Oria Gate Guard and accept the mission.\010\010A map of Davoi can be purchased for 3000 Gil from Violitte \226\128\147 Southern San d'Oria (G-10) or Elesca \226\128\147 Northern San d'Oria (I-8), but it is not required.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to Davoi. Zone into Jugner Forest from La Theine Plateau at (La Theine Plateau (M-8)). Then follow the right wall of Jugner Forest to the zone into Davoi at (Jugner Forest (G-12)).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to the NPC Zantaviat just inside the zone. Walk south until you reach a pond at (Davoi (J-8)). On the South bank of the pond you will find a ! targetable location. Click on it to receive the Lost Document.",["zone"]="Davoi",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Zantaviat to recieve the Temple Knights' Davoi Report.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to a Gate Guard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to the Papal Chamber, which is on the top floor of the Cathedral in Northern San d'Oria.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene, the mission will be completed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57448",["title"]="The Die Is Cast",["page_title"]="The Die Is Cast",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Die_Is_Cast",["revision"]="121564",["requirements"]="Start: Ratihb \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-12) / Map 1\010Requirements: Access to Aht Urhgan Whitegate\010Fame: None\010Items: Lamian Fang Key (standard route)",["rewards"]="Random Ring",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Yadhiwa cheated Balajaha out of a large sum of money. Help him get back the gold he lost to her crafty devices.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Ratihb at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-12) / Map 1 to begin the quest.\010\010 Ratihb also starts Luck of the Draw. The correct cutscene for this quest concerns Balajaha, Yadhiwa, and a game of dice; other Ratihb cutscenes belong to different quests.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="J-12 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Ekhu Pesshyadha at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-6) / Map 1 for another cutscene.\010\010 The dialogue choices do not affect quest progression.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="H-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Nashmau and speak with Jijiroon at Nashmau (H-8) / Map 1.\010\010 The dialogue choices during this cutscene do not affect quest progression.",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Lamian Fang Key before taking the standard route into Arrapago Reef.\010\010 A key can be obtained once per Vana'diel day from the ??? at Caedarva Mire (I-7) / Map 1.\010\010 The key is consumed when used to open the locked Iron Gate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Leave Nashmau through the northern exit at Nashmau (H-6) / Map 1 and enter Caedarva Mire.",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="H-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Caedarva Mire (I-6) / Map 1 and enter Arrapago Reef.",["zone"]="Caedarva Mire",["grid"]="I-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow this route through Arrapago Reef:\010\010 On Map 1, use the Lamian Fang Key to open the locked Iron Gate at Arrapago Reef (J-10) / Map 1.\010\010 Take the first passage west, cross the wrecked ship and two bridges, and reach the western shore around Arrapago Reef (G-10) / Map 1.\010\010 Continue west to Arrapago Reef (F-10) / Map 1 and cross the next two bridges.\010\010 The route changes to Map 2 near Arrapago Reef (K-11) / Map 2.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head north and check the ??? at Arrapago Reef (K-10) / Map 2 for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Arrapago Reef",["grid"]="K-10 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the ??? again to spawn Bukki.\010\010 Bukki spawns with 3,000 TP.\010\010 It uses Manafont at a random point between 10% and 50% HP.\010\010 At a random point between 5% and 15% HP, it stops casting and uses Frenetic Rip as its only TP move.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Bukki.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the ??? again after the battle for another cutscene and the Bag of Gold Pieces key item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Ratihb at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-12) / Map 1 to complete the quest and receive the Random Ring.\010\010 Ensure that you have at least one free inventory slot before speaking with Ratihb.\010\010 The Bag of Gold Pieces is removed when the quest is completed.\010\010 Random Ring is a Rare/Exclusive level 60 ring equippable by all jobs. Its enchantment grants DEX +1\226\128\1478.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="J-12 / Map 1",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6867",["title"]="The Dismayed Customer",["page_title"]="The Dismayed Customer",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Dismayed_Customer",["revision"]="60794",["requirements"]="Start: Gulemont \226\128\148 Port San d'Oria (G-7)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Key item: Gulemont's Document\010Previous: A Taste For Meat",["rewards"]="560g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A patron lost a document somewhere in West Ronfaure. Find it for him.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Gulemont has lost some very important documents, and needs you to help him find them.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He can only think of three places they may be, and they're all in West Ronfaure:\010\010Near the entrance to La Theine Plateau F-11\010\010Near Ronfaure Outpost G-9\010\010Near the Knightwell Border of G-10/11\010\010The ??? may exist at all three locations, but only the correct location will give you the key item, while the incorrect location will produce the message, \034You find some worthless scraps of paper.\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to these locations and look around for a ???.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click on it and obtain the Gulemont's Document Key item: .",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have the papers, return to Gulemont for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57125",["title"]="The Dolphin Crest",["page_title"]="The Dolphin Crest",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Dolphin_Crest",["revision"]="122498",["requirements"]="Start: Jazaraat's Headstone \226\128\148 Caedarva Mire (E-10) / Map 1\010Previous: Lost Kingdom",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="In a cemetery on Azouph Isle, you have found an ancient coin bearing an unfamiliar crest. Report your meeting with the ghost to President Naja.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Lost Kingdom; this mission begins immediately after its ending cutscene at Jazaraat's Headstone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Salaheem's Sentinels in Aht Urhgan Whitegate and speak with Naja Salaheem at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.\010\010 The resulting cutscene completes the mission and begins The Black Coffin.\010\010 The Key item: Ephramadian Gold Coin obtained during Lost Kingdom is required to trigger the initial Arrapago Reef sequence in the next mission.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7547",["title"]="The Doorman",["page_title"]="The Doorman",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Doorman",["revision"]="113090",["requirements"]="Start: Phara \226\128\148 Bastok Mines (J-9)\010Requirements: Warrior 40+",["rewards"]="Razor Axe",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="Phara needs some sword grip material to repair her son's sword. The material can be found in a tent in Davoi. Once repaired, Phara wants to give the sword to her grandson.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Phara, an elderly Hume woman at (Bastok Mines (J-9)) in Bastok Mines will ask you for some Key item: Sword Grip Material from Davoi.\010\010Your job no longer needs to be Warrior.\010\010Your job must be warrior when initiating the quest with Phara [confirmed 10/13/25].",["zone"]="Bastok Mines",["grid"]="J-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Davoi and head almost directly south to a small open area, down to a short, narrow path until you reach the wide-open area of (Davoi (K-9)) and (Davoi (K-10)). \010\010The Orcs (including tier 4) here are aggressive to Sight only.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Scout around for the 'Hide Flap' on one of the tents scattered around the area of K-9/10. Kill off all nearby Orcs to avoid any potential links, buff and when ready, touch the \226\128\152Hide Flap\226\128\153 and spawn two NM Orcs, Gavotvut and Barakbok.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Barakbok is a Dark Knight and should be killed first. Gavotvut is a Warrior.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Both Orcs are highly resistant to sleep.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zoning the Orcs and fighting them one by one does not work. However, it is possible to only fight the WAR by pulling the orcs, along with a large train down to the river. Upon hitting the water they will lose hate, and you will be able to fight only the WAR NM. (See Talk:The Doorman)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Or just wait for the NMs to despawn then check the Hide Flap.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After both have died, find where the \226\128\152Hide Flap\226\128\153 has moved to (still in the same area, it should not be very far away) and examine it again to be presented with the Sword Grip Material. \010\010Warning: If you have multiple warriors doing this quest, you will have to kill the notorious monsters for each warrior. Only the warrior that spawned the NMs will get the key item upon inspecting that hide flap; if another warrior inspects that flap the NMs will spawn again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take this back to Phara, who asks you to come back tomorrow.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait until the next Vana'diel day. No need to rezone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Phara and you will receive Key item: Yasin's Sword , which she asks you to take to her grandson Naji, who is a doorman at the Presidential Office in the Metalworks (J-8).",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After a cut scene, Naji will give you the Razor Axe.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Warrior (WAR)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Warrior (WAR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Razor Axe",["revision"]="118209"},{["job"]="Warrior (WAR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="The Doorman",["revision"]="113090"}}},{["id"]="wiki_7497",["title"]="The Eleventh's Hour",["page_title"]="The Eleventh's Hour",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Eleventh%27s_Hour",["revision"]="122130",["requirements"]="Start: Elki \226\128\148 Bastok Mines (H-5)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 3\010Previous: Hearts of Mythril",["rewards"]="Small Sword",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Elki wants you to find information regarding the identity of the eleventh Palborough Pioneer. You might be able to find some hints in the mines themselves.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Elki. (You must zone between this quest and Hearts of Mythril.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Palborough Mines and take the elevator at I-8 to the third floor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to the LEFT side of the split chamber to the west. But you can't just go west. That would be too easy. See map, to notice how you have to thread your way through an obscene amount of dead ends.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At the line between Palborough Mines (H-7, H-8) examine the Old Toolbox and obtain the Key item: Old Toolbox.",["zone"]="Palborough Mines",["grid"]="H-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Bastok and talk to Elki. (Quickest way back, is to take the one-way boat, near top of elevator. Again, see inset map on this page).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Babenn at (Bastok Mines (J-6)) to receive the reward of a Small Sword.",["zone"]="Bastok Mines",["grid"]="J-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) After completing Beauty and the Galka, return to Parraggoh at (Bastok Mines (H-5)) for additional dialogue.",["zone"]="Bastok Mines",["grid"]="H-5",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7506",["title"]="The Elvaan Goldsmith",["page_title"]="The Elvaan Goldsmith",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Elvaan_Goldsmith",["revision"]="104276",["requirements"]="Start: Michea \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (F-10)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Copper Ingot x 1",["rewards"]="180 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes (after zoning), see below",["summary"]="Help Michea, a free goldsmith, complete her order by bringing her a copper ingot.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Michea.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Copper Ingot to Michea.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The quest is repeatable, but once you attain Bastok reputation 2, speaking to Michea begins Father Figure and prevents this quest from being available until completion of The Return of the Adventurer.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_326",["title"]="The Emissary (Bastok Mission 2-3)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 2-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_2-3",["revision"]="104121",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Level: 25 (recommended)\010Previous: Bastok Mission 2-2|Wading Beasts",["rewards"]="Rank 3\0103,000 gil\010Mog Wardrobe: 10 Slots [Horizon change] \010Level 10 Outpost Teleportation from Jeuno [Horizon change] \010Key item: Adventurer's Certificate",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Gather information on San d'Oria and Windurst. The Bastokan consulates in those two countries will provide you with a detailed briefing.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57195",["title"]="The Empress Crowned",["page_title"]="The Empress Crowned",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Empress_Crowned",["revision"]="120938",["requirements"]="Previous: Imperial Coronation",["rewards"]="Glory Crown",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have been bestowed with the honor of crowning Empress Nashmeira II. There can be no higher acknowledgment of your achievements as a mercenary. Perhaps now President Naja will return your rightful reward...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Imperial Coronation; this mission begins during its ending cutscene at the Imperial Whitegate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the second platform of Salaheem's Sentinels in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10) / Map 1.\010\010 The cutscene triggers automatically as you enter the platform; speaking with Naja Salaheem is not required.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The cutscene completes the mission, grants the Glory Crown, awards the title \034Eternal Mercenary,\034 and begins Eternal Mercenary.\010\010 No zoning or time wait is required before continuing the final mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_560",["title"]="The Enduring Tumult of War (Promathia Mission 5-1)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 5-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_5-1",["revision"]="118732",["requirements"]="Previous: Slanderous Utterings",["rewards"]="Key item: Light of Vahzl",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="The airship piloted by Louverance did not arrive in San d'Oria, but Port Bastok. How much longer will Nag'molada wait for your arrival at the northwestern tower of Pso'Xja?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Head to Northern San d'Oria (L-6) and talk to Chasalvige (Manuscript Room, Cathedral) he will tell you to investigate the port.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="L-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Port San d'Oria (H-6) and talk to Anoki who will say that he hasn't seen anything that you describe.",["zone"]="Port San d'Oria",["grid"]="H-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Port Bastok for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Metalworks and talk to Cid located at Metalworks (H-8) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into the Pso'Xja tower at Beaucedine Glacier (F-7) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Beaucedine Glacier",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This Pso'Xja tower is uncapped. Follow the path forward until you find a stone door, which, when checked, spawns an NM Golem named Nunyunuwi.\010\010This NM has approximately 3500 HP, though offset by an innate Auto Regen trait that restores 100 HP per tick. If improperly handled, this effect can draw the battle out indefinitely. As a result, Nunyunuwi is often defeated with as much damage in as short a period as possible. Among the methods known (or theorized to be) effective are: \010\010Level 3 Darkness Skillchains at 300% TP\010\010Use of Ancient Magic in Magic Bursts, or coupled with layering of DOT effects like Poison II and Bio II\010\010Use of high-level SMN Blood Pacts (when melee or additional SMN support is available)\010\010This NM is known soloable by some jobs at, or over, Level 74 (RNG, MNK, BLM, RDM, DRG, DRK, SAM). Soloing at slightly lower levels may be possible.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When Nunyunuwi is defeated, check the door to move past it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Stone Door for a cutscene. You will arrive in Promyvion - Vahzl, where you will get another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_462",["title"]="The Fanged One",["page_title"]="The Fanged One",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Fanged_One",["revision"]="122457",["requirements"]="Start: Perih Vashai \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (K-7)\010Requirements: Level 30+\010Fame: windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Key item: Old Tiger's Fang\010Previous: None",["rewards"]="Grants the ability to become a Ranger\010Ranger's Necklace\010 [Horizon change] Mog Wardrobe: 5 slots for first advanced job",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Perih Vashai in Windurst Woods (K-7) for a cutscene.\010\010You may have to talk to her multiple times to get the cutscene.\010Optional: Talk to Muhk Johldy for the hint on where to go.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="K-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Sauromugue Champaign (L-8), go up the cliff and head south to touch the Tiger Bones inside the cave Sauromugue Champaign (L-10) to spawn Old Sabertooth.\010\010 3 Sabertooth Tigers (Aggressive) roam outside the cave.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait for Old Sabertooth to die from damage over time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="What do you do if you're a psychopath and you kill the tiger prematurely?\010\010If you (un)accidentally kill him, wait five minutes, then re-examine and he will pop again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Touch the Tiger Bones again to receive the key item Key item: Old Tiger's Fang",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Perih Vashai to complete the quest and receive a Ranger's Necklace.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={"Ranger (RNG)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Ranger (RNG)",["kind"]="Job unlock",["page"]="Ranger",["revision"]="120981"}}},{["id"]="wiki_335",["title"]="The Final Image (Bastok Mission 7-1)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 7-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_7-1",["revision"]="60998",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 6-2|The Pirate's Cove",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You are to investigate the Zilart ruins of Ro'Maeve. Chief Engineer Cid has more details.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 20~22 Crystals to a gate guard to unlock this mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to a Gate Guard to accept the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Cid for a cutscene.\010\010You will be instructed to go to Ro'Maeve. Special caution is to be used in Ro'Maeve, as everything there will aggro magic. Most aggro sound, and there is some sight aggro as well.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You are looking for a ???, which can spawn in the following locations:\010\010(Ro'Maeve (D-10)), (Ro'Maeve (E-9)), (Ro'Maeve (E-10)), (Ro'Maeve (G-9)), (Ro'Maeve (I-8)), (Ro'Maeve (K-10)), (Ro'Maeve (K-11)), (Ro'Maeve (L-10)) or (Ro'Maeve (L-7)). \010\010The ??? appears to not move until the NMs are popped",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the ??? to spawn two Golem NMs named Mokkurkalfi. Despite Golems being sight aggro, you CAN sneak pull these. However they are not overly difficult. The biggest concern is time, and you'll probably not have much time to clear the area before hand, as the ??? can move without realizing it. \010\010The ??? may have moved during the fight, and if so, you'll have to look for it. \010\010Should you die in the process, you WILL be required to fight the NMs again. Zoning has the same effect.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the ??? again to receive the Key item: Reinforced Cermet",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Cid for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_351",["title"]="The Final Seal (Windurst Mission 5-1)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 5-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_5-1",["revision"]="116595",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Level: 50\010Previous: Windurst Mission 4-1|Magicite",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="On the Star Sibyl's command, you are to head north to the ruins of Fei'Yin, somewhere on the Beaucedine Glacier. There, you are to confirm whether the final seal is doing its job.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Inspect the Vestal Chamber at the top of Heavens Tower to start the mission and to receive Key item: New Fei'Yin Seal.\010\010[Template :Nation Mission 5-1: ]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Finishing the Mission",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Vestal Chamber at the top of Heavens Tower to complete the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7538",["title"]="The First Meeting",["page_title"]="The First Meeting",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_First_Meeting",["revision"]="118353",["requirements"]="Start: Oggbi \226\128\148 Port Bastok (E-6)\010Requirements: Monk 50+\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: none\010Previous: Ghosts of the Past",["rewards"]="Temple Gaiters",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="You have been asked to head to Fei'Yin and help Dalzakk, one of Oggbi's students, with his task.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="NOTEYou must zone after obtaining your artifact weapon (Beat Cesti) to flag this quest. If you changed jobs to complete Ghosts of the Past you must change your main job back to Monk.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Oggbi in Port Bastok inside the Steaming Sheep Restaurant located at (Port Bastok (E-6)). He will ask you to travel to Fei'Yin to meet Dalzakk.\010\010 Once the quest shows up in your quest log, you may feel free to change jobs to continue the quest with another job (preferably a higher leveled job).",["zone"]="Port Bastok",["grid"]="E-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Qu'Bia Arena and upon exiting back into Fei'Yin you will trigger a cutscene and receive Key item: Letter from Dalzakk.\010\010You will not trigger the cutscene zoning into Fei'Yin from Beaucedine Glacier. The cutscene will only trigger from an exit from Qu'Bia Arena.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After that, head to Davoi and look for a 'Hide Flap' on one of the tents at (Davoi (F-7)). \010\010 The NMs seemingly don't spawn at the 'Hide Flap', but from the north side.\010\010 Clear the area of any Orcs wandering around the area as they will link to the NMs once they are spawned.\010\010 This can spell disaster, even for a job at level 75.",["zone"]="Davoi",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Interact with the Hide Flap to trigger two NM Orcs to spawn: Bilopdop (MNK) and Deloknok (PLD). \010\010Message will say \034There is nothing here.\034, but they spawn and will run from the north-side.\010\010Bilopdop is immune to sleep.\010\010See also: Testimonials.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill them and investigate the 'Hide Flap' on the tent again to receive the Key item: San d'Orian Martial Arts Scroll.\010\010If you are doing this quest as a party, each member will have to pop a new set of NMs before obtaining the Key Item. The cooldown timer seems to be about 4 minutes since the last party member got his KI. \010Note: The 'Hide Flap' may have moved to another tent while you attack the NMs but will have re-popped within the same area. If this happens just examine the flap on the new tent to receive the key item. The second 'Hide Flap' spawns when you POP the two NMs, not when you KILL them, so if you have someone along who can take hate after the NMs are popped, it is not necessary to kill them. Also, do not try to examine the flap with a bunch or orcs hitting on you. The game might bug out with you not being able to move and not get the item either, resulting in death.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Oggbi to obtain the Temple Gaiters.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional: Talk to Michea in Bastok Markets (Bastok Markets (F-10)), second floor over the Bruhilde Armourer shop for an extra cutscene.",["zone"]="Bastok Markets",["grid"]="F-10",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={"Monk (MNK)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Monk (MNK)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Temple Gaiters",["revision"]="28616"},{["job"]="Monk (MNK)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="The First Meeting",["revision"]="118353"}}},{["id"]="wiki_327",["title"]="The Four Musketeers (Bastok Mission 3-1)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 3-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_3-1",["revision"]="119743",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 2-3|The Emissary",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You are to join a surprise attack on the Quadav stronghold in Beadeaux. See Iron Eater in the President's Office for details.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 4-6 crystal to a gate guard to unlock the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Accept the mission from any gate guard and then speak to Iron Eater at the President's office (Metalworks (J-8)).",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You'll be instructed to go to Beadeaux. Gather up a party, but this is easily soloed if you are high enough.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone in to Beadeaux for a cutscene. You will then need to kill 20 Copper Quadavs. If you are with a party, all kills count towards the total, so you can split up to speed the process up.\010\010 Copper Quadavs in Beadeaux are level 22 - 27. \010\010There are 7 Copper Quadavs in the entry area, before the tunnel, and at least 10 in the tunnel around first afflictor.\010\010They have a respawn timer of 16 minutes.\010\010The game will track how many you've killed, and you don't need to kill them all at once.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon killing 20 Copper Quadavs, zone out to Pashhow Marshlands for another cutscene. This ends the mission.\010\010Make sure you get the cutscene with Ayame\010\010If you do not get your 20 Copper Quadav kills, you will receive a different cutscene.\010\010If you use Escape, you will not receive the cutscene. -- As of 6/6/2026 Escape works, no rezoning needed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade 5 crystals to unlock Bastok Mission 3-2 (optional) or a total of 13 crystals to unlock Bastok Mission 3-3.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Recommendations",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="While you are in Beadeaux, it will help you prepare for mission 4-1 if you are able to acquire drops from two NMs in the area.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="View this walkthrough on the Mission 4-1 page under the heading Beadeaux (Prerequisite)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can save some time by also accepting the DRK quest Blade of Darkness which is similar in cutscene zones and kill order. Warning though, this is a slow method as the weapon is a high delay great sword, weapon skill killshots don't give credit, copper quadav arent simple to kill, and please participate in this method if you do not intend to continue missions in a group as it is slow as mentioned.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_594",["title"]="The Garden of Antiquity (Promathia Mission 8-1)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 8-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_8-1",["revision"]="120243",["requirements"]="Previous: The Warrior's Path",["rewards"]="Tavnazian Ring",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="The celestial capital of Al'Taieu truly exists. Though vastly altered during the ten thousand-year span of their seclusion, the ancients remain alive in the city. Nag'molada heads for the palace, while you and your companions follow in his wake...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After you arrive at Al'Taieu you will get the title Seeker of the Light and your mission Log Change to Chapter 8. Make your way to the spires you can see on the horizon.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Watch for the Quasilumin NPCs, if you talk to each one of them you will receive information on Al'Taieu, as well as the map after you talk to them all.\010\010You have to talk twice to the last to get the map.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to a large bridge leading up to a Crystalline Field Al'Taieu (H-11) Click on the Crystalline Field for a cutscene. \010\010Note that the Auroral Updraft (Al'Taieu (H-12) - looks like a red pillar of light) will take you back to the Sealion's Den. Sueleen in the Sealion's Den will send you back to Al'Taieu.",["zone"]="Al'Taieu",["grid"]="H-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene you need to visit three Rubious Crystals. The first crystal is located at a small tower south of the bridge with the Crystalline Field. Checking each crystal will spawn three Ru'aern NMs, each with their own job and appropriate 2-hours.\010\010The Ru'aerns can be slept with Elemental Seal, but are otherwise quite resistant to Lullaby.\010\010They also seem resistant to Silence without Elemental Seal.\010\010They do not Reraise as normal Aern do.\010\010A Thief can pop the Ru'aerns and kite two of them while the party kills the first one.\010\010A solid Darkness chain can take down an Aern quickly.\010\010Black Mage can sleep the Ru'aern without any problems. \010\010Elemental Seal + Sleepga II was resisted by all mobs following the rebase. (2/7/26)\010Southern Tower Al'Taieu (H-13)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Spawns (from left to right) White Mage, Warrior, and Samurai Ru'aern.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Rubious Crystal after they are dead for a cutscene. \010Western Tower Al'Taieu (D-10)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Spawns (from left to right) Red Mage, Dark Knight, and Ranger Ru'aern.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Rubious Crystal after they are dead for a cutscene. \010Eastern Tower Al'Taieu (L-10)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The area around this tower is much more dangerous than the other two. 3 Om'phuabo can aggro you if you stand on the ramp. There is a patch of land directly west of the tower that is a much safer place to camp if you can pull them there without aggro.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Spawns (from left to right) Black Mage, Paladin, and Monk Ru'aern.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Rubious Crystal after they are dead for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Note that north of each of the last two Rubious Crystal towers is another Auroral Updraft which takes you back to the Auroral Updraft that leads out of Al'Taieu. Using these updrafts, while you don\226\128\153t leave the zone, will cause aggro mobs to drop you as a target.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you visit all three towers and get the three cutscenes there, head back to the Crystalline Field Al'Taieu (H-11) and zone into the Grand Palace of Hu'Xzoi.",["zone"]="Al'Taieu",["grid"]="H-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head forward and check the Gate of the Gods Grand Palace of Hu'Xzoi (H-8) / Map 3 for a final cutscene and your reward.",["zone"]="Grand Palace of Hu'Xzoi",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Can pop with THF and chain powder boots through the zone, like mammets.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3688",["title"]="The Gate of the Gods (Zilart Mission 13)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 13",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_13",["revision"]="102087",["requirements"]="Previous: The Mithra and the Crystal",["rewards"]="Access to Tu'Lia\010Mog Wardrobe 2: 5 slots",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="The path to Tu'Lia has opened!",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Interact with a Shimmering Circle at the end of the path to trigger another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene walk straight through the doors, and into Ru'Aun Gardens, for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="rise of the zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1311",["title"]="The General's Secret",["page_title"]="The General's Secret",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_General%27s_Secret",["revision"]="60801",["requirements"]="Start: Curilla \226\128\148 Chateau d'Oraguille (I-9)\010Requirements: Access to Chateau d'Oraguille\010Fame: san d'oria\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Key item: Curilla's Bottle",["rewards"]="Lynx Baghnakhs",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Fetch some water from the hot spring on the peak of Horlais.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Curilla for a cutscene; agree twice to start the quest and obtain Key item: Curilla's Bottle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go through Yughott Grotto and exit at Yughott Grotto (K-5) into Fort Ghelsba. Follow the left wall to loop around and re-enter Yughott Grotto atFort Ghelsba (J-8). Once inside, go to (J-9) and zone into a small open area of Horlais Peak.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in Horlais Peak, head south to the Hot Springs and select it to fill Key item: Curilla's Bottle (this causes the key item's description to change).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Chateau d'Oraguille and talk to Curilla to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Norg quest Secret of the Damp Scroll also requires going to the Hot Springs and can be done at the same time. Also, you cannot start this quest if you have any RDM AF quests active that involve Curilla.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You need to be able to enter Chateau d'Oraguille, and therefore must be Rank 2 if you are from San d'Oria, or at least started the 2-3 Mission in Windurst or Bastok.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="san d'oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4812",["title"]="The Gift",["page_title"]="The Gift",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Gift",["revision"]="109607",["requirements"]="Start: Oswald \226\128\148 Selbina (I-9)\010Fame: Selbina\010Items: Danceshroom\010Previous: Under the Sea\010The Sand Charm",["rewards"]="Sleep Dagger",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Oswald wants to order something nutrious to cheer his girlfriend up a bit. Get him the special ingredient, a danceshroom.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You need to finish Under the Sea and have begun The Sand Charm to get this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Oswald. He asks you to get him a Danceshroom.\010\010Danceshrooms drop off Shriekers (Ordelle's Caves), Myxomycetes (Sanctuary of Zi'Tah), Killer Mushrooms (Crawlers' Nest), Exorays (Crawlers' Nest), and Death Caps (The Boyahda Tree).\010\010Danceshrooms can be bought from the regional vendor for Movalpolos in each of the three major cities.\010\010Danceshrooms can also be obtained from the BCNM Toadal Recall, Chocobo Digging in Yuhtunga Jungle, Harvesting in Yuhtunga Jungle and Yhoator Jungle, and Gardening.\010\010Danceshrooms can be found under Auction House Category: Food >> Ingredients.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Danceshroom to Oswald for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Selbina",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1624",["title"]="The Gobbiebag Part I",["page_title"]="The Gobbiebag Part I",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Gobbiebag_Part_I",["revision"]="12184",["requirements"]="Start: Bluffnix \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (H-9)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Dhalmel Leather\010Steel Ingot\010Linen Cloth\010Peridot",["rewards"]="Gobbiebag increased to 35 slots",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Bluffnix promises to enlarge your pack if you bring him the following: some Dhalmel Leather, a Steel Ingot, a square of Linen Cloth, and a Peridot.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Bluffnix to start the quest.\010\010If you are unable to start the quest, verify your reputation through Mendi at Lower Jeuno (H-8) across from Waag-Deeg's Magic Shop.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Dhalmel Leather, Steel Ingot, Linen Cloth, and Peridot to Bluffnix (these items can all be found on the Auction House and/or crafted).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After trading the items, your Gobbiebag capacity increases by 5 slots to a new total of 35. \010\010Note: See Inventory for full list of items required for inventory expansion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1637",["title"]="The Gobbiebag Part II",["page_title"]="The Gobbiebag Part II",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Gobbiebag_Part_II",["revision"]="60711",["requirements"]="Start: Bluffnix \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (H-9)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Ram Leather\010Mythril Ingot\010Wool Cloth\010Turquoise\010Previous: The Gobbiebag Part I",["rewards"]="Gobbiebag increased to 40 slots",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Bluffnix promises to enlarge your pack further if you bring him the following: some ram leather, a mythril ingot, a square of wool cloth, and a turquoise.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Bluffnix to start the quest.\010\010If you are unable to start the quest, verify your reputation through Mendi at Lower Jeuno (H-8) across from Waag-Deeg's Magic Shop.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Ram Leather, Mythril Ingot, Wool Cloth, and Turquoise to Bluffnix (these items can all be found on the Auction House and/or crafted).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After trading the items, your Gobbiebag capacity increases by 5 slots to a new total of 40.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1646",["title"]="The Gobbiebag Part III",["page_title"]="The Gobbiebag Part III",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Gobbiebag_Part_III",["revision"]="118270",["requirements"]="Start: Bluffnix \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (H-9)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 5/6 [Wiki: needs verification]\010Items: Tiger Leather\010Gold Ingot\010Velvet Cloth\010Painite\010Previous: The Gobbiebag Part II",["rewards"]="Gobbiebag increased to 45 slots",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Bluffnix promises to enlarge your pack even more if you bring him the following: square of black tiger leather, a gold ingot, a square of velvet cloth, and a painite.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Bluffnix to start the quest.\010\010If you are unable to start the quest, verify your reputation through Mendi at Lower Jeuno (H-8) across from Waag-Deeg's Magic Shop.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Tiger Leather, Gold Ingot, Velvet Cloth, and Painite to Bluffnix (these items can all be found on the Auction House and/or crafted).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After trading the items, your Gobbiebag capacity increases by 5 slots to a new total of 45.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1655",["title"]="The Gobbiebag Part IV",["page_title"]="The Gobbiebag Part IV",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Gobbiebag_Part_IV",["revision"]="61381",["requirements"]="Start: Bluffnix \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (H-9)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 5 [Wiki: needs verification]\010Items: Cermet Chunk\010Darksteel Ingot\010Silk Cloth\010Goshenite\010Previous: The Gobbiebag Part III",["rewards"]="Gobbiebag increased to 50 slots",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Bluffnix will make your pack as big as a Gobbiebag if you bring him the following: a cermet chunk, a darksteel ingot, a square of silk cloth, and a goshenite.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Bluffnix to start the quest.\010\010If you are unable to start the quest, verify your reputation through Mendi at Lower Jeuno (H-8) across from Waag-Deeg's Magic Shop.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Cermet Chunk, Darksteel Ingot, Silk Cloth, and Goshenite to Bluffnix (these items can all be found on the Auction House and/or crafted).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After trading the items, your Gobbiebag capacity increases by 5 slots to a new total of 50.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2795",["title"]="The Gobbiebag Part V",["page_title"]="The Gobbiebag Part V",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Gobbiebag_Part_V",["revision"]="61631",["requirements"]="Start: Bluffnix \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (H-9)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 7\010Items: Bugard Leather\010Paktong Ingot\010Moblinweave\010Rhodonite\010Previous: The Gobbiebag Part IV",["rewards"]="Gobbiebag increased to 55 slots",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Bluffnix will make your pack bigger than a Gobbiebag if you bring him the following: a square of bugard leather, a paktong ingot, a square of Moblinweave, and a rhodonite.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Bluffnix to start the quest.\010\010If you are unable to start the quest, verify your reputation through Mendi at Lower Jeuno (H-8) across from Waag-Deeg's Magic Shop.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Bugard Leather, Paktong Ingot, Moblinweave, and Rhodonite to Bluffnix (these items can all be found on the Auction House and/or crafted).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After trading the items, your Gobbiebag capacity increases by 5 slots to a new total of 55.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2796",["title"]="The Gobbiebag Part VI",["page_title"]="The Gobbiebag Part VI",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Gobbiebag_Part_VI",["revision"]="106795",["requirements"]="Start: Bluffnix \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (H-9)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 7\010Items: High-Quality Eft Skin\010Iolite\010Balloon Cloth\010Shakudo Ingot\010Previous: The Gobbiebag Part V",["rewards"]="Gobbiebag increased to 60 slots",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Bluffnix will make your pack even bigger if you bring him the following: a square of balloon cloth, a shakudo ingot, a high quality eft skin, and a iolite.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Bluffnix to start the quest.\010\010If you are unable to start the quest, verify your reputation through Mendi at Lower Jeuno (H-8) across from Waag-Deeg's Magic Shop.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the High-Quality Eft Skin, Iolite, Balloon Cloth, and Shakudo Ingot to Bluffnix (these items can all be found on the Auction House and/or crafted).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After trading the items, your Gobbiebag capacity increases by 5 slots to a new total of 60.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_9142",["title"]="The Gobbiebag Part VII",["page_title"]="The Gobbiebag Part VII",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Gobbiebag_Part_VII",["revision"]="61633",["requirements"]="Start: Bluffnix \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (H-9)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 7\010Items: Lynx Leather\010Adaman Ingot\010Rainbow Cloth\010Deathstone\010Previous: The Gobbiebag Part VI",["rewards"]="Gobbiebag increased to 65 slots",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Bluffnix will make your pack even bigger if you bring him the following: a square of lynx leather, a adaman ingot, a square of rainbow cloth, and a deathstone.",["changes"]="This quest was only available in the Wings of the Goddess expansion in era, but can be obtained via crafting custom content HENM drops on Horizon.",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Bluffnix to start the quest.\010\010If you are unable to start the quest, verify your reputation through Mendi at Lower Jeuno (H-8) across from Waag-Deeg's Magic Shop.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Lynx Leather, Adaman Ingot, Rainbow Cloth, and Deathstone to Bluffnix (these items can all be found on the Auction House and/or crafted).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After trading the items, your Gobbiebag capacity increases by 5 slots to a new total of 65.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_20967",["title"]="The Gobbiebag Part VIII",["page_title"]="The Gobbiebag Part VIII",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Gobbiebag_Part_VIII",["revision"]="53039",["requirements"]="Start: Bluffnix \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (H-9)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 5/6 [Wiki: needs verification]\010Items: Smilodon Leather\010Electrum Ingot\010Square of Cilice\010Angelstone\010Previous: The Gobbiebag Part VII",["rewards"]="Gobbiebag increased to 70 slots",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Bluffnix will make your pack even bigger if you bring him the following: a square of smilodon leather, an electrum ingot, a square of cilice, and an angelstone.",["changes"]="This quest was only available in the Wings of the Goddess expansion in era, but can be obtained via crafting custom content HENM drops on Horizon.",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Bluffnix to start the quest.\010\010If you are unable to start the quest, verify your reputation through Mendi at Lower Jeuno (H-8) across from Waag-Deeg's Magic Shop.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Smilodon Leather, Electrum Ingot, Square of Cilice, and Angelstone to Bluffnix (these items can all be found on the Auction House and/or crafted).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After trading the items, your Gobbiebag capacity increases by 5 slots to a new total of 70.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_24007",["title"]="The Goblin Tailor",["page_title"]="The Goblin Tailor",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Goblin_Tailor",["revision"]="120113",["requirements"]="Start: Guttrix \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (H-10)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Ordelle Chest Key or \010 Gusgen Chest Key or \010 Shakhrami Chest Key",["rewards"]="RSE",["repeatable"]="Yes x4 (Once for each reward). Not repeatable after all rewards have been obtained.",["summary"]="Each week a different magical pattern appears inside a treasure chest somewhere. Give it to Guttrix and he'll reward you.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Guttrix wants a Key item: Magical Pattern from a treasure chest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Key item: Magical Pattern only drops with the quest active.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The treasure chest location changes every game week, Guttrix will let you know which location and race or see Horizogenes.\010\010Locations: Gusgen Mines, Ordelle's Caves, or Maze of Shakhrami\010\010game week: Starts on Firesday and ends on Darksday\010\010Race Order: Galka, Hume Male, Hume Female, Elvaan Male, Elvaan Female, Tarutaru Male, Tarutaru Female, Mithra\010\010See below for times and locations",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can only carry one Key item: Magical Pattern at a time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Race Order",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes\010\010Guttrix: \034Look, you bring me a magical pattern, and I'll give you somethin' pretty to wear. Capiche?\034 \010\010Guttrix: \034This week my Gobbie bros say that you can find the magical pattern for Tarutaru guys in a treasure chest in the Maze of Shakhrami.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7533",["title"]="The Gustaberg Tour",["page_title"]="The Gustaberg Tour",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Gustaberg_Tour",["revision"]="120765",["requirements"]="Start: Izabele \226\128\148 Metalworks (G-8)\010Requirements: To complete:\010Six party members.\010At least one party member must be level 10 to 15 for Level Sync, or, all members must be level 1-15.\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1",["rewards"]="500 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have been asked to form a party with five other people of level fifteen and below to test Izabele's business idea. Your party is to make its way to Drachenfall in North Gustaberg where Hunting Bear, Izabele's partner, is waiting.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Izabele to begin the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make a party of six members.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="One of you must be level 10-15 if you want to use Level Sync to meet the level requirement. Remember that Level Sync does not work if the sync designee is below level 10. Alternatively, all party members can naturally be levels 1-15.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When everyone has the quest, go to North Gustaberg (west section) and talk to Hunting Bear near the falls (F-8, south side of the river) to get a short cutscene that completes the quest.\010\010There is some chance of aggro on the way to the falls, but it is easily killed if either of you are level 8+.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3686",["title"]="The Hall of the Gods (Zilart Mission 11)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 11",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_11",["revision"]="20474",["requirements"]="Start: None\010Previous: The Temple of Desolation",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A strange grate prohibits you from journeying deeper into the Hall of the Gods. The depression in the center may be the key to getting through. You should probably report this find to Gilgamesh.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Unable to progress any further, head back to Norg and speak to Gilgamesh. He will speak of a Mithra who was once trying to sell a crystal...",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="rise of the zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_342",["title"]="The Heart of the Matter (Windurst Mission 1-2)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 1-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_1-2",["revision"]="119601",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Previous: Windurst Mission 1-1|The Horutoto Ruins Experiment",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Assist the Manustery in the creation of Cardians. You must go to the southeastern magic tower of the Horutoto Ruins in East Sarutabaruta, and energize the Mana Orbs that serve as the hearts of the Cardians. Inquire at the Manustery first for details.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="NOTE: You are not eligible to skip missions by trading in crystals until you are rank 2 or higher.\010\010Please note the \034Notes\034 section below for information on aggressive monsters encountered during this mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Windurst",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to any Windurst Gate Guard to accept the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Manustery (Windurst Woods (H-9)) and speak with Apururu.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She will give you six Dark Mana Orbs and instruct you to energize them within the Outer Horutoto Ruins.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="East Sarutabaruta",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Warning: Some monsters in this area will aggro up to around level 10.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the Marguerite Tower (#4) at East Sarutabaruta (J-11).",["zone"]="East Sarutabaruta",["grid"]="J-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Before entering, talk to Pore-Ohre, who will give you the Key item: Southeastern Star Charm.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Outer Horutoto Ruins\010\010{|\010|align=\034left\034|",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Inside, you must charge all six Dark Mana Orbs by examining the Outer Horutoto Ruins / Marguerite Tower found throughout the ruins.",["zone"]="Outer Horutoto Ruins",["grid"]=" / Marguerite Tower",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Each time you examine a Gizmo, you\226\128\153ll see a cutscene as the orb becomes energized.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There are six Gizmos in total:\010\010 Four located at the corners of the large central chamber.\010\010 Two more hidden behind secret doors along the north and south walls \226\128\148 examine each door to open it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After charging all six orbs, head east and look for a crack in the wall. Inside, examine the Gate: Magical Gizmo to trigger another cutscene.\010\010 There is a Balloon in this room that may aggro lower-level party members.\010\010 If you receive the message \226\128\156The door is firmly shut.\226\128\157, return and speak with Pore-Ohre again before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene, you\226\128\153ll receive the message: \226\128\156The six Mana Orbs have been successfully energized with magic!\226\128\157",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Re-examine each Ancient Magical Gizmo to recollect your orbs, which are now Key item: Glowing Mana Orbs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional: Exit the ruins back into East Sarutabaruta for an additional cutscene featuring the Ace Cardians.\010\010 If you left via warp, escape etc. without seeing the cutscene but still want to see it, re-enter and recollect the orbs before reporting back.\010\010|align=\034right\034|\010|width=\03450%\034|\010<blockquote>",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Within the main room, you\226\128\153ll encounter Goblins (sight) and Bats (sound) that aggro; Battue Bats do not. Behind each cracked wall, two Balloons (sight) will also aggro.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Those around level 21 or higher will avoid aggro from all enemies. Alternatively, you may use oils and powders, though this may be costly for new adventurers.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Completing this mission with a party is the safest approach for those who are lower-level.\010\010|}",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Windurst",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Windurst Woods (H-9) and speak with Apururu to complete the mission.\010\010[Template Mission/Description: orders = Assist the Manustery in the creation of Cardians. You must go to the southeastern magic tower of the Horutoto Ruins in East Sarutabaruta, and energize the Mana Orbs that serve as the hearts of the Cardians. Inquire at the Manustery first for details.]",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_380",["title"]="The Heir to the Light (San d'Oria Mission 9-2)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 9-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_9-2",["revision"]="119752",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 9-1|Breaking Barriers",["rewards"]="Rank 10\010100,000 gil\010San d'Orian Flag\010Mog Wardrobe: 10 Slots",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The Rites of Succession will be held at the cathedral in Northern San d'Oria. You are to report there for guard duty.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 2 stacks of crystals to a Conquest NPC to unlock this mission, then speak to a San d'Oria Gate Guard to start it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Northern San d'Oria for a lengthy cutscene.\010\010If you accepted the mission from the Northern San d'Oria gate guard, you can talk to Arnau to see they are still preparing the Rites.\010\010You will be prohibited from zoning into Chateau d'Oraguille due to increased security until you've triggered the cutscene in Northern San d'Oria.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Chateau d'Oraguille for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Fei'Yin for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Qu'Bia Arena located at Fei'Yin (K-8). Only people who are on 9-2 or have completed it may enter.\010\010Sandy does NOT need to be your current home nation. You just have to have previously completed the fight.",["zone"]="Fei'Yin",["grid"]="K-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="BCNM Fight",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to Qu'Bia Arena for a BCNM fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This is a 2 part BCNM.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Part One will have: \010\010Death Clan Destroyer (WHM Warmachine)\010\010Yukvok of Clan Death (Is 100% sleepable Orc Ranger)\010\0103 Worgbut of Clan Death\010\0103 Rallbrog of Clan Death\010\0103 Vangknok of Clan Death\010\010Open with Elemental Seal+Sleepga II or Horde Lullaby, and start attacking the Ranger mob first. Make sure you silence the Warmachine, as it is a WHM who can Curaga and wake everything up. Defeat the Ranger, followed by the Warmachine, and then take our the rest.\010\010Sleep the last mob before killing it, and give yourself a rest. There will be no time after the first part of the fight to rest.\010\010WARNING: Do not use /fps 0 or addons to un-limit your frame rate for the mid-fight cutscene as it will bug the 2nd phase.\010\010Every member of the group must have a frame rate of 30. so /fps 2 or you will not get the CS",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Part Two will include Prince Trion fighting by your side, against:\010\010Warlord Rojgnoj (PLD, unsleepable)\010\010Rojgnoj's Left Hand (BLM)\010\010Rojgnoj's Right Hand (DRK). \010\010Trion will randomly attack a mob, and should be helped. Preferably, the order to kill the NMs is BLM > PLD > DRK. Trion can be cured and can die in the BC. Should he die, you will be ejected from the BC. Despite being a Paladin, he isn't great at keeping himself alive.\010\010Keep the other mobs silenced, a Paladin with Invincible is useful here for keeping attention.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Final Cutscenes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon clearing the battlefield, zone into Northern San d'Oria for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Chateau and check the Great Hall for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to (King Ranperre's Tomb (H-8)) in King Ranperre's Tomb and check the Heavy Stone Door -- the same from a previous mission -- for yet another cutscene.",["zone"]="King Ranperre's Tomb",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back to the Chateau and speak to Halver and you will be awarded with Rank 10, 100,000 gil, and the San d'Orian Flag.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional: Exit to Northern San d'Oria and proceed to the Papal Chamber door to find out what happens to Shamonde.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Southern San d'Oria for a final epilogue cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3721",["title"]="The Holy Crest",["page_title"]="The Holy Crest",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Holy_Crest",["revision"]="123393",["requirements"]="Start: Ceraulian or Arminibit \226\128\148 Port San d'Oria (I-9)\010Requirements: Level 30\010Chateau d'Oraguille access \010Rise of the Zilart expansion\010Items: Pickaxe\010Wyvern Egg\010Key item: Dragon Curse Remedy",["rewards"]="Unlocks Dragoon job",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Excavate the Wyvern Egg that lies beneath the Maze of Shakhrami. Protect it from dragonslayers.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="See Notes regarding anything with ** if having trouble",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Arminibit or Ceraulian in Port San d'Oria Cargo Room A.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Novalmauge** in Bostaunieux Oubliette (beneath Chateau d'Oraguille**).\010\010Novalmauge** patrols between Bostaunieux Oubliette (F-8, G-8).\010\010You might need to speak to him twice to get the CS.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Morjean in Northern San d'Oria (L-7) manuscript room in the Cathedral. \010\010You might need to speak to him twice to get the CS.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="L-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Buy a few pickaxes (they can break).\010\010Ostalie in Southern San d'Oria (E-9) sells pickaxes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Maze of Shakhrami \010\010Sneak and Invisible needed if around level 30\010\010Entrance to Maze of Shakhrami is in Tahrongi Canyon (K-5) near Teleport-Mea. Alternatively, outpost warp from Kolshushu.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Locate an Excavation Point",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade your pickaxe to an Excavation Point until you receive a Wyvern Egg.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Morjean in Northern San d'Oria (L-7) manuscript room in the Cathedral, and view a cut scene",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="L-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Meriphataud Mountains (K-8) and find the ??? located on the eastern edge of Drogaroga's Spine.",["zone"]="Meriphataud Mountains",["grid"]="K-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Wyvern Egg to the ??? for a cut scene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Rahal in Chateau d'Oraguille (H-9) the Royal Knight's Quarters (on the left as you enter the Chateau). \010\010Rahal will give you the Dragon Curse Remedy and send you to the Ghelsba Outpost.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the hut at Ghelsba Outpost (F-10), click on the door and enter the battlefield \034The Holy Crest\034 with Cyranuce M Cutauleon.\010\010This is a six-person, uncapped battlefield (TP and buffs are not lost upon entering).",["zone"]="Ghelsba Outpost",["grid"]="F-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Cyranuce M Cutauleon to complete the quest.\010\010Defeated solo by most non-mage jobs at level 45 rather than 30. May need a higher level for mage jobs. Individual experience may vary depending on job/gear/buffs/etc. See Testimonials.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Rise of the Zilart",["jobs"]={"Dragoon (DRG)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Dragoon (DRG)",["kind"]="Job unlock",["page"]="Dragoon",["revision"]="121965"}}},{["id"]="wiki_341",["title"]="The Horutoto Ruins Experiment (Windurst Mission 1-1)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 1-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_1-1",["revision"]="113674",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The minister of the Orastery in conducting an experiment in the eastern magic tower of the Horutoto Ruins, located in East Sarutabaruta. Inquire at the Orastery first, then go assist him.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="NOTE: You are not eligible to skip missions by trading in crystals until you are rank 2 or higher.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Windurst",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to any Windurst Gate Guard to accept the mission:\010\010 Mokyokyo, Windurst Waters (Windurst Waters (F-5) / North)\010\010 Janshura-Rashura, Port Windurst (Port Windurst (B-5))\010\010 Rakoh Buuma, Windurst Woods (Windurst Woods (K-10))\010\010 Zokima-Rokima, Windurst Walls (Windurst Walls (H-7))",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Then speak to Hakkuru-Rinkuru (Port Windurst (E-7)) in the Orastery for instructions.",["zone"]="Port Windurst",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Inner Horutoto Ruins",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the ruins through entrance (#5) at East Sarutabaruta (J-7) in East Sarutabaruta.\010\010Optional: Speak with Sama Gohjima outside the entrance for a hint about the minister\226\128\153s location.",["zone"]="East Sarutabaruta",["grid"]="J-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go down the stairs to the main chamber, then circle around and head south.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Look for a cracked wall at (Inner Horutoto Ruins (H-9) / Lily Tower).\010\010If you see dirt instead of brick floors, you've taken the wrong cracked wall opening.",["zone"]="Inner Horutoto Ruins",["grid"]="H-9 / Lily Tower",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go through and head east (left from your view).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Gate: Magical Gizmo at (Inner Horutoto Ruins (I-10) / Lily Tower) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Inner Horutoto Ruins",["grid"]="I-10 / Lily Tower",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Search the six Ancient Magical Gizmos until you find the Key item: Cracked Mana Orb:\010\010 (Inner Horutoto Ruins (G-8) / Lily Tower), (Inner Horutoto Ruins (G-9) / Lily Tower), (Inner Horutoto Ruins (H-8) / Lily Tower), (Inner Horutoto Ruins (H-9) / Lily Tower), (Inner Horutoto Ruins (I-8) / Lily Tower), (Inner Horutoto Ruins (I-9) / Lily Tower)\010\010 The Cracked Mana Orb is randomly assigned to an Ancient Magical Gizmo for each party member.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return the Cracked Mana Orb to Hakkuru-Rinkuru in the Orastery (Port Windurst (E-7)) to complete the mission.",["zone"]="Port Windurst",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1189",["title"]="The Immortal Lu Shang",["page_title"]="The Immortal Lu Shang",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Immortal_Lu_Shang",["revision"]="113426",["requirements"]="Start: Irmilant \226\128\148 Rabao (G-7)\010Fame: Selbina/Rabao\010Items: Broken Lu Shang's Rod\010Ancient Lumber\010Light Crystal",["rewards"]="Lu Shang's Fishing Rod",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Irmilant has said he will repair your broken Lu Shang's fishing rod. Along with the broken fishing rod, you must bring him a piece of ancient lumber and two light crystals.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You first need to obtain a Broken Lu Shang's Rod before you may activate this quest.\010\010It doesn't matter whether you break your own Lu Shang's Fishing Rod or buy a broken one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Irmilant at Rabao (G-7). He will offer to repair your rod. To do so, you must bring him one piece of Ancient Lumber and one Light Crystal.",["zone"]="Rabao",["grid"]="G-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade all three items to Irmilant and he will repair your Lu Shang's Fishing Rod.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Selbina/Rabao",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_358",["title"]="The Jester Who'd Be King (Windurst Mission 8-2)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 8-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_8-2",["revision"]="120347",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Previous: Windurst Mission 8-1|Vain",["rewards"]="Rank 9\01080,000 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The time for the Dark Dungeon jailbreak is at hand! At the request of the Manustery, you are to collect the ministry rings from all five ministers.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 22~23 crystals to any Conquest Overseer to unlock the mission then accept it from any Windurst Gate Guard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Meeting the Ministry Leaders",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Apururu at Windurst Woods (H-9) inside the Manustery for a cutscene after which you will obtain the Key item: Manustery Ring.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can talk to the following three NPCs in any order to receive a cutscene and a key item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Rukususu at Fei'Yin (F-6) / Map 2. Click the Cermet Door for a cutscene and the Key item: Rhinostery Ring.",["zone"]="Fei'Yin",["grid"]="F-6 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Sedal-Godjal at Davoi (J-8). You will receive a cutscene and obtain the Key item: Aurastery Ring.\010Note: He can only be reached by going through Monastic Cavern. Enter Monastic Cavern from entrance 2 at Davoi (H-11), proceed through Monastic Cavern and enter Davoi exit 4 at Monastic Cavern (I-8).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Tosuka-Porika at Windurst Waters (G-8) / North inside the eastern building of the Optistery. You will receive a cutscene and obtain the Key item: Optistery Ring.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="G-8 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Apururu at Windurst Woods (H-9) for dialogue regarding the final ring.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Kupipi in Heavens Tower for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Horutoto Ruins",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the Amaryllis Tower of Outer Horutoto Ruins from West Sarutabaruta (F-4).\010\010The West Sarutabaruta Outpost is close to the entrance.",["zone"]="West Sarutabaruta",["grid"]="F-4",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go through the Cracked Wall at Outer Horutoto Ruins (I-6) / Amaryllis Tower 1.",["zone"]="Outer Horutoto Ruins",["grid"]="I-6 / Amaryllis Tower 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On the next map, find the Cracked Wall at Outer Horutoto Ruins (G-8) / Amaryllis Tower 2. Touching it will pop Queen of Coins (RDM) and Queen of Swords (PLD).\010\010You can Sneak Pull and fight one at a time.\010Sneak pull didn't work post rebase (Feb 28, 2026) \010\010You can let one despawn before killing the one you Sneak pull.\010Cardians do do not despawn if you die during the fight. They remain if you home point. You can carefully pull them one at a time if this is the case and you time it properly. They have true sound and link. If they used their 2hr during the previous fight, they do not regain its use.\010\010Both Cardians are immune to Sleep and Silence, but are susceptible to other debuffs.",["zone"]="Outer Horutoto Ruins",["grid"]="G-8 / Amaryllis Tower 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the fight, click the Cracked Wall again for a cutscene and to obtain the Key item: Orastery Ring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Gate of Darkness",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the Cardian Queens' fight, return to Apururu at Windurst Woods (H-9) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Shantotto at Windurst Walls (K-7) for a cutscene and to obtain the Key item: Glove of Perpetual Twilight.\010\010You may need to speak to Shantotto multiple times for the correct cutscene.",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="K-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Apururu at Windurst Woods (H-9) for a cutscene (again).",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, you need to go to the Gate of Darkness inside the Rose Tower of the Inner Horutoto Ruins. \010\010If you possess the Key item: Portal Charm or are in a party with a Black Mage, a Red Mage and a White Mage, you can enter the Lily Tower at East Sarutabaruta (J-7). A quick way to get to Lili Tower, is entering Rose Tower at West Sarutabaruta (J-8) and using Escape.\010\010If you possess the Key item: Rhinostery Certificate, you can travel through Toraimarai Canal by passing through the Priming Gate at Windurst Walls (H-3).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed to the Gate of Darkness at Inner Horutoto Ruins (I-7) / Rose Tower 2 for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Inner Horutoto Ruins",["grid"]="I-7 / Rose Tower 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Apururu at Windurst Woods (H-9) for a cutscene that completes the mission.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Return to Shantotto Windurst Walls (K-7) for dialogue regarding the Key item: Glove of Perpetual Twilight.",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="K-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Return to Tosuka-Porika at Windurst Waters (G-8) / North in the Optistery to report about the Book of the Gods as promised.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="G-8 / North",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5950",["title"]="The Kind Cardian",["page_title"]="The Kind Cardian",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Kind_Cardian",["revision"]="117671",["requirements"]="Start: Panta-Putta (Infirmary Monberaux, Upper Jeuno)\010Requirements: Jeuno Reputation: ?\010Items: Key item: Two of Swords (Key Item)\010Ten of Cups (Card)\010Previous: The Lost Cardian",["rewards"]="Green Cape",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Deliver the Key item: Two of Swords (Key Item) to Apururu Windurst Woods (H-9) at the Manustery.",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you are on The Jester Who'd Be King or Moon Reading you will be unable to deliver Two of Swords to Apururu.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After receiving the cutscene from Apururu, go to the Outer Horutoto Ruins - southwest tower in West Sarutabaruta (F-11). Ten of Cups appears at Outer Horutoto Ruins (J-8) / Dahlia Tower on that map, which is a hidden area behind another hidden area behind a cracked wall.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have the Ten of Cups (Card), take it back to the Manustery (North) and trade it to Apururu Windurst Woods (H-9) at the Manustery..",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Panta-Putta Lower Jeuno (G-10) to finish the quest.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="G-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Game Description\010\010Client: Panta-Putta (Infirmary Monberaux, Upper Jeuno)\010\010Summary:\010Panta wants you to take the Two of Swords to the Manustery in Windurst to restore the Cardian's magical power.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6936",["title"]="The Kuftal Tour",["page_title"]="The Kuftal Tour",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Kuftal_Tour",["revision"]="120232",["requirements"]="Start: Datta \226\128\148 Rabao (F-7)\010Requirements: Selbina/Rabao Reputation 3?\010Previous: The Gustaberg Tour",["rewards"]="8000 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have been asked to participate in a tour planned by Datta. Travel to the cliff inside the entrance to the Kuftal Tunnel with a party of six people of level forty or less, then meet with Datta's partner, Hawk Nose.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Datta, who asks you to participate in a tour of Kuftal Tunnel.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make a party of six members below level 40. \010\010There is no level cap, so your actual job level must be level 40 or below.\010\010Level Sync works on this quest. Thus, you only need one level 40 or below player in the party, and then Level Sync to his or her level.\010\010You can avoid aggro by renting a Chocobo to get there, and, once inside the tunnel, the only monsters around are Lizards who do not aggro.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Kuftal Tunnel and examine the ??? that is just inside the entrance to get a cutscene with Hawk Nose. Your party must be close to the ??? in order to receive cs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Then return to Datta to get another cutscene and finish the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_634",["title"]="The Last Verse",["page_title"]="The Last Verse",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Last_Verse",["revision"]="20483",["requirements"]="Start: Esha'ntarl, Ru'Lude Gardens (-)\010Previous: Apocalypse Nigh",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="This is the last chapter in both the Chains of Promathia and Rise of the Zilart storylines. It is automatically activated after finishing Apocalypse Nigh. It does not have a mission description and simply signifies that you have finished the storylines.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="chains of promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5951",["title"]="The Lost Cardian",["page_title"]="The Lost Cardian",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Lost_Cardian",["revision"]="10752",["requirements"]="Start: Monberaux - Upper Jeuno (G-10)\010Requirements: Jeuno Reputation: ? (>1)\010Previous: Cook's Pride",["rewards"]="Key item: Two of Swords (Key Item)\0102100 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="The Two of Swords has gone missing. Nobody knows where he has gone off to.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Teigero-Bangero Lower Jeuno (H-10) and Panta-Putta Lower Jeuno (G-10), who tell you they haven't seen it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, speak to Monberaux in Upper Jeuno (G-10) / Infirmary (opposite of where Bozz is), who tells you he found the Two of Swords after he shut himself down because Panta-Putta broke his heart.\010\010He gives you the Key item: Two of Swords, the reward and title.\010\010You may have to talk to him several times (up to 7), even if he repeats things he has already said relating to other quests and/or missions.\010It is only after receiving this cut scene from Monberaux that this quest will appear in your completed quest menu and the next quest The Kind Cardian will show up in the current quest log.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Panta-Putta (Merchant's House, Lower Jeuno)\010 / summary=The Two of Swords has gone missing. Nobody knows where he has gone off to.]",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-10 / Infirmary",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_534",["title"]="The Lost City (Promathia Mission 2-2)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 2-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_2-2",["revision"]="9502",["requirements"]="Start: N/A\010Previous: An Invitation West",["rewards"]="Access to Phomiuna Aqueducts",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="According to its inhabitants, the Tavnazian Safehold was carved out of solid rock by survivors of the Great War. Speak with the city's inhabitants to learn more of their grave situation.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Head to the top floor of Tavnazian Safehold and pass through the Walnut Door at Tavnazian Safehold (K-9) / Map 2.\010\010 To save some time, consider doing the Tavnazian Safehold map quest Unforgiven at the same time, as you can get the key item on the way to Despachiaire.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="K-9 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Despachiaire at Tavnazian Safehold (K-10) / Map 2 for a cutscene.\010\010 (Optional) Talk to Justinius at Tavnazian Safehold (J-6) / Map 2, as he will warn you not to go to the Sewer Entrance.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="K-10 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head all the way down to the basement level and examine the Sewer Entrance at Tavnazian Safehold (I-7) / Map 3, at the zone to Phomiuna Aqueducts.\010\010 During the cutscene, you will be able to trigger the next mission Distant Beliefs.\010\010[Template Mission/Description: orders = According to its inhabitants, the Tavnazian Safehold was carved out of solid rock by survivors of the Great War. Speak with the city's inhabitants to learn more of their grave situation.]",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="I-7 / Map 3",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7426",["title"]="The Medicine Woman",["page_title"]="The Medicine Woman",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Medicine_Woman",["revision"]="104393",["requirements"]="Start: Abeaule \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (F-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Malboro Vine\010Zinc Ore\010Insect Wing\010Previous: The Trader in the Forest",["rewards"]="2100g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A guest at the inn has fallen ill. Call on Amaura in Southern San d'Oria to get some cold medicine.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Abeaule, at the inn in Northern San d'Oria, says a customer got sick and needs medicine. (You don't need to zone if you just finished the last quest)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Southern San d'Oria to the second house in Watchdog Alley and talk to Amaura (G-6), who gives you Key item: Amaura's formula, which lists the items she needs to make the medicine. She needs one each of the following: \010\010Malboro Vine\010\010Zinc Ore \010\010Insect Wing",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade these to Amaura and she will give you the Key item: Cold Medicine .",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Abeaule to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6856",["title"]="The Merchant's Bidding",["page_title"]="The Merchant's Bidding",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Merchant%27s_Bidding",["revision"]="60831",["requirements"]="Start: Parvipon \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (E-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Rabbit Hide x 3",["rewards"]="120g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Fetch three rabbit hides.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Parvipon needs rabbit hides. Bring him 3 to reap your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5955",["title"]="The Missing Piece",["page_title"]="The Missing Piece",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Missing_Piece",["revision"]="112034",["requirements"]="Start: Alfesar \226\128\148 Rabao (H-7)\010Fame: Rabao\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Key item: Ancient Tablet Fragment \010Key item: Tablet of Ancient Magic \010Key item: Letter from Alfesar",["rewards"]="Scroll of Teleport-Altep",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The friar Alfesar has asked you to find the remaining part of a stone tablet that was found in the Quicksand Caves that lie beneath the Altepa Desert.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Alfesar to start the quest. He needs your help in finding an Key item: Ancient Tablet Fragment in the Quicksand Caves. (May need to speak with him up to 3 times to trigger the quest)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Key item: Ancient Tablet Fragment spawns at one of five randomly chosen locations in the Quicksand Caves.\010\010Spawnpoints on Map 1: Quicksand Caves (H-6, H-10, E-9) / Map 1\010\010Spawnpoints on Map 2: Quicksand Caves (D-9, L-11) / Map 2",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To get to the ??? at Quicksand Caves (H-6) / Map 1 (Point 1 on the map), enter the Quicksand Caves from Eastern Altepa Desert (J-7) (Entrance #1 on the Map). \010\010You will zone in Quicksand Caves (L-4) / Map 1 on Map 1.\010\010Go to Quicksand Caves (I-7) / Map 1, be sure you are on the right (west) wall then fall down. \010\010There will be a beetle at the spawn point. If the ??? is not there, head out of the caves at Quicksand Caves (D-5) / Map 1. You will exit at Eastern Altepa Desert (H-8) (Entrance #2 on the Map).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To reach the other four points, again enter the Quicksand Caves from Eastern Altepa Desert (J-7).\010\010This time drop down at Quicksand Caves (J-7) / Map 1, on the left (east) wall.\010\010On Map 1 you can check points 2 Quicksand Caves (E-9) / Map 1 and 3 Quicksand Caves (H-10) / Map 1.\010\010If not at either point, drop down at Quicksand Caves (F-10) / Map 1. As you drop down, be sure you are on the east wall. Take Tunnel A.\010\010Points 4 Quicksand Caves (D-9) / Map 2 and 5 Quicksand Caves (L-11) / Map 2 are on Map 2.",["zone"]="Eastern Altepa Desert",["grid"]="J-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you find the ???, check it and you will receive the Key item: Ancient Tablet Fragment.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Alfesar. He will give you the Key item: Tablet of Ancient Magic and the Key item: Letter from Alfesar.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take both items to Charlaimagnat at the cathedral in Northern San d'Oria (bottom floor, when you enter the cathedral take an immediate left, followed by a U-Turn down the stairs). He asks for you to come back another day because he needs to decipher the tablet.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait for JP midnight and talk to Charlaimagnat again to receive your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Rabao",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3687",["title"]="The Mithra and the Crystal (Zilart Mission 12)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 12",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_12",["revision"]="119751",["requirements"]="Start: None\010Previous: The Hall of the Gods|The Hall of the Gods",["rewards"]="Key item: Cerulean Crystal",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="According to Gilgamesh, a Mithra carrying a mysterious crystal she found in Zi'Tah was recently in Norg. Her name was something like Mary or Maroo or Maree...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Go to Rabao and speak to Maryoh Comyujah, who is in (Rabao (G-7)) in front of the windmill.\010\010Choose the top option, \034Sounds fair\034.",["zone"]="Rabao",["grid"]="G-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She will ask you to go to the Quicksand Caves again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head for the secret entrance in Western Altepa Desert (Western Altepa Desert (C-11)) / (Western Altepa Desert (D-11)) , (Same hidden zone as Through the Quicksand Caves.)\010\010 This Mission happens in a similar location in the caves, but on the opposite side of the area where you went before. Check the coordinates below to be sure.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Inside, go to (Quicksand Caves (K-8) / Map 4) and through the pressure door. On the next map, head for (Quicksand Caves (G-8) / Map 7) for another pressure door.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter and fall down the hole. Near where you fall, there is a ???. Buff up and check it to spawn a Pot NM Ancient Vessel. Dispose of it and check the ??? again. You will receive the Key item: Scrap of Papyrus.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Rabao and speak to Maryoh Comyujah again. She will give you the Key item: Cerulean Crystal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the Hall of the Gods, and click the gate at the end of the hall, as you did in Zilart Mission 10. A cutscene will follow.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="rise of the zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3750",["title"]="The Moogle's Picnic!",["page_title"]="The Moogle's Picnic!",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Moogle%27s_Picnic%21",["revision"]="119604",["requirements"]="Start: Moogle - Mog House in your home city\010Requirements: Reputation: 5 in your home city\010Items: Mahogany Bed\010Selbina Butter\010Shrimp Lure\010Previous: Give a Moogle a Break",["rewards"]="Upgrades the Mog Safe to a 70 item capacity.",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="When you attain the required Reputation, your moogle will mention Mahogany Beds.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In order for this quest to become available, you must place the bed in your Mog House at least one full Vana'diel day before the weekly conquest results are tallied.\010\010A mahogany bed can be crafted with Woodworking or purchased at the Auction House under Furnishings.\010\010Other Furniture Quests such as Unexpected Treasure may override this quest. To guarantee you get this quest, remove any other quest-giving furniture from your Layout. The furniture can remain in your safe.\010\010The mahogany bed may be removed at any time after the quest has been flagged; it does not need to be in the mog house for the quest to be completed.\010\010This quest cannot be started in a Rent-a-Room. It can, however, be completed in one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If any other Mog House Moogle quest starts you must zone and talk to your moogle again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Your moogle asks if he can go home for a Moogle festival. Allow him to do so.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Your moogle wants to take a Shrimp Lure and Selbina Butter.\010\010A shrimp lure can be crafted with Alchemy or purchased at the Auction House under Weapons > Ammo & Misc > Fishing Gear.\010\010Selbina butter can be crafted with Cooking or purchased at the Auction House under Food > Ingredients.\010\010Selbina butter can also be bought from Kopopo if a player has recently sold one to the guild, and Chomo Jinjahl will sell butter to players who are at least rank Novice in the Culinarians' Guild. Both NPCs are located at Windurst Waters (E-8) / North.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the moogle both items. You can make the trade at any mog house, it does not need to be in your home nation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After going away on his trip -- oddly, he doesn't physically leave your Mog House as far as you can tell -- he will come back with a new Mog Safe that now holds 70 items! This takes until Japanese Midnight to occur.\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Moogle - Mog House in your home city\010 / summary=Your moogle wants to take a shrimp lure and some Selbina butter back home. He sure would be happy if you found them for him.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2558",["title"]="The Moonlit Path",["page_title"]="The Moonlit Path",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Moonlit_Path",["revision"]="121046",["requirements"]="Start: Leepe-Hoppe \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (J-9) / South\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 5\010Items: First time only:\010Key item: Whisper of Flames\010Key item: Whisper of Frost\010Key item: Whisper of Gales\010Key item: Whisper of Storms\010Key item: Whisper of Tides\010Key item: Whisper of Tremors\010Always:\010Key item: Moon Bauble\010Key item: Whisper of the Moon\010Previous: Trial by Earth\010Trial by Fire\010Trial by Ice\010Trial by Lightning\010Trial by Water\010Trial by Wind",["rewards"]="The avatar Fenrir or\010Ancients' Key or\010Fenrir's Cape or\010Fenrir's Earring or\010Fenrir's Stone or\010Fenrir's Torque or\01015,000 Gil \010Under certain conditions:\010Key item: Dark Mana Orb",["repeatable"]="daily",["summary"]="Leepe-Hoppe wants you to take on Carbuncle's request to gather the six \034whispers,\034 then pay a visit to the Full Moon Fountain...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Leepe-Hoppe (located on the roof) and answer his question affirmatively for a cutscene.\010\010If Leepe-Hoppe gives you the cutscene for Tuning In, zone and talk to him again to get the cutscene for this quest.\010\010Talking to Leepe-Hoppe twice after receiving Tuning In may also start the dialog for The Moonlit Path.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat each of the six prime avatars and collect their whispers. Do not return to the original NPC who gave you the fork or you will lose the whisper.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take all six whispers back to Leepe-Hoppe for another cutscene. You will lose your six whispers and receive a Key item: Moon Bauble.\010\010You keep your Key item: Moon Bauble if Fenrir Prime defeats you, so you do not have to get all the whispers again if you lose.\010\010If you are repeating this quest, you do not need to have all 6 whispers to get a new Key item: Moon Bauble; simply talk to Leepe-Hoppe after JP midnight following your previous completion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Inner Horutoto Ruins and go through the Three Mage Gate. \010\010Have a Red Mage, White Mage, and Black Mage stand on the corresponding colored circles, or have someone who has the Key item: Portal Charm open it.\010\010Alternately, if you have started the Windurst Waters quest, Toraimarai Turmoil, you may enter Toraimarai Canal from Windurst Walls. From the T-intersection at (H-7) on the second map, go west and take the steps down into the water. Then go north and then west putting you back on the first map. Go north then west (in the water) until the T-intersection at (H-7) on the first map. Now head south then up the steps at (G-8) and make your way toward the fountain.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the Moon Bauble to Full Moon Fountain, enter the battlefield, and defeat Fenrir Prime to receive the Key item: Whisper of the Moon.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Leepe-Hoppe for a cutscene and your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To fight Fenrir again, simply talk to Leepe-Hoppe for another Moon Bauble after JP midnight following your previous completion of this quest; you do not need to fight the six avatars again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Key item: Dark Mana Orb is received as an additional award if you have attained Rank 10 in Windurst, and are a citizen of Windurst when completing the quest. It is used to obtain an additional cutscene tying together the Star Onion Brigade quests with the Windurst storyline, after also completing The Promise.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Strategies\010\010See the The Moonlit Path Strategies page.\010[Template Prime Avatar Quest Index: ]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_528",["title"]="The Mothercrystals (Promathia Mission 1-3)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 1-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_1-3",["revision"]="118663",["requirements"]="Start: N/A\010Level: 30\010Items: Key item: Light of Holla\010Key item: Light of Dem\010Key item: Light of Mea\010Previous: Below the Arks",["rewards"]="Access to Lufaise Meadows/Tavnazian Archipelago\0101500 Experience Points\010Mog Wardrobe 2: 5 slots",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The first mothercrystal has been tainted with Emptiness. Hurry to the remaining crags to find out if any other stones have met the same fate.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Head to any of the Shattered Telepoints at Crag of Mea, Crag of Dem, Crag of Holla to enter Promyvion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To complete this mission, you will need to complete the other two promyvion areas (besides the one you completed in the previous mission).\010\010If you have entered one of the 3 areas before and then go to another without clearing the one you previously enter, you have to seal your memories of the previous one, which you will be prompted to do when checking the Shattered Telepoint at a different Crag.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Monster Behavior",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enemies in Promyvion are called \034The Empty\034. Each Promyvion has 4 different kinds of Empty: Wanderers, Weepers, Seethers, and a final type that is exclusive to each Promyvion. The monsters have a level range depending on islands like so:\010\0101st: Easy Prey to Decent Challenge to level 30\010\0102nd: Even Match to Tough to level 30\010\0103rd (note that there are two possible third islands, and the one you get warped to varies by Memory Stream): Very Tough to Incredibly Tough to level 30",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Weepers and Wanderers are the weakest monster types, besides Strays.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Do not bother with Sneak or Invisible, because all monsters on all islands are True Sight and aggressive, but only enemies with similar elemental cores will link.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="General Information",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To proceed to the next island in the sequence, you must find and defeat a Memory Receptacle. They appear on teleport platforms found on each island. There are several possible locations on the second and third islands. The locations of those Memory Receptacles is random. Receptacles spawn several Strays. If the Memory Receptacle is real, a Memory Stream appears upon defeat, and you have three minutes to enter this stream and proceed to the next island. If the Memory Receptacle is a decoy, nothing appears.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you need to return to a previous island, search for a platform that has a live portal, but no Memory Receptacle in it. That is the portal back.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On the final island, there is no Memory Receptacle, but a zoneline to the Spire (battlefield entrance). It may be very difficult to avoid aggro on the fourth floor if you have no high level players to clear the path, but if you get caught and the castle-like structure is nearby, you should be able to zone easily.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If using anima in a party, you may want to agree on an order of use for anima. They last 30 seconds and overlap (using one during the effect of another of the same type resets the duration to 30 seconds), but panicking and using three at once is a waste. Also note that the effects of anima stack, so you can use Psychoanima and Hysteroanima in pairs to stop all attacks.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ancient Flames Beckon",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Boss fights allow up to six players to fight. The fight is called \034Ancient Flames Beckon.\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Buffs except food cancel upon entering the battlefield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Anima have the same effects on all three bosses:\010\010 Psychoanima causes the boss to be 100% intimidated by players for ~30 seconds, stopping all normal attacks (prevents 7-8 attacks).\010\010 Hysteroanima causes the boss's special attacks to fail for ~20 seconds. They are still readied, but do not execute. This is especially useful in the last 20% of the boss' HP, when they start to spam their TP attacks.\010\010 Terroanima causes the boss to run away from the player with hate for ~30 seconds.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Promyvion - Mea\010\010Mea's boss is the Delver (Craver type). Its TP attacks are:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Brain Spike: Single-target damage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Carousel: AoE damage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Promyvion Brume: AoE damage, Poison, and resets hate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Empty Crush: Single-target damage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Impalement: Drops the target to 5% HP and reduces target's enmity, similiar to Throat Stab. Can be avoided by running out of range.\010Don't panic when it uses this attack because it reduces enmity to a minimum, causing the Delver to move onto someone else, giving time to cure. If solo, it is worthwhile to have medicines ready for this attack. This is its deadliest TP move.\010\010Beating Promyvion - Mea grants the Key item: Light of Mea.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Promyvion - Dem\010\010Dem's boss is the Progenerator (Gorger type). Its TP attacks are:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Fission: Spawns a pet.\010\010 This TP move can be used at any time, but happens most beginning at 50% HP. The Progenerator is immune to Sleep and Bind, but the pets are not. This is its deadliest TP move. The additional monsters can cause problems if not dealt with and killed. The pets continue to be generated if some are killed, up to a maximum of 6 pets, and they share hate with the Progenerator.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Vanity Drive: Directional AoE damage. Make sure people stand behind the Progenerator for the duration of the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Spirit Absorption: Drains 200 HP from the target, ignoring Utsusemi.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Promyvion Barrier: Defense Boost.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Stygian Flatus: AoE Paralyze. Barparalyzra at the start of the fight can be very worthwhile. This is quite a deadly move that can cause a weak party to wipe.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Quadratic Continuum: Single target damage.\010\010Beating Promyvion - Dem grants the Key item: Light of Dem.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Promyvion - Holla\010\010Holla's boss is the Wreaker (Thinker type). Its TP attacks are:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trinary Tap: Drains 1-3 status effects (including Food and Utsusemi) or 200 HP from the target if no positive status effects are present.\010\010 It is usually recommended that the tank eat no food for this NM fight. Other ideas used are to buff somewhat useless buffs like: Barsilencera, Barpoisonra, or Bard songs. Avoid using elemental barspells if you have a Black Mage nuking in your party.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trinary Absorption: Drains HP from the target.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Shadow Spread: AoE Curse, Blind, and Sleep. Use Poison Potions to prevent sleep and Holy Water to remove Curse. This is its deadliest TP move.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Stygian Vapor: Short range AoE Plague.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Negative Whirl: AoE Ice [Wiki: needs verification] damage plus Slow.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Winds of Promyvion: Removes one negative status from the NM. It's useful to enfeeble the NM, as he may often use this in place of more devastating TP attacks. Slow works well for activating this TP move.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Empty Cutter: Single-target physical damage.\010\010Beating Promyvion - Holla grants the Key item: Light of Holla.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After Completion\010\010After obtaining your third light, you appear in Lufaise Meadows after a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_52127",["title"]="The Naming Game",["page_title"]="The Naming Game",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Naming_Game",["revision"]="104323",["requirements"]="Start: Raibaht \226\128\148 Metalworks (G-8)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 5\010Items: Ordrynite\010Previous: Hyper Active",["rewards"]="3,600 gil \010Ability to name the new airship in CoP 5-1.",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Cid's dream of completing a \034semi-perpetual motion engine\034 can only be realized if he obtains a chunk of legendary ordrynite.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade an Ordrynite to Raibaht for a cutscene and your rewards.\010\010Obtain an Ordrynite from a Cryptonberry Plaguer or Cryptonberry Stalker in Pso'Xja. These mobs can be found in the entrances from Beaucedine Glacier (G-9) or Beaucedine Glacier (I-7), but (G-9) is recommended over (I-7) since it has more spawns.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Here is the list of names for naming the airship:\010{| class=\034horizon-table editing-table sortable\034\010! width=\03416%\034|Line 1\010! width=\03416%\034|Line 2\010! width=\03417%\034|Line 3\010|-\010|",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ultra",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Hyper",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Psycho",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Eternal",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Neo",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Lovely",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Pretty",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Final",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Extra",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Deadly",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Savage",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Aero",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Pseudo",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Universal",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exciting",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Celestial",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Super",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mighty",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mega",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Omni",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Poly\010|",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Terror",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Perfect",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Royale",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Gorgeous",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Pretty",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Hell",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Fantasy",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Stealth",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Powerful",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Invincible",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Explosive",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Storm",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Fantastic",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Duper",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go-Go",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Morphing",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Retro",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Sonic",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Cloud",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Sky",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Stellar\010|",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Hyper",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Neo",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Lovely",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Happy",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Caller",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Hound",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="XI",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Armored",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Brutal",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Buster",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Alpha",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Chief",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Provoker",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mincer",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Streak",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="King",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Prince",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Power",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Robo",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Delver",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mystic\010|}",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_637",["title"]="The New Frontier (Zilart Mission 1)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_1",["revision"]="116981",["requirements"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["rewards"]="Map of Norg",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Vana'diel is expanding day by day. What adventures await you in the Outlands?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After defeating the Shadow Lord and gaining rank 6, head to Norg for a cut-scene.\010\010Players may now decline to start The Rise of the Zilart.\010Declining no longer forces progression to Mission 2. Re-entering Norg will continue to prompt until the Mission 1 cutscene is viewed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Rise of the Zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4844",["title"]="The Old Lady",["page_title"]="The Old Lady",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Old_Lady",["revision"]="122300",["requirements"]="Start: Vera - Mhaura Mhaura (G-10)\010Requirements: Level 18+\010Items: Wild Rabbit Tail\010Dhalmel Saliva\010Bloody Robe",["rewards"]="Ability to use Support Job\0105 Mog Wardrobe [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Fulfill her request if you want the promised rewards.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Isacio Selbina (G-10) Selbina to activate quest Elder Memories or talk to Vera Mhaura (G-10) Mhaura to activate quest The Old Lady.\010\010Once one quest is active the other can never be activated.\010\010Both quests have varied objectives but will result in the same reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you talked to Vera, obtain Wild Rabbit Tail, Dhalmel Saliva, and Bloody Robe.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade in the items to the respective NPCs to unlock Support Job access for player.\010\010You will not be able to change your Support Job until after changing zones.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3161",["title"]="The Old Monument",["page_title"]="The Old Monument",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Old_Monument",["revision"]="103264",["requirements"]="Start: Mertaire \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (I-8)\010Level: 30\010Items: Parchment",["rewards"]="Poetic Parchment",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Copy the lyrics from the ancient monument to a sheet of parchment.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="This quest is hidden and cannot be seen in your quest list until completed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Mertaire inside the Merry Minstrel Meadhouse at Lower Jeuno (I-8), who will lament on a lost love.\010\010OPTIONAL: Talk to Mataligeat at the counter for a related observation.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Bki Tbujhja, behind the counter in the same room, who talks about the Song Runes in Buburimu Peninsula and how it would cheer up the broken-hearted.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Parchment and Head to Buburimu Peninsula\010\010If you do not have enough skill to craft a Parchment, you can buy one for around 2000 gil from Pikini-Mikini, found at the Warehouse in Mhaura.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On the western edge of the Khoonta Dunes (beach), there is a hidden path in the shallows Buburimu Peninsula (G-10) that takes you to Buburimu Peninsula (G-9)/Buburimu Peninsula (F-9).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click the Song Runes, on the west side up from the beach for a cutscene with Lewenhart.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Parchment to the the Song Runes to obtain the Poetic Parchment.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This completes this quest and can be verified in your Jeuno: Completed Quests log. The next prerequisite quest for getting the Bard job is A Minstrel in Despair.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_10194",["title"]="The Opo-opo and I",["page_title"]="The Opo-opo and I",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Opo-opo_and_I",["revision"]="113541",["requirements"]="Start: Lulupp \226\128\148 Kazham (G-7)\010Fame: Kazham\010Fame level: 7\010Items: Broken Mithran Rod\010Workbench\010Ten of Coins (Card)\010Sands of Silence\010Wandering Bulb\010Giant Fish Bones\010Blackened Toad\010Wyvern Skull\010Ancient Salt\010Lucky Egg\010Previous: Even More Gullible's Travels",["rewards"]="Opo-opo Crown\010Pamamas",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The Opo-opo in Kazham love your new \034fragrance.\034 Bring them what they want--in the correct order-- and they will make you their king!",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Once you have received the scent from Even More Gullible's Travels, speak with Lulupp the Opo-opo on the airship dock (G-7), where you will be introduced to Vuih Stecoppah in the cutscene.\010\010You must trade the following items to the corresponding Opo-opos in the correct order:\010\010Serious Note: Failure to trade in correct order will result in the loss of all previously traded items, and you must start from the beginning. \010HXI Note: The text response is always the same. Don't stress if they don't say exactly what's in the text below. \010\0101. Lulupp (G-7) on lower dock, near Dheo Nbolo.\010\010Broken Mithran Rod - Can be obtained by breaking a Mithran Fishing Rod through fishing, or purchased from the Auction House.\010\010See Breaking the Rod for tips & tricks.\010\010Says \034Opopopopo! Opo-opo! Oppo! Oppo-opo!\034\010\0102. Kukupp (I-11) in-between Migho's & Pakhroib's Residences.\010\010Workbench - Can be crafted using Woodworking (7), or bought from the Auction House.\010\010Says \034Opoh opo!\034\010\0103. Mumupp (J-9) inside Wahcondalo's Residence.\010\010Ten of Coins (Card) - Obtained from Ten of Coins in the Outer Horutoto Ruins, or bought from the Auction House.\010\010Says \034Opopoppo!\034\010\0104. Roropp (H-9) in-between Poshei's Combat Gear and Ryuhkow\226\128\153a Mercenary Merchandise.\010\010Sands of Silence - Obtained from Demon Magistrates and Demon Chancellors in Castle Zvahl Baileys, or bought from the Auction House.\010\010Says \034Oh! Ohpo!\034\010\0105. Popopp (H-9) with Nomad Moogle.\010\010Wandering Bulb - Obtained from Utukkus in Fei'Yin, or bought from the Auction House.\010\010Says \034Opopoh-o...\034\010\0106. Bubupp (I-8) behind M&P's Market.\010\010Giant Fish Bones RareExclusive - Obtained from Tonberry Stalkers in the Temple of Uggalepih.\010\010Says \034Popo-o Popo-o!\034\010\0107. Tatapp (G/H/I7-10) wandering around.\010\010Blackened Toad - Obtained from Brook Sahagins in the Sea Serpent Grotto, or bought from the Auction House.\010\010Says \034Poppo-opo!\034\010\0108. Kakapp (J-9) inside Wahcondalo\226\128\153s Residence.\010\010Wyvern Skull RareExclusive [Horizon change] - Obtained from Hurricane Wyverns in Ifrit's Cauldron.\010\010Says \034Po-oppo Opo-opo!\034\010\0109. Lalapp (F-9) Chocobo NPC, behind the hut.\010\010Ancient Salt RareExclusive - Obtained from Sand Diggers in the Quicksand Caves.\010\010Says \034Opo-opo-po-opo-o! Popopo-opopo!\034\010\01010. Nenepp (H-11) behind Mihgo\226\128\153s Residence; can be out of reach; wait for it to walk closer.\010\010Lucky Egg RareExclusive - Obtained from Knight Crawlers in The Boyahda Tree.\010\010Says \034Ohpo-opo! Poh-opo-o!\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Kazham",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6868",["title"]="The Pickpocket",["page_title"]="The Pickpocket",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Pickpocket",["revision"]="99223",["requirements"]="Start: Miene \226\128\148 Port San d'Oria (I-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1",["rewards"]="Light Axe",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Retrieve the gilt glasses stolen by the pickpocket.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speaking with the little elvaan girl, Miene, will activate a cutscene. You will see a burglar steal something from Altiret, one of the guards.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene ends, speak with Altiret. He asks you to retrieve his wife's glasses for him, since he cannot leave his post.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Miene again to get a quest item Eagle Button.\010\010Informational: You can talk to nearby guards and by-standers, some will report having seen the thief allowing you to pick up the trail.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to West Ronfaure (F-6). You will find Esca in the tower there. Speak with her, and she will deny any accusation, demanding proof.",["zone"]="West Ronfaure",["grid"]="F-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Esca the Eagle Button and she will admit her guilt. She then gives you the Gilt Glasses.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Port San d'Oria and trade the Gilt Glasses to Altiret for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_334",["title"]="The Pirates' Cove (Bastok Mission 6-2)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 6-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_6-2",["revision"]="119239",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 6-1|Return of the Talekeeper",["rewards"]="Rank 7\01040,000 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You are being sent to Norg as an emissary of Bastok. Meet Sir Naji in front of the President's Office for a full briefing.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Donate 18-21 crystals to a Conquest representative if unable to receive mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to a Gate Guard to accept the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Naji for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Norg and speak with Gilgamesh. Continue speaking with him until he mentions Frag Rocks.\010\010Note:You can only open the Oaken Door to reach Gilgamesh after starting Rise of the Zilart Missions. If you skipped ZM1 upon zoning into Norg, you will be unable to complete the mission until you re-zone and accept starting Rise of the Zilart, but anyone can receive a Frag Rock if someone else pops the NM.\010\010Note:You will receive up to 6 Frag Rocks per fight. Obtain one Adaman Ore for every 6 players in your party/alliance.\010\010These can be obtained from the Auction House under Materials>Smithing.\010https://horizonffxi.wiki/w/images/c/c5/IfritsCauldron1.png",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Yhoator Jungle (I-5) and enter Ifrit's Cauldron. The ??? isn't too far inside. You may need use Sneak and Invisible to get there, as there are bats and bombs in the way.",["zone"]="Yhoator Jungle",["grid"]="I-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head left at the first intersection, and then the next right. The ??? is in a lava flow area around (H-7), Map 1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Buff up and prepare for a fight against a Lizard and Bomb NM. Barfira is recommended.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade an Adaman Ore to the ???. This will spawn Magma (Bomb) and Salamander (lizard). Sneak pulling is recommended, as you only need to defeat the bomb, and you do not need to wait for the lizard to depop - however, Magma will aggro immediately and likely result in the spawner losing Sneak. Salamander is immune to Sleep. Magma can, rarely, use Self-Destruct.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon defeating Magma, it will drop 6 Rare/Ex Frag Rocks. If doing this fight for more than 6 people, you will need to spawn them again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When everyone has their Frag Rock, head back to Norg and trade it to Gilgamesh for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Naji for a final cutscene and your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2475",["title"]="The Postman Always K.O.s Twice",["page_title"]="The Postman Always K.O.s Twice",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Postman_Always_K.O.s_Twice",["revision"]="123259",["requirements"]="Start: Ambrosius \226\128\148 Windurst Walls (J-12)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Damp Envelope\010Muddy Bar Tab\010Odd Postcard\010Torn Epistle",["rewards"]="50 - 500 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="The auction house's postman was knocked out by a monster (again). Ambrosius, who runs the auction house, wants help in recovering all the mail that was lost.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Return the following dropped Letters to Ambrosius, who will reward you.\010\010Muddy Bar Tab drops off of Savanna Rarabs in East Sarutabaruta.\010\010Torn Epistle drops off of Savanna Rarabs in West Sarutabaruta.\010\010Odd Postcard and Damp Envelope drop off Canyon Rarabs in Tahrongi Canyon.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Turn in one letter for 50 gil, two for 150 gil, three for 250 gil, or all four for 500 gil. (This is not cumulative -- the items must all be turned in at the same time for the reward fee to \034stack\034; otherwise, the reward is 50 gil.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="use 'Trade' from the menu, don't just talk to him.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_52035",["title"]="The Potential Within",["page_title"]="The Potential Within",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Potential_Within",["revision"]="101592",["requirements"]="Start: Jaucribaix - Norg (K-8)\010Requirements: Samurai 71+\010Great Katana Skill 250+\010Items: Tachi of Trials\010\010Key item: Weapon Training Guide\010Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth\010Key item: Annals of Truth",["rewards"]="The weapon skill Tachi: Kasha",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Use the katana given to you by Jaucribaix to find your true potential. When the blade has lost its power, then you will know you have been accepted.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Jaucribaix in Norg as Samurai level 71+ to receive the Tachi of Trials and a Key item: Weapon Training Guide.\010\010Your Great Katana skill must be at base 250 or higher. Gear and merits do not count towards your skill when activating this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the Tachi of Trials until the latent effect disappears. \010\010You must perform Weapon Skills and Skillchains on monsters that directly grant experience points.\010\010Weapon Skills performed under Level Sync count.\010\010Weapon Skills performed in Reives will count.\010\010You receive 1 point for opening/soloing a weapon skill, 2 points for closing a Lv.1 Skillchain, 3 points for closing a Lv.2 Skillchain and 5 points for closing a level 3 skillchain.\010\010You must accumulate 300 total points.\010\010The latent effect vanishes when you have accumulated 300 WS points. You do not need to unequip and reequip the weapon for the latent effect to disappear.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you no longer receive the latent effect, head back to Norg and trade the Tachi of Trials back to Jaucribaix. The weapon is lost and you receive a Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth and instructions to head to Kuftal Tunnel.\010\010NOTE:You can be any job from this part forward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in Kuftal Tunnel go to (L-7) on the map to the right and click the ??? to spawn the NM named Kettenkaefer.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the NM is dead, reexamine the ??? to obtain the Key item: Annals of Truth.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring this back to Jaucribaix for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57447",["title"]="The Prankster",["page_title"]="The Prankster",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Prankster",["revision"]="121563",["requirements"]="Start: Ahaadah \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-6) / Map 1\010Requirements: Access to Aht Urhgan Whitegate\010Fame: None\010Items: None",["rewards"]="Map of Caedarva Mire",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Alcander and Ahaadah want you to help Tinga-Matonga become a respectable citizen.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Ahaadah at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-6) / Map 1 to begin the quest.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="G-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Walk beneath the roofed stall at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-11) / Map 1 to trigger a cutscene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-11 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue to the end of the upper walkway at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-12) / Map 1 to trigger another cutscene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-12 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Bhaflau Thickets through the northern exit from Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-7) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="H-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the ??? among the grass at Bhaflau Thickets (I-8) / Map 1 for a cutscene.\010\010 Plague Chigoe appears when the cutscene ends.",["zone"]="Bhaflau Thickets",["grid"]="I-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Plague Chigoe.\010\010 It has a 75% Triple Attack rate.\010\010 Its additional effect normally drains MP equal to 1% of the target's maximum MP.\010\010 When the target is not already afflicted, there is a 5% chance for the additional effect to inflict Plague instead.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the ??? again after defeating Plague Chigoe to complete the quest and receive the Map of Caedarva Mire.\010\010 You do not need to return to Ahaadah.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_343",["title"]="The Price of Peace (Windurst Mission 1-3)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 1-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_1-3",["revision"]="113697",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Previous: Windurst Mission 1-2|The Heart of the Matter",["rewards"]="Rank 2\0101,000 gil\010Windurstian Ring [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Recieve two bags of food offerings from the Rhinostery, and deliver one bag to each of the Yagudo who stand by the altars of offerings in Giddeus. Don't forget to report back to the Rhinostery after completing the mission.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="NOTE: You are not eligible to skip missions by trading crystals until reaching Rank 2 or higher.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Windurst",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to any Windurst Gate Guard to accept the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the Rhinostery at Windurst Waters (J-9) / South and talk to Leepe-Hoppe at the top of the building (take the side stairs).",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="J-9 / South",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Receive a Key item: Food Offering and a Key item: Drink Offering to deliver to Giddeus. \010\010Optional: Speak with Ohbiru-Dohbiru inside the Rhinostery.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Giddeus",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Giddeus via West Sarutabaruta, (West Sarutabaruta (F-8)).\010\010If you already have the warp, the Outpost at (West Sarutabaruta (H-6)) is the fastest access point.",["zone"]="West Sarutabaruta",["grid"]="F-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow the path, always turning left at each intersection, until reaching (Giddeus (H-7) / Ground Level).",["zone"]="Giddeus",["grid"]="H-7 / Ground Level",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Give the Key item: Food Offering to the Yagudo, Laa Mozi, at the cave entrance.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back along the same path, still making left turns, until you reach (Giddeus (G-7) / Ground Level) and give the Key item: Drink Offering to Ghoo Pakya.",["zone"]="Giddeus",["grid"]="G-7 / Ground Level",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Windurst",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the roof of the Rhinostery to trigger a cutscene with Leepe-Hoppe. \010\010Optional: Speak with Leepe-Hoppe for extra dialog.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Report to any Windurst Gate Guard to complete the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57445",["title"]="The Prince and the Hopper",["page_title"]="The Prince and the Hopper",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Prince_and_the_Hopper",["revision"]="122306",["requirements"]="Start: Maudaal \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (E-9) / Map 1\010Requirements: Access to Aht Urhgan Whitegate\010Fame: None\010Items: None",["rewards"]="Chanoix's Gorget",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Professor Clavauert B Chanoix has hired you to escort him and his guinea toad, Salwa-Molwa, into Mamook to study the elusive Poroggo.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Maudaal at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (E-9) / Map 1 and accept the request to begin the quest.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="E-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Leave Aht Urhgan Whitegate for Wajaom Woodlands through the tunnel at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-10) / Map 1 to trigger a cutscene while zoning.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel through Wajaom Woodlands and enter Mamook from the cave at Wajaom Woodlands (D-12).",["zone"]="Wajaom Woodlands",["grid"]="D-12",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Toad's Footprint at Mamook (J-7) / Map 1 for a sequence of cutscenes.",["zone"]="Mamook",["grid"]="J-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head west to the passage beside the small pond at Mamook (G-7) / Map 1 and check the second Toad's Footprint for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Mamook",["grid"]="G-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Toad's Footprint a second time to begin the encounter.\010\010 The encounter consists of Poroggo Casanova and five helper toads:\010\010 Mikilulu\010\010 Mikiruru\010\010 Nikilulu\010\010 Mikiluru\010\010 Mikirulu\010\010 Defeating Poroggo Casanova advances the quest and causes all five helpers to despawn. The helpers do not need to be defeated.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After defeating Poroggo Casanova, check the Toad's Footprint again for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Maudaal at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (E-9) / Map 1 to complete the quest and receive Chanoix's Gorget.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="E-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2523",["title"]="The Promise",["page_title"]="The Promise",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Promise",["revision"]="121047",["requirements"]="Start: Kohlo-Lakolo \226\128\148 Port Windurst (G-5)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 6\010Items: Shoalweed\010Previous: Wild Card",["rewards"]="Promise Badge",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="To help the Joker Cardian escape far away from Windurst, the Star Onion Brigade wants you to have Pichichi's mother, Chamama, make him an \034Invisible Man Sticker.\034",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Kohlo-Lakolo to start the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Pichichi's mother Chamama at the Rarab Tail Hostelry in the northern map of Windurst Waters at Windurst Waters (F-10) / North.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="F-10 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Chamama says she will make an Key item: Invisible Man Sticker, but that you must get her a clump of Shoalweed first.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Shoalweed is rare/Ex and can be found by killing Recluse Spiders in Kuftal Tunnel. \010\010Recluse Spiders can be found on the main map next to the exit to Cape Teriggan. Watch out for Robber Crabs roaming around, which aggro any level. The worms in the area do not aggro.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade her the Shoalweed for an Invisible Man Sticker, and return to Kohlo-Lakolo for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you are rank 10 in Windurst, your nation is currently Windurst, and complete The Moonlit Path, you will get a key item: Dark Mana Orb. When you have that, you can talk to Kohlo-Lakolo for a final cutscene that ties together the S.O.B. quests with the Windurst mission story line.\010\010Note: If you already have rank 10 in Windurst and you have the Dark Mana Orb you must re-zone first to receive the bonus cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2480",["title"]="The Puppet Master",["page_title"]="The Puppet Master",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Puppet_Master",["revision"]="123068",["requirements"]="Start: Carbuncle \226\128\148 Windurst Walls (G-4)\010Requirements: Summoner 40+\010Items: Earth Pendulum\010Previous: I Can Hear a Rainbow",["rewards"]="Kukulcan's Staff",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="According to the words of Carbuncle, the thief that is stealing the avatars' energy from adventurers is currently in Bastok. You must travel to Bastok to confront the situation.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Go to the House of the Hero in Windurst Walls (G-4) and speak to Carbuncle as a SMN.",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="G-4",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From this point on, this quest can be complete on any job.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Port Bastok (I-8) and talk to Juroro for a cutscene, Juroro is the same NPC for titan. Ildy-Goldy hands you an Earth Pendulum and tells you to travel to the Quicksand Caves entrance in Eastern Altepa Desert (J-7).\010\010The trial-sized tuning forks can be used to reduce travel time if you want to do the fight as SMN.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Within Quicksand Caves, make your way to the Cloister of Tremors (Quicksand Caves (C-8) / Map 1). and trade the Earth Pendulum to the Earth Protocrystal. Select The Puppet Master to start the battlefield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This is an uncapped BCNM fight, buffs do not wear. You have 30 minutes to kill Galgalim (a Hecteyes NM).\010\010Galgalim can be silenced, paralyzed and slowed. Can be Reposed. Cannot be slept by a 75 BLM, resisted all sleeps, even aga's. THF75, Sleep Bolt worked just fine.\010\010Galgalim has about 3,000-3500 hp [Wiki: needs verification] .\010\010Easily soloed by any job level 70+. \010\010Easily Soloed by SMN 65+\010\010Easily Soloed by SMN 50",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If there are Multiple SMN's in the party that need this fight, you only need to do the fight once.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After defeating Galgalim, return to Port Bastok and speak with Juroro (Port Bastok (I-8)). for another cutscene. \010\010The Earth Pendulum can be tossed once you have completed the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Finally, return to Windurst Walls (Windurst Walls (E-7)) and talk to Koru-Moru to complete the quest and receive your reward.\010\010You may get dialogue relating to a different quest. You must speak to him again if he does not give you a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Summoner (SMN)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Summoner (SMN)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Kukulcan's Staff",["revision"]="16924"},{["job"]="Summoner (SMN)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="The Puppet Master",["revision"]="123068"}}},{["id"]="wiki_565",["title"]="The Pursuit of Paradise (Promathia Mission 5-3/Tenzen's Path)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 5-3/Tenzen's Path",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_5-3%2FTenzen%27s_Path",["revision"]="121178",["requirements"]="Start: Cid \226\128\148 Metalworks (H-8)\010Previous: Desires of Emptiness",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Tenzen left for the La Theine Plateau to seek out the terrestrial avatar Carbuncle, and request his assistance in your battle with the Emptiness.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Visit the ??? at (La Theine Plateau (G-6)) in La Theine Plateau where you met Carbuncle in I Can Hear a Rainbow.\010\010 PLEASE NOTE: There are at least two other cutscenes involved with this ??? that have nothing to do with this mission. If you get a cutscene here that does not include Tenzen, then you have gotten the wrong one (it was a cutscene to start the quest Waking the Beast) and are not ready to continue. Click on the ??? again until you get the proper cutscene that includes Tenzen.",["zone"]="La Theine Plateau",["grid"]="G-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="5-3T1: Spiral",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Pso'Xja from the tower at (Beaucedine Glacier (J-8)) in Beaucedine Glacier - the tower closest to Fei'Yin. Inside this tower is not a maze, but rather a gauntlet of enemies and force-spawned monsters.",["zone"]="Beaucedine Glacier",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This section of Pso'Xja has a level cap of 50.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In this tower you will encounter sixteen stone doors.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In order to pass through each of these doors you must fight a doll NM Gargoyle, after defeating it you must run through the stone door within a brief period of time (approximately 30 seconds). Everyone must pass through the door before it closes, else they will be stuck. Touching the doors from behind will warp them out of the tower. Clicking on the next door springs a trap and spawns the Gargoyle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Gargoyle mobs become progressively more and more difficult, take this into account between sections.\010\010Their max HP and attack power increase with each version.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The sixteen doors are split into four sections.\010\010The first set has only Maze Lizards, which don't aggro.\010\010The second has Blubber Eyes and Cryptonberry mobs.\010\010The third has Camazotz, Magic Millstones (pots) and Snolls during ice weather. The Camazotz may be invisible and untargetable.\010\010The fourth set has Cryptonberries.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="These mobs can and will aggro through a door. Take care to fight away from doors to avoid aggro.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Thieves can attempt to open the doors with skeleton keys in order to avoid the traps and Gargoyle battles, but they only succeed occasionally.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Occasionally, doors will have a broken trap and the Gargoyle will not spawn.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once past the final door, sneak to the elevator and past the Diremite Assaulters.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Avatar Gate (H-8) for a cutscene.\010\010PLEASE NOTE: It is completely possible to make it to the Avatar Gate without being ready to do this mission. If you get to the Avatar Gate and it does not give you a cutscene when you click it, chances are you have not talked to Carbuncle at the ??? in La Theine Plateau about this mission. (See above.)\010\010ALSO NOTE: If someone clicks back on a door to exit and leaves in the middle of your group. After completing the mission leave someone with Tractor at the elevator, go through the first 4 doors (which are easy) and have them die in the middle, and they can be Tractor'd across the gap. If someone gets left behind one room you can Provoke the Golem through the wall as well to clear the door for them.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="5-3T2: Branded",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Monberaux in the Upper Jeuno hospital (Upper Jeuno (G-10)). Obtain: Envelope from Monberaux",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Pherimociel in the Guard Post of the Ducal Palace, Ru'Lude Gardens (Ru'Lude Gardens (G-6)) to get a cutscene involving Wolfgang.",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="G-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Monberaux again. (no cutscene)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="5-3T3: Pride and Honor",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Walk out of Upper Jeuno into Batallia Downs and out through the gate in the wall. Turn left and examine the ??? twice, once for a cutscene and then a second time for a key item Delkfutt Recognition Device.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Lower Delkfutt's Tower and head to the North Cermet Door at (H-5) (Lower Delkfutt's Tower (H-5)) on the first floor. This is not the gate that leads to the basement, but rather one on the north side of the same level.",["zone"]="Lower Delkfutt's Tower",["grid"]="H-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Touch the gate to spawn a NM Disaster Idol, a doll which casts spells which vary depending upon the elemental day. It is susceptible to Blind, Poison and the elemental debuffs, but resists Elegy, Requiem, Silence, Stun, and Flash. Since it resists Stun, it probably does not use Meltdown. It is exceptionally easy on Lightsday (only casts Banish and buff spells) and extremely difficult on Lightningsday (casts Thundaga III, Thunder IV, etc.) Choose the day on which you fight it wisely. He is also suceptible to Gravity, which can help in kiting to avoid the dangerious moves.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the gate after the fight for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="5-3T4: And the Compass Guides",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Pso'Xja, entering the tower closest to Batallia Downs at (Beaucedine Glacier (H-10)). This area is uncapped.",["zone"]="Beaucedine Glacier",["grid"]="H-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Get to the elevator in the middle of the verticle maze. \010\010Use Silent Oil and Prism Powder here.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow the WALL on your RIGHT all the way around the outside of the map until you get back to (I-8),\010\010then turn WEST and DROP DOWN. at (I-8),\010\010After the DROP DOWN go SOUTH into a hallway which leads to the next room, then turn RIGHT to FACE NORTH. \010The elevator should be visible.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you reach the Elevator MAKE SURE that you have Sneak and invisible up as again there are Diremites, Pots and a Goblin at the bottom.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Avatar Gate for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Cid in Metalworks for a cutscene.\010\010If Tenzen's Path is your final path to complete on mission 5-3, you will get an additional cutscene at Cid that leads into the next mission, if not, head to another fork.\010\010! colspan=\0343\034 | Three Paths Overview\010|- class=\034copmissions-alt\034\010! Fork 1\010! Fork 2\010! Fork 3\010|-\010|align=\034center\034 | Tenzen Path\010|align=\034center\034 | Ulmia Path\010|align=\034center\034 | Louverance Path",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7501",["title"]="The Quadav's Curse",["page_title"]="The Quadav's Curse",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Quadav%27s_Curse",["revision"]="104181",["requirements"]="Start: Corann \226\128\148 Port Bastok (K-6)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Quadav Backplate x 1",["rewards"]="Bronze Subligar",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Corann wants to shut himself away from the rest of the world. Find him an item to hide in -- something big enough to hide his whole body.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Corann inside the house at Port Bastok (K-6). He's got a phobia about going outside, but he thinks that if you brought him something large to hide in it would help.",["zone"]="Port Bastok",["grid"]="K-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Taking a hint from the name of the quest, obtain a Quadav Backplate and trade it to Corann to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4814",["title"]="The Real Gift",["page_title"]="The Real Gift",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Real_Gift",["revision"]="8503",["requirements"]="Start: Oswald - Selbina (I-9)\010Requirements: Selbina/Rabao Reputation ?\010Items: Shall Shell\010Previous: The Gift\010The Sand Charm",["rewards"]="Glass Fiber Fishing Rod",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Oswald to begin the quest. He will ask you for a Shall Shell. He might also ask for a danceshroom instead.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Oswald a Shall Shell to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="OPTIONAL: After receiving your reward, talk with Oswald again for an epilogue.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Note: No zoning is needed between Under the Sea, The Gift and The Real Gift.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Note: The quest The Sand Charm needs to be completed before this quest can be flagged.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Oswald (Shepherd's Muster, Selbina)\010 / summary=With his girlfriend still in the doldrums, Oswald wants to give her a pearl necklace. Find him a shall shell so he can make one.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5952",["title"]="The Requiem",["page_title"]="The Requiem",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Requiem",["revision"]="120327",["requirements"]="Start: Bki Tbujhja \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (H-8))\010Requirements: Bard 50+\010Items: Holy Water\010Key item: Star ring\010Previous: Painful Memory",["rewards"]="Choral Slippers",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="A certain post is rotated at the meadhouse. Now, it's your turn.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must be on BRD to activate the cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Bki Tbujhja in the Merry Minstrel, in Lower Jeuno (Lower Jeuno (H-8)) who asks for a vial of Holy Water.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Bki Tbujhja the Holy Water and she will inform you that you need to pay your respects to the Bard of yesteryear. She returns the Holy Water and directs you to pour the flask onto a sarcophagus in The Eldieme Necropolis. \010\010OPTIONAL: Speak to Mataligeat on the other side of the counter from Bki Tbujhja for some insight about this bard, and how he came to a horrible end.\010From this point on, the quest can be completed on any (presumably higher-level) job.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Beaucedine Glacier then zone into the isolated area of Batallia Downs at (Beaucedine Glacier (H-11)). Once there, enter the Eldieme Necropolis via the entrance at (Batallia Downs (F-5)).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to the dead-end room filled with five sarcophagi at (The Eldieme Necropolis (D-4) / Map 2). When ready, trade the vial of Holy Water to one of the sarcophagi to spawn three Skeleton Notorious Monsters: A Black Mage, Yum Kimil, and two Warriors, Owl Guardian and Dog Guardian.\010\010The sarcophagus you need to trade to is random.\010\010Like all skeletons, only light based sleep will work (Lullaby, Sheep Song, etc.). Yum Kimil cannot be slept. \010\010Spawning them while sneaked will not prevent aggro.\010\010A party will only need to kill the NMs once.\010\010If you zone or die after popping them, the rest of your party can pull one at a time.\010\010It isn't necessary to kill all three NMs. If you pull one NM and then wait for the other two to despawn before killing it, you only need to fight one.\010\010If you are defeated, immediately touching the Sarcophagus will result in \034Nothing Happens\034. Wait a few minutes and when you touch it again the NMs will respawn. You do not need to trade another Holy Water. If you already killed Yum Kimil, you will get the cutscene and your reward instead.",["zone"]="The Eldieme Necropolis",["grid"]="D-4 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once they have been defeated, re-investigate the same sarcophagus onto which you poured the Holy Water for a cutscene and the Key item: Star ring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Lower Jeuno and talk with Bki Tbujhja to complete the quest.\010\010OPTIONAL: Speak to Mataligeat again for a bit of admonishment.\010NOTE: If you've just completed The Requiem on another job, you can save a bit of time and immediately flag The Circle of Time with Mertaire while on that job.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="For strategy information see testimonials.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Yum Kimil has approximately 8000 HP.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Owl Guardian has approximately 5800 HP.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Dog Guardian has approximately 6000 HP.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Yum Kimil can be silenced.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Yum Kimil has a powerful innate Enfire, Barfire is recommended.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Bard (BRD)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Bard (BRD)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Choral Slippers",["revision"]="21433"},{["job"]="Bard (BRD)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="The Requiem",["revision"]="120327"}}},{["id"]="wiki_15671",["title"]="The Rescue",["page_title"]="The Rescue",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Rescue",["revision"]="49546",["requirements"]="Start: Thunder Hawk - Selbina (G-9)\010Requirements: Selbina/Rabao Reputation\010Items: Quadav Charm",["rewards"]="Map of the Ranguemont Pass\0103,000g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Rescue two merchants from captivity. They should be somewhere in the Quadav camp of Beadeaux.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Thunder Hawk wants you to rescue two merchants who were kidnapped by Quadav and being held at the jail in Beadeaux.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Beadeaux (I-8).\010\010 Note: If you check the ???, it says \034A piece of parchment has been nailed here.\034 If you select \034Yes.\034 to the choice whether to read the parchment or not, it reads: Mrahcva dauqe htsi yekllec eht. Vada uqons naem dnuos on. Read backwards (and respaced,) it translates to: \034The cell key is the quadav charm. No sound means no quadav.\034",["zone"]="Beadeaux",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To get into the jail cell, you first need to get a Quadav Charm which drops from De'Vyu Headhunter (I-9) of Beadeaux.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you get the item, trade it to the jail door at (I-8) (You will need to drop to reach the door) and trigger a cutscene with the merchants Serafin and Evrard. They will give you the Key item: Trader's Sack to return to Thunder Hawk.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Thunder Hawk to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_364",["title"]="The Rescue Drill (San d'Oria Mission 2-1)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 2-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_2-1",["revision"]="119444",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 1-3|Save the Children",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Participate in the Temple Knights' rescue drill out on La Theine Plateau.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 2 Crystals to any San d'Orian Conquest Overseer to unlock this mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to any San d'Oria Gate Guard and accept the mission from the list.\010\010A Map of La Theine Plateau and Ordelle's Caves can be purchased from the Map NPC's in Northern San d'Oria and Southern San d'Oria, but it is not required.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to La Theine Plateau and speak to Galaihaurat at La Theine Plateau (E-6), standing at the edge of a stone wall.",["zone"]="La Theine Plateau",["grid"]="E-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Descend into the fissure at La Theine Plateau (F-6) from the east side. Equesobillot will be at the start of the decent. Continue down the slope and then south to Ordelle's Caves. \010\010Optional: Talk to Vicorpasse for mission context. Talk to the other NPCs, Equesobillot, Deaufrain, Augevinne, Yaucevouchat, Laurisse, and Narvecaint for additional dialogue.\010\010Tip: Be careful of the Funguars as they will aggro you by sound if you are doing this mission at low level. Silent Oils are not necessary as long as you are patient since there is plenty of space to avoid them. To add, while it is excessive, doing this quest right after Japanese Midnight will almost guarantee that some kind adventurer will pass by and revive you in this otherwise low traffic area because of Eco-Warrior (San d'Oria).",["zone"]="La Theine Plateau",["grid"]="F-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you are inside Ordelle's Caves, follow the left wall until you come to Ordelle's Caves (G-3) \226\128\148 Map 2, where there is a small pond. Talk to Ruillont crouching behind a stalagmite.",["zone"]="Ordelle's Caves",["grid"]="G-3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return the way you came to La Theine Plateau. One of three NPCs at random will give you Ruillont's Bronze Sword if you talk to them, in order from closest to furthest: Either Deaufrain, Equesobillot, and if unfortunate, Galaihaurat by the road.\010\010Tip: You cannot prepare a Bronze Sword beforehand and hand it to Ruillont, for he will reject it saying it's not his sword. Once one of the three NPCs hands you his sword, then you are able to trade a different Bronze Sword to Ruillont. This impractical option exists as a way to save a player who might have accidentally lost the sword given from the NPCs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Ruillont at Ordelle's Caves (G-3) \226\128\148 Map 2 and trade him the sword.",["zone"]="Ordelle's Caves",["grid"]="G-3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back to La Theine Plateau and talk to Vicorpasse at La Theine Plateau (F-6) for Rescue Training Certificate.",["zone"]="La Theine Plateau",["grid"]="F-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to a San d'Oria Gate Guard to complete the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7520",["title"]="The Return of the Adventurer",["page_title"]="The Return of the Adventurer",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Return_of_the_Adventurer",["revision"]="104282",["requirements"]="Start: Gwill \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (E-11)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Cinnamon x 1\010Previous: Father Figure",["rewards"]="Cotton Headband",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Gwill needs some cinnamon to put the final touch on a present he's making for Dalzakk.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Gwill.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Cinnamon to Gwill.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_523",["title"]="The Rites of Life (Promathia Mission 1-1)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 1-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_1-1",["revision"]="116982",["requirements"]="Start: N/A",["rewards"]="Key item: Mysterious Amulet",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Brilliant lights, fearsome beasts, a mysterious laboratory... What do all these have to do with the strange boy brought back to Doctor Monberaux's clinic in Upper Jeuno?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Players may now decline to start Chains of Promathia without being forced into the opening cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To start this mission, enter Lower Delkfutt's Tower for a cutscene after installing the Chains of Promathia expansion pack.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene has finished, enter Upper Jeuno for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the second cutscene finishes, speak to Monberaux (Upper Jeuno (G-10), inside the Infirmary) for final cutscene and a Key item: Mysterious Amulet.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="G-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Important note* There are still two more people in Jeuno that you will need to speak to during the next mission.\010\010[Template Mission/Description: orders = Brilliant lights, fearsome beasts, a mysterious laboratory... What do all these have to do with the strange boy brought back to Doctor Monberaux's clinic in Upper Jeuno?]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7435",["title"]="The Rivalry",["page_title"]="The Rivalry",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Rivalry",["revision"]="60838",["requirements"]="Start: Gallijaux \226\128\148 Port San d'Oria (H-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Moat Carp and/or Forest Carp x10,000",["rewards"]="Lu Shang's Fishing Rod\010Key item: Testimonial\01010g per Moat Carp\01015g per Forest Carp\010(Average 100,000 - 150,000 total gil)",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Catch moat carp by any means possible so Gallijaux can win a fishing contest against his little brother, Joulet.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Gallijaux to begin The Rivalry.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade 10,000 Moat Carps and/or Forest Carps to him.\010\010You can talk to either brother to see which one you've agreed to help.\010\010You can trade multiple stacks at a time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You receive 10 gil for each Moat Carp and 15 gil for every Forest Carp.\010\010To learn your current total of fish, speak with Ufanne, who stands watch behind the two bickering fishermen. You may need to talk to the latter multiple times before she'll tell you.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will get Lu Shang's Fishing Rod and the Key item: Testimonial upon trading the 10,000th carp.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_11806",["title"]="The Road to Aht Urhgan",["page_title"]="The Road to Aht Urhgan",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Road_to_Aht_Urhgan",["revision"]="122012",["requirements"]="Start: Faursel \226\128\148 Tenshodo, Lower Jeuno (J-8)\010Requirements: Tenshodo Membership\010Level: 30 [Horizon change]\010Items: 0, 1, 2, 3, 6, or 8 access items, based on final Imperial Relief Effort tier",["rewards"]="Key item: Boarding Permit",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="If you want to ride the mercenary transport ship from Mhaura, you must obtain a boarding permit from the Tenshodo.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Faursel inside Neptune's Spire in Lower Jeuno at Lower Jeuno (J-8).",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select the hidden third option during the first cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Faursel again and choose either the hidden third option or the first option.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Your final Imperial Standing total earned through the now-ended Imperial Relief Effort determines your Boarding Permit requirement and temporary launch benefits.\010\010 The event total is locked. Imperial Standing earned after the event ended does not improve this launch-access tier.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the highest threshold you reached in the table below.\010\010 The 5,000 and 10,000 IS tiers require no access items.\010\010 Lower tiers may turn in the required number of different items from the eight access items; no specific subset is required.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If access items are required, obtain the needed items from level 30 or higher monsters.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the required access items to Faursel, then complete his remaining dialogue to receive the Key item: Boarding Permit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="ToAU",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2752",["title"]="The Root of the Problem",["page_title"]="The Root of the Problem",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Root_of_the_Problem",["revision"]="110073",["requirements"]="Start: Chumimi \226\128\148 Heavens Tower / Basement\010Requirements: Black Mage Level: 50+\010Items: Silk Cloth\010Previous: Recollections",["rewards"]="Wizard's Petasos",["repeatable"]="af",["summary"]="The cause of the star trees' poor growth seems to lie in the Toraimarai Canal. First, bring some silk cloth to Professor Koru-Moru so he can improve his magic doll. Then take the magic doll into the Toraimarai Canal to carry out an inspection.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Chumimi in Heavens Tower to get a cutscene. Zoning out of Heavens Tower is required after finishing the Recollections quest. You will need to be Black Mage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Then talk to Koru-Moru at (Windurst Walls (E-7)) in Windurst Walls and trade him a Silk Cloth.",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go back to Chumimi for another cutscene. You will receive a Key item: Sluice Surveyor Mark I, which is a magic doll.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head into Toraimarai Canal via the Three Mage Gate, or through Windurst Walls if you have the Key item: Rhinostery Certificate.\010\010You must stay on BLM while investigating the first two ???s. At one point the magic doll will tell you to use your \034BLACK POWER,\034 and you will need to use Manafont. You can change to any job afterwards.\010\010 Tractor doesn't work to by-pass the Rhino gate. The other side of the gate is protected from it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Black Mage (BLM)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Black Mage (BLM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Wizard's Petasos",["revision"]="18811"},{["job"]="Black Mage (BLM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="The Root of the Problem",["revision"]="110073"}}},{["id"]="wiki_371",["title"]="The Ruins of Fei'Yin (San d'Oria Mission 5-1)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 5-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_5-1",["revision"]="116593",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Level: 50\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 4-1|Magicite",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="This mission involves traveling to Fei'Yin, located on the Beaucedine Glacier. Visit Chateau d'Oraguille to learn more.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Head to Chateau d'Oraguille for a cut-scene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cut-scene, you must speak with Halver before you can continue.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Visit a San d'Oria Gate Guard and accept the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Halver, and he will give you the Key item: New Fei'Yin Seal.\010\010[Template :Nation Mission 5-1: ]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Finishing the Mission",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Halver to complete the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1479",["title"]="The Rumor",["page_title"]="The Rumor",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Rumor",["revision"]="113740",["requirements"]="Start: Novalmauge \226\128\148 Bostaunieux Oubliette (G-8)\010Requirements: Access to Chateau d'Oraguille\010Level: 10\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Beastman Blood",["rewards"]="Scroll of Drain",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The jailer wants you to bring him the blood of a beastman. Some people say he is a vampire.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must be Rank 2 or higher in San d'Oria or on Mission 2-3 or higher in Windurst or Bastok to pass through Chateau d'Oraguille and enter Bostaunieux Oubliette.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon entering the Chateau d'Oraguille, go east through an open door, north down a corridor, and down curving stairs to Bostaunieux Oubliette (I-8). Zone through to the Oubliette.",["zone"]="Bostaunieux Oubliette",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel straight south to Bostaunieux Oubliette (H-8), and turn right (West). You will find Novalmauge patrolling this hallway on the south side of Bostaunieux Oubliette (F-8) to Bostaunieux Oubliette (G-8).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Novalmauge a vial of Beastman Blood.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_14707",["title"]="The Sacred Katana",["page_title"]="The Sacred Katana",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Sacred_Katana",["revision"]="32078",["requirements"]="Start: Jaucribaix \226\128\148 Norg (K-8)\010Requirements: Samurai 40+\010Items: Mumeito\010Sack of Fish Bait\010Key item: Handful of Crystal Scales\010Previous: Forge Your Destiny",["rewards"]="Magoroku",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="Your mumeito and a handful of crystal scales are needed to forge a katana that will be used in a Norg ritual.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Jaucribaix in Norg (K-8) as a Samurai; he asks you to bring him the Mumeito he gave you when you became a Samurai and a Key item: Handful of Crystal Scales.\010\010If you dropped the Mumeito, Ranemaud will sell you another one for 30,000 gil after you accept the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Sack of Fish Bait from Goblin Robbers in the Sanctuary of Zi'Tah.\010\010Many Goblin Robbers can be found at (H-8) north of the outpost.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Sack of Fish Bait to the ??? at (E-8) near a lake in the Sanctuary of Zi'Tah to spawn a pugil NM: Isonade. \010\010You can spawn this NM on any job.\010\010Use Sneak to prevent the NM from aggroing the trader.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Isonade and reexamine the ??? to obtain a Key item: Handful of Crystal Scales.\010\010If you change areas or lose connection, you will need another Sack of Fish Bait to spawn and defeat Isonade again. Be sure to check the ??? after defeating Isonade.\010\010If you have multiple people on the quest, you only need to kill Isonade once. Therefore, one Sack of Fish Bait is enough for the entire group.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Norg and trade the Mumeito to Jaucribaix to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Zilart",["jobs"]={"Samurai (SAM)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Samurai (SAM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Magoroku",["revision"]="18207"},{["job"]="Samurai (SAM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="The Sacred Katana",["revision"]="32078"}}},{["id"]="wiki_3136",["title"]="The Sahagin's Stash",["page_title"]="The Sahagin's Stash",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Sahagin%27s_Stash",["revision"]="118460",["requirements"]="Start: Laisrean \226\128\148 Norg (H-7)\010Requirements: Key item: Airship pass for Kazham\010Job level 5+\010Fame: Tenshodo\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Silver Beastcoin\010Key item: Sea Serpent Statue",["rewards"]="Scroll of Utsusemi: Ichi",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Bring back something from the Sahagins' storage area in the Sea Serpent Grotto. Anything will do.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Laisrean, behind the two shopkeepers at Norg (H-7).",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="H-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Silver Door.\010\010Exit Norg and make your way to the door at (Sea Serpent Grotto (H-6) / Map 1).\010\010Refer to the maps on the right.\010\010Head to the area at (Sea Serpent Grotto (K-8) / Map 1). The arrow indicates that you can only go one way here. Once you drop down, you can't go back the same way.\010\010Once you've dropped down, continue along the path to the door in the southeast marked Silver Door (Sea Serpent Grotto (N-14) / Map 1).\010\010If you haven't done so before, you must examine the door 6 times; the description changes each time. Eventually you receive a message saying \034you see something silver glittering around the indentation\034 in the door.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Silver Beastcoin to the door to pass through to point Silver Door on Map #2. \010\010You get to keep the Silver Beastcoin; it isn't removed from your inventory.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From here, follow the tunnel until you arrive at the cliff (Sea Serpent Grotto (H-8) / Map 2).",["zone"]="Sea Serpent Grotto",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you've dropped down the cliff, follow this tunnel to the door at (Sea Serpent Grotto (H-4, H-5) / Map 2).",["zone"]="Sea Serpent Grotto",["grid"]="H-4 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the ??? at (Sea Serpent Grotto (H-3) / Map 2) for a cutscene where you receive the Key item: Sea Serpent Statue from Ren.\010\010 If you wish to return to Norg on foot from this point, travel to A (Sea Serpent Grotto (F-7) / Map 2) on Map #2, which brings you to A (Sea Serpent Grotto (M-10) / Map 1) on Map #1. From here it's a simple walk back to Norg.\010\010You may prefer to bring some form of Warp or Escape to avoid backtracking through Sea Serpent Grotto.",["zone"]="Sea Serpent Grotto",["grid"]="H-3 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the statue back to Laisrean to receive a scroll of Utsusemi: Ichi.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Every monster in this area detects by sound, so some form of Sneak is necessary if you are low-leveled. Silent Oils work, but Circumspection (5 Tabs for Sneak/Invisible effects) from the Grounds Tome outside Norg should be sufficient. There is a second Grounds Tome at the Silver Beastcoin door, halfway to the quest destination; you can cancel and repurchase Circumspection to renew the duration. Invisible is not necessary. \010\010At level 63 there are easy prey monsters near the end that are just low enough not to aggro.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The most popular way to raise your fame for this quest is to complete the quest Mihgo's Amigo with 212 necklaces, or the Shady Business quest with ~104 ores. [Wiki: needs verification] \010\010A way to check your Norg fame without travelling to Norg is to check the price of Rice Balls with Ghebi Damomohe in Neptune's Spire. If the price of the Rice Balls are 150g or lower, you should have sufficient reputation for this quest (prices for Rice Balls may vary a little). (However, the Reputation page claims 155 or lower).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Tenshodo",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_339",["title"]="The Salt of the Earth (Bastok Mission 9-1)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 9-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_9-1",["revision"]="118188",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 8-2|Enter the Talekeeper",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have been assigned to an investigation in the Vollbow Region. Speak with senator Alois for further details.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 37 Crystal's to unlock the mission, then speak with a Gate Guard to accept it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Visit Alois in the President's Office Conference Room in Metalworks (Metalworks (J-8)).",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Rabao and speak to Dancing Wolf in (Rabao (G-7)) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Rabao",["grid"]="G-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to (Gustav Tunnel (G-6) / Map 2) on the second map in Gustav Tunnel and check the ??? located in the pond.\010\010This area is somewhat dangerous, as EVERYTHING aggros in the area. Have your party wait at (Gustav Tunnel (H-7) / Map 2), as it is safe there from aggro. Carefully Sneak pull the NM by checking the ??? and then sleeping the NM. Run back to camp. The NM will eventually make its way there.\010\010Post Rebase: Sneak pull does NOT work. The mob will begin attacking on pop.",["zone"]="Gustav Tunnel",["grid"]="G-6 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will be fighting slime NMs which have high melee resistance. Casters will be very important, and sleeping the mobs will be imperative. You will start against one Gigaplasm.\010\010Defeating the Gigaplasm will cause it to divide in two Macroplasms. Each of those will divide into two Microplasms, and those will divide into two Nanoplasms. Try to keep as many mobs asleep as you can. Commence by killing one line of Macroplasms (defeat one, defeat its microplasms, and then its nanoplasms), and then the second. Sleep repeatedly. The HP of the mobs gets progressively lower, to the point where a decently equipped BLM should be able to one-shot a Nanoplasm with a single Thunder III. The key to this fight is keeping everything asleep. \010\010Avoid giving the mobs too much TP, as they can use the typical nasty slime TP attacks, like Fluid Spread. \010\010Defeat all of them and Sneak everyone to the ???. Check it to receive the Miraclesalt.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Rabao and speak to Dancing Wolf for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Alois to finish the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4813",["title"]="The Sand Charm",["page_title"]="The Sand Charm",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Sand_Charm",["revision"]="108389",["requirements"]="Start: Blandine \226\128\148 Mhaura (I-9)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Sand Charm",["rewards"]="Map of Bostaunieux Oubliette",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Retrieve the sand charm Celestina's father carried. Your one clue: a sailor saw a pirate wearing it.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Blandine to activate the quest, then enter the docking area and talk to Zexu for a cutscene. They will mention how sad it is that Blandine is still waiting for her husband, though they heard he had an encounter with pirates and is not likely to have lived.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exit the docking area and talk to Blandine, who will have a cutscene conversation with Celestina.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go up to the Goldsmiths' Guild (Mhaura) (G-9) and talk to Celestina to accept the quest. She will ask you to obtain a Sand Charm.\010\010This quest will now appear in the Other Areas quest log.\010\010Sand Charms drop from Crossbones on the Mhaura - Selbina ferry (going either direction) when it's attacked by Pirates.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Celestina the Sand Charm to get a final cutscene and your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_554",["title"]="The Savage (Promathia Mission 4-2)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 4-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_4-2",["revision"]="118980",["requirements"]="Level: 50 Cap\010Items: Giant Scale\010Previous: Sheltering Doubt",["rewards"]="1500 Experience Points\010Mog Wardrobe 2: 3 Slots",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Ulmia is determined to know the truth, and is ready to revisit Bahamut to learn it. Enlist the aid of Tenzen and Justinius to help you find Ulmia before something terrible occurs.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Note before starting: You will NOT be able to start the weekly quest, Uninvited Guests while this mission is active",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Talk to Justinius (J-6) on the top floor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Misareaux Coast (E-6) and enter Riverne - Site B01 after a CS.",["zone"]="Misareaux Coast",["grid"]="E-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed to Monarch Linn located at Riverne - Site B01 (E-8).\010\010You'll need a Giant Scale to pass through an Unstable Displacement to get to Monarch Linn.",["zone"]="Riverne - Site B01",["grid"]="E-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the BCNM (capped at level 50) and fight Ouryu.\010\010Note: Normal buffs wear off when entering the BCNM - food will stay.\010\010After defeating Ouryu, your title will become Mist Melter.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You'll return at the exit for Monarch Linn and can either come back to the entrance of Monarch Linn or exit out.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Tavnazian Safehold and talk to Justinius again for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ouryu\010\010Ouryu is an earth-based dragon and casts Stoneskin and Stone-based damage spells.\010\010His TP attacks:\010\010On the ground:\010\010Absolute Terror: Terrorizes the target for a few seconds, making them unable do anything.\010\010Geotic Breath: Cone Attack Earth damage. ~700 damage if tank is directly in front of the dragon.\010\010Spike Flail: Only used if someone behind him has hate. Huge AoE physical damage. Absorbed by Utsusemi.\010\010Horrid Roar: Dispel up to 8 buffs on a single target, including food.\010\010Typhoon Wing: Frontal AoE ~100-180 dmg and Blind.\010\010In the air:\010\010Bai Wing: AoE Earth damage (~385 unresisted) and Slow\010\010Ochre Blast: AoE Earth 400+ damage.\010\010Touchdown: Not based on TP, used when he lands (but not if you used a Mistmelt). AoE magic damage (element unknown, ~140 each).\010He uses Invincible at about 50% - 80% HP.\010He alternates between flying and standing every two minutes.\010He also casts Stoneskin, Stonega II, and Slowga.\010On the ground, his attacks are physical; in the air, they are earth elemental and ignore Utsusemi. His air attacks do 280 damage minus Shell and any resistance; kiting may also reduce their damage.\010He gives up at about 30% health power",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring Ouryu to the ground with Mistmelt, which is obtained from the quest Fly High.\010\010Suggested to bring 6-8 Mistmelt depending on your DPS to keep him on the ground the whole fight.\010\010Suggested macro - /item \034Mistmelt\034 Ouryu\010\010When using a Mistmelt you have to be close to Ouryu (ideal position is between front legs just below the head, will not agro you if you just throw Mistmelt and don't engage it)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ouryu is a lot easier to sleep on the ground\010\0103 Blackmages with a paladin is a good setup using freeze sleep rest repeat.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After defeating Ouryu, everyone in the party that is alive gains 1500 Experience/Limit Points, regardless of whether they have completed the mission or not.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Justinius (J-6) on the top floor in Tavnazian Safehold to complete the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3691",["title"]="The Sealed Shrine (Zilart Mission 15)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 15",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_15",["revision"]="111274",["requirements"]="Start: None\010Previous: Ark Angels",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The door deep within the Shrine of Ru'Avitau is sealed with some form of supernatural power. Could this be the work of Eald'narche?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="If you completed the previous mission by way of Divine Might and have yet to choose your reward, enter the Shrine of Ru'Avitau through the (Ru'Aun Gardens (H-9)) entrance in Ru'Aun Gardens. This should force your log to change. Otherwise, simply select your earring from the location where you started Divine Might and choose your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head for Norg and speak to Gilgamesh.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Ru'Aun Gardens and zone into the Shrine of Ru'Avitau(any entrance) for a cutscene",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Rise of the Zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6857",["title"]="The Seamstress",["page_title"]="The Seamstress",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Seamstress",["revision"]="60795",["requirements"]="Start: Hanaa Punaa \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (E-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Sheepskin x 3",["rewards"]="Leather Gloves",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Collect three giant sheepskins for Hanaa, and she'll make some fine clothes for you.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Hanaa Punaa needs sheepskins to practice her skills. Trade her 3 Sheepskins for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5262",["title"]="The Search for Goldmane",["page_title"]="The Search for Goldmane",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Search_for_Goldmane",["revision"]="9202",["requirements"]="Start: Zoriboh - Rabao (F-6)/(F-7)\010Requirements: Chains of Promathia Expansion : Ancient Vows\010Items: Copper Key\010Giant Scale\010Previous: Chasing Dreams",["rewards"]="Deluxe Carbine\0103,000g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Zoriboh and agree to start the quest to receive the Care package (key item).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Tavnazian Safehold and talk with Quelveuiat ((I-10), 1st Floor near \034Altar of the Dawn\034 ) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Get a Copper Key from a Riverne Vulture in Riverne - Site #A01. You will also need to kill a Firedrake for a Giant Scale to get through the Unstable Displacements.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At Riverne - Site #A01 go through the portals to the island at I-11. You will receive a cutscene upon reaching the island. Trade the Copper Key to the Trunk (a treasure box) there for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the Bastok Metalworks upper floor and talk to Vladinek at H-8 in the Craftsmen's Eatery for a long cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Bibiki Bay and take the Manaclipper to Purgonorgo Isle. To board the Manaclipper, you need to buy a ticket from Tswe Panipahr.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There are multiple Manaclipper that go to different islands. Speak to Fheli Lapatzuo (H-7) at the docks before boarding a boat to make sure it's the correct one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the beach at F-9 by the Weathered Boat.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select the Weathered Boat for a short cutscene. The NM Rohemolipaud, an Elvaan Ranger around level 55, will spawn after the cutscene is done.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once about 1400 damage is done to him, or the fight goes on long enough, he will use Camouflage and run off, ending the fight.\010Note: If you are in a party, and have more than one party member who needs to complete the same quest, you will need to activate the NM battle for each person. You can activate the NM right after the previous person completed the long cutscene after the NM battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select the Weathered Boat again for a cutscene and your reward - Deluxe Carbine",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Finally, go back to Rabao and talk to Zoriboh to complete the quest and receive your 3000 gil.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Zoriboh (Near the oasis, Rabao)\010 / summary=How is little Sanctia doing? Zoriboh wants you to take her a present from her father and see that she is keeping out of trouble.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_376",["title"]="The Secret Weapon (San d'Oria Mission 7-2)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 7-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_7-2",["revision"]="119736",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 7-1|Prestige of the Papsque",["rewards"]="Rank 8\01060,000 gil\010Mog Wardrobe: 10 Slots",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Reports from Ghelsba indicate that the Orcs in Yughott Grotto are up to something. Investigate, but speak of this to no one.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 16~24 crystals to a Conquest NPC to unlock this mission, then speak with a San d'Oria Gate Guard, who will instruct you to go to the garden in the Chateau.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head for the Chateau d'Oraguille (F-7) and go towards (F-7). You will receive a cutscene.",["zone"]="Chateau d'Oraguille",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to the Gate Guard to receive the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="BCNM Fight",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Gather a party and head for Horlais Peak. Only people who are on 7-2 or have completed it may enter. \010\010Sandy does NOT need to be your current home nation. You just have to have previously completed the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It is recommended that you bring a BLM and/or a BRD for sleeping the mobs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Get ready and enter the BC. The fight is against 3 Orcs and 2 Orcish Warmachines:\010\010Darokbok of Clan Reaper (Level 68, PLD)\010\010Derakbak of Clan Wolf (Level 68, DRG)\010\010Jagidbod of Clan Reaper (Level 68, RNG)\010\010Wolf Clan Warmachine \010\010Reaper Clan Warmachine",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Open the fight with Elemental Seal + Sleepga II. (Sheepsong worked with Melodia as well) Fight the Warmachines first, then the Paladin, the Dragoon and Wyvern, and the Ranger last. A Melee/NIN can pretty easily solo any of the NMs. Prioritize the Warmachines.\010\010(2025-Nov-22) Soloed it as 75 BST/NIN with Reraise. Kill order is Warmachines, RNG, DRG, Dragoon pet, PLD. They don't aggro on sight, so initiate by sending sheep to one of the Warmachines, use Sheep Song and keep using Sheep Song as they wake up. Sic merits help. At some point sheep will die. You can try recovering from that by using Sheep Song + Reward, but you will probably die anyways. Just reraise (they won't aggro even if in range), heal up and use the same strategy to kill the remaining. Focusing on PLD first is a bad idea because you want to reduce number of enemies as fast as possible. PLD will use Invincible and you will get in trouble as they build resistance to Sheep Song over time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When finished, you'll receive another cutscene, and receive the Crystal Dowser.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to San d'Oria and speak to any Gate Guard to finish the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_556",["title"]="The Secrets of Worship (Promathia Mission 4-3)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 4-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_4-3",["revision"]="119451",["requirements"]="Level: 50 Cap\010Previous: The Savage",["rewards"]="Access to Sacrarium (Given at the start of the quest after interacting with the Walnut Door)",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Now that you have learned the Wyrmking's plan, you must travel to the fourth mothercrystal. Nag'molada has informed you where the stone lies. However, you will need the amulet you lent to Prishe before you are to make your way there.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Preparation",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It is highly recommended to bring at least 1 SMN that know hows to Carby pull--multiple SMN are helpful.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It's a good idea for non-casters to bring multiple stacks of Silent Oil. Sneak is needed constantly, and for almost every enemy, with the exclusion of Taurus (true sight,) and NM's.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Fomor notes: in addition to hearing, these also blood aggro and may do so through walls; try to keep away from walls if possible.\010\010Sleep does not land very reliably on Fomor but it may be worth trying if unexpected links occur.\010\010SMN Carby Pull should be your go-to choice for initiating any fight with Fomor. Each pull will link with 2+ other Fomor, and fighting 2+ of them simultaneously can be very rough. Carby pull allows you to solo pull consistently.\010\010Anyone with access to Silence should coordinate with your Carby Puller to Silence bomb any Fomor Black Mages; they can wipe parties very easily if left unchecked.\010\010Fomor have a TP move that resets party members' TP to 0 in an AoE, so melee have it a bit rough in this zone. Summoners are great for performing skillchains here!",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Highly recommended to bring one or multiple forms of Reraise, as chance of death is pretty high here.\010\010Pay attention to the last 'safe' spot where you could heal or Reraise, and be ready to run there if death/wipe is imminent.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This mission requires passing through a locked door in Sacrarium. A considerable part of the mission is farming the required keys (2x Coral Crest Key and 1x Sealion Crest Key) to open the door. Alternatively, the door can be open by someone in possession of Key item: Temple Knight Key. \010\010The Key item: Temple Knight Key can be obtained by trading 1x Coral Crest Key and 1x Sealion Crest Key to Quelveuiat in Tavnazian Safehold (I-10) / Map 1 after the quest A Hard Day's Knight has been completed. \010Before starting the mission, consider your options:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Farming 2x Coral Crest Key and 1x Sealion Crest Key.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Farming 1x Coral Crest Key and 1x Sealion Crest Key and have someone who completed A Hard Day's Knight run back to Tavnazian Safehold to obtain the Key item: Temple Knight Key.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring someone who already has a Key item: Temple Knight Key.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The final NM of this mission spawns in a room full of Fomor. Consider clearing your Fomor Hate by killing Orcs and Gigas in Misareaux Coast. Note that if you have to farm Coral Crest Keys, you will have to kill Fomor to get them, increasing your Fomor Hate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mission Start",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Justinius at Tavnazian Safehold (J-6) / Top Floor.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="J-6 / Top Floor",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On the same floor, click the Walnut Door at Tavnazian Safehold (K-7) / Top Floor, which is next to Parelbriaux, for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="K-7 / Top Floor",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Iron Gate in the northernmost part of Misareaux Coast (G-4) for a cutscene.\010\010This is the entrance to the Sacrarium. This area is capped at level 50.",["zone"]="Misareaux Coast",["grid"]="G-4",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon entering Sacrarium, proceed to Sacrarium (J-10) / Map 1 (Connection 'B'). \010\010Note that the maze walls will shift with each Vana'diel day (see 'Sacrarium Map 1' below).",["zone"]="Sacrarium",["grid"]="J-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Entering Map 2 through Connection 'B', you arrive at Sacrarium (E-9) / Map 2.",["zone"]="Sacrarium",["grid"]="E-9 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Farming the Keys\010\010Note: This part of the mission can be skipped if someone has a Key item: Temple Knight Key in their possession.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Fomors until you get two Coral Crest Keys.\010\010You can do this mission with only one Coral Crest Key, but since they break on use, it will be necessary to have an extra person to stay behind to operate the door. They cannot participate in the final NM fight. \010\010Optional, but recommended - Head back to Misareaux Coast and kill Orcs and Gigas to lower your Fomor Hate. Check with Resauchamet at Tavnazian Safehold (J-7, K-6) / Upper Floor. Lower your Fomor Hate to level 1, where Resauchamet will tell you that you have a \226\128\156good head start.\226\128\157",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, kill Keremet, a Corse NM located in the large room at Sacrarium (K-8, L-8) / Map 2, to obtain the Sealion Crest Key. \010\010The two hallways leading into the large room are lined with 6 Skeletons each. The Skeletons don't aggro and are weak, but if anyone attacks Keremet they will rush to aid him. Defeat all 12 Skeletons first before you pass through one of the doors into the large room at Sacrarium (K-8, L-8) / Map 2. \010\010Carby pulling does not work on Keremet--the 12 Skeletons will aggro the SMN and start sewing chaos on anyone that generated enmity after that.\010\010Keremet is at the far side of the room at Sacrarium (L-8) / Map 2. Wait for the Tauri to wander to one side and then pull Keremet back through one of the doors into one of the hallways where the Skeletons were. Only one person should pull Keremet while the others wait in the hallway. \010\010You have 30 minutes to kill him before the Skeletons begin to repop and aggro you.\010\010Keremet can be Silenced. He is highly resistant to Stun, Sleep, and Ice-based spells.\010\010Like all Corse, Keremet can Charm members of your party with the Danse Macabre TP attack. Charmed party members MUST be slept. This fight is pretty tough as he has a nasty AoE Paralyze move and can Charm multiple targets. \010\010A Beastmaster makes this fight much easier: a Blubber Eyes under Familiar does a lot of damage and pets are immune to Keremet's Charm. Two Blubber Eyes can duo Keremet. \010\010From Keremet you obtain the Sealion Crest Key. \010\010If you did the quest A Hard Day's Knight, you can return to Tavnazian Safehold and go trade Quelveuiat the a Coral Crest Key along with the Sealion Crest Key to obtain the permanent Key item: Temple Knight Key to be able to open the door solo. \010\010If you do not intend to get the Key item: Temple Knight Key but use the Coral Crest Keys and the Sealion Crest Key to directly open the door, let someone take the Sealion Crest Key who doesn\226\128\153t have either of the Coral Crest Keys since one person cannot open the door by trading both keys.",["zone"]="Sacrarium",["grid"]="K-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mission Continues",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="With either a Key item: Temple Knight Key OR the Coral Crest Keys and a Sealion Crest Key head to Sacrarium (H-7) / Map 2 in the Sacrarium and look for a door with two keyholes: one LARGE and one SMALL.",["zone"]="Sacrarium",["grid"]="H-7 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Opening the door: The first party member will trade the Coral Crest Key to the SMALL HOLE; you will hear a click. \010The other party member will trade the Sealion Crest Key to the large hole; the door will then open. **You have a limited amount of time to trade the Sealion Crest Key after the Coral Crest Key has been traded, so make sure the key holders are both ready. (Both locks cannot be opened by a single person!)\010\010You will keep your Sealion Crest Key, but your Coral Crest Key will break. If the Sealion Crest Key isn't traded quickly enough, you will have lost your opportunity to get the door open, and will have to get another Coral Crest Key.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Find and click on the Wooden Gate at Sacrarium (G-8) / Map 2 for a cutscene (This is necessary to be able to proceed with the mission).",["zone"]="Sacrarium",["grid"]="G-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back out the locked door. \010\010If you do not have another Coral Crest Key, you can leave a member behind to open the door with the switch but they cannot participate in the NM fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You are looking to spawn and defeat the NM Old Professor Mariselle. They are located in one of the six classrooms: three on the north side at Sacrarium (F-5, G-5, H-5) / Map 2 and three on the south side at Sacrarium (F-11, G-11, H-11) / Map 2. Each classroom has a ??? in it. Check each ??? until you spawn the Ghost NM Old Professor Mariselle and his two Mariselle's Pupils.\010\010Sneak pulling is ineffective; the NM spawns aggressive.\010\010The correct ??? is randomly selected each time the NM is spawned. Unsure whether it can select the same ??? twice in a row. Additionally, it seems to remain spawned for multiple minutes, even if all party/alliance members are KO'd.\010\010Old Professor Mariselle teleports, casts Sleepga II and Silence, and uses Ghost abilities. It seems to have a fair bit of regen, so continuing to keep damage on after it teleports is important.\010\010Don\226\128\153t use AoE abilities or you risk aggroing the Fomor.\010\010Don\226\128\153t use Tractor during the fight with Old Professor Mariselle, as it will cause the player to zone and the NM will have to be repopped before they can get their Key item: Reliquiarium Key!\010\010The Mariselle's Pupils are weak, but if you kill them Old Professor Mariselle will summon more. They CANNOT be slept.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Mariselle's Pupils can however be slept through the use of Lullaby. Recently tested this (May, 2026)\010\010Highly recommend clearing the Fomor out of each room before clicking the ???, as the Fomor will Blood aggro, chain link, and probably wipe your group. Additionally, Mariselle warps, so melee players will only have a couple safe places in the room to stand if Fomor are still alive. This strat may take quite a bit of time to check all 6 rooms, but wiping will also take ages.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Old Professor Mariselle and check the ??? again for the Reliquiarium Key. Any ??? in any of the rooms will allow you to obtain the Key item: Reliquiarium Key.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed back to the locked door and open it with your second Coral Crest Key and the Sealion Crest Key, using the same method as before. Alternatively, have someone operate the switch on the other side.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Behind the locked door, head to the Wooden Gate again for a final cutscene and to end the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7433",["title"]="The Setting Sun",["page_title"]="The Setting Sun",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Setting_Sun",["revision"]="118731",["requirements"]="Start: Vamorcote \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (F-5)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 5\010Items: Engraved Key\010Previous: Blackmail",["rewards"]="10,000g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Retrieve the key to a document box holding a copy of the castle floor plans. The key was buried long ago on a small island to the south of Batallia Downs.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Vamorcote needs you to find a key that was apparently buried in the Batallia Downs. \010\010If you already have the Engraved Key you do not need to zone and can trade the key to Vamorcote immediately after flagging the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Engraved Key he is looking for is dropped from an Ahtu, a NM Treant that spawns at (J-11) in the Batallia Downs on a small island. The key is 100% drop.\010\010You should consider doing the quest An Explorer's Footsteps for the Monument in Batallia Downs (J-11) because it is on the same island.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Vamorcote in Northern San d'Oria, and trade him the key to receive your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Directions to the Island",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To get to the island, head out to Batallia Downs, go to (I-10) inside the small cave, and enter Eldieme Necropolis. Your goal is to get to (G-9). To do this, you must have two people to operate the gates.\010\010 There are switches that manipulate all the gates at each of the 4 main sections with graves in them. Two will be available at the start; they are at (H-8) and (F-8).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to the room at (G-9).\010\010 Have someone move to (H-9) where the lich spawns and have them face the south closed gate (it should be named Titan's Gate). \010\010 Once there, have the person at the switch open Titan's gate for you. Once through the gate, run to the switch in your area at (G-9). \010\010 Now whoever is at the (G-9) switch must open and close the gates for the person at the other switch.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once everyone is now gathered at (G-9), find the grave in the middle of the 9 graves and walk over it (If lich and tomb wolves aggro, you must put Sneak up first) and fall through the hole.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you're down the hole, follow the path until you end up at a fork. Turn right here and proceed south until you find the zone at (J-9) to Batallia.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will now be at (J-11) on the island.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill Ahtu and get the Engraved Key from him.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_352",["title"]="The Shadow Awaits (Windurst Mission 5-2)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 5-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_5-2",["revision"]="123829",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Previous: Windurst Mission 5-1|The Final Seal",["rewards"]="Rank 6\010Unlock Rise of the Zilart Missions\010Unlock Dynamis\01020,000 gil\010Mog Wardrobe: 10 Slots [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="As written in the stars and interpreted by the Star Sibyl, you are destined to journey to Castle Zvahl, which towers over Xarcabard, the end of the known lands. There, you are to witness what fate has in store for our world.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade about 23 crystals to any Conquest Overseer to unlock the mission then accept it from any Windurst Gate Guard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click the \034Door:Vestal Chamber\034 at the top of Heavens Tower.\010\010You will want physical AND Magic damage for this mission. (Can be duoed by 2 Lv.75)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Throne Room and clear the BCNM \034The Shadow Lord Battle\034.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you clear the BCNM, you'll get another cutscene. At the end, you'll be returned to the entrance of Castle Zvahl Baileys. You will also receive the Key item: Shadow Fragment.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Heavens Tower for a brief cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click the \034Door:Vestal Chamber\034 for a final cutscene, Rank 6 and gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Castle Zvahl Baileys\010\010Head for Xarcabard. Castle Zvahl is on the far west of the area.\010\010Enter Castle Zvahl Baileys, follow the one-way path until you come to the first intersection. Turn right, head north then west and down a small flight of stairs.\010\010Turn left and follow the right wall until you reach the next map.\010\010On the next map, turn right and head all the way to the top right corner of the map.\010\010Head up the stairs and you will be on the second \034level\034.\010\010Next, get to the top left part of the map and walk back down the set of stairs and you'll be back on the first \034level\034.\010\010Work your way into the center of the map from here and you will be in an outdoor courtyard. Go back up to the second \034level\034 then through the gate on the right and you'll be in a long hall with a large flight of stairs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Castle Zvahl Keep\010\010Inside, walk out of the hallway and turn right. Ahead, you will have to go through a few gates, there are a lot of mobs in the area which detect sight, however your party should have no problems disposing of them. \010\010Once on the second level, you will be overlooking a room below. Follow the narrow path to more stairs and another hallway. You'll eventually reach an area with teleporters. These teleporters take awhile to activate, so just stand on the center and be patient. Using them will cause your Invisible (Status Effect) to drop. \010\010Follow the teleporters four times until you reach a new map. Run to the west/middle of this area and you'll see a door. Passing through this door will result in a zone to the Throne Room.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Throne Room\010\010You will now have some time to prepare for the fight, run to the other side of the Throne Room and gather up. When ready, check the door and enter the BCNM.\010\010The Shadow Lord has 2 forms. In the first form, he can switch between physical or magical immunity. Take time during magic immunity to rest MP, and hold off on melee attacks while in physical. \010\010While immune to magic, he will use Dark Nova (AOE Darkness damage) and can cast Black Magic. Dark Nova tends to indicate that he will switch to physical immunity. \010\010During physical immunity, he can use a variety of TP attacks, including Giga Slash, Kick Back and Umbra Smash. \010\010Defeating the first form will get you a cutscene. You will immediately be returned to the fight. Rest quickly and get ready for the second form.\010\010The second form will only use AoE attacks, but has less HP (approximately 4,000 HP). At this point, use your 2hrs and take him down as fast as possible. Curaga should be used liberally here to help counter the AoE damage. He will not rotate immunities like the first form.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_372",["title"]="The Shadow Lord (San d'Oria Mission 5-2)",["page_title"]="San d'Oria Mission 5-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/San_d%27Oria_Mission_5-2",["revision"]="98953",["requirements"]="Start: Any San d'Oria Gate Guard\010Previous: San d'Oria Mission 5-1|The Ruins of Fei'Yin",["rewards"]="Rank 6\010Unlock Rise of the Zilart Missions\010Unlock Dynamis\01020,000 gil\010Mog Wardrobe: 10 Slots",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Head to Castle Zvahl in Xarcabard. Visit Chateau d'Oraguille to learn more.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Accept the mission by speaking to any San d'Oria Gate Guard.\010\010Trade crystals to the Conquest NPC to unlock this mission. 20 to 24 crystals.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Halver. He will tell you to go see Prince Trion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Prince Trion in his chamber for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Form a full party (recommended level 55-60 or higher), and head for Xarcabard. Castle Zvahl is on the far west of the area.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Castle Zvahl Baileys",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Castle Zvahl Baileys, follow the one-way path until you come to the first intersection. Turn right, head north then west and down a small flight of stairs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Turn left and follow the right wall until you reach the next map.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On the next map, turn right and head all the way to the top right corner of the map.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head up the stairs and you will be on the second \034level\034.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, get to the top left part of the map and walk back down the set of stairs and youll be back on the first \034level\034.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Work your way into the center of the map from here and you will be in an outdoor courtyard. Go back up to the second \034level\034 then through the gate on the right and you'll be in a long hall with a large flight of stairs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Castle Zvahl Keep",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Inside, walk out of the hallway and turn right. Ahead, you will have to go through a few gates and ore doors. There are a lot of mobs in the area which detect sight, however your party should have no problems disposing of them.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once on the second level, you will be overlooking a room below. Follow the narrow path to more stairs and another hallway. You'll eventually reach an area with teleporters. These teleporters take awhile to activate, so just stand on the center and be patient.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow the teleporters four times until you reach a new map. Run to the west/middle of this area and you'll see a door. Passing through this door will result in a zone to the Throne Room.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Throne Room",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will now have some time to prepare for the fight, run to the other side of the Throne Room and gather up. When ready, check the door for a cutscene involving Zeid and the Shadow Lord, then click the door a second time and enter the BCNM.\010\010The Shadow Lord has 2 forms. In the first form, he can switch between physical or magical immunity. Take time during magic immunity to rest MP, and hold off on melee attacks while in physical. \010\010While immune to magic, he will use Dark Nova (AOE Darkness damage) and can cast Black Magic. Dark Nova tends to indicate that he will switch to physical immunity. \010\010During physical immunity, he can use a variety of TP attacks, including Giga Slash, Kick Back and Umbra Smash. \010\010Defeating the first form will get you a cutscene. You will immediately be returned to the fight. Rest quickly and get ready for the second form.\010\010The second form will only use AoE attacks, but has less HP (approximately 4,000 HP). At this point, use your 2hrs and take him down as fast as possible. Curaga should be used liberally here to help counter the AoE damage. He will not rotate immunities like the first form.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the second form is defeated, you'll get another cutscene. At the end, you'll be returned to the entrance of Castle Zvahl Baileys. You will also receive the Key item: Shadow Fragment.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Halver for your reward: Rank 6 and gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the door to the Great Hall for a final cutscene involving the royal family.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="sandoria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7514",["title"]="The Signpost Marks the Spot",["page_title"]="The Signpost Marks the Spot",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Signpost_Marks_the_Spot",["revision"]="104288",["requirements"]="Start: Nbu Latteh \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (J-9)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 2\010Previous: Mom, the Adventurer?",["rewards"]="Linen Robe",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Find the key item buried under one of the signposts on the Konschtat Highlands and bring it to Nbu Latteh's house.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Nbu Latteh.\010\010Note: If you have not zoned from the prior quest,\194\160Mom, the Adventurer? Nbu will just chat with you about her work.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Konschtat Highlands and select the signpost at G-5 to receive the Key item: Painting of a Windmill .",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Bastok, and talk to Roh Latteh in Bastok Mines to complete the quest and receive the Linen Robe reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7489",["title"]="The Siren's Tear",["page_title"]="The Siren's Tear",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Siren%27s_Tear",["revision"]="104177",["requirements"]="Start: Wahid \226\128\148 Bastok Mines (I-8)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Siren's Tear",["rewards"]="150 gil",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Find the Siren's Tear for Wahid. This rare gem is known to occasionally appear on the shores of the Gustaberg River. Seek the bard in the Port Bastok restaurant and listen to his story.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Wahid; he's a collector of precious gems and is looking for a Siren's Tear. He says they can be found near the rivers of the Gustaberg Mountains but will slip through your fingers unless they are handled in a special way. Also, there is a bard in a tavern somewhere who has advice on how to get the jewel.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Talk to Otto at the Steaming Sheep in Port Bastok (E-6); he will point to the bard mentioned above, Carmelo.",["zone"]="Port Bastok",["grid"]="E-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(Optional) Talk to Carmelo; he sings a cryptic song explaining how to get the tear and he explains its meaning.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to North Gustaberg (east section) and locate the ??? along the river at North Gustaberg (J-8, J-9). (You can avoid aggro by going via Port Bastok.) The ??? will move around the shore line, so it's not always in the same spot. A good strategy is to check one side of the river, then the other until you find the ???.",["zone"]="North Gustaberg",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Unequip your weapon and shield and examine the ??? to pick up the Siren's Tear.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the tear to Wahid to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To get Siren's Tear again, you MUST talk to Carmelo and he will say, \034And once again, a Siren's Tear floats down the river, seeking shelter from the tides of war...\034",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You may be unable to attain the Siren's Tear if your current Job is Monk. It will say that the object has slipped from your hands regardless if you have unequipped your weapons or not.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you fight anything with your bare hands, you will not be able to obtain the Siren's Tear without zoning out and back in.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_355",["title"]="The Sixth Ministry (Windurst Mission 7-1)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 7-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_7-1",["revision"]="114882",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Previous: Windurst Mission 6-2|Saintly Invitation",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="At the request of the Optistery, you are to find former minister Karaha-Baruha's laboratory in Toraimarai Canal, and delve deeper into the mystery of the Book of the Gods.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 24 crystals to any Conquest Overseer to unlock the mission then accept it from any Windurst Gate Guard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Tosuka-Porika in the Optistery in Windurst Waters (G-8) / North to receive the Key item: Optistery Ring.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="G-8 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Toraimarai Canal (G-8) / Map 2 and defeat the four Hinge Oils in the room\010\010You can Charm and Depop the Hinge Oils if you have BST leveled. The door will open even if you depop all 4 slimes this way without fighting whatsoever.\010\010Tested at level 75 BST\010\010They should depop if you drag them out of the room towards the corner at G-9; if not, go a little further until you can see the water below at F-9. If they don't disappear, just recharm. The command is \034/pet Leave <me>\034 for anyone new to the strat.\010\010You can depop the Hinge Oils if you train them to the zone.\010\010Tested at level 75 SMN with Fenrir\010\010 Quickest route: [Template collapsible: The Quickest way to get there is to enter through Windurst Walls (H-3) using the Key item: Rhinostery Certificate, take a right at the bottom of the stairs, get into the water and keep turning left until you reach some stairs, which you should go up. From here, head South then East then North to reach the Slimes.]\010\010 While Horizon has 5 minute dungeon respawn timers, these NM's still only spawn every 16 minutes. - See patch notes.\010\010All four Hinge Oils must be defeated before you can enter The Animastery.",["zone"]="Toraimarai Canal",["grid"]="G-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After defeating the 4 Slimes, head northeast to the stairs at Toraimarai Canal (H-8) / Map 2 and examine the Marble Door at the top.",["zone"]="Toraimarai Canal",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Tome of Magic lying on the ground to begin a cutscene.\010\010This is near the desk and a skull resting on a chair.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is a teleport outside one of the other doors that will take you to the bottom level of Heavens Tower",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Tosuka-Porika at Windurst Waters (G-8) / North to complete the mission. You will receive the Key item: Book of the Gods.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="G-8 / North",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7491",["title"]="The Stars of Ifrit",["page_title"]="The Stars of Ifrit",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Stars_of_Ifrit",["revision"]="104339",["requirements"]="Start: Agapito \226\128\148 Port Bastok (G-6)\010Requirements: Key item: Airship Pass\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Key item: Carrier Pigeon Letter",["rewards"]="2,100g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Agapito wants you to find out the meaning of the following words: \034Under a full moon, toward the stars of Ifrit, a bird delivers a letter to the ship in the sky.\034 Also, try to bring back this \034letter\034 to satisfy Agapito's curiosity.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Agapito, who is outside the air travel agency in Port Bastok.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next you have to ride the San d'Oria-Jeuno Airship under the right conditions, which are nighttime and Full Moon (19:40 - 06:00 and moon \226\137\165 90%). Either direction will work.\010\010Do not board in Port Bastok; you cannot receive the item on this route.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Search the rail of the ship for a ??? and check it to obtain a Key item: Carrier Pigeon Letter.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Agapito with the letter to receive your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6861",["title"]="The Sweetest Things",["page_title"]="The Sweetest Things",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Sweetest_Things",["revision"]="60792",["requirements"]="Start: Raimbroy \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (F-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Honey x 5",["rewards"]="400g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Collect five pots of honey for the grocer.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Raimbroy hasn't gotten his supplies in yet, and wants you to help. Fetch and trade him 5 honey and he'll reward you.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will have to talk to Raimbroy twice. The first gets you a cutscene, and the second starts the quest proper.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7548",["title"]="The Talekeeper's Gift",["page_title"]="The Talekeeper's Gift",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Talekeeper%27s_Gift",["revision"]="122360",["requirements"]="Start: Deidogg \226\128\148 Bastok Mines (H-6)\010Requirements: Warrior 50+\010Items: Ginger Cookie\010Previous: The Talekeeper's Truth",["rewards"]="Fighter's Lorica",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="Raogrimm's gift to the San d'Orians was stolen by a band of Goblin thieves from the Behemoth's Dominion. The Musketeers are in search of the item, but Deidogg wants you to take it for yourself.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After receiving your Fighter's Calligae, you must zone and wait until the following game day, then speak to Deidogg as a Warrior.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head around the corner to the small Galka child, Detzo, who will tell you Deidogg secretly likes Ginger Cookies.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Ginger Cookie to Deidogg for the quest to register on your quest log.\010\010From this point on, the quest can be completed on any job.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Behemoth's Dominion\010\010From Qufim Island (at (Qufim Island (G-5)) near Delkfutt's Tower, there is a long tunnel that leads to Behemoth's Dominion that is not shown on the map).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in Behemoth's Dominion, go to the spot at (Behemoth's Dominion (K-9)) where the ??? is, clear the area of Bats and Weapons if they aggro you, buff and get ready to go.",["zone"]="Behemoth's Dominion",["grid"]="K-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the ??? to spawn three Goblin NMs:\010\010Doglix Muttsnout, a White Mage, who uses Benediction.\010\010Moxnix Nightgoggle, a Ranger, who uses Eagle Eye Shot.\010\010Picklix Longindex, a Thief, who uses Perfect Dodge.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When all the Goblins are dead, head back to Qufim (reexamining the ??? does not do anything), and upon zoning back to Qufim Island, you will receive a cutscene and your Fighter's Lorica.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The NMs can be popped only once per game day.\010\010If you get the message \034It is too blurry to read\034, someone as already popped the NM for that game day.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Players can spawn the NMs on any job.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Goblins generally cannot be Slept without Elemental Seal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Ranger will only stand and shoot until low health, so it can safely be left for last as long as you don't move into its melee range.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The White Mage is easy to kite around the rocks in the big room, as it will frequently stop to cast and is known to be resistant to Stun.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Picklix Longindex, the Thief, is immune to stun.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If multiple warriors with this quest active are in the alliance, the NMs only have to be fought once.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you (while solo) disconnect during the fight, call for help, or your party/alliance loses claim on all the NMs, you will not be able to get the CS. Even if you zone back in quickly and kill the NMs, you will not get it.\010\010If party holds hate you can still complete the mission as long as you get hate on the NM before last one is killed, then touch the ??? as normal.\010(See Talk:The Talekeeper's Gift)\010NOT SOLOABLE! BRING FRIENDS!",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Warrior (WAR)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Warrior (WAR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Fighter's Lorica",["revision"]="109772"},{["job"]="Warrior (WAR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="The Talekeeper's Gift",["revision"]="122360"}}},{["id"]="wiki_5073",["title"]="The Talekeeper's Truth",["page_title"]="The Talekeeper's Truth",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Talekeeper%27s_Truth",["revision"]="104256",["requirements"]="Start: Deidogg \226\128\148 Bastok Mines (H-6)\010Requirements: Warrior 50+\010Items: Mottled Quadav Egg\010Parasite Skin\010Previous: The Doorman",["rewards"]="Fighter's Calligae",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="Deidogg wants to prove that the Talekeeper Raogrimm was no hero. First, he wants you to defeat the Quadav nest guardian in the Palborough Mines that Raogrimm claimed to have killed, and take from it the mottled Quadav egg the Talekeeper failed to bring back.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Phara, at Bastok Mines (J-9) in the Bastok Mines tells you about the Galka Deidogg at Bastok Mines (H-6) in the Bastok Mines.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will need to speak with Deidogg twice with Warrior set as your main job to receive the cutscene where he will ask you for a Mottled Quadav Egg dropped by Ni'Ghu Nestfender in Palborough Mines.\010\010From the first map in Palborough Mines, take the elevator at Palborough Mines (I-8) / Map 1 up to the Third Floor. Ni'Ghu Nestfender spawns from a ??? located in Palborough Mines (G-10) / Map 3. Nothing here will be high enough to aggro you, and the room is usually empty, but if some Quadav have wandered in, of course, clear the area beforehand.\010\010Note: You do not have to go with Warrior as your main job in order to spawn the NM but must have the quest active.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When your party is ready, examine the ??? to spawn Ni'Ghu Nestfender. He is a Paladin, and will use Invincible and Flash.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When he is defeated, he will drop the Mottled Quadav Egg. \010\010Make sure you do not touch the ??? again or it will spawn another Ni'Ghu Nestfender and you will have to do the fight again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you haven't set a Bastok Home Point, there is a ferry from Palborough MinesPalborough Mines (H-8) / Map 3 to Zeruhn Mines which will put you right next to Bastok Mines.",["zone"]="Palborough Mines",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After you bring the Mottled Quadav Egg to Deidogg, the cutscene suggests that you get a Parasite Skin from Castle Oztroja.\010\010Note: Since Parasite Skin is a Rare/Ex drop off the leeches in Castle Oztroja, you can save yourself a trip to Bastok if you catch a Teleport-Mea and head to Castle Oztroja before returning to town. You can kill two birds with one stone this way, and trade the skin after trading the egg to Deidogg when you arrive in Bastok Mines.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you get to Castle Oztroja you need to go past the first doorway with the trapdoor and proceed up to the 4 lever door at the SW corner of G-8. You can find the combination to the door at the dead-end at (I-10).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once inside this doorway proceed all the way up the stairs to a chamber with a pool in the middle of it. This pool will be surrounded by Tier 6 Yagudo and full of the leeches you need to kill. \010\010The leeches aggro by sound and the Yagudo aggro by sight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill a Yagudo Parasite and obtain the Parasite Skin.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Deidogg and trade him the Parasite Skin. He will ask you to return the next Vana'diel day.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you return, he will present you with your hard-earned Fighter's Calligae.\010\010(See Testimonials)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Warrior (WAR)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Warrior (WAR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Fighter's Calligae",["revision"]="99989"},{["job"]="Warrior (WAR)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="The Talekeeper's Truth",["revision"]="104256"}}},{["id"]="wiki_3685",["title"]="The Temple of Desolation (Zilart Mission 10)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 10",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_10",["revision"]="20473",["requirements"]="Start: None\010Previous: Ro'Maeve(Mission)|Ro'Maeve",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="On the northernmost point of Mindartia and deep within the wilderness known as the Sanctuary of Zi'Tah lies a body of ruins feared by many: Ro'Maeve, the Temple of Desolation.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Go to Ro'Maeve. You will need Sneak and Invisible through this area, but everything in-zone detects magic, so use Silent Oils and Prism Powders or cast Sneak and Invisible at the zone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head for (Ro'Maeve (H-5)) and zone in to Hall of the Gods. Run to the other side and check the gate two times.",["zone"]="Ro'Maeve",["grid"]="H-5",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="rise of the zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_643",["title"]="The Temple of Uggalepih (Zilart Mission 4)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 4",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_4",["revision"]="103274",["requirements"]="Start: None\010Level: 60+\010Previous: Kazham's Chieftainess",["rewards"]="Key item: Dark Fragment\010Mog Wardrobe 2: 5 slots",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="The Temple of Uggalepih is an ancient place where it is said that evil deities were once worshiped. Gilgamesh has ordered you to travel there and search out a strange, old hermit.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Walk through the Temple of Uggalepih",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To get into the Den of Rancor, at least one person will need a Key item: Paintbrush of Souls.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The NMs involved with this mission use a variant of Everyone's Grudge called Everyone's Rancor which does ten times as much damage as Grudge, and will often kill your tank in one attack if they haven't reset their Tonberry Hate.\010\010You have to kill some Tonberries for Unlit Lanterns, so you will need to reset your hate after that.\010\010If you Call for Help when killing a Tonberry, no Tonberry Hate will be accrued.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It is strongly recommended that at least one party member be level 75, as the weak monsters you will go past inside the Temple will not aggro them. This will allow them to open doors inside the Temple while the lower level party members remain invisible. Only invisible is needed inside the Temple, while both sneak and invisible are needed for all party members inside the Den of Rancor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Uggalepih",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To get into the Sacrificial Chamber in the Den of Rancor you will need to obtain four Unlit Lanterns which will help open the gate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The lanterns are dropped by Tonberry Maledictors in the Temple of Uggalepih as well as Tonberry Imprecators in Den of Rancor. There are a lot of spots to find Maledictors:\010\010From the main entrance of Temple of Uggalepih, head to (Temple of Uggalepih (J-7)) and open the secret door, exit at (Temple of Uggalepih (K-3)) to Yhoator Jungle. Go to another entrance at the right side of (Yhoator Jungle (K-9)) in Yhoator Jungle. Once in the temple, go to (Temple of Uggalepih (H-7) / Map 2). There should be (2-3) Tonberry Maledictors there.\010\010Enter the Den of Rancor from Yhoator Jungle (Yhoator Jungle (J-7)). Be careful not to fall through the hole as you sneak southeast to (Den of Rancor (J-9) / Map 7) and enter the Temple of Uggalepih. You can camp safely on the stairs here, and there are Maledictors nearby.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have the four Unlit Lanterns, go back to the main entrance and enter the Temple again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On the first map, head down to (Temple of Uggalepih (F-11)) and open the secret door to reset Tonberry hate. The tank must do this, as even a small amount of hate could result in a lot of damage.\010\010After this point, if you have to kill any Tonberries, Call for Help on them so you don't get any more hate.",["zone"]="Temple of Uggalepih",["grid"]="F-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to (Temple of Uggalepih (F-5)) to enter Yhoator Jungle, and re-enter the temple at (Yhoator Jungle (H-11)).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in the temple, head to (Temple of Uggalepih (I-10) / Map 2) and defeat the Temple Guardian. Make sure to prevent the Temple Guardian from using Meltdown ability by using Stun because it can kill the whole party. After you kill the Temple Guardian, the door in front will open.",["zone"]="Temple of Uggalepih",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once through, head northward to (Temple of Uggalepih (I-7) / Map 2). There'll be a room with a bunch of paintings and 2 with just an empty frame. Whoever has the paintbrush go to the empty frame on the east wall, face it directly and examine it. Once you get the \034a new painting begins to appear on the canvas\034 message, wait at least 30 seconds before hitting Enter to get the next message and open the door.\010\010If anything at all happens to the player using the paintbrush during the 30 seconds, you have to start over, so don't let them get aggro, and don't cast buffs on them.",["zone"]="Temple of Uggalepih",["grid"]="I-7 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the door is open run in and zone to Den of Rancor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Den of Rancor",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Invisible and Sneak everyone in the party and go to (Den of Rancor (E-5)). Clear the room and have people with the unlit lanterns trade them to the Altar of Rancor to get a Rancor Flame.\010\010There are other Altars in the Den, but only this one gives the right Flame.\010\010If you chose to come here to get Unlit Lanterns you can find Tonberry Imprecators in the first room you come upon after entering from Temple of Uggalepih.",["zone"]="Den of Rancor",["grid"]="E-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once that is done, drop through the hole in the northeast corner of (Den of Rancor (F-7)), which will take you to another map.",["zone"]="Den of Rancor",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On the second map, go to (Den of Rancor (E-5) / Map 2). It is recommended to clear this room because you can't light the lanterns while getting hit.",["zone"]="Den of Rancor",["grid"]="E-5 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To open the gate, have each person with a Rancor Flame light one of the four lanterns by trading their Rancor Flame to it. You will still have the Unlit Lantern after using the Rancor Flame, in case you need to help other people at another time. \010\010If you have more than six people going through this, keep in mind that the gate can be opened from the inside by having someone to target Switch and press it. Thus, the lanterns only need to be lit once.\010\010If you do get aggro after this, the entrance to the Sacrificial Chamber is a short run past the gate.\010\010You can actually light all the lanterns with fewer than four Unlit Lanterns; you just need to make multiple trips between the Altar and the stone lanterns.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Sacrificial Chamber",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After entering the Sacrificial Chamber, examine the heavy door to enter the Battlefield. \010\010The Battlefield is capped at 75, and thus enhancements/buffs wear off when entering the Battlefield.\010\010The Battlefield is limited to 6 players. A balanced party with an average level of 60+ should be able to clear the fight with only moderate difficulty.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There are three Tonberry NMs. All three must be defeated to clear the battlfield. The recommended order in which to kill them is:\010\010Grav'iton - Thief, with a crown on its head\010\010Molyb'iton - Black Mage\010\010Tungs'iton - Summoner",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Thief is completely immune to sleep, so you'll probably want to kill it while you Silence and/or Sleep the other two NMs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Summoner comes with a pet; a fire, water, or light elemental, chosen at random. It dies when its master does, so it need not be killed. The element of the pet is not an indication of which Astral Flow the Summoner will choose to use later in the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At approximately 25% HP, the Thief will attempt to use Everyone's Rancor, which does 10x the damage of Everyone's Grudge (Grudge does 5 damage for each Tonberry kill, Rancor does 50 damage per kill). The person this hits is liable to be K.O.'d in one shot if they have not recently reset their Tonberry hate (See Everyone's Grudge for more information). It will only use Everyone's Rancor once.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Summoner will summon a random avatar for Astral Flow even if its elemental pet is asleep, so make sure your party is healed up before waking it up. The maximum damage done by Astral Flow is approximately 700-800 without Shell or any sort of magical protection.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On clearing the Battlefield, you will receive a cutscene and exit in a different location to the entrance. Following this path leads back into Temple of Uggalepih away from the entrance to the Den.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Game Description\010\010Mission Orders The Temple of Uggalepih is an ancient place where it is said that evil deities were once worshipped. Gilgamesh has ordered you to travel there and search out a strange, old hermit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Game Script",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Rise of the Zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2121",["title"]="The Tenshodo Showdown",["page_title"]="The Tenshodo Showdown",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Tenshodo_Showdown",["revision"]="106644",["requirements"]="Start: Nanaa Mihgo \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (J-3)\010Requirements: Thief 40+\010Key item: Tenshodo Member's Card\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Key item: Letter from the Tenshodo\010Key item: Tenshodo Envelope\010Quadav Stew\010Key item: Signed Envelope",["rewards"]="Marauder's Knife",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="The Tenshodo is gathering expert thieves to its fold. Carry out your orders by handing the Tenshodo envelopes to the appropriate people and having them sign the documents within.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={"Thief (THF)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Thief (THF)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Marauder's Knife",["revision"]="21446"},{["job"]="Thief (THF)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="The Tenshodo Showdown",["revision"]="106644"}}},{["id"]="wiki_346",["title"]="The Three Kingdoms (Windurst Mission 2-3)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 2-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_2-3",["revision"]="111284",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Level: 25 (recommended)\010Items: Mythril Sand (Bastok Path)\010Previous: Windurst Mission 2-2|A Testing Time",["rewards"]="Rank 3\0103,000 gil\010Mog Wardrobe: 10 Slots [Horizon change] \010Level 10 Outpost Teleportation from Jeuno [Horizon change] \010Key item: Adventurer's Certificate",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Determine the state of affairs in San d'Oria and Bastok, and render assistance on behalf of Heavens Tower. Inquire at our consulate in each country for more information. Traveling by ship from Mhaura to Selbina is recommended.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2750",["title"]="The Three Magi",["page_title"]="The Three Magi",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Three_Magi",["revision"]="115845",["requirements"]="Start: Chumimi \226\128\148 Heavens Tower / Basement\010Level: 40 (Black Mage)\010Items: Faded Crystal\010Glowstone",["rewards"]="Casting Wand",["repeatable"]="af",["summary"]="The star tree saplings at the farm in the basement of Heavens Tower aren't growing very well. Doctor Shantotto and co. have ordered an investigation to try and solve the problem. Help them by bringing back a glowstone from the crevasse of Xarcabard.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="From Windurst Walls, enter Heavens Tower and take the right-hand stairs down to the basement until you reach Chumimi.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Chumimi to view a cutscene with Shantotto, Koru-Moru, and Yoran-Oran.\010\010 You will be asked to agree with one of them. Your choice does not affect quest progress; the message \034No one paid any attention to you.\034 will appear regardless.\010\010 Your choice only determines which title you receive:\010\010 Doctor Shantotto: Doctor Shantotto Supporter\010\010 Professor Koru-Moru: Professor Koru-Moru Supporter\010\010 Doctor Yoran-Oran: Doctor Yoran-Oran Supporter\010\010 After completing the quest, you can obtain the other two titles from Burute-Sorute in Windurst Walls.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene, Shantotto asks you to toss a Faded Crystal into the gorge in Xarcabard and bring back a Glowstone.\010\010 Before continuing, make sure you have at least one elemental Crystal (any type) so you can obtain a Faded Crystal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From this point onward, you no longer need to be a Black Mage (as with most AF quests).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Faded Crystal:\010\010 Travel to any Telepoint and trade one elemental Crystal to it.\010\010 Since the fight is in Xarcabard, Telepoint Vazhl at Xarcabard (H-8) is the most convenient.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Xarcabard and head to Xarcabard (E-8). There are two ??? points:\010\010 Use the one inside the gorge (left side as you approach Castle Zvahl).\010\010 Do not use the one on the cliff near the torch.\010\010 See the annotated map for reference.",["zone"]="Xarcabard",["grid"]="E-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Be ready for nearby enemies (e.g. Demon Pawns and Demon Knights) around the ???.\010\010 Note: If multiple players are doing this quest, there is a ~10-minute cooldown before the ??? can be traded again to respawn the Chaos Elemental.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Faded Crystal to the ??? to spawn the Chaos Elemental.\010\010 You can spawn it on any job. A Lv. 75 character can defeat it easily; /BLM for Warp is convenient.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat the Chaos Elemental and obtain the Glowstone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return the Glowstone to Chumimi to receive the Casting Wand.\010\010 (Hint: come as Black Mage if you plan to start the next AF quest immediately.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Black Mage (BLM)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Black Mage (BLM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Casting Wand",["revision"]="119377"}}},{["id"]="wiki_6850",["title"]="The Trader in the Forest",["page_title"]="The Trader in the Forest",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Trader_in_the_Forest",["revision"]="119277",["requirements"]="Start: Abeaule \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (F-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Batagreens",["rewards"]="Robe",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Purchase some batagreens from Phairet. Find him in the tower on the southern fringes of West Ronfaure.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Abeaule in the Phoenix Perch Inn, who will explain he needs someone to go out and fill an order he has. If you accept, he will give you a Supplies Order (speak with him again if you lose it).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Abeaule a clump of Batagreens to complete the quest.\010\010You are supposed to receive Batagreens by trading the Supplies Order to Phairet in the tower at West Ronfaure (I-11) . Or you can purchase them from the Cooking Guild in Windurst.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon completing this quest, you can receive a single Batagreens from Phairet by trading him 50 gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7518",["title"]="The Usual",["page_title"]="The Usual",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Usual",["revision"]="104321",["requirements"]="Start: Hilda \226\128\148 Port Bastok (E-6)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 5\010Items: King Truffle\010Previous: Cid's Secret",["rewards"]="Speed Bow",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Bring a king truffle to Hilda so she can serve it to an old Steaming Sheep customer.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Hilda.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a King Truffle to Hilda and she will give you the Key item: Steaming Sheep Invitation.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the Metalworks and talk to Raibaht in Cid's Lab.\010\010 You may need to talk to Raibaht twice if you have the quest \034Teak Me to the Stars\034 or The Naming Game active.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the restaurant and talk to Hilda to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1214",["title"]="The Vicasque's Sermon",["page_title"]="The Vicasque's Sermon",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Vicasque%27s_Sermon",["revision"]="60791",["requirements"]="Start: Abioleget \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (M-7)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Blue Peas\010Previous: Waters of the Cheval",["rewards"]="Brass Ring",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Deliver blue peas to a friar on retreat. Find him in a tower in the southeast area of East Ronfaure.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Note: You do not need to zone if you just finished the previous quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Abioleget in Northern San d'Oria in the Cathedral and a cutscene sermon will take place with you in attendance.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Abioleget again, and he will offer to sell you some Blue Peas. You can trade 70 gil to Abioleget for some Blue Peas.\010Note: Blue Peas can also be purchased from Machielle in Southern San d'Oria (G-9) for 25~29 gil, if San d\226\128\153Oria controls the Norvallen region.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the tower in the south-east corner of East Ronfaure (J-11). Trade Andelain a single Blue Peas despite his mentioning of 3 Blue Peas.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Northern San d'Oria, and talk to Abioleget to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3716",["title"]="The Walls of Your Mind",["page_title"]="The Walls of Your Mind",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Walls_of_Your_Mind",["revision"]="104385",["requirements"]="Start: Oggbi \226\128\148 Port Bastok (E-6)\010Requirements: Monk Level 71 minimum\010Hand-to-Hand Skill 250 minimum\010No other WSNM quest active\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: none\010Items: Knuckles of Trials\010Key item: Weapon Training Guide\010Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth\010Key item: Annals of Truth",["rewards"]="The weapon skill Asuran Fists",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Use the cesti granted to you by Master Oggbi to break the barriers that cloud your spirit. When you feel the weapon can assist you no further, return to the master for further instructions.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Oggbi in Port Bastok as a Monk level 71 minimum with 250 Hand-to-Hand skill minimum (merit bonuses do not count for beginning the quest) to obtain the Knuckles of Trials and a Key item: Weapon Training Guide.\010\010You cannot begin this quest if you have any other quest involving the Key item: Weapon Training Guide active.\010\010You must be level 71 minimum to begin the quest, but after beginning the quest, deleveling to 70 does not affect the quest progress in any way.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Perform weapon skills with the Knuckles of Trials until the latent effect disappears. \010\010You must accumulate 300 Weapon Skill Points on experience-yielding monsters.\010\010Weapon Skills performed while under Level Sync do count. Your latent effect may disappear when level sync is applied due to equipment adjustment. Remove sync to ensure the weapon is broken.\010\010You receive 1 point for opening/soloing a weapon skill, 2 points for closing a Lv.1 skillchain, 3 points for closing a Lv.2 skillchain, and 5 points for closing a level 3 skillchain.\010\010Wheeling Thrust (DRG, Spear)--> Dragon's Kick (H2H) Light Skillchain.\010\010To check to see if the latent effect has disappeared, simply check your equipment page for the elemental resistance bonuses, and if you do not have the bonus stats anymore, you are done.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you no longer receive the latent effect bonus, head back to Port Bastok and trade the Knuckles of Trials back to Oggbi, who takes the weapon from you and gives you a Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth, telling you to head to Bostaunieux Oubliette.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in Bostaunieux Oubliette, follow the path south, then turn west into a long corridor. Go through the Wooden Door at the end of the corridor and talk to the NPC there to access the trap door, which takes you to the lower level with monsters.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to the small room at (I-8) on the third map, clear the room of leeches, rest up, and click the ??? in the center of the room to spawn the NM warrior skeleton Bodach.\010\010You can spawn Bodach on any job.\010\010Bodach uses Blood Saber, Hell Slash, and Horror Cloud; possesses very high HP and higher-than-average evasion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the NM is dead, reexamine the ??? to obtain the Key item: Annals of Truth.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Oggbi for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_591",["title"]="The Warrior's Path (Promathia Mission 7-5)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 7-5",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_7-5",["revision"]="119256",["requirements"]="Previous: Calm Before the Storm",["rewards"]="Access to Al'Taieu\010Access to Limbus\010Mog Wardrobe 2: 5 Slots",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Board the newly repaired airship and head for the fifth mothercrystal. Will your path be intercepted by Nag'molada? The dreadful wyrms? Or a completely unexpected opponent...?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Click the Iron Gate for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After cutscene, click the Iron Gate again and select \034The Warrior's Path\034 to enter.\010\010This battle is uncapped. However, buffs and TP wear off upon entry.\010\010You cannot exit once you enter.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After defeating Tenzen, you will receive a cutscene and zone into Al'Taieu.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57030",["title"]="The Wayward Automaton",["page_title"]="The Wayward Automaton",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Wayward_Automaton",["revision"]="123900",["requirements"]="Start: Iruki-Waraki \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-9)\010Requirements: Puppetmaster unlocked\010Level: Puppetmaster 40\010Fame: Aht Urhgan\010Items: None\010Previous: No Strings Attached",["rewards"]="Turbo Animator",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Iruki-Waraki's automaton has been stolen! Go to Nashmau and see if you can find some information on its whereabouts.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Iruki-Waraki in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-9) as Puppetmaster level 40 or higher.\010After initiating the quest with Iruki-Waraki, you may complete all following steps from this moment onward as any job.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Nashmau and speak with Dnegan at Nashmau (H-6).",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="H-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exit Nashmau through the east gate into Caedarva Mire.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the ??? on the island at Caedarva Mire (I-10) to spawn Caedarva Toad.",["zone"]="Caedarva Mire",["grid"]="I-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Caedarva Toad.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the ??? again for a cutscene.\010\010 If you zone before checking the ??? after the fight, you may need to defeat Caedarva Toad again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Iruki-Waraki in Aht Urhgan Whitegate to receive the Turbo Animator.\010\010Testimonials: \010 1. Easily solo'd as 57PUP w/ WHM head.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="ToAU",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3717",["title"]="The Weight of Your Limits",["page_title"]="The Weight of Your Limits",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Weight_of_Your_Limits",["revision"]="123162",["requirements"]="Start: Iron Eater \226\128\148 Metalworks (J-8)\010Requirements: Able to wield Axe of Trials lv71\010Great Axe Skill 240+\010No other WSNM quest active\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: none\010Items: Axe of Trials\010Key item: Weapon Training Guide\010Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth\010Key item: Annals of Truth",["rewards"]="Grants the weaponskill Steel Cyclone",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Use the axe given to you by Iron Eater to test your might. When you feel that you have reached your limits, bring the weapon back to the President's Office.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Iron Eater in Metalworks who will give you the Axe of Trials and the Key item: Weapon Training Guide.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the Axe of Trials until the latent effect disappears. \010\010How to remove the latent effect: \010\010You must perform Weapon Skills and Skillchains on monsters that check as Easy Prey or higher. \010\010Weapon Skills performed while under Level Sync count.\010\010You receive 1 point for opening/soloing a weapon skill, 2 points for closing a Lv.1 Skillchain, 3 points for closing a Lv.2 Skillchain and 5 points for closing a level 3 skillchain.\010\010You must accumulate 300 total points.\010\010To check to see if the latent effect has disappeared, simply look at your elemental resistances. If you are not receiving the elemental bonus from the Axe of Trials then you have broken the latent. It is NOT necessary to un-equip/re-equip the weapon.\010\010You will not be able to tell if the latent is broken while under the effect of Level Sync. You will not receive the elemental bonuses while Level Sync is in effect. Therefore, you must be unsynced to check.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you no longer receive the latent effect bonus, head back to Metalworks and trade the Axe of Trials back to Iron Eater who will take the weapon from you and give you a Key item: Map to the Annals of Truth and tell you to head to Sanctuary of Zi'Tah.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in Sanctuary of Zi'Tah go to F-6 and click the ??? (ignore map's mark, it's just wrong) in the far northwestern corner of the square to spawn the NM named Greenman.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the NM is dead, re-examine the ??? to obtain the Key item: Annals of Truth. If you zone and forget to check the ???, you will have to fight the Greenman again to get the key item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="More than one person can gain the key item from a single fight, as long as they check the ???.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring this back to Iron Eater for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Testimonials\010\010 Duo'd with DRK/NIN RDM/WHM - neither with special gear - standard de-buffs - drk got low HP once - grav/bind was used as needed, vert used then the rest of the fight was easy\010\010 13/01/26 - Duo BST/NIN, BST/NIN. let the pets do the damage and stay out of the way. Leafstorm removes shadows and deals damage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="19/05/26 - Soloed on THF with bolts, eva set, and eva merits, took a bit of dmg but negated with a perskos au lait\010Would be very difficult solo as THF. i duo with DRG/RDM as THF with full EVA setup and merits and it was still pretty accurate. blood bolts 18HP with INT. Blind bolts only enfeeble that sticks. regen drinks on board. killed just fine but was in red toward end. also opened with light skillchain is suggested.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1168",["title"]="The Wisdom of Elders",["page_title"]="The Wisdom of Elders",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Wisdom_of_Elders",["revision"]="74748",["requirements"]="Start: Benita \226\128\148 Port Bastok (J-6)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Bomb Ash",["rewards"]="Traveler's Hat",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The chimney in Benita's house is clogged with soot. Her mother-in-law, who's gone outside with Benita's daughter, knows the perfect item for clearing chimneys. Go consult the elderly woman, and find the item.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Benita; she's having problems cleaning her chimney but says her mother-in-law has a secret for doing it easily.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to the mother-in-law (outside at Port Bastok (I-5)), Tete, to find out about Bomb Ash.",["zone"]="Port Bastok",["grid"]="I-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Bomb Ash to Benita to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5914",["title"]="The Wonder Magic Set",["page_title"]="The Wonder Magic Set",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Wonder_Magic_Set",["revision"]="120721",["requirements"]="Start: Panta-Putta - Lower Jeuno (H-10)\010Requirements: Jeuno Reputation 4\010Items: White Rock\010Key item: Wonder Magic Set\010Previous: Child's Play",["rewards"]="Mythril Earring",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Panta-Putta, located at the merchant's house at Lower Jeuno (G-10) in Lower Jeuno, for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="G-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to him again. He wants you to bring him a Key item: Wonder Magic Set.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Key item: Wonder Magic Set is obtained from the related quest Child's Play. To summarize:\010\010Go to Port Jeuno and talk to Karl at Port Jeuno (H-8), who is standing near the stairs down to the Chocobo stables. He tells you that he'll trade you the Key item: Wonder Magic Set for a White Rock.\010\010White Rock is available from Goldsmithing Guild Merchants hobbies, and may be for sale from the Auction House fairly cheap.\010\010Trade Karl the White Rock to obtain the Wonder Magic Set.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Lower Jeuno and talk to Panta-Putta Lower Jeuno (G-10) to complete the quest.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="G-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Game Description\010\010Client: Panta-Putta (Merchant's House, Lower Jeuno)\010\010Summary:\010You are to bring Panta the popular Wonder Magic Set. Don't say a word to his family, or else.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_321",["title"]="The Zeruhn Report (Bastok Mission 1-1)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 1-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_1-1",["revision"]="27745",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Collect Overseer Makarim's report from the Zeruhn Mines, in the western section of the Bastok Mines District. Deliver said report to Sir Naji, a Musketeer stationed near the President's Office.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Select the mission from one of the Bastok Gate Guards.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Makarim in Zeruhn Mines (H-11) for the Zeruhn Report. The mines can be located via Bastok Mines (D-7).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Metalworks (J-8) and speak to Naji for a cutscene and to complete the mission.\010\010 Should you examine the Zeruhn report key item, Naji will chastise you. It does not seem to affect the mission though.",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7453",["title"]="Thick Shells",["page_title"]="Thick Shells",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Thick_Shells",["revision"]="108332",["requirements"]="Start: Vounebariont \226\128\148 Port San d'Oria (I-10)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Beetle Shell x5",["rewards"]="750g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Collect five beetle shells suitable for making medicine.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Vounebariont needs 5 Beetle Shells. Trade them to him for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57386",["title"]="Three Men and a Closet",["page_title"]="Three Men and a Closet",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Three_Men_and_a_Closet",["revision"]="121429",["requirements"]="Start: Kubhe Ijyuhla \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-8) / Map 1 \226\128\148 Serpentking Square.\010Requirements: Completion of Got It All\010Fame: none\010Items: None\010Previous: Got It All",["rewards"]="Imperial Bronze Piece",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Kubhe Ijyuhla asks you to investigate the strange behavior of Foudeel, Wahboud, and Bashraf, beginning with a training session in the Wajaom Woodlands.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Kubhe Ijyuhla in Serpentking Square at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-8) / Map 1 to begin the quest.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Leave Aht Urhgan Whitegate for Wajaom Woodlands through the exit at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-10) / Map 1 to trigger a cutscene while zoning.\010\010 Your previous zone must be Aht Urhgan Whitegate. Entering Wajaom Woodlands from another zone does not advance the quest.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Kubhe Ijyuhla at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-8) / Map 1 for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Ratihb on the second floor of the Shararat Teahouse at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-12) / Map 1 for a cutscene.\010\010 Ratihb is involved in several quests. If another quest cutscene plays first, speak with him again.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="J-12 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Tehf Kimasnahya on Balrahn Way at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-8) / Map 1 for a cutscene.\010\010 Choose \034You look nice.\034 to advance the quest.\010\010 Choosing the other response does not advance the quest; speak with Tehf Kimasnahya again to retry.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="F-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Kubhe Ijyuhla to complete the quest and receive an Imperial Bronze Piece.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_564",["title"]="Three Paths (Promathia Mission 5-3)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 5-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_5-3",["revision"]="105257",["requirements"]="Start: Cid \226\128\148 Metalworks (H-8)\010Previous: Desires of Emptiness",["rewards"]="1000 Experience Points for each battlefield cleared.\010Mog Wardrobe 2: 5 Slots",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="To break the Wyrmking's pact, you must locate the Keeper of the Apocalypse as quickly as possible. To do that you must first learn more of Al'Taieu, as well as find Prishe and the mysterious boy.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Note This is a long mission with two dungeons, an uncapped NM, and three BCNM fights.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Metalworks and talk to Cid Metalworks (H-8) to get started.\010\010It doesn't matter what path you choose when you talk to Cid; you don't have to start that fork first. \010\010You can be working on more than one path at a time.",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete all three paths below to complete the mission. \010\010! colspan=\0343\034 | Three Paths Overview\010|- class=\034copmissions-alt\034\010! Fork 1\010! Fork 2\010! Fork 3\010|-\010|align=\034center\034 | Tenzen Path\010|align=\034center\034 | Ulmia Path\010|align=\034center\034 | Louverance Path",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3681",["title"]="Through the Quicksand Caves (Zilart Mission 6)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 6",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_6",["revision"]="120710",["requirements"]="Start: None\010Level: 75\010Previous: Headstone Pilgrimage",["rewards"]="Mog Wardrobe 2: 5 slots",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You must hurry to Zepwell's Island's ancient temple.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="rise of the zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7425",["title"]="Tiger's Teeth",["page_title"]="Tiger's Teeth",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Tiger%27s_Teeth",["revision"]="60784",["requirements"]="Start: Taumila \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (E-9)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Black Tiger Fang x 3",["rewards"]="2,100g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Collect three black tiger fangs.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Taumila of Taumila's Sundries wants tiger fangs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring her 3 Black Tiger Fangs and she will reward you.\010\010Note: you end up with 8,400 gil per stack; compare prices with AH before choosing what to do.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7510",["title"]="Till Death Do Us Part",["page_title"]="Till Death Do Us Part",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Till_Death_Do_Us_Part",["revision"]="104373",["requirements"]="Start: Romilda \226\128\148 Port Bastok (I-7)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Cotton Gloves\010Previous: Forever to Hold",["rewards"]="2,000g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Romilda wants you to get her a pair of cotton gloves to give to her husband, Qiji, as a present.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Zone after Forever to Hold quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Romilda.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade some Cotton Gloves to Romilda to complete the quest and receive your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2042",["title"]="To Bee or Not to Bee?",["page_title"]="To Bee or Not to Bee?",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/To_Bee_or_Not_to_Bee%3F",["revision"]="75379",["requirements"]="Start: Raamimi \226\128\148 Windurst Walls (F-7)\010Fame: windurst\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Honey x4\010Previous: The Postman Always K.O.s Twice",["rewards"]="Mulsum x 3",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Zayhi-Bauhi, the old man who constantly gives public speeches by the bridge to Heavens Tower, has come down with a sore throat. Follow Raamimi's advice on how to sooth this little pain in the neck.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Zayhi-Bauhi needs honey for his voice. \010\010If Zayhi-Bauhi gives his speech fine without coughing, speak to Kalupa-Tawalupa and Rutango-Botango, his audience, to activate the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Raamimi and she will give you some honey.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the honey to Zayhi-Bauhi, which seems to help, and then talk to the NPCs around him.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Get 4 more pots of honey and trade them to Zayhi-Bauhi one at a time. \010\010Honey can be bought on the Auction House or obtained as drops from Bees.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Then go back to Raamimi to receive your reward of three Mulsum.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2514",["title"]="To Catch a Falling Star",["page_title"]="To Catch a Falling Star",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/To_Catch_a_Falling_Star",["revision"]="75367",["requirements"]="Start: Sigismund \226\128\148 Port Windurst (E-7)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Pugil Scales x 1\010Starfall Tear x 1",["rewards"]="Fish Scale Shield",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Sigismund wants you to bring him a \034Starfall Tear\034 so he can take it back to his country as a souvenir of Windurst.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Sigismund on the roof of the Orastery at Port Windurst (E-7).",["zone"]="Port Windurst",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He will tell you that he wants a Starfall Tear as a souvenir of Windurst.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Tohopka (beside Sigismund) to find out that you need pugil scales to collect the tear.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Get one set of Pugil Scales. You can get these from just about any Pugil, but the closest are Pug Pugils in East Sarutabaruta or Giddeus Pugil in Giddeus.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the Twinkle Tree on Starfall Hillock in West Sarutabaruta (I-6).",["zone"]="West Sarutabaruta",["grid"]="I-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Target the base of the tree. Between the hours of 0:00 and 3:00, examining this spot will give you the message: A frost deposit at the base of the tree twinkles in the starlight.\010\010During this time, you can trade a pugil scale to the tree to receive a Starfall Tear.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Port Windurst and trade the Starfall Tear to Sigismund. He will reward you with a Fish Scale Shield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7424",["title"]="To Cure a Cough",["page_title"]="To Cure a Cough",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/To_Cure_a_Cough",["revision"]="119009",["requirements"]="Start: Nenne \226\128\148 Southern San d'Oria (F-6)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 3 [Wiki: needs verification]\010Items: Key item: Thyme Moss\010Previous: The Medicine Woman",["rewards"]="3,000g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Bring Amaura some thyme moss, and she'll concoct a brew with curative powers.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Nenne, who can be found in the third house in Watchdog Alley.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="On the top floor of the first house in Watchdog Alley (G-7), there is a diary. Read all three pages. You must read one page in order for the next one to show up, so you have to read the pages in order. If you do not get the option to read all three pages, you may not have enough fame.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Page 3 may not be viewed while the quest: The Medicine Woman is active but will show up immediately after completion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Amaura in the second house in Watchdog Alley. She will require a piece of Key item: Thyme Moss.\010\010The quest will appear in the quest log at this point.\010\010You may need to speak with Amaura more than once to receive the correct dialogue/quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Key item: Thyme Moss can be found by clicking on the ??? at (F-9) in Davoi, the Orc stronghold. To get there you must enter the river at (H-8) and travel west through the river to get to the land at (D-9). Next go east all the way till you find a ramp. Under the ramp is the ???.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Amaura and she will give you the Key item: Cough Medicine.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the syrup to Nenne, who will give you a Key item: Scroll of Treasure as a reward. Now the quest will show up on your completed quests list.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The map you got will lead you to a signpost at (H-6) in East Ronfaure. Click on this to receive 3000g.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_347",["title"]="To Each His Own Right (Windurst Mission 3-1)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 3-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_3-1",["revision"]="106148",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Previous: Windurst Mission 2-3|The Three Kingdoms",["rewards"]="Rank Points\010Key item: Starway Stairway bauble",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="On the command of Semih Lafihna, captain of the Sibyl Guards, you are requested to track down the Minister of the Orastery, Ajido-Marujido, and discover his true intentions. Inquire at the Orastery if you lose track of him.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 6 crystals to any Conquest Overseer to unlock this mission or do the repeatable mission (2-2) until you have enough Rank Points.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After starting the mission at any Windurst Gate Guard speak to Kupipi in Heavens Tower who will give you the Key item: Starway Stairway bauble. \010\010You will be granted access to the upper portion of Heavens Tower. Check the door on the left to go up.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Rhy Epocan at the top of the tower for a cutscene.\010\010Use the blue teleporter at the top of the tower to return to the main floor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak to Hakkuru-Rinkuru at the Orastery in Port Windurst (Port Windurst (E-7)) for hints on Ajido-Marujido's whereabouts.",["zone"]="Port Windurst",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Castle Oztroja and fall down the trap door ((Castle Oztroja (I-8)) First map.) it will trigger a cutscene upon landing.\010\010Enter and go to (I-8). There will be two switches (not torches) and a fairly obvious floor panel. One switch will open the door, one will open the floor. Stand in between the two switches and check one. If it opens the door, check the other. They randomly switch, so it will never be the same, day by day.\010\010The person doing the mission must be the one to pull the lever. Multiple people doing this mission will need to stand back until the trap door closes then individually pull the lever.\010\010In the same room you drop into there is a trap door on the floor (blank target), which is for the Onion Rings quest. You can collect Key item: Old Ring without having the quest flagged.",["zone"]="Castle Oztroja",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Rhy Epocan to complete the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_328",["title"]="To the Forsaken Mines (Bastok Mission 3-2)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 3-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_3-2",["revision"]="119856",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 3-1|The Four Musketeers",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Bring back a rare ore from the Gusgen Mines on the Konschtat Highlands. First ask Davyad, an adventurer residing in the Mines District, how he acquired his load of the ore.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="This mission is optional. If you decide to do this mission, give the Guard a crystal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Hare Meat.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Accept the mission and then speak to Davyad (K-6) in Bastok Mines.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Gusgen Mines in Konschtat Highlands. \010\010You will need Sneak or Silent Oils in here unless you are of sufficient level, /check the monsters to make sure they are incredibly easy prey or too weak.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once inside the mines, take a right. \010\010At the next intersection, take a left. \010\010At the fork, take a right, and then another right at the next intersection. \010\010You should be at (J-7). \010\010Take caution of Smothered Schmidt who spawns in the same area at either 0:00, 1:00, or 2:00 when the siren in the zone sounds.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Hare Meat to the ??? to spawn Blind Moby, a Pugil NM. \010\010It will drop a Rare/Ex item called Glocolite. Everyone doing this mission will require one, so defeat the NM as many times as required.\010\010 You must wait 3 minute between pops.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Glocolite to Rashid (H-10) in Bastok Mines to finish the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2564",["title"]="Toraimarai Turmoil",["page_title"]="Toraimarai Turmoil",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Toraimarai_Turmoil",["revision"]="75374",["requirements"]="Start: Ohbiru-Dohbiru \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (J-9) / South\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 6\010Items: Starmite Shell x3\010Previous: Blue Ribbon Blues",["rewards"]="4,500 gil\010Key item: Rhinostery Certificate",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Become a certified Rhinostery adventurer in order to enter the Toraimarai Canal and cull the Starmites that are causing havoc there. Bring back the shells of three Starmites to receive your reward.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Note: After Blue Ribbon Blues, you will have to zone out and back in to get the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon accepting the quest, you will receive a Key item: Rhinostery Certificate which will provide access to Toraimarai Canal via Windurst Walls.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Ohbiru-Dohbiru. The Rhinostery wants you to kill Starmites in Toraimarai Canal. Collect all the Starmite Shells you can gather and bring them back to the Rhinostery.\010\010There are 2 paths to the Toraimarai Canal (G-8):",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Path 1 (Priming Gate)\010\010This path requires the Key item: Rhinostery Certificate for access.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Starting from the Priming Gate at Windurst Walls (H-3), zone into Toraimarai Canal (requires the Key item: Rhinostery Certificate).",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="H-3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At first intersection head east, follow path",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Down stairs at I-8 & head east",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make 2 right turns at I-10",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Up stairs at I-9",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You find the Starmites at (Toraimarai Canal (G-8))",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Path 2 (Horutoto Ruins)\010\010This path requires a WHM, a BLM and a RDM OR the Key item: Portal Charm for access.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Starting from the Lily Tower at East Sarutabaruta (J-7), zone into Inner Horutoto Ruins.",["zone"]="East Sarutabaruta",["grid"]="J-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Cracked wall at G-8",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Magic Gate of Horutoto at E-10",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Cracked Wall at D-10",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Pass through the Three Mage Gate at Inner Horutoto Ruins (H-9) \226\128\148 Rose Tower 1 (requires a WHM, a BLM and a RDM OR the Key item: Portal Charm)",["zone"]="Inner Horutoto Ruins",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Through false wall at H-8",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Toraimarai Canal door at H-6 & zone into Toraimarai Canal",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Cross bridge at H-6",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Down stairs at H-7 & turn right at intersection",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Up stairs at H-9",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Cross bridge at I-8",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Down stairs at J-9 & head east to 2nd map",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Up stairs at F-8",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Down stairs at H-10",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Up stairs at I-9",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You find the Starmites at (Toraimarai Canal (G-8))",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Finishing the Quest",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ohbiru-Dohbiru will reward you with 4,500 gil for every 3 Starmite Shells that you bring him. Must talk to him each time to trade another 3.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57522",["title"]="Totoroon's Treasure Hunt",["page_title"]="Totoroon's Treasure Hunt",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Totoroon%27s_Treasure_Hunt",["revision"]="121853",["requirements"]="Start: Totoroon \226\128\148 Nashmau (G-8) / Map 1\010Fame: Treasures of Aht Urhgan\010Items: One Date, Pamamas, or Kazham Pineapple\010Several Sickles, Hatchets, or Pickaxes, depending on the assigned zone",["rewards"]="Various crafting materials or a ??? Box",["repeatable"]="yes",["summary"]="Totoroon has found a \034soooper-doooper\034 treasure. He will tell you where it is hidden in exchange for something sweet.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="The gathering outcomes, quest-completion trigger, and reward pools below are based on original-era documentation and require confirmation on HorizonXI. [Wiki: needs verification]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Starting the Quest",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Totoroon in the port area of Nashmau at Nashmau (G-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="G-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Totoroon asks you to bring him something sweet.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade him one of the following:\010\010 1 Date\010\010 1 Pamamas\010\010 1 Kazham Pineapple",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Totoroon will direct you to one of four gathering zones.\010\010 Speak with him again if you forget the assigned zone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone Assignment\010\010The fruit determines which pair of zones may be selected:\010\010! Sweet\010! Possible Assigned Zones\010! Activity\010! Tool\010! Possible Notorious Monster\010|-\010| Date\010| Wajaom Woodlands or Bhaflau Thickets\010| Harvesting\010| Sickle\010| Berried Chigoe, assisted by five Chigoe's Nits\010|-\010| Pamamas\010| Wajaom Woodlands or Bhaflau Thickets\010| Harvesting\010| Sickle\010| Berried Chigoe, assisted by five Chigoe's Nits\010|-\010| Kazham Pineapple\010| Caedarva Mire\010| Logging\010| Hatchet\010| Ravin Raven\010|-\010| Kazham Pineapple\010| Mount Zhayolm\010| Mining\010| Pickaxe\010| Ancient Bombs",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The exact zone chosen from the applicable pair is random.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring several gathering tools because they may break during use.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The quest target may be obtained from any normal gathering point within the assigned zone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Gathering the Treasure",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the zone specified by Totoroon.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the appropriate gathering tool at its normal gathering points:\010\010 Wajaom Woodlands or Bhaflau Thickets: Harvest with a Sickle.\010\010 Caedarva Mire: Log with a Hatchet.\010\010 Mount Zhayolm: Mine with a Pickaxe.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue gathering until a quest-specific result occurs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Successful Gathering",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A message indicates that you have a feeling something may be found there.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You receive a special crafting material or a ??? Box without a battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the special item is obtained, return to Totoroon.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notorious Monster Result",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A warning message indicates that you have a bad feeling.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The corresponding Notorious Monster appears:\010\010 Berried Chigoe and five Chigoe's Nits in Wajaom Woodlands or Bhaflau Thickets.\010\010 Ravin Raven in Caedarva Mire.\010\010 Ancient Bombs in Mount Zhayolm.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeating the monster is strongly recommended so it does not remain near the gathering point and attack other players.\010\010 Check the monster's treasure pool after the battle.\010\010 Continue gathering afterward until a quest-specific item is obtained.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Returning to Totoroon",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After obtaining a special reward\226\128\148or after completing the Notorious Monster event\226\128\148return to Totoroon at Nashmau (G-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="G-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with him to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Appraising a ??? Box",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the ??? Box to Memeroon, the item appraiser at Nashmau (G-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="G-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The box appraises into a crafting material.\010\010 Wajaom Woodlands and Bhaflau Thickets boxes are reported to favor Clothcraft materials.\010\010 Caedarva Mire and Mount Zhayolm boxes are reported to favor Goldsmithingmaterials.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57397",["title"]="Transformations",["page_title"]="Transformations",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Transformations",["revision"]="123636",["requirements"]="Start: Waoud \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-10) / Map 1 \226\128\148 On the upper level of Heretic's Alley.\010Requirements: Blue Mage level 50+ as the player's main job to begin\010Complete Omens\010Zone and wait until the following Vana'diel day\0101,000 gil\010Level: 50\010Fame: None\010Items: Up to 2 Imperial Silver Pieces unless another form of access to the Alzadaal Undersea Ruins is available\010Previous: Omens",["rewards"]="Magus Keffiyeh",["repeatable"]="af",["summary"]="A juvenile soulflayer has been discovered in the Alzadaal Undersea Ruins. Make your way to the ruins and eliminate this threat.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Starting the Quest",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete Omens.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone and wait until the following Vana'diel day.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Set Blue Mage as your main job at level 50 or higher.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Waoud at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (J-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="J-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select Gaze away. and pay 1,000 gil for a divination.\010\010 Waoud will direct you toward the gate of nobility.\010\010 This divination is required to advance the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Imperial Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-8) / Map 1 for a cutscene.\010\010 The quest is formally added to the current quest log after this cutscene.\010\010 Lathuya can begin commissioning the remaining three pieces of Blue Mage Artifact Armor after this cutscene.\010\010 Blue Mage is no longer required as the main job for the remaining quest steps.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="L-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Alzadaal Undersea Ruins Cutscenes\010\010The following route obtains both required cutscenes through the eastern side of Caedarva Mire.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Nashmau.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Leave Nashmau through the eastern exit at Nashmau (H-8) / Map 1 to enter Caedarva Mire.",["zone"]="Nashmau",["grid"]="H-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Tyamah at Caedarva Mire (J-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Caedarva Mire",["grid"]="J-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the Alzadaal Undersea Ruins using one of the following methods:\010\010 Trade one Imperial Silver Piece to Tyamah.\010\010 Speak with Tyamah while possessing the Key item: Captain Wildcat Badge.\010\010 Speak with Tyamah while possessing a Key item: Remnants Permit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After entering the ruins, proceed south toward the room containing the teleporters.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The first required cutscene triggers automatically before reaching the teleporters.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the western teleporter.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After taking the teleporter, walk toward the Mount Zhayolm exit for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After viewing both cutscenes, leave the ruins or return to Nashmau.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Alternative Cutscene Route\010\010The two cutscenes may also be reached through the Nyzul Isle Staging Point teleporter network if that destination is available. The Tyamah route above is generally more direct and does not require navigating the central Alzadaal teleporter hub.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Nepionic Soulflayer",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Nashmau and leave through the western exit into Caedarva Mire.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel west to Nasheefa at Caedarva Mire (E-11) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Caedarva Mire",["grid"]="E-11 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the Alzadaal Undersea Ruins using one of the following methods:\010\010 Trade one Imperial Silver Piece to Nasheefa.\010\010 Speak with Nasheefa while possessing the Key item: Captain Wildcat Badge.\010Speak with Nasheefa while possessing a Key item: Remnants Permit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After entering Alzadaal Undersea Ruins, use the northern teleporter at Alzadaal Undersea Ruins (I-9) / Map 12.",["zone"]="Alzadaal Undersea Ruins",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 12",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the unnamed target in the northwestern corner at Alzadaal Undersea Ruins (G-7) / Map 12.",["zone"]="Alzadaal Undersea Ruins",["grid"]="G-7 / Map 12",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A short cutscene plays and the Nepionic Soulflayer appears.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat the Nepionic Soulflayer.\010\010 NOTE: This was easily defeated by a solo 75SMN.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the same target at Alzadaal Undersea Ruins (G-7) / Map 12 again.",["zone"]="Alzadaal Undersea Ruins",["grid"]="G-7 / Map 12",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete the resulting cutscene to receive:\010\010 Magus Keffiyeh\010\010 The title Paragon of Blue Mage Excellence",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Dvucca Isle Alternative\010\010The battle area can also be approached from the Dvucca Isle Staging Point. Do not take this path unless you have already completed the cutscenes in the ruins.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the Dvucca Isle Staging Point.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head south through Caedarva Mire Map 2 to Nuimahn at Caedarva Mire (I-10) / Map 2.",["zone"]="Caedarva Mire",["grid"]="I-10 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the Alzadaal Undersea Ruins by trading an Imperial Silver Piece or using another valid form of entry.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed to the unnamed target at Alzadaal Undersea Ruins (G-7) / Map 12.",["zone"]="Alzadaal Undersea Ruins",["grid"]="G-7 / Map 12",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={"Blue Mage (BLU)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Blue Mage (BLU)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Magus Keffiyeh",["revision"]="120736"},{["job"]="Blue Mage (BLU)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Transformations",["revision"]="123636"}}},{["id"]="wiki_3712",["title"]="Trial by Earth",["page_title"]="Trial by Earth",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Trial_by_Earth",["revision"]="115173",["requirements"]="Start: Juroro \226\128\148 Port Bastok (I-8)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 6",["rewards"]="Ability to summon Titan or\01010,000g or\010Desert Light or\010Earth Belt or\010Earth Ring or\010Titan's Cudgel",["repeatable"]="Yes, after Japanese midnight after receiving your reward.",["summary"]="Bring the tuning fork of earth upon the protocrystal in the Quicksand Caves. A path will open to the trial that awaits.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Juroro in Port Bastok, located at I-8 (near the drawbridge). If you have sufficient fame, she will give you a Tuning fork of earth after accepting her request. \010If you have never talked to this NPC before you may have to talk to her a few times before she gives you the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Quicksand Caves, and head to the Cloister of Tremors.\010\010Enter from Eastern Altepa Desert at (Eastern Altepa Desert (J-7)). \010\010In the first room, follow the east wall (hug left), dropping to the east, and following a passage south.\010\010When the path opens into the next room, head due west along the north wall. Through another small passage and into a third room (E/F-9), go to the west wall and drop west.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In the Cloister of Tremors, stick to the right wall to get to the Earth Protocrystal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you defeat Titan Prime, you will acquire the Key item: Whisper of Tremors.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return the Key item: Whisper of Tremors to Juroro for your reward.\010\010Alternatively, hold onto it and when you have all six whispers, you may start the quest The Moonlit Path to fight Fenrir Prime.\010\010If you are collecting items for the Evoker's Ring, you want the Desert Light.\010\010If you see an airship moving through the background of the reward cutscene, this is because an airship arrived or departed during the cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Fight",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Everyone who is involved in the fight must have a tuning fork of the correct protocrystal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is no level cap on this battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is a 30-minute time limit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can buff up before entering the protocrystal, so feel free to do so and rest up while still outside.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Try to fight Titan Prime on Windsday, and do not fight him on Earthsday.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Keep up Barstonra at all times.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Do not use Earth-based spells, weaponskills, or weapons that have Additional effect: Earth, as they will heal Titan Prime.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The battlefield is shaped like a long path up the side of hill, with a switchback about halfway to the top. This allows the mages to stand above the fight (and out of easy reach of the avatar) while still being able to cast spells upon the combatants.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="See testimonials.\010\010See Trial by Earth/Strategies for strategy and videos.\010[Template Prime Avatar Quest Index: ]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_19975",["title"]="Trial by Fire",["page_title"]="Trial by Fire",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Trial_by_Fire",["revision"]="118640",["requirements"]="Start: Ronta-Onta \226\128\148 Kazham (J-9)\010Fame: Kazham\010Fame level: 6",["rewards"]="Ability to summon Ifrit or\01010,000g or\010Egil's Torch or\010Fire Belt or\010Fire Ring or\010Ifrit's Blade",["repeatable"]="Yes, after Japanese midnight after receiving your reward.",["summary"]="Ring the tuning fork of fire upon the protocrystal in Ifrit's Cauldron. A path will open to the trial that awaits.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Ronta-Onta in Kazham (J-9). If you have sufficient fame, he will give you a Key item: Tuning fork of fire.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Ifrit's Cauldron and head to the Cloister of Flames where you face Ifrit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Reaching the Cloister",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To get to the Cloister of Flames, enter Ifrit's Cauldron from Yhoator Jungle (I-5).",["zone"]="Yhoator Jungle",["grid"]="I-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon entering, follow the right-hand wall (northwest). A flame spout will block your path and you can either wait for it to go down (may take up to 15 minutes), or trade an Ice Cluster to it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow the path west. When it splits, continue west through the cave to the end of the path. Turn south and fall down to a lower level at Ifrit's Cauldron (I-8) / Map 2 (drop P).",["zone"]="Ifrit's Cauldron",["grid"]="I-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After falling, head back north until you come to two sets of posts at Ifrit's Cauldron (H-7) / Map 7 and walk off the edge between them. Once you drop, there's only one path you can take. Do so, and take the first left.",["zone"]="Ifrit's Cauldron",["grid"]="H-7 / Map 7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the Battle",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you defeat Ifrit Prime, you will acquire the Key item: Whisper of Flames.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return the Key item: Whisper of Flames to Ronta-Onta for your reward.\010\010Alternatively, hold onto it and when you have all six whispers, you may start the quest The Moonlit Path to fight Fenrir Prime.\010\010If you are collecting items for the Evoker's Ring, you will want the Egil's Torch from Ronta-Onta.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Fight",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Everyone who is involved in the fight must have a tuning fork of the correct protocrystal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is no cap on this battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is a 30-minute time limit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can buff up before entering the protocrystal, so feel free to do so and rest up while still outside.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Try to fight Ifrit Prime on Watersday and do not fight him on Firesday.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Keep up Barfira at all times.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Do not use Fire-based spells, weaponskills, or weapons that have Additional effect: Fire, as they will heal Ifrit Prime.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The battlefield is shaped like a long path up the side of a hill, with a switchback about halfway to the top. This allows the mages to stand above the fight (and out of easy reach of the avatar) while still being able to cast spells on party members. \010\010[Template Prime Avatar Quest Index: ]\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Ronta-Onta (Near Wahcondalo's Residence, Kazham)]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Kazham",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7455",["title"]="Trial by Ice",["page_title"]="Trial by Ice",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Trial_by_Ice",["revision"]="101812",["requirements"]="Start: Gulmama \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (E-7)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 6",["rewards"]="Ability to summon Shiva or\01010,000g or\010Rust 'B' Gone or\010Ice Belt or\010Ice Ring or\010Shiva's Claws",["repeatable"]="Yes, after Japanese midnight after receiving your reward.",["summary"]="Ring the tuning fork of ice upon the protocrystal in Fei'Yin. A path will open to the trial that awaits.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Gulmama in Northern San d'Oria (E-7). If you have sufficient fame, she will give you a Key item: Tuning fork of ice.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Fei'Yin and head to the Cloister of Frost.\010\010To get to the Cloister of Frost, enter Fei'Yin from Beaucedine Glacier (J-4). \010\010Follow the path to a large room and take the east passage. Ignore the branch south and pass through a small room, turn north and follow the path back west. Ignore the branch north and descend the stairs; leading you to the second map. \010\010The path forces you north and east, again, and into a small room (H-8). Here, follow the left wall (north) until it opens into a large room (full of Utukkus, Golems and Bats); continue north. \010\010The north exit (a short distance from where you entered) leads a winding path through several small rooms (populated by Specters, then Weapons), eventually leading to the Cloister of Frost.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you defeat Shiva Prime, you will acquire the Key item: Whisper of Frost.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return the Whisper to Gulmama for your reward.\010\010Alternatively, hold onto it and when you have all six whispers, you may start the quest The Moonlit Path to fight Fenrir Prime.\010\010If you are collecting items for the Evoker's Ring, you will want the Rust 'B' Gone from Gulmama.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Fight",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Everyone who is involved in the fight must have a tuning fork of the correct protocrystal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is no cap on this battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is a 30-minute time limit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can buff up before entering the protocrystal, so feel free to do so and rest up while still outside.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Try to fight Shiva Prime on Firesday and do not fight her on Iceday.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Keep up Barblizzara at all times.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Do not use Ice-based spells, weaponskills, or weapons that have Additional effect: Ice, as they will heal Shiva Prime.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The battlefield is shaped like a long path up the side of hill, with a switchback about halfway to the top. This allows the mages to stand above the fight (and out of easy reach of the avatar) while still being able to cast spells upon the combatants.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="See testimonials.\010\010See Trial by Ice/Strategies for strategy and videos.\010[Template Prime Avatar Quest Index: ]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_11866",["title"]="Trial by Lightning",["page_title"]="Trial by Lightning",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Trial_by_Lightning",["revision"]="24588",["requirements"]="Start: Ripapa \226\128\148 Mhaura (I-9)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 6",["rewards"]="Ability to summon Ramuh or\01010,000g or\010Elder Branch or\010Lightning Belt or\010Lightning Ring or\010Ramuh's Staff",["repeatable"]="avatar",["summary"]="Ring the tuning fork of lightning upon the protocrystal in the Boyahda Tree. A path will open to the trial that awaits.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Ripapa in Mhaura. If you have sufficient fame, she will give you a Key item: Tuning fork of lightning. \010If you have never talked to this NPC before you may have to talk to her a few times before she gives you the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Boyahda Tree and find the Cloister of Storms.\010\010Enter Boyahda Tree from The Sanctuary of Zi'Tah at (The Sanctuary of Zi'Tah (K-12)). \010\010Follow the path to the first fork, take a left. Take the next right and follow that until you come to a large room with a huge tree in the middle. \010\010Travel northwest through the big room and through a second big room until you get to (The Boyahda Tree (A-7) / Map 1) and head up the tunnel. You will go up another level and eventually come out at (The Boyahda Tree (E-6) / Map 2) of another map and another huge room. \010\010Head south-east as much as possible until you see an immense waterfall. Walk under the big waterfall and down the passageway behind it. You will zone into the Cloister of Storms.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you defeat Ramuh, you will acquire the Key item: Whisper of Storms.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return the Whisper to Ripapa for your reward.\010\010Alternatively, hold onto it and when you have all six whispers, you may start the quest The Moonlit Path to fight Fenrir Prime.\010\010If you are collecting items for the Evoker's Ring, you will want the Elder Branch from Ripapa.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Fight",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Alliances are not allowed, they will be broken up into separate battlefields.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Everyone who is involved in the fight must have a tuning fork of the correct protocrystal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is no cap on this battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is a 30-minute time limit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can buff up before entering the protocrystal, so feel free to do so and rest up while still outside.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Try to fight Ramuh Prime on Earthsday and do not fight him on Lightningday or during a New Moon Phase [Wiki: needs verification] .",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Keep up Barthundra at all times.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Do not use Thunder-based spells, weaponskills, or weapons that have Additional effect: Lightning, as they will heal Ramuh Prime.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The battlefield is shaped like a long path up the side of hill, with a switchback about halfway to the top. This allows the mages to stand above the fight (and out of easy reach of the avatar) while still being able to cast spells upon the combatants.\010\010[Template Prime Avatar Quest Index: ]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_10507",["title"]="Trial by Water",["page_title"]="Trial by Water",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Trial_by_Water",["revision"]="114870",["requirements"]="Start: Edal-Tahdal \226\128\148 Norg (H-9)\010Fame: Tenshodo\010Fame level: 4",["rewards"]="Ability to summon Leviathan or\01010,000 Gil or\010Eye of Nept or\010Water Belt or\010Water Ring or\010Leviathan's Rod",["repeatable"]="Yes, after Japanese midnight after receiving your reward.",["summary"]="Ring the tuning fork of water upon the protocrystal in the Den of Rancor. A path will open to the trial that awaits.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Edal-Tahdal located at Norg (H-9). If you have sufficient fame, he will give you a Key item: Tuning fork of water.",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Den of Rancor and find the Cloister of Tides.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Reaching the Cloister",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To get to the Cloister of Tides, head to the main entrance of Temple of Uggalepih at (J-11) in Yhoator Jungle) and go inside. One person will need a Key item: Paintbrush of Souls to enter the Den of Rancor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From the entrance take every right until you zone back out to Yhoator Jungle, then take every left you can until you zone back into the Temple.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take a right and once you come to the corner, head south. There is a wooden gate here that someone will have to open. Head south as far as you can, around the small square, then east until you come to a granite door. To get through this door, you need to kill the Temple Guardian. Once the Temple Guardian is dead, the door will open automatically and stay open for a couple of minutes.\010\010WARNING: If you go through this door and it closes behind you, you cannot get back out unless someone kills the Temple Guardian on the previous side.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head through the door and go north through the Manipulator room, following the path toward a another granite door.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go through the door and have someone with the Key item: Paintbrush of Souls examine the stone picture frame on the east wall.\010\010Once the prompt says: \034By focusing your thoughts on the paintbrush of souls, a new painting begins to appear on the canvas...\034 you must then wait 30 seconds to a minute before advancing the dialogue, or the door will not open. If you fail to focus an image on the canvas, wait a few moments and try again.\010\010If the chat log mentions the paintbrush twitching, your character is too far away from the wall.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A door will open to the north, head through it to enter the Den of Rancor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Descending the path brings you to a room with many exits. Head to the southeast corner of that room and take the easternmost passage. Follow the right wall of that tunnel until you see a hole in the floor at (J-7).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Drop through the hole and head northeast, zoning into the Cloister of Tides.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the Battle",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After defeating Leviathan Prime, you will acquire Key item: Whisper of Tides.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return the Whisper to Edal-Tahdal for your reward.\010\010Alternatively, hold onto it and when you have all six whispers, you may start the quest The Moonlit Path to fight Fenrir Prime.\010\010If you are collecting items for the Evoker's Ring, you will want the Eye of Nept from Edal-Tahdal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Fight",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Everyone who is involved in the fight must have a tuning fork of the correct protocrystal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is no cap on this battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is a 30-minute time limit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can buff up before entering the protocrystal, so feel free to do so and rest up while still outside.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Try to fight Leviathan Prime on Lightningday and do not fight him on Watersday.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Keep up Barwatera at all times.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Leviathan will use his ability, Grand Fall. Beware, as this attack bypasses shadows.\010\010He will also use Tidal Wave.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Do not use Water-based spells, weaponskills, or weapons that have Additional effect: Water, as they will heal Leviathan Prime.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The battlefield is shaped like a long path up the side of a hill, with a switchback about halfway to the top. This allows the mages to stand above the fight (and out of easy reach of the avatar) while still being able to cast spells on party members. \010See Trial by Water strategies for strategies.\010\010Can be solo'd by a 75 BST.\010[Template Prime Avatar Quest Index: ]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Tenshodo",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_11825",["title"]="Trial by Wind",["page_title"]="Trial by Wind",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Trial_by_Wind",["revision"]="101799",["requirements"]="Start: Agado-Pugado \226\128\148 Rabao (G-9)\010Fame: Selbina/Rabao\010Fame level: 5\010Items: Key item: Tuning fork of wind",["rewards"]="Ability to summon Garuda or\01010,000g or\010Bubbly Water or\010Wind Belt or\010Wind Ring or\010Garuda's Dagger",["repeatable"]="avatar",["summary"]="Ring the tuning fork of wind upon the protocrystal in Cape Teriggan. A path will open to the trial that awaits.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Agado-Pugado in Rabao. If you have sufficient fame, he will give you a Key item: Tuning fork of wind.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Cape Teriggan and head to the Cloister of Gales.\010\010To get to the Cloister of Gales, travel to F-7 in Cape Teriggan. From here, follow a tunnel west, off the map. \010This area is filled with very dangerous creatures, such as Manticores and high-level goblins. Sneak and Invisible are needed at all times.\010\010Follow the left wall as it leads northeast, then northwest and you will eventually find the Cloister of Gales.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Target the protocrystal and select \034Trial by Wind\034 to enter the battlefield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you defeat Garuda Prime, you will acquire the Key item: Whisper of Gales.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return the Whisper to Agado-Pugado for your reward.\010\010Alternatively, hold onto it and when you have all six whispers, you may start the quest The Moonlit Path to fight Fenrir Prime.\010\010If you are collecting items for the Evoker's Ring, you will want the Bubbly Water from Agado-Pugado.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Fight",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Everyone who is involved in the fight must have a tuning fork of the correct protocrystal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is no cap on this battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is a 30-minute time limit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can buff up before entering the protocrystal, so feel free to do so and rest up while still outside.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Try to fight Garuda on Ice and not on Wind.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The battlefield is shaped like a long path up the side of hill, with a switchback about halfway to the top. This allows the mages to stand above the fight (and out of easy reach of the avatar) while still being able to cast spells upon the combatants.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If soloing as DRG make sure to have Call Wyvern ready as its a great chance the wyvern will die before the fight is over.(Wyvern died every prime fight for me since i didnt use Spirit Link to cure it as i didnt want Avatar to 2hr while I was down to about 10% hp due to ability use.)\010See Trial by Wind/Strategies for strategies and videos.\010\010[Template Prime Avatar Quest Index: ]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Selbina/Rabao",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3711",["title"]="Trial Size Trial by Earth",["page_title"]="Trial Size Trial by Earth",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Trial_Size_Trial_by_Earth",["revision"]="104352",["requirements"]="Start: Ferrol \226\128\148 Port Bastok (I-8)\010Requirements: Summoner Level 20+\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 2",["rewards"]="Ability to summon Titan\010Scroll of Instant Warp",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The Rhinostery has developed a new \034mini\034 tuning fork of earth. Ringing it upon the protocrystal in the Quicksand Caves will open the path to a one-on-one battle with the beast that awaits inside. However, only summoners are allowed to take up this challenge.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Ferrol in Port Bastok, located at I-8 near the drawbridge. You must speak to Ferrol as a Summoner.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you qualify, he will give you a Mini Tuning Fork of Earth. \010\010This item is not a Key Item like the regular Tuning Forks, but is a Rare/Exclusive item that needs to go in your inventory.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you are ready to go, return to Ferrol and trade him the Mini Tuning Fork of Earth (he does not keep the fork) and be warped to the Cloister of Tremors for the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Mini Tuning Fork to the protocrystal to enter the battle. \010\010Note that if you do not trade the Mini Tuning Fork and instead just select the protocrystal, you will enter the regular level 60+ party avatar battle if you have the regular tuning fork key item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat him for your reward.\010\010If you loose the fight, drop the fork and talk to Ferrol after 1 Vanadiel Day for another fork and repeat the process.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This is a solo battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is a level 20 cap on this battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is a 15 minute time limit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can only use Carbuncle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Keep up Barstonra at all times.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Try to fight Titan Prime on Windsday and do not fight him on Earthsday.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you complete this quest you keep the Mini Tuning Fork of Earth, [Horizon change] Horizon specific change is when you obtain an Avatar any route you can no longer use a mini fork for teleport to a Protocrystal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_51888",["title"]="Trial Size Trial by Fire",["page_title"]="Trial Size Trial by Fire",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Trial_Size_Trial_by_Fire",["revision"]="119725",["requirements"]="Start: Dodmos \226\128\148 Kazham (J-9)\010Requirements: Summoner Level 20+\010Fame: Kazham\010Fame level: 2",["rewards"]="Ability to summon Ifrit\010Scroll of Instant Warp",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Dodmos in Kazham, located at J-9 near the homepoint crystal. You must speak to Dodmos as a Summoner.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you qualify, he will give you a Mini Tuning Fork of Fire. \010\010This item is not a Key Item like the regular Tuning Forks, but is a Rare/Exclusive item that needs to go in your inventory.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you are ready to go, return to Dodmos and trade him the Mini Tuning Fork of Fire (he does not keep the fork) and be warped to the Cloister of Flames for the fight.\010\010Note: the NPC warp only works when your main job is Summoner.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Mini Tuning Fork to the protocrystal to enter the battle. \010\010Note that if you do not trade the Mini Tuning Fork and instead just select the protocrystal, you will enter the regular level 60+ party avatar battle if you have the regular tuning fork key item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat him for your reward.\010\010If you lose the fight, drop the fork and talk to Dodmos after 1 Vanadiel Day for another fork and repeat the process.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Kazham",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7454",["title"]="Trial Size Trial by Ice",["page_title"]="Trial Size Trial by Ice",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Trial_Size_Trial_by_Ice",["revision"]="119726",["requirements"]="Start: Castilchat \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (E-7)\010Requirements: Summoner Level 20+\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 2",["rewards"]="Ability to summon Shiva\010Scroll of Instant Warp",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Castilchat in Northern San d'Oria. You must speak to Castilchat as a Summoner.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you qualify, he will give you a Mini Tuning Fork of Ice.\010\010This item is not a Key Item like the regular Tuning Forks, but is a Rare/Exclusive item that needs to go in your inventory.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you are ready to go, return to Castilchat and trade him the Mini Tuning Fork of Ice (he does not keep the fork) and be warped to the Cloister of Frost for the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Mini Tuning Fork to the protocrystal to enter the battle. \010\010Note that if you do not trade the Mini Tuning Fork and instead just select the protocrystal, you will enter the regular level 60+ party avatar battle if you have the regular tuning fork key item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat her for your reward.\010\010If you loose the fight, drop the fork and talk to Castilchat after 1 Vanadiel Day for another fork and repeat the process.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This is a solo battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is a level 20 cap on this battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is a 15 minute time limit.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can only use Carbuncle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Try to fight Shiva on Firesday and do not fight her on Iceday.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you complete this quest you keep the Mini Tuning Fork of Ice, [Horizon change] Horizon specific change is when you obtain an Avatar any route you can no longer use a mini fork for teleport to a Protocrystal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_51896",["title"]="Trial Size Trial by Lightning",["page_title"]="Trial Size Trial by Lightning",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Trial_Size_Trial_by_Lightning",["revision"]="119727",["requirements"]="Start: Lacia \226\128\148 Mhaura (I-9)\010Requirements: Summoner Level 20+\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 2",["rewards"]="Ability to summon Ramuh\010Scroll of Instant Warp",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Lacia in Mhaura, located at I-9, on the second level, across from the Sailors' Stay. You must speak to Lacia as a Summoner.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you qualify, she will give you a Mini Tuning Fork of Lightning. \010\010This item is not a Key Item like the regular Tuning Forks, but is a Rare/Exclusive item that needs to go in your inventory.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you are ready to go, return to Lacia and trade her the Mini Tuning Fork of Lightning (she does not keep the fork) and be warped to the Cloister of Storms for the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Mini Tuning Fork to the protocrystal to enter the battle. \010\010Note that if you do not trade the Mini Tuning Fork and instead just select the protocrystal, you will enter the regular level 60+ party avatar battle if you have the regular tuning fork key item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat him for your reward.\010\010If you loose the fight, drop the fork and talk to Lacia after 1 Vanadiel Day for another fork and repeat the process.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_51895",["title"]="Trial Size Trial by Water",["page_title"]="Trial Size Trial by Water",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Trial_Size_Trial_by_Water",["revision"]="119723",["requirements"]="Start: Verctissa \226\128\148 Norg (H-9)\010Requirements: Summoner Level 20+\010Fame: Norg\010Fame level: 2",["rewards"]="Ability to summon Leviathan\010Scroll of Instant Warp",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Verctissa (H-9) in Norg. You must speak to Verctissa as a Summoner.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you qualify, she will give you a Mini Tuning Fork of Water. \010\010This item is not a Key Item like the regular Tuning Forks, but is a Rare/Exclusive item that needs to go in your inventory.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you are ready to go, return to Verctissa and trade her the Mini Tuning Fork of Water (she does not keep the fork) and be warped to the Cloister of Tides for the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Mini Tuning Fork to the protocrystal to enter the battle. \010\010Note that if you do not trade the Mini Tuning Fork and instead just select the protocrystal, you will enter the regular level 60+ party avatar battle if you have the regular tuning fork key item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat him for your reward.\010\010If you loose the fight, drop the fork and talk to Verctissa after 1 Vanadiel Day for another fork and repeat the process.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Norg",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2716",["title"]="Trial Size Trial by Wind",["page_title"]="Trial Size Trial by Wind",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Trial_Size_Trial_by_Wind",["revision"]="119724",["requirements"]="Start: Rahi Fohlatti \226\128\148 Rabao (G-9)\010Requirements: Summoner Level 20+\010Fame: Rabao\010Fame level: 2",["rewards"]="Ability to summon Garuda\010Scroll of Instant Warp",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Rahi Fohlatti in Rabao as a Summoner.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you qualify, she will give you a Mini Tuning Fork of Wind. \010\010This item is not a Key Item like the regular Tuning Forks, but is a Rare/Exclusive item that needs to go in your inventory.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you are ready to go, return to Rahi Fohlatti and trade her the Mini Tuning Fork of Wind (she does not keep the fork) to be warped to the Cloister of Gales for the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Mini Tuning Fork to the protocrystal to enter the battle. \010\010Note that if you do not trade the Mini Tuning Fork and instead just select the protocrystal, you will enter the regular level 60+ party avatar battle if you have the regular tuning fork key item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat her for your reward.\010\010If you lose the fight, drop the fork and talk to Rahi Fohlatti after 1 Vanadiel Day for another fork and repeat the process.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Rabao",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1482",["title"]="Trouble at the Sluice",["page_title"]="Trouble at the Sluice",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Trouble_at_the_Sluice",["revision"]="60830",["requirements"]="Start: Belgidiveau \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (G-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Dahlia\010Previous: The Rumor",["rewards"]="Heavy Axe",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="It seems poison was thrown into the water near the sluice gates. Find an antidote before someone falls ill.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Belgidiveau thinks the watergate may have been poisoned and asks you to get a counteragent for it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Bostaunieux Oubliette and talk to Novalmauge and ask him to make the counteragent.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He needs you to get a Dahlia first.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Dahlia to Novalmauge and receive the Key item: Neutralizer.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Belgidiveau to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7546",["title"]="True Strength",["page_title"]="True Strength",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/True_Strength",["revision"]="114585",["requirements"]="Start: Ayame \226\128\148 Metalworks (K-7)\010Requirements: Monk 50+\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: non\010Items: Yagudo Drink, Xalmo Feather\010Previous: The First Meeting",["rewards"]="Temple Hose",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="You must defeat a powerful Yagudo in Castle Oztroja. The Yagudo in question can be lured out with a bottle of Yagudo drink.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Ayame in the top level of the Metalworks at K-7. (Ayame is linked to many quests, make sure you get the right one.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="She asks you to defeat a powerful Yagudo, Huu Xalmo the Savage, in Castle Oztroja and recover the Xalmo Feather as proof. \010\010 Note: Once you have talked to Ayame, the quest will show up in your quest log, at this point you may switch to another job to complete the quest. You do not have to fight Huu Xalmo the Savage as a MNK.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will need to trade a Yagudo Drink to a ??? on map 5 H-8 of Castle Oztroja to spawn Huu Xalmo the Savage.\010\010 Note: If more than one person needs the feather you will need to spawn the NM multiple times. There is a cooldown (approx 5-15 mins) on the ???, which will result in a \034But nothing happens.\034 message after a trade. Wait and try again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Ayame and trade the Xalmo Feather to receive the Temple Hose.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={"Monk (MNK)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Monk (MNK)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Temple Hose",["revision"]="19378"},{["job"]="Monk (MNK)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="True Strength",["revision"]="114585"}}},{["id"]="wiki_11948",["title"]="True Will",["page_title"]="True Will",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/True_Will",["revision"]="114780",["requirements"]="Start: Ryoma \226\128\148 Norg (H-8)\010Requirements: Ninja 50+\010Items: Kuftal Coffer Key\010Previous: I'll Take the Big Box",["rewards"]="Ninja Chainmail",["repeatable"]="af",["summary"]="The Sahagin have stolen Mitsunari's treasure and hid it somewhere in the Jungle on Elshimo Island. It is your job to find it.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="With your main job as Ninja, speak with Ryoma Norg (H-8) in Norg who will give you the quest and sends you to Yhoator Jungle.\010\010If you are eligible for the quest Bugi Soden you will be offered that quest instead. \010Speak with him again to receive True Will.</small>",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="H-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the ??? at Yhoator Jungle (I-7) to spawn 3 NM Sahagins:\010Kappa Akuso (Monk) Uses Hundred Fists.\010Kappa Biwa (Bard) Uses Soul Voice.\010Kappa Bonze (White Mage) Uses Benediction.\010Your main job does not need to be NIN to spawn the NM's.\010\010Kappa Bonze may be slept with Lullaby, Sleep or Repose. Akuso and Biwa appear to be immune to the effect.\010\010Only one Kappa needs to be defeated, one strategy for doing this is to run to the Den of Rancor zone, let the other two Kappas move back to the spawn point, and fight one Kappa at the zone. As with other fights using this strategy, you must wait for the other two Kappas to de-spawn before defeating the one you choose to fight.\010\010When using this strategy, it is highly recommended that you do not choose Kappa Akuso as the one you fight. If you do choose to fight Kappa Akuso, fight near the Ifrit's Cauldron zone. Zone immediately after he uses Hundred Fists and wait 20 seconds. Zone back into Yhoator Jungle and fight him again. \010\010Kappa Akuso is also susceptible to Bind and Gravity which may prove to be an easier technique for avoiding Hundred Fists.\010\010You are unable to sneak pop these mobs.\010\010When using this strategy, this fight is known soloable by most jobs at 75 given a solo-friendly job/subjob, and by some jobs at 60.\010\010Take caution if Woodland Sage pops.",["zone"]="Yhoator Jungle",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kill them and examine ??? again to get Key item: Old Trick Box.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take it back to Ryoma who then sends you to Rabao to talk with Leodarion at Rabao (F-7).",["zone"]="Rabao",["grid"]="F-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Leodarion sends you to Kuftal Tunnel.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Open a Treasure Coffer to receive Key item: Large Trick Box.\010\010This can be done as any job; the Large Trick Box can be attained by picking the lock as Thief, or with a Kuftal Coffer Key.If you have the quest Knight Stalker (DRG AF) active, it is possible that you may receive the Key Item associated with that quest, rather than the Large Trick Box.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Lastly, bring the Large Trick Box back to Leodarion to complete the quest and receive your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Ninja (NIN)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Ninja (NIN)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Ninja Chainmail",["revision"]="19578"},{["job"]="Ninja (NIN)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="True Will",["revision"]="114780"}}},{["id"]="wiki_1211",["title"]="Truth, Justice, and the Onion Way!",["page_title"]="Truth, Justice, and the Onion Way!",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Truth%2C_Justice%2C_and_the_Onion_Way%21",["revision"]="75029",["requirements"]="Start: Kohlo-Lakolo \226\128\148 Port Windurst (G-5)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Rarab Tail",["rewards"]="Justice Badge",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="If you want to join the Star Onion Brigade, you had better bring Kohlo-Lakolo some kind of \034tail.\034",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Kohlo-Lakolo Port Windurst (G-5) and watch a cutscene explaining the current situation.",["zone"]="Port Windurst",["grid"]="G-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Kohlo-Lakolo will ask that you bring him a Rarab Tail, an item that is dropped by bumblebees. It can also be bought from a regional vendor (Baehu-Faehu) for 22-24 gil at Windurst Waters (G-5) / North.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="G-5 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a Rarab Tail to Kohlo-Lakolo to receive your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2566",["title"]="Tuning In",["page_title"]="Tuning In",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Tuning_In",["revision"]="119986",["requirements"]="Start: Leepe-Hoppe \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (J-9) / South\010Requirements: Access to Phomiuna Aqueducts (not needed to accept)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Extra-fine File\010Magicked Steel\010Spruce Lumber",["rewards"]="4,000g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="A Mithran Tracker has demanded the construction of a new type of tuning fork so she can converse with the sleeping gods. Help Leepe-Hoppe gather the necessary materials.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Leepe-Hoppe Windurst Waters (J-9) / South requires three items:\010\010Magicked Steel (drops from Bugbear and Goblins in Oldton Movalpolos, and Bugbears in Newton Movalpolos).\010\010Spruce Lumber (drops from Tauri in Phomiuna Aqueducts).\010\010Extra-fine File (drop from the Fomor Warrior, Fomor Samurai, and Fomor Monk that spawn in the watchtower Lufaise Meadows (H-8) and around the campfire Lufaise Meadows (G-6) at night.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="J-9 / South",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade all 3 items to Leepe-Hoppe Windurst Waters (G-3) / North for a final cut-scene and your reward.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="G-3 / North",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2567",["title"]="Tuning Out",["page_title"]="Tuning Out",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Tuning_Out",["revision"]="118841",["requirements"]="Start: Leepe-Hoppe \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (J-9) / South\010Requirements: Promathia Mission 2-3: Distant Beliefs\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Black Curry\010Habaneros\010Mutton Tortilla\010Previous: Tuning In",["rewards"]="6,000g\010Cache-nez",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The Mithran Tracker has taken the new tuning fork and left for a fabled protocrystal said to exist in the Northlands. She has failed to return. Assist Ildy-Goldy in gathering information about the tracker's whereabouts.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Leepe-Hoppe. following Japanese midnight after completing Tuning In to receive this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Kazham and speak with Jakoh Wahcondalo (the Chieftainess) at Kazham (J-9).",["zone"]="Kazham",["grid"]="J-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the Mihgo's residence and speak with Romaa Mihgo at Kazham (H-11). \010\010She will ask you to travel to Gemini Falls in Yuhtunga Jungle (K-7).",["zone"]="Kazham",["grid"]="H-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There, you will see a ??? overlooking the falls and some pools of water.\010You do not need to go through Ifrit's Cauldron to reach the ???.\010Drop down the hole in Yuhtunga Jungle (H-6), go south.\010Take the south-east tunnel in the lower level of Yuhtunga Jungle (I-7).\010When you emerge, the ??? is located at the edge of the cliff on the upper level.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click on the ???, watch a cutscene, and fight the five spawned NM bees called Nasus .",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once defeated, re-examine the ??? and watch another small cutscene.\010Only one person may progress per fight. The fight must be re-done for each person completing this scene, with a respawn time of 15 minutes between fights.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the fight, talk to Romaa Mihgo again for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, to get by Gilgamesh's guard, you will need to gather:\010\010A bunch of Habaneros (dropped from Mantraps in Misareaux Coast)\010\010A serving of Black Curry\010\010A Mutton Tortilla",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Norg and speak with Comitiolus at Norg (K-8) who guards the door to Gilgamesh. Trade him the Black Curry, the Mutton Tortilla, and the Habaneros. \010\010Watch a cutscene with Kamui where you are told by Ildy-Goldy to travel to Beaucedine Glacier and talk with the Tarutaru Rhinostery adventurers in the tower at Beaucedine Glacier (I-7).",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="K-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you arrive at the glacier, talk to Torino-Samarino for another cutscene and 6000 gil.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Leepe-Hoppe in Windurst Waters to get the finishing dialogue and the Cache-nez.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2032",["title"]="Twinstone Bonding",["page_title"]="Twinstone Bonding",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Twinstone_Bonding",["revision"]="114511",["requirements"]="Start: Gioh Ajihri \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (K-5)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Twinstone Earring",["rewards"]="Wrapped Bow (on first completion)\010or\010900 gil (on subsequent completions)",["repeatable"]="yes",["summary"]="Twenty years ago, there was a great battle between the Mithra and the Yagudo in the Meriphataud Mountains. Gioh wants you to collect the twinstone earrings that belonged to the Mithra warriors who fell there.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Kill Hill Lizards or Ridge Lizards in Meriphataud Mountains until they drop a Twinstone Earring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring it back to Gioh Ajihri at Windurst Woods (K-5) for a reward. (If you have the earring already in inventory, you must zone before the earring will be accepted.)",["zone"]="Windurst Woods",["grid"]="K-5",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57521",["title"]="Two Horn the Savage",["page_title"]="Two Horn the Savage",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Two_Horn_the_Savage",["revision"]="121852",["requirements"]="Start: Milazahn \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-8) / Map 1\010Fame: None\010Items: 1,000 gil",["rewards"]="Imperial Mythril Piece",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="The ferocious \034Two Horn the Savage\034 has been wreaking havoc around the Empire, but nobody knows the creature's identity or its whereabouts. You are to lead an investigation into the facts surrounding this frightening beast.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Milazahn at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="G-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Agree to investigate the reports concerning Two Horn the Savage.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Cacaroon at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-11) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="G-11 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade exactly 1,000 gil to Cacaroon.\010\010 Speak with him again after the trade for additional information directing you to Mamook.\010\010 Cacaroon is involved in several other Aht Urhgan quests and missions. If the expected interaction does not occur, exhaust any unrelated dialogue and retry the exact 1,000-gil trade.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to the quest-specific Viscous Liquid at Mamook (E-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Mamook",["grid"]="E-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Mamook",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Via an Activated Mamool Ja Staging Point",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the Chamber of Passage at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (L-7) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="L-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Use the Runic Portal to travel to the Mamool Ja Staging Point.\010\010 The destination must already be activated.\010\010 Use a Runic Portal Use Permit. Players traveling under Mamool Ja Assault orders cannot leave through the exterior gate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You arrive in Bhaflau Thickets at Bhaflau Thickets (H-11) / Map 2.",["zone"]="Bhaflau Thickets",["grid"]="H-11 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Exit the staging point through the Heavy Iron Gate at Bhaflau Thickets (H-10) / Map 2.",["zone"]="Bhaflau Thickets",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Bhaflau Thickets (I-9) / Map 2 and enter Mamook.",["zone"]="Bhaflau Thickets",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You arrive in Mamook near Mamook (F-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Mamook",["grid"]="F-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel northwest to the Viscous Liquid at Mamook (E-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Mamook",["grid"]="E-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Overland Route",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Leave Aht Urhgan Whitegate for Wajaom Woodlands through the gate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (H-10) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="H-10 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You enter Wajaom Woodlands near Wajaom Woodlands (M-7).",["zone"]="Wajaom Woodlands",["grid"]="M-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel southwest and enter Mamook at Wajaom Woodlands (D-12).",["zone"]="Wajaom Woodlands",["grid"]="D-12",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You arrive in Mamook at Mamook (J-7) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Mamook",["grid"]="J-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed through Mamook Map 1 to the Viscous Liquid at Mamook (E-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Mamook",["grid"]="E-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Mamook Investigation",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Viscous Liquid for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine it a second time to spawn a Mamool Ja.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat the Mamool Ja.\010\010 Nearby Mamool Ja may link or interfere with the battle, so clear or avoid the surrounding enemies before spawning it.\010\010 Once the quest NM has been defeated, changing areas does not erase the kill progress.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Examine the Viscous Liquid again after defeating the Mamool Ja for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Milazahn at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (G-8) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="G-8 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ensure that you have at least one free inventory slot, then speak with Milazahn to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You receive an Imperial Mythril Piece.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2126",["title"]="Unbridled Passion",["page_title"]="Unbridled Passion",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Unbridled_Passion",["revision"]="118979",["requirements"]="Start: Perih Vashai \226\128\148 Windurst Woods (K-7)\010Requirements: Ranger 50+\010Items: Gold Earring\010Previous: Fire and Brimstone",["rewards"]="Hunter's Socks\010Ice Arrow x99",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="Semih Lafihna has set out to find the truth. Track her down and help her in any way possible.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After you have completed Fire and Brimstone, (YOU MUST PHYSICALLY WALK AND ZONE OUT TO SARUTABARUTA, you cannot mog house or teleport or the quest wont trigger.) talk to Perih Vashai to continue the search for the sinner.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You are sent to Mhaura to find a mithra. Koh Lenbalalako is standing in the corner of the Blacksmiths' Guild (Mhaura) at mhaura (F-9) and tells you part of a story and wont tell the rest until you give her a Gold Earring.",["zone"]="mhaura",["grid"]="F-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Gold Earring and give it to Koh Lenbalalako for her to finish her story about the sinner and Xarcabard. She will give you Key item: Koh's Letter.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow the sinner to Xarcabard and watch a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the cave at Xarcabard (E-7) and examine the ???. After a cutscene, a NM called Koenigstiger will spawn.",["zone"]="Xarcabard",["grid"]="E-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After killing Koenigstiger, go to the cave at Xarcabard (E-8), examine the ??? and watch another cutscene.",["zone"]="Xarcabard",["grid"]="E-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next examine the ??? at Xarcabard (E-8) again to get a reward of 99 Ice Arrow.",["zone"]="Xarcabard",["grid"]="E-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel back to Perih Vashai in Windurst and talk to her to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Ranger (RNG)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Ranger (RNG)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Hunter's Socks",["revision"]="21448"},{["job"]="Ranger (RNG)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Unbridled Passion",["revision"]="118979"}}},{["id"]="wiki_7442",["title"]="Under Oath",["page_title"]="Under Oath",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Under_Oath",["revision"]="118463",["requirements"]="Start: Trion \226\128\148 Chateau d'Oraguille\010Requirements: Paladin Level 50+\010San d'Oria Rank: 2\010or Bastok/Windurst Rank: 3\010Items: Zvahl Coffer Key\010Key item: Mique's Paintbrush\010Key item: Strange Sheet of Paper\010Well Weight\010Key item: Knight's Confession\010Previous: A Boy's Dream",["rewards"]="Gallant Surcoat",["repeatable"]="Yes, see Vingijard after AF is complete.",["summary"]="Knights whisper of a traitor in their midst. An outsider is needed to investigate.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Go to Chateau d'Oraguille and click on the door to Prince Trion's chambers. (If you were a Paladin when you completed A Boy's Dream, you may have already received this cutscene.)\010\010You may finish the quest as any job at this point.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene, head to Southern San d'Oria (M-7) and talk to Vemalpeau , who lives inside the small house nearest Lion Square, on the bottom floor.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="M-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Then go to Lion Spring's Tavern Southern San d'Oria (K-6) and talk to Najjar.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="K-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, head to Count Caffaule's Manor Southern San d'Oria (B-6) and talk to Ullasa. Ullasa mentions Key item: Mique's Paintbrush. Once you see the paintbrush mentioned, you can go key hunting.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="B-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Castle Zvahl Baileys and obtain a Zvahl Coffer Key. (You can just pick the lock on Thief and skip the key farming. \010\010Keys can be dropped by Ahriman, Abyssal Demons, Arch Demons, Blood Demons, and Doom Demons.\010\010To the right is a map of the coffer locations. Basically, the key dropping monsters are in the four corners and the tunnels leading to the four corners. To get to these corners, you need to drop down into four different holes. However, the northwest hole will only lead to the northwest corner, and once you drop, you must make your way back up to get to a different hole.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Open a coffer to obtain Key item: Mique's Paintbrush. Coffer can be opened on any job.\010\010Note: If you have a current artifact quest active from this coffer, the coffer will produce the artifact and not Key item: Mique's Paintbrush. \010\010Note: If you have completed an AF quest but the item is stored on a slip you will get AF and not the Key item*\010\010Note: This can be picked as a Thief, since Paladin does not have to be your main job to obtain the paintbrush, but be sure to have Rogue's Vest in your inventory.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to and talk to Vemalpeau at Southern San d'Oria (M-7).",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="M-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed upstairs in Vemalpeau's house. Immediately to your left, there are three spots that can be examined. Click on the painting on the wall above the first spot and select the option to \034look behind the frame\034 and then \034open and examine\034 to obtain a Key item: Strange Sheet of Paper.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="(optional) Return to Vemalpeau who mentions his son's commanding officer.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to \034Helbort's Blades\034 located at Southern San d'Oria (K-7) and talk to Exoroche, who tells you to go to Davoi.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="K-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Davoi (G-9) there is a Village Well. The person who needs this quest is the one who will touch the well and immediately spawn two NMs: Three-eyed Prozpuz (RNG) and One-eyed Gwajboj (PLD).\010\010A full alliance of level 55+, a full well rounded party, or a FEW level 75's help is HIGHLY recommended. \010\010The area should be cleared of Orcs, which link with the NMs.\010\010Three-eyed Prozpuz range attacks hit very hard, even to level 75's.",["zone"]="Davoi",["grid"]="G-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat the NMs to obtain the Well Weight. \010\010One-eyed Gwajboj drops the Well Weight regardless of whether or not the other NM is killed.\010\010After killing the NMs, only one Well Weight drops. So if you have more than one PLD who needs the quest, you must kill them both again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Well Weight to the Village Well for a cutscene and the Key item: Knight's Confession.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next head to Northern San d'Oria (J-9) and talk to Ailbeche, who mentions Jugner Forest.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="J-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the Maiden's Spring located at Jugner Forest (E-6). Approach the edge of the pond for a cutscene. \010\010If you arrive by chocobo, you do not need to dismount to get the cutscene.",["zone"]="Jugner Forest",["grid"]="E-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Finally, head back to San d'Oria where you may optionally talk to Ailbeche and Exoroche or simply head to Chateau d'Oraguille and talk to Prince Trion for a final cutscene and your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Although the quest is technically over after talking with Trion, the Key item: Knight's Confession will remain in your inventory until speaking with Vemalpeau at Southern San d'Oria (M-7) one last time. Giving him his son's confession serves as a bit of closure, though this is entirely optional.",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="M-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Paladin (PLD)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Paladin (PLD)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Gallant Surcoat",["revision"]="19609"},{["job"]="Paladin (PLD)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Under Oath",["revision"]="118463"}}},{["id"]="wiki_4811",["title"]="Under the Sea",["page_title"]="Under the Sea",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Under_the_Sea",["revision"]="106228",["requirements"]="Start: Yaya \226\128\148 Selbina (H-9)\010Fame: Selbina\010Items: Fat Greedie",["rewards"]="Amber Earring",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Oswald needs help retrieving his ring from the jaws of the ocean.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Yaya (Selbina (H-9), Under the Fishermen's Guild) for a cutscene and to start the quest.",["zone"]="Selbina",["grid"]="H-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Oswald (Selbina (I-9), Inside the Shepherd's Muster) who mentions he lost his favorite ring.",["zone"]="Selbina",["grid"]="I-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Jimaida (Selbina (H-9), behind Yaya) who tells you to go talk to Zaldon. (Selbina (H-9), Fishermen's Guild)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zaldon mentions that Greedies like to swallow shiny things.\010\010You will need to Fish up a Fat Greedie in Selbina.\010\010The Fat Greedie is best caught with Lugworms or Sardine Balls and a small fishing rod such as a Halcyon Rod.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Zaldon the Fat Greedie to obtain the Key item: Etched Ring.\010\010You might need to trade more than one fish in order to receive the Key item: Etched Ring.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Oswald for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Selbina",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57122",["title"]="Undersea Scouting",["page_title"]="Undersea Scouting",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Undersea_Scouting",["revision"]="121715",["requirements"]="Start: Naja Salaheem \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10)\010Previous: A Mercenary Life",["rewards"]="Key item: Astral Compass",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Enter the Alzadaal Undersea Ruins from Bhaflau Thickets and survey the interior.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete A Mercenary Life. This mission begins immediately afterward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Bhaflau Thickets and speak with Kamih Mapokhalam at Bhaflau Thickets (F-6) / Map 1.\010\010 Trade her 1 Imperial Silver Piece to enter the Alzadaal Undersea Ruins.\010\010 Optional: Before entering, trade her 3 Imperial Mythril Pieces to obtain the Key item: Map of Alzadaal Ruins.",["zone"]="Bhaflau Thickets",["grid"]="F-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed east toward the Gilded Doors at H-8 for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete the cutscene to receive the Key item: Astral Compass. This completes this mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional: Nyzul Isle Attunement\010\010If you have not yet attuned to Nyzul Isle:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the cutscene, use the North Teleporter (Bhaflau Remnants).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once teleported, use the West Teleporter (Nyzul Isle).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed east toward the large room either from the northern or southern path.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In the big room, use any runic portal to attune yourself by teleporting back to Whitegate.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next Mission\010\010Proceed with the next mission, Astral Waves.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1167",["title"]="Undying Flames",["page_title"]="Undying Flames",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Undying_Flames",["revision"]="105326",["requirements"]="Start: Pagisalis \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (M-6)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Beeswax x2",["rewards"]="Friar's Rope",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Collect two lumps of beeswax for making candles to light the late papsque's road to Paradise.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak to Pagisalis in the Reliquary on the bottom floor of the Cathedral.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="He wants 2 beeswax to make sacred candles.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Buy or craft these and give them to him for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4808",["title"]="Unending Chase",["page_title"]="Unending Chase",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Unending_Chase",["revision"]="107657",["requirements"]="Start: Rycharde \226\128\148 Mhaura (I-8)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Puffball\010Previous: Way of the Cook",["rewards"]="2100g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Rycharde wants you to get him an ingredient called a puffball.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must wait approximately 8 game days after finishing Way of the Cook before Rycharde will give you this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Rycharde. He will ask you to bring him a puffball.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade him a puffball to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7431",["title"]="Unexpected Treasure",["page_title"]="Unexpected Treasure",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Unexpected_Treasure",["revision"]="60832",["requirements"]="Start: Morunaude \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (G-8)\010Requirements: Cupboard placed in Mog House Layout\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 4\010Items: Key item: Small teacup\010Cupboard\010Mistletoe",["rewards"]="12,000g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The small teacup found in the cupboard sold at this store appears to have royal origins. The owner would doubtlessly be grateful to have it back.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Buy a Cupboard from Justi's Furniture shop in Northern San d'Oria, place it in your Mog House, and display it using Layout.\010\010The Cupboard is Exclusive, but this item can be sent via Delivery Box to other characters on the same Playonline ID.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone out of and back into your Mog House and talk to your Moogle to receive a Key item: Small teacup.\010\010If zoning out and back doesn't work, try zoning out, travel to another Mog House Home Point in the same city, and re-enter the Mog House.\010\010If you have already completed a Furniture Quest this Conquest Tally, remove all other Furniture Quest furniture items, and then try again.\010\010Once the Small teacup is acquired, the Cupboard can be removed. It is not necessary to keep it displayed to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to the furniture shop and talk to Morunaude.\010\010Optional: Talk with Morunaude a second time; she mentions Calovour.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to the Cathedral in Northern San d'Oria and talk to Calovour, who asks you for a Mistletoe.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade a mistletoe to Calovour to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_53526",["title"]="Unforgiven",["page_title"]="Unforgiven",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Unforgiven",["revision"]="107844",["requirements"]="Start: Elysia \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold (G-10) / Map 1\010Requirements: Chains of Promathia Mission 2-1: An Invitation West Completed\010Items: Key item: Alabaster Hairpin",["rewards"]="Key item: Map of Tavnazia",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Find and bring back the hairpin that Elysia dropped while doing her shopping.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Elysia on the middle floor of Tavnazian Safehold at (G-10) (entrance level).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Afterwards, go up to the top floor of the Tavnazian Safehold and examine the ??? behind a pillar at (K-9) to obtain an Key item: Alabaster Hairpin. (Near the walnut door).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Elysia and talk to her.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, talk to Pradiulot on the middle floor at (H-9) for a cutscene (head back to the main circle and turn left).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Optional: After the cutscene above, head back to Elysia and talk to her, then speak to Pradiulot again for an extra cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_12314",["title"]="Uninvited Guests",["page_title"]="Uninvited Guests",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Uninvited_Guests",["revision"]="118597",["requirements"]="Start: Justinius \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold (J-6) / Map 2\010Items: Key item: Monarch Linn Patrol Permit\010Giant Scale (1-2)\010Previous: The Savage",["rewards"]="One of the listed below.",["repeatable"]="conquest",["summary"]="You have been asked to expel the black-robed intruders lurking around Monarch Linn.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Justinius at Tavnazian Safehold (J-6) / Map 2 of the upper level in Tavnazian Safehold for a cutscene to start the quest and receive the Key item: Monarch Linn Patrol Permit. This is required for all players in order to enter the battlefield and is lost upon entry.",["zone"]="Tavnazian Safehold",["grid"]="J-6 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Monarch Linn through either Riverne - Site A01 or Riverne - Site B01.\010\010For B01 you will require 1 Giant Scale and for A01 you will require 2 to pass through the unstable displacements.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the battle, return to Tavnazian Safehold and talk with Justinius to complete the quest, and receive your reward for success.\010\010Success or failure, the battle can be repeated after the next conquest tally.\010\010It is possible to complete this successfully on certain jobs around level 75.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Battle",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The battlefield has a 30 minute time limit, and a maximum of 18 characters are allowed to enter.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is no Level Restriction so buffs including TP do not wear off upon entering and experience points will be lost from a knock out.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="One Mammet-800 is in the battlefield at first. When it is approached, the additional Mammets spawn, depending on the number of adventurers in the fight.\010\010One Mammet will be fought for every two characters: 1 Mammet for 1-2 characters, 2 Mammets for 3-4 characters, etc.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Mammets are very similar to the ones encountered during Promathia Mission 2-5: Ancient Vows and Promathia Mission 6-4: One to be Feared, just scaled up in difficulty.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="They have approximately 3500HP.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="They are immune to Sleep, Lullaby, and Gravity, but susceptible to Bind and Silence.\010\010They do build resistance to Bind, so it will be difficult to kite indefinitely if Bind is your only defense.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Depending of the form, they can use abilities that allow them to absorb damage from physical or magical damage.\010\010When in the hand-to-hand form, they will use Transmogrification that absorbs physical damage.\010\010When in the staff form, they will use Mind Wall that absorbs magic damage.\010\010Using Yellow Liquid will make them unable to change their form.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="All of the Mammets must be defeated to win the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57173",["title"]="Unraveling Reason",["page_title"]="Unraveling Reason",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unavailable",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Unraveling_Reason",["revision"]="120884",["requirements"]="Start: Pherimociel \226\128\148 Ru'Lude Gardens (G-6) / Map 1\010Previous: Allied Rumblings",["rewards"]="None",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have been asked to participate in the Wajaom Infiltration Operation. A high-speed airship is being prepared for this mission. Speak with Pherimociel when you are ready to depart.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Allied Rumblings; this mission begins immediately afterward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone once and wait until the next Vana'diel day.\010\010 Speaking with Pherimociel before the wait has elapsed triggers an optional cutscene explaining that the airship is not ready.\010\010 After viewing that early cutscene, zone again before attempting to continue.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Pherimociel at Ru'Lude Gardens (G-6) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Ru'Lude Gardens",["grid"]="G-6 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When prompted, select \034Ready!\034 to depart.\010\010 Declining does not advance the mission. Speak with Pherimociel again when ready; no additional zoning is required.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue through the chained cutscenes in Wajaom Woodlands.\010\010 You are placed at the Leypoint at Wajaom Woodlands (G-8) / Map 1.\010\010 The game automatically reloads your position at the Leypoint between scenes. No further interaction is required.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The final cutscene completes the mission, grants the title \034Endymion Paratrooper,\034 and begins Light of Judgment.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_357",["title"]="Vain (Windurst Mission 8-1)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 8-1",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_8-1",["revision"]="109564",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Previous: Windurst Mission 7-2|Awakening of the Gods",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="At the request of the Aurastery, you are to discover the whereabouts of their former minister who fled from his duties several years ago.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 25 crystals to any Conquest Overseer to unlock the mission then accept it from any Windurst Gate Guard.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Moreno-Toeno at the Aurastery (Windurst Waters (L-6) / North northern section, eastern building) for a cutscene and to obtain the Key item: \034Star Seeker\034.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="L-6 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Ro'Maeve and click the Qu'Hau Spring at (Ro'Maeve (H-6)) for a cutscene with a Talking Doll .",["zone"]="Ro'Maeve",["grid"]="H-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Davoi and talk to Sedal-Godjal at Sedal-Godjal for a cutscene. (You may need to talk to him multiple times to get the correct cutscene). He will turn your Key item: \034Star Seeker\034 into the Key item: Magic-drained \034Star Seeker\034. \010\010He is located on an elevated section of the map, which you can only reach through Monastic Cavern. Enter Monastic Cavern from entrance 2 at (Davoi (H-11)) in Davoi and keep going until exit 4 (Monastic Cavern (I-8)). \010\010You can also do this after you kill Dirtyhanded Gochakzuk so you do not have to run to Sedal-Godjal twice.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Next, kill Dirtyhanded Gochakzuk for a Curse Wand. \010\010He is located on the center island at (Davoi (H-8)). From the exit of Monastic Cavern follow the road around the hill to a wooden elevator, pull the lever to get to the monastery building. Inside, after 2 doors, the NM will be sitting on a big \034throne\034. \010\010He drops two wands and has a respawn time of 16-30 minutes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Sedal-Godjal and trade the Curse Wand to him for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Moreno-Toeno located in Windurst Waters (L-6) / North, in the Aurastery for a cutscene that completes the mission.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="L-6 / North",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_57452",["title"]="Vanishing Act",["page_title"]="Vanishing Act",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Vanishing_Act",["revision"]="121569",["requirements"]="Start: Ulamaal or Qutiba \226\128\148 Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-12) / Map 1\010Requirements: Completion of Delivering the Goods\010Wait until after the next Japanese midnight and change zones\010Fame: None\010Items: Sickle\010Previous: Delivering the Goods",["rewards"]="Imperial Silver Piece",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Ulamaal and Qutiba ask you to find the missing leader of the Epicureans, who disappeared after saying he was going to the port.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After completing Delivering the Goods, wait until after the next Japanese midnight and change zones.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with either Ulamaal or Qutiba on the second floor of the Shararat Teahouse at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-12) / Map 1 to begin the quest.\010\010 Either NPC can begin and complete the quest; you do not need to speak with both.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-12 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Fochacha in Serpentking Square at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-9) / Map 1 for a cutscene.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-9 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Walk through the passage beside the Alchemists' Guild at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (F-5, G-5) / Map 1 to trigger another cutscene automatically.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="F-5 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take a Sickle to Wajaom Woodlands and trade it to any Harvesting Point in Wajaom Woodlands to receive the Rainbow Berry key item.\010\010 The first valid Sickle trade advances the quest; repeated harvesting is not required.",["zone"]="Wajaom Woodlands",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to either Ulamaal or Qutiba at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-12) / Map 1 to complete the quest and receive an Imperial Silver Piece.\010\010 The Rainbow Berry is removed when the quest is completed.\010\010 Ensure that you have at least one free inventory slot before completing the quest.\010\010 To begin A Taste of Honey, wait until after the next Japanese midnight and change zones.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-12 / Map 1",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7522",["title"]="Vengeful Wrath",["page_title"]="Vengeful Wrath",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Vengeful_Wrath",["revision"]="104242",["requirements"]="Start: Goraow \226\128\148 Bastok Mines (I-6)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Quadav Helm",["rewards"]="900g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Kill some Quadav to avenge Goraow's fallen comrades, and bring back a Quadav Helm as proof of your deeds.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Goraow.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Quadav Helm and trade it to Goraow to receive your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Quadav Helm are dropped from Old Quadav in Pashhow Marshlands and Beadeaux as well as Darksteel Quadav in Beadeaux and Qulun Dome",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Notes",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This quest can be repeated by continuing to turn in Quadav Helms; zoning between each repeat is not required.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you come back to Goraow, you have to speak to him first to get him to tell you that he wants the Quadav Helm as proof of your deeds.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_544",["title"]="Vessel Without a Captain (Promathia Mission 3-2)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 3-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_3-2",["revision"]="115553",["requirements"]="Previous: Call of the Wyrmking",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Prishe has left for the Tenshodo in Jeuno to find her acquaintance, Grezzo. A visit to the Grand Duke Palace may also be necessary...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Head to Lower Jeuno and enter Neptune's Spire.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click on the door near the back of the room (leading into Tenshodo HQ).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to Ru'Lude Gardens and approach the palace stairs that lead up to the Audience Chamber doors to receive the final cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_325",["title"]="Wading Beasts (Bastok Mission 2-2)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 2-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_2-2",["revision"]="27766",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 2-1|The Crystal Line",["rewards"]="Rank Points",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Procure a lizard egg from monsters in the Dangruf Wadi. Deliver the egg to Senator Alois in the President's Office.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="This mission is optional.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Select the mission from one of the Bastok Gate Guards",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Lizard Egg, always purchasable from Chomo Jinjahl in Windurst Waters Windurst Waters (E-8) / Map 1 or from the Auction House . Any lizard drops them as well, regardless what the mission description states.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once obtained, Trade the egg to Senator Alois in the Metalworks (J-8)",["zone"]="Metalworks",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2568",["title"]="Waking Dreams",["page_title"]="Waking Dreams",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Waking_Dreams",["revision"]="118121",["requirements"]="Start: Kerutoto \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (J-8) / South\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Key item: Vial of Dream Incense\010Previous: Promathia Mission 3-5: Darkness Named",["rewards"]="Choice of one of the following:\010Diabolos summoning spell or\010Diabolos's Pole or\010Diabolos's Earring or\010Diabolos's Ring or\010Diabolos's Torque or\01015,000 Gil",["repeatable"]="daily",["summary"]="Diabolos has informed Kerutoto that he is waiting for you at the Shrouded Maw in Pso'Xja, buried deep in the northern lands. You must respond to his summons so that Kerutoto can meditate free of trouble.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="This quest can not be started if the quest Food_for_Thought has been started.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to south Windurst Waters and speak to Kerutoto Windurst Waters (J-8) / South in the Rhinostery's north wing to receive a Key item: Vial of Dream Incense.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="J-8 / South",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to The Shrouded Maw to enter the BCNM Waking Dreams. \010\010To get there, enter the Pso'Xja tower next to the Outpost at Beaucedine Glacier (H-8).\010\010In this tower, there are shimmering walls of different colors. Every time you enter one you zone. The order of walls you want is red, purple, red, purple. After the last purple zone, ride the elevator down.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Diabolos to acquire a Key item: Whisper of Dreams.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the Key item: Whisper of Dreams to Kerutoto to choose your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_6171",["title"]="Waking the Beast",["page_title"]="Waking the Beast",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Waking_the_Beast",["revision"]="106546",["requirements"]="Start: ??? \226\128\148 La Theine Plateau (G-6)\010Requirements: Ifrit, Titan, Leviathan, Garuda, Shiva and Ramuh acquired\010Items: Key item: Eye of Flames\010Key item: Eye of Frost\010Key item: Eye of Gales\010Key item: Eye of Storms\010Key item: Eye of Tides\010Key item: Eye of Tremors\010Key item: Faded Ruby\010Previous: Trial by Fire\010Trial by Earth\010Trial by Water\010Trial by Wind\010Trial by Ice\010Trial by Lightning",["rewards"]="Carbuncle's Pole",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Carbuncle wants you to visit all the protocrystals and gather the elemental energy of the sleeping gods. Will their imminent awakening mean fortune or doom for Vana'diel? Only Carbuncle's ancient friend at the Full Moon Fountain may know...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Carbuncle at the ??? in La Theine Plateau (G-6) and receive the Key item: Rainbow Resonator.",["zone"]="La Theine Plateau",["grid"]="G-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Elemental Avatar Battles",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat the six Prime Celestial Avatars.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Like in the \034Trial by\034 family of quests, the Prime avatars have access to the level 75 meritable Blood Pact: Rages.\010\010These attacks ignore Utsusemi and do ~1000 damage unresisted, be sure to keep Barspells and Carol on at all times.\010Ifrit Prime: Meteor Strike\010Shiva Prime: Heavenly Strike\010Garuda Prime: Wind Blade\010Titan Prime: Geocrush\010Ramuh Prime: Thunderstorm\010Leviathan Prime: Grand Fall",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Avatars can use their Astral Flow attack at anytime, and is independent of the Avatar's HP.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can either tank the Avatar with Ninjas, or if you have enough Summoners, they can kill the avatar by themselves with physical Blood Pacts.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Elemental Magic nukes of the Avatar's weak element do decent damage, but are better used on the elemental pets.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Each Avatar is supported by four elementals that share hate with the avatar.\010\010 A significant amount of damage must be inflicted on the elementals to pull them off of the avatar's target.\010\010As well as attacking the players, the elementals cure the avatar with tier IV elemental nukes.\010\010Elementals do not respawn when killed, but rather one is created when the avatar uses their level 75 meritable Blood Pact: Rages. A maximum number of four elementals will be out at any given time.\010\010The elementals' melee attacks have an added effect of the appropriate debuff of that element.\010\010The elementals are weak to melee attacks.\010\010A good number of Black Mages are important for killing the elementals. 5 -ga III spells of the opposing element will take out all of the elementals.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You only need to defeat the avatar in order to win.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Each BCNM will drop a few elemental clusters of the appropriate element after the win and each person will receive the following key items: \010Key item: Eye of Flames (Cloister of Flames)\010Key item: Eye of Tremors (Cloister of Tremors)\010Key item: Eye of Tides (Cloister of Tides)\010Key item: Eye of Gales (Cloister of Gales)\010Key item: Eye of Frost (Cloister of Frost)\010Key item: Eye of Storms (Cloister of Storms)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Final Battle",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have all 6 key items, proceed to Full Moon Fountain for the final battlefield and a cut scene.\010\010Battle name: \034Waking the Beast\034. Player limit: 18. Time limit: 30 minutes.\010\010Buffs will NOT wear upon entry.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you defeat this final battlefield, random Avatar weapons may drop, and you will also receive a Key item: Faded Ruby.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The sequence for the battle is as such: \010\010Carbuncle Prime will appear and will stay until he reaches 75% HP, at which point he'll disappear.\010\010In its place a random avatar prime will appear. When it's dead, Carbuncle Prime will appear.\010\010Deplete Carbuncle Prime's HP to 50%, and he'll disappear.\010\010In its place will appear two random avatar primes that have not appeared before. When they're dead, Carbuncle Prime will reappear.\010\010Deplete Carbuncle Prime's HP to 25%, and he'll disappear.\010\010In its place will appear three celestial avatar primes that have not appeared previously. Defeat them and Carbuncle Prime will reappear.\010\010This time there will be five Carbuncle Primes with 25% HP. The Carbuncles will astral flow upon the first prime defeat or their astral flow timer is up (about 1 minute). Defeat all five Carbuncles to win the battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After the battle choose either yes (\034Disturber of Slumber\034 title) or no (\034Interrupter of Dreams\034 title), if you want to give the energy back to the fountain or not.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return the Key item: Faded Ruby to Carbuncle in La Theine Plateau to finish the quest and receive Carbuncle's Pole.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You may restart the quest after the weekly Conquest Tally Results.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you fail, you will lose your KI if you homepoint. To retain your KI, you must wait to get kicked out (either the 3 min KO timer or the 30 minute battlefield timer).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will also lose your KI if you enter and \034Run Away\034 (Exit BC).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Additional Rewards from Final Battle\010\010Drops occur as the following:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It was previously believed that a piece of equipment would drop per party in the alliance, but this was later proven invalid.\010\010|- \010! Zero to One of: [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Carbuncle's Cuffs\010|-\010|Garuda's Sickle\010|-\010|Ifrit's Bow\010|-\010|Leviathan's Couse\010|-\010|Ramuh's Mace\010|-\010|Shiva's Shotel\010|-\010|Titan's Baselarde\010\010|- \010! Zero to One of: [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Carbuncle's Cuffs\010|-\010|Garuda's Sickle\010|-\010|Ifrit's Bow\010|-\010|Leviathan's Couse\010|-\010|Ramuh's Mace\010|-\010|Shiva's Shotel\010|-\010|Titan's Baselarde\010\010|- \010! Zero to One of: [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 0 / 0]\010|-\010|Carbuncle's Cuffs\010|-\010|Garuda's Sickle\010|-\010|Ifrit's Bow\010|-\010|Leviathan's Couse\010|-\010|Ramuh's Mace\010|-\010|Shiva's Shotel\010|-\010|Titan's Baselarde\010\010|- \010! Zero to One of: [Template Hxi Drop Rate: asb=0/1000 / 50% / 0]*\010|-\010| Yinyang Robe [Horizon change]*Yinyang Robe is its own pool with a 50% drop. confirmed by Aerec",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="See Also",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Waking the Beast/Strategies",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_9807",["title"]="Wandering Souls",["page_title"]="Wandering Souls",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Wandering_Souls",["revision"]="19183",["requirements"]="Start: None - Cape Teriggan\010Requirements: Started ZM 5 - Headstone Pilgrimage\010Items: Rain Lily",["rewards"]="Flagellant's Rope",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must first have Zilart Mission 5 - Headstone Pilgrimage activated.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After completing your business for ZM5 at the Cermet Headstone in Cape Teriggan, trade a Rain Lily to the headstone. You will get a cutscene.\010\010Rain Lilies can be purchased from Areebah in Upper Jeuno, Dabih Jajalioh in Ru'Lude Gardens or from Auction House: Materials >> Alchemy.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At the end of the cutscene, you will receive the Flagellant's Rope.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=None\010 / summary=Is there any way to soothe the spirits that wander about Cape Teriggan?]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7438",["title"]="Warding Vampires",["page_title"]="Warding Vampires",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Warding_Vampires",["revision"]="62020",["requirements"]="Start: Maloquedil \226\128\148 Northern San d'Oria (J-8)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 3\010Items: Shaman Garlic x2",["rewards"]="900g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Fetch two cloves of Orc garlic to keep vampires away.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Maloquedil needs garlic to ward off the vampire living in the dungeon under the Chateau d'Oraguille.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Shaman Garlic can be obtained by killing Orcish Cursemakers.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade him two Shaman Garlic to receive your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2569",["title"]="Water Way to Go",["page_title"]="Water Way to Go",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Water_Way_to_Go",["revision"]="106793",["requirements"]="Start: Ohbiru-Dohbiru \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (J-9) / South\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 3\010Previous: Overnight Delivery",["rewards"]="900g",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="Ohbiru-Dohburu is running out of the Giddeus water needed to raise Fluoro-flora. He wants you to take a Rhinostery canteen to the springs at the back off Giddeus in order to refill his supply.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must change areas after completing the previous quest.\010If you have triggered Say It with Flowers, you must complete it first (even if it does not appear in your log).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Ohbiru-Dohbiru in the Rhinostery in Windurst Waters (J-9) / South, he will ask you to go to Giddeus and get him some water from the spring there.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="J-9 / South",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take the Rhinostery Canteen he gives you to Giddeus to the spring at (Giddeus (K-12) / Ground Level) or (Giddeus (E-12) / Ground Level) and trade to it for a Canteen of Giddeus Water. \010\010The Rhinostery Canteen is a usable item, and you can 'use' it on the spring. As such, it will appear at the beginning of the item list, not after the equipment items.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Canteen of Giddeus Water to Ohbiru-Dohbiru for your reward.\010This quest cannot be repeated if you have activated the quest Curses, Foiled A-Golem!?. Talking to Leepe-Hoppe on the roof may activate Tuning In, this quest will be locked until Tuning In is finished if you activated it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1215",["title"]="Waters of the Cheval",["page_title"]="Waters of the Cheval",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Waters_of_the_Cheval",["revision"]="121306",["requirements"]="Start: Miageau, Northern San d'Oria (L-7)\010Fame: San d'Oria\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Cheval Water",["rewards"]="Wing Pendant",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Draw water from the Cheval River in East Ronfaure.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Speak with Miageau in Northern San d'Oria (L-7) just past the entrance to the Cathedral. \010\010Buy a Blessed Waterskin by trading 10g to Nouveil (to your right).",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="L-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the waterskin to the Cheval River target in East Ronfaure (H-5) to receive Cheval Water.",["zone"]="East Ronfaure",["grid"]="H-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Northern San d'Oria and trade the Cheval Water to Miageau.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="San d'Oria",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_4809",["title"]="Way of the Cook",["page_title"]="Way of the Cook",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Way_of_the_Cook",["revision"]="107655",["requirements"]="Start: Rycharde \226\128\148 Mhaura (I-8)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Dhalmel Meat\010Beehive Chip\010Previous: Rycharde the Chef",["rewards"]="1500g or 1000g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Rycharde needs your help finding some ingredients. He needs a Beehive Chip and some Dhalmel Meat.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must wait approximately 8 game days before Rycharde will give you this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Rycharde will ask you to bring a piece of Dhalmel Meat and a Beehive Chip.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Dhalmel Meat drops from Dhalmels. Beehive Chips drop from Killer Bees in Tahrongi Canyon.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you bring Rycharde the items after three game days he says he just got someone else to do it for him and will only reward you with 1000g and the old title of Purveyor In Training, rather than the full 1500g and the new title.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_639",["title"]="Welcome t'Norg (Zilart Mission 2)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_2",["revision"]="20464",["requirements"]="Start: Gilgamesh \226\128\148 Norg (L-8)\010Previous: The New Frontier",["rewards"]="Not specified in the imported header.",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Lion has someone she wants you to meet. She will be waiting for you at the room at the end of the hallway on the second floor of Norg.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Click on the \034Oaken Door\034 at (Norg (K-8)) in Norg for a cutscene with Gilgamesh.\010\010The dialog will ask if you want to open the door, choose Yes.",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="K-8",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Rise of the Zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_7499",["title"]="Welcome to Bastok",["page_title"]="Welcome to Bastok",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Welcome_to_Bastok",["revision"]="117441",["requirements"]="Start: Powhatan \226\128\148 Port Bastok (E-6)\010Requirements: Level 7+ WAR, RDM, PLD, BST, or SAM, are required to complete, but not to flag, quest\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Shell Shield",["rewards"]="Spatha",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Greet Powhattan's guest at the air travel agency. Wear a shell shield so he'll know who you are.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Powhatan; he's foolishly told someone coming into the port that he'll meet him wearing a shell shield when he doesn't have one.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Shell Shield and equip it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk with the clerk Bartolomeo in the Arrivals section of the Air Travel Agency with the Shell Shield equipped. This triggers a cutscene where an NPC named Evrain appears. You exchange greetings and then he finds his own way to the tavern where Powhatan is waiting.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Powhatan again to complete the quest. \010\010You keep the Shell Shield.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_56999",["title"]="Westerly Winds",["page_title"]="Westerly Winds",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Westerly_Winds",["revision"]="122481",["requirements"]="Previous: Easterly Winds",["rewards"]="Key item: Raillefal's Note\0102 Imperial Silver Pieces",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have been assigned the task of infiltrating the inner political circle of the Empire as an agent of the allied forces. Report to Raillefal.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Complete Easterly Winds.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter the second floor of Shararat Teahouse in Aht Urhgan Whitegate at Aht Urhgan Whitegate (K-11) for a cutscene.\010\010 You receive the Key item: Raillefal's Note and 1 Imperial Silver Piece.",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="K-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Naja Salaheem at Salaheem's Sentinels, Aht Urhgan Whitegate (I-10).",["zone"]="Aht Urhgan Whitegate",["grid"]="I-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Complete the cutscene to receive 1 Imperial Silver Piece and finish the mission.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue to A Mercenary Life.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Treasures of Aht Urhgan",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_598",["title"]="When Angels Fall (Promathia Mission 8-3)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 8-3",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_8-3",["revision"]="120282",["requirements"]="Previous: A Fate Decided",["rewards"]="1000 Experience Points (Once per Day)\010Mog Wardrobe 2: 2 slots",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="The Gate of the Gods--the portal leading to the highest level of the palace--has opened. While your companions scramble to reach the audience chamber, you must find which of the five towers will return you into the light...",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Zone into The Garden of Ru'Hmet for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Part 1",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The first objective is for you to climb a specific tower of The Garden of Ru'Hmet, which are located in the five points of the map. Each tower corresponds to a specific race.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This can be done solo, or with your party, but each person will need to get to the top of their race's tower.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="A spinning Aw'zdei at the long hallway to each tower spins in the direction of the fastest way to the first elevator.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In each of the larger rooms are an alcove with another Aw'zdei. You can make your way around it twice or sleep it and run to the elevator.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There are two more floors of enemies in the towers. The elevators going up alternate sides. If the first elevator was on the east side, for example, the second will be on the west, and the third on the east again.\010\010Flee makes this part easier; run about halfway around, then Flee to the elevator so you get there well ahead of any aggro and teleport away.\010\010 Another technique on the 3rd floor is have a paladin or someone run right through the center. Then sleepga them all at the end and just zone them up.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The fourth floor has no enemies. Run in and check the Ebon Panel in the center of the room. Any race can check it in any tower to get the first cutscene. After that cutscene, people of the right race in the right tower check it again for a second cutscene, a key item and a new title, Warrior of the Crystal.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Climb towers until everyone has the required key item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The key items are race specific. They are:\010\010 Light of Mea- for Elvaan.\010\010 Light of Dem- for Mithra.\010\010 Light of Holla- for Tarutaru.\010\010 Light of Vahzl- for Humes.\010\010 Light of Al'Taieu- for Galka.\010https://horizonffxi.wiki/The_Garden_of_Ru%27Hmet/Maps",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Part 2",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once your tower is complete, you need to progress up the central area of The Garden of Ru'Hmet (the green dot marks the elevator you want to reach).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="This can be done solo, or with your party, but each person will need to get both brands.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In each direction off the central elevator are spinning Qn'zdei pots in groups of four. When they aggro you and move off their starting positions, the door at the far end of the room slams shut and won\226\128\153t open until they return to their starting positions. These Qn'zdei are totally immune to Sleep and Lullaby.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The east and west access paths have a very fast spinning Qn'zdei in them, which makes getting by next to impossible. The North access path is slightly easier, although harder to get to.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can make your way around the the spinning Qn'zdei, fight them, or run past them and reraise.\010\010If you walk down one side of the room, in effect you only need to make your way around two of them. The left side seems easier.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once in the elevator room, step onto the platform and choose to ascend.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The BC is on the floor above you but the path upward is closed. The nearby Quasilumin will explain that you need to get two key items (Brand of Dawn and Brand of Twilight) to access the third floor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Brand of Twilight is to the south and the Brand of Dawn is to the north.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="See the map to the right for recommended path to the brands.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The pink dots are warps which count as a zone so aggro enemies will leave you alone if you warp.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain the two brands (along with two cutscenes). (Do not escape or you will need to run past the 4 spinning Qn'zdei again)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Part 3",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to the central elevator and ascend to the top floor of The Garden of Ru'Hmet. Check the Particle Gate for a cutscene and enter the battlefield when you\226\128\153re ready.\010Ix\226\128\153zdei Battle",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The BC is against four Ix'zdei NMs.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When you warp into the \226\128\156BC\226\128\157 you\226\128\153ll be at the north end of the room, facing south at the pots. This means that if you want to run away from the battle, you have to cross the room and choose the southern door to leave. The door at the north won\226\128\153t let you leave.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The two larger, closer Ix'zdeis are RDMs (with ~7000 HP) and the two smaller, farther ones are BLMs (with ~6250 HP). All of them are immune to silence and are heavily resistant to sleep.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The black mages are the more dangerous, having tier-3 aga spells, tier-4 single-target spells, and ancient magic. Target one of them first and give it your all.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Sleepga with Elemental Seal works.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When a pot gets low on life it may attempt to flee to its starting pedestal. If it sits there for a mere few seconds, it will regenerate to full HP. Stun or use a weapon skill when this is attempted.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If/when you are about to get KO'd, try to wipe at the door at the southern end of the room near the BLM pots. Wait for the pots to go back to their starting spots (they only regen life if they flee in battle, so they won\226\128\153t be healing), reraise up, rest to full, and continue to kill. On Eden this is not true, the pots will not return to their starting spots after a wipe and they WILL quickly regen to full HP.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you beat the pots, cross the empty room and check the Luminous Convergence for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Every living party member will receive 1000 Experience Points or Limit Points upon winning. (Only once per day)\010Strategy tips\010\010 You can't build TP on mobs in the garden before going into the battle anymore since March 2007's update. Also you lose buffs after entering the fight.\010\010 Keep reraise up at all times. RDM pots can dispel it. In addition, the best method to counter this is to put up as many dummy buffs (Stoneskin, Blink, Aquaveil, Phalanx, Bar Spell, Enspell, etc.) as possible, as this can largely lower the chances of Reraise being dispeled. \010\010 Sleepga the pots right off the bat. \010\010 Black magic is very powerful against the pots.\010\010 Skill chains are effective damage, too. Two two-step level 3 chains or one three step level 3 chain will take a BLM pot at least to half HP. A SAM can be effective for opening up multiple level 3 skill chains quickly.\010\010 Do everything possible to kill the two small BLM pots before wiping.\010\010 RDM and BLM in party can stagger Elemental Seal Sleepga II, Elemental Seal Sleepga to keep pots asleep long enough to kill both BLM and possibly a RDM(leaving you with only one pot to kill).\010\010 RDM can kite a pot back and forth across the zone after sleeps wear off with Gravity, Stoneskin, and Blink. RDM might need to Dispel, Sleep, or Blind to keep hate off the other sleeper in your party.\010\010 Fight and wipe at the far door of the room.\010\010 Stun and hit hard any pot that flees from the tank and attempts to return to its starting position.\010\010 Be ready to dispel the pots and remove a lot of status effects from party members, including silence, paralyze, and petrify.\010\010 Echo Drops are necessary for anyone that uses spells. Antidotes are also useful.\010\010 Utsusemi blocks most of the pots' TP attacks, and thus the status effects they inflict. Most are AoE, but some are only cone, so keep them facing away from your mages.\010\010 Stun Optic Induration if you can, it will usually one-shot everyone in front of the pot. It is used when pots have no rings or bars out, and there is a long charging animation (that includes a puff of fire) before the \034readies\034 message in the log.\010\010The Zdeis will not regen health after a wipe, so keep fighting until you are KO'd. 20% taken off of a Zdei before a wipe is 20% you won't have to do after recovery. On Eden this is not true, the pots will not return to their starting spots after a wipe and they WILL quickly regen to full HP.\010\010 You have 30 minutes to kill the Ix'zdeis. Time will be an issue if you wipe twice, but you can still win. Wiping three times is not a feasible option in this battle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have exited the Battlefield, check the Luminous Convergence for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1772",["title"]="Whence Blows the Wind",["page_title"]="Whence Blows the Wind",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Whence_Blows_the_Wind",["revision"]="123825",["requirements"]="Start: Maat \226\128\148 Ru'Lude Gardens (H-5)\010Requirements: Started Nation Mission 4-1 (Magicite)\010Level: 56\010Items: Key item: Orcish Crest\010Key item: Quadav Crest\010Key item: Yagudo Crest\010Previous: Atop the Highest Mountains",["rewards"]="Raises level cap to 65\010Mog Wardrobe: 5 Slots [Horizon change]",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="Your innate limits can be pushed further by collecting the crests of the Orcs, the Quadav, and the Yagudo.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Maat asks you to get the Key item: Orcish Crest, the Key item: Quadav Crest and the Key item: Yagudo Crest. Each Key Item is hidden in the corresponding beastman stronghold as a ???.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Orcish Crest\010\010NOTE: You will need Invisibility for this entire section.\010\010You need to pass the Wall of Banishing on the upper level at Davoi (J-9). The Wall of Banishing can only be opened by someone with the Key item: Crimson Orb in their possession. So either obtain one yourself (for a walkthrough see Obtaining a Crimson Orb) or bring someone who has it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Davoi and enter Monastic Cavern at Davoi (H-11).",["zone"]="Davoi",["grid"]="H-11",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the path at Monastic Cavern (I-8) and zone back to Davoi. This will put you in the house area at the center of Davoi in the SE corner of Davoi (H-8).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head east across the bridge, and then south to the Wall of Banishing in the the SW corner of Davoi (J-9). \010\010You need a Key item: Crimson Orb to open the Wall of Banishing. If no one in your party has one, see Obtaining a Crimson Orb.",["zone"]="Davoi",["grid"]="J-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Have a person with the Key item: Crimson Orb open the Wall of Banishing by clicking on it. This will open a hole in the wall which anyone can walk through.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow the path and zone into Monastic Cavern.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Hug the left wall and proceed to the SW corner of Monastic Cavern (J-6). Note: The ??? is at the western wall on the upper level, do not drop down the ledge.\010\010WARNING: There are true sight Orc NMs that lurk in the big room before the ledge.",["zone"]="Monastic Cavern",["grid"]="J-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click the ??? to receive your Key item: Orcish Crest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Quadav Crest\010\010NOTE: You will want Sneak for this section, but Invisible is not needed (unless you come across Broo). A party member must have completed Mysteries of Beadeaux I and II (can only be flagged if you were on Magicite mission) to be able to complete this part.\010NOTE: The Mute's silence effect will last a very long time. (Approximately 10-15 real life minutes.)NOTE: The Afflictor's curse will bring your HP and MP down far more than the average curse effect. (Approximately 10% of max HP and 50% of max MP.)\010TIP: Casters should bring Echo Drops to remove silence. The Afflictor machines you must pass will curse you, however you can avoid this by muting yourself with one of the Mute machines, and then using an echo drop to cure yourself once past the Afflictor. Alternatively, you can bring Silent Oil so you can sneak yourself without curing Mute.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Beadeaux and follow the tunnel down at Beadeaux (H-7) / Map 1.",["zone"]="Beadeaux",["grid"]="H-7 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Then proceed to the tunnel up at Beadeaux (F-8) / Map 2.",["zone"]="Beadeaux",["grid"]="F-8 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once above ground again, hug the right wall to the ramp at Beadeaux (E-10) / Map 1. (Please note there is one Afflictor on your way to the ramp.) and head to the north east section of the map without falling down until you get to Beadeaux (K-6) / Map 1. Then jump down and enter the tunnel. Make sure you have sneak on even if nothing aggroed you so far!",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once underground again, follow the path to Beadeaux (M-8) / Map 2 and then zone into Qulun Dome. There are three Afflictors in a row here, so Mute yourself at Beadeaux (K-8) / Map 2 first.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="In the first room of Qulun Dome is most likely a Notorious Monster, the Ruby Quadav. This NM has True Hearing, which ignores Sneak. However, you will want to have Sneak up because there are many other Quadavs that do not have True Hearing. \010\010A party member that has all three key items (same key items required to enter Magicite Room) must open the door after turning right at the first room. This door opens for the entire party/alliance. It can also be opened from the inside.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you enter the second room, there will also be two to three different NMs with True Hearing, including Ruby Quadav and Adaman Quadav. Avoid them and find the ??? as quickly as possible, which is located on the western wall, at around Qulun Dome (I-6).\010\010As soon as you hit it and receive the Key item: Quadav Crest, warp away.",["zone"]="Qulun Dome",["grid"]="I-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Yagudo Crest\010\010NOTE: These directions are incomplete with missing segments.\010NOTE: On Horizon, you only need to light one torch on the top floor, and can walk to the door at normal movement speed.\010\010NOTE: You will only need Invisibility for this entire section. You might need Sneak around bats if you bring a low-level player. This is also incorrect, the leeches can aggro you too.\010NOTE: It is recommended that you start this quest at the very beginning of a new Vana'diel day as the passwords will change each day.\010NOTE: You may want a Thief with Hide in your party.\010NOTE: To light the torches you must have the Yagudo Torch from Mission 4-1.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Enter Castle Oztroja at Meriphataud Mountains (L-8).",["zone"]="Meriphataud Mountains",["grid"]="L-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="For the first part you will need to find out what the password of the day is, which requires collecting information from three different brass statues. \010\010First password: Head to the SE corner of Castle Oztroja (H-8) / Map 1 and open the brass door. Click on the statue inside to receive the 1st password. \010NOTE: This next section is missing directions and/or guides you to places not listed.\010\010Second password: Now head to the door at Castle Oztroja (I-8) / Map 1 and open it by selecting the correct lever. (If you select the wrong one, then it should take about five minutes to get back to this door.) Go up the stairs. Head to the exit at Castle Oztroja (G-7) / Map 3 and zone over onto the next map. Head north to Castle Oztroja (I-7) / Map 7 and zone over to yet another map. Now head to the SE corner of Castle Oztroja (H-9) / Map 2 and open the brass door and receive the 2nd password from the statue.\010\010Third password: Proceed back along the same path until you reach Castle Oztroja / Map 3. The 3rd statue is located on the NW corner of Castle Oztroja (I-8) / Map 3. If you've never been to this section of the map before, there are blocker points preventing most of the \034obvious\034 paths and forcing you to walk around the outside. \010\010NOTE:It does not actually matter which order you visit the statues, but visiting the statues in the order listed in this walkthrough is the most convenient as it requires the least backtracking.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Now that you have visited all three statues, you should have 3 passwords, which will be used near the end of this section of the quest.\010\010The possible passwords are: Domi, Puqu, Gadu, Deggi, Mjuu, Xalmo, Haqa, Mong, Ouzi, Duzu, Buxu, Quu, Misu, Xicu, Ovzi, Duxo and Zhuu.\010\010Use these if the day changes and you are forced to \034guess\034 later on in the quest.\010\010The passwords are also case sensitive.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="From the 3rd statue point head to the 4 lever door at the SW corner of Castle Oztroja (G-8) / Map 3. You can find the combination to the door at the room at Castle Oztroja (I-10) / Map 3. It is a sequence of four directions, either up or down. For example, (Up, Down, Up, Up).\010\010Note: The combination also resets every Vana'diel day.\010\010Be wary of aggro once you pass through this door, the enemies beyond this door are at a higher level!",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you pass through the door, head up the stairs and zone through Castle Oztroja (G-9) / Map 3 onto a new map.",["zone"]="Castle Oztroja",["grid"]="G-9 / Map 3",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The next map is pretty straightforward, just remain invis and stay clear of the Yagudo Parasites (leeches), which aggro by hearing. Proceed to the next map at Castle Oztroja (H-11) / Map 4.",["zone"]="Castle Oztroja",["grid"]="H-11 / Map 4",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You want to proceed through the Brass Door at Castle Oztroja (H-7) / Map 5 from here. \010\010NOTE: This next part is -NOT- solo-able.\010\010This note is technically false, as it IS possible to solo by using flee and re-raise, if very lucky with enemy positioning you can even survive it without dying.\010\010To open the Brass Door, someone must light one of the four torches at G-7, G-8, H-7, or H-8 (which requires the Key item: Yagudo Torch), while the other players remain in front of the Brass Door. \010\010Once the torch is lit, the Brass Door will open, allowing the players to pass through.\010\010If you've brought a Thief, they should be the one to light the torch. Put Invisible on the Thief first so they can safely arrive at the torch. Once they de-invis and light the torch, they can use Flee then Hide to make it back to the Brass Door. Even if they are spotted by a Yagudo before using Hide, Hide removes aggro from all enemies that detect by sight, so the Yagudo will stop chasing them. \010\010If the torch player cannot make it through the door in time, there is a lever behind the door that will briefly open it.",["zone"]="Castle Oztroja",["grid"]="H-7 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once through the Brass Door, there will be a wooden plank with a red circle (trap door) in front of a Brass Statue. Have everyone stand on the plank. Click on the statue and input the passwords in the order that you received them (again, being mindful of case sensitivity). The trap door will open and everyone will fall through to the bottom. Don't worry about invisibility as the bottom of the trap door is safe.\010\010NOTE: Before continuing, if players are planning to warp out of the dungeon using Warp Cudgel, it is recommended to equip it now so they don't have to wait 30 seconds to ready the item.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once everyone has dropped down through the trap door, recast Invisible, and run down the long corridor leading to a large room with a series of ramps up to the center platform. The ??? to get the Yagudo Crest is located on the platform at Castle Oztroja (H-6) / Map 5, right besides the Yagudo High Priest, a Yagudo NM that has True Sight (aggroes by sight, but ignores Invisible). \010\010Invisible will also be ineffective against the following Yagudo Notorious Monsters: Tzee Xicu the Manifest, Yagudo Avatar, and Yagudo Templar. They are further away from the ??? than the Yagudo High Priest, but exercise caution all the same.",["zone"]="Castle Oztroja",["grid"]="H-6 / Map 5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Wait for the Yagudo NM to be sufficiently far away from the center platform, then travel up the ramps to the center platform, standing \034behind\034 any regular Yagudo which may be on that platform. As soon as you find a safe opportunity, remove invis, click the ???, then immediately re-invis.\010\010If you do get aggroed by the Yagudo High Priest, it is susceptible to Sleep.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After obtaining the Key Item, warp out as quickly as possible. \010\010Once you have the three crests, return to Maat.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_566",["title"]="Where Messengers Gather (Ulmia's Path) (Promathia Mission 5-3/Ulmia's Path)",["page_title"]="Promathia Mission 5-3/Ulmia's Path",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Promathia_Mission_5-3%2FUlmia%27s_Path",["revision"]="119097",["requirements"]="Start: Cid \226\128\148 Metalworks (H-8)\010Previous: Desires of Emptiness",["rewards"]="1000 Experience Points",["repeatable"]="Not specified",["summary"]="Ulmia has journeyed to San d'Oria to search for any word on the whereabouts of Prishe.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Hinaree in the Count Chaffaules Manor in Southern San d'Oria (B-6).",["zone"]="Southern San d'Oria",["grid"]="B-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upstairs behind the door to the right.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="5-3U1: Entanglement",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Zone into Port San d'Oria for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Chasalvige in the manuscript room of the Northern San d'Oria (L-6) in the cathedral, the first door on the left as you enter.",["zone"]="Northern San d'Oria",["grid"]="L-6",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="5-3U2: Head Wind",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Kerutoto in the Rhinostery, Windurst Waters (J-8) / South.\010\010Note: This is the same NPC that gives you the key item for the uncapped Diabolos fight. If you receive this cutscene first, talk to her twice afterwards to watch the correct cutscene to continue on with this mission.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="J-8 / South",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Yoran-Oran in Yoran-Oran's Manor in Windurst Walls (E-5). \010\010Note: It might be necessary to talk to Yoran-Oran multiple times to trigger the needed dialogue. Make sure he mentions Attohwa Chasm.",["zone"]="Windurst Walls",["grid"]="E-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Boneyard Gully\010\010Travel to Attohwa Chasm (exit Tahrongi Canyon (K-5) into Maze of Shakhrami then follow the left wall until you zone into Attohwa Chasm @ Maze of Shakhrami (F-5). \010\010Once inside Boneyard Gully follow the left wall to the top of F-6.\010When you zone into Boneyard Gully, follow the left wall until you come to a Dark Miasm for a cutscene and a level-50 BCNM battle (Head Wind).\010\010Note: In Attohwa Chasm, you will need antidotes and sneak. There are purple flowers that spray a purple mist of poison. The Antilions in this area are decent-challenge at level 75, they will aggro to sound and low-HP. \010 \010Level 50 Cap BCNM - Head Wind",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="There is a large ridge in the center of the Boneyard Gully and on the far side of the ridge are your three opponents: the Mithran Trackers Shikaree X, Shikaree Y, and Shikaree Z.\010\010Shikaree X is a BST/NIN wielding two daggers. She calls Shikaree X's Rabbit.\010\010Shikaree Y is a DRK/MNK wielding a Scythe. Be sure not to attack her from the front, as she can Counter.\010\010Shikaree Z is a DRG/WHM wielding a Polearm. She calls Shikaree Z's Wyvern.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The three Trackers have a strong innate Regain effect, giving them high rate of TP gain. They can use all standard Weapon Skills up to and including Level 240+ WSes (Evisceration, Spiral Hell, Impulse Drive). They will use these WSes rapidly, producing Skillchains in turn (even with themselves, in some cases).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Using a Blackened Muddy Siredon (obtained from the quest Mithran Delicacies) on the Trackers will remove their Regain effect for an unknown amount of time.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Trackers have about 2000 HP each; the pets have about 900.\010Strategy tips\010\010 The Trackers' hate works in a different manner than most other fights. It's not completely shared\226\128\148they will attack different targets if they are Provoked by different players\226\128\148but when they have TP for a weaponskill they all attack the same target so they can skillchain (They talk to each before doing this so you can Stun/Bind them to stop weaponskills connecting).\010\010 Their pets have normal hate rules, and can be kited away.\010\010 Sleep any Trackers and pets you aren't fighting to prevent Skillchains. Note that the Tracker you are fighting can wake the others up by talking to them.\010\010 Beastmaster pets and dragoon wyverns will not vanish when their masters fall. They must be defeated separately.\010\010 Shikaree X can resummon her pet.\010\010 Pets will despawn if you have killed there master and wiped\010\010 Sleepga, when combined with Elemental Seal, can be of use on the Trackers, however it may not last very long.\010\010 Astral Flow is known to be an effective method to assist in clearing this battle. Two Astral Flow Blood Pacts are known to be enough to defeat both pets and leave the three Trackers with severe damage.\010\010 Drag the Trackers away from the arena; on a wipe, all enemies will return to their positions in the battlefield, leaving you to Reraise/Raise, rest to full, and return to fight remaining opponents. The Trackers will recover HP in the meantime, though any defeated Trackers or pets will remain defeated until the battle ends.\010\010 Highly damaging two hours, used in conjunction by your party damage dealers, is another good way to quickly improve your chances of winning. Hundred Fists, Meikyo Shisui, Mighty Strikes, and Eagle Eye Shot all used simultaneously at the beginning of a fight will quickly take down a Mithra's low overall HP. The faster your party can take one out, the less liabilities you have to deal with. Invincible from a Paladin tank is a good way to make sure this method works at its full potential. By taking out at least one mithra, you have increased your chances of winning in the event of a wipe and reraise.\010\010 You receive 1000 experience/limit points upon defeating the Mithra\010\010Note: It is not necessary to kill the pets. You only need to kill the 3 Mithra.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="5-3U3: Flames for the Dead",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bearclaw Pinnacle - Level 60 Cap BCNM",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Bearclaw Pinnacle from Uleguerand Range (J-9). Enter the battlefield. Flames for the Dead",["zone"]="Uleguerand Range",["grid"]="J-9",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Take as much time as you want to buff, Meditate, etc. The Snoll Tzar won't aggro until you enter the ice circle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once the Snoll Tzar aggroes you have 45 seconds to defeat it before it blows up. At 15 and 30 seconds it will grow in both actual size and in brute force of attacks. Once the 45 seconds are up it will use a Hypothermal Combustion move that does heavy damage to everyone. If this happens, even if someone survives the blast, you lose, and are ejected from the battlefield. Even if this ability is stunned or you kill it during the animation, you will lose the fight. It must not proc at all for successful completion.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If your party wipes before Snoll Tzar uses Hypothermal Combustion you will not be ejected from BC. You will either have to Raise and hope he does not aggro, or you HP. Even if one of your party members HP's and returns he/she will not be able to re-enter battleifled to raise you. So it would be wise to fight near the tunnel.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Snoll Tzar's TP attacks are:\010\010 Arctic Impact: AoE ice damage (~275 each).\010\010 Cold Wave: Nasty AoE Frost (31 HP/tick).\010\010 Hiemal Storm: Extreme directional AoE ice damage (600-1400 to Paladin, be careful of this, one shotted our tank many times).\010\010 Berserk: Gives the Snoll Berserk. This makes the fight much easier, but is very rare.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The AoE attacks have a fairly small area, so it's not hard for mages to avoid them.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Snoll Tzar's basic attacks do (~290) damage per hit to a Paladin Tank.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="It is estimated that the Snoll Tzar has 7500 HP.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You can complete the quest Bombs Away! to obtain the Shu'Meyo Salt, which can be used to gain an additional 20 seconds. Alternatively, you may purchase the salt from the Auction House.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The Shu'Meyo Salt takes 10 second to use; when used, you'll see a message that \034The Snoll Tzar has begun to melt!\034. 7 and 14 seconds later, you see \034The Snoll Tzar is emitting a large amount of steam.\034 Finally, 21 seconds after the first message you see \226\128\156The Snoll Tzar shakes off the salt!\226\128\157 The melting time does not count against you. You can use multiple salts in a given battle, but do not overlap their use, for it'll have \034no effect\034. You should also note that you will be unable to execute any commands after a salt activates for a second or two, same as potions or any other items.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Upon defeating the Snoll Tzar, everyone in the party will receive 1000 Experience Points (or Limit Points)\010Strategy tips\010\010 Shu'Meyo Salt has a use timer of 10 second. Plan out a salt strategy, and keep an eye on the chat log. Once the Snoll Tzar shakes off the Salt, its time to have the next person in line use their salt. Keep a watch for it, every second counts!\010\010 Don't panic and keep calm. This is one of the most tense missions in the game. Go over your plan and do some dry runs on normal enemies to get the procedures down.\010\010 2-hour abilities are not necessary for victory if you have the salts to spare, although they are a great bonus.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Cid in Metalworks for a cutscene.\010\010If Ulmia's Path is your final path to complete on mission 5-3, you will get an additional cutscene at Cid that leads into the next mission; if not, head to another fork.\010\010! colspan=\0343\034 | Three Paths Overview\010|- class=\034copmissions-alt\034\010! Fork 1\010! Fork 2\010! Fork 3\010|-\010|align=\034center\034 | Tenzen Path\010|align=\034center\034 | Ulmia Path\010|align=\034center\034 | Louverance Path",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Chains of Promathia",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_340",["title"]="Where Two Paths Converge (Bastok Mission 9-2)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 9-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_9-2",["revision"]="118641",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 9-1|Salt of the Earth",["rewards"]="Rank 10\010100,000 gil\01010 Mog Wardrobe\010Bastokan Flag",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="An adventurer has been attacked while on an investigation to Xarcabard -- and the attacker is said to be none other than the Dark Knight, Zeid! Report to the President's Office for a briefing on the situation at hand.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 12~16 Crystals to unlock this mission, then speak with a Gate Guard to accept it. (13 Water Crystals was enough)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Iron Eater in Metalworks (J-8) for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Make your way to the Throne Room in Castle Zvahl.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Gather up, and enter when ready. Buffs will wear off, so do it inside.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You'll be facing a two-part fight against Zeid.\010\010Part one will consist of a simple fight. Zeid can use an AoE WS that has a Sleep effect, so consider using Poison Potions. At around 65% health, you will get a small cutscene and Volker will now join your fight. Make sure everyone is done with cutscene before continuing.\010\010Part two involves Volker. You will need to keep him alive, should he fall, you will fail and be ejected from the BC. Zeid will now be able to summon two mobs called Shadow of Rage. They have a decent attack, but low HP. They are immune to Sleep, so don't bother (they were not immune to Sheep Song). Zeid will resummon them if they are defeated. Let the tank take all of them, and focus your damage on Zeid himself. Zeid CAN skillchain with his shadows, so be careful. Use your 2hrs if necessary, the fight isn't too difficult.\010\010HP is shared between part 1 and part 2, with it being impossible to one-shot Zeid in Part 1. It is, however, possible to nuke him to 1% HP and then kill him before he swings in the next round.\010\010HP will regen if Zeid in not attacked after the CS.\010\010There appears to be a bug on horizon. Volker(s) may not attack.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Clear the BC for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to the President's Office and speak to Iron Eater for another cutscene. You will be rewarded, and complete the Bastok story.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2522",["title"]="Wild Card (Quest)",["page_title"]="Wild Card (Quest)",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Wild_Card_%28Quest%29",["revision"]="118940",["requirements"]="Start: Honoi-Gomoi \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (E-7) / South\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 6\010Items: Toraimarai Coffer Key\010Previous: Crying Over Onions",["rewards"]="8,000 gil",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You have been asked to take apart the Joker Cardian and steal its Mana Orb. But ... Where, o where has the Joker gone? O where, o where can he be?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk with Honoi-Gomoi again after zoning.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Kohlo-Lakolo Port Windurst Port Windurst (G-5)",["zone"]="Port Windurst",["grid"]="G-5",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to the House of the Hero in Windurst Walls. You will meet either Joker or Apururu.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Toraimarai Canal and open a coffer for the Key item: Joker Card.\010\010Picking the coffer as a Thief will work.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return the card for your reward.\010\010If you spoke to Joker, return to the House of the Hero, \010\010If you spoke to Apururu, find her at the Manustery in Windurst Woods.\010\010Even if you spoke to Apururu, returning to the House of the Hero will still progress the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Finally, talk to Honoi-Gomoi to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2106",["title"]="Wings of Gold",["page_title"]="Wings of Gold",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Wings_of_Gold",["revision"]="101164",["requirements"]="Start: Brutus \226\128\148 Upper Jeuno (G-7)\010Requirements: Beastmaster 40+\010Fame level: 1\010Items: Delkfutt Key or Thief's Tools\010Previous: Path of the Beastmaster",["rewards"]="Barbaroi Axe",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="The guiding bell is hidden somewhere inside Delkfutt's Tower. Brutus wants you to bring it back for his deceased chocobo.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="A walkthrough could not be extracted from this page. See the source before proceeding.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Walkthrough missing. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={"Beastmaster (BST)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Beastmaster (BST)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Barbaroi Axe",["revision"]="118211"},{["job"]="Beastmaster (BST)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Wings of Gold",["revision"]="101164"}}},{["id"]="wiki_7552",["title"]="Wish Upon a Star",["page_title"]="Wish Upon a Star",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Wish_Upon_a_Star",["revision"]="104295",["requirements"]="Start: Zacc \226\128\148 Bastok Markets (G-9)\010Fame: Bastok\010Fame level: 5\010Items: Fallen Star",["rewards"]="Cactus Stems x 4",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Fallen stars are said to grant any wish. Enu wants you to bring one back from a southern jungle. She thinks it might be hidden inside a tree.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Zacc near the fountain in Bastok Markets (G-9) and watch a cut scene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Malene at Bastok Markets (I-5).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Enu at Bastok Markets (G-9) and watch another cut scene, where she will ask you to find a Fallen Star to help her father. This logs the quest in your quest log.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Bring a hatchet to Yuhtunga Jungle or Yhoator Jungle and use it on a Logging Point to receive the Fallen Star (Rare/Ex).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Bastok Markets and trade the fallen star to Enu on a clear starry night (20:00 - 4:00) for your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_1497",["title"]="Wonder Wands",["page_title"]="Wonder Wands",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Wonder_Wands",["revision"]="119971",["requirements"]="Start: Hakkuru-Rinkuru \226\128\148 Port Windurst (E-7)\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 5\010Items: Mythril Rod\010Oak Staff\010Rose Wand\010Previous: Making Amens!",["rewards"]="4,800 Gil\010New Moon Armlets",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Hakkuru-Rinkuru. If you just completed Making Amens! you might need to rezone.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="First: Talk with following NPCs who are all in the Orastery, where you just talked with Hakkuru-Rinkuru\010\010 Goltata, Captain of the WHM brigade, who talks about an Oak Staff.\010\010 Yaman-Hachuman, Captain of the BLM brigade, who talks about a Mythril Rod.\010\010 Ohruru, Captain of the RDM brigade, who talks about a Rose Wand.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the weapons to Hakkuru-Rinkuru.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Your reward is a New Moon Armlets, 4800g and two of the three items back.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=Hakkuru-Rinkuru (Orastery, Port Windurst)\010 / summary=The black, white, and red mage brigades of the War Warlocks are arguing over how the Orastery's budget should be spent. The captains of the three brigades each want you to obtain a sample of the wands they want so they can decide which to buy.]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_2570",["title"]="Wondering Minstrel",["page_title"]="Wondering Minstrel",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Wondering_Minstrel",["revision"]="111263",["requirements"]="Start: Jatan-Paratan \226\128\148 Windurst Waters (F-10) / North\010Fame: Windurst\010Fame level: 5\010Items: Rosewood Lumber",["rewards"]="Faerie Piccolo",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The flutist Jatan-Paratan, who plays at the tavern, has lost his swing and now blows. It sounds as though a Hume bard who visited him lately is to blame, or maybe it's just a case of \034bard luck\034...?",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Go to Windurst Waters (F-10) / North and talk to Yuli Yaam and Yung Yaam to find that they have been worried about Jatan-Paratan lately.",["zone"]="Windurst Waters",["grid"]="F-10 / North",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Jatan-Paratan and he'll ask you how you feel about his music. Answer his question. It may take several answers until he will start to talk about the tavern and ask you your opinion. Saying that you don't recall the music (the last possible answer) and then talking to him again should start him talking about the tavern. The quest should now enter your log.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="When he asks your opinion on the tavern, talk to Aramu-Paramu, and he will also express his worries about Jatan-Paratan.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You must seek out the bearded man mentioned: Ruslan in the Merry Minstrel's Meadhouse in Lower Jeuno. Chat with him and he tells you to give a Rosewood Lumber to Jatan-Paratan.\010\010Obtain a piece of Rosewood Lumber by buying it from the Auction House or crafting it if you are skilled enough in Woodworking.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Rosewood Lumber to Jatan-Paratan for a cutscene and your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_9803",["title"]="Wrath of the Opo-opos",["page_title"]="Wrath of the Opo-opos",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Wrath_of_the_Opo-opos",["revision"]="19177",["requirements"]="Start: None - Yuhtunga Jungle\010Requirements: Started ZM 5 - Headstone Pilgrimage\010Items: Garnet",["rewards"]="Opo-opo Necklace",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="You must first have Zilart Mission 5 - Headstone Pilgrimage activated or completed.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After completing your business for ZM5 at the Cermet Headstone in Yuhtunga Jungle, trade a Garnet to the headstone. You will get a cutscene.\010\010Garnets can be obtained from various Treasure Chests, purchased at the Auction House (under Materials > Goldsmithing) or synthesized.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="At the end of the cutscene, you will receive the Opo-opo Necklace.\010\010[Template Quest/Description: client=None\010 / summary=The Opo-opo are not happy that you stole their \034red treasure.\034]",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_348",["title"]="Written in the Stars (Windurst Mission 3-2)",["page_title"]="Windurst Mission 3-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Windurst_Mission_3-2",["revision"]="120116",["requirements"]="Start: Any Windurst Gate Guard\010Previous: Windurst Mission 3-1|To Each His Own Right",["rewards"]="Rank Points\010Key item: Portal Charm",["repeatable"]="Yes",["summary"]="On the command of Zubaba, the head lady-in-waiting, you are to journey beneath the central magic tower of the Horutoto Ruins. There, you are to report to the facility managed by Heavens Tower, which protects the talisman that seals Castle Zvahl. Render whatever assistance is necessary.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Accept the mission from any Windurst Gate Guard and make your way to Heavens Tower and proceed to the second floor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Zubaba who will give you the Key item: Charm of Light. \010\010Note: The next part of the mission requires you to pass the Three Mage Gate. For this, you need a Black Mage, a Red Mage and a White Mage in the party or someone in possession of the Key item: Portal Charm. See the Three Mage Gate page for details on your options. \010Alternatively you if you have already done the quest Toraimarai Turmoil to obtain the Rhinostery Certificate, you can avoid having to take the Three Mage Gate and instead go through Toraimarai Canal from Windurst Walls (H-2).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to East Sarutabaruta (J-7) and enter the Inner Horutoto Ruins through the tower.",["zone"]="East Sarutabaruta",["grid"]="J-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Proceed to the Three Mage Gate:\010\010Travel through the door at the location marked \034A\034 in Inner Horutoto Ruins (G-8) / Lily Tower.\010\010Go through \034C\034 at Inner Horutoto Ruins (D-10) / Beetle's Burrow\010\010You will find the Three Mage Gate at Inner Horutoto Ruins (H-9) / Rose Tower 1, proceed through.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Continue on to the small room at Inner Horutoto Ruins (G-7) / Rose Tower 2, where you will find the Gate of Light.",["zone"]="Inner Horutoto Ruins",["grid"]="G-7 / Rose Tower 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Check the Gate of Light for a cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Heavens Tower then go through the Starway Stairway door leading to the second floor and speak to Zubaba to finish the mission.\010Note: Zubaba does not give you the Key item: Portal Charm. To obtain it, finish the mission, go down stairs the Clerical Chamber, then trade a Rolanberry to Kupipi.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Repeating the mission",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="If you have skipped this mission and obtained a higher rank, or are repeating it, the mission will work differently:",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Accept the mission and speak to Zubaba. She will ask for you to bring her 3 Rusty Daggers. These can be purchased on the Auction House (but may be rare), or obtained from the Wendigos past the Three Mage Gate (the same skeletons that drop Test Answers).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Zubaba the Rusty Daggers to complete the mission. Obtaining the Key item: Portal Charm is done the same way as completing the mission regularly.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="windurst",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_12466",["title"]="X Marks the Spot",["page_title"]="X Marks the Spot",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/X_Marks_the_Spot",["revision"]="117483",["requirements"]="Start: Despachiaire \226\128\148 Tavnazian Safehold (K-10)\010Requirements: Chains of Promathia Mission 2-5 Ancient Vows Completed\010Items: Tavnazian Liver\010Bronze Key (or Thief's Tools if main job is Thief)",["rewards"]="4000g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Despachiaire has asked you to investigate the Mithran Tracker who has come looking for Cardinal Mildaurion.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Talk to Despachiaire (K-10 Upper Level) (he's behind the Walnut Door at K-9) to start the quest. (You may have to talk to him twice if you haven't started the quest Tango with a Tracker )",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Parelbriaux. (K-7 Upper Level)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Odeya. (J-10 Upper Level)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Tavnazian Liver from the Orcs in Lufaise Meadows or the Tavnazian Sheep in Lufaise Meadows or Misareaux Coast.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Tavnazian Safehold and trade the Tavnazian Liver to Odeya.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to Phomiuna Aqueducts:\010\010Map 1: Climb the ladder at F-6. Go to the point marked A at G-4.\010\010Map 2: From the point marked A, go to M-8 and climb the ladder at M-8. \010\010To get there you'll need to open the Iron Gate at J-6 with a Bronze Key (or use a thief to pick the lock, bring several Thief's Tools as it usually takes more than one try). \010\010Map 3: Take the south corridor. Check the ??? at the north-east corner of (J-9) to open the secret door to the hidden hallway. \010\010Hidden Hallway: Behind the southern door is a passage Phomiuna Aqueducts (K-8) / Map 3 where you must solve a puzzle. \010\010 The puzzle varies based on the current Vana'diel day. \010\010 Push the torches simultaneously that correspond to the following:\010\010 To push the switches, have someone count down, and press theirs before giving the \034Go\034 command. The second player should press theirs as soon as they see \034Go\034\010\010 On Firesday: Fire and Ice\010\010 On Icesday: Ice and Wind\010\010 On Windsday: Wind and Earth\010\010 On Earthsday: Earth and Thunder\010\010 On Lightningday: Thunder and Water\010\010 On Watersday: Water and Fire\010\010 On Lightsday: Light and Dark\010\010 On Darksday: Dark and Light",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Odeya for the next cutscene and your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_332",["title"]="Xarcabard, Land of Truths (Bastok Mission 5-2)",["page_title"]="Bastok Mission 5-2",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Bastok_Mission_5-2",["revision"]="115958",["requirements"]="Start: Any Bastok Gate Guard\010Previous: Bastok Mission 5-1|Darkness Rising",["rewards"]="Rank 6\010Unlock Rise of the Zilart Missions\010Unlock Dynamis\01020,000 gil\010Mog Wardrobe: 10 Slots",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="You must go to Castle Zvahl in Xarcabard. The President himself will brief you in his office.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Trade 16~18 crystals to a Conquest Overseer to progress.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Accept the mission from any Bastok Gate Guard\010\010Malduc right beside Naji can give the mission, as any other gate guards.\010\010If your rank points are low you will still need to head back to the gate prior to accepting the new mission",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Click on the Door: President's Office next to Iron Eater and enter to speak to President Karst for another cutscene.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head for Xarcabard. Castle Zvahl is on the far west of the area.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="bastok",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_11969",["title"]="Yagudo Torch (Yagudo Torch (Quest))",["page_title"]="Yagudo Torch (Quest)",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Yagudo_Torch_%28Quest%29",["revision"]="122450",["requirements"]="Start: Muckvix \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (H-10)\010Requirements: Magicite Mission active",["rewards"]="Key item: Yagudo Torch",["repeatable"]="no",["summary"]="",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="note: you must have spoken with Aldo at Lower Jeuno (J-8) to obtain Key item: Silver Bell needed for this quest. This is a sub quest of the Magicite missions: Magicite (San d'Oria), Magicite (Windurst), and Magicite (Bastok)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Muckvix at Lower Jeuno (H-10) inside Muckvix's Junk Shop.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="H-10",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Upper Jeuno (I-8) and speak with Paya-Sabya.",["zone"]="Upper Jeuno",["grid"]="I-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head back to Lower Jeuno and speak with Muckvix again for the Key item: Yagudo Torch.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_14713",["title"]="Yomi Okuri",["page_title"]="Yomi Okuri",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Yomi_Okuri",["revision"]="119336",["requirements"]="Start: Jaucribaix \226\128\148 Norg (K-8)\010Requirements: Samurai 50+\010Items: Giant Sheep Meat\010Frost Turnip\010Bastore Sardine\010Hecteyes Eye\010Previous: The Sacred Katana",["rewards"]="Myochin Sune-Ate",["repeatable"]="AF",["summary"]="Twenty years ago, a small nation was destroyed by the flames of war, and many died without reason. Your assistance is required in holding a ritual to send these troubled souls to their proper resting place in the afterlife.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="After completing The Sacred Katana, you must wait until Japanese Midnight and change areas (logging out does not count as zoning) before you can initiate this quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Part One",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head to Norg and as a Samurai, talk to Jaucribaix Norg (K-8) who will mention that a sacred ritual to guide the lost spirits of the dead is needed, but that he's missing a feather from a special bird, found only in the Labyrinth of Onzozo.",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="K-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Washu at Norg (J-8) who will tell you to bring her a piece of Giant Sheep Meat, a Frost Turnip, a Bastore Sardine, and a Hecteyes Eye if you want the Key item: Washu's Tasty Wurst that is needed to lure the bird out.",["zone"]="Norg",["grid"]="J-8",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After obtaining Key item: Washu's Tasty Wurst, head to Buburimu Peninsula and enter the Labyrinth of Onzozo.\010\010Stick to the left wall all the way until you see a hut with a ??? at Labyrinth of Onzozo (F-8).\010\010Click the ??? and choose to lay down the Key item: Washu's Tasty Wurst to spawn a Notorious Monster Roc, Ubume.\010\010Be prepared for AoE Sleep from Horde Lullaby about every 30 seconds.\010\010Ubume can be silenced.\010\010You do not need to have Samurai as your main job to kill Ubume",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Defeat Ubume and re-examine the ??? to obtain the Key item: Yomotsu Feather.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Norg with the feather and speak with Jaucribaix (Samurai as main job not needed).",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Part Two",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Speak with Jaucribaix again, and he will say that he has finally forged the katana, which he named the Yomotsu Hirasaka.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You will receive the Key item: Yomotsu Hirasaka and are asked to take it to Valkurm Dunes.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel to Valkurm Dunes and head to the secret beach at Valkurm Dunes (B-7) in the upper Northwest corner of the map.\010\010Search the shoreline for a ??? spot, wait until nightfall (19:00 - 5:00) [Wiki: needs verification] , and click the spot and choose to initiate the ritual.\010\010You do not need to have Samurai as your main job.\010\010The Notorious Monsters Doman, a shadow, and Onryo, a ghost, will spawn.\010\010Both are mages. Onryo can use Ancient Magic.\010\010Both NMs are somewhat magic resistant. Doman's magic resistance could be as high as 50%.\010\010Both NMs are resistant to Stun.\010[Conditional wiki content: wotg \226\128\148 They can be slept by using Repose]",["zone"]="Valkurm Dunes",["grid"]="B-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="After defeating the NMs, re-examine the ??? to obtain the Key item: Faded Yomotsu Hirasaka.\010\010If you get the message \034What do you think you are doing?!\034 just wait a bit.\010\010If multiple characters are in your party, it is possible for all of them to obtain the Key item: Faded Yomotsu Hirasaka after this battle, regardless of which one uses the Key item: Yomotsu Hirasaka on the ??? to begin the fight. \010\010Make sure everyone are on the quest and have obtained the Key item: Yomotsu Hirasaka from Jaucribaix before the Valkurm Dunes Notorious Monsters.\010\010If you change areas and don't examine the ???, you will need to repeat the fight.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Travel back to Norg and talk to Jaucribaix to complete the quest and obtain your reward.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="Contains template/conditional content; compare with the wiki. ",["group"]="Zilart",["jobs"]={"Samurai (SAM)"},["job_sources"]={{["job"]="Samurai (SAM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Myochin Sune-Ate",["revision"]="21234"},{["job"]="Samurai (SAM)",["kind"]="Artifact quest",["page"]="Yomi Okuri",["revision"]="119336"}}},{["id"]="wiki_6917",["title"]="You Call That a Knife?",["page_title"]="You Call That a Knife?",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/You_Call_That_a_Knife%3F",["revision"]="121004",["requirements"]="Start: Mhebi Juhbily \226\128\148 Kazham (I-10)\010Requirements: Kazham Reputation: 6+\010Items: Sandfish\010Tonberry Board",["rewards"]="7,200g",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Mhebi wants to set her Tonberry free, but first, someone has to do something about his rusty knife.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Mhebi Juhbily tells you to go away and stop pestering. Grab a buddy (and a Sandfish) and have your buddy trade the Sandfish to her. While this is happening, check the Shed behind her. If you do it correctly, you'll see she's hiding a tonberry and get a cutscene about repairing a rusted tonberry knife. Please note that you will not lose the Sandfish so only one is needed if you are getting the cutscene for multiple people. (She will take the fish, if she ask for it and you say yes.)",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Vah Keshura in the Weapons shop who will tell you about a kitchen in Temple of Uggalepih and a master chef named Chef Nonberry.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain a Tonberry Board from either a Tonberry Pursuer in the Temple of Uggalepih or from a Tonberry Shadower in Yhoator Jungle or from a Tonberry Trailer in Den of Rancor.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to J-12 in Yhoator Jungle and enter the Temple of Uggalepih.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Follow the path until you hit the junction in H-9 and head North. Once you hit the next intersection at G-7, head North until you zone back into Yhoator Jungle.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Stay on the ledge, go left and zone in to the temple again at H-11.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Head west then south until you reach a gate. Head through the gate and keep heading south until you reach H-10. Once here, turn west and go past the Granite door.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Talk to Chef Nonberry and then trade him the Tonberry Board and he will give you a Key item: Nonberry's Knife to take back to Mhebi Juhbily.\010\010If you trade anything other than a Tonberry Board to Chef Nonberry, he will take the item traded and summon four chef NMs: Cook Nalberry who is a THF, Cook Minberry who is a NIN, Cook Solberry who is a BLM, and Cook Fulberry who is a SMN. They're capable of using their 2-hours and can be dangerous. It's recommended not to pop these.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Return to Mhebi Juhbily to complete the quest.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Quests",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_5953",["title"]="Your Crystal Ball",["page_title"]="Your Crystal Ball",["kind"]="quest",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Your_Crystal_Ball",["revision"]="111373",["requirements"]="Start: Kurou-Morou \226\128\148 Lower Jeuno (I-7)\010Fame: Jeuno\010Fame level: 2\010Items: Ahriman Lens\010Divination Sphere",["rewards"]="Kurou-Morou begins fortune-telling",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="Create your own crystal ball to have your fortune told.",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="Kurou-Morou Lower Jeuno (I-7) asks for a crystal ball.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Obtain an Ahriman Lens, which is dropped by Ahrimans. The lens is Exclusive, and cannot be traded, purchased from the Auction House, or sent via Delivery Box to another player.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you have the lens, head to the Maze of Shakhrami.\010\010You do not have to trade the lens to Kurou-Morou Lower Jeuno (I-7). You can proceed to the Rockwell without issue.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade the Ahriman Lens to the Rockwell, located at (Maze of Shakhrami (G-5) / Map 1) of the first map when entering from Tahrongi Canyon.\010\010For those without a map, hug the left wall from the entrance until you reach the Attohwa Chasm zone. Turn east right before zoning into Attohwa Chasm to reach the Rockwell.",["zone"]="Maze of Shakhrami",["grid"]="G-5 / Map 1",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Once you reach the Rockwell, trade the lens to it.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You have to wait till the next actual day reset (Japanese Midnight) to receive your Divination Sphere by clicking on the Rockwell again.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Trade Kurou-Morou Lower Jeuno (I-7) the Divination Sphere to complete the quest.\010\010If you have not completed Collect Tarut Cards, then you will receive a cutscene with Chululu.\010\01004/10/2024 cutscene with Chululu seen even after completing Collect Tarut Cards.",["zone"]="Lower Jeuno",["grid"]="I-7",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="Jeuno",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}},{["id"]="wiki_3692",["title"]="ZM16 The Celestial Nexus (Zilart Mission 16)",["page_title"]="Zilart Mission 16",["kind"]="mission",["availability"]="unverified",["source"]="https://horizonffxi.wiki/Zilart_Mission_16",["revision"]="109470",["requirements"]="Start: None\010Previous: The Sealed Shrine",["rewards"]="Mog Wardrobe 2: 5 slots",["repeatable"]="No",["summary"]="The fate of Vana'diel awaits you in the Celestial Nexus!",["changes"]="",["steps"]={{["text"]="{| width=100% |\010|- valign=top |\010|",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="The The Shrine of Ru'Avitau is full of magic aggro, so even mages should bring along Silent Oil and Prism Powder.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Anyone who can sub Ninja will have a far easier time of this BC. That includes mages, as most of the attacks in the fight are absorbed by Utsusemi.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="You may need someone to operate the Yellow door. The closest Monolith to your location is around I/J-9/10.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go to (Ru'Aun Gardens (I-6)) in front of Genbu's Island and enter the Shrine. You'll be on Map 2. Sneak and head south. Go past (The Shrine of Ru'Avitau (J-7) / Map 2) through the first yellow door. Go west from here, to the room with 2 Monoliths in (The Shrine of Ru'Avitau (H-7) / Map 2). You'll need Invisible, then go south to a room with 2 Dark Elementals around (The Shrine of Ru'Avitau (H-10) / Map 2.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Go north, down a flight of stairs to the Celestial Nexus at (The Shrine of Ru'Avitau (H-9) / Map 2).",["zone"]="The Shrine of Ru'Avitau",["grid"]="H-9 / Map 2",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="Gather together and get ready for the last BC of the expansion. You'll be fighting Eald'narche, who has two forms.",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""},{["text"]="To note; Sometime there is a bug with the Exoplates, and they are not where the target marker is. its invisible somewhere else. The pets can guide you to where it really is so its recommanded to have at least one pet job.\010||\010\010|}",["zone"]="",["grid"]="",["npc"]=""}},["review"]="Imported from wiki; not verified in game.",["warnings"]="",["group"]="rise of the zilart",["jobs"]={},["job_sources"]={}}}
